{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":1922,"timestamp":"2026-10-01T16:17:42.914425599Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"55c5c20f-caac-4131-a396-f42418deebb7","comment_uuid":"5950fe6c-71bb-4ccf-82b0-a79c0d623b33","author":"6ME5","content":"Installed exact PR #105 head 29d877de and exercised one ordinary repository-writing task through the real TUI, public CLI, daemon, provider, managed worktree, and WebUI HTTP route.\n\nTask: create docs/ci-qualification-consolidation.md from current repository evidence, review it, and leave a candidate for acceptance.\n\nPassed:\n- packaged artifact installed into an isolated home; installed hashes matched the package and version reported 0.0.4\n- trusted-workspace onboarding, provider execution, and real repository reads worked\n- TUI detach/relaunch retained the run and live event stream\n- forced exact test-daemon crash was detected; Ctrl-R respawned the daemon and restored the same run\n- indeterminate provider work was not silently replayed\n- public CLI exact retry requeued the same run\n- cancellation reached durable terminal state and left no provider child\n- managed worktree stayed clean and source checkout remained at exact pushed head\n- exact WebUI built, started, and returned HTTP 200 with security headers\n\nDaily-driver blockers reproduced:\n- after more than 40 minutes, the task produced no edit and no candidate; pre-crash durable counters already showed 8 provider requests, 25 tool calls, and 367.1k tokens\n- CLI progress counters and durable timestamp stayed stale while the TUI showed live post-retry work, so an operator could not tell progress from a hang\n- recovery says explicit retry is required, but TUI has no /retry; /resume opens the unrelated durable-goal path. Retry required the public CLI\n- steering to stop reading and return the design was accepted but not promptly enforced; further tool calls occurred and terminal UI reported input received 5 / incorporated 4\n- provider turns remained opaque for multi-minute intervals without a useful attempt deadline or heartbeat\n- reconnect reset the visible working timer\n- no candidate meant review, accept, and commit routes could not be exercised\n\nRequired repair order before a sustained soak:\n1. Add a direct TUI retry action or make recovery text name the actual /runs -> retry and CLI route.\n2. Publish phase-independent live progress: current provider-turn age, last event time, request/tool/token counters.\n3. Add a visible configurable provider-turn deadline that settles into exact-id recovery.\n4. Apply steering at the next provider boundary and block later tool dispatch after a stop-tools instruction.\n5. Preserve elapsed-time origin across reconnect.\n6. Bound repeated immutable-workspace reads.\n\nQualification after repair: run ten real installed workflows across docs, small bugs, cross-platform edits, investigations, failing tests, review-only, recovery, and next-day resume. Each must exercise plan/build/review/accept/commit plus detach, daemon crash, timeout/retry, steering, cancel/discard, and concurrent TUI/CLI/WebUI observation. Gates: first actionable edit <=10m, status freshness <=5s, cancel <=10s, zero source-checkout mutation, exact run-id recovery, no duplicate side effects, and no unincorporated steering at terminal.\n\nEvidence is retained under /tmp/peritus-human-route-29d877dee.","created_at":"2026-10-01T16:17:42.902815536Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA5S+2AMFLLGtqEEnUjLE9ech4u6P5cymWVavWUaVD4KnW+6SjCL1mLAVnifrlkDk6zJM814ajuwAi8/vlNrMBCg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZD