{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2090,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:09:44.266994620Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"1d5342a0-e55e-4413-b2dd-ad4438934bc7","comment_uuid":"42bcef03-27c2-41fe-98fa-1e71200e3727","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L003: checkpoint storage must be independent of patch-command payload admission.\n\nThe causal coupling is in peritus-daemon checkpoint capture and the product-runner BeforeMutation observer: a recoverable file-size/storage failure becomes StaleRevision and prevents command dispatch. A checkpoint is an immutable recoverable workspace snapshot; a patch is an authorized mutation transaction. They need separate representations and admission rules.\n\nChange capture to stream file content into chunked immutable artifacts and persist a manifest of exact path, kind, content digest, revision and ownership. Align automatic capture, manual capture, sealing, writable fork validation and rewind with that snapshot contract. Preflight must confirm a restorable snapshot before permitting the mutation. Restore large snapshots through one durable transaction with recoverable progress, not unrelated partial patches. A real storage shortage enters an observable recoverable wait under the same task and native-session identity. Return typed storage, contention, stale-preimage and integrity failures; only actual revision mismatch is StaleRevision.\n\nPreserve protected paths, canonical path identity, symlink/ancestor checks, exact preimages, explicit user cancellation and exactly-once effect receipts. Already accepted checkpoint evidence cannot be invalidated by a newer admission policy. Retain old manifest decoders; publish a versioned manifest/artifact representation atomically, verify its recovery roots before switching writers, and keep the prior generation readable during rollback. Coordinate L006, L010, L013 and L020 so capture never promises a restore that downstream encoding cannot perform.\n\nAcceptance requires automatic capture and command execution with files just above 8 MiB; manual capture and restoration across more than 1,024 paths and an aggregate above 8 MiB; fault injection during chunk write, manifest publication and restore; exact saved-workspace restoration after reopen; and retained task/native-thread identity. Changing a preimage, introducing a protected path or an unsafe ancestor must still reject the mutation. Existing small snapshots and commands must retain their behavior. Read the remaining callers and run applicable ordinary and formal checks on the final migration; no source-only plan guarantees nonregression before those checks.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:09:44.262904970Z","kind":"decision","signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAm1BJirKso82mA6F/Fz5dyaBFRcYWqy/BDBvon5SimVqUn29kUx3q8nHVWZWJEIZmtT8LwLoUu79bCuilpvoaDg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQI98Xr6JQmu4QgFhsjHuNrPpX4osKsT2a509jQlf+Z6buvoqnlFpZOrl7Jjgl/dHOX6KWAB+rIk3xtLp8VzTHgo="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2091,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:16:26.276169548Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"d1db310b-7731-5d58-9369-497f32b29bef","title":"[L004] Checkpoint coverage omits partial selections and empty directories","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L004.\n\n- `capture.rs:30-50` excludes deselected files, external imports without a workspace path, partial file ranges, folder-identity mismatches, and duplicate references from selected restore coverage.\n- Lines 190-226 record an empty-directory exclusion because an automatic checkpoint cannot restore the directory; the directory must be empty when observed.\n- Daily-driving effect: whole-file capture and directory restoration are distinct capabilities. A selected range cannot become a whole-file restore point under this implementation, and removed empty directories lack restoration coverage. Callers and recovery behavior remain pending.\n- `checkpoints.rs:42-45` explicitly excludes credentials, approvals, process state, and external side effects while preserving conversation/goal/accounting history. Lines 65-69 allow a read-only fork without captured-path validation but reject a writable fork with no checkpoint paths.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHpfpKiLOLSItQq/6sz7lAc7hEIQC9r4/lYD+U/SGE1/eUXSWY63MXMdOALAAJnO5QJWmEs0t42B9XOz7X//Jwk="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2092,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:16:26.279569900Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"d1db310b-7731-5d58-9369-497f32b29bef","comment_uuid":"b75714c0-60fa-45fd-8e81-478193ece6e6","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L004: Checkpoint coverage omits partial selections and empty directories.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: capture.rs:30-50; checkpoints.rs:42-45. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nMake checkpoint coverage a typed capability manifest: whole files, selected ranges, absent paths and empty directories have distinct restore operations. Record what is covered and why anything is excluded before promising a writable fork. Restore directory identity and range preimages through the same transaction and conflict rules as files; keep credentials, approvals and external effects outside workspace rewind.\n\nPreserve: exact snapshot/preimage identity, protected paths, ancestor and symlink safety, writable-fork coverage, conflict detection, one logical restore transaction and exact effect receipts. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large-file and many-path capture/restore, divergent preimage rejection, interrupted staging/publication/restore, then reopen and continue the same conversation with an exact restored workspace. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:16:26.167Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNd505yeQvh2hnuTxSAEUIeZsEg1Wt35XUHc4QPGdPYwW+EEIoHG5QNcRyZzQzEYRJAqvPpS5nA4g9uk5tVM3wQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2093,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.850887080Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"46c35a83-e54c-50cb-b7d9-dce83600dd40","title":"[L006] Patch creation, replacement, deletion, and encoding admission limits","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L006.\n\n- `crates/runtime/peritus-patch/src/set.rs:11-16,40-60` declares **8 MiB per file**, **8 MiB aggregate final payload**, and **1,024 operations**. Any present preimage above 8 MiB is rejected, including a delete operation with no final bytes. `content.rs:31-39` rejects transformed final bytes above 8 MiB.\n- `verified.rs:19-32` requires a nonempty patch and enforces both operation count and final-byte totals. `set.rs:158-196` canonicalizes through `CodecLimits::PRODUCTION`; encoder errors collapse to a generic patch-bounds error. `set.rs:88` additionally requires transaction-manifest capacity.\n- Daily-driving effect: ordinary large files cannot be edited or deleted through this patch representation; a sufficiently large multi-file change cannot be admitted as one patch. The production codec and transaction-manifest bounds may further restrict payloads; those definitions/callers are pending complete reads.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJs+T4IxMtHqlPjeZ1q+5/QkJveyPd/sMzjScAFRn20XRghRvZUrMM1FekXBHooFOimexcYkelP76N96FbxcRwQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2094,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.853673444Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"46c35a83-e54c-50cb-b7d9-dce83600dd40","comment_uuid":"2b84b21a-5df1-4fea-aa92-6630befc6619","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L006: Patch creation, replacement, deletion, and encoding admission limits.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/runtime/peritus-patch/src/set.rs:11-16,40-60; content.rs:31-39; verified.rs:19-32; set.rs:158-196; set.rs:88. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nSeparate mutation identity from inline file bodies. Stage large preimages and final bodies as streamed immutable artifacts, bind their digests to one authorized transaction, and page the operation manifest without turning each page into an independently accepted partial mutation. Validate capture, canonical identity, manifest publication, recovery and restoration under the same versioned contract before dispatch.\n\nPreserve: exact snapshot/preimage identity, protected paths, ancestor and symlink safety, writable-fork coverage, conflict detection, one logical restore transaction and exact effect receipts. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large-file and many-path capture/restore, divergent preimage rejection, interrupted staging/publication/restore, then reopen and continue the same conversation with an exact restored workspace. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQO1H72iFA0C7f8i2t0BMCRV4k23jbHeTkOZXEAgOcNQwjWmjiKXicQ893N/rOZ1SS5aiGkxfuYBxEdTa2T02sgQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2095,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.855919839Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"eff711ca-d8a7-5368-a6e8-0918230974e1","title":"[L007] Independent source-scan and included-content ceilings","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L007.\n\n- `crates/runtime/peritus-workspace/src/scoped_inspection.rs:16-17` caps the **complete source at 64 MiB**. `scoped_inspection/read.rs:98-109` rejects it before scanning even for a small selected range.\n- `inspection.rs:9-10` caps **included content at 8 MiB**. `scoped_inspection/read.rs:30-32` refuses a zero or larger caller bound; whole files and selected ranges are rejected rather than truncated at lines 101-109 and 134-138.\n- `scoped_inspection/selection.rs:26-38` rejects byte ranges beyond 64 MiB and line selections beyond **67,108,864** lines. Full source hashing and metadata checks are coupled to range reads, so selecting fewer bytes cannot bypass the source cap.\n- Daily-driving effect: inspection/attachment/checkpoint callers can refuse ordinary large build artifacts and datasets. Checkpoint capture supplies the full-file 8 MiB bound (L003); remaining callers are pending.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNuNmqJMg2hv0crY2UsgofJ1F5rkD06gsCU69etW7o7ItDU8u6XiUhXg4LpFB8JpRAFzNM51jHaY9ridrMZxnQ0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2096,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.858794664Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"eff711ca-d8a7-5368-a6e8-0918230974e1","comment_uuid":"82202de9-b05c-4363-b095-61523e3c53d2","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L007: Independent source-scan and included-content ceilings.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/runtime/peritus-workspace/src/scoped_inspection.rs:16-17; scoped_inspection/read.rs:98-109; inspection.rs:9-10; scoped_inspection/read.rs:30-32; scoped_inspection/selection.rs:26-38. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nRepresent inspection as an exact source identity plus a resumable range cursor. Stream hashing and selected bytes instead of requiring the complete source to fit an allocation policy; make each output page carry the actual observed interval and explicit continuation. Keep before/after identity checks so a changing source cannot masquerade as a complete stable read.\n\nPreserve: exact snapshot/preimage identity, protected paths, ancestor and symlink safety, writable-fork coverage, conflict detection, one logical restore transaction and exact effect receipts. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large-file and many-path capture/restore, divergent preimage rejection, interrupted staging/publication/restore, then reopen and continue the same conversation with an exact restored workspace. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQI33szKjIuKw8L0+72UG5m0h2MmMpqwy+9hjJxNY/VqeRPFv4U/8aW9uGiXmE+VhhcypbihH7wr21FDdRYvn7wA="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2097,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.861171552Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"9a6dfce0-f7af-5007-9212-db912e47510a","title":"[L008] Path representation and all-or-nothing directory inspection","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L008.\n\n- `crates/runtime/peritus-patch/src/path.rs:7-12,27-49,84-105` limits components to **255 UTF-8 bytes**, paths to **4,096 bytes**, and depth to **256 components**. The actual path/depth predicate repeats literal values in `verified.rs:9-15`.\n- The path schema also rejects noncanonical/traversal paths, control characters, backslashes, colons, trailing dots/spaces, Windows device names on every platform, and protected Git/Peritus metadata. Traversal/protected-path checks are authority boundaries; portability and representational ceilings have separate daily-driving consequences.\n- `peritus-workspace/src/inspection.rs:109-124,161-171` rejects an entire directory listing when one child name is non-UTF-8/nonrepresentable or one child is a symlink/special node. This file skips protected metadata, but does not skip or report individual unsupported ordinary entries.\n- Daily-driving effect: an otherwise usable Unix folder can become unlistable because a single child is outside this portable schema. More directory/tool callers and error presentation remain pending.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFt48R3MjqRCbavCLhP1gUaj5JIDqTTiGnG9nzUiFtykHhYLf7+xgVlWUH2xf+s02r3f3xkUUFJ4icME+q1f3Qk="}
