ation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large-file and many-path capture/restore, divergent preimage rejection, interrupted staging/publication/restore, then reopen and continue the same conversation with an exact restored workspace. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNp7z2USzx0sHAA3fGAlHbY1QUPq8nOWEHrzqRc0S/TECbJpOS1H0tp2PTTcg8KIKuoOr2eWxyUkj822SaJA6Qo="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2101,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.869927038Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"633c55c1-fab0-55bb-ba3f-cea264bee961","title":"[L010] Checkpoint manifest count and text-field ceilings","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L010.\n\n- `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/control/checkpoint.rs:114,156-160,178-182,313-319` limits each path/exclusion/external-effect vector through `u16` conversion (**65,535 entries**). Field types are `ControlText<4096>` for paths, `<256>` for names, and `<512>` for exclusions/external effects; `control/text.rs:20-25,36-39` enforces the byte ceiling on construction and deserialization.\n- `checkpoint/restore.rs:31,132-138` applies a 65,535 conflict-path count and `ControlText<4096>` path text; invalid settlement/count combinations return `InvalidInput`.\n- Potential cross-type blocker: automatic empty-directory capture places a path plus explanation in a 512-byte exclusion field while accepting paths up to 4,096 bytes (L004/L008). The ControlText byte check is verified. This is a source-established admission mismatch; an executable reproduction has not yet been run.\n- Ownership/run/revision/idempotency checks are recorded separately from count/byte ceilings; file bodies are explicitly separate artifacts, not manifest fields.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQC4q/blFlEROc9dGpm1wDbV9wpIHE7aNrQksZwSlhs8HCbUgKA9H2qyNEC+dzH1GBApw4PeOef6FRH+515mBgAw="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2102,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.872075103Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"633c55c1-fab0-55bb-ba3f-cea264bee961","comment_uuid":"8357a967-4411-4c0b-9e7e-027c67947c24","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L010: Checkpoint manifest count and text-field ceilings.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/control/checkpoint.rs:114,156-160,178-182,313-319; control/text.rs:20-25,36-39; checkpoint/restore.rs:31,132-138. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nStore checkpoint entries in a digest-bound paged manifest with stable path identities. Separate exclusion reason codes and display explanations from path fields, so a valid path never becomes invalid when a label is appended. Derive restore coverage from the same manifest contract and remove narrow u16 counts from lifetime snapshot identity.\n\nPreserve: exact snapshot/preimage identity, protected paths, ancestor and symlink safety, writable-fork coverage, conflict detection, one logical restore transaction and exact effect receipts. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large-file and many-path capture/restore, divergent preimage rejection, interrupted staging/publication/restore, then reopen and continue the same conversation with an exact restored workspace. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAh6ek4eCWhszkyYF1s4ANXs5jXsvR62RbPdSf5JUCjQBUHXQDKpr2g6Nw7vVzDGc/JAKK9bjEPt5VjEVhOeEg4="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2103,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.874151959Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"0e256da4-2478-5e71-8178-98da87d15c6c","title":"[L011] Durable control and request-context size admission","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L011.\n\n- `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/control.rs:62-68` binds maximum control-operation/current-state bytes to `peritus_journal::MAX_STATE_BYTES`, and combined request-context bytes to `ProtocolLimits::PRODUCTION.max_text_bytes()`. `peritus-journal/src/record/state.rs:8-11,87-99` defines and enforces **16 MiB per durable state value** and **1,024 bytes per state key**; the request-context text value is **16 MiB** in `peritus-model-protocol/src/bounds.rs:32`. Growing-state serialization enforcement is still being traced.\n- Its public errors at lines 91-99 describe `StaleRevision` as “control state changed; refresh and reapply the exact intent,” and `Capacity` as “control state capacity exceeded.” This confirms the misleading user-visible wording reached by checkpoint inspection error collapse (L003).\n- The schema is explicitly versioned; unsupported persisted generations are rejected. Migration/recovery behavior remains pending.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKLrPaSax+X3N3/02OM2Rh69S11oTmYLaq0o5s6YLa1pgIehm3zJu/89tAkP52w1Zk0Bk352WW1QWSBDQe53uwA="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2104,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.876488552Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"0e256da4-2478-5e71-8178-98da87d15c6c","comment_uuid":"3b6d02ca-c3ef-4e9e-b976-d55e648b9763","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L011: Durable control and request-context size admission.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/control.rs:62-68; peritus-journal/src/record/state.rs:8-11,87-99; peritus-model-protocol/src/bounds.rs:32. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nReplace whole growing ConversationRecord/control-state values with append-only operations, indexed receipts and verified projection checkpoints. Separate governing request references from model-visible text. Publish a complete readable successor atomically, keep the predecessor on admission failure, and share the stored schema contract with recovery instead of canceling work when a projection grows.\n\nPreserve: governing inputs, complete pending tool protocol pairs, exact source/lineage references, explicit permissions, unresolved effect truth and task-role/native-provider identity. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long productive read/write sessions through repeated compaction and segment boundaries, source/dependency changes, non-ASCII and large evidence, interrupted checkpoint publication, then reopen the same lineage and prove that valid grounding is reused and stale targets are reread. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHnTSbEV1AmXgypl6SOTLSRB2DkybYZP+hb1kv5GC4VBAlBrGwgc/kF8aNDR97Kqai4E7kJXzTJXOrDbdWLJKwY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2105,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.878590704Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"808122f8-a0f1-5dd3-bdd2-98ea221add6e","title":"[L012] Derived text can exceed otherwise valid field capacity","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L012.\n\n- `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/control/text.rs:20-25` rejects a string above its const byte ceiling. There is no truncation or overflow accommodation.\n- Automatic empty-directory checkpoint exclusions concatenate an otherwise accepted path and explanatory text before storing it in `ControlText<512>` (L010). A sufficiently long valid path therefore fails automatic checkpoint admission.\n- `peritus-daemon/src/product_run/workbench/checkpoints/logical.rs:34-37` prefixes an existing conversation title with `Rewind of `, then applies `ConversationTitle::new`; its failure becomes `ControlError::Capacity`. Exact title ceiling and public callers are pending.\n- Structural issue: transformations enlarge already-admitted values while reusing the original destination ceiling. This can block recovery/branching because of incidental label length.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQM0+Tp4fhOwAnuyREcOkOJMR8OhjyvgrX3UvBDtGwqo4LLlAX/rGxU6xFmMu860SgBS6Nl7d2D4S4h64eXDZdQY="}
