on must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large-file and many-path capture/restore, divergent preimage rejection, interrupted staging/publication/restore, then reopen and continue the same conversation with an exact restored workspace. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMkU1lLXMMi8MegNsAoVSuQCMtExqFqDC/EZp9+swanjp5HnD9itoHvsYli8UJWA1mGlkBNVtLvmrwWHT0PjTwY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2107,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.883275721Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"52660b7a-dec4-5ecd-ab9e-e9858164ba0e","title":"[L013] Checkpoint coverage and restore capabilities disagree","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L013.\n\n- `checkpoints/rewind/plan.rs:29-73` creates one PatchOperation per changed Restore path and constructs bounded `FinalFile`/`PatchSet` values. Checkpoint admission allows 65,535 paths (L010), while patch admission accepts only 1,024 operations and 8 MiB of final bytes (L006).\n- A manual checkpoint of more than 1,024 small files can fit its capture limits, but restoring all those files in one rewind exceeds patch operation admission. This conclusion follows from the fully read implementations; executable reproduction is pending.\n- `checkpoints/projection.rs:152-154` collapses every PatchError into `InvalidInput`, discarding the actual byte/count/recovery classification. Preview and apply also re-read current files through L003's capped capture path.\n- Required structural repair must align capture, durable representation, restore execution, and recovery capability; changing the capture ceiling alone would leave an unrestorable checkpoint path.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQG2lF6MRQHWOXIUexy//bFUm1orJAmVnGqVOMg0ORAr7EW7BK+Le9CJCJgRPEzCi+H06nwzVIhIWjvkNZ3k+6gs="}
