y owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large-file and many-path capture/restore, divergent preimage rejection, interrupted staging/publication/restore, then reopen and continue the same conversation with an exact restored workspace. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOqsAarXP9+Yp9/mX8BKflpy2sDjTpWzy9z5ysrXl+DRZRRphcb0WIIo01x6XBYsli+KiP0Q24hhlNo/75mudQM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2109,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.887560141Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"04c8c96b-1eb3-515f-8f10-02232808760a","title":"[L014] RecoveryRequired restore can become a persistent recovery barrier","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L014.\n\n- `checkpoints/rewind.rs:60-65` refuses every new rewind preview if any prior restore is Prepared or RecoveryRequired, including a conversation-only preview.\n- `checkpoints/recovery.rs:68-75,104-120` discards plan reconstruction, C1 reconciliation, and checkpoint inspection errors. Missing/uncertain evidence yields RecoveryRequired at lines 125-151 and 197-229.\n- `checkpoints/lookup.rs:105-157` reconciles only Prepared records; an existing RecoveryRequired record takes the terminal receipt path instead. `control/checkpoint/restore.rs:129-136` only permits settlement from Prepared, and `control/record/transition/checkpoint.rs:127-139` calls that same transition.\n- Daily-driving consequence: a transient capacity/I/O/inspection failure during recovery can produce a durable state that blocks subsequent rewind attempts and is not retried by the inspected recovery entrypoint. Whether another explicit repair path exists elsewhere remains pending whole-codebase coverage.\n- Exact preimage/postimage and ownership evidence are real recovery constraints; the concern is loss of the error cause and terminal classification of unresolved recovery.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQ