{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2110,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.889959850Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"04c8c96b-1eb3-515f-8f10-02232808760a","comment_uuid":"124ea7a4-e0c3-41cd-ba46-436bf7d07233","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L014: RecoveryRequired restore can become a persistent recovery barrier.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: checkpoints/rewind.rs:60-65; checkpoints/recovery.rs:68-75,104-120; checkpoints/lookup.rs:105-157; control/checkpoint/restore.rs:129-136; control/record/transition/checkpoint.rs:127-139. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nModel RecoveryRequired as an unresolved durable obligation with its retained cause, ownership and evidence, not a terminal receipt that cannot settle. Provide a reconciliation transition that can re-observe exact identities and resume the same Prepared restore after transient failures. Only a proven conflicting preimage fences the affected workspace; conversation-only operations should not inherit unrelated workspace uncertainty.\n\nPreserve: exact snapshot/preimage identity, protected paths, ancestor and symlink safety, writable-fork coverage, conflict detection, one logical restore transaction and exact effect receipts. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large-file and many-path capture/restore, divergent preimage rejection, interrupted staging/publication/restore, then reopen and continue the same conversation with an exact restored workspace. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCjyMHcpJIkmAG5teSHE9dT7qOc6KghuW7M66iPVKvFtL1TyLYNbs1QorcuPc7tMAnOPp7PdSOLZg+8ZQUPwwAg="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2111,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.892015907Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"146f6777-df2a-5b23-9842-5232ea8d88a5","title":"[L015] Workspace run admission, folder mode, and result pagination","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L015.\n\n- `peritus-daemon/src/product_run.rs:159-177` rejects duplicate run IDs, an existing active run in the same workspace, and any workspace barrier enforced by deliverable discard. The active-run predicate and discard implementation are pending full reads.\n- Lines 241-245 reject Build mode for a registered ordinary folder with GitRequired. This is a mode/workspace capability restriction, not an elapsed deadline.\n- Lines 262-265 cap each run-list page at `MAX_PRODUCT_RUN_PAGE` and support an offset. Pagination alone does not prove lost records or stopped work; its definition/callers remain pending.\n- Provider fallbacks at lines 289-298 are populated only when automatic provider failover is configured.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQL0mFQkB2TrlDJnfUqUZQW6STQbSIte3mLf0Jdf8eAw83huHzirpKi1oW80pM9+BE8snOy0LERrILqIEJW2iYwo="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2112,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.894109811Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"146f6777-df2a-5b23-9842-5232ea8d88a5","comment_uuid":"40709502-690d-46ae-83f4-f0634a24b696","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L015: Workspace run admission, folder mode, and result pagination.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: peritus-daemon/src/product_run.rs:159-177. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nDefine activity by owned live effects and workspace mutation authority rather than by an idle conversation existing. Separate ordinary-folder and Git delivery capabilities so folder Build has an explicit supported delivery contract. Keep run pagination lossless with stable cursors and selected-run lookup; preserve duplicate run identity and simultaneous writer exclusion.\n\nPreserve: exact snapshot/preimage identity, protected paths, ancestor and symlink safety, writable-fork coverage, conflict detection, one logical restore transaction and exact effect receipts. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large-file and many-path capture/restore, divergent preimage rejection, interrupted staging/publication/restore, then reopen and continue the same conversation with an exact restored workspace. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMGIAW9hcvXGUVX7mdg2exdW5LJEp9+ygvZzuEp0ZUAfNm9aAYu7qUspP08C/2R/wXfm1g9c03G1ocdsAmvk4gU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2113,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.896777327Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"8cbf8fe1-28aa-551e-89e2-9876a10d0e48","title":"[L017] Model protocol hard ceilings cannot be widened by profiles","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L017.\n\n- `crates/model/peritus-model-protocol/src/bounds.rs:29-43` declares: **4,096 messages**, **16,384 content blocks**, **16 MiB text**, **32 MiB per inline media value**, **128 MiB aggregate inline media**, **1,024 tools**, **2 MiB schema**, **1,000,000 events**, **65,536 response items**, **8 MiB per event**, **256 MiB assembled output**, **16 MiB tool arguments**, and **2 MiB provider extension**.\n- `ProtocolLimits::new` at lines 50-59 rejects zero and any value above production. Provider profiles can only narrow these ceilings; a user cannot request a wider value through this constructor.\n- Daily-driving effect depends on request construction, stream reducers, provider profiles, and whether cumulative retained context crosses these bounds. Request count/capability enforcement, nested JSON bounds and canonical encoding are now fully read in L457-L460; provider and higher-level caller coverage remains tracked individually. `control.rs` already uses the 16 MiB text value for combined request-context admission (L011).\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNZhH0eXmqPJy0S9Y1y9IN/K0gQEGn8R2xcnJnF+EnbCBYw2KUwf1rhgKI7Xzu776tO3C23sDYP8TcIJSdFdLQ4="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2114,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.899195131Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"8cbf8fe1-28aa-551e-89e2-9876a10d0e48","comment_uuid":"317b8e12-2664-4676-9146-88ea51f1990c","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L017: Model protocol hard ceilings cannot be widened by profiles.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/model/peritus-model-protocol/src/bounds.rs:29-43; control.rs. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nDistinguish real provider/model capabilities, bounded transport allocations and durable task history. Negotiate per-message limits and stream/page large requests or store media by reference; select a model-visible frontier from archived exact history. Remove compiled lifetime event/message allowances and make genuine provider capacity an explicit recoverable selection/routing condition under the same task identity.\n\nPreserve: canonical digest and schema identity, shared writer/reader admissibility, malformed-input rejection before allocation, exact causal ordering, actual provider/OS capability boundaries and preserved accepted historical evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPn8d4AJNo3WZK4lQK1HGVKDyUdvVItsZPWhi7srfUZJAihiDhQmHi2Jsf0aU790oVcDxqOkz0VR+eE2W551sAY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2115,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.901279082Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"9b20dd9c-f5e3-5e49-b319-f992c3ebbf6c","title":"[L018] Journal causal-parent, frame, and global-query bounds","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L018.\n\n- `crates/state/peritus-journal/src/record.rs:14-15,55-56,141-147` declares **4,096 records per global query window** and enforces **4,096 causal parents per event**. ExactFrame construction at lines 74-81 validates production codec framing (L009).\n- Retention-gap reporting at lines 48-52 compares the caller's next position with the earliest retained position. This declaration does not establish whether events are actually deleted or whether a consumer fails to page; journal options/query/retention callers remain pending.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFrQ+OaWs4208OPhRmjHQ8975ATP+NWBSrumN4R1I0otP8N3NEgHUg0f6v5L3NPmtp3Z51qdZMWHOCLvEk7m1gY="}
