{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2136,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.947389316Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"7c170f63-9de4-5493-ba0b-7863d714a6da","comment_uuid":"7508c6b0-fa95-433b-8be9-44667bff9379","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L028: Accounting failures cancel the active run.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: product_run/execution/goal.rs:59-96; product_control/goal.rs:158-200,292-335. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nSeparate accounting delivery from execution cancellation. Journal accounting observations through an idempotent durable queue and reconcile a failed write under the same reservation; defer new billable effects if authoritative accounting cannot be established. Keep current owned work observable and resumable rather than killing its provider because a progress or presentation write encountered transient storage contention.\n\nPreserve: canonical digest and schema identity, shared writer/reader admissibility, malformed-input rejection before allocation, exact causal ordering, actual provider/OS capability boundaries and preserved accepted historical evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBLpOt9fn4/5jnOKrvTrIaLbjqrRdt5LxOxBqfwgIgIwCgBaF36istcz562ftfXDOOcYgmgj5sfXOxt2BA/6qw0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2137,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.949742321Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"141fdff9-bf4f-53f2-85b0-6fc769572be9","title":"[L029] Application-protocol default and negotiated capacity ceilings","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L029.\n\n- `peritus-app-protocol/src/limits.rs:40-53,240-243` defaults to production codec limits (L009), **16 version ranges**, **64 feature names**, **4,096 retained idempotency entries**, **64 subscription topics**, **256 unacknowledged events**, **256 KiB artifact chunks**, **64 prompt choices**, **64 KiB terminal chunks**, **4 KiB diagnostic text**, and **256 remaining-work items**.\n- Lines 97-118 negotiate the pointwise minimum of both peers' capacities. Constructor validation at lines 198-237 requires positive values that fit their chosen enclosing codec dimensions; these application dimensions are not individually hard-capped to production by this constructor.\n- Effect depends on the owning state machine: chunk/page boundaries can permit unbounded total progress, while retained state and one-message collections can reject work. All declarations are recorded; actual owner/caller enforcement is pending rather than assumed identical across dimensions.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIkFsTOCFqAhI2jjMAwykpaYbGLcHVHLjUv9jU0AJXscZIsKf4C5YXthqgsI5Uy9wckxZGHptDa4nxznhpOqfQ0="}
