ed effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large histories and non-ASCII fields, queue/connection pressure, delayed acknowledgements, subscription gaps, disconnect/reconnect and daemon restart, proving snapshot recovery, preserved selection/context, responsive controls and no duplicate command. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPTmy+gILpoISBYeI6EoUNlMQN6wejOWEc3LfKNV9SZY9ugU47Cyfx8JStFN7V2PbQ4eKtUIhpVb6+svNfUFbAo="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2139,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.953981168Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"aef11bf6-f167-51e0-a7a9-76ae5baead6f","title":"[L030] Product task, detail, deliverable, and page admission","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L030.\n\n- `peritus-app-protocol/src/product.rs:38-43` declares **64 KiB task text**, **1 MiB per run detail field**, and **256 runs per page**. Task-construction callers remain pending; the daemon list caller was read in L015 and supports an offset.\n- `ProductDeliverable::checked` at lines 67-78 rejects an empty changed-path collection, more than **65,535 changed paths or successful commands**, and fields above 1 MiB. Some restore constructors additionally require a successful command. Absolute/traversal/Git paths are rejected at lines 79-85 as authority/path constraints.\n- Large deliverables can be rejected even when their underlying work succeeded. One-page size does not by itself imply old runs are deleted; retention/pagination client behavior remains pending.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGTeprVeenAmAuFWvRUEMIKghwIMVhnBKaxQZCWH3mTDTO1zcnumI1RhvExu/TbAkWom38xFQ8R4jKSt9BsBgA4="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2140,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.955980113Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"aef11bf6-f167-51e0-a7a9-76ae5baead6f","comment_uuid":"9db7676c-f7af-4174-82e4-b5eb41aa87ca","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L030: Product task, detail, deliverable, and page admission.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: peritus-app-protocol/src/product.rs:38-43. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nStore task text and deliverable evidence in exact referenced artifacts with paged changed-path/command indexes. Validate deliverable readiness before sealing the successful result, so presentation capacity cannot retroactively turn a completed effect into failure. Keep nonempty delivery semantics, authority-safe paths and lossless run-list cursors.\n\nPreserve: canonical digest and schema identity, shared writer/reader admissibility, malformed-input rejection before allocation, exact causal ordering, actual provider/OS capability boundaries and preserved accepted historical evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGr18Dx8itPwA+p4BrJzjdOpYyPX1z339yIitFjE5a9/zCGmMMXB5FLOf6q5Q0XpO2jOuBNZBDWLT41ZicgdNw8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2141,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.957993759Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"2dcc6f3a-cdd4-5c64-8f16-949896a16645","title":"[L031] Legacy goal-tool replay is a schema barrier","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L031.\n\n- `peritus-daemon/src/product_control/goal/replay.rs:17-22` rejects a tool-goal reservation/completion when its current identity is absent but the legacy identity exists, returning `ControlError::UnsupportedSchema` instead of migrating/reconciling that legacy operation.\n- `goal.rs:112-125,147-155` propagates this through live tool admission/completion. Scope is exact legacy identity, not every older conversation. Other migration/recovery paths have not yet been read.\n- `goal.rs:356-363` maps Paused/Cancelled to Paused admission and WaitingForUser/Blocked/Achieved to Inactive; Active/Pausing remain accepted. These durable goal states stop work through L026. Budget triggers and resume paths remain pending.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLXkz7TtXpwhZaFiWhFmWMjJBU877P0JPjGw9WpvjuernWUwJj6zgo7O54CHjqaM3wYo16hqx+OrLJPM9LYk9ww="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2142,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.960179199Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"2dcc6f3a-cdd4-5c64-8f16-949896a16645","comment_uuid":"ac957073-bfdd-4a48-b094-4cf8750efe66","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L031: Legacy goal-tool replay is a schema barrier.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: peritus-daemon/src/product_control/goal/replay.rs:17-22; goal.rs:112-125,147-155; goal.rs:356-363. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nAdd an explicit versioned identity migration for legacy tool-goal reservations and completions. Resolve the historical command and its settlement before adopting the new identity; never create a second billable effect to bypass an old record. Distinguish unsupported evidence requiring repair from a user-paused or completed goal, and expose a same-conversation reconciliation operation.\n\nPreserve: committed command/event identity, exact causal and digest roots, exclusive ownership, atomic publication, reference-safe artifact retention and verified recovery from the last durable frontier. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNrJjgRqaS/pcuSJ9vDsKiif71Nw8YAp0ZhR42RvVsx5JSwNzXIztQdmJL9yWFEpEGYvnFpxyk1tDoaGKEAzsA4="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2143,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.962483561Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"4e64680b-f624-5c4f-9cb9-ec8c1d0601c7","title":"[L032] Goal text/count representation and checked counter exhaustion","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L032.\n\n- `peritus-product-runner/src/control/goal.rs:103,165-168` limits objective text to **8,192 bytes**, criterion descriptions to **2,048 bytes**, and transition reasons to **512 bytes** through ControlText. `goal/lifecycle.rs:17-25` and `goal/validation.rs:43-57` require a nonempty criteria collection of at most **65,535**, including a mandatory RunnerAcceptance criterion.\n- `goal/accounting.rs:32-41,111-118` uses `u32` request/tool/retry/compaction/failover counters and `u64` token/time/resource counters. `goal/execution.rs:24,43-64,93,134-153,288-289` returns Capacity on checked arithmetic exhaustion; summary queries saturate across roles at `accounting.rs:129-135,159-165`. These are representation limits rather than smaller synthetic daily-work quotas.\n- The complete goal implementation has now been read: it does **not** enforce the former request/tool/token/day ceilings. `goal/tests.rs:28-53` asserts continued admission beyond those former values; this audit has read those tests, not rerun them. Provider/storage/context ceilings remain independent.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQATZaRh0ih53RBWmld9eIFsQ/KJ9HI25uwyJaH0YFSJrzq6yFjUTRgP/Fh4HiAWnHQkWowWcPJTuMvucKhMvzQM="}
