{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2145,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.966568467Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"0485f745-0425-5558-9af5-8f4897c83b7d","title":"[L033] Optional run horizon and provider-circuit lifetime","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L033.\n\n- `peritus-product-runner/src/budget.rs:34-45,149-163` accepts an optional caller-selected elapsed horizon; `None` imposes none. A selected zero duration is rejected, and elapsed time strictly above the selected horizon returns ProductRunnerErrorKind::Budget at event/resource boundaries (lines 68-72,122-130).\n- The daemon ordinary launch was already read with `max_elapsed: None` (L023). Other callers and configuration inputs remain pending; retaining a user-selected horizon is distinct from imposing an unrequested default.\n- Lines 110-120 retain an unavailable-provider circuit in a per-run set until an explicit caller closes it. Whether retry reconnects/reopens the same native context depends on the pending failover/turn callers.\n- Fallible host-resource probing at lines 122-135 also propagates as a run error even without an elapsed horizon. Actual probe exclusions, traversal bounds, and error behavior remain pending.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAsOdOc0vBn/woYHLtd8VZTPqjqr1+IAcH2Yh1TxzHZAA2mxE8Nm/bYCmrWJOFEWYNOnt34nlV2pg+22qyqdew8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2146,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.968695016Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"0485f745-0425-5558-9af5-8f4897c83b7d","comment_uuid":"7bbadb8f-0aa8-4c21-8c23-dbc11e77d71f","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L033: Optional run horizon and provider-circuit lifetime.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: peritus-product-runner/src/budget.rs:34-45,149-163. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nKeep elapsed horizons optional and only user-selected. Separate transient provider availability from a permanent per-run circuit: retain the failed attempt identity, schedule safe retries or explicit route recovery, and reopen availability when new evidence permits it. Resource-probe failure needs a typed observable recovery state, not a fabricated deadline or abandoned context.\n\nPreserve: definitely-unaccepted versus ambiguously-accepted request state, exact native thread/profile identity, ordered provider observations, tool-result protocol, explicit cancellation and real provider/model capabilities. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPM0TKHH5FlOH4nUbU4XYkcnYZwzSwD7T2wxYYOH8q2QIK155xqNyozrUmHkN4XrrUpzI2ug0xrQ9i8/k9vbkwA="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2147,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.971084862Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"3e12729f-5f87-5bdc-8f4d-4cf620638244","title":"[L034] Goal continuation requires lifecycle/evidence admission","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L034.\n\n- `goal/execution.rs:179-235` makes incomplete or stale acceptance evidence Blocked, missing external evidence WaitingForUser, and recovery-required settlement Blocked. `goal/lifecycle.rs:114-118` marks only Active as automatically restart-eligible.\n- `lifecycle.rs:149-162` permits explicit resume from Paused, WaitingForUser, or Blocked while retaining history and usage. It rejects resume from Active, Pausing, Achieved, or Cancelled. Changes to a confirmed objective or previously achieved evidence can block continuation at lines 179-211.\n- These are explicit goal/evidence/pause semantics, not elapsed quotas. Daily-driving concern is whether product callers classify transient infrastructure/capacity errors as a terminal lifecycle state and supply a usable recovery path; those callers remain partly pending (L026/L028).\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQILTdTCAIa6jYkQ3ywMp5XncBMB/eH2OP5wfl3J08KRIva9iDYGjBCNrCWqYCmIdZQMgv4NXgZ8CEfaBrGuPPwo="}
