{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2163,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.007026009Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"6c82afc9-49f6-5c57-a3ba-c973ae69a342","title":"[L042] Tool argument schema, scope, and stdin capacities","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L042.\n\n- `developer_tools/arguments.rs:54-88` rejects schemas/arguments deeper than **16** and any unsupported keyword/type. A `OnceLock<Result<...>>` caches catalog construction failure for the process lifetime (lines 12-13,30-32). Invalid inputs fail before effects, with retry guidance.\n- `catalog.rs:114` limits one in-place scope declaration to **1..256 paths**. `catalog.rs:64` limits stdin text to **1..65,536 Unicode characters**, enforced by `arguments.rs:103-105`; downstream byte capacity may be different and is pending.\n- Resize schema requires dimensions **1..65,535** even though its parser permits zero (L037); the schema runs first. Timeout schema uses the same millisecond-representable ceiling as its parser.\n- `wire.rs:19-25` parses every observation through production CanonicalJson/JsonBounds. The exact nested JSON item/depth/byte dimensions and their interaction with list/search results remain pending.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNlYAoxqTti5Sfb1sqYKVxqvJFg3NbQ335goewglwEmzOu62bkQ5WLfJf/462OClpVJKJTApjRDV+niJQ4/eWA8="}
