{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2165,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.011605766Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"0af59d93-eb2a-5623-86ba-4a8d3d2a4a95","title":"[L043] Grounding evidence can reset at tool-executor reconstruction","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L043.\n\n- `developer_tools/grounding.rs:23-31,49-72` requires a successful workspace listing and at least one targeted read (unless the root was observed empty), plus an exact existing-target read before mutation. `executor.rs:190-192,302-304` exposes this as required-tool and completion-blocker admission.\n- `executor/construction.rs:20,52` initializes this evidence to Default for each tool executor. `catalog.rs:18,28,33,38,48` instructs grounding again in every fresh writer/fixer host invocation/current turn.\n- Potential daily-driving effect: retained provider context and host grounding evidence can have different lifetimes. Reconstructing tools can require rereading already-known files before work resumes. `peritus-product-runner/src/turn.rs:65-99,142-163,254-291` now confirms fresh writable-tool construction for each outer role invocation, including retries, while only ownership and rendered verification/command evidence merge back at lines 100-105. Per-role working memory and native session directory are retained separately (lines 54,89,295,314). This establishes mismatched lifetimes on that retry path; inner segment-continuation behavior remains pending.\n- `executor/in_place.rs:24-38` also enrolls workspace reads before dispatch and refuses command start when no exact task path is enrolled. `workspace_delivery/scope.rs` now verifies journal bounds (L046) but hashes whole files by streaming without a file-size ceiling. Do not attribute the checkpoint 8 MiB source limit to baseline stamping; these are separate implementations.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJ1/kUCND7XRogNUAZe0tu8Syl9o/0PZhFP5OOM/pFShElmYNLeMy4nXP3mB6cotPbONcNrQGFxy5HOA1Uewyw0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2166,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.013704914Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"0af59d93-eb2a-5623-86ba-4a8d3d2a4a95","comment_uuid":"051620e9-4269-4fed-9afa-41cb84a952f1","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L043: Grounding evidence can reset at tool-executor reconstruction.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: developer_tools/grounding.rs:23-31,49-72; executor.rs:190-192,302-304; executor/construction.rs:20,52; catalog.rs:18,28,33,38,48; peritus-product-runner/src/turn.rs:65-99,142-163,254-291; executor/in_place.rs:24-38; workspace_delivery/scope.rs. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nMove grounding evidence into the durable task-role state, bound to workspace revision, path identity and exact observed bytes. Tool executor reconstruction, provider retries and segment continuation must reattach that state and the same native context. Invalidate only observations whose dependencies changed; require a new read for a genuinely stale mutation target, not a new global listing on every invocation.\n\nPreserve: governing inputs, complete pending tool protocol pairs, exact source/lineage references, explicit permissions, unresolved effect truth and task-role/native-provider identity. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long productive read/write sessions through repeated compaction and segment boundaries, source/dependency changes, non-ASCII and large evidence, interrupted checkpoint publication, then reopen the same lineage and prove that valid grounding is reused and stale targets are reread. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQN5DjmFLFuN6DJI19qaWr6E4+0VXh5uuhMW5pagVICBraFFligcIyc7WC3mG7vpkNzV1DYJg8ki/EnD3fywLLgQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2167,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.015780147Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"7ae24be5-e4f6-580a-8ab3-a3698d303311","title":"[L044] Any leave-alone path disables all unconfined commands","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L044.\n\n- `developer_tools/access_policy.rs:175-180` refuses run_command, command_start, and command_stdin whenever the live hard-constraint path set is nonempty, because the configured backend cannot confine process writes away from those paths. File writes to unrelated paths remain permitted.\n- `access_policy.rs:36-48,61-78` refreshes those constraints from ConversationView each tool call. Combined with L026's whole-workspace protection fallback on a control read failure, infrastructure failure can reach process refusal through this mechanism.\n- This preserves explicit authority but exposes a capability gap: an unrelated protected file prevents even a potentially observational command. Actual process sandbox enforcement and permission/review callers remain pending; removing authority safeguards is not proposed by this audit.\n- Lines 82-119 additionally infer opaque-file/hidden-identifier restrictions by lexical matching of transcript phrases; lines 122-211 enforce those restrictions. These inferred restrictions are separate from explicit durable constraints and may misclassify ordinary prose; no live false-positive reproduction has been run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHqpMWvNEi