{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2168,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.017868202Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"7ae24be5-e4f6-580a-8ab3-a3698d303311","comment_uuid":"64d7dd60-bf87-4b29-8257-3f862c5f3ecc","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L044: Any leave-alone path disables all unconfined commands.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: developer_tools/access_policy.rs:175-180; access_policy.rs:36-48,61-78. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nRepresent explicit protected paths as enforceable backend confinement requirements. Select a sandbox capable of excluding them or expose a scoped missing capability; do not infer hard authority constraints from lexical transcript phrases. Observational commands need a confined read-only path, while writable processes must retain the leave-alone guarantee for every descendant.\n\nPreserve: canonical digest and schema identity, shared writer/reader admissibility, malformed-input rejection before allocation, exact causal ordering, actual provider/OS capability boundaries and preserved accepted historical evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJCsAezDyFWXb4GKwyWCfHQYIrXRjO5357+ARf2oCNmTjSnhDcIyEEvHEBG4rpj2kTdFOnFCM5qeIfq1TF1SMw0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2169,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.019885423Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"e7df6947-3508-5f1b-9476-5932fa95823b","title":"[L045] Tool output and filesystem-coverage exclusions","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L045.\n\n- `developer_tools/effect.rs:9,49-54` truncates text to its first **512 KiB** plus `[output truncated]`. The workspace read caller uses this prefix cut (L041), independent of its 2 MiB file/line bounds.\n- `developer_tools/path.rs:57-63` excludes any path containing `.git`, `target`, `node_modules`, `.venv`, or `__pycache__` from ordinary list/search. Targeted reads still use separate path checks. Symlink paths are rejected at lines 31-34.\n- `effect.rs:18-26` rejects direct rm/unlink/rmdir, git clean, and find -delete. `removal.rs:22-46` supports only one owned regular file or one grounded empty directory, with no recursive deletion.\n- These scope/deletion/identity restrictions are recorded alongside numeric capacities. Broader authority and explicit-user deletion callers remain pending; this audit does not silently classify them as elapsed limits.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNI4y4/kJkP8c9ScRdsemYrhC9Gju8O7HXDt69z+rBGT6HCZphaf8XyoTesGygIj8hKX0i40tvC4Mb9y4RcU3wU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2170,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.021829320Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"e7df6947-3508-5f1b-9476-5932fa95823b","comment_uuid":"b3cd8236-696a-4ca9-8c1c-72e3966636c7","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L045: Tool output and filesystem-coverage exclusions.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: developer_tools/effect.rs:9,49-54; developer_tools/path.rs:57-63; effect.rs:18-26; removal.rs:22-46. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nSeparate bounded output previews from retrievable exact evidence and make exclusions explicit in a coverage manifest. Provide authorized targeted traversal and a typed recursive deletion transaction when the user requests it, with enumerated ownership/preimages and recoverable progress. Preserve protected metadata and symlink identity checks rather than treating common cache names as universal authority prohibitions.\n\nPreserve: canonical digest and schema identity, shared writer/reader admissibility, malformed-input rejection before allocation, exact causal ordering, actual provider/OS capability boundaries and preserved accepted historical evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFHuuwIKy8b9VzLKBHSbqPN2isIpo9oYV512/AeX7OdjPaC+1UKh22yL/2JrxhBt0X0YeaKOEntmTjN6uI2wXwA="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2171,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.023855996Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"70168ce9-f55d-5cb9-809b-21798ef4c444","title":"[L046] In-place scope journal has a lifetime byte ceiling and strict torn-record barrier","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L046.\n\n- `workspace_delivery/scope.rs:14-15,86-102,165-215` limits the append-only scope evidence journal to **64 MiB** and each record to **512 KiB**. Enrollment fails when the next record crosses the total ceiling. A torn/non-newline/oversized record, wrong schema/scope, or duplicate path rejects the whole load.\n- Every paths/enroll/changed-paths/diff query loads that journal; changed paths additionally stamp every enrolled path. There is no journal rotation, chunked state migration, or torn-tail reconciliation in this file. Other recovery implementations are pending before claiming none exist.\n- File previews stop at **16 KiB** and rendered diffs at **512 KiB** (lines 122-153,260-279). Exact hashing streams whole files with an 8,192-byte buffer and has no source byte ceiling in this implementation; a buffer size is not a file limit.\n- Nonempty directories cannot be scope declarations (lines 243-248); effects therefore require explicit file paths rather than directory inventories. New read enrollment can fail for journal/schema corruption before the read tool dispatches (L043).\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNAAdGoWjJ2JtrF0UPu4nyMkJTrHVpTe0TsdQxrLkwekQEIiz1dznec0KDayhgbGK0xGbxvxq1hxIdv2pBG4gQE="}
