fects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBBT42REJZm/V+oiLWVrpsxf/nGmxFuxbb5E2fMMPgGCdly63XU5L7s4E0pb29foNdZZPfEd+x1D8CImqIDOcgo="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2173,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.028366924Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"29d7aee7-f4c3-54ad-b30c-6075a298b3a2","title":"[L047] Writer/fixer loop parameters and error-to-budget mapping","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L047.\n\n- `peritus-product-runner/src/turn.rs:292-321` constructs `DeveloperLoopLimits::new(48, 512)` for writer/fixer execution. The type definition and local-context continuation caller remain pending, so these numbers are recorded as supplied parameters rather than assumed terminal task quotas.\n- Lines 334-346 map both LimitExceeded and SegmentExhausted to ProductRunnerErrorKind::Budget. `turn/provider.rs:34-38` now verifies SegmentExhausted is handled **before** this mapping for writer/fixer: it resets recovery and starts another outer invocation with a segment-boundary correction. This avoids a terminal quota on that path but reconstructs empty grounding evidence (L043). Other role/caller paths remain pending.\n- Outer invocation count saturates at `u32::MAX` (line 74), rejected terminal output retries at lines 149-163, and changing unverified questions may retry at lines 180-187. No fixed outer retry count appears in this file. Durable invocation identity and convergence/ambiguity policy remain pending.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQF6co3ZJO0UMOpfdOkA4nxBbFwByEzqdpYCgCwAXW+zwY/lda7GkxgZ8sQQA47rYbM08BQTAaG00+ruT6PHlSwA="}
