{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2177,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.036977698Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"1de38acc-b56f-5e56-8cc6-ef6ea61bc667","title":"[L049] Developer-loop admission and generation ceilings","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L049.\n\n- `peritus-agent/src/developer/types.rs:25-41` permits only **1..128 model turns** and **1..2,048 tool calls** per loop, sets default **three attempts per model turn**, and requests **32,768 output tokens**. `with_max_attempts_per_turn` permits only **1..8** and `with_max_output_tokens` only **1..32,768** (lines 48-71).\n- `developer/execution.rs:51,258-265,392-393` enforces the selected model/tool segment and returns SegmentExhausted. A response's entire tool batch is counted before dispatch; a batch crossing the tool cap is not executed, and yielded/skipped calls count toward that segment. Writer/fixer passes 48/512 (L047); `turn/provider.rs:34-38` now confirms writer/fixer continues segments rather than terminating at that boundary. Its new segment still rebuilds the tool executor and requires grounding again (L043). Other callers remain pending.\n- `developer/model_request.rs:71-102` clips generation to the smaller profile/request ceiling, with semantic compaction additionally clipped to **8,192 output tokens**. Provider/model true limits and imposed request policy are distinct.\n- Retry/compaction outcome counters are `u16`; `execution.rs:103-104,154-156,177-182` rejects arithmetic exhaustion as LimitExceeded. These representation failures are separate from selected segment sizes. Context construction and tool-capability negotiation can also stop a turn before provider work.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed