{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2178,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.039230089Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"1de38acc-b56f-5e56-8cc6-ef6ea61bc667","comment_uuid":"7e48fdee-5a67-4a23-9b0a-8c4f7a31b288","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L049: Developer-loop admission and generation ceilings.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: peritus-agent/src/developer/types.rs:25-41; developer/execution.rs:51,258-265,392-393; turn/provider.rs:34-38; developer/model_request.rs:71-102; execution.rs:103-104,154-156,177-182. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nSeparate in-flight batches and real provider generation capacity from total task work. Continue segments with the same durable tool/context frontier, permit safe recoverable provider retries without a mandatory attempt quota, and page cumulative counters/history. Batch admission must leave unexecuted calls pending with exact identities instead of losing them at a segment boundary.\n\nPreserve: canonical digest and schema identity, shared writer/reader admissibility, malformed-input rejection before allocation, exact causal ordering, actual provider/OS capability boundaries and preserved accepted historical evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPCK4wJpGIVhFM6LKGs7Ma3oPecNelWNi/YFHpnZhV2Y8pWjrSFEe8orv4fdt21pxMPLkOHJoaONWpFl9/6h5wI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2179,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.041710760Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"2a1528e5-14df-5217-89e0-977b1e509374","title":"[L050] Retry attempts remain finite while elapsed retry horizon is absent","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L050.\n\n- `peritus-agent/src/developer/retry.rs:18-20,129-157` supplies **250 ms base delay**, **30,000 ms maximum delay**, and deterministic jitter up to **250,000 millionths (25%)** to the retry planner. These wait parameters are backoff policy, not a total execution deadline.\n- RetryInput explicitly uses `max_elapsed_millis: None`, but retains the selected finite attempt count (default three/hard maximum eight, L049). Plan Stop/Resume becomes no new attempt. Provider-required retry-after handling and final attempt outcomes remain pending complete reads.\n- `developer/execution/invocation.rs:19-26,40-48` can force exactly one declared grounding tool on a retry while disallowing a terminal answer. Model request construction disables parallel calls while a prerequisite is active (`model_request.rs:33-40,58-70`). The current executor state controls this; historical successful grounding is not accepted after executor reconstruction (L043).\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIfDmrNLg7YyaSFhB6QYLnZhpquVauwFCfnE9Sw0My8zSQIe/MPe/rLr9SmGj9FL2Vi/BwS5L7p2IkCayTqpCQM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2180,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.043920679Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"2a1528e5-14df-5217-89e0-977b1e509374","comment_uuid":"4d39cd98-eb1d-4287-88cc-219de2ffa0de","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L050: Retry attempts remain finite while elapsed retry horizon is absent.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: peritus-agent/src/developer/retry.rs:18-20,129-157; developer/execution/invocation.rs:19-26,40-48; model_request.rs:33-40,58-70. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nReplace finite transient retry attempts with a durable retry state carrying acceptance certainty, provider-request identity and next eligible time. Continue safe definitely-unaccepted retries until cancellation or a real unrecoverable condition; reconcile ambiguous accepted attempts instead of resending them. Reuse valid grounding attestations and native context rather than forcing another prerequisite after reconstruction.\n\nPreserve: canonical digest and schema identity, shared writer/reader admissibility, malformed-input rejection before allocation, exact causal ordering, actual provider/OS capability boundaries and preserved accepted historical evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQD5LSiT5isVY4VNrRT5ijHJXnsujV6ZQTH60n+kk+FhmH3LNX4YScmUw947fUXW7Fc4/CAaHPWSulDyTDHrEKgY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2181,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.046037642Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"d367639a-e1d4-5f3e-9325-513f8a9c88e0","title":"[L051] Same-provider recovery has a three-invocation cap without material progress","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L051.\n\n- `peritus-product-runner/src/failover.rs:12,26-35` permits fewer than **three failed same-provider role invocations** before recovery stops; the first two failures retry, the third does not. This is independent of each invocation's default three per-turn attempts (L050).\n- `turn/provider.rs:39-57` resets this counter when the workspace checkpoint changed, otherwise retries under the cap, then advances to an available configured fallback or returns the error. A provider outage during useful read-only reasoning can reach the cap without a filesystem change.\n- Segment exhaustion is handled separately with unrestricted outer continuation; successful provider output and material progress reset recovery. `failover.rs:38-50` instructs each restarted segment/provider invocation to list/read again, confirming the repeated-grounding path (L043).\n- Fallback selection advances through the configured chain and can open a per-run circuit for the previous provider (lines 82-89,196-207,232-250). Policy/ambiguous-acceptance failures do not automatically retry. Distinguish those integrity boundaries from the fixed transient-recovery count.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQ