{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2182,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.048226918Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"d367639a-e1d4-5f3e-9325-513f8a9c88e0","comment_uuid":"cad5faf5-ec24-451d-a34f-8dd000298a05","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L051: Same-provider recovery has a three-invocation cap without material progress.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: peritus-product-runner/src/failover.rs:12,26-35; turn/provider.rs:39-57; failover.rs:38-50. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nReplace the three-invocation material-progress gate with durable provider recovery keyed by task, role, native context and acceptance state. Read-only reasoning and new evidence are progress too. Safe outages should wait and reconnect under the same context; configured failover is an explicit state transfer preserving obligations, not a counter-triggered fresh session.\n\nPreserve: definitely-unaccepted versus ambiguously-accepted request state, exact native thread/profile identity, ordered provider observations, tool-result protocol, explicit cancellation and real provider/model capabilities. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEZFfRHGVLrwNROaGqgR5SpeV6ijm5uLeay4z1YBY8FxllF0HqM04pN7d4RuuiXjKBhTYp2G7E2ffP83YlaFBgY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2183,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.050242472Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"0da45103-4854-5d5b-98e1-1ff9f5978b2c","title":"[L052] Candidate freshness capture retries exactly three times","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L052.\n\n- `peritus-product-runner/src/execution/checkpoint.rs:244-257` attempts a before-checkpoint/content-hash/after-checkpoint identity capture **three times**, then returns a Repository error if concurrent workspace changes prevent a stable observation.\n- This is a fixed consistency retry ceiling. Concurrent generators/services can cause failure despite otherwise progressing work. Actual CandidateBaseline snapshot/digest callers, later user presentation, and backoff/reconciliation remain pending.\n- Checkpoint sequence is checked `u64` and poisoned owner mutex errors stop capture (lines 154-155,260-267). These identity/representation failures are distinct from the fixed attempt count.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJ9VGZgxgsoEcsPP4glbvnmW0DLgmmK9wsGk9aFpAcluMAROHMqmFYTTq+l1BNx8Y2kenXEw0W9WSF9AJjII+wA="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2184,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.052374156Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"0da45103-4854-5d5b-98e1-1ff9f5978b2c","comment_uuid":"52534d5a-9656-49a2-b4e5-7ac2d85a138d","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L052: Candidate freshness capture retries exactly three times.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: peritus-product-runner/src/execution/checkpoint.rs:244-257. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nUse a cancellable consistency observation state that waits for a stable exact workspace revision or a snapshot-capable backend. Retain the capture intent and original contention cause rather than failing after three probes. Never accept mismatched before/after hashes; only confirmed consistency can publish the candidate baseline.\n\nPreserve: exact candidate revision and artifact binding, complete finding/provenance conservation, independent reviewer evidence, truthful gate outcomes, protected user constraints and acceptance fail-closed on invalid evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCBij7dpv+MZeAxOHgtRv9lJgkt4HvULHwdA55pgN5xI6G4Ahe2oeWM2YGMcYndGCsGtGLShFSCcvZNaiT/0ggY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2185,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.054621756Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"22cca0dd-326a-526e-a870-14e80145f043","title":"[L053] Failure to publish a waiting notice cancels provider work","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L053.\n\n- `peritus-agent/src/developer/execution/provider_turn/progress.rs:10,36-58` publishes a waiting observation every **20 seconds** while the same provider future is pending; the interval is not a response deadline.\n- Any notice-observer error cancels the owned attempt and returns that error at lines 48-52. In the daemon, public activity observation persists the record (L023/L026), so a presentation/history storage failure can interrupt a provider even without any elapsed run limit.\n- Public streamed text disables these waiting notices, and reasoning summaries postpone them. Test-only one-second/25 ms outer deadlines at lines 109-113,127-130,161 test responsiveness and are not production provider timeouts.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFsaoPhkxlDn/B65hP4OafPzE2fRV72HJRsR9RZg0iTTDhkciy4aedqZMww9V/awIz4fkbZFfJZ7iwnm+WYPHAE="}
