{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2201,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.090544830Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"ed93b8f1-be6f-587e-bb61-5e438bd3a9ba","title":"[L061] Working-memory lineage has hard observation and entry-count ceilings","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L061.\n\n- `peritus-context/src/working/limits.rs:31-40,64-72` sets and hard-caps **65,535 exact observation locators per lineage**, **512 retained working entries**, **2,048 bytes per entry**, **32 items per source/dependency/file-validity list**, and **32 operations per atomic delta**. Construction permits only positive narrower limits.\n- Getter contracts explicitly include stale/superseded entries in the retained-entry count (lines 75-99). A persistent memory lineage can therefore exhaust representational policy without a wall-clock timeout. Actual insertion/compaction/retirement behavior and user recovery remain pending complete reducer/host reads.\n- `context_config.rs:140-142` uses this same hard envelope by default. These are fixed allocation policies, not a provider's actual context-window size. Preferred rendering token budgets (L058) are a separate layer.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPGckZYq4T9c1wkAiFkC6NlNSIeXa6jnC2sd3ARQF7/yClTsk7ZiwQgatSVjPfqGGVSGe+to/Tp2pq4GXSkbBAQ="}
