{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2203,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.095039252Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"b7e7ee71-9505-5a16-89fc-7b7d0804a7d8","title":"[L062] Generic artifact quota admission and storage-location fences","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L062.\n\n- `peritus-artifact-store/src/config.rs:28-43` requires a nonempty root, positive artifact/quota values, artifact size at most total quota, and quota at most **i64::MAX** for SQLite durable accounting. It imposes no fixed 1 GiB generic ceiling; that value is selected by the local-context caller (L057).\n- `local_context/storage/location.rs:12-31` requires absolute traversal-free storage outside editable workspace ancestry, except specifically protected private roots. This is a storage-ownership boundary, not session expiration.\n- Reference/garbage-collection and actual quota enforcement are pending; the public facade exposes them, so a declaration alone is insufficient to claim all archives can never be reclaimed.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQA+zk2eyz+yDNBKhRC2R2l5Wr8Rm+jJNqu2BrBKrV8AHrTTGXApIun+ly2pgOWuNCG69OAUYLLEyp1xNlrknkQc="}
