{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2211,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.111514851Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"e460d261-f5c9-517c-9848-1901712c063b","title":"[L066] Artifact catalog adds a separate five-second lock deadline","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L066.\n\n- `peritus-artifact-store/src/catalog.rs:38-45` independently sets SQLite's busy timeout to **5 seconds**. This is distinct from the 250 ms control/local-memory database deadlines (L019/L056), and is reached while finalizing archival writes or changing roots.\n- `catalog.rs:387-389` wraps SQLite failures as generic Initialize I/O errors; `error.rs:141-148` classifies its generic Other I/O as Retry; the typed SQLite busy category is not preserved. The code does not wait indefinitely for a catalog writer.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKEDJvjtqEPkfiUek0QirX+X6JTnRD+K5nojr3MYc5goN7CE+bHezJfDDX3V6VqcN+bGUyWZqdgK6E63+4BZUgU="}
