{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2219,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.128442429Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"fd789260-0ed5-5fa2-9a2f-3ae47469db86","title":"[L070] Artifact metadata has narrow textual capacities","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L070.\n\n- `metadata.rs:7-8,23-35,71-85` limits ASCII media type text to **255 bytes** and an encryption algorithm token to **64 bytes**. Invalid values produce CorrectRequest-class InvalidMetadata; these protocol metadata capacities are separate from session and file-body limits.\n- Reference admission also requires finalized, active, healthy content (`metadata.rs:242-248`); this is an integrity requirement, not a throughput quota.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEOmtc4itF3Do8V3tmObmbOMdmg6VfI4rDbDgDBiKCD16kGuG5Dn2o1y45bQxXFY2uqUp6WvpMQHZ9a7q4EJbQM="}
