{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2221,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.132709477Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"0628ffe4-dfdd-5fc1-bd97-40321eb807c8","title":"[L071] Working-memory admission counts history that its update API cannot retire","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L071.\n\n- `working/state.rs:259-295` enforces the observation cap before appending the next source; at standard limits this blocks the **65,536th observation**. Each successful append clones the retained state. Refresh retains the observation prefix (`306-367`).\n- `delta.rs:14-20,109-116,142-169` exposes ordered upserts, with **32 proposals per delta** at standard limits. `delta_reducer.rs:22-36,63-75` replaces existing identities or adds new ones up to **512 total retained entries**; supersession changes status without removing its predecessor. Superseded identities cannot be reused and stale entries need newer sources (`96-110`). There is no deletion/retirement operation in this reducer API.\n- The same entry limit separately caps observed environment files (`state.rs:127,350`, `validity.rs:78-94`), active literal requirements and unresolved operations (`protocol.rs:75-101,201-224`). It is not a shared sum, but a reused maximum for each list. Per-entry file/link lists remain capped at **32**.\n- These are source-verified finite-lifetime admission rules, distinct from exact binding/source-integrity checks. Application recovery/rotation behavior remains pending; no live exhaustion reproduction is claimed.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAA