{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2222,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.134917792Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"0628ffe4-dfdd-5fc1-bd97-40321eb807c8","comment_uuid":"d089c9e7-2e0b-48c9-bc52-9fc56c1c1407","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L071: Working-memory admission counts history that its update API cannot retire.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: working/state.rs:259-295; delta.rs:14-20,109-116,142-169; delta_reducer.rs:22-36,63-75; state.rs:127,350; validity.rs:78-94; protocol.rs:75-101,201-224. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nAdd explicit retirement of superseded/stale working entries from the active projection while preserving immutable historical receipts and dependency roots. Segment observation history and separate protocol/environment indexes from the entry-selection budget. Admission must depend on the final usable prompt frontier, not all entries ever seen; all source bindings remain exact across reopen.\n\nPreserve: governing inputs, complete pending tool protocol pairs, exact source/lineage references, explicit permissions, unresolved effect truth and task-role/native-provider identity. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long productive read/write sessions through repeated compaction and segment boundaries, source/dependency changes, non-ASCII and large evidence, interrupted checkpoint publication, then reopen the same lineage and prove that valid grounding is reused and stale targets are reread. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPMfHhEurtxbtnmFGroQsnbae2SlEOdhg4XkjJt7K0ZRP7MTgErG+vJwiVvOUgV6ZYefbIKBHwj83aNnYB5VFAY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2223,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.137212553Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"b03518d5-ef43-508f-947a-504c2d528e66","title":"[L072] Required working-memory closure can block prompt assembly","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L072.\n\n- `working/selection.rs:45-85` creates a render graph with **32,768 bytes per node** and at most five visible roles, then limits preferred selection to actual available input headroom. Token and byte estimates use roughly **three bytes per token** (`67,91`). Exact underlying context-limit admission and token-budget constructors remain pending.\n- Contradictions, unresolved failed approaches, and unfinished plans become required roots (`94-103`). Their dependency closure may increase the preferred allocation, but exceeding available headroom returns generic WorkingError::Capacity (`73-80`); optional omitted entries remain available in stored memory.\n- A finite model context window is a provider capacity. The chosen required-root policy and generic failure behavior are separate potential daily-driving blockers; their host fallback/recovery is being traced.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGkfvFVkGARE/nhQxqQj/wfar3J+kzrpRlUVUeCeZh3ogNAnMRbJoLV+MHj5D6q9U+RJeN3yk3zGXXxdF4yhHwg="}
