{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2229,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.150473867Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"33880668-0112-50fb-bd0a-c1d770ede69a","title":"[L075] Prompt reconstruction has hard failure paths and narrow evidence heuristics","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L075.\n\n- `local_context/assembly.rs:24-43,63-106` aborts when pinned instructions/pending operations consume provider input capacity or required working closure cannot fit. `assembly/working.rs:42-49` maps all renderer failures to a generic capacity message; this path contains no automatic memory retirement or recovery fallback.\n- The **85%** compaction trigger and configured recent-message window affect optional exchanges (`assembly.rs:138-169`). Complete groups are preserved when they fit the actual model; omitted groups remain archived. If even the required omission notice cannot fit, assembly fails (`170-190`). Model input capacity is distinct from the chosen prompt policy.\n- `assembly/exchanges.rs:18-63` exposes at most **8 tool-result handles** in the omission notice. `assembly/evidence.rs:81-122` supplements working links with only the latest **8 prior tool outputs**, **8 errors**, and **8 prior assistant outputs**.\n- Optional evidence previews stop below **256 remaining bytes**, reserve **192 bytes** for framing, and halve content until it fits (`evidence.rs:18-76`). The byte allowance is `min(retrieved_tokens * 3, max_read_bytes)`; full artifacts remain retrievable but are read completely before preview truncation. These are information-selection limits and repeat-read risks, not proven attribution to the live loop.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvs