{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2233,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.159052888Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"bb178142-4a44-5695-ad45-8e29b5540fff","title":"[L077] Derived failure records, pending handles, and view-binding capacities","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L077.\n\n- `memory/ingestion/facts.rs:36-115` automatically creates or updates a FailedApproach keyed by tool name and arguments digest. Distinct tool failures consume the retained **512-entry** capacity (L071); unresolved entries become required prompt roots (L072). A state-event rejection propagates before advancing the facts frontier. The model need not call context_update to encounter this capacity.\n- `memory/ingestion/pending.rs:94-114` rejects command handles above **256 bytes**. Running/unknown handles stay pinned; only an explicit completed disposition removes the matching handle. Protocol/source integrity and recovery-owned effect behavior are separate from this text cap.\n- `view_binding.rs:16-26` has its own **128 MiB frame/payload**, **1,100,000 collection items**, **32 MiB string/opaque**, and depth **16** canonical envelope for tool policy and exact-view binding. Existing narrower payload/field limits can bind first. Version/binding mismatch blocks checkpoint verification (`80-108`); it is an integrity barrier, not session expiration.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKQOOrEjw4/b/pZCPGaLKL8G42h6LP8YIj/m7YsZHE6C9ULseI3qL+PfcsGh2JoiGQzQx2ltE/jpLFIQE8JDTwA="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2234,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.161269911Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"bb178142-4a44-5695-ad45-8e29b5540fff","comment_uuid":"0500562b-df7f-4786-bd8f-be5f7fa4f644","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L077: Derived failure records, pending handles, and view-binding capacities.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: memory/ingestion/facts.rs:36-115; memory/ingestion/pending.rs:94-114; view_binding.rs:16-26. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nStore failure facts as deduplicated durable obligations with explicit resolution/supersession, and select their active summaries for the prompt. Keep complete pending-effect identities in typed references rather than bounded display handles. Bind views to paged policy/evidence roots, sharing encoder/recovery contracts so automatically derived facts cannot exhaust the lineage.\n\nPreserve: governing inputs, complete pending tool protocol pairs, exact source/lineage references, explicit permissions, unresolved effect truth and task-role/native-provider identity. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long productive read/write sessions through repeated compaction and segment boundaries, source/dependency changes, non-ASCII and large evidence, interrupted checkpoint publication, then reopen the same lineage and prove that valid grounding is reused and stale targets are reread. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQD3QOXTLtlrJFjARldJRD20XgRC0HUNMVcoMU4TsTVsttlnqAObP+/lACVy6rq/wyHgKHaur8tUnAd9ny0s5xQs="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2235,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.163787760Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"0d0d00d5-22ef-5644-9b7b-8c309ea54f01","title":"[L078] Memory retrieval has small pages, scan caps, and conservative byte packing","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L078.\n\n- `tools/read.rs:19-43,265-285` limits a raw request to **8 KiB**, explicit handles to **32**, query text to **256 bytes**, cursors to **100 bytes**, and response requests to **256..configured max_read_bytes** (default 16 KiB, configurable up to 64 KiB). Source handle numbers are limited to 20 digits (`tools.rs:133-148`), a u64 representation constraint.\n- Search scans at most **32 sources** per page (`read.rs:87-91`) and stops before exceeding **64 MiB scanned bytes** after its first artifact (`111-121`); it materializes complete artifacts. Only the first literal occurrence in each artifact determines the preview (`122-124`). Pagination/explicit offsets allow further reads but do not enumerate all matching occurrences.\n- Packing reserves worst-case escaped expansion at **six output bytes per source byte**, plus metadata/cursor overhead (`167-185`). A nominal 16 KiB page therefore returns substantially less source text. If even metadata or the next full entry cannot fit, it returns a rejection requiring a larger page (`128-141,240-244`). These policies can amplify repeated reads; exact archived evidence remains retained.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQC9arhu4QMiCNzU9xG8ABA4TdsG8jaB4C81tvS2yKh2WgakKUtjjmUiICeFOHYt7oRPCbADvj9xzMBSh3cEMwQo="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2236,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.165790499Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"0d0d00d5-22ef-5644-9b7b-8c309ea54f01","comment_uuid":"49d108f7-4a82-4e44-b1c4-41953008af43","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L078: Memory retrieval has small pages, scan caps, and conservative byte packing.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: tools/read.rs:19-43,265-285; tools.rs:133-148; read.rs:87-91. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nProvide lossless cursor-based retrieval of all occurrences and byte ranges, using streamed artifact access and actual encoded page sizes. A too-large next entry must yield a smaller fragment with continuation rather than make pagination impossible. Stable source/offset identities and exact displayed coverage should let the model retrieve evidence without repeated full-artifact scans.\n\nPreserve: governing inputs, complete pending tool protocol pairs, exact source/lineage references, explicit permissions, unresolved effect truth and task-role/native-provider identity. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long productive read/write sessions through repeated compaction and segment boundaries, source/dependency changes, non-ASCII and large evidence, interrupted checkpoint publication, then reopen the same lineage and prove that valid grounding is reused and stale targets are reread. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMuWST2PnPC9bZZ5TPrweckIelPW6diZVRXKLZCxJkD4gjbwFfCKz8JLb4z0QjJUOm4TUVZctlDxgbQ8y/ftQgQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2237,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.167880174Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"b095bfae-6642-5756-a757-db8c7778350a","title":"[L079] Memory updates have independent request/text/path admission gates","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L079.\n\n- `tools/update.rs:65-90,124-162,196-198,224-262` limits raw update JSON to **256 KiB**, proposals to **32 operations**, labels to **128 bytes**, entry text to **2,048 bytes**, each source/dependency/file list to **32**, paths to **4,096 bytes**, and the accumulated remembered-file list to **512**.\n- Public schema lengths use JSON string character counts (`tools/schema.rs:13-26,35-39`), while parser checks use bytes for labels, text, paths, and query. Non-ASCII input can pass the advertised length and still fail actual admission. This mismatch is source-verified; no new runtime test was run.\n- Context updates require current Read+Write permission (`tools.rs:62-89`), role-derived-memory eligibility, valid source/lineage, fresh revision, and a usable successor prompt. These authority/integrity checks are distinct from synthetic byte/count limits.\n- The credential-shape heuristic (`secret_text.rs:6-32`) rejects private-key markers and recognizable prefixes with **20 or more** trailing token-like bytes in derived entries. It protects derived-memory disclosure and can also reject quoted examples; it does not remove authorized source artifacts.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKn2M1MVhFz6Heq9Z7f8Ga6c+abkALaJN0kG/Last1vuuQL1Xdjx8HU3ZiznWC+/29R+9IOoCnYylLisobDdhg4="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2238,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.169968405Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"b095bfae-6642-5756-a757-db8c7778350a","comment_uuid":"09597491-7ca5-49a2-9a0f-9a4ef30dfd51","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L079: Memory updates have independent request/text/path admission gates.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: tools/update.rs:65-90,124-162,196-198,224-262; tools/schema.rs:13-26,35-39; tools.rs:62-89; secret_text.rs:6-32. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nShare one explicit UTF-8 byte contract between context-update schemas and parsers, and page large deltas/file-link sets under one revision-bound update intent. Archive large text and dependencies by exact reference while validating that the successor prompt remains usable before commit. Preserve permission/source lineage and scoped secret-disclosure controls with an explicit route for authorized quoted source evidence.\n\nPreserve: governing inputs, complete pending tool protocol pairs, exact source/lineage references, explicit permissions, unresolved effect truth and task-role/native-provider identity. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long productive read/write sessions through repeated compaction and segment boundaries, source/dependency changes, non-ASCII and large evidence, interrupted checkpoint publication, then reopen the same lineage and prove that valid grounding is reused and stale targets are reread. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJYr753pQwSdsMPTu4p66Oi8HGkv/uNEmqqE5EJv/K3jNMrQjFTF/p6yOuU8fazFsfx5ki9DDogGYcCnRAYvCAc="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2239,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.172119862Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"2126dc7d-342b-590c-a5a3-cc8de3ca2786","title":"[L080] Optional local inference still depends on durable-capacity admission","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L080.\n\n- `local_context/semantic.rs:13-60` skips the backend when disabled or role-excluded. A process error, missing/empty/oversized output, or rejected proposal records a failed attempt and continues with deterministic memory; this is distinct from stopping the main provider on a compactor deadline.\n- Its input includes all working entries and only the latest **8 tool observations**, with each initial excerpt capped at **one quarter** of selected input bytes and then repeatedly halved (`63-126`). If the base input alone is too large, no process runs.\n- Refresh, update execution, input/output artifact storage, and the failure receipt can themselves fail and propagate (`35-52`), including the fixed archive quota. Thus the optional inference fallback does not bypass failed mandatory storage admission. The selected sandbox/process deadline remains L059; runtime execution callers are pending.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQB3WRW4CjtClPSYgrijlEqgIntXzSVwmkQwZQxFsR0Pdt0PyS89Y5PQ1QhUliXAha0o3rzBM1buIu7yt2VPuggk="}
