nce and nonregression: long productive read/write sessions through repeated compaction and segment boundaries, source/dependency changes, non-ASCII and large evidence, interrupted checkpoint publication, then reopen the same lineage and prove that valid grounding is reused and stale targets are reread. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNCU4ENS5w7wnYn2stGMU7lN1WmQJ6ikYLB1U4G26ZPxT6xxG/RfRhG+743vAn9nezRTVAEVOvwmC6RKpFK+zAM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2241,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.176486792Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"cfa65dd8-ef70-55d3-9427-c9d0cb810749","title":"[L081] Exact context inspection has a 32-MiB output stop and growing validation cost","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L081.\n\n- `local_context/storage/inspection.rs:93-105` builds one response containing the complete source index, readable messages, and a **hex copy** of the canonical view, then rejects output above **32 MiB**. There is no pagination in this API; duplicated/hex-encoded bytes can hit this ceiling before the archived view's own body limit.\n- `checkpoint_validation.rs:98-116` resolves each source through `WorkingState::observation`, whose implementation linearly scans the retained prefix (`working/state_access.rs:43-50`). Exact full-index validation therefore performs quadratic source comparisons as the prefix grows. This is source-derived scaling behavior, not a benchmark or proven live hang.\n- Legacy checkpoint validation walks predecessors back to generation 1 (`checkpoint_validation.rs:15-43`), and missing or mismatched generations prevent recovery/inspection. These are lineage-integrity checks with no elapsed cutoff; retaining every historical dependency adds work rather than an expiration timer.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHnYucCIqP+gkoFHyfxnQR2OjSpCKP0MAz+kSgzbP3YXALIpq+CpDOVWGkayAJv7Ud4fB+9i8Tlbg4lPWAUNkQw="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2242,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.178714597Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"cfa65dd8-ef70-55d3-9427-c9d0cb810749","comment_uuid":"6b40358c-a163-4714-8527-e137ecd80b7c","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L081: Exact context inspection has a 32-MiB output stop and growing validation cost.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: local_context/storage/inspection.rs:93-105; checkpoint_validation.rs:98-116; working/state_access.rs:43-50; checkpoint_validation.rs:15-43. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nExpose context inspection as paged exact records and an independently downloadable canonical view artifact instead of a complete hex-duplicated response. Index source identity lookup and verify checkpoint lineage incrementally from trusted roots. Preserve complete predecessor/binding validation through resumable traversal rather than quadratic full-index scans on each query.\n\nPreserve: governing inputs, complete pending tool protocol pairs, exact source/lineage references, explicit permissions, unresolved effect truth and task-role/native-provider identity. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long productive read/write sessions through repeated compaction and segment boundaries, source/dependency changes, non-ASCII and large evidence, interrupted checkpoint publication, then reopen the same lineage and prove that valid grounding is reused and stale targets are reread. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQK0G+c6Z1lrqUBfKfcvOMkl8ZlKdlA7zL5PCbKzooMedqMpDo2I1P8w5EVCuuXeU80jz5DLoMQDKLgIUMe77twg="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2243,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.180700696Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"45816f0f-8aed-58eb-85e9-79b5d41baa18","title":"[L082] Command router eventually exhausts its retained replay ledger","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L082.\n\n- `command_runtime/construction.rs:79-99` selects a separate **1 GiB command artifact quota**, **8 MiB maximum artifact**, **64 active invocations**, and **4,096 replay entries**.\n- `peritus-tool-router/src/router.rs:121-129` rejects active-table exhaustion before effect dispatch. `replay.rs:76-95` rejects new identities at the replay maximum; terminal and indeterminate results retain their entry (`98-121`) and this ledger exposes no retirement/deletion path.\n- A long-lived command runtime can therefore refuse its **4,097th distinct reserved invocation** even if all earlier commands completed and none remains active. Per-command ordinal allocation happens before that admission; this is source-derived, not a live 4,097-command reproduction.\n- Restart creates a fresh router and loads separate projections; that is not transparent lifelong replay retention. Projection loss/eviction is L086. Exact one-use/replay integrity must remain enforceable independently of the fixed in-memory count.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLGuWsn4i9iz5Lnw/a1riKfvQyWT1y2mm+96KNozT11PkU0f7uBKjxdSN3aAhGPpgRD7nmvfpu5GU+lPaxEC2wI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2244,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.182918314Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"45816f0f-8aed-58eb-85e9-79b5d41baa18","comment_uuid":"9bc1609b-d651-49bc-b919-fd9847ba577e","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L082: Command router eventually exhausts its retained replay ledger.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: command_runtime/construction.rs:79-99; peritus-tool-router/src/router.rs:121-129; replay.rs:76-95. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nSeparate bounded active invocations from a durable indexed ledger of immutable historical command receipts. Retire terminal entries from the active table only after their outcome and one-use tombstone are durably addressable. Router reconstruction must reconnect those receipts and pending owners rather than reset replay protection or impose a 4096-command task lifetime.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNGQURLQayIG1uMudQSHn+2m7/arFoiA9XzpmngRW3I3MUdHX0+dU35MOpuhMbsa77todFZOXyVR6FxRLDqJiQI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2245,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.184981978Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"07ed22ce-1c09-581d-b7be-1a32f7f2e296","title":"[L083] Command caller applies fixed resource, output, and shutdown policies","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L083.\n\n- `command_runtime/plan.rs:26-31,109-136` selects **8 MiB output/artifact allowance**, **16 KiB model output fields**, **64 KiB stdin chunks**, **16 MiB cumulative stdin**, **12 GiB memory**, **50 GiB disk**, **4,096 processes**, and **8,192 file descriptors**. Process CPU time is selected wall time multiplied by **64**, and absent when wall time is absent. Actual enforcement and parameter-field definitions are being read.\n- Output overflow requests ContinueIncomplete rather than automatic termination (`115-124`). This means missing output evidence remains possible even if the command continues; the supervisor continues reading but retains only bytes within the per-stream and shared spool allowances (`supervisor/io.rs:244-259`). Later bytes are counted as dropped and never enter the displayed window; no output-limit cancellation is requested under this caller policy (`205-220`).\n- `DeadlinePolicy::new` keeps ordinary wall time optional, but selects **500 ms graceful shutdown** and **5,000 ms reap** (`170-171`). These are cancellation/termination completion policies, not established deadlines on ordinary successful execution.\n- `peritus-tool-router/src/execution.rs:140-144` confirms the unselected wall deadline is ignored for elapsed-time checks. A changed authority epoch still cancels. The placeholder logical tick 21 in the compiled call is therefore not a one-millisecond timeout when no timeout was selected.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEJr220eF93mZkSMz3p+wx3gNf46r3ME2Qn9id1jTOFu9M6+RFUc/kksrh/boAdG+2GTDoMsDc5IkcI//gjuJg4="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2246,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.187225581Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"07ed22ce-1c09-581d-b7be-1a32f7f2e296","comment_uuid":"4a2e4f79-dfa3-4d3e-9dfe-5a74dfcbce8a","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L083: Command caller applies fixed resource, output, and shutdown policies.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: command_runtime/plan.rs:26-31,109-136; supervisor/io.rs:244-259; peritus-tool-router/src/execution.rs:140-144. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nMake command resources explicitly selected physical policies, with no synthetic total-work allowance by default. Stream exact output to durable segmented spools and expose a rolling live tail independently of archived retention. Grace and reap settings may control escalation/observation, but timeout must leave a durable unresolved ownership obligation until actual tree quiescence is proven.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQP6pV47TO5TyabcBVxnmFOjFMTAD//5WHcBXrMm7dB1UaPxioLC9H3USOJb5G/ai+UM6/V+4b1BU1xgoSHcHJgc="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2247,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.189323217Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"38ff6001-ab24-5fc4-800e-26f2c7311ddf","title":"[L084] Command authority still mints finite validity, lease, and budget envelopes","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L084.\n\n- `command_runtime/authority.rs:179-182` uses fixed logical capability validity **10..1,000,000** and a **three-use** limit. `lease.rs:24-60` acquires a workspace lease for **selected command milliseconds + 10,000**, then consumes it at fixed logical tick 20; an unbounded command receives a 10,000-ms lease envelope.\n- Effect budget amounts are `10,10,selected_wall+1,000,2,1` (`authority.rs:301-327`). Kernel child/root envelopes use `selected_wall+5,000` and twice that, with fixed other dimensions (`kernel.rs:191-215`). Names, settlement, and sustained enforcement in the lower budget/process APIs remain pending.\n- These declarations are recorded without claiming a ten-second kill or a 1,000,000-ms running-command cutoff. The active router read so far rechecks only selected call deadline/epoch, not capability validity or lease expiry. The launch gateway validates capability validity at the fixed request tick and lease expiry only on admission (`peritus-process/src/gateway.rs:191-196,314-321`). Its budget predicate checks reserved `ActiveEffectMilliseconds` against the selected wall duration, or zero when absent (`262-263`). The complete supervisor owner loop has no capability-validity or lease-expiry timer: it checks selected wall/resource limits, control requests, backend observations, and exit (`supervisor/owner.rs:172-220,262-297`). These finite launch envelopes therefore do not establish an elapsed lease kill in this path. External lease fencing and budget settlement callers remain under review.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOmRjouzJ/D7ClMo3qAOvyS1oAxzs7dwQrt7zAKo77OLDlTro4vN2UP8t64fqvRP6famSJDW8hA7zJX6gLtPwwg="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2248,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.191808566Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"38ff6001-ab24-5fc4-800e-26f2c7311ddf","comment_uuid":"147f4f42-13c3-45ec-b8fe-d3027b487e34","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L084: Command authority still mints finite validity, lease, and budget envelopes.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: command_runtime/authority.rs:179-182; lease.rs:24-60; authority.rs:301-327; kernel.rs:191-215; peritus-process/src/gateway.rs:191-196,314-321; supervisor/owner.rs:172-220,262-297. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nRepresent command authority as a durable scoped grant plus renewable fenced ownership, separate from an optional user-selected execution deadline. Bind effect reservations to actual resource dimensions and settle them from truthful process facts. Preserve admission-time validity, use-count/replay checks and epoch revocation; do not reinterpret launch-clock placeholders as runtime duration or remove authorization fencing.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBLMlismmjSlMKEaLS5bNGgD5yOUMgGGB1anNWOvk/BUpTSZJOafl55VG7OWnx9hyAU14i9hdDb1zSPgIEtV4wc="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2249,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.193982283Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"8eeca47d-b1a5-5cf1-a128-128d743c7ff6","title":"[L085] Command ordinal allocation adds another five-second artificial deadline","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L085.\n\n- `command_runtime/ordinal.rs:17-37` opens the durable allocator and sets SQLite busy timeout to **5 seconds**. The comment explicitly says it replaced the prior **250 ms** allowance; it widened the deadline rather than removing it.\n- Allocation errors abort before command authority/process creation. The test only exercises contention held for **500 ms** (`138-172`), not longer-than-five-second contention or indefinite recoverable waiting.\n- Ordinals additionally cannot exceed SQLite's **i64 maximum** (`55-70`), a representation limit. Collisions with legacy identities are skipped without a fixed retry count.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDhIzT4x6vwV+qcw1A28z1ePUsdLNtlKRDp5OX6fIPhZ7PUdABxo5tyWdXVMf3d4umMpWA7sEmb12FrHa7xO5gw="}
