nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFmB3vXODGwogHbrDB2f58X3dHy5H7Kb99gqWFM6daBAYC01wSEqf7sxJK/93iupwEqNgWLvaS/TaMYRraZTTAM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2251,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.198226480Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"8243cc28-f48e-571a-9e2b-5a7affe6b252","title":"[L086] Reconnect command projections are evicted and active control cannot survive restart","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L086.\n\n- `command_runtime/projections.rs:15-16,68-86` keeps at most **4,096 projections / 64 MiB**, evicting oldest entries to fit. Every update reads and rewrites the full JSON file. Handles over **128 bytes** are ignored at load (`51-54`).\n- Oversized, malformed, unsupported-version, or excessive-entry files are quarantined and load an **empty reconnect map** (`32-49`); this removes the projection surface even though authoritative process/tool records remain elsewhere.\n- A previously running projection becomes indeterminate after daemon restart with explicit “live control cannot be resumed” behavior (`55-60`). This is a process-control persistence limitation distinct from retaining the provider's native context window.\n- Projection write failures are diagnostic-only after dispatch (`command_runtime/mod.rs:359-366`), which preserves current caller results but can leave reconnect state stale. Lower authoritative recovery paths and UI affordances are still being audited.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEoDOFN/tu+61DOfr1meulCj/6ooGvJoKdgbQwtmM5/jVxuNmqSpugYNBx5ur5phCmyLrjtOVHWBTgphQyWttAI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2252,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.200632239Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"8243cc28-f48e-571a-9e2b-5a7affe6b252","comment_uuid":"45168d20-c656-4629-8c47-056c3119c896","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L086: Reconnect command projections are evicted and active control cannot survive restart.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: command_runtime/projections.rs:15-16,68-86; command_runtime/mod.rs:359-366. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nRebuild reconnect projections from authoritative indexed command/process receipts, with paged storage and stable handles. A malformed derived projection must be repairable without emptying the logical history. Persist process control ownership in a supervisor that survives client/daemon attachment loss, or provide exact fenced adoption of the same live process tree; projection eviction is never permission to redispatch.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNDozDgKxvhAt52AncD8dxNxkOzjNxrGuXgGd0OQArx0ydjqCRwwhJtd4E3POOVv30S4sNuC/kg+cyQ2+lgF4gE="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2253,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.202767506Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"b9bb5fe5-203f-517f-925f-fcd033bf253c","title":"[L087] Process policy constructors require bounded I/O and impose hard maxima","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L087.\n\n- `peritus-process/src/io_policy.rs:5-8,133-141,175-211` imposes **16 MiB cumulative stdin**, **16 GiB output fields**, and **16,777,216 output events** as implementation maxima. Stdin has no unbounded policy; zero or inverted bounds fail construction. Output requires positive chunk/window/spool/event values and a chunk no larger than its window/spool.\n- `resource.rs:52-82` requires positive memory, disk, output, process, descriptor, and concurrency ceilings. CPU and wall time can be absent. The fixed caller values in L083 are choices below these constructor maxima; actual operating-system and sampled enforcement is being traced.\n- Graceful termination and post-force reap durations must be positive and at most **30 days** (`io_policy.rs:292-300`). The optional ordinary wall limit has no corresponding 30-day constructor ceiling. The L083 5,000-ms field is a reap limit, corrected after reading its definition.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHE+8q3FUDta/GHPMqc9Rl1jg/9fjafjlZwTp1N8eIlkcwHx/F5SVlc26ToL49yVFV7U7diX7KdNU265yWPIvQQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2254,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.204855258Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"b9bb5fe5-203f-517f-925f-fcd033bf253c","comment_uuid":"bc9da1bd-0bcd-4782-afb8-fe0be152aeca","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L087: Process policy constructors require bounded I/O and impose hard maxima.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: peritus-process/src/io_policy.rs:5-8,133-141,175-211; resource.rs:52-82; io_policy.rs:292-300. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nSeparate bounded I/O chunks and in-flight windows from cumulative stdin/output/event lifetime. Stream acknowledged input and exact output through durable segments, using explicit adjustable resource policy tied to backend enforcement. Cleanup grace/reap is a cancellation protocol with retained unresolved ownership, not a mandatory execution cutoff or a fabricated terminal result.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLlHDiCqI+s46nCF98G6pVzb5+gAHwbAL5tEtXyfxYc5/z4BOvBtDooe9cyaZlfr1x1L34N7cPnBSWcgDPuQ4w8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2255,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.207448665Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"94cc7111-187d-5de5-8e85-94727655bff3","title":"[L088] Durable process registry can block launch at 16,384 unsettled records","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L088.\n\n- `peritus-process/src/consumption.rs:34-35,132-141,180-198` retains at most **16,384 execution records**, trying to retire to **15,360** on startup or capacity pressure. If enough records cannot retire, opening the store or consuming a new execution identity fails with recovery-required state.\n- Retirement requires both `ownership_settled` and an exactly matching claim/manifest (`consumption/retention.rs:27-33`), sorted by age. Completed phase alone does not qualify. Retirement deletes the claim, spool, and manifest (`registry_storage.rs:203-223`); no tombstone is written by that helper. Unlike L082, this registry does have an automatic retirement path, but it removes this layer's old identity/result record. Higher-level ordinal/replay safeguards must be assessed independently.\n- Consumption is persisted before process creation. A subsequent spawn failure cannot simply reuse the already-consumed identity. Quiescence scans all retained manifests and refuses unresolved ownership or live phases (`quiescence.rs:114-142`); these are ownership-integrity barriers rather than ordinary wall deadlines.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKLYEOmG6C0hQ9hQBmHARTMlx2KGmOI0YtsQTT