{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2256,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.209597105Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"94cc7111-187d-5de5-8e85-94727655bff3","comment_uuid":"ea314648-dbad-43ea-90f1-e074411fb254","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L088: Durable process registry can block launch at 16,384 unsettled records.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: peritus-process/src/consumption.rs:34-35,132-141,180-198; consumption/retention.rs:27-33; registry_storage.rs:203-223; quiescence.rs:114-142. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nMaintain a paged durable process registry with a bounded active ownership index. Retire only fully settled and published results into immutable tombstones; unsettled identities remain visible and individually reconcilable without preventing unrelated launches. Record Prepared/Consumed/Spawned acceptance phases so definite spawn failure can settle safely without reusing an accepted dispatch.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAdAGrvW7PNdfUTvyP53/ToUXsW5KHj4HlIKiYtp2Wit5EHScNAel0Oz/dtfXdYqlR61oF8zSeCOr+jmwm2Zswg="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2257,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.211710123Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"f397a87b-9789-5b27-b8dd-39e375ec2c1a","title":"[L089] Resource sampling can stop execution on observation failure and repeatedly walk the workspace","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L089.\n\n- `supervisor/resource.rs:72-89,109-126,205-214` baselines the entire working directory and resamples disk growth each **1 second**, plus process resources each **20 ms**. These intervals are sampling cadence, not elapsed execution deadlines. Exceeding CPU, memory, disk growth, process count, or descriptors requests resource-limit cancellation (`owner.rs:164-188,244-259`), even when ordinary wall time is absent.\n- `supervisor/resource/disk.rs:13-56` recursively enumerates all regular files without the tooling layer's build/cache exclusions. Deleted descendants are tolerated, but unreadable directories, entries, or metadata cause an error. Owner-loop sampling errors become supervisor failure and cleanup (`owner.rs:133-146`), so inability to measure a descendant can terminate otherwise working execution.\n- Repeated full-tree scans can delay output/control observation in a large workspace. This is source-derived synchronous work, not a benchmark or diagnosis of the reported live lockup. Symlinks are skipped; growth uses logical file sizes above the baseline, not physical filesystem capacity.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKEAtfUi9LadZJwrYEAsIFIHJ3WjobQ4VXU9xHFCfa8T18td25yHa6KEICi9OrZrxv07c7+3YCR/CJB8wHhUdgc="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2258,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.213801912Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"f397a87b-9789-5b27-b8dd-39e375ec2c1a","comment_uuid":"318126f2-516f-44cc-b5c6-7c579fc938ee","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L089: Resource sampling can stop execution on observation failure and repeatedly walk the workspace.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: supervisor/resource.rs:72-89,109-126,205-214; owner.rs:164-188,244-259; supervisor/resource/disk.rs:13-56; owner.rs:133-146. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nMove resource observation off the serialized process-control loop and replace repeated full-tree disk scans with indexed/incremental accounting plus resumable verification. Report unavailable measurement as typed evidence, not automatic process failure. Enforce only actually selected resources with an explicit unknown-enforcement recovery policy, preserving controls and output while measurement is repaired.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNbPDE4j6dE9rovdN2iJqq1NRXWpWQ56pAXGmG9tsN5Gub2ApGw+FvGOx7PLZEK/5D+7T/Ka3oXV6B8xDVCtVwU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2259,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.215834636Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"8fa987d2-fa99-5d19-a602-9d9620ea5045","title":"[L090] Output retention is a finite prefix, and its displayed tail freezes after quota exhaustion","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L090.\n\n- `supervisor/io.rs:244-259` limits accepted output by both each stream's remaining bytes and the **shared aggregate spool allowance**. `output.rs:96-107` counts the remainder as dropped; only accepted bytes enter spools, events, and the retained window.\n- For L083's ContinueIncomplete policy, the command keeps running after its **8 MiB shared output prefix** is full. Its **512 KiB displayed window** is a tail of that accepted prefix, not a continually updated tail of all observed output (`output/window.rs:27-48`). Late build/test errors can therefore disappear from both retained artifacts and the current view.\n- The **16,384-event caller window** evicts oldest events (`events.rs:155-160`). Resource sample events share this window with output/lifecycle events. Eviction itself does not stop execution, and a caller-selected event-wait duration only ends an observation wait (`control.rs:155-171`). Event sequence/counters saturate at u64 representation limits.\n- Spool publication retains terminal accounting on failure and supports explicit retry (`supervisor/artifact.rs:17-52`), but collapses underlying archive/quota errors into generic publication errors (`80-96`). Its 16-KiB copy/hash buffers are streaming buffers, not total-byte limits.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQF37HZZzFMx3PYOc70IvYhsdhvJ+5K4i/WVkElIh7NEfnp6LkbH/ES7COhcSg8ZvTsQuQYwRRLuiAmDgeQbvcAo="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2260,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.217876223Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"8fa987d2-fa99-5d19-a602-9d9620ea5045","comment_uuid":"1b632ca1-96b7-4281-b2ae-6d16f2168bfa","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L090: Output retention is a finite prefix, and its displayed tail freezes after quota exhaustion.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: supervisor/io.rs:244-259; output.rs:96-107; output/window.rs:27-48; events.rs:155-160; control.rs:155-171; supervisor/artifact.rs:17-52. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nDecouple the live rolling output tail from the archived output allowance. Keep accepting observed bytes into a bounded rolling window even when archival pressure requires a recoverable spool wait or explicit retention policy. Store exact stream offsets, loss markers and terminal accounting; late errors must remain visible and artifact publication must be retryable with its original cause.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQK1dHAId9aD/KMbNsyoGCjtJdptWH0YjjWOcB3ZcNfXs7CX7+Rs0LrzrHvawbljFf+180EgMdheawpVnRonfRQ8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2261,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.219983816Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"327a2b4b-41b7-54ab-94ad-011e5d88925e","title":"[L091] Root exit and owner loss end child-process ownership; cleanup uses finite reap deadlines","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L091.\n\n- `supervisor/owner.rs:204-217` immediately calls tree cleanup when the root exits. `supervisor/ownership.rs:23-43` force-kills any remaining owned tree before waiting up to the selected reap duration. This can end intentionally surviving children even after a successful root exit.\n- Owner-loop normal wall enforcement uses only optional deadline/resource wall fields (`owner.rs:262-287`). Cancellation escalates after the selected **500 ms grace**. A running process with both wall fields absent has no ordinary elapsed cutoff in this loop.\n- Cleanup has separate **5,000-ms caller reap windows** for root observation, tree quiescence, and output EOF (`owner/finalize.rs:69-138`). Failure yields SupervisorFailed/unsettled ownership; readers without EOF are detached rather than joined. These windows do not guarantee all cleanup completes within one five-second total.\n- Dropping the owning process handle requests SupervisorShutdown and joins its owner thread (`supervisor.rs:96-103`); dropping an incomplete spawned owner force-kills the tree (`owner.rs:318-326`). Observation handles alone cannot preserve ownership across daemon loss. Crash-watchdog/recovery behavior remains under review.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJfMEoJTE9Wi2nr5K82KNUBq7o741RvM++Czp3+dNJrV+WGTFUZulNB2OXPCnCecpaw5gO5jmyZZ/rcBOhzc5gQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2262,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.221965275Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"327a2b4b-41b7-54ab-94ad-011e5d88925e","comment_uuid":"8895b0e5-76bd-4f7a-aef9-8d6da79eab09","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L091: Root exit and owner loss end child-process ownership; cleanup uses finite reap deadlines.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: supervisor/owner.rs:204-217; supervisor/ownership.rs:23-43; owner.rs:262-287; owner/finalize.rs:69-138; supervisor.rs:96-103; owner.rs:318-326. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nMake root exit, descendant lifetime, supervisor ownership and cleanup obligations separate durable states. Explicitly transfer intentionally surviving descendants into an authorized persistent owner; cancellation escalation may force-stop exact owned trees, but a reap observation timeout cannot declare them settled. Dropping a client attachment must not implicitly own task cancellation.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKgXuwBGmxtvWN1bFxfuAS+xAmXgB42Az+bF/OBylMYmKAq+dNmrqItbIXSDjENh70wtsFuaIQSRcQ3h7u0PQgY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2263,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.224578977Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"97a70cb8-6c45-5023-abb2-a40faad23449","title":"[L092] Bounded control admission and synchronous stdin can obstruct cancellation and observation","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L092.\n\n- The supervisor control queue holds **64 messages**. All controls, including cancellation, use nonblocking `try_send`; a full queue returns an input error with CorrectRequest recovery (`control.rs:221-235`). There is no separate cancellation reservation in this queue.\n- The **16 MiB cumulative stdin** ceiling is enforced inside the owner thread, after individual writes have been accepted into the control queue (`supervisor/io.rs:147-169`). Exceeding the cumulative limit errors the tick and enters supervisor-failure cleanup; it is not merely a rejected write returned synchronously to the sender.\n- `write_all` and `flush` run synchronously on the supervisor thread (`159`). A process that stops reading its input can block resource sampling, output draining, signals, and cancellation on that owner. Control/output drains also run until their queues are empty (`99-136,192-229`), with no fairness budget in these routines. Windows native terminal controls likewise lock a shared writer and synchronously write/flush resize or graceful-stop frames (`native/windows_channel.rs:93-101`), adding a helper-reader stall path. These are source-derived stall paths, not yet live reproductions.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDwU6fQIloukWE2cbN/W/TDRthRQFdYU/SpmOI870fw2ZhN55mHphz6i5ynzBOa8L5rIVzCa8+e4KeLvQPeFmwc="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2264,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.226761567Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"97a70cb8-6c45-5023-abb2-a40faad23449","comment_uuid":"331dcafe-2a09-4a31-83b6-f7fb482e9602","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L092: Bounded control admission and synchronous stdin can obstruct cancellation and observation.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: control.rs:221-235; supervisor/io.rs:147-169; native/windows_channel.rs:93-101. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nGive cancel/signal/observation an independent control lane and run stdin writes through nonblocking or separately owned cancellable I/O. Admit cumulative input against acknowledged physical chunks before accepting it, so rejected stdin cannot become a supervisor failure. Use fair drains across input, output and resource work while retaining exact ordering and cancellation intent.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCUTQmBn9U7sfBzaXVbv5dRcQamL0Gl7E0qCfWpmBtHhHvF86/Hl5TWzv7Cx/AW+nX8JIttd/02TNYA/uWfezgM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2265,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.229205294Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"e4471d65-5d3b-5625-aba0-cf436c2bef20","title":"[L093] Process retention removes settled results and one-use records under count pressure","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L093.\n\n- `registry_storage.rs:203-223` retires an execution by deleting its **consumption claim**, the entire **spool directory**, and its **manifest**. This helper writes no durable tombstone. Old terminal results/publication retry inputs can therefore disappear when L088's count-driven retirement runs; surviving archive objects are separate.\n- Eligibility is only Closed/Terminal plus tree quiescence and joined support tasks (`recovery/manifest.rs:133-137`), not artifact-publication completion. A record whose retained spool has not been archived can still qualify for count retirement. This is source-derived from the complete retention predicate. The existing retirement test (`consumption/tests.rs:199-233`) explicitly removes a settled terminal with retained output and no published artifact, then asserts its result and claim are gone; the test was read, not executed during this audit.\n- The process store's replay rejection uses the retained maps/exclusive claim file. Deleting both removes that layer's old identity guard; the product ordinal allocator and tool router provide separate protection that must not be conflated with a permanent process tombstone.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGCFr1a+iabMOpyI6nVbjEjqlFEGj40ScKtZ1gnYhW41Z82XkAzh+Ao15b4gSbVgIYXtiCtdDpgSjDBYIv0uXgg="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2266,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.231495472Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"e4471d65-5d3b-5625-aba0-cf436c2bef20","comment_uuid":"5088c995-1deb-4745-bfc9-475f568d2fe2","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L093: Process retention removes settled results and one-use records under count pressure.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: registry_storage.rs:203-223; recovery/manifest.rs:133-137; consumption/tests.rs:199-233. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nRetire process records only after exact output publication and ownership settlement, keeping a durable one-use tombstone and indexed terminal receipt. Spools still required for publication/retry remain recovery roots. Active-table capacity can be reclaimed independently of historical identity, so count pressure neither loses results nor permits redispatch.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQH3PpRDdSMrQObXJO8qQ+VXwh+HfjLMamn32jSMSeJelu4sU6f7sISl9IzuvpIxIEqEMepGMcFZSSG2sjESXRg0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2267,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.233698590Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"80f4e639-cd92-5b93-9642-991833b5a053","title":"[L094] Restart reconciliation terminates exact live trees instead of reconnecting control","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L094.\n\n- `recovery/reconcile.rs:124-168` probes every unresolved manifest. An exact live tree is **terminated**, then marked ownership-unsettled; it is not adopted into a new supervisor/control handle. Absent processes are reconciled without inventing successful completion. PID mismatch/unverifiable identity remains indeterminate, and orphan claims remain blockers.\n- Complete settled terminal records are preserved; rebuilding live command control across daemon restart is not supported by this reconciliation path. This substantiates L086's reconnect limitation while keeping native provider conversation retention a separate question.\n- `consumption/watchdog.rs:7-28` optionally configures a crash watchdog on Linux only. `platform/watchdog.rs:142-156` imposes an additional **1-second watchdog reap deadline**, then kills/waits for the watchdog and returns an ownership error. An unexpectedly exited armed watchdog fails process observation (`120-128`). `platform/inheritance.rs:12-32` separately installs Linux **SIGKILL on parent death**, used by pipe and native-PTY launch (`platform/pipe.rs:51-52`, `platform/pty.rs:124-125`). Product watchdog selection and the watchdog executable's owner-death action remain under review. Portable local PTY launch does not invoke that kernel parent-death helper in the inspected branch.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGbeHCF9kqZkvQ0tBbLCg9eaDlUF+0YLZzbA+TX6raAmgBBNxqPkDabKGdoYOY6s5sPYB8sw41XjmzpiLPrYHAQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2268,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.236202785Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"80f4e639-cd92-5b93-9642-991833b5a053","comment_uuid":"8d31a6a5-8dae-454c-a887-0a46a02c32ae","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L094: Restart reconciliation terminates exact live trees instead of reconnecting control.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: recovery/reconcile.rs:124-168; consumption/watchdog.rs:7-28; platform/watchdog.rs:142-156; platform/inheritance.rs:12-32; platform/pipe.rs:51-52; platform/pty.rs:124-125. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nMove running process ownership to a durable supervisor boundary independent of the daemon attachment, or implement fenced adoption using exact birth/containment identity and persisted control channels. Reconcile the same live tree after restart rather than killing it as the default recovery action. Keep explicit cancel cleanup and PID-reuse safeguards; migrate parent-death/watchdog semantics together with the new ownership contract.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQG8UYER1AkGuH9oDqmDKODvDAR3vZYZQJoR0R2SHR2RyUAY/j1wEUKarLsUKpDUklRO6drkeA420qx5oj1xdsgg="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2269,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.238326163Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"c5d860f6-2bd3-5cbb-8358-6a4a0c121e7a","title":"[L095] Process recovery records impose a 16-KiB canonical manifest bound","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L095.\n\n- `recovery/manifest/codec.rs:23,55-68` rejects encoded/decoded manifests above **16 KiB**, including embedded terminal payload, digests, lease identity, and checksum. Platform signal names are capped at **128 UTF-8 bytes** (`277-285,302`). All encoding-bound failures are classified as CorruptRecovery/Quarantine, even for a newly produced oversized record.\n- Registry loading reads the entire file with `fs::read` before this decoding bound is applied (`registry_storage.rs:43-45,76-78`), so the bound is a validity stop rather than a pre-read allocation bound. Invalid claims/manifests are quarantined; existing quarantine entries keep recovery's `all_terminal` false across reopen (`consumption/tests/recovery.rs:88-106`).\n- Checksum, identity, exact output accounting, and terminal-digest binding are integrity requirements. The hard aggregate manifest maximum is a separate implementation ceiling; the complete terminal codec also caps each collection at **64 items** and signal names at **128 bytes** (`terminal/canonical.rs:23-24,121-185,347-357`). Unique closed vocabularies independently restrict valid streams/artifacts to three and resource dimensions to eight, so the 64-item guard is not a reachable smaller daily-driving ceiling for those currently valid collections. Canonical round-trip/digest tests were read, not executed.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIYaffY+ezINyE6mapf+6XcbYHlXYB61ynnENLJeKnIf7HXRvvcAt9TMQJ/xwb1tTzDfyqmDDXRKC7o0gERDLAI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2270,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.240501713Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"c5d860f6-2bd3-5cbb-8358-6a4a0c121e7a","comment_uuid":"ef4dce0d-508d-416e-a5bd-a90296c5a998","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L095: Process recovery records impose a 16-KiB canonical manifest bound.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: recovery/manifest/codec.rs:23,55-68; registry_storage.rs:43-45,76-78; consumption/tests/recovery.rs:88-106; terminal/canonical.rs:23-24,121-185,347-357. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nStore process recovery metadata as a small versioned root with referenced paged terminal/output evidence. Validate final records before publication using the same restart contract, and bound reads before allocation. Newly valid large metadata is a representation/admission condition, not corruption; actual checksum or identity failure remains a scoped integrity repair obligation.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCcdNDnWaJMvAkpA5FvyabQQt4npzEmr8L6Fe4jn5F2+J9+6gxdR0pbe+gVJGpOy2Pi25cT7qO7OWUoWWfxscQw="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2271,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.243309871Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"915063ba-9169-57e6-a863-8281e16d9fd0","title":"[L096] Structured command/environment admission has fixed size and portability restrictions","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L096.\n\n- `command.rs:5-8,29-53` caps executable text at **4,096 bytes**, each argument at **64 KiB**, argument count at **4,096**, and complete argv at **2 MiB**. These are application constructor limits, separate from the operating system's actual argv/environment limits. Empty executable/NUL checks are format constraints.\n- `environment.rs:7-10,132-189` caps allowlisted/final variable count at **1,024**, names at **255 bytes**, each value at **64 KiB**, and aggregate environment at **2 MiB**. Names must follow a portable ASCII identifier grammar. Names are folded to uppercase for collisions on every platform, so differently cased Unix environment names cannot coexist through this representation.\n- Non-Unicode allowlisted ambient values reject the entire environment (`147-151`). A non-Unicode canonical working directory also rejects execution (`working_directory.rs:55-60`); these portability restrictions can block otherwise representable native Unix paths/environments.\n- Backend name/version tokens have a **128-byte ASCII-token** limit (`plan.rs:22,357-363`). `plan_canonical.rs:241-249` adds u32 representation limits for lengths but no independent total canonical-byte ceiling. Exact target/revision, selected backend enforcement, and policy projection checks are authority/integrity constraints rather than elapsed cutoffs.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFF5RpAn3yPJ7BTCD6AS0MX4/Jx6tenOKgCqQxYQNssQ8pgmYvR99pYka1r+P2UDJXAXrsA/HtQETPzOCWT2Wgo="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2272,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.245614248Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"915063ba-9169-57e6-a863-8281e16d9fd0","comment_uuid":"bd70efdc-6ebf-4923-ae36-0e662bbcd9f1","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L096: Structured command/environment admission has fixed size and portability restrictions.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: command.rs:5-8,29-53; environment.rs:7-10,132-189; working_directory.rs:55-60; plan.rs:22,357-363; plan_canonical.rs:241-249. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nRepresent native argv, environment and working-directory identity without lossy portable text conversion; use platform-specific collision rules and explicit structured exec versus script authority. Validate against actual backend/OS argument capacity, with response files or referenced scripts when supported. Share canonical identity and launch admission so valid Unix names/case distinctions do not fail an unrelated portable schema.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHScItOEOM8qgOMVrTul9WbtjrfWbcipQFBgReUVMbMkLxgOrsZ1ZMhyrzc4qV9UQCv3iRPJEy61kG6d1zfbRgc="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2273,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.247747500Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"e41aee25-f211-5970-9fdb-f07c0613c23f","title":"[L097] Native helper admission is bounded, but synchronous startup can stall ownership","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L097.\n\n- `native.rs:41-42,104-117,143-156` caps helper identity at **256 ASCII bytes**, helper manifest at **4 MiB**, and protected-handle count at **256**. Staged protected payloads are capped at **1 MiB** and their ASCII labels at **256 bytes** (`native/protected_handle.rs:14-15,43-50,146-150`); pre-opened channel handles have no finite staged-payload cap. Duplicate handles/labels and mismatched digests are integrity failures; byte/count ceilings are independent implementation bounds.\n- Native startup synchronously reads exact ready/activation records, writes/flushes the manifest, and on Windows reads the target-started record (`platform.rs:117-148`, `platform/pipe.rs:89-128`, `platform/pty.rs:143-163`). There is **no elapsed timeout in these routines**. A helper that stays alive without completing the handshake can hold startup before the active `SpawnedOwner` control-draining loop exists.\n- Removing synthetic deadlines alone does not provide a cancellation path through blocking handshake I/O. This is an identified source stall path; backend/helper implementations and selected product launch behavior remain pending before attributing any live symptom to it.\n- A native backend preparation error records incomplete cleanup (`gateway/native.rs:47-54`), leaving durable ownership unresolved rather than assuming Rust Drop succeeded. That preserves honest recovery evidence but can contribute to L088's blocked admission until reconciled.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQL8CFMIL+Cb75emUBqvQF6PSLbwO5dfh1rVwVeet6DDwvnMQ3aPi3J3X1kn16V2FCwaCaqJKdlTVSJphMfcYdgA="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2274,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.250210392Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"e41aee25-f211-5970-9fdb-f07c0613c23f","comment_uuid":"9d44bcbd-9cdb-4d2f-a777-ee396ab64c6e","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L097: Native helper admission is bounded, but synchronous startup can stall ownership.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: native.rs:41-42,104-117,143-156; native/protected_handle.rs:14-15,43-50,146-150; platform.rs:117-148; platform/pipe.rs:89-128; platform/pty.rs:143-163; gateway/native.rs:47-54. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nModel helper startup as an owned cancellable handshake with explicit Prepared/Ready/Activated states and asynchronous framed I/O. Control and shutdown must operate before readiness; stream manifest/protected payload pages under exact digests. Preserve retained ownership on incomplete cleanup and reconcile it from actual helper/target facts rather than adding another startup timer.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:07.750Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKXMz+ZlXUOU6RCE5boQ0tw76PxuMmjc1b55J8pGO/dhM0FhSf6PTb4gpyuiMA62pPlaIyu3GyxELZ2UqNJK+AM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2275,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:19:08.252344830Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"fad0487d-6eed-5ee3-bbe5-a286b5a831b1","title":"[L098] Platform-specific process observation/PTY restrictions can reject otherwise selected work","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L098.\n\n- macOS group observation allocates a fixed **16,384-process** buffer and fails when the observed count is **at least** that capacity (`platform/resource/macos.rs:16-29,52-56`). This measurement ceiling is independent of the selected process ceiling; observation failure enters owner cleanup. Included tests explicitly require the full-buffer rejection and were read, not run.\n- Complete local resource sampling is declared available only on Linux (`platform/resource.rs:36-75`); local launch with a non-reference resource backend refuses unavailable enforcement (`supervisor/resource.rs:31-39`). Native backend-specific enforcement is separate and remains under review.\n- Local Windows PTY launch is explicitly unsupported for complete job containment (`platform/pty.rs:32-44`). A native Windows helper with channels uses the pipe adapter instead (`platform.rs:98-103`), so this is not a blanket Windows terminal prohibition.\n- Windows job cleanup uses a background wait and completion queue of **one**, with its elapsed reap bound supplied by the supervisor (`platform/pipe/windows_reap.rs:34-80`). That queue is a one-result handoff, not a one-command session limit.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAA