{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2312,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.630509341Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"c288e7c2-c8ae-567f-973e-bfef122425f1","comment_uuid":"07f54d90-651c-47d6-bfb6-465f521bc95e","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L116: Restart resets every post-writing phase to checks and cannot restore private gate state.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/execution/resume/durable.rs:183-185,324-331; resume/tests.rs:43-67; resume/knowledge.rs:58-88; knowledge.rs:225-226; peritus-run-knowledge/src/limits.rs:34-62. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nPersist phase-specific gate/review/finalization state with its exact candidate and execution-fact bindings. Restart should invalidate only evidence whose dependencies actually changed and reconstruct the remaining phase, rather than reset every later phase to Checking. Knowledge indexes must retain exact sources through paged roots and distinguish reusable content evidence from execution facts requiring reobservation.\n\nPreserve: exact candidate revision and artifact binding, complete finding/provenance conservation, independent reviewer evidence, truthful gate outcomes, protected user constraints and acceptance fail-closed on invalid evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQL3V1fGt4GCArQqvyuGMsO0UW9NyhSmAw2Xwg9vyMP27tNp1IjJQlprKkO2J4gOHjti1MC60uuLh+I6xM6j9SQw="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2313,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.632818789Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"bdf6e0d3-ae73-5cdd-abfa-a05dc70844db","title":"[L117] Settlement converts all budget-category errors into deadline reports","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L117.\n\n- `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/execution/settlement.rs:275-296` maps any `ProductRunnerErrorKind::Budget` to `SettlementCause::Deadline`, even when the explicit deadline-reached flag is false. `remaining_work` consequently says to continue with a fresh phase budget (`settlement.rs:327-329`). The complete accounting callers confirm non-expiry cases: provider usage/work-counter overflow also uses Budget (`budget.rs:62-96`), and unreadable workspace root or accounting arithmetic failure uses Budget (`resource_probe.rs:52-66,75-77,140-142`). Those failures can therefore report Deadline even with an untimed run. The true optional elapsed policy is separate (`accounting/limits.rs:19-24`, `budget.rs:158-163`).\n- Context failures are classified from three lowercase message substrings rather than a typed provider failure (`settlement.rs:299-304`). Other errors become Provider, Adapter, Repository or Recovery causes. This can obscure the original blocker category; it is not an elapsed limiter by itself.\n- Fatal InvalidPrecondition/InternalInvariant errors bypass retained candidate settlement both at initialization and final refresh (`settlement.rs:39-45,97-105,268-272`). Ordinary material-capture errors retain fallback diff/paths and downgrade completion, but fallible checkpoint, knowledge and finding serialization can still prevent constructing the handoff. Exact callers remain under examination.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOD3pJWMdyIDxb7niHfGH1gGMY+8BjnSgZjrJt+y6xWk+ngdnCu7Gk4Wg/NjnSYzlndoYoA4Yh4NkS1VFNHrsgI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2314,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.635226201Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"bdf6e0d3-ae73-5cdd-abfa-a05dc70844db","comment_uuid":"d47a44e9-6d48-42a0-bd98-0e4e9f27236d","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L117: Settlement converts all budget-category errors into deadline reports.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/execution/settlement.rs:275-296; settlement.rs:327-329; budget.rs:62-96; resource_probe.rs:52-66,75-77,140-142; accounting/limits.rs:19-24; budget.rs:158-163; settlement.rs:299-304; settlement.rs:39-45,97-105,268-272. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nIntroduce typed failure causes for selected deadline expiry, counter representation, resource observation, context capacity, provider acceptance and repository integrity. Preserve the original cause and recovery action through settlement; only actual elapsed expiry reports Deadline. Fatal admission errors still need durable retained work/effect reconciliation, without lexical substring classification.\n\nPreserve: canonical digest and schema identity, shared writer/reader admissibility, malformed-input rejection before allocation, exact causal ordering, actual provider/OS capability boundaries and preserved accepted historical evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQF/U/+1rlJzdSAcywM50SM+inOwSqmbIzqi9rzNm/rYlyGc6zUKzsqB276BDpMIHxtrLY4MIoqIqooZ1p3d35gI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2315,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.637842023Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"fa1da797-ba30-5a36-aed1-ee134e9d6d0d","title":"[L118] Whole conversation is capped at one MiB before a persistent run can execute","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L118.\n\n- `crates/orchestration/peritus-obligations/src/limits.rs:67-84` sets production public source to **1 MiB**, each clause to **64 KiB**, **4096 requirements**, **256 paths per requirement**, **1024 schema fields**, and **8192 evidence records**. `PublicTaskSource::from_parts` rejects empty or oversized source (`provenance.rs:31-54`); it has no paged/archive representation.\n- The product passes the **entire rendered conversation** into this source on execution preparation (`peritus-product-runner/src/execution/state.rs:41-42`, `execution/obligations.rs:50-70`). Once that transcript exceeds 1 MiB, a resumed pipeline fails `InvalidPrecondition` before design/writer execution. Initial-error settlement treats that category as fatal (L117). This is a source-confirmed total-history admission cap, independent of provider context compaction and selected elapsed budgets.\n- Source construction hashes the complete supplied bytes before checking size (`provenance.rs:211-217`). Requirement extraction enforces nonempty/at-most4096 drafts, clause size and path counts (`ledger/validation.rs:85-103,118-124`); Schema requirement and observation constructors enforce the selected schema-field maximum (`schema.rs:107-124,168-187`, `schema_validation.rs:71-86,137-150`); production therefore rejects more than 1,024 fields. Required field sets must also be nonempty, while observed sets may be empty; field-name byte limits are supplied separately to `SchemaField::new`. Qualification enforces the selected evidence-record maximum before ordering and known-identity checks (`qualification/validation.rs:91-160`), confirming the production 8,192 ceiling. However, valid evidence is strictly unique by requirement identity and must belong to the at-most-4,096-entry ledger, so that production evidence ceiling does not independently bind a valid input under these defaults. Conditions have strict ordering/uniqueness but no separate count ceiling here. Evidence-bound observed candidate paths independently use the selected 256-path maximum (`evidence/binding.rs:78-105`). Schema coverage is an actual linear two-cursor subset check (`schema_coverage.rs:236-302`), not a quadratic scan or work deadline. Product segmentation under the 1 MiB source cap normally creates at most 16 full-size clauses, so the 4096 draft ceiling is not its immediate limiting factor.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMHxXn/qAFg5gBuk3obRQ5kQA4brBXF3QmgzWPPQU7W8DEbs27Gfaa7DGiNvvbrSQhMFaWchaIP+rnl2lmHyKQU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2316,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.640549606Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"fa1da797-ba30-5a36-aed1-ee134e9d6d0d","comment_uuid":"ab7edf00-df55-4b66-8078-eb8179ea3872","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L118: Whole conversation is capped at one MiB before a persistent run can execute.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/orchestration/peritus-obligations/src/limits.rs:67-84; provenance.rs:31-54; peritus-product-runner/src/execution/state.rs:41-42; execution/obligations.rs:50-70; provenance.rs:211-217; ledger/validation.rs:85-103,118-124; schema.rs:107-124,168-187; schema_validation.rs:71-86,137-150; qualification/validation.rs:91-160; evidence/binding.rs:78-105; schema_coverage.rs:236-302. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nDerive obligations from a durable indexed conversation source with exact message/span identities, not one inline whole-transcript string. Page clauses and evidence under a stable task source root and retain complete governing input provenance. Model selection capacity separately from total conversation history, so a resumed long conversation can prepare its next phase without losing requirements.\n\nPreserve: committed command/event identity, exact causal and digest roots, exclusive ownership, atomic publication, reference-safe artifact retention and verified recovery from the last durable frontier. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIPj8amY9OPMwckKY5wsP//aigKalNmXgoVaeD+Qws2ukKBfizHSToYhpIcj3TsSMy/9koIdCAo6RvkNBbCISgE="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2317,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.644052049Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"c72dfc64-7c74-5e71-8127-6212967297b4","title":"[L119] Repeated conversation chunks collide as obligation identities and abort admission","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L119.\n\n- `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/execution/obligations.rs:58-70,131-143` splits the transcript into consecutive at-most64 KiB byte spans and derives each requirement ID from **only that chunk's exact bytes**, without its source offset. It then sorts every draft by that content-derived ID.\n- If two chunks have identical bytes, they receive identical IDs; `peritus-obligations/src/ledger/validation.rs:43-52` rejects adjacent equal IDs as DuplicateValue. Repeated/pasted transcript blocks can therefore fail the entire ledger instead of retaining two distinct source occurrences. This is a source-confirmed identity/provenance mismatch; no runtime reproduction was run during the audit.\n- Error Display includes only the category and omits the stored expected/actual numeric values and requirement ID (`peritus-obligations/src/error.rs:134-138`). The product stringifies this into its InvalidPrecondition error, making both the one-MiB threshold and duplicate source occurrence less explicit to the user.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIuhSZXL1J2fPmUZ2k4ljFImhTc/s62KM1shEBWVLeIeBuFGTixHw43B4vYPx+SsT+pKCP2XHqb6X1jT+m9tcg8="}
