jected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJrhaHHFMKR0S4SoJDuz+GzFaPRSbQIlQ1JBVGEu2M/FIV1TyX8qPaIt3G60E9T6BeE/uItMTZbOugBG72RnDgU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2331,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.678539580Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"8416812f-2fe9-5261-be54-4d7201151912","title":"[L126] Image attachments have independent host ceilings","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L126.\n\n- `peritus-product-runner/src/attachment.rs` declares **4 MiB per encoded image**, **12 MiB aggregate encoded images**, **16 images**, **8,192 pixels per side**, **16 Mi pixels per image**, **64 animation frames**, and **128 MiB decoded bytes**.\n- The per-image byte check uses the smaller of the host 4 MiB limit and the provider's inline-media allowance. Image count and aggregate host byte admission reject the request rather than resizing, splitting, or dropping an attachment. The complete `attachment/decode.rs` read verifies nonzero dimensions, side and pixel admission at lines 80-89, cumulative decoded output at lines 92-126, and a 64-frame maximum at lines 108-111. The image-library 128 MiB allocation allowance is explicitly best-effort, not a hard process-memory ceiling. PNG default-image bytes are charged in addition to animation frames; unsupported formats outside PNG/JPEG/GIF/WebP are rejected.\n- These are host media/resource bounds independent of session persistence or an elapsed run limit. Daily-driving consequence: a provider that could otherwise accept a larger image cannot bypass the lower host cap. Exact provider aggregate-media admission is tracked separately in L017.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1M