decessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIDpehDZeB3Zf569hwR0MQbeykGxN2WrQipcQe58Ky3gv/lw18/1ulP/RJ4bFtoXEy12CQ6mgSlrj36zAZbiGAg="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2333,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.683031654Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"829c3f12-cb87-55cf-9d48-dce78449365d","title":"[L127] Initial reviewer evidence is capped independently of available provider context","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L127.\n\n- `peritus-product-runner/src/turn/evidence.rs:7-16,51-77` budgets initial evidence at the smaller of **50% of model input tokens**, space below a **75% request target** after framing, and **384 KiB**, using an estimate of **three bytes per token**. Weighted section shares start at 64/144/48/80/32/16 KiB for conversation/diff/gates/developer evidence/prior findings/correction; spare bytes are redistributed in fixed priority order.\n- `turn/reviewer_prompt.rs:33-69` rejects review before provider invocation when system/prompt/tool framing reaches that 75% target, even if the provider's full context limit has not been reached. Oversized individual evidence sections keep a head and tail with a SHA-256 omission marker; very small allocations can contain only a partial marker (`evidence.rs:79-95`). This projection also applies to the authoritative conversation and prior findings, not only diagnostic output.\n- Daily-driving effect: large-context providers still receive at most 384 KiB of this initial packet; important middle clauses or prior defects can be omitted. The reviewer is instructed to recover exact current file details through fresh read-only tools, but this file does not provide a corresponding tool for the omitted conversation clauses. Full history remains in host state; omission is not proof of history deletion. Tests explicitly expect an 8,000-token profile to fail framing admission; they have been read, not rerun.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCUV+p46stV909xIk6PLtPyieQ/WQnvuyeSg2a9pX4cztUp1p/OEfXxcR/Mx51B4eKSYeUsKH+PGNUgO3WebpgQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2334,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.685093457Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"829c3f12-cb87-55cf-9d48-dce78449365d","comment_uuid":"c83c7b96-095e-4f80-b8ab-d437b18fb296","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L127: Initial reviewer evidence is capped independently of available provider context.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: peritus-product-runner/src/turn/evidence.rs:7-16,51-77; turn/reviewer_prompt.rs:33-69; evidence.rs:79-95. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nBuild reviewer input from actual provider headroom and exact evidence handles, with retrievable conversation clauses and finding pages. Treat initial section shares as preferences and report precise omitted coverage; do not hard-fail at an arbitrary 75 percent target. Reviewer conclusions must bind to the complete candidate and required evidence actually observed.\n\nPreserve: definitely-unaccepted versus ambiguously-accepted request state, exact native thread/profile identity, ordered provider observations, tool-result protocol, explicit cancellation and real provider/model capabilities. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMRiky5kUBAh5eyTxVaWM8TUgKm/uRtrtLLbVOPZGWhW/whg+yAx3HQjEvSrHkJPnwUZCYuBvsH8Nm33Qvzeuww="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2335,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.687218908Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"3099bc35-d22e-5512-a29f-103262dcfa4c","title":"[L128] Explicit text attachments have separate selection admission ceilings","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L128.\n\n- `peritus-product-runner/src/attachment/text.rs:6-11,25-32` declares **256 KiB per selected text attachment**, **512 KiB aggregate selection**, and **32 eligible file references**. The constructor verifies the per-file bound and rejects invalid UTF-8 and control characters other than tab/CR/LF, retaining exact bytes and their digest.\n- Aggregate/count enforcers and selection callers remain pending. These limits are distinct from whole-source inspection (64 MiB), workspace tool reads, checkpoint payloads, model text, and image attachment bounds; reducing a selected range can address only this selected-text boundary, not a whole-source scan failure.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQADclXcnBWMBtM2bULbPX2RW2Ju4es563u3ZIDdKVyOlJs1ksVluVgnPWjRizN3954NXIWoFRk7k06ufObYJJwQ="}
