{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2339,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.695716465Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"e9099d72-fe8f-561b-b197-caa7f6632653","title":"[L130] Product review derives blockers from a fixed category/severity policy","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L130.\n\n- `peritus-review/src/product/finding.rs:31-41,58-69,209-213` admits only seven named categories. Every non-advisory correctness, requested-behavior, build-coverage, test-coverage, or security finding blocks delivery, including **low** severity. Maintainability/documentation block at **high** or **critical**.\n- `product/ledger.rs:81-85,99-106,130-134` closes an omitted old finding only after a fixer proposal; omission alone cannot remove an untouched blocker. The product adapter does not expose a waiver transition here. These are acceptance and conservation policy constraints rather than artificial time limits; their relevance is whether a model-generated finding has concrete requested-behavior evidence.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAC46LLh2PLDKX9sPRmM105BQJ89Htej9Bnax4Yf5j/8zhIFDwmot7Q0Gnycmn4atJrdDFZDF/HPdTzcJmiVGAk="}
