{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2341,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.700190150Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"e7cb466b-a6e4-5185-b410-434b78affa56","title":"[L131] The separate D2 review-domain engine compiles fixed history and wire ceilings","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L131.\n\n- `peritus-review/src/limits.rs:57-86` compiles maximum **1,024 cycles**, **1,024 assignments**, **1,024 submissions**, **65,535 retained findings**, **256 categories**, **1,024 requirement IDs and locations**, **4,096 evidence references**, **1,024 provenance sources**, **4,096 disposition records**, **4,096 path bytes**, **256 KiB required text**, **1 MiB opaque fields**, and **16 MiB minus 16 bytes** for both command payload and aggregate state.\n- `ReviewLimits::new` at lines 110-132 rejects zero or any larger value; callers can only narrow these ceilings. `Confidence` independently restricts its fixed-point probability to 0..10,000. Probability validity is a semantic type bound, not a run blocker by itself.\n- `binding.rs:52-59,197-209` rejects a contract whose review-cycle policy exceeds selected cycle/assignment limits and requires a positive immutable maximum cycle count. Complete `finding.rs:274-329`, `finding/submission.rs:83-125`, `finding/location.rs:110-141`, and `reviewer.rs:130-189` reads now verify field, collection, relative-path, nonzero u32 coordinate, assignment ordinal/category, and provenance/history enforcers. Canonical/authority constraints are recorded separately from the numeric ceilings. `reducer/apply.rs:225-239` now verifies assignment refuses after selected assignments, selected cycles, or immutable contract cycles are consumed; lines 268-277 refuse excess submission/finding history or reused finding IDs. `reducer.rs:27-31,52-56,84-101` verifies payload/state admission. Production selection and durable restart handling remain pending. This domain engine is distinct from the product-facing finding ledger (L129); do not attribute its 1,024-cycle cap to that adapter without a caller.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNBuPAha5eq1kvy3LjVyUEXR9itKnSPWOEw+tv3dDjvIjuQ31aXWEInaC3D2xAHryqC4EEgEUOey0lD+7a3H5Ag="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2342,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.702464150Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"e7cb466b-a6e4-5185-b410-434b78affa56","comment_uuid":"a9a80c61-d1f2-4b34-9493-2fb5f813b034","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L131: The separate D2 review-domain engine compiles fixed history and wire ceilings.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: peritus-review/src/limits.rs:57-86; binding.rs:52-59,197-209; finding.rs:274-329; finding/submission.rs:83-125; finding/location.rs:110-141; reviewer.rs:130-189; reducer/apply.rs:225-239; reducer.rs:27-31,52-56,84-101. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nSeparate bounded active review assignments/submissions from paged immutable review, finding and disposition history. Version the binding so review cycles can continue under the same run without an immutable cumulative cycle allowance. Keep actual probability, location, evidence, authority and canonical validity checks and share durable framing with the complete final successor.\n\nPreserve: exact candidate revision and artifact binding, complete finding/provenance conservation, independent reviewer evidence, truthful gate outcomes, protected user constraints and acceptance fail-closed on invalid evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDvzYLcm8YLiJ0JxnObVwFDvTZB2TmrXX29VcRg+c/RuuGAknj7evUNAiUH7vgLctkctqDO9+P5c5ZR1XZdtBAM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2343,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.704573792Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"4eb90adf-3ce9-5415-8845-7dd3b6486cd1","title":"[L132] D2 oscillation policy can stop on unchanged severity after two candidate bindings","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L132.\n\n- `peritus-review/src/oscillation.rs:67-89,118-122` triggers on a repeated nonempty finding set, **equal maximum severity** across the last two candidate-binding groups, increased severity, a current disputed finding, or consumed contract cycle count. Equal severity can trigger even when finding identities changed or several defects were fixed.\n- The report defines any nonempty trigger set as requiring an autonomous stop; cycle exhaustion uses all assigned history, including invalidated bindings, rather than resetting for a fresh candidate. This file uses no wall clock. The implementation exposes no threshold or enable option in `OscillationReport::evaluate`; the equality/regression trigger is fixed. `reducer/apply.rs:321-340` now verifies finalization turns any oscillation trigger into terminal **NeedsHuman**, before evaluating quorum/conservation. All subsequent commands against terminal state are fenced closed (`reducer.rs:151-154`), so this aggregate cannot be resumed. Product caller selection remains pending; this is not yet evidence of the observed live product run stopping.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJzcnvaR0u7QyR61BpcD5cX6lQP8m3ciKEGgrD4v