{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2344,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.706674848Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"4eb90adf-3ce9-5415-8845-7dd3b6486cd1","comment_uuid":"2b818d9a-f467-4942-86df-82bb45a4451f","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L132: D2 oscillation policy can stop on unchanged severity after two candidate bindings.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: peritus-review/src/oscillation.rs:67-89,118-122; reducer/apply.rs:321-340; reducer.rs:151-154. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nReplace equal-severity/two-candidate terminal oscillation with a durable progress diagnosis over finding identities, fixes and evidence. Retain the task in a resumable repair or explicit waiting state when progress needs user input; no closed NeedsHuman aggregate should be required merely because severity is unchanged. Preserve unresolved defect conservation and never convert repeated failure into acceptance.\n\nPreserve: exact candidate revision and artifact binding, complete finding/provenance conservation, independent reviewer evidence, truthful gate outcomes, protected user constraints and acceptance fail-closed on invalid evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJ83POLJmU6nf0eRrHHYffu7Hkf/LopAcjFJF2oaygzqEh8ZoG9kFhBTYtJ2/aSJDDEe0Dt+jd7CMpKo2AMZSgw="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2345,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.708802725Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"40457b9e-1dd8-5b41-8bf5-c7b46077b4b0","title":"[L133] Review command-history exhaustion also rejects cancellation and recovery controls","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L133.\n\n- `peritus-review/src/reducer.rs:151-160` rejects every next command when **65,535 used command identities** have been retained. This guard runs before command dispatch and has no exception for CancelRun, FailRun, ExhaustBudget, PauseRun, or FinalizeRun. Event-sequence overflow separately rejects at lines 90-93.\n- Paused state admits only resume/cancel/budget-exhaust/failure controls (`reducer/apply.rs:25-34`); terminal state admits none. Pause/resume otherwise preserve the aggregate. Contract revision changes cannot change maximum cycles or acceptance policy (lines 200-215), and cancelled/invalidated cycles continue occupying history/assignment capacity.\n- `replay.rs:38-54` rebuilds the complete chain from genesis and rejects an absent, ahead, behind, or semantically different checkpoint instead of using a valid prefix or rebuilding the cache. This is a durable consistency/recovery barrier, not evidence of context expiry. Journal loading and production reachability remain pending.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNqaGKTuGbSZxig5pg145s+srk80LjShwEbYqqPGA+mYQxIv+nLZq6w3tqLLCLffJ8u/BAy9qxyq+ylh3I00UQg="}
