{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2347,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.712962687Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"2f453758-e761-54c8-ab31-c8e8196d2b77","title":"[L134] D2 persists and replays complete duplicated finding history inside one bounded state","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L134.\n\n- `peritus-review/src/state.rs:231-275` charges all retained findings, finding copies inside every submitted cycle, all cycles/waivers, and all consumed command identities to one aggregate estimate. There is no history retirement in `state/mutation.rs`; advancing a candidate invalidates old cycles and keeps them. The **16 MiB minus 16 bytes** state ceiling (L131) can therefore be reached through ordinary accumulated review history before the independent count limits are reached.\n- `durability.rs:64-80` canonically encodes the complete command, event, and state on every transition with production codec limits, then independently verifies actual payload sizes. In-memory reduction estimates size before appending the next command identity (`reducer.rs:97-103`; `state/mutation.rs:16-25`); final storage admission can consequently reject a transition later than its estimate.\n- Restart loads every aggregate event and the whole state, rejects any decoded record mismatch, and requires head/checkpoint agreement (`durability.rs:196-254`). Codec/integrity mismatch is classified Quarantine; journal errors request ReplayAggregate. No wall-clock expiry is implemented here, but durable storage is coupled to a fixed aggregate ceiling and whole-history validation. Production use of this separate engine remains pending.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+