{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2353,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.726248583Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"779aaff3-c46a-5b52-8342-36f3dc197fcb","title":"[L137] Review reconciliation rejects summed provenance before deduplication","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L137.\n\n- `peritus-review/src/reconciliation.rs:67-93,164-174` compares the sum of source and evidence counts against selected production **1,024 provenance sources** and **4,096 evidence references** before merging. `state/mutation.rs:117-123` subsequently deduplicates both collections. Two findings sharing most evidence can therefore be refused even when the final distinct set would fit; for example, two 4,000-reference copies of the same evidence exceed the precheck while their union has 4,000 references.\n- Disposition histories are retained rather than deduplicated and have the independent **4,096-record** cap. Superseded duplicates stay in aggregate history. Reconciliation thus cannot serve as unlimited history retirement and can itself become blocked by a capacity precheck.\n- `reducer/apply/finding_lifecycle.rs:240-242` binds retained waiver history to the selected finding limit (**65,535** production maximum). Exact revision, independent confirmation, external authority, and reused approval-request checks are integrity/authority requirements; they are not synthetic deadlines. Product use of this domain engine remains pending.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCFJG+X