{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2357,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.735564519Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"74780bf9-5a1d-51bc-b086-f883998dbb97","title":"[L140] Embedded engineering prompts impose additional layout and loop policies","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L140.\n\n- `peritus-product-runner/src/engineering_workflow/reviewer.rs:5-7` tells reviewers to treat a production file above **500 lines** as a concrete finding. No file-specific exception is consulted in this prompt. Product blocker policy still depends on the returned category/severity (L130), so the instruction is not by itself a deterministic 500-line build rejection.\n- `engineering_workflow.rs:297-299` and developer/reviewer role strings require external pagination/retry code to have finite attempts and repeated-token guards, but choose no numeric default themselves. These are instructions about code produced for the user's task, not an enforcer that ends the Peritus role after a fixed duration. `engineering_workflow.rs:314-318` additionally requires **at least three observations** for requested periodic polling; this is an imposed evidence-shape minimum.\n- The same embedded workflow blocks acceptance after a forbidden black-box/private observation remains in the retained trace (lines 15-23), and requires package build/tests/lint and exact requested interface/effect evidence. These are task/acceptance authority constraints, recorded separately from arbitrary numeric bounds. The fixed workflow is injected into architect/developer/reviewer policies and contributes to the context-framing admission failure in L127; this audit has not measured its exact token cost on each provider.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHgjKsV8E+5AOyeP36DfPAhzDXFSuCa5/qDYZrEXl80qCEqmPBUo6MLwgMS0LZnE5wSlXjh8a9RyXQeNAqmtkw4="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2358,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.738040490Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"74780bf9-5a1d-51bc-b086-f883998dbb97","comment_uuid":"f6d6898e-4124-4276-b111-208fbf5fe66d","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L140: Embedded engineering prompts impose additional layout and loop policies.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: peritus-product-runner/src/engineering_workflow/reviewer.rs:5-7; engineering_workflow.rs:297-299; engineering_workflow.rs:314-318. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nReplace fixed prompt heuristics for file length, retry attempts and minimum observation counts with task-specific maintainability, recovery and evidence contracts. Generated code should use real cancellation/continuation semantics rather than mandatory synthetic retries. Keep explicit private-observation prohibitions and requested interface/effect acceptance, and make workflow guidance select relevant rules without consuming arbitrary provider framing headroom.\n\nPreserve: exact candidate revision and artifact binding, complete finding/provenance conservation, independent reviewer evidence, truthful gate outcomes, protected user constraints and acceptance fail-closed on invalid evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOz7kmr6XNA7aR0XB3/94ue3qYogDVFjuoihLbK4XNglUdWGoXEOnx1igV9LgcBrBPJzzp+4W3U9uhMVOsvZxw0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2359,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.740336462Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"fc32ec76-2a63-5413-a71d-44679c5ac7a6","title":"[L142] Managed workspace image discovery silently drops candidates and can stop the whole traversal on depth","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L142.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/workspace_media.rs:17-21,53-69,103-139,150-180,258-282`; caller `workspace_delivery.rs:83-100`.\n- **Limits/enforcement:** Discovery retains at most 1,024 image paths, selects only the first 16 sorted matches, excludes six named directory components, and limits traversal depth to 16. Encountering any pending directory deeper than 16 uses `break`, ending the entire traversal rather than skipping that directory. Directory entries are collected and sorted before the image limit helps; there is no directory-entry bound or cancellation inside this synchronous walk.\n- **Failure/recovery:** Each candidate must be nonempty, at most 4 MiB or the provider's lower inline limit, with at most 12 MiB aggregate bytes. Oversized candidates silently disappear from the attachment manifest; if every candidate is rejected, the entire operation fails with a Provider error. A content/extension signature mismatch or any directory/read error fails discovery. A visual request with a provider lacking image support is refused. Supported discovery types are PNG, JPEG, GIF, and WebP, selected through fixed phrase/path heuristics. Explicit-media hosts bypass this legacy discovery.\n- **Classification:** Product-selected discovery/attachment ceilings and truncation, separate from provider capacity and integrity checks. No paging, resizing, or continuation is implemented here. The explicit in-place child is now fully read: it accepts only explicit tokens that pass protected-file checks, silently discards invalid paths/errors, and takes 16 candidates BEFORE deduplication; repeated early references can therefore consume the entire selection allowance. Its tests and the managed discovery tests are fully read, not executed. This is source-confirmed behavior, not evidence that it caused the current live run to stall.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOmaXDwAxKxb1PwrNpL8QS7jidRIYqoV9E1+FPZ4TUyIw5SK2xfWg+ArZKcDL/Z/99LjuYzT2By00MTnm/RurAc="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2360,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.742938188Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"fc32ec76-2a63-5413-a71d-44679c5ac7a6","comment_uuid":"c9ad857b-a154-4367-8ed1-4154dfef7e4e","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L142: Managed workspace image discovery silently drops candidates and can stop the whole traversal on depth.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/workspace_media.rs:17-21,53-69,103-139,150-180,258-282; workspace_delivery.rs:83-100. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nMake media discovery a cancellable paged enumeration with per-candidate status and stable selection identity. A deep branch must be skipped or continued without ending sibling traversal; deduplicate explicit paths before applying physical page capacity. Keep rejected/large images visible by reference with an explicit transform/provider-capability choice instead of silently losing them.\n\nPreserve: exact candidate revision and artifact binding, complete finding/provenance conservation, independent reviewer evidence, truthful gate outcomes, protected user constraints and acceptance fail-closed on invalid evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQL/hebWpVQyGzqnP5IQdlelrAq16BF6Vv4Kb4HAiW/8cWfxd3KtuN5qy1gkrH8sZFqoYNVju6BgtyPLrxMHZCQI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2361,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.745026258Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"ed06cf74-0eb0-5a66-bfe9-3eafc9e0cab2","title":"[L143] Candidate exclusion names classify entire directory components as generated","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L143.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/workspace_filter.rs:5-27`; delivery boundary `workspace_delivery.rs:16-61,110-119` and `workspace_kind.rs:7-33`.\n- **Limits/enforcement:** Any path component named `target`, `node_modules`, `.venv`, `venv`, `__pycache__`, `build`, `.eggs`, `.pytest_cache`, `.mypy_cache`, or `.ruff_cache`, or ending `.egg-info`/`.dist-info`, classifies the entire descendant path as generated, without inspecting its purpose. A legitimate source directory named `build` also qualifies. Capture callers are now fully read: `candidate/managed/capture.rs:32-43` and `capture/directories.rs:28-48` apply these exclusions to new untracked paths; tracked and previously owned paths remain included. Git ignore rules independently hide new paths. Export is now fully read: `candidate/managed/export.rs:8-69` constructs a binary patch from the captured entry maps, so files excluded by capture are absent from delivery. Newly created nested repositories are flattened into source entries; full blobs and patches are buffered without an additional cap in this layer.\n- **Boundary distinction:** Managed and in-place runs use different baseline/ownership paths. In-place scope uses a revision-specific durable journal; provider-session storage is derived from the trace path and role rather than an elapsed expiry. Protected paths are caller-selected authority restrictions. The in-place delivery prompt requires declarations before commands and offers no automatic rollback; it is not a sandbox or timer.\n- **Classification:** Fixed candidate inclusion policy can omit deliverable source. It is not a session deadline. Capture omission is confirmed for newly untracked files; previously owned files survive changed ignore rules. The export consumer confirms the omission propagates into deliverable patches.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKh6bzzWClokXVR7UN9kNX5kOzbuD53o4IzKJvdG39SUj94o3m28Y9JQLkDSOKyh5E7qIYOXAvaM7BY61Q/TuAQ="}
