ation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGO2gN1+qMcBaV96TFhqLnb0VdAEH7IOqBg9gMop/wXRjGjj8mDUo1KV0WgdBC2UCmDHhfwmVRW0qHZ4F4MGDg8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2381,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.790667185Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"f49a3e04-8bf9-5a46-b38d-5e4ca00326bb","title":"[L154] Brief, fork, and attachment selection impose fixed text/history representation limits","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L154.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/control/branch.rs:33-37,174-217`; `control/brief.rs:93-145,158-200`; `control/files/ledger.rs:125-178`; `control/files/source.rs:8,24-56,72-105`; `control/files/version.rs:70-81,133-145`; related attachment limits L007/L128.\n- **Limits/enforcement:** Fork titles use 256-byte control text and objectives 8,192-byte control text; the entire fork lineage and optional historical seed must fit MAX_CONTROL_BYTES. Every brief field uses 8,192-byte text, with exactly four semantic field types, and full brief rendering must fit MAX_REQUEST_CONTEXT_BYTES. The control root was fully reread to resolve values: `control.rs:62-66` selects the journal's 16 MiB state ceiling and model protocol's 16 MiB text ceiling; no extra capacity is negotiated here.\n- **Attachment caller confirmation:** File-ledger validation checks eligible selected references against the attachment layer's 32-reference / 512 KiB aggregate limit, including after refresh. Complete source metadata and byte/line bounds are limited to 64 MiB even for small selected ranges; each selected version must fit 256 KiB and match its source range/digest. Captions use 8,192-byte control text, workspace paths 4,096 bytes, imported labels 1,024 bytes. Every refresh stays in immutable history; deselected entries and old versions remain in whole-record serialization, without an independent history compaction mechanism here.\n- **Boundary distinction:** Read-only forks share the workspace, writable forks require a separate registered workspace plus objective and criteria; this preserves write ownership. Historical file selections are frozen snapshots, not expired grants. Identity/digest/authority constraints are separate from product-selected text/storage ceilings.\n- **Classification:** Synthetic content/storage ceilings and representation policy; no elapsed expiry in these files. Fully read source and brief tests, not executed. Lifecycle consumers and stale-pin handling remain under review.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQM4J57/2nG8kYyZHm9daewb49Upu63aalO+Tl0cr2jPOLBVj2sFi8kCddhaK0LKZ/VpWmLMikUboZnzUCFfFpAk="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2382,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.792857768Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"f49a3e04-8bf9-5a46-b38d-5e4ca00326bb","comment_uuid":"75a8d1e9-5a48-4ac4-a83d-35c93e5045bc","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L154: Brief, fork, and attachment selection impose fixed text/history representation limits.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/control/branch.rs:33-37,174-217; control/brief.rs:93-145,158-200; control/files/ledger.rs:125-178; control/files/source.rs:8,24-56,72-105; control/files/version.rs:70-81,133-145; control.rs:62-66. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nStore brief, fork and attachment history as paged exact records with a bounded current selection projection. Separate selected source ranges from complete source identity and stream inspection. Version fork creation so copied context and independent child write authority remain internally consistent, while old frozen selections stay addressable without forcing all history into one conversation record.\n\nPreserve: durable logical session and run identity, exact command receipts, atomic snapshot/cursor binding, explicit authority, selected UI state, complete history retrieval and owned-effect reconciliation. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large histories and non-ASCII fields, queue/connection pressure, delayed acknowledgements, subscription gaps, disconnect/reconnect and daemon restart, proving snapshot recovery, preserved selection/context, responsive controls and no duplicate command. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQC2LIsAoUWMt6/vyW1UHQGRi5OU6nW3XnwXvnFOZjT+HlX35MB2/7qsBEJU3/FwctJ2DyW9VbvIFgAGgCkQXpQk="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2383,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.794941458Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"8a6b4892-b9a3-5917-8c25-7a44939b91cd","title":"[L155] Public-reply compaction has fixed source/focus/replacement bounds and can reject a valid focus","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L155.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/control/compaction.rs:16-17,95-145,149-172,176-206,211-265`.\n- **Limits/enforcement:** Focus and structural replacement each allow 1,024 bytes, while every replacement also adds a fixed source-identity/digest/size explanation and focus wrapper. A focus valid at the input limit cannot fit the replacement limit. Such a reply is silently skipped; if no replacement remains, compaction returns InvalidInput. At most 65,535 source/replacement entries are accepted. Each source passes a C6 graph configured with four nodes, 1 MiB content, two dependencies, and two visibility roles; oversize source content becomes generic InvalidInput rather than a size-specific diagnostic, though the PublicReplyReference constructor independently already restricts supported replies to 1 MiB (`control/reply.rs:29-30`). Tokens are estimated as ceil(bytes/4), with a minimum of one.\n- **Failure/recovery:** Replacement must be strictly smaller than original, exact digest/bytes must match, and entries cannot duplicate invocations. These identity/conservation checks are necessary. Exact reply artifacts remain retained; compaction changes only the active prompt view and does not shrink whole durable history. There is no split-source compaction or accommodation for a maximal otherwise-valid focus here.\n- **Classification:** Product-selected compaction bounds and misleading error behavior; no elapsed timer or deletion expiry. Source confirmed, not reproduced in this audit. Automatic/caller selection remains under review.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNx3Kulv4OJWKq56J+FSXaY92Ow7wY6Zr26rhwzMTqqkA4rf7EcNqNBaDWCmWGo8DsFri1uSa43GfdzMe/9ggAw="}
