ther; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long productive read/write sessions through repeated compaction and segment boundaries, source/dependency changes, non-ASCII and large evidence, interrupted checkpoint publication, then reopen the same lineage and prove that valid grounding is reused and stale targets are reread. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJLhcUGxcrN28EAYLG2m1Ovr3MGNW45q4XAZkduKHMmr4qlVoQs0XLsKZF/3x+YP0xJj/XJA86fiSYVRyUxsVg8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2385,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.799084307Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"c4602667-6652-52f6-8bef-161a9b6dbc46","title":"[L156] Guidance and permission projections retain fixed text/schema bounds separately from authority","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L156.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/control/guidance.rs:19-24,69-92,155-163,181-234`; `control/permissions.rs:117-174`.\n- **Limits/enforcement:** Saved/revised guidance uses 8,192-byte control text, and forget explanations use 1,024 bytes. Permission decoding rejects inputs above 4,096 bytes, unknown fields, noncanonical encodings, any schema other than 1, or bits outside four capabilities. Permission revision uses checked u64 increments. Selected guidance requires nonzero exact record/dependency revisions except initial empty-catalog save.\n- **Boundary distinction:** Permissions intersect user restrictions with the immutable host ceiling; stale revisions, no-op changes, and grants above that ceiling are refused. Accepted-reply guidance must match its exact user-approved text digest and stays within its project/conversation scope. These authority and provenance requirements should survive synthetic limiter removal.\n- **Classification:** Fixed text/storage/schema representation ceilings plus real authority fences. No duration or expiry in these files; guidance sidecar capacity/retrieval consumers remain pending. Inline permission test fully read, not executed.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAA