{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2386,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.801384114Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"c4602667-6652-52f6-8bef-161a9b6dbc46","comment_uuid":"96ca9f82-525c-49bf-a3e6-29651eb065b0","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L156: Guidance and permission projections retain fixed text/schema bounds separately from authority.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/control/guidance.rs:19-24,69-92,155-163,181-234; control/permissions.rs:117-174. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nKeep guidance as exact scoped approved artifacts with paged revision history, separating display text from permission grants. Use an explicit versioned permission migration and retain the immutable host ceiling and user restriction intersection. Longer guidance must not alter authority; stale or conflicting guidance bindings require actionable reconciliation.\n\nPreserve: explicit user authority, credential secrecy, exact target/resource binding, fencing, scope confinement, replay rejection for changed command content and fail-closed acceptance evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: renewal/adoption under the same authorized identity, revoked authority, stale epoch/revision, cross-scope requests, lost acknowledgements and restart, proving legitimate continuation without admitting unauthorized or duplicate effects. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLK0ewqiyHDTOR6nOM1cHbJu63r57dxVqzOSC7JVnZfDLSp4OwTA6zGMyMiZrDk4ECHMBqsJSLT0tw/pyg6d7wY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2387,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.803316196Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"7c614c8b-af19-5e12-8cb3-9e5c2a690d58","title":"[L157] Request capture checks full reply history before exclusions or compacted replacements","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L157.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/control/inputs/capture.rs:105-162,165-211`; caller `control/record/projection.rs:129-167`; public-reply ceiling `control/reply.rs:23-32`.\n- **Limits/enforcement:** `capture_with_reply_view` first renders ALL incorporated user inputs and eligible pending instructions against MAX_REQUEST_CONTEXT_BYTES (16 MiB via `control.rs:65-66`). It then sums EVERY supplied reply's ORIGINAL byte length plus 32 bytes, and refuses Capacity if that total exceeds the same fixed ceiling. This precheck happens BEFORE excluding replies, omitting trailing replies, or substituting compacted source handles. Brief and file context add their own checks against this ceiling afterward. Each reply separately permits at most 1 MiB and cannot be empty.\n- **Failure/recovery:** A conversation can stop admitting requests because original history exceeds the limit even when its actual compacted/excluded next view would fit. User-input history is always rendered and cannot be excluded through context preferences. Local provider-context compaction does not bypass this upstream control capture. The exact host-supplied reply-map retention/selection policy remains to be read; the check is confirmed for all entries supplied, not an assumption that every historical artifact always enters this map.\n- **Classification:** Synthetic context admission ceiling and ordering defect that can defeat intended history compaction. Source-confirmed, not a live-size reproduction. Repair must retain immutable history while admitting an appropriate provider view, not delete or expire the conversation.\n\n- Production caller traced: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_control/inputs.rs:156-180` first captures eligibility using empty reply text, selects only eligible replies, then rejects **the sum of their original immutable byte lengths plus framing and the eligibility capture** above 16 MiB before loading the text and applying the real capture. Excluded and trailing replies are filtered here, so this is not an all-history reply charge in that caller. **Compacted replacements do not reduce the original-byte charge**, confirming the compaction/admission mismatch on the production path. Images/files are checked again after effective pin/selection resolution (L162), preventing those overrides from producing an unbounded provider request.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQO0ewGsOW2NyZrP3HTCoHG6hZcVStpb9XSXSisT/xYkNpXKEN/kNd8wBrUm4R5oQ50O0+8fqmRjmkyo8/vkk9Qs="}
