{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2399,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.829370263Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"10c0ec72-eff9-54da-bddd-dbf1ae2b70e3","title":"[L163] Review comments accept 8 KiB of text but their mandatory prompt wrapper must fit the same 8 KiB","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L163.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/control/review.rs:17,219-228,257-267`; `control/review/ledger.rs:48-76,79-106,229-274`.\n- **Limits/enforcement:** Review comments use ControlText<8192> and paths have a 4,096-byte lossy-display bound. Adding/rebinding a comment then adds action instructions, exact run/workspace IDs, five SHA-256 identities, path, target, and line ranges, and constructs another ControlText<8192> from the entire wrapper plus comment. An otherwise-valid 8,192-byte comment therefore cannot be added or rebound; long paths consume still more of the undocumented effective comment allowance. No dynamic allowance, separate structured identity channel, or precise effective-limit diagnostic is present.\n- **Failure/recovery:** Whole transition rejects before publication; message/path history remains preserved. Rebind/dismiss operations require exact current input revisions and refuse withdrawn/superseded/dismissed states. Revisions use checked u64 except automatic explanation addressing which saturates. All comments remain in the aggregate with no local count limit beyond whole-state limits.\n- **Classification:** Synthetic text-bound composition mismatch; identity/freshness requirements themselves remain necessary. Source confirmed; maximal-comment reproduction not run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGW