{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2404,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.839954111Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"d056ad9c-597a-52c8-976e-031fe6f23b75","comment_uuid":"c6b9b180-250c-486d-816a-ebcb69232249","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L165: Durable effect receipts have fixed per-record and lifetime storage ceilings.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/developer_tools/receipt.rs:21-23,181-221; receipt/storage.rs:44-88,96-105. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nUse segmented append-only effect receipts with immutable indexed outcomes and bounded active Started obligations. Store the completed result once by artifact reference instead of duplicating Applied/Completed bodies. Preflight settlement reachability and keep controls independently admitted, so lifetime journal growth or a result wrapper cannot lose an already performed effect.\n\nPreserve: committed command/event identity, exact causal and digest roots, exclusive ownership, atomic publication, reference-safe artifact retention and verified recovery from the last durable frontier. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHMmiyFxsceNhgdd7nGrEMT85RWsTppZuVNXrTM0XWr39RGa7pFiwNTMhopGrj9PhD8KLHPBLCJzCRhLLMxtFQw="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2405,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.841903578Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"36e24822-5264-5ec4-89b9-3ab8dd05fd9d","title":"[L166] An interrupted command receipt becomes ambiguous, with an epoch-wide barrier that survives acknowledgement","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L166.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/developer_tools/receipt.rs:101-158,224-299`.\n- Resuming a Started command receipt appends Ambiguous and refuses execution. The prior-command barrier scans other scopes in the same run and requirements revision for Started, Ambiguous, or Reviewed command records. A Reviewed record only replays the same tool and request digest; a different request remains blocked with instructions to obtain new input.\n- This prevents blind re-execution of an effect with an unknown outcome. It is an integrity boundary, but these methods do not reconcile native command ownership or establish the prior outcome. Acknowledgement alone does not resolve the unknown effect. Advancing the requirements revision changes the barrier epoch.\n- `receipt/replay.rs:19-24` invokes the cross-scope barrier before mutation-specific checkpoint preflight. `receipt/inspection.rs:85-118` acknowledges by appending Reviewed with an explicit unknown-outcome error; it requires its caller to prove the run owner is inactive. The complete `receipt/uncertainty.rs` tests cover same-call replay, cross-role mutation blocking, and admission after a new requirements revision. **Source and test assertions read; tests were not run, and host ownership checks/native reconciliation remain pending.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsO