{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2412,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.857702947Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"12223f2e-e022-59f7-b683-85b363db2362","comment_uuid":"4bd0b4fc-e5ca-49be-8c40-63b2fac0b3b0","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L169: Preview admission permits untimed operation but retains payload bounds and a narrower downstream process contract.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/developer_tools/preview.rs:9-11,43-71,157-165. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nShare one preview launch contract from UI/schema through typed admission and process gateway, including native argv/environment, optional deadlines and terminal dimensions. Stage large payloads by reference when supported and validate downstream capability before accepting launch. Preserve exact idempotency and authority rather than admitting a broader profile that inevitably fails later.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQL4nlSeix8zygolSO7WWDVe10WQKeINg2dUzT/oZavVvMxgw9VrZ3K+fHzi3GprWXm6umDz4HUgs8Ndb6KfkUAY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2413,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.859896414Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"eec80d75-0da3-569e-9d2e-e10679d522f0","title":"[L212] A pre-spawn Codex started marker can permanently fence a session without a native thread ID","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L212.\n\n- Source: `crates/model/peritus-provider-openai/src/runtime/provider/invocation.rs:99-116`; `invocation/sessions.rs:16-27,42-65,69-116`.\n- Before transport.run, the initial persistent session creates and synchronizes invocation-started. If spawn or another pre-submission transport step then fails before a thread.started event is journaled, Session::open later rejects the namespace as an interrupted invocation with no recoverable identity. This applies even to an outcome known to be definitely absent at the transport boundary; no such phase distinction or marker repair appears in these files.\n- Identity recovery scans every turn directory but examines only the first **64 KiB of each native.jsonl**. It accepts complete newline-delimited thread.started records with an ID of at most **512 bytes** using ASCII alphanumeric/hyphen characters, rejects conflicting IDs, and does not use a global latest-thread fallback. A thread event outside the prefix or in a torn final frame cannot establish continuity. Exact identity/conflict protection is necessary; the fixed prefix and lack of definitely-absent launch recovery are separate barriers.\n- Started state without identity remains retained and blocked rather than silently starting a fresh context. Inline tests cover torn trailing output, exact thread recovery, role/model isolation and lost-identity refusal; they do not cover a failed spawn after the marker or late identity beyond the prefix.\n- **Complete source/tests read; no failed-spawn reproduction run.** A repair needs durable launch phase/identity reconciliation that distinguishes absent effects from ambiguous effects, while preserving existing threads and preventing duplicate starts.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAJaoElzJe0dC5xY6WFjbUtyf/TAPPUxQMiOcxvcw6NLcx2i3muQ9FaovHw83nGCVccu8oVrbrZyYPr+rfwyIQI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2414,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.862246358Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"eec80d75-0da3-569e-9d2e-e10679d522f0","comment_uuid":"196c1d87-d75f-4216-bfb8-7c82f7a9c406","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L212: A pre-spawn Codex started marker can permanently fence a session without a native thread ID.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/model/peritus-provider-openai/src/runtime/provider/invocation.rs:99-116; invocation/sessions.rs:16-27,42-65,69-116. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nrepair needs durable launch phase/identity reconciliation that distinguishes absent effects from ambiguous effects, while preserving existing threads and preventing duplicate starts.\n\nPreserve: definitely-unaccepted versus ambiguously-accepted request state, exact native thread/profile identity, ordered provider observations, tool-result protocol, explicit cancellation and real provider/model capabilities. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQISmMkil85/YvsrBtXqdQIfinLmEAWzA5NbVHD130Xsdpe1hw8L1wqmK5GTb+D6PaLajcMAPNt3/OgX8sQZUxQM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2415,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.864707188Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"e21c9eff-d890-59bd-ab07-66c8fc017166","title":"[L224] Writer follow-ups use a role that enabled local memory rejects, and disabled memory selects another native context","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L224.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/execution.rs:72-95`; `turn.rs:53-54,292-310`; `local_context/port.rs:58-67`; `workspace_delivery.rs:103-112`.\n- When conversation revision differs from retained execution state, the production loop creates a fresh design and invokes complete_developer_turn with role **writer-follow-up**. That function calls input.working_memory(role) before its loop. With local memory enabled, LocalContextHandle accepts only writer/designer/fixer/reviewer, so writer-follow-up returns unsupported local memory role and the authorized follow-up is rejected **before any model inference**. The daemon default enables local memory (L204).\n- If local memory is disabled, the rejection is bypassed, but native_session_directory joins the literal role into trace.context/<role>/provider-sessions. Therefore writer-follow-up selects a different parent directory from writer, even with the same run/profile/revision/model, losing automatic reuse of the original writer thread on this path. The repair should separate stable role identity from invocation purpose and retain the same exact writer ownership/context through follow-ups.\n- Ordinary design/writer/fixer/reviewer/conversation requests all explicitly supply Some(native_session_directory); run_live_invocation forwards it, and Developer model request construction preserves it. Their bound namespaces have no ephemeral expiry. SemanticCompaction requests intentionally omit that metadata and do not execute host tools. This closes the main production metadata uncertainty in L215, while daemon run/trace identity persistence remains separately audited in L183-L187.\n- **Every named implementation and caller fully read; no follow-up execution test run.** This is a source-confirmed production routing incompatibility, not a claim that it caused the earlier observed live lockup.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIx1tLVO4QNnR0WnFpWERLfRpNu1K6S2VgffbHHmoK4Giz/C2JHzp6/R2vNJDM1caeQQy7MTqQSONDZosujNXgA="}
