cessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEeYBfg59tuHZu3VQTyKF1OnlkkHIVxsAErVjBXvrjnq45IPwD6fe5/FPOFxXHQ7RuijG9kr1QCe4c4l4nOmNgQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2435,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.910093302Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"d263553e-294b-5dff-a6f0-289a230790e7","title":"[L280] Partial artifact transfer progress is ephemeral even though ownership and publication identity are durable","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L280.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/artifact/service.rs:33-57,167-183,204-241,293-332`; `artifact/publication.rs`; `artifact/service/scoped.rs`; disconnect cleanup in L236.\n- Active reader/writer/ordinal/offset state lives only in the authority's BTreeMap. Cancel/abandon/disconnect or daemon restart drops it. The exact scoped claim and artifact catalog remain durable, but this service has no offset-based restart/resume API; recovery begins a new transfer and sends/verifies all bytes again.\n- complete_upload checks foreign ownership first, then removes the owned transfer **before** validating completion metadata, committing acceptance, finalizing the content object, and publishing catalog availability. Any later error loses that transfer's in-memory writer/progress and can leave intermediate durable facts. Exact full reupload is supported: the publication resolver retains the original command/receipt, and complete tests verify fresh transfer IDs preserve it. This is not proof of byte-progress resume.\n- Scoped read takes a positive whole-object maximum no greater than the configured object cap, reconstructs all bytes with 64 KiB chunks, then hashes the complete object inside the sole owner. No range read/continuation is exposed here.\n- Repair needs durable transfer/commit-phase reconciliation and restartable byte progress while keeping immutable identity. It must not make old partial bytes available merely because a receipt exists. **Complete source/tests read; no midcompletion storage failure/crash test executed.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHJ6vTsFvhcsHebvx9PVhpDy6j6k8yak+znX0SHAaNuwPxeabLoSoKucAeOfCyE6rHBNLg+XupSNg6u7e2osFwo="}
