mand histories, smaller configured bindings, saturation with cancellation and acknowledgements, delayed start/completion races, terminal roots with live descendants, lost receipts after subsequent progress, and save/reopen equivalence. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNpR3oR6cIjhg5B8T7gPG4SDMQVNQHXY4x5NZlD7KeKbZ7JxbT3m3qcy4SJ30kwEzkaLMq1Kx401llcugxCgXAQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2445,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.933844839Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"37a8852b-e911-5da3-babd-62eda01e9e4b","title":"[L294] CancelWorkTree refuses a terminal root even when live descendants remain","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L294.\n\n- Source: `crates/orchestration/peritus-scheduler/src/reducer/apply/cancellation/command.rs:91-102`; `cancellation.rs:18-33,137-159`; `cancellation/tests.rs:102-115`; `admission/checks.rs:52-64`.\n- Parent admission requires an already retained identity, not a live parent. Root cancellation, including descendants=true, rejects **any terminal root before traversing descendants**. Therefore a completed/canceled ancestor with retained live children cannot be used as the subtree cancellation root through this command.\n- The traversal itself deliberately follows terminal ancestor edges and selects only live targets. The source-module tests cover a terminal *middle* ancestor. The subsequently read integration test `tests/cancellation_tree.rs:143-150` explicitly requires terminal-root rejection even though its child and grandchild remain live; the blocker is therefore enforced by an existing regression expectation. Callers would have to discover and cancel each still-live child instead.\n- This is a lifecycle/cancellation usability blocker, not a duration limit. Repair should define subtree cancellation over a durable root identity independently of whether that root's own work is already terminal. **Complete root admission, closure and tests read; no runtime reproduction executed.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAool7n1p+n+cFXeMAm40oSlU+bbk37y65wiWLCR/me+NTyvzXmzFmR4/ahcwj1d18dtn9OuH5UyPp2i0tezdgU="}
