{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2451,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.948243756Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"b515fb47-ecfb-58d4-bd9b-52e5ec088565","title":"[L297] State-size admission runs before adding the accepted command to history","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L297.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/orchestration/peritus-scheduler/src/reducer.rs:42-47,70-82`; `state.rs:308-321`; `state/mutation/cursor.rs:28-51`; `state/validation.rs:9-23`; `limits.rs:163-210`; `wire/state.rs:102-210`; `durability.rs:123-207,309-338`.\n- **Mechanism:** each used command contributes 16 bytes to the state estimate. Ordinary reduction checks the estimate after applying the semantic change but before advancing the cursor, which appends another command. There is no subsequent estimate/inert validation before encoding and append. Reload checks the estimate including the newly appended command, so an admitted successor can exceed its immutable bound by 16 bytes and be rejected on restart even when its actual encoded frame fits. Genesis checks after its first command is present, making the ordinary-command ordering inconsistent with genesis.\n- **Concrete source arithmetic:** positive state bound 1,040 is permitted. Empty genesis has estimated size 1,024 + 16 = 1,040. A fresh PauseScheduler checks that unchanged estimate, succeeds, then appends a second command, producing estimate 1,056. With a small capacity vector the actual encoded state remains below 1,040, so the separate actual-byte commit gate does not repair the error. The restart estimate gate rejects it. This arithmetic follows the complete source; no executable test was run in this audit.\n- **Daily-driving effect:** any accepted transition close to a configured estimate boundary can turn into a restart-time quarantine, including control commands meant to manage existing work. The broader lifetime growth and conservative rejection issues remain recorded in L286/L289.\n- **Ontological repair requirement:** validate the final post-cursor successor once, using the same durable invariant and size contract as reopening. Remove heuristic lifetime ceilings from control admission as part of the separately authorized limiter repair; merely increasing the bound preserves this inconsistency.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEP4bKJeG9dfHWTan0QRNbE+TAEt5yBPOY7CqJCBC9qeozhEej+gMvjzEZ2awjcua0jSjq53JxyIEnl+fFZbRQw="}
