ust leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long task/message/command histories, smaller configured bindings, saturation with cancellation and acknowledgements, delayed start/completion races, terminal roots with live descendants, lost receipts after subsequent progress, and save/reopen equivalence. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDUpFJv/6RX90v6qvlXm9WyTz9CnDXY3rDnicDiJ0dVN2rtH+2Qnt6GKgieECSb2MHCdIxSMLiur8lEeqlFYlgU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2453,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.953623441Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"54e1fcf7-d4cf-5f38-aeb2-80218e532192","title":"[L298] Dependency refresh finishes synchronously by repeatedly rescanning all retained work","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L298.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/orchestration/peritus-scheduler/src/state/mutation.rs:263-398`; `state/mutation/dependency_action.rs:159-246`; `dependency_round.rs:242-383`; `dependency_round/apply.rs:195-280`; `dependency_measure.rs:16-95,225-261`; `state/lookup.rs:116-199`; `reducer.rs:70-82`. Owner serialization is traced in L274.\n- **Mechanism:** every ordinary command invokes dependency refresh. A round scans the entire retained work vector, looks up each dependency of WaitingDependencies/Queued records by binary search, collects all changes from the pre-round snapshot, then applies them synchronously. It repeats until a fixed point. The two-halves remaining counter derives from a decreasing natural measure of existing records; this is a termination witness, not an arbitrary timer or turn allowance, and valid-state proofs establish completion rather than silently leaving dependency work unfinished.\n- **Daily-driving effect:** terminal records remain in the scanned vector. A failure cascading through a dependency chain advances only one edge per snapshot round and can require a number of full-history scans proportional to chain depth. Source loops therefore permit quadratic retained-record visitation for a long chain, with additional dependency lookup and mutation costs. There is no yield, incremental dependency index, or persisted progress boundary inside refresh. A serialized authority owner can delay unrelated control work while computing an accepted transition. No latency benchmark or live-lockup attribution is claimed.\n- **Ontological repair requirement:** preserve complete dependency truth with indexed affected-node propagation and a responsive ownership boundary. Do not remove the structural termination reasoning as if it were a synthetic daily quota; remove whole-history work from routine control admission, and qualify long-history cancellation/status responsiveness independently of proof-only termination.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIGA5Zlypr4rLFazKYvZAUE84LqXq+fsPkuzRKjygXPon10kAsYVW+3CrkSxwqRMnAlPA94OUhLtBPY6qbam2gY="}
