{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2467,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.985468745Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"fb2c669b-199c-5120-92c2-63421c6d58d4","title":"[L306] Collaboration exact retries require the current checkpoint to remain the original successor","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L306.\n\n- Source: `crates/orchestration/peritus-collaboration/src/durability.rs:81-92,148-196,263-279`; `error.rs:115-123`; `reducer.rs:132-153`.\n- The commit helper resolves the exact command ID/frame digest before checking current heads, but compares its expected successor with the **current** state checkpoint. If that checkpoint has advanced, it returns Journal/ReplayAggregate despite the original command and exact event already being committed. It does not resolve against the retained successor revision for that batch.\n- A benign late exact retry therefore is not an ordinary successful idempotent result. Stale pure-command fences map to Quarantine through reject; generic journal errors map to ReplayAggregate even though the journal retains more specific causes. This repeats scheduler L284's current-checkpoint coupling.\n- Repair should return an exact historical committed receipt/state observation without authorizing a stale new effect, and retain actionable capacity/transport/integrity classifications. **Complete exact-resolution and error mapping read; tests and app callers continue to be audited.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQExT/632auWI