{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2469,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.990132789Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"fcc51810-36c4-5a45-8419-7c3608c15fe8","title":"[L307] E0 mandates immutable positive lifetime cycle and retention budgets","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L307.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/orchestration/peritus-orchestrator/src/limits.rs:22-46,116-150`; `src/binding.rs:71-102,151-173,231-247,291-342`; `src/state/counters.rs:21-34,61-81,131-137`; `src/state/mutation.rs:180-203`; `src/reducer.rs:68-95`; `src/reducer/apply/role_cycle.rs:39-45,323-350`; `src/reducer/apply/acceptance.rs:15-51` (all latter paths in the same crate).\n- **Limiter:** Twelve dimensions must be positive and stay below compiled maxima: revisions/writer/fixer cycles 256 each; gate/review cycles 1,024 each; handoffs/directives/cancellation reconciliations 4,096 each; retained observations 8,192; artifact references 1,024; event/checkpoint payloads 16 MiB minus the frame header each. Gate/review cycles also use the smaller immutable acceptance-contract ceiling. Genesis already consumes one revision and handoff. Limits participate in the binding digest; no unlimited representation or budget-changing command exists in the closed reducer dispatch.\n- **Consequence:** New role activation, revision advancement, handoff, and observation admission can return `LimitExceeded / NeedsHuman` solely because cumulative work reached a fixed count. Counters never reset or release capacity when work finishes. The reducer returns an error rather than automatically committing an Exhausted outcome or creating a durable continuation with the same authority and context.\n- **Repair direction:** Separate operational backpressure and bounded wire batches from lifetime work accounting. Persist unbounded logical progress using a versioned history/frontier representation and preserve context/authority across continuation. Any user-selected stopping policy should be explicit and optional.\n- **Evidence scope:** Complete source inspection, not a live-run reproduction. `src/product.rs:16-123` independently keeps choosing Accept or Fix at `u32::MAX`; these E0 quotas must not be attributed to that installed quality adapter without its actual aggregate caller.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMgG2ebZ8Au+I4GcOXGDRyWoTGnkSXeVpcYUbPdLEBFAh7fAjfNPdI/NT8bQWDnhHg7msCPRDRoRpvP0fwprrww="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2470,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.992276535Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"fcc51810-36c4-5a45-8419-7c3608c15fe8","comment_uuid":"b2c5b837-e77c-479e-8bc2-cdd641b3500e","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L307: E0 mandates immutable positive lifetime cycle and retention budgets.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/orchestration/peritus-orchestrator/src/limits.rs:22-46,116-150; src/binding.rs:71-102,151-173,231-247,291-342; src/state/counters.rs:21-34,61-81,131-137; src/state/mutation.rs:180-203; src/reducer.rs:68-95; src/reducer/apply/role_cycle.rs:39-45,323-350; src/reducer/apply/acceptance.rs:15-51; src/product.rs:16-123. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nSeparate operational backpressure and bounded wire batches from lifetime work accounting. Persist unbounded logical progress using a versioned history/frontier representation and preserve context/authority across continuation. Any user-selected stopping policy should be explicit and optional.\n\nPreserve: canonical digest and schema identity, shared writer/reader admissibility, malformed-input rejection before allocation, exact causal ordering, actual provider/OS capability boundaries and preserved accepted historical evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAN+QlvXy9sl9KVfCaPmMw7PkmE7Jmy+RocgxJXlEdZKLly+Kpa1nSDwz7rBsYarRYxMXNaB5oX4uX+0k25u+AU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2471,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.994436719Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"951596fb-3a0f-5f56-9bf8-f3b775dd0da2","title":"[L308] E0 cleanup consumes the same exhaustible budgets as normal work","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L308.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/orchestration/peritus-orchestrator/src/reducer/apply/directives.rs:15-42,45-94,143-163`; `src/reducer/apply.rs:15-21`; `src/reducer/apply/acceptance.rs:183-230,232-301,304-330`; `src/state/counters.rs:61-81`; `src/state/mutation.rs:180-203`; `src/reducer.rs:155-175`; `src/state/validation.rs:122-145`.\n- **Blocker:** Publishing a fresh child-cancel, pause, or resume directive increments the immutable child-directive counter. Cancellation reconciliation increments both cancellation-reconciliation and retained-observation counters. Every control command also appends a used command ID; the complete state requires at most 65,535 IDs. No capacity is reserved for settlement or control operations.\n- **Consequence:** At the directive ceiling, Cancel may commit but its needed CancelChildren publication fails. At the observation or cancellation-reconciliation ceiling, truthful child settlement cannot be admitted, so active children remain authoritative and Finalize cannot close the run. Reject/Fail/Exhaust cannot bypass reconciliation once Cancelling. At the command-history ceiling, even a zero-work control successor is rejected by final state validation. This is an accounting dead end, not proof that a child failed or that the user's task ended.\n- **Repair direction:** Give cancellation and authoritative settlement an independent durable path that remains admissible under workload backpressure. Store lifetime receipts in a versioned history rather than a bounded in-state vector. Preserve truthful child outcomes instead of skipping reconciliation or introducing another timer.\n- **Evidence scope:** Source-derived boundary behavior; no saturated aggregate was executed and no live lockup is attributed to this finding yet.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHQDZWIejDE0BPnJlhIGdk/FbPMG1Ec59J6GnNwjlSd0/7jkgU9hEGMXo/gQQ7X8I3/f6g4C28+jCC1ZOgCygAM="}
