{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2473,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.998767435Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"23497d7a-7835-5f1e-afc9-e915fb93ed87","title":"[L309] Every E0 directive requires a finite immutable delivery-attempt allowance","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L309.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/orchestration/peritus-orchestrator/src/directive.rs:171-219,318-345,366-385`; `src/reducer/apply/directives.rs:15-42`; `src/runtime/driver.rs:78-106`; `src/runtime/recovery.rs:109-149`; `src/durability.rs:278-299`; `src/durability/acknowledgement.rs:74-94`.\n- **Limiter:** A directive's `maximum_deliveries` is a positive `u16` (1 through 65,535), fixed in the durable payload. `mark_published` consumes the allowance before the external publisher is invoked. Reaching the count returns `LimitExceeded / NeedsHuman`. There is no unlimited value, reset/replenishment command, or replace-pending operation. The first publication also passes this finite allowance to C0's independently counted outbox delivery attempts (see L251/L264/L265).\n- **Consequence:** Transient delivery failures and restart boundaries can consume a finite retry policy while the same exact work remains unfinished. Recovery can classify a Published-but-Absent destination as Deliverable even though a new E0 publication is forbidden by its remaining allowance; a terminal/failed delivery is not automatically recorded by this helper. E0 publication and C0 claim counts are separate, so this does not establish that a crash before the first effect necessarily prevents the existing outbox row's first delivery.\n- **Repair direction:** Keep exact stable effect identity and reconciliation, but make stopping after transient delivery failures an explicit optional policy. Persist delivery outcomes separately from publication intent, and coordinate E0 recovery with C0's remaining authoritative delivery state rather than classifying deliverability without checking it.\n- **Evidence scope:** Complete directive, driver, durability and recovery source inspection; no exhausted outbox was executed during this audit.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLoYI2xKK1Ilfq28nRJvTL39ghubwsxKxxl2+jfB8jefL4O009v/60EIj0xrYkKtB2v3mqWtFflxYfJe5NkQlAY="}
