ild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAjrDrPbGLgrwz6EebqtpV9s2tsYR7E3kN9v8FAe/7dpY69xNt5+U03SvSskOtqlY+6AO+XWM1g5faehWRR9igk="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2475,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:21:38.003121258Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"4ae56008-1b49-58f8-8e74-3ce4b9aaf737","title":"[L310] Pausing with no active children creates an unrecoverable resume-in-progress state","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L310.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/orchestration/peritus-orchestrator/src/command/records.rs:63-114`; `src/state.rs:60-86`; `src/reducer/apply/acceptance.rs:150-180`; `src/reducer/apply.rs:29-41`; `src/reducer/apply/directives.rs:78-91,96-108`; `src/runtime/recovery.rs:36-62`; `src/integration_tests/cancellation.rs:14-97`.\n- **Blocker:** Genesis WriterPending has no active children. An empty child-head reconciliation is legal, so Pause commits it. Resume checks that paused and active child lists match (both empty), restores Active(WriterPending), and retains `paused_reconciliation`. The dispatch guard then admits only resume publications, acknowledgments, or Cancel. ResumeChildren requires an active paused destination; none exists. Only its acknowledgment clears the reconciliation, and none can be created.\n- **Consequence:** The source-derived legal sequence Start -> Pause(empty heads) -> Resume(same heads) permanently blocks StartWriter and normal lifecycle commands. The user can cancel the run, but cannot continue it in the same aggregate. The same empty-child issue applies to other phases before child activation. This is a state-transition defect and does not require a timeout, workload saturation, or a failed provider.\n- **Repair direction:** Complete the resume barrier immediately when no children require resumption. Define the barrier by remaining durable child acknowledgments and prove that every admitted paused state has a resumable successor, including zero children and a pending publication. Preserve exact child ownership and do not silently discard active work.\n- **Evidence scope:** Source-derived transition trace, not an executed regression test or live diagnosis. The fully read cancellation test activates three child domains before Pause and clears the flag through their acknowledgments; it does not cover Pause/Resume at genesis.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJYte4sJY9vAleljKtVnOJZ//CLdPokFSxA7BM3jASufOQMXB62UmAiTf4zXWIwoXN8D15VQpC5lLwgtM5DWUAw="}
