ted new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:37.467Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEjS07HJniMhM8qIiwhLKywqSj0i6kd+svE/CPg/N7TX2LkrK2J6VBbz/z1yg0YpEmLX3Q2Gk8cPT1yEosCJvAU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2493,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.682297535Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"4527858c-19cb-50b9-b792-6fdaef217a93","title":"[L170] Independent review receives a rolling, truncated command-observation window","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L170.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/developer_tools/evidence.rs:7-9,41-77,90-117`.\n- Command observations retain at most **32 records** and **128 KiB** of stored record text. Each request is previewed to **4 KiB** and its result to **12 KiB**; a truncation marker and framing are added outside those preview allowances. Older records are evicted when either aggregate ceiling is exceeded. Rendering adds labels outside the stored-byte accounting; cross-invocation merging keeps the last 128 KiB plus its omission marker.\n- Full JSON is serialized before taking the preview. Successful commands explicitly marked external_effect or verification are preserved in a separate unbounded vector, but that vector retains command text and purpose rather than the full observed output. Acceptance evidence therefore survives the rolling window while detailed output available to review can disappear.\n- This is an information-loss limiter, not a command timeout. Review evidence should retain durable result references and provide retrieval instead of relying on a lossy window. **Complete implementation and all inline tests read; tests not run and review-consumer retrieval still pending.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEdvY7jhIqK4C6KtYtY7MwON+2cpEQjjPo3qjiMuGucKfb3nbiWTbZQnyAuOqWYNAuSaS+LxNhYrxTCpkLwM9ww="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2494,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.686562826Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"4527858c-19cb-50b9-b792-6fdaef217a93","comment_uuid":"7322923b-4e61-4269-b9f7-dba021715c0c","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L170: Independent review receives a rolling, truncated command-observation window.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/developer_tools/evidence.rs:7-9,41-77,90-117. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nKeep exact command-result artifacts and indexed purpose/provenance receipts beyond the rolling review preview. Reviewer packets carry retrieval handles and explicit observed coverage, so every command relevant to acceptance can be inspected after window eviction. Stream preview construction and separate rendering bytes from durable evidence retention.\n\nPreserve: exact candidate revision and artifact binding, complete finding/provenance conservation, independent reviewer evidence, truthful gate outcomes, protected user constraints and acceptance fail-closed on invalid evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMHVBKlQ71OIguivhQhXkI0HncZm4mJb8LiueLc2nzEqi97INfKyGGv+Hm76eBPddMsFVDT4VIJz7fqdIZ+/VAU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2495,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.689100092Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"4cfd5033-4f0b-5554-9129-c367c2bb5584","title":"[L172] CSV validation has a fixed whole-file ceiling and a single mandatory dialect","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L172.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/gates/artifact_csv.rs:7,19-56,65-95,122-245`.\n- A selected changed CSV file above **64 MiB** fails validation before reading. Accepted files are read entirely into memory and parsed synchronously without cancellation, paging, or a caller-selected byte allowance. This is a synthetic artifact ceiling rather than a CSV format requirement.\n- The parser requires UTF-8, nonempty data, comma separators, double-quote escaping, and consistent field counts based on the first record. It tolerates blank lines/BOM and quoted newlines, but rejects variable-width rows, other delimiters, backslash-escaped quotes, or text following a closing quote. These are fixed gate policies whose appropriateness depends on the requested artifact contract; preserve requested structural correctness rather than blindly accepting malformed results.\n- `run` marks any selected file failure as exit 1 and continues checking the rest. Missing selected paths fail metadata inspection; whether deleted CSV paths reach this gate remains a caller question. **Implementation and all inline tests read; invocation policy and large-file failure not exercised.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAA