{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2497,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.693766405Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"055dada5-1625-5f0c-92d8-5cfdcbe37e52","title":"[L173] JSON and YAML structural validation reject files above 16 MiB","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L173.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/gates/json_structure.rs:7,19-48,57-72`; `gates/yaml_structure.rs:8,20-52,61-75`.\n- Each selected changed JSON/YAML file above **16 MiB** fails its gate regardless of valid syntax. Both implementations load and parse complete files synchronously, without cancellation or streamed validation. Neither exposes a policy knob or a retrieval/large-file alternative.\n- JSON builds a complete serde_json Value. YAML requires UTF-8 text and rejects an empty/whitespace-only file or a parser result with no documents. Those empty-file checks are fixed acceptance policy; appropriateness depends on the requested configuration contract. Any selected missing path is a failure, with deleted-file selection still to be traced.\n- A selected failure sets exit 1, but inspection continues for the remaining files. Syntax correctness is a real delivery requirement; the arbitrary size ceiling should be separated from it. **Full implementations and inline tests read, not run; gate selection pending.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDT9rwurQSXGmh6vmBUt802NkbEit1/DHJDc67h4IBJ7itr2DQqB/xzO7s/WXkOjM+t6+Tb3/A5h6ob47Rg3cQ8="}
