{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2499,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.698779013Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"0f50f468-e595-5983-a00f-40f7192bd82f","title":"[L174] SQLite qualification fixes file size, workspace shape, and repeatability policy","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L174.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/gates/sqlite_migration.rs:8,27-66,76-101`.\n- SQL files are capped at **16 MiB** and read fully as UTF-8. Qualification always starts with an in-memory database, requires `schema.sql` and exactly the conventional `migration.sql`, then executes the migration **twice** against the same database. A valid one-time migration such as CREATE TABLE without IF NOT EXISTS fails the second pass; the inline test explicitly demands that failure.\n- Optional `postcheck.sql` and `rollback.sql` are executed afterward. Query rows from postcheck are not interpreted as assertions. Foreign-key violations fail after each migration and rollback; no generic transaction, interruption/progress hook, or caller-selected repeatability policy appears here.\n- The size and filename/repeatability constraints are hard-coded gate admission policies, not elapsed deadlines. Whether idempotence is required must come from the requested task rather than the generic SQLite project kind. **Complete source and tests read; host selection and affected real tasks not exercised.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOpBxqSABLiryJsPjFvp6JaCkHC94HtuU8fVlX+