{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2503,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.707742661Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"1ae46c72-0073-5544-ae01-1a4a8635dcf6","title":"[L176] Deterministic output gates turn limited language heuristics into hard delivery requirements","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L176.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/src/gates/explicit_paths.rs:198-266`; `explicit_paths/extraction.rs:22-118`; `explicit_paths/language.rs:5-66,86-140`; `explicit_paths/alternatives.rs:7-43`.\n- Output recognition only considers the previous **12 words** in a clause, negation within **2 words** before the output verb, and naming nouns within **6 words**. Single-file recognition uses a **6-word** verb window and a **4-word** negation window. These fixed language windows can miss long instructions or negate them incorrectly; gate failures are then decisive rather than advisory.\n- Extraction splits every line on whitespace, including quoted paths containing spaces. Parsing strips terminal periods and delimiter punctuation, ignores paths containing *, $, = or unresolved placeholder brackets, requires absolute paths to be under the exact root, and recognizes a fixed English verb/noun/conditional vocabulary. These rules are interpretation constraints, not filesystem capacity or user-selected limits.\n- Presence checks treat any symlink_metadata success as present without establishing file kind. Chronological reduction understands explicit removal and recreation, alternatives, and output-list indentation, but the single-file flag is true if any historical line matches; there is no later explicit relaxation of that flag in this implementation. Supersession depends on the supplied task history and remains to be traced.\n- Preserve actual user requirements and path authority. A structured current contract should determine hard delivery gates; heuristic interpretation uncertainty should be recoverable rather than inventing obligations. **All implementation files and contextual-language tests read; untested edge-case risks, not demonstrated failures.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFj9gxP+snord+kY08D9KgkqH6o5eeOZAWw7sZ4meyYyQ/2Iijmm6/STb5r7e/AmycdWvr1RI5EF2O+GxESnlA8="}
