{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2511,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.725806556Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"2b5aa84d-7d55-534b-8909-57a37d33ff9d","title":"[L180] Durable request admission caps the entire serialized model request at 16 MiB","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L180.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_control/inputs/archive.rs:69-143,175-237`; `inputs/files.rs:7-61`; `inputs/manifest.rs:59-84`.\n- After context capture, request archival applies another **16 MiB ceiling to the complete canonical ModelRequest**, including message encoding, media, tool definitions and other request metadata. A text/media selection admitted by its separate raw-byte limits can still fail at this enclosing representation bound. InvalidLimit is mapped to Capacity; other encoding failures become InvalidInput.\n- The immutable manifest has its own journal state-byte ceiling, schema version **1**, deny_unknown_fields, at most **4 brief bindings**, protocol message limits, source input size **1–8,192 bytes**, existing image selection bounds and guidance-render bounds. No version migration or segmented request archive is present in these files. These are persisted data envelopes; they must not become an unexplained lifetime cutoff.\n- File references are loaded from immutable authenticated artifacts and JSON-wrapped with source/version/digest/range fields; the wrapper also has a 16 MiB aggregate check. Included images must exactly match the request image sequence, and file/guidance text must be present before incorporation. Those are provenance checks, separate from artificial capacity policy.\n- **Complete source read; exact encoded overhead for a maximum attachment selection has not been measured.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_