tion must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPpFPVoMsNV3V2e00tQFRNqVRV7JpOiorUDhOFJz+cxgydXMQ3RYdEEwVKLxYg/W6/eeWH8F8BC8Odfk844JMAo="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2513,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.730700493Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"0e78d96c-098d-5844-bd14-daabf54c276e","title":"[L181] Restart invalidates execution-qualified candidates without comparing current execution facts","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L181.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_run/recovery.rs:17-98,109-178`.\n- Startup reconciliation examines terminal, uncommitted, undiscarded candidates. It re-observes repository and source digests, but **any retained execution_digest being Some is itself sufficient to mark the candidate stale**, even when those other digests match. No current execution-context comparison appears here.\n- Reconciliation preserves historical evidence and exported patches, advances the checkpoint identity and marks qualification for reacquisition. A qualified but uncommitted candidate can therefore lose actionable status simply through restart. This is a freshness policy rather than elapsed expiration; an actual change in observed execution dependencies must be distinguished from an unobserved assumption.\n- Missing configuration or inaccessible candidate facts marks actions unavailable and requests workspace access restoration; it does not discard the evidence. **Complete source read; repeated gate execution after a real restart not reproduced.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMJ1Sk7dndgS5sjMVV4hSb/MK/1ISxpaFHPnYO1NONCEzxmBz9bjpHcNqqS8QYtXx0K2/Br+6