{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2514,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.732906935Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"0e78d96c-098d-5844-bd14-daabf54c276e","comment_uuid":"4234b4ea-726d-4ed7-b713-518c1ef31944","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L181: Restart invalidates execution-qualified candidates without comparing current execution facts.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_run/recovery.rs:17-98,109-178. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nReobserve and compare actual execution-context dependencies against the recorded digest before invalidating a candidate on restart. Record unavailable facts as an explicit requalification obligation and preserve still-valid evidence. Mere presence of a historical execution digest must not stale unchanged artifacts or force all gates to run again.\n\nPreserve: exact candidate revision and artifact binding, complete finding/provenance conservation, independent reviewer evidence, truthful gate outcomes, protected user constraints and acceptance fail-closed on invalid evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBzaeey680iUC8gxEZr0Y/AE0yMZ+TnWyReOc/1IT4LoQwFnCK/vCxXMHKGz/Z3AyimS8w8/ln5XW9+vNEeE8gM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2515,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.735182255Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"7b5a7b8c-1ae3-52b1-a6b3-5532021fdb13","title":"[L182] Shutdown uses a finite join allowance and marks recovery without proving every task has stopped","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L182.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_run/lifecycle.rs:20-71`.\n- The caller supplies a shutdown timeout, applied separately to every drained task. The timeout result is ignored, and this method contains no explicit abort-and-join or native-owner reconciliation after an expired wait. It then marks an originally interrupted non-user-cancelled run RecoveryRequired unless its phase is Complete, and ignores persistence errors during these status updates.\n- This timeout is a shutdown coordination allowance, **not an ordinary active session lifetime**. The defect risk is interpreting a failed join as settled ownership: the subsequent projection can offer unknown-outcome acknowledgement based on terminal phase, while this method has not established that the original effect owner is inactive.\n- Cancellation is requested before joins. Whether a particular tool can outlive that request depends on its owner/cancellation implementation and the daemon shutdown caller. **Source-confirmed missing join-result handling; active-effect race is an inference requiring reproduction and caller tracing.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFcVLdgaEL9TF