{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2516,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.737680102Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"7b5a7b8c-1ae3-52b1-a6b3-5532021fdb13","comment_uuid":"4e91001d-51e1-41b0-9f30-7a1c0b57634c","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L182: Shutdown uses a finite join allowance and marks recovery without proving every task has stopped.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_run/lifecycle.rs:20-71. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nModel shutdown as durable detach/cancel and effect reconciliation, with explicit join outcomes and retained ownership. A join allowance ending cannot prove inactivity or permit unknown-outcome acknowledgement; keep the unresolved task visible until the real owner stops or is adopted. Persist shutdown progress/errors and preserve live native context through a restart attachment.\n\nPreserve: canonical digest and schema identity, shared writer/reader admissibility, malformed-input rejection before allocation, exact causal ordering, actual provider/OS capability boundaries and preserved accepted historical evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDLgnmYOyLfX2SpO8JXCZBAiEjK97CSOxyzSkMgrqh3GWnnTHlOOpi0JjftUdY7iTvJjQwRgAuZMT4+ixvXvIgA="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2517,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.739984164Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"ddea4a0b-b277-5c86-9192-7e4da59902bf","title":"[L183] Unknown command projection blocks retry and delivery controls without native outcome reconciliation","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L183.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_run/operation.rs:31-65,68-183`; `workbench/run_control.rs:53-87`.\n- Public projection reads the entire effect ledger and gives unresolved commands priority over execution and deliverable state. A Started receipt with a nonterminal run phase permits only Cancel. Every other unresolved command permits only Acknowledge; Retry, Export, Commit and Discard are omitted by this early return, even if a separate candidate exists.\n- Acknowledgement validates that projection, appends Reviewed, and retains the explicit unknown-outcome mutation freeze. The inactive-owner proof is **the run phase**, not a C2 process/command ownership lookup in these methods. This meets the projection's state contract but leaves the shutdown proof gap in L182 unresolved.\n- Each control legality check and diagnostic projection reloads/decodes the receipt history under the run records lock. Oversized/corrupt ledger inspection errors abort the projection and authenticated control before their actions. A valid ledger at its append ceiling can still permit dashboard Cancel, which bypasses receipt append; Acknowledge needs another receipt and remains subject to L165.\n- Preserve no-duplicate-effect protection while adding durable command identity/outcome reconciliation and a repair projection. **Full caller/source read; no end-to-end lockup or liveness race reproduced.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPWVhLmWZjpyaGCfnbRPrGNzlnCl9wyOZWAHvx2hK8DsnrFP8WEhh6kEXGDs9tuYIRgM+wmmgLlZDcRADOnbSAE="}
