evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQD60TxhNjI99dBalsDRzAazckC+Ja7h3i2t+/poJakw4R757gj7h1b+yN/sBZWmmiDIdcQ5SXbprv5fcpAxA7Q4="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2519,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.745147866Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"9bb7926d-21e2-5556-84d6-a942c8df1837","title":"[L184] The complete persisted run record is capped at 16 MiB and crossing it cancels live work","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L184.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_run/persistence.rs:53-92`; `persistence/workbench.rs:13,37-74`.\n- Every update constructs and pretty-serializes the entire run projection before applying a fixed **16 MiB record ceiling**. Persistence failure records a failure marker, sets the run cancellation flag and cancels the provider token. The same ceiling rejects an existing run file during startup and moves it to quarantine.\n- This is a lifetime-growth limiter on persistent state. `persistence/types.rs:9-44` and `record.rs:14-82` confirm that snapshot diff/gates/review/summary, finding_state, full encoded continuation, task baseline, preview page/operations/output and interaction state all share this record. Resume and preview wire bytes are Vec<u8> values serialized as JSON arrays, so enclosing pretty JSON expands their byte representation beyond the original encoded size. There is no paging/segmented-record mechanism or configurable lifetime allowance here; exact worst-case expansion has not been measured.\n- Writes use a synced temporary file, rename, and Unix directory sync. Isolation preserves files rather than deleting them, but removes them from ordinary loaded run projections. **Complete persistence and startup loader read; no maximum-size live record constructed.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPYlc2tqiWdjMiF8XHdKLuSJxXdgrLwFK5kYeLBj3uQlm3gG50f2ZPi/G5Z1bgxv2JI36h2XTzCoSmuL4jQaQQU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2520,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.747337183Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"9bb7926d-21e2-5556-84d6-a942c8df1837","comment_uuid":"0a92584c-62c6-4ef8-b319-b8df22cfd358","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L184: The complete persisted run record is capped at 16 MiB and crossing it cancels live work.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_run/persistence.rs:53-92; persistence/workbench.rs:13,37-74; persistence/types.rs:9-44; record.rs:14-82. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nReplace the whole pretty-JSON run file with an append-only durable event/receipt journal and paged projection checkpoints referencing large continuation, diff and output artifacts. Keep task/native context identity independent of projection byte size. Presentation growth or a recoverable storage write failure must create a resumable persistence obligation rather than cancel the provider or quarantine a valid run as too large.\n\nPreserve: committed command/event identity, exact causal and digest roots, exclusive ownership, atomic publication, reference-safe artifact retention and verified recovery from the last durable frontier. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQB+Mhm/mNI5AT5vNg3xh83dm0s7ZY9NOiqrpH+JT0bcxoWHyP15nX/QplFk2aerL3i//NVWVNH1Ms9/GoZScwgE="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2521,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.749321617Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"978e1637-2cc6-5c34-9836-c1c3080c48ea","title":"[L185] Recovery depends on admitting the current full context, and ordinary quarantined executions are not retried by the loader","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L185.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_run/persistence/workbench.rs:15-38,76-125,161-194,216-242`.\n- For every accepted start, startup invokes ControlStore.capture_execution before reconstructing the run. A current conversation/context/attachment admission failure—including the quotas in L157/L162—quarantines the run projection instead of retaining a visible blocked run. Persisted run recovery therefore depends on the latest full context being admissible, not just the saved execution boundary.\n- Quarantine scanning only republishes records with a **StartGoal** operation. An ordinary StartExecution record already in quarantine is skipped even after its cause is corrected. Governing control receipts remain enforced; opening the generation never automatically launches a staged or admitted run.\n- If reading the projection directory itself fails, projection_paths silently returns an empty list. Entry failures are logged and skipped. This can produce an empty loaded run inventory despite retained files; it is a recovery/visibility defect, not evidence that data was deleted.\n- Exact control receipts, identity/fence checks and valid resume provenance should be preserved. Unavailable/oversized current views need an explicit retained repair state rather than making the old run vanish. **Source-confirmed paths; a restart-induced quarantine disappearance has not been reproduced in this audit.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQE/I9EV++S1CQlUvW5K4wNAC/sGyNX01DwVGdx0j3SM9zAUJ1POhSOzswcPS2O6o7NjNcwKNG1D1S8nLwrQp3Q0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2522,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.752177379Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"978e1637-2cc6-5c34-9836-c1c3080c48ea","comment_uuid":"039ada6c-6ffb-4587-83d8-7fde1d0ead11","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L185: Recovery depends on admitting the current full context, and ordinary quarantined executions are not retried by the loader.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_run/persistence/workbench.rs:15-38,76-125,161-194,216-242. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nRecover from the saved accepted execution boundary and exact control receipt before assembling a fresh model view. Retain unavailable contexts as visible blocked runs with retryable repair for both StartGoal and ordinary StartExecution. Enumerate quarantined/incompatible evidence without silently dropping the inventory, and reconcile the same native/task identity once the cause is corrected.\n\nPreserve: governing inputs, complete pending tool protocol pairs, exact source/lineage references, explicit permissions, unresolved effect truth and task-role/native-provider identity. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long productive read/write sessions through repeated compaction and segment boundaries, source/dependency changes, non-ASCII and large evidence, interrupted checkpoint publication, then reopen the same lineage and prove that valid grounding is reused and stale targets are reread. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKFu3+y6ZQ3yf85jFlmGtQv/uxgdiHalnxpDPJPlntZljbGOer3NYm4lxb382/v+EUg8nVCLASaaYT2csAltBws="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2523,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.754380166Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"5e60ed26-6542-59ee-a4d4-1f268d8a0d9f","title":"[L186] Run persistence accepts only format 6 and requires full governed context even for terminal records","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L186.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_run/persistence/types.rs:7-44`; `persistence/record.rs:11,89-173`; `persistence/interaction.rs:15-104`.\n- Rehydration rejects every format_version other than **6**, with deny_unknown_fields on the enclosing record and interaction. This converter has no older-version migration or incompatible-state projection; the loader routes such failures to quarantine. Whether an earlier startup migration covers historical release records remains pending.\n- Every record requires governed context, even terminal records without a continuation. Resumable records additionally decode their retained continuation against that current context and exact checkpoint/run/workspace lineage. Active phases become RecoveryRequired on restart rather than automatically relaunching an indeterminate effect; user-cancelled active phases become Cancelled.\n- The interaction restores at most the protocol activity window (L025), strictly increasing sequences, fixed three roles and supported mode/effort tags. Legacy provider deadline data is accepted by the progress schema but retained as an ignored compatibility field rather than a clock.\n- Retaining authority and avoiding duplicate effects are necessary. Schema evolution and historical context unavailable at startup need explicit recovery states rather than silent session disappearance. **Complete conversion/schema source read; upgrade fixture and broader startup migration not inspected yet.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGbUSUr8fKPHgCf3de0ezBDi80oCwA1ldTIES1+yBYS5ph1IoGa+jpZhpj1BrV9cc25J54wDt1FBt5qm448y1Qg="}
