{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2525,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.758829601Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"4c52a349-bef6-579a-8566-38174685d2fa","title":"[L187] The staged-start recovery projection is unreachable when the start receipt is absent","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L187.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_run/persistence/workbench.rs:85-125,143-159`; `persistence/record.rs:160`.\n- An unaccepted start produces no CapturedConversation. The loader passes None as governed context into into_record_with_context, which unconditionally rejects None. It then quarantines/continues before reaching the later intended \"Start intent was not committed; retry the exact original operation\" projection.\n- This is a source-confirmed recovery contradiction: staged execution must remain unprivileged and visible, but its rehydration currently requires authority-bound context that is only supplied after acceptance. It is not a timeout or proof that the provider executed anything.\n- An exact authenticated start operation may still be resubmitted through other host code; that caller path remains pending. **Both full files read; absent-receipt restart fixture not executed.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNjIlchuUbWr8nz1FPCTcm5ixURi3rx0vzAMwuE2vCAGQavJNUMde3R25GAJWGaBJtYsKb3bwDP1jx5+4YtXwAQ="}
