{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2535,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.781261832Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"a221022d-cbc9-5e61-a5e8-8e4ebc067eb9","title":"[L192] Preview capture has a 16 MiB PNG ceiling and only an X11/ImageMagick backend","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L192.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_run/workbench/launch.rs:47`; `launch/capture.rs:74-139,154-172,271-302,321-344`.\n- Capture requires DISPLAY, a PATH-discovered ImageMagick import executable, an exact preview runtime and an explicitly consented X11 window target. Other native capture surfaces are unavailable in this implementation. The helper is untimed; it executes synchronously through the owned command runtime before the async publication stage.\n- A resulting PNG must be nonempty, regular and at most **16 MiB**. It is then fully loaded and decoded without the product attachment module's explicit dimension/frame/decoded-memory guard. Rejected oversize/helper-failure paths do not reach the temporary-file cleanup. This cap is synthetic capture admission, not session expiration.\n- Upload metadata prefers **64 KiB chunks** or the negotiated smaller maximum; actual chunk iteration uses the negotiated maximum. Ordinal/offset overflow is checked. Consent, exact target and artifact actor/session/scope remain necessary authority boundaries.\n- Failed artifact publication is ignored by the Ok-only branch after admission; the retained capture stays Failed/unobserved and exact retry only replays admission/qualification. **Complete capture source read; protocol capture bounds, artifact limits and backend failure tests pending.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8e