{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2539,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.789868387Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"a8734b0f-cd23-5344-8182-4468b78a322c","title":"[L194] Host Network availability is inferred from provider configuration, and previews require it unconditionally","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L194.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_run/permissions.rs:21-54,191-211,244-263`.\n- The host permission catalog exposes Network whenever the provider map is nonempty, without examining provider locality or the network requirements of a particular tool. StartPreview, InteractPreview and CapturePreview all request Read, Write, Process and Network; StopPreview and behavior/feedback controls request no tool permission set. This confirms L190's blanket Network requirement for local preview actions.\n- Current authority is the intersection of host availability, durable workspace policy and branch policy. Every provider/tool boundary reloads that policy under the shared controls mutex. Read-only branch restrictions and actor/scope checks are deliberate authority constraints; provider-map coupling and blanket preview capability selection are separate admission policies.\n- **Complete source and inline permission tests read; no provider-empty/local-preview reproduction.** No synthetic elapsed limit occurs in this file.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBlNcj0pjTVslJd1mRCUt9QacBrR2yZJOiMryIJm70xLFMvBYMamNyXlpQK6Vrq6nAT6cW9X58QUw