{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2540,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.792157626Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"a8734b0f-cd23-5344-8182-4468b78a322c","comment_uuid":"071680fd-305f-4efe-bd6e-f5c2388b4b66","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L194: Host Network availability is inferred from provider configuration, and previews require it unconditionally.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_run/permissions.rs:21-54,191-211,244-263. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nSeparate host network capability, provider connectivity and preview command permission. Select confinement and required grants from the actual launch plan, including fully local previews without Network. Keep network access explicit and test that an online provider configuration does not grant unrelated host network authority.\n\nPreserve: definitely-unaccepted versus ambiguously-accepted request state, exact native thread/profile identity, ordered provider observations, tool-result protocol, explicit cancellation and real provider/model capabilities. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKq78clWt1hkWzK3P24/4s9uJNbTCehh1YxVG2c1Zvv3B0y7fLfALLRynUeXP3Sc4AZkU1kIBkVNdt0+VfUBngs="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2541,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.794431938Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"20ab4104-29c9-5280-b157-a7bdae34bca2","title":"[L195] Guidance identities accumulate in a single 16 MiB catalog, including forgotten records","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L195.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_control/guidance.rs:24-25,79-108,153-219,244-343`.\n- Guidance storage uses schema version **1** and the journal's **16 MiB** maximum state size. Saving inserts an identity into a sorted catalog; forgetting writes a content-free slot and tombstone but does not remove the identity. Each subsequent mutation clones and rewrites that entire catalog through bounded StateInstall admission.\n- The identity count therefore has a lifetime encoded-size ceiling. Forgetting cannot shrink this catalog, and once it cannot be installed, even another forget/revise/pin/scope mutation needs the same oversized catalog write. No catalog segmentation, paging, metadata retirement or version migration appears in this file. Per-guidance content/rendering limits and stored codec details remain to be inspected.\n- Canonical storage, monotonic revisions, tombstone dominance and refusal to reactivate forgotten guidance are integrity requirements, not session expiration. Catalog replay rejects unsupported schema/noncanonical state; error mapping turns LimitExceeded into Capacity and most other application validation errors into InvalidInput.\n- **Complete source read; capacity failure not reproduced.** The 16 MiB threshold is encoded bytes, not a measured maximum guidance count.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPPENouUBqhQEeFm+LStmXy9XFi0iXW629xNGnLAhW2JRxYZJgekz669ZGEcfsWYdBfQY4oDJmTA5RVK7mMyag8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2542,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.797184436Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"20ab4104-29c9-5280-b157-a7bdae34bca2","comment_uuid":"83b6f1cf-9892-4b89-93df-13013996728a","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L195: Guidance identities accumulate in a single 16 MiB catalog, including forgotten records.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_control/guidance.rs:24-25,79-108,153-219,244-343. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nKeep guidance identities/revisions in segmented immutable history with an indexed active catalog. Forgetting removes active eligibility through a durable disposition while preserving provenance; it must not continue charging all historical text to one catalog frame. Share migration and exact guidance scope across readers and writers.\n\nPreserve: durable logical session and run identity, exact command receipts, atomic snapshot/cursor binding, explicit authority, selected UI state, complete history retrieval and owned-effect reconciliation. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large histories and non-ASCII fields, queue/connection pressure, delayed acknowledgements, subscription gaps, disconnect/reconnect and daemon restart, proving snapshot recovery, preserved selection/context, responsive controls and no duplicate command. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQH1NRZgAYGzAMf7OLCMcxJzuFUs/1ALoOcD29G/iLVK1C1hr/zqV0t9coaspXIC1S1C2R2V/JJzo94qER4xOrws="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2543,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.799532015Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"366a538f-406f-5695-85f8-a5573da0c2ac","title":"[L196] Guidance paging follows full replay, and all eligible guidance must fit a 64 KiB request block","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L196.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_control/storage/guidance.rs:52-98,116-144`; `crates/app/peritus-app-protocol/src/workbench/memory.rs:16-23`; `memory/render.rs:61-129,183-192`.\n- Inspection allocates and validates every catalog identity before scope/forgotten filtering and before returning a **32-row page**. Missing/corrupt state for an invisible or forgotten record aborts the query; changing the page offset cannot avoid it. Row totals/offsets are u32/usize checked, while actor/workspace authorization is required.\n- Future-request capture similarly rebuilds all catalog rows, filters eligible active guidance and renders all selected records. Exact rendered text, provenance framing and escapes must fit **64 KiB**; overflow fails the entire render and the daemon maps that failure to InvalidInput. Pinning affects ordering, not selection or size. There is no overflow selection/compaction branch in these files. The declaration's comment mentions a row limit for rendering, but the renderer itself enforces bytes rather than the inspection page's 32-row count.\n- Each guidance text is limited to **8 KiB**, each forget reason to **1 KiB** (also L156); newline, tab, quote and backslash escaping can expand accepted raw text. All storage DTOs deny unknown fields and require schema 1 without a compatibility decoder (extends L195). The reopen test verifies forgotten identity retention and immutable audit content, but does not test capacity/replay-isolation failures.\n- **All named implementation files and guidance reopen test fully read; no new tests executed.** Numeric bounds and full-scan behavior are confirmed; latency and end-to-end failure remain unmeasured.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHzmrADLoreplGwzHRJfxL128lhkjLu8Q20q06dF1wlJQmv7DBRxs5dZFSmLfGDf1L/xDQcUQYCmCsJ0KayRAQ8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2544,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.801665830Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"366a538f-406f-5695-85f8-a5573da0c2ac","comment_uuid":"32a28e00-68b3-46d8-89bc-1f7cb2feafd1","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L196: Guidance paging follows full replay, and all eligible guidance must fit a 64 KiB request block.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_control/storage/guidance.rs:52-98,116-144; crates/app/peritus-app-protocol/src/workbench/memory.rs:16-23; memory/render.rs:61-129,183-192. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nPage guidance from an indexed verified frontier and select a bounded request block with exact retrieval handles for remaining eligible guidance. Mandatory governing clauses retain a typed selection obligation if actual model capacity cannot fit them. Avoid replaying the complete archive before each page or requiring all history in a fixed 64 KiB wrapper.\n\nPreserve: committed command/event identity, exact causal and digest roots, exclusive ownership, atomic publication, reference-safe artifact retention and verified recovery from the last durable frontier. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDLSjA2N59aIjj7GQqw+HtKrEb7og6259NzMDui9ylrDDTrs1K1gVglTGbLYV106PcbxaKN1K42ujcVzGKUXzgQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2545,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.803867927Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"374e9e06-11d5-540a-8c51-2d9f718b0bea","title":"[L197] Any unresolved native process record puts the entire daemon in read-only mode","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L197.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/startup/recovery.rs:63-94`; `startup/runtime/runner.rs:105-151,191-202`.\n- Startup reconciles the complete process registry and combines every Indeterminate disposition and quarantined record. A nonzero total marks the daemon lifecycle read-only and prevents the outbox runtime from starting, without selecting the affected workspace/run. This is a global recovery barrier, not an elapsed deadline. Exact native ownership reconciliation is necessary; the global scope and operator-only diagnostic need separate evaluation.\n- Product-run records are opened before this native-process reconciliation. The startup migration path handles the journal database, then ProductRunService opens the retained run files directly; no product-run schema compatibility adapter is inserted here (extends L183/L186). Linux selects the optional configured crash watchdog; absence uses the ordinary ProcessStore path. Watchdog configuration/default selection remains pending.\n- Application command recovery repeatedly reads **4,096-row batches until empty**; 4,096 is a page size rather than a lifetime recovery ceiling. DefinitelyAbsent durable domain operations are settled as UnsupportedFamily; conflicting request identities abort startup. No finite retry count or startup timer appears in these files.\n- **Full startup composition and recovery read; no mixed-workspace unresolved-process test run.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-