{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2549,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.813173328Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"81de4d31-d08d-5f85-9436-7044098b6d75","title":"[L199] Shutdown applies finite join bounds separately, while product-run cleanup failures are not counted","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L199.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/startup/runtime/teardown.rs:23-43,127-175,178-205`; `product_run/lifecycle.rs` (L182).\n- A configured shutdown-millis duration is passed separately to outbox, product runs and supervised workers, then used for authority and endpoint-server joins. Authority timeout aborts its task; server timeout aborts and joins it. These are cleanup deadlines rather than ordinary session lifetimes. Earlier product-run cleanup ignores each timed join result and persistence failure; its unit return value cannot feed this caller's indeterminate-effects accounting.\n- Several preceding authority/control/event deliveries are awaited without a timeout in this caller, so the finite join duration is not an overall wall-clock shutdown bound. The result is computed and ShutdownComplete can be delivered before the endpoint-server join, which can still return UncleanShutdown afterward.\n- Remaining outbox work is supplied as zero to every recorded stage here; cleanup errors add a generic indeterminate count. Exact native-process and terminal ownership are reconciled later. **Full source read; duration default/validation and worker shutdown implementation pending, no hang/outcome-order test run.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3g