 and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGlwal0DJmPObRcNfdJdsYc134Pyhyagz4DhqVE7hDan8b8N8lMwYVUW/uW4u+FQPI7fNYbXOT9wK3DgiyUD3AA="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2553,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.823125655Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"9badbc1b-147e-5fdb-ac62-004b13346001","title":"[L201] An isolated writable fork without a goal can be created but cannot start execution","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L201.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_run/workbench/fork.rs:102-144,172-217`; `workbench/execution.rs:40-47,90-123`.\n- Fork governance explicitly permits an ungoverned parent and historical revision with goal_revision zero. The branch constructor preserves that zero for either fork mode. Execution admission permits ReadOnlyCurrentWorkspace plus zero plus StartExecution in Chat mode, but has no corresponding IsolatedWritableWorkspace/zero/StartExecution case; its fallback returns false. StartGoal on that zero-revision branch also fails. Thus an otherwise valid isolated writable ungoverned child is created with no admitted start intent through this matcher.\n- Governed branches additionally require the initial objective and criteria to equal the retained branch contract; read-only children permit only Chat. Read-only authority and exact lineage are necessary boundaries. The missing ungoverned writable case is separate from those constraints.\n- Fork workspaces must already exist in the configured catalog, differ for writable mode and have canonical roots that do not contain each other. Exact checkpoint/reference and source revision checks preserve provenance. **Full fork/start implementation and inline read-only branch tests read; no writable zero-goal integration reproduction yet.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oI