ether; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOlEfBMRCVl4kejBYQZSwVSBWHdSdo+uMb4T1eS47sQRarxI5crQYieEoDimWJGGq55Jhp0+p1vEXTElGRsTyQk="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2555,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.827443152Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"b2991773-e8ef-5090-bdce-8ef9ae4885a0","title":"[L202] Daemon configuration hard-caps queues, connections, workers and shutdown duration","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L202.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/config.rs:65-149`; `config/deserialize.rs:58-91`; `startup/runtime/runner.rs:84-89,135-164`.\n- Default capacities are **1,024 authority requests**, **256 per-connection requests**, **64 connections** and **32 workers**. Config validation imposes absolute maxima **65,536 / 4,096 / 1,024 / 1,024**, respectively, and rejects zero. The configured worker ceiling is narrower than the supervisor's 4,096 constructor maximum (L200). Connection-queue enforcement/selection remains pending in IPC.\n- Default artifact admission is **1 GiB per artifact / 64 GiB total logical quota**; both must be positive, maximum artifact cannot exceed quota, and quota cannot exceed i64::MAX. These daemon-store bounds differ from the local-context-store limits in L057. Artifact quota recovery/retirement callers remain pending.\n- Shutdown defaults to **30 seconds**, must be positive and cannot exceed **600,000 ms**. There is no unbounded/disabled shutdown choice in this configuration, even though ordinary product requests are untimed. Startup forwards this duration to worker/outbox/product cleanup (L199/L200).\n- Omitted limits use all production defaults; a supplied limits object has required fields and denies unknown fields. Configuration schema is exactly **version 1**. **All declarations/validation/caller lines read; no saturation tests run.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDJxOP0F5J0fJcsAQ2Bw/iZfVCEKHJ0hHyMTv/cXRLlhZMNqdureKRhHLZALCAVDwr0Iy4ghTFMuCEtgsUsgyA8="}
