{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2557,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.832116696Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"38081c58-5e85-5358-84c9-75ecf857add1","title":"[L203] Configuration limits project/workspace/provider/tool/direct-folder inventories and fixes storage layout","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L203.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/config/catalog.rs:14-16,117-165`; `config/folder.rs:45-77`; `config/paths.rs:93-125`; `config/provider.rs:21-22,247-328`.\n- Admission permits at most **1,024 projects**, **4,096 managed workspace declarations**, **256 tool names**, **256 provider routes**, **32 direct folders** and **16 protected paths per direct folder**. Tool names are at most **128 bytes** and use a closed ASCII alphabet; profile capability names are closed to 18 recognized values, with duplicates rejected. These are configured inventory ceilings rather than session timers.\n- All protected component roots must be distinct nonoverlapping descendants of state_root. Runtime additionally rejects symlink/alias roots and protects them with 0700 on Unix. Registration paths must be unique absolute normalized paths; direct folders retain exact observed directory identity and require reselect/trust when it changes. These identity and protection checks are authority boundaries, while fixed inventory maxima and single-parent layout constrain deployment choices.\n- Provider kind constrains accepted endpoint/credential/executable fields; first-party OpenAI endpoint override is rejected, and noncompatible provider-name overrides are rejected. Explicit route/profile identity conflicts fail validation. **Full config files read; inventory-cap and custom-layout behavior not exercised.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18