{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2558,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.834894617Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"38081c58-5e85-5358-84c9-75ecf857add1","comment_uuid":"e53ff527-66cd-449b-859e-5435e8db63ef","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L203: Configuration limits project/workspace/provider/tool/direct-folder inventories and fixes storage layout.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/config/catalog.rs:14-16,117-165; config/folder.rs:45-77; config/paths.rs:93-125; config/provider.rs:21-22,247-328. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nStore project/workspace/provider/tool/direct-folder registries as indexed paged catalogs and negotiate backend-supported inventories. Separate storage location/ownership from an incidental fixed layout, with explicit migration/adoption under the same identities. Preserve protected roots, credential scopes and unique registration bindings while removing lifetime catalog caps.\n\nPreserve: definitely-unaccepted versus ambiguously-accepted request state, exact native thread/profile identity, ordered provider observations, tool-result protocol, explicit cancellation and real provider/model capabilities. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQH7ippA60PYkGpt40eGqKhGc3POveXvzA5dBYmpNL27+HkaLFJshqDL+ZTcE/7HVIzlPSCgS7OceoGeDv/Fr1gw="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2559,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.837166978Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"aa3669dc-f8be-5f16-af1a-73eeeee47576","title":"[L204] Explicit fully-offline mode admits only literal-loopback compatible HTTP routes","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L204.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/config/context.rs:31-44,93-114`; `config/provider/locality.rs:5-13`.\n- Fully-offline mode rejects automatic provider failover and any configured route other than CompatibleResponses/CompatibleChatCompletions with a literal loopback endpoint. Even localhost by DNS, first-party routes pointed at loopback and native Codex/Claude routes fail this validation. An unused remote route also prevents startup in that mode.\n- This is an explicitly selected offline guarantee rather than a hidden deadline. Literal address checks avoid treating DNS or a subprocess as proof of offline inference; any broader admission needs equivalent network confinement. Local context is default-enabled, but fully_offline defaults false. **Full implementation and inline validation tests read; tests not run.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLGjDWi3bZpAwjShoapkMXLyFMPJko1kPk8x5CJ3mOJ7l+gqywiIR6SlD1UFbZLmH015pF1RAsy+eLxi9k8B1gc="}
