{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2561,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.842827041Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"17ffc1fc-1f0f-5700-9377-b2a605bb3d54","title":"[L205] Some production provider routes retain a three-attempt retry ceiling and 64 MiB policy argument","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L205.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/config/provider/values.rs:31-37`; `config/provider.rs:131-154`.\n- Anthropic and both Google route constructors receive RetryPolicy::without_deadline with **3 attempts**, delay inputs **100 ms / 2 seconds / 2 seconds**, and a **64 MiB** argument. There is no elapsed retry deadline at this caller, but retries are not unlimited. Meaning/enforcement of the byte argument and delay positions remains pending in provider-core; other adapters select their own configuration paths.\n- Initial declared profiles are constructed as StatelessReplay, ResumeKind::Unsupported and BestEffortLocalAbort, even for runtime route dialects. Adapter construction may replace those fields, so this declaration alone is not evidence that the native provider session is dropped; the factory/adapter continuation path remains pending.\n- **Complete route/capability/retry implementation read; no transport retry or native-context test run.** Model token/tool/media limits are supplied explicitly by each configured profile and passed to checked ModelLimits rather than derived from this retry policy.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQORA