{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2562,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.845033890Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"17ffc1fc-1f0f-5700-9377-b2a605bb3d54","comment_uuid":"033acdf2-1b50-4314-8b6f-cae47383b2e9","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L205: Some production provider routes retain a three-attempt retry ceiling and 64 MiB policy argument.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/config/provider/values.rs:31-37; config/provider.rs:131-154. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nUnify production provider recovery under durable acceptance-aware retry scheduling with no fixed transient attempt allowance. Treat response bytes as stream/page resources rather than a task lifetime, honor provider retry eligibility, and preserve request/native context through outages. Ambiguous accepted work must be reconciled before any resend or fallback.\n\nPreserve: definitely-unaccepted versus ambiguously-accepted request state, exact native thread/profile identity, ordered provider observations, tool-result protocol, explicit cancellation and real provider/model capabilities. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQB7tDFIQ1o4l9JInYjofz1+SGHwgXvXU7VBbo94iC4sakkYfLXnodGgf/dyR4AAaDtnmmXZy8fYHlQHeD0eMpAY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2563,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.847494164Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"3974128a-1356-571f-8c61-ee538d06bf92","title":"[L206] Preview protocol exposes 8 KiB output tails and accepts collections beyond downstream process bounds","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L206.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-app-protocol/src/workbench/launch.rs:5-6`; `launch/output.rs:6-33,68-79`; `launch/profile.rs:16-23,50-54,194-230`; `launch/result.rs:33-51,193-203`.\n- The public preview snapshot exposes at most **8,192 UTF-8 bytes per stdout/stderr stream**, narrower than daemon retention of 128 KiB (L193). Profile literal fields are at most **4,096 bytes**, interactive input writes **64 KiB**, and argument/environment/evidence/launch collections are limited only by **u16 representation (65,535)** here. The result query has no offset/page cursor, so all retained launches/evidence must be represented in one response before outer frame/storage admission.\n- C2 accepts fewer arguments/environment entries and imposes aggregate/name limits (L096), so a profile admitted by A3 can still fail downstream. Old totals of 16 launches/256 interactions/64 captures are absent from these constructors; the fully read tests explicitly admit 17/257/65. Those old constants must not be reported as current enforcement.\n- Readiness duration must be positive and cannot exceed an explicitly selected positive wall duration. Wall None stays untimed; no ten-minute wall ceiling remains here. Profile networking has only InheritedHost and cleanup has only TerminateOwnedTree: the Network permission fence in L190/L194 is necessary for this unconstrained native preview path, rather than permission that can safely be dropped. A denied-network local preview requires a confined backend, which this DTO does not offer.\n- Selected-window-only capture and nonzero region dimensions/coordinate overflow checks are consent/integrity boundaries. Failed launch state explicitly includes indeterminate outcome, so L191's restart rewrite conflates failure and uncertainty by design; it does not prove an observed native failure. **All six launch DTO/test files read; no protocol/downstream mismatch case run.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEldb/fyjICg+YGU5lRKYSDJkSP4MqoxiwB2Gmo0SPya0ROlRgjNkqY73p4WjKoddGXWKEriun8WmZMAd6SzIgk="}
