, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJYiJAckOAmxGXgysYxiiP3s5U7MJcJe6F+/c11/JRxYT63w2NkLpvM6/aPApEAPOIlXgDHfhQMGbKC8NFCP9QU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2565,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.852277906Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"66c5cfe5-5380-53a9-aece-9121d351dffe","title":"[L207] Provider retry policy forbids more than 16 attempts and rejects long Retry-After observations","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L207.\n\n- Source: `crates/model/peritus-provider-core/src/retry.rs:9-11,97-125,146-187,281-296,332-362`; daemon caller in L205.\n- RetryPolicy constructors impose at most **16 attempts**, a maximum backoff of **24 hours**, positive base delay/cumulative bytes and at most **1 GiB cumulative transfer**. An optional selected elapsed bound still exists; without_deadline omits only that bound. Attempt and cumulative-byte exhaustion stop otherwise legal recovery.\n- The daemon Anthropic/Google policy selects **3 attempts / 64 MiB cumulative bytes / 2-second maximum delay and Retry-After**. A Retry-After observation above that selected maximum is rejected as InvalidRetry rather than honored or converted to a longer wait. An observation beyond the byte/attempt/selected elapsed ceiling similarly errors before action planning. Actual HTTP Retry-After producer/adapter behavior remains pending.\n- Backoff uses deterministic **0.5-1.5 jitter** capped to max_delay; it is a delay, not a session timeout. Fresh retries after ambiguous acceptance and partial streams require exact idempotency/resume protection, respectively. Those restrictions protect against duplicate provider actions and must remain distinct from synthetic recovery exhaustion.\n- **Entire policy implementation read; no long Retry-After or reconnect test run.** This closes the previously unknown 64 MiB/delay argument semantics in L205.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQM9XtBTHoMi9R6Sa9arwQzv2/faZTTBtn1TgDuOduOzUwitLNzQlMyApkVc6iWkgaFWgSvU2TanrnGFIpnR4sgM="}
