d new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQI5t/nwYDCdS5P6zlzslFkHMHvHQ7bCZY++OWJJJ1IpC9i0cUpiTdFWes7hCV0CgTt0h8+jB6afygWyEC4zY2Q8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2567,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.858214209Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"086e32f3-0eda-5fac-8108-d1b071fedd98","title":"[L208] Startup provider registry admits only 64 profiles despite accepting 256 in config","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L208.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/component/providers.rs:18-44,100-128,163-175`; `component/inventory.rs:27-60`.\n- Configuration accepts 256 provider routes (L203), but production startup always selects ProviderRegistryLimits::PRODUCTION = **64 profiles**, with no daemon-config field to change that choice. A configuration with 65 otherwise valid routes passes the first inventory check and fails component startup. The registry constructor itself permits a maximum of 256.\n- Different revisions of one profile ID can coexist under exact (ID, revision) keys, yet current_provider returns None when more than one revision of that ID is configured. Product selection by ID can therefore become unavailable rather than choosing a designated current revision. Exact immutable revision resolution is necessary; an explicit active revision can avoid ambiguous automatic selection.\n- Components are immutable for the daemon lifetime. A configured unavailable executable or rejected provider declaration aborts construction of the whole provider inventory. Native runtime declarations pass through their runtime configuration constructor; profile state/resume transformation remains pending there. Tool router limits are derived from configured workers/authority queue and can introduce further narrower checks.\n- **All component composition/provider files fully read, including a complete reread of the clipped profiles/providers batch. No oversized or multi-revision config reproduction.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPJ2NCnxkq/LxkPuNhxYQhTeDU9iQSp7FJSwWcFlmx+MezFSms+sUYVXobl4/+4CPW+IiNLMaOqV9yvQ/g9PEg0="}
