{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2570,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.864926443Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"4708117c-2783-59dc-ac2b-ce5d47384dfe","comment_uuid":"2591e2c1-af76-4f99-8f8a-00d3db0ee5bb","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L209: Provider transport limits still impose hard byte ceilings even with no execution deadline.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/model/peritus-provider-core/src/process/limits.rs:15-22,29-64; http/limits.rs:7-11,27-61. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nStream provider transport data into bounded chunks and durable response artifacts, separating per-allocation safety from total inference size. Negotiate actual adapter/provider frame capabilities and expose recoverable capacity/backpressure instead of terminating the logical task. No deadline is introduced when none was selected; retain the accepted request and exact response cursor.\n\nPreserve: definitely-unaccepted versus ambiguously-accepted request state, exact native thread/profile identity, ordered provider observations, tool-result protocol, explicit cancellation and real provider/model capabilities. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJInx/buz/DNBbVJcrueXF+laVBLJPwRE6Xa6IRuTJUb4vhQqH3OQlEYsC/RSuvDliGyIiEjhHs23aVph4dSXAA="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2571,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.867178920Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"4b25f9e9-e2d8-5b81-a7f5-893bfd8a48c3","title":"[L210] Generic provider subprocess overflow kills the invocation, including stderr-only overflow","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L210.\n\n- Source: `crates/model/peritus-provider-core/src/process.rs:17-19,92-102,130-168`; `process/tokio_transport.rs:29-83,136-239,253-256`; `process_containment.rs:14-38`.\n- Generic ProcessRequest admits at most **256 arguments / 2 MiB total argument bytes / 128 environment removals / 128 bytes per environment name**, plus the selected stdin cap. The Tokio transport reads all stdout/stderr into memory and errors as soon as either crosses its total byte cap. With L209 defaults, **64 KiB of diagnostic stderr alone** suffices to fail the invocation and trigger child termination even if stdout remains valid. This is effect termination, not display truncation.\n- Stdout journaling writes and syncs each accepted read chunk (buffer **8 KiB**, not a total cap). The overflowing chunk is rejected before journaling, and stderr has no journal here. Cancellation, selected timeout, stdin/output/journal IO errors all terminate the child. Both production native adapters were subsequently confirmed to use this transport (L211/L213), so overflow termination applies to those routes.\n- Termination targets the direct child and awaits child.wait without a cleanup bound. Linux configuration creates a process group but uses a direct-child parent-death SIGKILL and kill_on_drop; this code does not terminate/join the whole group or adopt it on restart. A surviving descendant holding a pipe can also delay EOF after child exit. These are ownership/completion risks requiring reproduction, distinct from preserving the durable provider context identity.\n- **Entire request/transport/containment implementation read; no overflow or descendant-EOF case run.** Canonical executable pinning and environment/argv integrity remain necessary checks.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDrnVJxE2rtK4KUpIZkMpY2HEMM/TX0cR47oG9WcawlMfXrLIHdxLkxKQwqZXsQAnx9x2l6fukXVk4qGDgUxrQk="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2572,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.869556849Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"4b25f9e9-e2d8-5b81-a7f5-893bfd8a48c3","comment_uuid":"8a639311-9989-466f-b504-bb64ddde4c2a","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L210: Generic provider subprocess overflow kills the invocation, including stderr-only overflow.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/model/peritus-provider-core/src/process.rs:17-19,92-102,130-168; process/tokio_transport.rs:29-83,136-239,253-256; process_containment.rs:14-38. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nDrain native subprocess stdout/stderr through owned asynchronous I/O with bounded buffers and durable segmented spooling. Stderr diagnostic retention must not kill an accepted inference; propagate backpressure or a visible recoverable storage condition while preserving native request/thread identity. Cleanup still owns the complete process tree and truthfully reconciles its outcome.\n\nPreserve: definitely-unaccepted versus ambiguously-accepted request state, exact native thread/profile identity, ordered provider observations, tool-result protocol, explicit cancellation and real provider/model capabilities. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOn7zhlflFDCku3Ag+kpX+q6Zj4LOwBBi4+ZpagncExg3SaOml25lGnu8i0fo1DKtXJLpL3zTbMYtSmC8e8a8Qs="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2573,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.871759618Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"ade7fa93-45d3-531a-8929-f9f4c616c671","title":"[L213] Claude marks transient capacity refusal as Never retry and derives resume from a pre-spawn marker","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L213.\n\n- Source: `crates/model/peritus-provider-anthropic/src/runtime/provider/result.rs:25-34,80-96`; `runtime/provider.rs:165-220,355-381`; `runtime/provider/session.rs:13-88`.\n- A decoded Claude Capacity failure is TransientProvider and DefinitelyNotAccepted, but the common failure constructor gives every certainty except MaybeAccepted **Retryability::Never**. Thus an explicitly classified transient refusal does not offer the safe-new-request retry used by the Codex capacity path. Underlying capacity decoder and host interpretation need caller closure before a live outcome claim.\n- Claude durably allocates an exact **36-character UUID** before inference, initially uses --session-id and later --resume. Its invocation-started marker is synchronized **before transport.run**, and existence alone changes later attempts to --resume. A definitely-absent spawn failure can therefore select resume for an identity not yet accepted by the native runtime; there is no native-existence/launch-phase reconciliation in this module. Actual CLI treatment of an absent UUID remains unverified.\n- Session output must be one complete JSON value with the exact top-level session_id before result normalization. A missing identity in an otherwise actionable error response causes an earlier generic session/configuration failure, potentially hiding the typed capacity/context/model error. Exact UUID matching protects isolation; marker interpretation and classification order are separate recovery issues.\n- Production uses the same Tokio ProcessTransport, so L210's 16 MiB stdout/64 KiB stderr termination applies here too. Authentication is an untimed 64 KiB-output subprocess on every start. **All provider/session/result code and inline exact-session test fully read; no absent-UUID or transient-capacity reconnect run.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQO4lbtj9Y0SVNiQQ69n6ByqP56p2MB/K/Hl1uEIjc/cEfA5KRleZyToQmRNFA7NZrVkYEYq/dR7SG5qPPeegCwc="}
