from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLbTxNvEGfSe+xBNQTU5wI//Or7DILZx1nfojhGUN/x/eXm7LLaAzyTdvEeJLF4BbWI9o6G1DoBJtPj+BFxfVgY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2575,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.875990858Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"4697dd83-6831-5783-a863-42a126a626f5","title":"[L214] Native adapters enforce a single inert inference boundary and transport/control feature restrictions","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L214.\n\n- Source: `crates/model/peritus-provider-anthropic/src/runtime/provider.rs:178-203`; `runtime/request.rs:26-68,104-145,147-197,201-281`; OpenAI `runtime/request/schema.rs:18-106`; `runtime/provider/failure.rs:24-105`.\n- Claude passes **--max-turns 1** per native invocation and disables native tools/MCP/browser/slash execution. This is a single host-controlled inference boundary, not a one-turn Peritus task/session cap: the host is expected to execute proposed tools and invoke the same durable native session again. Removing the boundary without preserving host effect ownership would change authority.\n- Claude requires nonempty content (schema minLength **1**) and at least one non-system message. It rejects all media and nontext system blocks, Minimal/Ultra effort, adaptive effort/visible summaries, protocol continuation/storage/background/extensions and sampling/seed/stops. Codex's content schema permits empty prose alongside tool calls. Both schemas restrict proposal names to the actual catalog and min/max calls to selected ToolChoice/ParallelToolPolicy; these are explicit per-request restrictions, not global session budgets.\n- Full transcript JSON plus transport framing is constructed before ProcessRequest's **16 MiB stdin** check. JSON escaping/extra schema/provenance can make an otherwise raw-size-admitted context fail later; Claude system instructions are stored separately in a temporary file. Encoded boundary maxima have not been measured.\n- Codex distinguishes safe retries for rate/capacity versus Never for incomplete/multiple-message/native-tool/context-limit output; malformed envelope/tool/schema/usage cases require caller decision. No retry-after is supplied by these native decoder mappings. **All named files fully read; decoder behavior and schema-selection edge tests pending.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQO3DW1BV+Rx/RzDMcZLuJ0COGzkEoASE8DZ++09O2MK39UzUI2criDn2Wa8+OEpZjLvKTadsF7CHqaTMKrD1ngk="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2576,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.878272604Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"4697dd83-6831-5783-a863-42a126a626f5","comment_uuid":"7cacf1a0-9550-4cc5-b63e-c8e0ed77ce08","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L214: Native adapters enforce a single inert inference boundary and transport/control feature restrictions.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/model/peritus-provider-anthropic/src/runtime/provider.rs:178-203; runtime/request.rs:26-68,104-145,147-197,201-281; runtime/request/schema.rs:18-106; runtime/provider/failure.rs:24-105. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nModel the adapter inference boundary as a durable owned invocation with explicit supported transport/control/resumption capabilities. Preserve one active accepted inference while allowing its same-context recovery and next invocation; unsupported features need a scoped capability negotiation path. Do not add parallel inference or relax secret/authority isolation to remove an incidental single-use lifecycle fence.\n\nPreserve: definitely-unaccepted versus ambiguously-accepted request state, exact native thread/profile identity, ordered provider observations, tool-result protocol, explicit cancellation and real provider/model capabilities. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBRjfhg98tlLADXpYG5PGNVMNR1pjXe1gpApS1XL1N5y6G6VZKAov8tshsSpg3/Chdp6Gi8L/HBHSinMOLdH4AA="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2577,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.880464126Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"ce408639-cefc-5201-bf1b-260bc6107929","title":"[L215] Native persistence depends on host metadata, while route changes create a separate namespace","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L215.\n\n- Source: `crates/model/peritus-provider-core/src/runtime_session.rs:43-76,85-101`; native session callers in L212/L213.\n- A request without local_session_directory gets an ephemeral TempDir whose artifacts disappear on drop. A request with an absolute host directory retains every turn directory and exclusively locks one namespace. The namespace suffix hashes **profile ID + profile revision + model name**; changing any of those selects a different native context even if the outer Peritus task is unchanged. Production supplies trace.context/<role>/provider-sessions for all ordinary role/conversation requests; the writer-follow-up role incompatibility is separately documented in L224.\n- Ownership uses immediate try_lock: contention or any lock failure becomes a configuration error without waiting/retry classification here. Exclusive same-lineage ownership prevents duplicate inference; a typed busy/reconcile result is separate from abandoning the durable context. There is no elapsed session expiry or automatic deletion for bound turns in this implementation.\n- Every bound invocation retains its schema/system files, images, final output and native journal in a new turn directory; no retirement/index/physical quota is applied here. Codex identity recovery scans these directories on each invocation (L212), so accumulated storage/replay cost grows with use. File-system limits remain real; lifecycle accounting/retirement must preserve exact identities/evidence.\n- **Entire shared session implementation read.** Main production metadata coverage is closed in L224; route-change handoff remains pending. Temporary unbound behavior must not be mistaken for all product requests being ephemeral.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJ3FYIyRmn5RQDw6J6Es9W9q2jDLQNiLKApgT7TPSifA/Zdx5EPPg4BtJ7MMN84SW3k8+7lR5M+WetoJmLU9HAQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2578,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.882722183Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ce408639-cefc-5201-bf1b-260bc6107929","comment_uuid":"d7d34f48-4179-4d23-9187-791957536ecf","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L215: Native persistence depends on host metadata, while route changes create a separate namespace.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/model/peritus-provider-core/src/runtime_session.rs:43-76,85-101. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nPersist task-role/native-context identity in a durable catalog independent of temporary directories and route/model revision namespaces. Changes in provider route are explicit migration or fork decisions with retained historical context and capability checks. Reattach the same context after restart; do not silently create a fresh namespace as a persistence fallback.\n\nPreserve: definitely-unaccepted versus ambiguously-accepted request state, exact native thread/profile identity, ordered provider observations, tool-result protocol, explicit cancellation and real provider/model capabilities. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLxl0tvobayvPZSMfPNxUmZSJHrC1Bd2AtyRyKi7iyQCnlzPjG93FAwLJwl0rtz/4brGZxZ9oPy5dlzssE1XMgA="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2579,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.885067918Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"4eb071e6-bece-5f10-a7da-280c9c5a4697","title":"[L216] Claude completion admission depends on exact native fields and a lexical prose classifier","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L216.\n\n- Source: `crates/model/peritus-provider-anthropic/src/runtime/output.rs:35-78,81-110,113-151,160-183`; `runtime/output/completion.rs:5-66`.\n- Tool-free native public prose is admitted only with exact type=result/subtype=success/stop_reason=end_turn/terminal_reason=completed, is_error false, **num_turns exactly 1**, empty permission_denials, no queued/subagent/deferred/local-command activity and a matching optional origin. A complete response lacking one required field falls through to private-envelope decoding and can become Incomplete/Malformed rather than a public answer.\n- Except for Markdown headed with **1-6 leading # characters**, any line starting with JSON/array/fence or prose containing tool_calls, content plus a brace, or a colon before a bracket is treated as a private candidate. Legitimate tool-free prose with code/examples can therefore be rejected by transport-shape policy. Preventing accidental tool execution is necessary; conflating visible prose with the private envelope is a separate acceptance heuristic needing edge tests.\n- Reported error classification uses a fixed English substring list for auth/capacity/context/model failures. Native error_max_turns/error_max_budget_usd/error_max_structured_output_retries are recognized terminal error subtypes; those names describe upstream-reported limits and are not new Peritus duration defaults. The capacity decoder confirms the source of L213's Never retry mapping.\n- Entire transport JSON is validated with production CanonicalJson bounds before result classification; tool proposal count is capped by the request maximum, exact catalog names required, content nonempty/no NUL. Bounded healing is restricted to private envelopes. **Both decoder files fully read; missing-field/prose-classifier cases not run and upstream version compatibility unverified.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKjx/ES70DPK5K4WMin5DcXepXm9DOejy8RyOZZDMfWXICWHk8g38fb2npTQgzW+gwhZ1nm2ujZ/vDfIV72q2As="}
