{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2581,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.889612689Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"aa2cfabe-fbce-5696-8388-42e738efc331","title":"[L217] HTTP stream framing enforces nonwidenable 8 MiB frame and 16 MiB pending-buffer limits","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L217.\n\n- Source: `crates/model/peritus-provider-core/src/framing.rs:11-48`; `framing/ndjson.rs:47-60,83-110`; `framing/sse.rs:111-124,146-157,172-200,204-228`.\n- Production framing admits at most **8 MiB per NDJSON record/SSE frame** and **16 MiB pending bytes**; constructors require positive consistent values and refuse any wider limit. A too-large record, unterminated line, comment or cumulative SSE frame becomes LimitExceeded. These are fixed transport acceptance ceilings, independent of total HTTP response/model limits.\n- push checks pending+entire incoming chunk before draining complete records, so an alternate caller's large chunk can fail even when its individual records fit. Production HTTP has a separate 1 MiB pull ceiling (L209), whose actual caller enforcement remains pending. Parsers repeatedly split/copy the remaining buffer for each line; latency for many short records is unmeasured.\n- Final unterminated nonempty NDJSON records and SSE lines/events are accepted through finish; malformed UTF-8, repeated finish and push-after-finish are rejected. Comments are exposed without canceling inference; no idle/elapsed deadline is present. **All three framing files fully read; no new frame-boundary/performance test run.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3g