{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2582,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.891981481Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"aa2cfabe-fbce-5696-8388-42e738efc331","comment_uuid":"40fe77d4-8d29-4022-9483-12723ca2f198","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L217: HTTP stream framing enforces nonwidenable 8 MiB frame and 16 MiB pending-buffer limits.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/model/peritus-provider-core/src/framing.rs:11-48; framing/ndjson.rs:47-60,83-110; framing/sse.rs:111-124,146-157,172-200,204-228. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nImplement HTTP framing as a streaming incremental parser with bounded physical buffers and spool/reference support for large frames where the provider protocol permits it. The aggregate pending buffer is not a lifetime response allowance. Preserve delimiter, encoding and actual provider frame validation across arbitrary network chunk splits, with actionable capacity rather than context abandonment.\n\nPreserve: definitely-unaccepted versus ambiguously-accepted request state, exact native thread/profile identity, ordered provider observations, tool-result protocol, explicit cancellation and real provider/model capabilities. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBiyCDlYtKbv9AcFEUj+n11nz+5+dCZopYjNeVJlvRfiPpwmu5Nlnp0L/anVArWcDd2QP7xo6S2rwgzEJvYgXwY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2583,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.894290452Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"09db7df8-72a7-5758-9bc6-bf4461159f29","title":"[L218] Codex decoding caps raw events, event size and completed assistant messages, with closed event kinds","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L218.\n\n- Source: `crates/model/peritus-provider-openai/src/runtime/output.rs:18-20,199-229,256-304,308-343`; `output/selection.rs:15-36`; `output/failure.rs:7-50`.\n- Native JSONL accepts at most **100,000 nonempty raw lines**, **4 MiB per line** and **1,024 completed agent messages**. Raw lines count before byte-identical deduplication, so replayed duplicates consume the event ceiling. The line limit is narrower than the protocol's 16 MiB public text limit and includes escaped JSON framing; total transport output is separately 16 MiB (L210/L211).\n- Only thread.started/turn.started/known item lifecycle/turn.completed/error/turn.failed are accepted; unknown event or item kinds fail the whole turn. A nonduplicate event after terminal completion also fails. Protocol drift or nonessential new native notifications can therefore block inference completion rather than being retained as opaque observations. Native host effects remain prohibited and must not be accepted as ordinary notifications.\n- With an authoritative final-response file, its trimmed contents must equal the last agent message, and the first decodable nonempty host-tool proposal is the suspension boundary. Without the final file, exactly one agent message is required. The production caller also requires final-file read success before admitting a turn, so decoder fallback alone does not supply recovery from a missing final file.\n- Fixed typed codes/English substrings classify capacity/rate/quota/context failures; L214 records their retry categories. **Entire decoder/selection/failure files read; boundary/forward-event cases not run.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLTWpzBRIYa1Ubfp8ZUpmZxSGZ/F5lWB9JdOJQbV59B2vRa5XtQ8AAD8wqyey68/JCWiYdwydgz5gRmALDT4ugc="}
