producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNxdBFKlFWKvamtretqkdo+OTkeZuII59kno39AFvPo9UUJca+zlqzJjjJBZ8uoPkvYIF2SDq9JPhxSHkVI16Qk="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2585,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.899285899Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"8613465b-8d13-5d71-a9b3-335e76c362bc","title":"[L219] Codex usage recovery inspects 64 KiB tails and lets old malformed evidence block new inference","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L219.\n\n- Source: `crates/model/peritus-provider-openai/src/runtime/provider/invocation/usage.rs:14-65`; `runtime/output/usage.rs:7-18,21-55`; `runtime/output.rs:160-175`; `runtime/provider/invocation.rs:78-80`.\n- The existing uncommitted usage follow-up reconstructs high-water counters by scanning every turn directory and reading only its last **64 KiB**, including one preceding byte for line-boundary alignment. A complete retained malformed JSON line or invalid usage counter aborts recovery before the new invocation starts; a torn final JSON fragment is tolerated. No per-record quarantine or independent baseline state appears here.\n- Usage records outside that retained tail are omitted. If no completed usage record remains in the tail, that turn contributes unknown/zero baseline rather than explicit coverage loss, potentially affecting later deltas. The code requires each reported counter to be monotonic; a regressed counter makes the model turn InvalidUsage and resets exposed usage to unknown. Total counters whose intervals disagree are withheld rather than falsely summed.\n- This protects against charging native cumulative totals repeatedly, but recovery is coupled to all old journals and a fixed tail window. Counter integrity must remain distinct from inference continuation and record repair. **Both usage files and all inline tests fully read; no new tests run, this follow-up is not installed or committed.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQE0GMU2Fq7WTaTr2/b29Esnpcl0O56BAhRw8rwMJi+j1LQOt2N3qln+8DssM+y/QMj/nvKRm4T73wkNmB50dxw4="}
