e evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQD7bVWLR57zvWQvI5DRWTI3TCZh6TtkCG/P8WGyTpD4j5M/B5rh6u1Lq/SDeVaA/2UIqSQocheN48/ijVpWwkgM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2587,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.903955844Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"93355f12-a324-578d-9a08-d3387f745450","title":"[L220] Native executable discovery stops at a nonexecutable file instead of trying later PATH entries","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L220.\n\n- Source: `crates/model/peritus-provider-openai/src/runtime/executable.rs:18-28`; `crates/model/peritus-provider-anthropic/src/runtime/executable.rs:18-28`; canonical pin validation in L210.\n- Discovery tests is_file, then immediately returns pin for the first candidate. If that regular file is not executable, canonical pinning rejects it and later PATH entries are never considered. A stale or nonexecutable file earlier on PATH can therefore block an otherwise installed native provider, and daemon component construction can then fail globally (L208).\n- Windows candidates include cmd/bat launchers; compatibility with direct process spawning remains unverified. Immutable exact executable pinning is necessary, but selecting only the first regular candidate is a separate discovery policy. **Both complete discovery implementations read; no PATH fixture or Windows launcher test run.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOygHlFu9k1fQmi+g5evKXOUAqsIKHYfoXZ8gMuGkNlB4d5UpCfFtVXunfuHu0fqD594QFUlPwcADEQIpqrtVAg="}
