umers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAYOuZiYHsgF0et27Qa4aUV7qaHCvm/AmOVoFQxVxUm7Kaz4NMO9nxaA5gj4si1ecL5B1F4wayIKuChZpN1r2gY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2589,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.908451430Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"e141d70a-fa77-5e1c-bf11-0258e25ce9ba","title":"[L221] Native responses are fully buffered, and Codex creates one event per 16 argument bytes","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L221.\n\n- Source: `crates/model/peritus-provider-openai/src/runtime/stream.rs:16,23-79,132-137,153-182`; `crates/model/peritus-provider-anthropic/src/runtime/stream.rs:16,23-86,113-118,134-163`; reducer L223.\n- Codex splits each tool argument into **16-byte** normalized events. Claude uses **4 KiB** text/argument fragments; Codex text uses the protocol event-byte maximum. Both construct the entire VecDeque before consumption, on top of the already fully buffered native process output. This creates avoidable event allocation and per-event trace/reducer work; a 4 MiB argument would approach 262,144 events before protocol framing. Actual adapter admission is additionally bounded by the 4 MiB raw Codex line limit (L218), so no production million-event overflow is inferred solely from the 16 MiB argument maximum.\n- Normalized stream next ignores the supplied cancellation token while draining the completed queue. The host's outer cancellation checks need separate verification; this is not proof that all cancellation is ignored. The shared reducer has a **1,000,000 event** response ceiling (L017/L223), while native builders use production fragment bounds rather than a negotiated narrower request bound.\n- **Both complete native stream implementations read; no allocation, latency or cancellation benchmark run.** Buffering and fixed fragmentation are implementation policies, not native model context limits or elapsed timers.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMr31VuRO9EwwAeHcmQKA9BKFHkESy+zqwHdmbHKZ0ErRj5HJ2jb920qIQGEbzB1CytT4OtDWlb0ABegw67wfQg="}
