{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2593,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.917247495Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"1e3d5807-f11d-522f-b9d6-e46fb857cdf2","title":"[L223] Response reduction makes event and ancillary observation limits terminal malformed failures","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L223.\n\n- Source: `crates/model/peritus-model-protocol/src/reducer/stream.rs:43-83,101-113,175-198`; `reducer/events.rs:46-67,88-109,166-183`; `reducer/terminal.rs:73-90,100-149`; production bounds in L017.\n- Each response is limited to **1,000,000 unique normalized events / 65,536 items / 256 MiB assembled bytes / 16 MiB per argument / 2 MiB reasoning replay** at production defaults, and narrower limits cannot widen them. Exact provider-ID duplicates are excluded from the event count, but native streams without provider IDs count every fragment. Item assemblies remain in the map after completion, so the item count is cumulative for the response.\n- Independently fixed ceilings allow **64 rate-limit observations / 64 cache observations / 128 provider extensions** per response. A harmless additional ancillary observation makes the entire response irreversibly MalformedPayload with **Retryability::Never**, just like malformed fragments or exceeded byte/event limits. These are closed acceptance policies, not provider session duration limits.\n- Heartbeats count toward max_events but do not start/reset any idle timer; ResponseFailed/Cancelled can settle before or after start. EOF without an explicit terminal is IncompleteStream. Exact sequence/identity/explicit completion checks prevent duplicate or incomplete tool admission and should be distinguished from arbitrary ancillary/count ceilings. **All four reducer implementation files fully read; no response-limit edge cases run.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQET9LZgI4jJ9CSOTqz6Xcfqo3Bw3ZtyWnL23HRX0tSFzwjDJmt1Vz9sgmF7IS9+v0b6kKgLz/LmvVpAemyQnww4="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2594,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.919511477Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"1e3d5807-f11d-522f-b9d6-e46fb857cdf2","comment_uuid":"93f15e25-4dee-43e9-ac4e-c60112e4c700","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L223: Response reduction makes event and ancillary observation limits terminal malformed failures.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/model/peritus-model-protocol/src/reducer/stream.rs:43-83,101-113,175-198; reducer/events.rs:46-67,88-109,166-183; reducer/terminal.rs:73-90,100-149. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nSeparate required semantic provider state from bounded ancillary observation views, storing exact ordered history in durable pages. Capacity pressure becomes a recoverable transport/selection condition, not terminal malformed data. Retain genuine ordering, identity and invalid-event errors and require a complete accepted terminal response before effect/result settlement.\n\nPreserve: definitely-unaccepted versus ambiguously-accepted request state, exact native thread/profile identity, ordered provider observations, tool-result protocol, explicit cancellation and real provider/model capabilities. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEtpfVCEbiz9Hs5mJi3tX6r0IRKNbQpEsxkxRUNvnNvqThGJcfElCM/6RBBOYPwh6OlDUd9T1DaT+E03rwOAXwI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2595,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.921702592Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"e170275e-c034-50c5-a38e-4bf8f546d75d","title":"[L225] HTTP pulls reject valid bodies based on upstream chunk boundaries, while default transport has no selected timer","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L225.\n\n- Source: `crates/model/peritus-provider-core/src/reqwest_transport.rs:36-66,75-93,147-170,183-231,304-312`; `transport.rs:126-155`; `http/message.rs:71-85,142-153`; `http/header.rs:25-32,178-193`.\n- Both ReqwestByteStream and BoundedByteStream reject an upstream chunk larger than **1 MiB**, rather than slicing it into allowed pulls. A response whose total and individual SSE/NDJSON frames are otherwise valid can therefore fail solely because the underlying transport groups bytes differently. At **256 MiB cumulative response**, content-length admission or accumulated streaming bytes also fail; full request body admission is **32 MiB**. This closes enforcement of L209/L217, though no large-chunk case has been reproduced.\n- Response header limits are **256 entries / 128 KiB aggregate**; a single name is at most **256 bytes**. Hop-by-hop/proxy/header-injection rejection is a separate integrity/credential boundary, not an arbitrary execution deadline.\n- Peritus default ReqwestTransport::new selects None for connect/header/body-idle deadlines; an explicit with_timeouts API still accepts three mandatory positive durations and applies header/idle timeout wrappers. AnthropicClient::new uses the untimed constructor. This audit does not infer dependency-internal defaults from the absence of a Peritus value. Redirects, ambient proxies and implicit HTTP retries are disabled deliberately by the transport contract.\n- OwnedModelStream stops after the first normalized terminal and cancels on error/drop, but relies on its inner stream to honor cancellation during pull; native adapters ignore the token (L221). The production developer driver additionally wraps drive in cancel_first and isolates cancellation per attempt, so native draining does not establish a general uncancelable run. **All six HTTP/stream implementations plus developer caller fully read; no new network/cancellation tests run.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEtvd0TbIIEq9C5fLQwnN0Mu7kHPqyS/ifNpuXfkYz1W5+WufcW7J1Ocylc2fqO6jEMND2xOAK1XiN9JlYAHtgg="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2596,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.924126295Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"e170275e-c034-50c5-a38e-4bf8f546d75d","comment_uuid":"5cd6a235-0274-4fdd-af26-17a2bfb14c1f","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L225: HTTP pulls reject valid bodies based on upstream chunk boundaries, while default transport has no selected timer.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/model/peritus-provider-core/src/reqwest_transport.rs:36-66,75-93,147-170,183-231,304-312; transport.rs:126-155; http/message.rs:71-85,142-153; http/header.rs:25-32,178-193. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nDecouple body admission from arbitrary upstream network chunk sizes. Slice every received chunk into admitted parser/spool pieces and count actual bytes at the intended physical or provider boundary. Preserve exact framing and cancellation; a transport buffer cannot reject the same valid body only because its chunk partition changed.\n\nPreserve: definitely-unaccepted versus ambiguously-accepted request state, exact native thread/profile identity, ordered provider observations, tool-result protocol, explicit cancellation and real provider/model capabilities. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative 