{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2597,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.926378654Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"76b0589a-16a2-59dc-9167-7e48b6bdf979","title":"[L226] Anthropic HTTP Retry-After above two seconds becomes InvalidRetry instead of a deferred retry","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L226.\n\n- Source: `crates/model/peritus-provider-anthropic/src/client.rs:97-111,140-173,324-345`; `crates/model/peritus-provider-core/src/retry.rs:146-187`; daemon-selected policy L205/L207.\n- Anthropic reads the first Retry-After header as decimal seconds with at most **three fractional digits**, converts it to milliseconds and passes it unmodified into RetryPolicy. A valid value such as **3 seconds** exceeds the daemon's selected **2-second maximum** and plan returns InvalidRetry, propagated before a normalized RateLimited terminal is returned. This closes the concrete production producer/caller chain for L207; Google remains separately pending.\n- Date-shaped values, surrounding whitespace or longer fractions do not parse in this helper, so the requested delay is omitted. Adapter status/content-type grammar is also closed: success requires exact **HTTP 200** plus text/event-stream; status 409/500/504/529 is transient, other server statuses follow the nonretryable default mapping.\n- Retry accounting increments only the encoded request body for each submission, with **3 attempts / 64 MiB** selected; response/error bytes are not added here. The policy is consulted after failure, not as pre-submission admission, so it is a recovery ceiling rather than an all-transfer quota. Error bodies are fully drained/buffered under the HTTP **256 MiB** maximum before classification; an error-drain failure propagates before the useful status failure is emitted.\n- **Complete client/config/error/client-tests source read; no long-delay reproduction or error-drain test run.** Existing tests exercise Retry-After zero, not this two-second rejection. Exact ambiguous-acceptance restrictions remain necessary to prevent duplicate provider submission.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIswqEzKJf87UL69lFFRJ56JlA82qTo+vC4Im5JopKXEm0rSxSO1sXvCZW9Jz7PnkvKZtxEPWYc/XMCD9Jlubwg="}
