{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2599,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.931169998Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"79fc9687-0389-5066-8bed-5f92a04f632f","title":"[L227] Provider catalog discovery fails entire results at fixed page, byte, frame and entry ceilings","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L227.\n\n- Source: `crates/model/peritus-provider-core/src/catalog.rs:17-18,42-48`; `catalog/http.rs:12-14,61-90,104-149`; `catalog/runtime.rs:12-13,118-133,141-167,179-193,206-233`; `catalog/parse.rs:8-54,61-68`.\n- HTTP discovery is capped at **16 pages / 4 MiB per page / 16 MiB total / 4,096 models**, with cursor at most **4,096 bytes** and each display label at most **512 bytes**. Native catalog queries also allow **16 Codex pages** and **4,096 accumulated entries / 4 MiB per frame / 16 MiB total**, plus at most **64 frames while waiting for each response** or Claude initialization. More harmless native notifications can exhaust that waiting-frame count before the matching response arrives.\n- A single malformed entry/label, conflicting HTTP duplicate metadata, oversized response or exhausted page/frame count rejects the entire discovery result rather than yielding usable pages and a continuation. Claude model initialization requires the exact nested models field. Missing optional token/tool metadata stays unknown; no fabricated fallback model list is inserted. Explicit model selection remains available through adapter APIs; UI dependence on successful discovery still needs caller closure.\n- Native discovery uses a fresh temporary directory for a **metadata-only subprocess**, then kills/waits for it after the query. This is not ephemeral inference context or a model-run timeout. No selected query elapsed deadline appears here; kill/wait cleanup is unbounded. Same-origin pagination and repeated-cursor detection protect credentials/progress and should remain separate from fixed catalog exhaustion.\n- A selected model derives a new immutable profile ID from original profile/revision/model and resets profile revision to **1**, preserving route limits/capabilities but demoting model-specific provenance to Profiled. This also selects another native namespace (L215). **All four catalog files fully read; no large catalog/notification test run.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPVPXNAotuEwcYYZRY9Tck1Xt9avOx2PAYDw1rIhRxybbVW6DqQDJeJjEO9urhaxU0eu7xzaazByb0+N0dIQ6AI="}
