er; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNBjBSn38lw2ym1LenwjtQLKXZO0XgvdUzUVIPuJ7c6EBk61Q2p7s6qAZvaapPQwREdCdbxirl13gJ9zj+CRnQk="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2603,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.940820352Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"b1189c10-82cc-5795-9ee3-cbe4b86cf940","title":"[L320] D0's durability boundary cannot return even an immediate exact committed retry","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L320.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/orchestration/peritus-agent/src/runtime/durability.rs:131-192`; `src/runtime/driver.rs:253-264,345-377` (remaining paths in the agent crate).\n- **Blocker:** commit_agent_transition checks the current head against the command's predecessor before passing the command identity to C0 append. After that exact transition has committed, the head is its successor, so repeating the same immutable command/event/checkpoint fails BindingMismatch before C0 can resolve its prior receipt. There is no committed-command lookup here.\n- **Consequence:** A lost response after successful append cannot be repaired by exact retry at this API, even without intervening progress. drive_once additionally reconstructs a fresh command against its current state for the supplied identity; repeating an identity after advancing changes its content and conflicts with the journal's original command binding. Callers must reload and independently determine what committed, but the error does not return the historical result.\n- **Repair direction:** Resolve exact command content and its committed historical receipt before current-head admission. Return both the immutable prior outcome and an explicit current-state frontier, without replaying effects or installing an old checkpoint over later progress.\n- **Evidence scope:** Source-derived immediate-retry behavior; no ambiguous commit injected. This is stricter than the latest-checkpoint-only retry restrictions already recorded for scheduler, collaboration and E0.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDRL9PXez9aDjhMZcbvdGd4PiO9D+G3Z6BXhJr+BOg/ddask1sr7rQ0u1kYC+hRrrDWMLUgXMtM1Uf41Q+Sr+wQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2604,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.943109430Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"b1189c10-82cc-5795-9ee3-cbe4b86cf940","comment_uuid":"e645dad0-ecb8-43b6-beb1-5748aaa8bc2d","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L320: D0's durability boundary cannot return even an immediate exact committed retry.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/orchestration/peritus-agent/src/runtime/durability.rs:131-192; src/runtime/driver.rs:253-264,345-377. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nResolve exact command content and its committed historical receipt before current-head admission. Return both the immutable prior outcome and an explicit current-state frontier, without replaying effects or installing an old checkpoint over later progress.\n\nPreserve: committed command/event identity, exact causal and digest roots, exclusive ownership, atomic publication, reference-safe artifact retention and verified recovery from the last durable frontier. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFxL28Iul+j8cN9GPjCzN1+zcMXIAp1YEsAY4D3wFxMt8RCYrpetvuU2v6IiCQpBS2Sb3FSqyHqfGGaPIeqyMwo="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2605,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.945277378Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"c3179996-9760-5fce-97c4-e07352d941a9","title":"[L321] D0 restores durable tool phases without a way to reattach unstarted authorized batches","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L321.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/orchestration/peritus-agent/src/runtime/driver.rs:267-295,315-335`; `src/runtime/driver/tool_steps.rs:51-72,74-135,137-153,255-272` (remaining paths in the agent crate).\n- **Blocker:** restore always creates tools=None. attach_prepared_tools accepts only ProposedToolCalls, although a batch may have durably reached AwaitingAuthorization or ExecutingTools with still-unstarted slots. recovery_report lists only Dispatched/Active slots and model-in-flight state, so an authorization-phase aggregate can report clean while lacking the coordinator necessary to progress.\n- **Consequence:** After restart during authorization, deny_tool_once cannot operate without runtime tools, and the public reattachment API rejects the phase. Pure authorization/execution commands can still advance, but a later dispatch records intent before failing RuntimeResourceUnavailable (L319). Unstarted authorized slots have no lost-effect classification until this false dispatch intent is introduced. Restart reconstruction is therefore incomplete even when no external effect is uncertain.\n- **Repair direction:** Reconstruct inert prepared batch state at every recoverable durable phase, validate exact proposals/authority independently, and distinguish runtime reconstruction needs from uncertain effects in recovery_report. Continue unstarted work under the same logical aggregate and context.\n- **Evidence scope:** Source-only restore/API reachability finding. No live restart performed and no claim that every installed product path uses AgentDriver.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOj36OpgzKl0c/YKEgvimEq1a4NuYr0j9u0zNjlXqXR0QFitINEZZD8csrxLQpN5a/zLL5FjAmmAQ4sg/n9GDg0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2606,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.947442868Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"c3179996-9760-5fce-97c4-e07352d941a9","comment_uuid":"37432d86-01d3-4b27-89d9-429c9be075a9","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L321: D0 restores durable tool phases without a way to reattach unstarted authorized batches.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/orchestration/peritus-agent/src/runtime/driver.rs:267-295,315-335; src/runtime/driver/tool_steps.rs:51-72,74-135,137-153,255-272. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nReconstruct inert prepared batch state at every recoverable durable phase, validate exact proposals/authority independently, and distinguish runtime reconstruction needs from uncertain effects in recovery_report. Continue unstarted work under the same logical aggregate and context.\n\nPreserve: exact snapshot/preimage identity, protected paths, ancestor and symlink safety, writable-fork coverage, conflict detection, one logical restore transaction and exact effect receipts. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large-file and many-path capture/restore, divergent preimage rejection, interrupted staging/publication/restore, then reopen and continue the same conversation with an exact restored workspace. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBsbTk7pz6fPOcfLxcp/n/3/54UjlpATk3D/+ZUeeM74JX4lnrk/Dlhe++IQYBAptuyyqjTgI96seEiFiyRmyQM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2607,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.949708243Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"170cdbf2-3977-5250-be6d-ccfea38172f4","title":"[L322] Legacy deterministic compaction retains an unbounded prompt lineage until it stops shrinking","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L322.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/orchestration/peritus-agent/src/developer/context.rs:16-19,41-105,129-157,233-322`; `src/developer/context_encoding.rs:7-26,62-111`; `src/developer/semantic.rs:28-61,101-133`; `src/developer/context_port.rs:195-233` (remaining paths in the agent crate).\n- **Blocker:** Legacy deterministic compaction preserves one text/tool-call/tool-result summary line per old block, with text previews 256 characters and tool previews 512. Recompacting a prior summary copies all prior_lineage, user_text, assistant_text, tool_call and tool_result lines into the next summary, then adds another lineage digest. There is no retirement or bounded external index for those lines. Candidate construction stops at the first noncompactable exchange rather than selecting later independent complete exchanges.\n- **Consequence:** Although each initial replacement can reduce full output, repeated long work grows a minimum retained summary proportional to all historical tool calls. compact_once returns None when the replacement cannot shrink its candidate, and prepare_messages then eventually rejects the request when the accumulated summary plus protected inputs/tools exceeds input capacity. The eight-message preference can fall back to zero recent messages, but cannot solve this retained-lineage growth or a noncompactable leading exchange. Compaction source count is additionally limited to u16.\n- **Repair direction:** Store exact lineage and old observations in a durable paged index, retain a bounded prompt frontier selected for current work, and retrieve omitted evidence under its stable identity. Preserve governing inputs and complete protocol obligations; make recovery from a full view an explicit selection operation rather than ending the logical task.\n- **Evidence scope:** Complete source inspection. Host-owned local context bypasses both legacy compaction paths; semantic compaction can shrink to a model-authored checkpoint when explicitly enabled. This finding applies to deterministic legacy/fallback selection, not every production request, and is separate from local-memory limits L058-L079.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKwgHi3+lBlNANn2NWJQesYbjfnEG5xRweUcyVX1W7DINc/AjzMpIID90kZdgoCZE8UENrjtj0Vyk2EBqh/78wI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2608,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.951924742Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"170cdbf2-3977-5250-be6d-ccfea38172f4","comment_uuid":"0c528c3a-bba8-43a5-827d-22cef25c4dda","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L322: Legacy deterministic compaction retains an unbounded prompt lineage until it stops shrinking.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/orchestration/peritus-agent/src/developer/context.rs:16-19,41-105,129-157,233-322; src/developer/context_encoding.rs:7-26,62-111; src/developer/semantic.rs:28-61,101-133; src/developer/context_port.rs:195-233. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nStore exact lineage and old observations in a durable paged index, retain a bounded prompt frontier selected for current work, and retrieve omitted evidence under its stable identity. Preserve governing inputs and complete protocol obligations; make recovery from a full view an explicit selection operation rather than ending the logical task.\n\nPreserve: governing inputs, complete pending tool protocol pairs, exact source/lineage references, explicit permissions, unresolved effect truth and task-role/native-provider identity. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long productive read/write sessions through repeated compaction and segment boundaries, source/dependency changes, non-ASCII and large evidence, interrupted checkpoint publication, then reopen the same lineage and prove that valid grounding is reused and stale targets are reread. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJYqBHzneHR1QLQu50oDbijuNA1E7jLpT1VQVz+AfuFyKJuUCUu1q1ijxa7KtVnWBQ2xZQSyYC3hBYoqFYv3YwE="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2609,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.954184263Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"e1963126-ff5e-50d2-aed9-40870db51283","title":"[L323] Model output limiting can hide the control identities and terminal status of an oversized tool result","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L323.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/orchestration/peritus-agent/src/developer/observation.rs:8-69,72-145`; `src/developer/context_port.rs:89-101,128-154` (remaining paths in the agent crate).\n- **Blocker:** Model-visible output gets a policy budget of one eighth of provider input, clamped to 512..10,000 estimated tokens and three bytes per token. Command projection first removes tool_result and all completed progress, or retains only eight active progress events. If the remaining JSON is still oversized, the generic truncator replaces the entire object with head/tail text and digest metadata; it does not separately preserve command handle, state, success/status, failure or recovery fields.\n- **Consequence:** A large result can leave the model without structured control/terminal truth even though the full observation was durably retained. The handle or decisive fields may fall outside both previews. A local-context source reference can enable retrieval and is added afterward, but ports need not provide one; legacy callers receive only the warning to make a narrower request. This can drive repeated inspection or prevent the model from selecting the exact poll/recovery action. Metadata insertion after truncation also increases the already selected view size.\n- **Repair direction:** Keep a bounded typed decision/control envelope independent of optional output text, with stable handles and explicit terminal/uncertain status. Expose paged exact observations through durable references and make any omitted decision field explicit, without removing the provider's physical input constraints.\n- **Evidence scope:** Source-derived information-loss condition; no oversized live result generated. The current fixture tests check small completed/running projections and do not exercise generic truncation of their control envelope.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHfCOR34gMsVDCwcjmOpDcXpmtFDCd/t7fF3KP/090T5HW/adQrgPA/x2k+TK9XOzccb7jkoGGI4YoVvqxEDzgs="}
