eration must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNDhHQVAJtR1ntcRHt12vN8rVVaHToy0xexcgOhbBcQFefITFdFW1SPi9vQB+u53RRXWO/z4LBtJaC7mSIe8ygs="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2611,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.958507318Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"c7af23be-6cd2-50be-8eba-300be0a5bdd7","title":"[L324] D0 retained text and evidence fields have independent fixed admission ceilings","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L324.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/orchestration/peritus-agent/src/identity.rs:28-55`; `src/completion.rs:95-130`; `src/tools.rs:218-240`; `src/command.rs:74-115`; `src/canonical/event_wire.rs:130-137,194-204,304-362,379-389` (remaining paths in the agent crate).\n- **Blocker:** SafeText must be nonempty and at most 16,384 UTF-8 bytes. Completion retains at most 1,024 exact evidence references and 64 uncertainties; each uncertainty and summary uses SafeText. Each tool result retains at most 256 evidence IDs. Each persisted provider envelope capsule is at most 8 MiB, even if the surrounding C5 protocol supports a larger event. Command decoding independently caps proposals at the compiled 256-call ceiling.\n- **Consequence:** Valid larger evidence/uncertainty sets or responses cannot be represented directly by these aggregate APIs. These limits are per record, separate from L316's accumulated-work counters and the global codec frame. Evidence order/revision checks and capsule SHA checks are integrity rules; the hard field counts/bytes are admission bounds. These constructors and decoders use matching counts, unlike the accepted/reload mismatches found in other crates.\n- **Repair direction:** Retain bounded projections with stable digest-bound paged source sets, and preserve full terminal/provider evidence externally before acknowledging it. Make field-size failure distinguishable from total-work exhaustion and recoverable without replacing the logical session.\n- **Evidence scope:** Complete definitions and codec reads. No oversized response fixture executed; physical encoding/input constraints are explicitly distinguished from mandatory lifetime quotas.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLIJFYIMCFFSNFL6cOLXvFt+GNL1/KXQy8OKzDItbNrB+u3gC2xOShMfhTdXxz1LOuZcRq22vJTsLwNHq3GSaQY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2612,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.960456054Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"c7af23be-6cd2-50be-8eba-300be0a5bdd7","comment_uuid":"02c41e21-8224-4af1-8974-dfcc0dab41c8","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L324: D0 retained text and evidence fields have independent fixed admission ceilings.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/orchestration/peritus-agent/src/identity.rs:28-55; src/completion.rs:95-130; src/tools.rs:218-240; src/command.rs:74-115; src/canonical/event_wire.rs:130-137,194-204,304-362,379-389. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nRetain bounded projections with stable digest-bound paged source sets, and preserve full terminal/provider evidence externally before acknowledging it. Make field-size failure distinguishable from total-work exhaustion and recoverable without replacing the logical session.\n\nPreserve: canonical digest and schema identity, shared writer/reader admissibility, malformed-input rejection before allocation, exact causal ordering, actual provider/OS capability boundaries and preserved accepted historical evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOpwDCp2TFM/vwtBdDysO6pye3ELpcx1+AK3+GseAtOxb9IyME7Ya4EGq+EbuuJCbenKW+xMxnQ/lN87wgfabAU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2613,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.962544744Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"a3d83273-9bcd-5ded-bb5d-750ad5cfa189","title":"[L325] D0 rejects an entire multi-call batch whenever any proposal mutates the workspace","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L325.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/orchestration/peritus-agent/src/tools/batch.rs:13-46`; `src/reducer.rs:271-284`; `src/runtime/tools.rs:305-345,584-600,637-644`; `src/runtime/driver/tool_steps.rs:25-48` (remaining paths in the agent crate).\n- **Blocker:** ToolBatch::new rejects proposals.len()>1 when even one proposal has Workspace side effect. This applies to two edits and to one edit alongside an inspection, regardless of their proposal order, concurrency allowance or runtime capacity. The runtime coordinator instead supports a complete batch and serializes unsafe calls against active work.\n- **Consequence:** A normal model response proposing several sequential edits is rejected before the batch reaches durable authorization; increasing tool-call/parallel limits cannot help. The driver has already finished the provider response and returns the pure rejection rather than scheduling these calls sequentially or supplying an exact corrective model exchange. A caller would have to construct another batch/turn policy itself.\n- **Repair direction:** Represent the complete proposed batch and its ordered serialization constraints, then admit one effect at a time. Keep current authorization and mutation exclusivity without requiring the model to produce only one call per response.\n- **Evidence scope:** Source-only admission behavior. Proposal uniqueness/ordinal/revision checks remain necessary integrity facts. Installed DeveloperLoop uses its own serial executor path, so this is not attributed to its live multi-call behavior.\n\n- **Additional fully read fixture evidence:** tests/tool_ordering.rs:94-108 requires rejection of one workspace mutation plus one inspection. tests/runtime_tools.rs:295-525 qualifies only one call per synthetic inspect/edit/run/test cycle, not ordered multi-edit responses. No test was executed.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKnb69/BIuvw8K9An9sTIIQk4CSbFVIbk6twymvsNTf9nHN39+9yq2TxG0BF4CdL8O3blFLQMxOUl3yky9OFIAg="}
