ready owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBh/vnotWwGOjpi7AgTg+gNY5oNqGxNGg7h6uRKy1yO40GscW9iVOGb4waiMj74ATv5rnCTzS8MkqAPGne5uXwI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2615,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.966854210Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"0916df39-e343-5861-bc9c-c93aab8f1d32","title":"[L326] D0 durable restart requires the caller to reconstruct its original binding and limits","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L326.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/orchestration/peritus-agent/src/protocol_bridge.rs:110-113,165-203`; `src/runtime/driver.rs:275-294`; `src/canonical.rs:15-35,63-71`; `src/identity.rs:145-205` (remaining paths in the agent crate).\n- **Blocker:** The pure genesis event carries AgentBinding and AgentLimits, but its durable B3 projection writes an empty payload. restore takes both values from its caller and recreates genesis before validating saved event digests. The checkpoint stores canonical state bytes containing limits but there is no state decoder/reconstruction path here; RoleProfile is omitted from those canonical bytes entirely.\n- **Consequence:** These saved D0 records alone do not reopen the original execution binding. A changed configured limit/profile revision or lost caller-side binding causes replay/checkpoint mismatch instead of retrieving the historical configuration and continuing the same aggregate. RoleProfile is not committed by the state hash, but the complete role-crate read establishes that its private fields and deterministic public constructors prevent different profiles for the same ActorRole within this build. The remaining policy-version concern is changes to those compiled tables across builds, not arbitrary caller configuration. This is an incomplete durable ownership model, distinct from explicit session expiration.\n- **Repair direction:** Persist and decode the complete versioned original binding, role capabilities and limit policy as durable genesis authority. Treat current provider/profile changes as explicit compatible successor bindings while retaining logical context and unresolved obligations; do not silently bypass revision fences.\n- **Evidence scope:** Complete bridge/canonical/restore reads, followed by all role constructors and policy tables. RoleProfile is currently deterministic from ActorRole. Other host records may retain enough original binding for particular callers; this finding identifies the D0 durability API's external reconstruction dependency, not a demonstrated installed restart failure.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMHUxdQiSAzc6/mDwPpJcTEGn/b/CwlLAlKhYrUaIP2jl4kOl+GatoGgyHlu2Bil09r0irfjhlLJ6EXTeuy/oQw="}
