eave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBG2BHTP0bRpLMI4qRIdtA8Ut1aLEQLfsV1O2FAZX/qRUp1cqb8H/64gre2h5WNZm9CdoyWUPuF/bSohH74IMQw="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2617,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.971141054Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"b7fef9f6-f82a-5231-9d04-e183e87f957a","title":"[L327] D0's fresh-start API can discard an exact provider-resume prefix before admission succeeds","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L327.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/orchestration/peritus-agent/src/runtime/driver.rs:389-420,491-547,642-677`; `src/runtime/model.rs:105-146`; `src/reducer.rs:256-267,382-406`; `src/state.rs:223-267` (remaining paths in the agent crate).\n- **Blocker:** start_model_once clears model_prefix before computing the request fingerprint or committing ModelRequestStarted. It does not reject a pending ExactResume retry. Pure model start preserves the old cursor for that retry, but this API constructs ModelSession::start with a fresh empty C5 reducer instead of rebuilding the durable prefix. The separate restore_model_once requires that prefix to be nonempty.\n- **Consequence:** Fingerprint, reduction or journal failure in a fresh-start attempt can erase the process's retained exact-resume prefix while leaving durable state unchanged, making the intended restore API unavailable until the whole driver is reloaded. If the exact retry takes this fresh-start route successfully, the pure old cursor and fresh normalized reducer disagree about the stream frontier; a correct same-stream continuation is not reconstructed. The API boundary relies on callers choosing the right path despite accepting the wrong one.\n- **Repair direction:** Encode fresh versus exact-resume admission in separate checked state/capability types, build the candidate session prefix before committing, and clear/replace runtime prefix only after the selected transition succeeds. Keep the same durable provider cursor and logical context across failures.\n- **Evidence scope:** Source-derived API misuse and failure-path counterexamples; no provider or journal failure injected. The exact restore path itself explicitly handles unsupported provider restoration and validates returned continuation identity.\n\n- **Additional fully read fixture evidence:** tests/runtime_driver.rs:361-507 performs exact recovery through restore_model_once with a retained prefix and fresh retry budget. It does not exercise accidental fresh-start admission or prefix preservation after failed commit. No test was executed.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAubliBsn6rH1uuQBnw5urCtwusO40fwryGy4yZLpDPFtzK7sccGV27EyWn0lohf9KXjuNblllYPLYVEIm3/wAE="}
