new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQN/S+J8iAI3SuIET+RHv2uAPgOmEa1YwGf7LrCZ7rJNZYma1iAdcgm0yMzmhSFTC0MX+v4bIyJgs4gAJz7pTmQo="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2619,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.975800899Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"0701f92a-2a08-5c4a-96cd-b7558111f32f","title":"[L328] D0 restart and per-envelope preview perform repeated synchronous full reconstruction","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L328.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/orchestration/peritus-agent/src/runtime/driver.rs:275-294,434-474,642-677`; `src/protocol_bridge.rs:171-203`; `src/reducer.rs:109-139,147-208`; `src/runtime/model.rs:127-146,207-225`; `src/runtime/durability.rs:201-247` (remaining paths in the agent crate).\n- **Blocker:** Restore loads and decodes the complete journal chain, recover_protocol_events reduces every command, then replay reduces the recovered chain again. It also rebuilds the normalized provider prefix and later replays that prefix again on exact resume. Every live provider envelope preview clones the current C5 ResponseReducer before acknowledging the same envelope into the original reducer. D0 cloning/hashing happens synchronously in these APIs.\n- **Consequence:** Large accumulated response items and long event chains increase work before control returns; repeated cloning of a growing response can produce quadratic cumulative copying. Removing only count ceilings does not provide daily-driving responsiveness or a bounded recovery frontier. This is a possible stall mechanism, not an elapsed deadline or measured performance claim.\n- **Repair direction:** Preserve an authenticated incremental replay frontier and indexed/paged events, verify only the required suffix, and preview new envelope admission without cloning all prior response material. Keep commit-before-ack truth and responsive control admission.\n- **Evidence scope:** Complete call-chain reads; no benchmark or live latency measurement performed. D0 state itself retains only the current batch/model projection, so no claim of an unbounded candidate history inside that state.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDVawNCMWi2ENnBw17CEsQQKLYUjlaPmgh9d3H73Hy2oL+nl3p+BMpWKYa86vh1SX5IZqaN4m7xNLVlI02P5Vgk="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2620,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.978151298Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"0701f92a-2a08-5c4a-96cd-b7558111f32f","comment_uuid":"1e1492fc-56da-47f8-8546-62ae8f380af6","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L328: D0 restart and per-envelope preview perform repeated synchronous full reconstruction.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/orchestration/peritus-agent/src/runtime/driver.rs:275-294,434-474,642-677; src/protocol_bridge.rs:171-203; src/reducer.rs:109-139,147-208; src/runtime/model.rs:127-146,207-225; src/runtime/durability.rs:201-247. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nPreserve an authenticated incremental replay frontier and indexed/paged events, verify only the required suffix, and preview new envelope admission without cloning all prior response material. Keep commit-before-ack truth and responsive control admission.\n\nPreserve: exact candidate revision and artifact binding, complete finding/provenance conservation, independent reviewer evidence, truthful gate outcomes, protected user constraints and acceptance fail-closed on invalid evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFOKMSuicqByslpDRDxnohtVLeLE20URiBngSWEW7L9lPonJgIB9RCU/1MtJ9EIg3pEDNnHKVp5mdlM//w3caA0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2621,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.980432833Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"04ee510f-af8d-575a-a37b-61a1a01d5e5d","title":"[L329] D0 cannot redrive its pending provider envelope after a failed durable commit","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L329.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/orchestration/peritus-agent/src/runtime/driver.rs:423-474`; `src/runtime/model.rs:155-177,181-225`; `src/runtime/durability.rs:131-192` (remaining paths in the agent crate).\n- **Blocker:** drive_model_once always begins with model.pull_one. After a reducer/projection/journal failure the existing envelope remains pending, as intended for commit-before-ack safety. But pull_one rejects any pending envelope, and the driver provides no branch that retries committing that retained envelope before another pull.\n- **Consequence:** Even a definitely uncommitted transient journal failure leaves the in-memory driver unable to redrive the same observation: the next step returns PendingEnvelope before reduction or append. The caller can cancel and rebuild from durable state, but this discards the uncommitted local envelope and depends on provider-specific exact restoration. The same trap applies to capsule or reducer-limit rejection while an envelope is retained. This undermines the documented pending-envelope durability boundary without an elapsed timer.\n- **Repair direction:** Treat pending-observation admission as its own durable retry state. Retry the exact immutable envelope/command until its commit outcome is resolved, then acknowledge once, and only afterward allow another provider pull. Preserve the same stream/context across transient storage failure.\n- **Evidence scope:** Complete source call chain; no storage failure injected. Current runtime-driver tests exercise normal acknowledgement, duplicate semantics, protocol failure and successful exact restart, but not retry of an uncommitted pending-envelope commit.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQC4HM3jaCNMLgkz5Wei+W4LcP+HvVNza8vEdSYYkpEVV+PjgkJaaFXrVPI+0w4s1guxixxOLolu4ejJEQFVdogU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2622,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.982585808Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"04ee510f-af8d-575a-a37b-61a1a01d5e5d","comment_uuid":"c2571e53-f7b4-4eeb-8eff-60395a79ef0d","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L329: D0 cannot redrive its pending provider envelope after a failed durable commit.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/orchestration/peritus-agent/src/runtime/driver.rs:423-474; src/runtime/model.rs:155-177,181-225; src/runtime/durability.rs:131-192. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nTreat pending-observation admission as its own durable retry state. Retry the exact immutable envelope/command until its commit outcome is resolved, then acknowledge once, and only afterward allow another provider pull. Preserve the same stream/context across transient storage failure.\n\nPreserve: definitely-unaccepted versus ambiguously-accepted request state, exact native thread/profile identity, ordered provider observations, tool-result protocol, explicit cancellation and real provider/model capabilities. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPfaQrALTCm4npnyIlOV0jRX/u98V/BbQ7eDZvnBo07bCUFMVHRNwG1Wv4YQfJSccKJroorvcVV8zXcxYP1o9A0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2623,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.984801206Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"9f74da89-5d8d-5595-bb7a-19cbacdd4285","title":"[L332] D1 immutable gate planning and attempt ceilings terminate retryable work","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L332.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/orchestration/peritus-gates/src/descriptor.rs:16-24,108-139,161-167,248-252`; `src/reducer/apply.rs:90-118,177-219`; `src/state.rs:227-264`; `src/command.rs:22-77` (remaining paths in the gates crate).\n- **Limits:** At most 1,024 gates, 1,024 direct dependencies per gate and 1,024 evidence requirements per gate. The product of declared gate count and immutable per-gate maximum attempts must fit 65,535 before any attempt begins. Per-slot attempts are u16 and remain consumed after recovery. Plan/state bind the maximum; the command vocabulary has no allowance amendment, replenishment or continuation successor.\n- **Blocker:** Even infrastructure failure with FreshAction permission becomes Failed once attempts reach the maximum. SafeToRetry recovery also becomes Failed at the maximum. Remaining dependent gates then become Blocked and finalization produces a non-pass. Large plans are rejected on worst-case attempt accounting even if actual work would use fewer attempts. This is a lifetime work quota, not an elapsed-time requirement.\n- **Deadline distinction:** B2 and C4 timeout declarations must match exactly, but the current declaration is optional and plan hashing encodes None; D1 does not itself require a positive wall timeout. The installed caller's choices remain separate findings.\n- **Repair direction:** Separate logical gate obligation and recovery authority from finite per-dispatch attempt/accounting representations. Continue safe, authorized infrastructure recovery with preserved gate identity and history; expose any deliberate operator stopping policy instead of silently exhausting an immutable counter.\n- **Evidence scope:** Complete plan/state/command/reducer reads. The embedded descriptor test explicitly rejects two gates with 32,768 attempts each. Tests were not executed; no installed trigger was generated.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHWFdQY7mpupQGvTirdWAnZXXbF2zf1rVy1+KIV40F33LJPrUHHeDfL56+hWyClOwm2nHBXdXESXXoWcYT5eqgs="}
