{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2627,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.993347754Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"351c6e2a-6c12-53e0-ae74-e19199171dc4","title":"[L334] D1 full checkpoints impose a cumulative evidence-size ceiling below advertised per-gate maxima","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L334.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/orchestration/peritus-gates/src/wire/state.rs:51-83,152-187,268-287`; `src/wire/mod.rs:252-280`; `src/canonical.rs:25-69`; `src/durability.rs:159-170,214-237`; `src/evidence/receipt.rs:91-119`; `src/descriptor.rs:16-24`.\n- **Blocker:** Every transition encodes one complete GateStateFrame under production codec limits: 16 MiB frame, with sixteen bytes of frame overhead. Passed gates retain full publication requirements, admitted evidence mappings and artifact metadata. No completed-gate receipt retirement, external receipt reference or whole-state capacity proof is applied by the reducer before progress.\n- **Bound analysis:** Each requirement is written once as a 32-byte declaration and again in a 104-byte admitted mapping. The individual advertised maxima of 1,024 gates and 1,024 requirements per gate therefore allow 136 MiB of those fields alone, before slots, attempts, artifacts and headers. This arithmetic describes the D1 representation mismatch; no maximally populated B2 contract or large passing fixture was built in this audit.\n- **Consequence:** Any otherwise admissible successor above the frame ceiling fails with Codec/Quarantine before C0 append. In-memory authority remains at the old state, so preserving the same candidate cannot complete further evidence publication through this representation. Earlier successful checks remain durable, and cancellation may still be representable; this is not a claim that every control command fails at the same threshold.\n- **Repair direction:** Use bounded current frontier plus exact immutable receipt references and independently paged records. Validate representation admission before effects and preserve post-effect observations separately from presentation/cumulative checkpoint capacity.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOjbg9iKYnOBEpsG08oIYW9clR3J8vTGcL2uXQIuieOK/KLZOJ93rZSmfPQHjypYaNOul52dopFiewEy0OambQ0="}
