r; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIe1wouvbw9YWLAMfguygUHwU65OuwiZOEx06zcmAbadUk7fitmI0FH809JKy5d071nGQJoBkh+a5+r2vE7RxAE="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2629,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.998272940Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"6584acd7-e633-53fb-8d88-4e5b9af89cad","title":"[L335] D1 progress and recovery synchronously copy complete state and replay complete history","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L335.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/orchestration/peritus-gates/src/reducer.rs:58-85,88-113,120-143`; `src/canonical.rs:11-79`; `src/durability.rs:79-95,295-345`; `src/durability/lifecycle.rs:24-61`; `src/engine/publication.rs:57-85`; `src/wire/state.rs:51-87`.\n- **Blocker:** Each accepted command clones and hashes every retained slot, receipt and consumed execution/action identity, then constructs and encodes another full checkpoint. Resume loads every aggregate record and semantically reduces every event from genesis. Each evidence publication independently reloads all records to locate one authoritative result. Plan-free pause/resume still loads the complete event collection and checkpoint.\n- **Consequence:** Growing attempt/evidence history increases synchronous CPU, allocation and database work for progress and controls. Replay that repeatedly hashes growing identity/evidence collections can be quadratic in retained history. No bounded incremental recovery frontier, indexed result lookup or cancellation/yield point is present in these paths. No latency measurement or live-lock reproduction was performed.\n- **Repair direction:** Preserve exact predecessor/authority validation using verified incremental checkpoints, paged/indexed history and immutable evidence roots, with responsive control admission independent of bulk reconstruction.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQI8cRSOKH80e4m/D+BXUWhTfmyHj/YC97AgA8PBLU+ZoiqXDZDOkWIXAilpFpNtxKtJ2RxGKHUiwOovO95vXUwo="}
