predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQChenCj0jils7Xynwu/WmZn3ZhZEl3KL0O7CwlhzQncNbYKOh11RPN61mynnqCPWw+SnqRwWNiS0b/sSo45+uwU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2631,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:49.002676152Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"afba0790-cc43-5bb1-be08-659f88ff1b4a","title":"[L336] D1 pause freezes effect observations and its effect shell is synchronous","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L336.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/orchestration/peritus-gates/src/reducer/apply.rs:26-37,55-59,121-133,246-278`; `src/engine.rs:160-179,231-287,294-315`.\n- **Blocker:** A paused run cannot record a result, classify recovery or publish evidence; only resuming/cancelling permits those observations again. GateEngine also refuses pause/resume and other commands while a local dispatch permit exists, except BeginCancellation. execute consumes that permit and calls a synchronous executor while mutably borrowing the engine; that call itself has no asynchronous control/cancellation parameter.\n- **Consequence:** Pause is an observation-admission barrier as well as a new-work barrier. A terminal arriving while paused must be retained by an external caller until resume; no durable pending-observation queue exists here. A slow executor blocks this engine call unless its adapter supplies independent process control. This establishes the API constraint, not that every installed adapter lacks such control.\n- **Repair direction:** Separate permission to start new work from permission to durably settle owned effects. Keep typed incoming observations and control responsiveness available while logical progress is paused, without weakening exact identity and authority checks.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMuppp7bSJ/23tb9W/I15mF4NbNZV8l6kHGheEUxumvo/gsAkn2zYDf41jV6jiBeRhwfPm8TEVjyQDOY/1wTdAQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2632,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:49.004873822Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"afba0790-cc43-5bb1-be08-659f88ff1b4a","comment_uuid":"f6463bd2-c676-4c0b-b023-b9d223ede25f","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L336: D1 pause freezes effect observations and its effect shell is synchronous.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/orchestration/peritus-gates/src/reducer/apply.rs:26-37,55-59,121-133,246-278; src/engine.rs:160-179,231-287,294-315. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nSeparate permission to start new work from permission to durably settle owned effects. Keep typed incoming observations and control responsiveness available while logical progress is paused, without weakening exact identity and authority checks.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQC9YPCfb6bJqqjMxcMZxlRBkOO6h7BC2lhvqrFRL+9/n7DEhYMp8cMoJS41SfLTHDfT+TYofFZbakMPuy+A08Qk="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2633,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:49.007065479Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"513d8140-354a-55ff-a982-ff20ba89bf15","title":"[L337] D1 exact retry requires current successor state and restart requires an external exact plan","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L337.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/orchestration/peritus-gates/src/durability.rs:79-95,159-181,240-287`; `src/durability/lifecycle.rs:65-126`; `src/engine.rs:216-224,231-257`; `src/event.rs:14-19`; `src/state.rs:227-240`.\n- **Blocker:** Durable genesis contains the snapshot binding; state contains the plan digest and cap, but GateEngine::resume still requires the original GatePlan supplied externally. Lower commit resolution requires the latest checkpoint to equal the old command's exact successor; later legitimate progress returns ReplayAggregate. Plan-free lifecycle retry recognizes only the latest event. GateEngine::commit first reduces against its current local state, so repeating an already acknowledged old command hits stale fences before lower receipt resolution.\n- **Consequence:** Recovery depends on reconstructing the exact historical plan, and delayed duplicate delivery cannot simply return its historical success receipt after progress. D1 deliberately returns replay rather than declaring the advanced aggregate corrupt; callers still need that recovery path. Other host records may supply the plan, so this is not proof that all installed restarts lose it.\n- **Repair direction:** Store/version the authoritative plan or an exact reconstructable plan artifact and resolve historical command outcomes independently of current-head admission. Refresh current authority after resolution without creating a second effect permit.\n- **Evidence scope:** Full durability/lifecycle/engine reads. No ambiguous commit failure, delayed delivery or missing-plan fixture was run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQL8MDPhrUIpAfMTO/o1OMLKTcjQc9/x5c6vH+69YDfTb5FPlMNm0d+u+amkdFt0FQ5hJXeSXVO7OGG3kH9e0NQ4="}
