e predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQC0IWOICzRjvAopgv/RR/d4mPBC3e/kRfyhiD5aPyfd/yJTKKhwXPmsjwHKTGzD8eVjTehkhdT4AXVyaWHVVeg0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2635,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:49.011467006Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"d01c899a-146f-56be-bccd-38b100ada894","title":"[L338] Product target-gate discovery is restricted to six project families and fixed marker conventions","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L338.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/orchestration/peritus-gates/src/product/plan.rs:12-30,128-168,194-212,214-354`; `src/product/commands.rs:290-311`; `src/product/report.rs:50-65`.\n- **Blocker:** Discovery recognizes Artifact, Cargo, Node, Python, conventional SQLite and Go. It walks upward only until the nearest recognized markers, using fixed manifest/test/file naming conventions. Unrecognized candidate paths remain uncovered unless they exactly match requested artifact paths or are covered by a recognized ancestor. Supporting documentation for manifestless Python/Node is covered only when adjacent to the project root. Artifact manifests must have exactly schema_version = 1 and kind = artifact with no other fields.\n- **Consequence:** A normal CMake-only C/C++ project, or another unrecognized build system, gets no executable project contract from its own manifest. Its changed paths cannot satisfy product coverage through this planner unless a separate recognized/explicit contract exists. Treating code as a generic artifact merely to bypass the missing build contract would lose the intended validation. Removal of the nearest manifest can also change discovery rather than reconstructing its historical contract.\n- **Repair direction:** Admit host-owned, explicit project contracts and supported toolchain adapters independent of naming heuristics. Preserve complete candidate coverage while representing unavailable discovery as recoverable configuration work rather than another code-fixing loop.\n- **Evidence scope:** Complete production planner/commands/report and all planner tests read. Existing fixtures exercise the recognized families; no CMake or other unsupported-family fixture was run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQF6Iqnwq7LsUTHlUFHj9Q+DakcfRZPqYcpCG4Kn0EX+ofGrjmef08LeP2RsvOJjGmE7udTkxc8ZXtStSVCmK+w0="}
