usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNKAuoDujgyHTUqDu4sWuxSB+x3q5pXj/5SdFG46EvX+BumZQpMb/yCi67Bhan9crxVHCHlH9E5qjULc2WAwYwQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2637,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:49.016264581Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"96e430e0-3c02-5f4f-b893-2aab5ace0068","title":"[L339] Fixed product gate commands can demand an invalid feature/toolchain/dependency configuration","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L339.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/orchestration/peritus-gates/src/product/commands.rs:60-103,106-143,146-212,221-249,263-279`; `src/product/plan/tests.rs:5-53`; `src/product/plan/tests/manifestless.rs:167-239`.\n- **Restrictions:** Rust always runs format plus check/build/test/clippy with locked inputs, all targets and all features; a literal standalone [workspace] line adds --workspace. Clippy denies every warning. Python requirements verification always uses pip install --dry-run --no-index; pytest/ruff selection uses fixed layout/text heuristics. The first present lockfile wins among uv, poetry, pdm, pipenv and pixi, then fixed virtualenv paths, then python from the host. There is no per-project command or feature selection parameter in this API.\n- **Consequence:** A legitimate project with mutually exclusive optional features, unavailable platform/GPU targets, an intentional warning policy, or dependencies requiring an authorized index lookup can fail these generated commands even when its requested configuration is valid. Merely changing candidate code cannot resolve every toolchain/dependency cause. These are conditional environmental/policy barriers, not elapsed deadlines; no representative incompatible project was executed here.\n- **Repair direction:** Bind gates to the project's explicit accepted configuration and failure ownership, preserving reproducibility and quality requirements. Recover or surface missing toolchain/dependency authority through the correct owner instead of indiscriminately sending the result to a fixer. Preserve an explicit offline policy where the actual execution contract requires it.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAU39lLUzQkQWlVHU2lqQ6q2d6CgxC8cGhH4sIrhjMnMBpPM0FU9J5MeZ00pBmCz+6zdhFJlluHiur4hYblOyA4="}
