oritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMqo7FQ5Glzk2HMZenCrm+Q+8UgMmQsiBLdnkziyXBS/HOt+SHUAsXGjxHXOfm1EQpx5v0Fw/L03ZM41K00TRw0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2639,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:49.020964100Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"25eab58b-753c-5eb2-b3f4-e6692050a706","title":"[L340] Product target-gate acceptance universally requires a nonempty changed-path inventory","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L340.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/orchestration/peritus-gates/src/product/plan.rs:194-205`; `src/product/report.rs:50-65,97-115`.\n- **Blocker:** has_complete_coverage returns false whenever changed_paths is empty, even if every task-specific constraint and all available observations pass. TargetGateReport requires that predicate before acceptance. This is a general planner rule, separate from the explicit single-file delta rule in L177.\n- **Consequence:** Verification-only work or a task whose requested state already exists cannot pass through this gate report without manufacturing a change. Applicability depends on whether the host assigns such tasks to this candidate-acceptance path; the API alone does not establish that every conversation uses it. The embedded empty-plan test demonstrates rejection but includes a failing constraint as well, so it is not an isolated reproduction of the all-constraints-passing case.\n- **Repair direction:** Decide whether an actual mutation is required from the current task's typed obligations, and permit truthful evidence-backed completion when the requested state is already satisfied. Retain delta coverage for tasks that do require candidate changes.\n- **Evidence scope:** Complete manual source read; no tests were executed or new fixtures generated. The report also trusts the supplied record count/success rather than matching each command identity, which callers must account for when claiming exact command coverage.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJMI3Nl4eu7UYkPQ4iPbAV/N+AtTM9IdA2zczs8wvXzLhVSz/tdjadMijs1qsk+zeiSO7GkyHxdoeUcXScApBAc="}
