ression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGEjGpumnncIECs2oyK2/zDuADGHnNAtotYDv+buc+TCvxDEvUYjCGHWCS/JAbGFpl5ASz7f/b8llCoCSaQn3g8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2641,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:49.025768520Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"17fe8ac0-1786-5593-ad92-4eb93386b8b9","title":"[L341] Run settlement makes user wait and recovery immutable terminal decisions","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L341.\n\n- **Source:** `crates/orchestration/peritus-run-settlement/src/cause.rs:9-33`; `src/disposition.rs:9-21`; `src/reducer.rs:21-33,47-64,67-91`; `src/settlement.rs:24-42,62-78`; `src/verified.rs:154-165`; `tests/reducer.rs:195-239,242-281`.\n- **Blocker:** settle stores one terminal decision for every cause, including UserWait, Recovery, Provider, Context and Deadline. After that, both observe and settle reject AlreadySettled; there is no answer/reconcile/resume transition on that reducer. A qualified candidate is retained but WaitingForUser and RecoveryRequired explicitly override Accepted. Deadline here is only a descriptive cause supplied by callers; this crate has no clock, timeout, TTL or deadline enforcement.\n- **Consequence:** Recoverable waiting/reconciliation cannot be represented as continued activity of the same settlement reducer. A host must create/reconstruct another unsettled reducer, carry forward the checkpoint and retain the enclosing logical execution separately. The candidate remains available and the original observation is not deleted. Whether a host does that correctly is a caller responsibility, so the domain alone does not prove session destruction.\n- **Repair direction:** Distinguish immutable delivery/settlement observations from the durable logical run's resumable lifecycle. User answers and resolved recovery should advance that logical execution without losing context, candidate obligations or historical truth; exactly-once final completion should apply at the actual final boundary.\n- **Evidence scope:** All sixteen crate files read. Existing tests explicitly preserve the candidate under wait/recovery and reject post-terminal updates, but do not reopen such a reducer. Tests/proofs were not executed. Source checks allow qualification to decrease and retain/reconcile provenance; these are evidence correctness rules, not arbitrary lifetime quotas.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFIbqZjjABFqJ5IFy3Beb4dxNEPHEUvI7wSCy6d8apL7Xs9cHdm+hZRM79fBTg2XUQUkv6sOrhsXthiJcDKzQQE="}
