{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2643,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:49.030409912Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"3ab99fcf-5d10-518c-ab57-f684a11c7cb0","title":"[L342] C6 memory has fixed per-record and whole-replay ceilings","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L342.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/orchestration/peritus-memory/src/claim.rs:11-16,182-185,298-313`, `src/evidence.rs:9-12,82-88`, `src/feedback.rs:1-73`, `src/retrieval/types.rs:12-15,167-178,249-263`, `src/retrieval/plan.rs:41-46,111-129`, `src/index/rebuild.rs:19-27` (all paths under the same crate).\n- Limits: 65,536 content bytes per memory, token estimate 1..1,000,000, 64 features/required feature keys, 256 source events and 256 identifiers in each evidence set, positive/negative feedback each at most 10,000. Retrieval accepts at most 4,096 records and 4,096 tombstones, selects 1..256 complete records under a mandatory positive u32 token budget, and has no continuation cursor. Index rebuild applies the 4,096-record cap to raw immutable revisions **before** selecting the latest revision per identity; superseded historical snapshots and deletion markers still consume the input count.\n- Consequence: a caller feeding full durable history can hit the rebuild ceiling with few live memories; a corpus over 4,096 active records cannot be passed to this retrieval API as a whole. Individual large procedures/evidence histories also require external partitioning. This crate has no streaming rebuild, paginated global ranking, or rollover operation. Feedback is supplied afresh by review/release, so the 10,000 bound is a representation restriction, not a proven automatically accumulated lifetime counter. Token selection excludes rather than cancels the whole run.\n- Repair direction: separate retained history from the active query view, support incremental/paged replay and global retrieval, and store complete claim/provenance artifacts behind references. Keep provider-window selection separate from logical memory lifetime. Scope: domain restrictions confirmed by full reads; installed memory growth path not reproduced here. Constructor/retrieval tests inspected, not run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPSNZePTzV1YpacjTKqwMeJkCPhoEayhJrN1tDY1H0aGKrIvy9RLxI0+YPMFR8MKShPyk6u4D53DgNp08Gr7DwU="}
