authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long productive read/write sessions through repeated compaction and segment boundaries, source/dependency changes, non-ASCII and large evidence, interrupted checkpoint publication, then reopen the same lineage and prove that valid grounding is reused and stale targets are reread. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJ9qO0rNrPV4Vlz4a7jHfkCqzirhSFQOk1g4UXyTfaDc88ZziVjSf3ovxOa444Lp6UsDPjMK8yU8P3w1TLVnqQE="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2645,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:49.036608013Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"1d1be852-35f0-56fc-bc66-dfe85f4c728f","title":"[L343] C6 optional expiry is immutable across review; freshness crosses an epoch barrier","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L343.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/orchestration/peritus-memory/src/record.rs:52-100`, `src/record/transitions.rs:22-55,90-129,131-167`, `src/retrieval/filter.rs:39-58,73-85,89-105`, `src/retrieval/ranking.rs:94-124`, `tests/retrieval_matrix.rs:153-175,223-265`, `tests/lifecycle_matrix.rs:93-109`.\n- Behavior: caller-supplied optional logical expiry excludes a record at `expiry <= query observation`. Review and explicit quarantine release preserve that original expiry; this API exposes no renewal/removal. Explicit Expired/Superseded states cannot reopen. Optional review-age policy rejects missing review or **any different logical epoch**, even without elapsed ticks exceeding the configured age. Confidence, accepted claim type, required features, supporting evidence, role visibility and optional negative/contradiction thresholds are additional eligibility barriers. A zero signal threshold can exclude even a zero negative ratio. Recency also falls to zero after 10,000 ticks or in another epoch, but is a ranking component rather than a standalone expiry.\n- Consequence: renewed evidence/review alone cannot restore eligibility after a previously supplied expiry. An epoch change makes all prior-epoch reviews stale whenever age policy is enabled. None expiry/age is supported; there is no wall-clock timer, mandatory default TTL, or physical session deletion in this crate. Logical expiry can require a replacement memory identity or caller reconstruction even while the claim remains useful.\n- Repair direction: distinguish explicit semantic invalidation from elapsed-time freshness; make accepted refresh/replacement policy explicit and preserve stable lineage and provenance. Persistent working context should not expire just because an observation clock changed. Scope: source-confirmed conditional behavior; caller policy/default selection and installed impact not established here. Existing tests inspected, not run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBrHBvA5VWUpb4y/gy35chNT0uYX+IfltyAuOFrvDfLYt8qtDun3UZaEyDlkzhaUnaCHRiXjS2JyT0IozyBL7gc="}
