ry root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long productive read/write sessions through repeated compaction and segment boundaries, source/dependency changes, non-ASCII and large evidence, interrupted checkpoint publication, then reopen the same lineage and prove that valid grounding is reused and stale targets are reread. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEwVDEy4T+ZebCLVZKKsE7piL2MwGSWvABGTiPuChS9sKTaICs6PLgEWVA1We/3DK814ATucm8qRS3opaSpGTgI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2647,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:49.041236740Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"85e210a8-121c-51fa-9839-84376eb34247","title":"[L344] C6 index retrieval still scans and copies the whole view synchronously","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L344.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/orchestration/peritus-memory/src/index/types.rs:113-122,149-159`, `src/index/rebuild.rs:126-155,173-285`, `src/index/canonical.rs:17-50,281-286`, `src/retrieval/plan.rs:181-238,240-271,301-328`, `src/retrieval/output.rs:287-309`.\n- Behavior: index rebuild cross-checks every tombstone against every input revision, scans tombstones for each latest record, clones each retained record, inserts posting groups through linear scans, and copies the entire canonical content/metadata into a new byte vector before hashing. Retrieval ignores those posting lists, scans the complete active view, insertion-sorts identities and ranks, and validates tombstones pairwise. These operations are synchronous and expose no cancellation/yield/paging contract.\n- Consequence: growing memory causes repeated full-view work and potentially quadratic ordering/replay work despite the index abstraction. That can delay the host lane that calls it; it is a structural responsiveness concern, **not** a measured explanation of the live lockup. The fixed 4,096 cap bounds this implementation by rejecting larger inputs rather than making persistent growth resumable.\n- Repair direction: incremental verified index maintenance, indexed candidate selection with global deterministic merging, streaming digests, and a cancellation-responsive host execution lane. Scope: full crate including tests read; no latency benchmark or installed-run reproduction during this audit.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQINTmw9XL6s5C8yIgTSnfUgPNAD/pMsNpKObVutByoG1aRXmC70Z/7vSzN3UmpvtCp/2eCCWWGbgiqrHSfC2jAY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2648,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:49.043476834Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"85e210a8-121c-51fa-9839-84376eb34247","comment_uuid":"0dd59a2a-b75d-4019-8079-7a660b154024","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L344: C6 index retrieval still scans and copies the whole view synchronously.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/orchestration/peritus-memory/src/index/types.rs:113-122,149-159; src/index/rebuild.rs:126-155,173-285; src/index/canonical.rs:17-50,281-286; src/retrieval/plan.rs:181-238,240-271,301-328; src/retrieval/output.rs:287-309. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nincremental verified index maintenance, indexed candidate selection with global deterministic merging, streaming digests, and a cancellation-responsive host execution lane. Scope: full crate including tests read; no latency benchmark or installed-run reproduction during this audit.\n\nPreserve: governing inputs, complete pending tool protocol pairs, exact source/lineage references, explicit permissions, unresolved effect truth and task-role/native-provider identity. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long productive read/write sessions through repeated compaction and segment boundaries, source/dependency changes, non-ASCII and large evidence, interrupted checkpoint publication, then reopen the same lineage and prove that valid grounding is reused and stale targets are reread. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEiFJMEmrm+ukfb4nX4RafoZPA1a+u9wgv/gAtLqhCWapPj9KBrWcVkQZDlKSK5VqZt8/ZVLhc6SZ+vTFsT9DgA="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2649,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:49.045943923Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"bb01e378-9d2a-52bd-a08a-16ca3ebbbc45","title":"[L345] B1 requires immutable finite budgets and cannot replenish consumed capacity","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L345.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/foundation/peritus-budget/src/limits.rs:8-20,115-137`, `src/amounts.rs:57-81`, `src/command/vocabulary.rs:18-41`, `src/transition/allocation/begin.rs:34-61,145-223`, `src/transition/lifecycle/retry.rs:29-107,127-147`, `src/transition/lifecycle/seal.rs:67-79`, `src/transition/lifecycle/close.rs:67-125,157-160,232-259` (all paths under the same crate).\n- Limits: every account has finite u64 limits for model tokens, provider cost microunits, accountable active-effect milliseconds, attempts and retries. Zero is immediately exhausted; there is no Unlimited, amendment, top-up, unseal, or reopen command. Every new Begin charges exactly one attempt; a new reservation for an already retained exact action/revision must charge one retry and wait for all prior matching attempts to become terminal. Consumed amounts remain inclusive at every ancestor. Closing a child returns only unused delegation, not consumption or charged attempts.\n- Consequence: once a root or immutable child consumes a dimension, ordinary settlement cannot replenish that consumption. `InsufficientBudget` says AfterAccountingChange, but no accounting transition can restore already consumed capacity; unused reservations/delegations can be released. A sealed account cannot resume new work. Per-operation reservation size can also deny work before actual usage reaches the account limit. Exact old Begin/allocation replay is resolved before new-work phase checks, a useful distinction from the broken latest-head-only replay paths recorded earlier.\n- Repair direction: distinguish descriptive accounting from explicitly requested spending/resource constraints; support unlimited logical execution and durable authorized budget amendments without replacing execution/context identity. Preserve actual costs and exactly-once accounting. Scope: B1 API confirmed; this effect-free crate does not schedule a wall-clock kill, and host defaults/installed bindings require caller evidence. No tests run.\n\n- Test evidence update: `tests/adversarial.rs:147-160` explicitly treats a zero root ceiling as valid but rejects the first attempt; `tests/retry.rs:12-50` exhausts two attempts/one retry. Small fixture values are not installed defaults. Tests read, not run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIAsCR3loeuteOsV1KgERZw/q6IjLyS2qmCRlla/zIP70tc/cc5JwTIP3Z3qApiCvqhigP5RvI97rri550SUqwI="}
