n under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long productive read/write sessions through repeated compaction and segment boundaries, source/dependency changes, non-ASCII and large evidence, interrupted checkpoint publication, then reopen the same lineage and prove that valid grounding is reused and stale targets are reread. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFwe/UKdbY6Gp1S7OqVL42pTimLEyYKhq3JkaUkGDSyfMYLvWfhGjipu19ScRH2KG/7dod5w8fQ8JNLllnUUVwQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2651,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:49.050248069Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"71b8b1e6-3922-5c31-8356-fa2869888985","title":"[L346] B1 one reservation overrun permanently faults the entire ancestor lineage","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L346.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/foundation/peritus-budget/src/transition/reconciliation/observation.rs:94-103,115-151,204-218`, `src/transition/reconciliation/observation/terminal.rs:151-182,232-233`, `src/transition/accounting/fault.rs:78-110`, `src/state.rs:23-34`, `src/transition/reconciliation/finalization.rs:174-225,236-271`, `src/transition/reconciliation/finalization/cancellation.rs:112-154`, `src/command/vocabulary.rs:18-41`.\n- Behavior: any cumulative usage dimension above the immutable **operation reservation** consumes the remaining reserved ceiling, stores the raw report, marks the reservation OverrunFaulted, and faults its account plus every ancestor through the root. This occurs even if total root capacity would otherwise be available. There is no reservation enlargement, corrected-overrun reconciliation, or account recovery command. Both exact full-ceiling settlement and ambiguous settlement consume all outstanding reservation; later accurate final usage is not accepted in those terminal phases. Cancelling Held releases the reservation but keeps the precharged attempt; active effects must settle through the other paths.\n- Consequence: one under-estimated operation or erroneous usage report can permanently deny new work to sibling accounts through the shared faulted root. Recovery of a truthful later usage report cannot undo that fault in this model. This is an accounting/lifecycle barrier, not a timer implemented here. Existing active reservations can still be reconciled: there is no general require-open check on settlement, so this finding does not claim cancellation/cleanup is blocked solely by exhausted amounts.\n- Repair direction: persist raw observations and resource incidents separately from logical run termination, admit truthful corrections with exact monotonic accounting rules, and make any spending stop an explicit resumable policy decision scoped to its owner. Do not silently turn a per-operation estimate miss into permanent whole-run loss. Scope: source-confirmed domain behavior; installed incident and tests not reproduced in this read-only audit.\n\n- Test evidence update: `tests/ledger.rs:245-289` uses root tokens 20 and child reservation 10, reports 11, asserts **both child and root Faulted**, and rejects later root work despite remaining root capacity. This is an existing source fixture, not a fresh execution.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCDbEHjvR0Q/TIp3gsUbZ09DVNDCihifwg15rDffBybxpJCgwck+qkNktYb5wR62yKrr+E5PSQD3rKDCcRjxpQc="}
