n or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long productive read/write sessions through repeated compaction and segment boundaries, source/dependency changes, non-ASCII and large evidence, interrupted checkpoint publication, then reopen the same lineage and prove that valid grounding is reused and stale targets are reread. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEpL5rEBpbAKGxUlJUtdekAmNr7MQY1qZebWiaxmrcS8e9a0tXKNnctkxk+c+KQFisbWeabdfAmlOWpcBphZCA0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2653,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:49.054809538Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"4c720477-a78e-5123-bb44-d6ee73ec4ed6","title":"[L347] B1 equal usage with new evidence can reject the final report","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L347.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/foundation/peritus-budget/src/transition/reconciliation/observation.rs:115-158,204-238`, `src/transition/reconciliation/observation/terminal/replay.rs:50-81`, `src/failure.rs:143-161`.\n- Behavior: when an active reservation already has usage evidence, **equal** cumulative amounts with a different evidence digest return BindingMismatch before the reducer considers Interim versus Final. A final report with unchanged usage but a distinct final-event digest is therefore rejected, leaving the reservation active and its unused ceiling reserved. Any downward component is separately rejected as NonmonotonicObservation. After terminal settlement only the exact stored raw report, finality and evidence replay is accepted.\n- Consequence: a provider/host that naturally binds evidence to each observation event must reuse the previous evidence digest or choose full-ceiling settlement to close unchanged usage. BindingMismatch is labeled Terminal even though the external work may have completed. This can strand accounting/retry admission if the caller lacks an explicit alternate reconciliation path. The crate README states same-evidence replay as an intended invariant; the problem is conflating an unchanged measurement with an exact event replay when finality advances.\n- Repair direction: model event identity, measurement high-water and lifecycle finality separately; allow a correctly correlated later final observation to finalize without charging the same usage twice, while retaining both evidence bindings. Scope: direct source consequence; host evidence construction not established here, no final-report reproduction run.\n\n- Test evidence update: `tests/model.rs:28-97` and `tests/retry.rs:69-110` deliberately reject unchanged interim usage with new evidence. `tests/ledger.rs:122-129` and `tests/lifecycle_reference.rs:139-155` use increased final usage; they do not cover unchanged-usage finality advancement. `tests/generated.rs:11-14,77-89` runs 4 x 64 x 24 **interim** samples. These are qualification bounds, not installed quotas; tests inspected, not run.\n\n\n\nFormal-contract evidence: `crates/foundation/peritus-budget/src/reachability/guards/outcomes.rs:36-53` requires absent/unchanged evidence when cumulative usage is unchanged even for a final report. `src/reachability/rejections/reservation.rs:65-90` specifies the same `BindingMismatch` without a finality exception. Repair therefore needs coordinated runtime, guard, rejection-model, and regression-fixture changes; the restriction is not an undocumented runtime-only branch. All budget crate files have now been read completely, with no alternate refill, reopen, root un-fault, or same-usage/new-evidence finality path found.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLTi+zAgZgFvEAiMZbVyx/XhCQ8Q0AIjy9eFLUEtEO0da+Rf4RoYUdwA6qpAtC1bkKRQVLcQRXTlFdhmzmqz0AM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2654,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:49.057097840Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"4c720477-a78e-5123-bb44-d6ee73ec4ed6","comment_uuid":"467f2b3f-fc78-4f0d-8459-dbaadd07477a","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L347: B1 equal usage with new evidence can reject the final report.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/foundation/peritus-budget/src/transition/reconciliation/observation.rs:115-158,204-238; src/transition/reconciliation/observation/terminal/replay.rs:50-81; src/failure.rs:143-161; tests/model.rs:28-97; tests/retry.rs:69-110; tests/ledger.rs:122-129; tests/lifecycle_reference.rs:139-155; tests/generated.rs:11-14,77-89; crates/foundation/peritus-budget/src/reachability/guards/outcomes.rs:36-53; src/reachability/rejections/reservation.rs:65-90. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nmodel event identity, measurement high-water and lifecycle finality separately; allow a correctly correlated later final observation to finalize without charging the same usage twice, while retaining both evidence bindings. Scope: direct source consequence; host evidence construction not established here, no final-report reproduction run.\n\nPreserve: governing inputs, complete pending tool protocol pairs, exact source/lineage references, explicit permissions, unresolved effect truth and task-role/native-provider identity. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long productive read/write sessions through repeated compaction and segment boundaries, source/dependency changes, non-ASCII and large evidence, interrupted checkpoint publication, then reopen the same lineage and prove that valid grounding is reused and stale targets are reread. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQF+44g7g/LJbakYfQjIeZBWXPWHvZUkYE9Ii4pP+Z/S3tT9xZoLa4p1VO57mW7d8UcG8YE+V4PZ5we8I4aksPg8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2655,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:49.059338964Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"2b095b4a-7410-5654-a261-8a695ec23b92","title":"[L348] B1 validates all retained accounting history on every transition and query","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L348.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/foundation/peritus-budget/src/transition.rs:89-112,149-192,254-265,297-308`, `src/state.rs:216-247,307-313`, `src/transition/validation/accounts.rs:55-115`, `src/transition/validation/reservations.rs:24-100`, `src/transition/validation/structure.rs:25-46,94-118`, `src/transition/validation/refinement.rs:60-64,113-119,157-161`, `src/transition/lifecycle/retry.rs:29-105`.\n- Behavior: each transition validates the complete input, copies all accounts and reservation tombstones, validates the complete output, and checks immutable/monotonic prefixes plus ancestor propagation. Even a checked single-account or single-reservation query revalidates the entire ledger. Each reservation performs earlier-prefix uniqueness and exact-action retry-history scans; each account recomputes child and operation-reservation sums. Closed accounts and settled/cancelled reservations remain in the vectors; shrinking them violates refinement. The closed command vocabulary has no retirement/checkpoint-fold command.\n- Consequence: reservation validation alone is quadratic in retained reservation count per query/transition; repeated operations over growing history can produce cumulative cubic validation work. There is no async yield/cancellation contract inside this pure synchronous call. It can delay whichever host lane invokes it, including observation or cancellation commands that also pay validation costs. This is a source-level complexity finding, not a measured live-session latency diagnosis or a claim that a numeric work-count cap exists here.\n- Repair direction: retain immutable receipts outside the active accounting frontier; verify incremental updates and ancestor balances, maintain identity/action indexes, and separate full-history validation from ordinary control admission. Preserve accounting integrity and old exact replay through durable indexed receipts. Scope: the complete 123-file budget crate, including proof modules and tests, is now read; no benchmark/test execution.\n\n\nAdditional source evidence: `src/accounting_prefix_model.rs:54-96,207-246` contains ordinary executable `fn` witnesses that recursively walk the remaining account/reservation suffix; the five-axis wrappers repeat that walk. `src/accounting_model.rs:257-345` and `src/accounting_model/aggregation.rs:16-78` add full-account recursive contribution witnesses to lineage charging. These are included by `src/lib.rs:11-12`, unlike erased `spec fn`/`proof fn` definitions. They add source-level recursion and traversal pressure; optimized release cost and stack behavior have not been measured, so no particular production stall or stack threshold is claimed. Account-count traversal fuel is a structural termination witness, not a configured daily-driving deadline.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGTIBEqk4L9fvs78bQcLZ2YdywsVOLDYquqAI2jjIj7wJ+ai0aMVXXcMVuGWKUpKUVugmYnpoge1OlqqjjwhNQA="}
