{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2659,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:49.068565406Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"dc244688-96fc-5c4e-a506-b4d39b193f01","title":"[L350] C6 selection rejects required context on independent finite node and byte ceilings","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L350.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/orchestration/peritus-context/src/selection.rs:39-89`, `src/selection/plan.rs:65-141,143-229`, `src/selection/certificate.rs:57-118,159-206`.\n- Behavior: selection requires positive finite maxima for selected nodes and selected bytes, in addition to the usable model input budget. Required roots are admitted with their entire dependency closure. Crossing either allocation ceiling returns `RequiredNodeLimitExceeded` or `RequiredByteLimitExceeded`, even when tokens fit; optional roots are omitted with their entire closure. There is no partial-range admission or automatic compaction in the selector. The independent certificate executes the same rejection rules.\n- Consequence: independently configured collection/byte ceilings can prevent a model turn. The physical model window remains a real capacity constraint; these additional ceilings are separate. This pure API permits constructing a larger policy, but exposes no continuation, paging, or negotiated allocation recovery itself. Installed values and error handling must be connected through callers before attributing the live session stall.\n- Repair direction: preserve the durable context inventory and required references separately from the materialized model view; admit ranges and dependency references under recoverable allocation policy. Capacity pressure must produce an actionable continuation or compaction path without dropping task/session identity. No tests or fresh runtime reproduction run.\n\n- Test-source corroboration: `tests/selection_matrix.rs:120-140,190-213` expects required byte/node hard errors and atomic optional capacity omissions; `tests/selection_certificate.rs:198-220` requires exact capacity-failure priority. These tests were read completely, not run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDJxCSnTG8Z1jaWd4GjUp5+7OMOMzBgItGf2xBiijUrw4C3h99XU3bYscAV+H+RZFB6xA2hN1r2QZZtZ5ZEPjAc="}
