e all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long productive read/write sessions through repeated compaction and segment boundaries, source/dependency changes, non-ASCII and large evidence, interrupted checkpoint publication, then reopen the same lineage and prove that valid grounding is reused and stale targets are reread. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCsMwSwiGhd6x3dRql5XVpO8tYB3S7EyL30rAmYSQSaDRgM6jaU4XyqICwWww6VbZ0BQSEFDQ7n1FUKHyWI1agY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2661,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:49.072966987Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"e32f10d2-9599-5413-95aa-cd6300a44dd1","title":"[L351] C6 synchronous selection repeats full closure computation and full-plan validation","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L351.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/orchestration/peritus-context/src/selection/closure.rs:38-83`, `src/selection/ordering.rs:34-51,65-98`, `src/selection/plan.rs:37-41,65-141,143-229,255-269`, `src/selection/certificate.rs:24-257,264-282`, `src/verified.rs:15-183`.\n- Behavior: each dependency closure executes graph-node-count complete passes without exiting when closure stops changing; dependency lookup scans the graph. Required roots recompute closure individually, including already selected roots. Optional ordering and render ordering use insertion sorts; render comparisons perform graph lookup. Production selection then calls an independent executable replay of the complete selection state machine. Production construction, certificate construction, and certificate acceptance each validate the full plan, with linear graph/dependency membership lookups and pairwise uniqueness scans.\n- Consequence: growing context can amplify synchronous work even when it is admissible. This is a source-grounded performance/blocking risk, not evidence of an artificial timeout or proof of the installed lockup. Node-count closure passes are a structural termination bound, not a work quota. No scheduling yield or cancellation boundary exists inside these pure calls; callers may isolate execution, which remains to be traced.\n- Repair direction: index stable node identities, compute reachability with a work queue or cached closures, exit on a fixed point, and use efficient deterministic sorting. Maintain independent validation using an incremental certificate rather than reproducing the entire constructor on every turn; preserve the checked relation and reject corrupt input. Runtime/optimized-build cost has not been measured.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNTlMxnTJGzkpmz2RHLc3AurY6oeVdKEQExDHxH6J22GBTRk0dgsCALgMUbAuWy/ozLrlTpRzX8uie+bMA9yagg="}
