rojections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long productive read/write sessions through repeated compaction and segment boundaries, source/dependency changes, non-ASCII and large evidence, interrupted checkpoint publication, then reopen the same lineage and prove that valid grounding is reused and stale targets are reread. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQINFylJLU4dPf7M9YEfURYTNlW9wLDwEN4FAbJkdYDekejfEm/VSIIBuZpAR59meEnVb0EZ1r/+BrWejiVwpTAU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2663,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:49.077428180Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"13565f9d-1ad5-5ecc-b436-dbcbc9e669bf","title":"[L352] C6 an oversized optional estimate can fail the whole selection before omission","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L352.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/orchestration/peritus-context/src/selection/closure.rs:118-170`, `src/selection/plan.rs:165-188`, `src/selection/certificate.rs:159-177`; positive token-estimate constructors previously read under L349.\n- Behavior: optional closure accounting and accumulated totals use checked arithmetic before comparing against the model budget. Overflow returns `ArithmeticOverflow` for the whole result rather than an optional omission. Positive `u64` token estimates have no constructor upper bound; an optional closure whose estimate overflows when added to already selected tokens takes this path even though it necessarily cannot fit any usable input budget.\n- Consequence: an oversized optional item can prevent otherwise valid required context from being returned. This is a representational arithmetic boundary, not a timer. The complete optional phases of production and independent replay both implement it; no alternative skip is present there. The concrete boundary case is inferred from the source and has not been executed.\n- Repair direction: compare optional costs against remaining headroom before addition, with an explicit over-capacity omission result; preserve checked exact accounting for accepted items and required-content failures. Migrate production and certificate semantics together.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do