{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2665,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:49.081967446Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"4ec0ed1b-b446-56dd-b087-2b91fe44f151","title":"[L353] C6 compaction cannot replace required sources and requires an already selected source set","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L353.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/orchestration/peritus-context/src/compaction/validation.rs:108-129,131-141,155-182,204-233`, `src/compaction/replacement.rs:119-128,206-260`, `src/compaction.rs:181-267`.\n- Behavior: validation accepts only source ranges whose complete nodes already appear in the supplied plan, rejects protected content and mixed context classes, retains complete source nodes in validation evidence, and requires a strict token reduction. It marks every required root or required dependency as required, including an otherwise optional source selected for a required root. Atomic replacement then rejects all such required sources with `RequiredCompactionSource`. Validation alone can produce evidence that replacement refuses. Source ranges are audit lineage, not a partial live-node replacement.\n- Consequence: this replacement path cannot recover a required closure that exceeds L350: it needs a preexisting selected source set and refuses to replace its required members. Omitted large optional nodes also cannot enter this compaction path from the same plan. This does not establish that every caller lacks another recovery path. Protection and authority rules preserve important semantics; removing them indiscriminately would lose required content rather than repair continuity.\n- Repair direction: separate immutable required evidence and original source references from their bounded render representation. Permit checked derived views while retaining durable originals, authority boundaries, required obligations, and exact lineage. Provide a capacity-recovery entry point that can inspect durable sources beyond the currently selected model view. Replacement graph/dependency implementation and tests remain under review; no tests run.\n\n- Test-source corroboration: `tests/compaction_matrix.rs:221-244,380-401` explicitly expects omitted sources to fail validation, while required sources pass validation and then fail replacement. All compaction implementation/model/test files are now completely read; no other replacement recovery entry point exists within this crate. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFUQtQ+hnGRMP9aZkIGP044XPWLLXdaMRKh9BO5AngMM9i6K8/2j8lU18yrLWQZfcyKhX2EZnnaPS7c9BQMICA4="}
