{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2667,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:49.086508010Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"de849c9c-7958-5930-bb88-fbcf38217a32","title":"[L354] C6 reducing compaction can fail on the union of individually admissible dependencies","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L354.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/orchestration/peritus-context/src/compaction/replacement/dependencies.rs:21-62,145-172,214-234`, `src/compaction/replacement/graph.rs:30-34,157-181,339`, `src/node/metadata.rs:191-254` (previously read).\n- Behavior: the replacement node receives the canonical union of every replaced source dependency outside the replaced set. Dependency metadata is reconstructed under the original graph's finite dependency-per-node limit. A set of optional, individually valid sources can have a larger union than that limit; a strictly smaller token summary is then rejected before graph replacement. Surviving nodes are all rebuilt with rewritten dependency vectors, followed by construction and validation of the entire new graph. Membership and canonical insertion use linear scans.\n- Consequence: token reduction alone does not guarantee an applicable compaction, and the replacement API has no parameter to negotiate more dependency capacity. This can obstruct the optional-context recovery path as well as the required-source exclusion in L353. Larger graph reconstruction is possible through the separate pure constructors; no installed automatic retry has been established. The union-over-bound scenario follows from source admission rules and is not a newly executed fixture.\n- Repair direction: keep external lineage/reference sets as durable indexed objects instead of requiring one materialized metadata vector to contain the complete union. Make allocation recovery explicit while preserving dependency closure and atomic publication. Avoid copying unchanged nodes and repeating full graph checks where an exact incremental certificate suffices. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQORs5510ICShPCWMr3rTVUprrh/v5EtDTPefj4U7PUgjOqR2rrcFPNbZ5EeFj1564Qd06w/NvrwdZNYYV070UQo="}
