s, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long productive read/write sessions through repeated compaction and segment boundaries, source/dependency changes, non-ASCII and large evidence, interrupted checkpoint publication, then reopen the same lineage and prove that valid grounding is reused and stale targets are reread. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFULfus/3dWGa/C7zSfIxAKJP1GCLoM5+K9+0wGnQKO6stLFqpVWpob40hpTZRHljK4StXWMv4pQ3ODKBucJ/A4="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2669,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:49.091630271Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"b2953da5-ea5e-5947-9166-94d6b1ea6c91","title":"[L355] E1 harness configuration has eleven compiled ceilings that can only tighten","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L355.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/orchestration/peritus-harness/src/domain/limits.rs:7-89,195-207`; imported patch bounds already completely read under L006 at `crates/runtime/peritus-patch/src/set.rs:11-16`.\n- Behavior: compiled maxima are 4 MiB manifest, 1,024 components, 32,768 dependency edges, 256 dependencies per component, 8 MiB per component, 8 MiB total materialized payload, 10,000 retained revisions, 10,000 retained receipts, 16 MiB event, 16 MiB state, and 1,024 retained diagnostics. All eleven fields are private. The only mutation API rejects zero and any value above the current value, so a previously tightened policy also cannot return to its compiled ceiling through that API. There is no unlimited variant or public arbitrary constructor.\n- Consequence: configuration cannot remove these synthetic collection/history/byte ceilings. Source admission, durable revision/receipt history and complete checkpoint encoding need separate caller analysis; declarations here alone do not prove when a live run stops. No run-duration timer or session TTL appears in this policy.\n- Repair direction: separate bounded in-memory/materialized batches from durable inventories and histories, use paged content and immutable history segments, and permit explicit allocation policy negotiation. Preserve exact artifact and lineage binding. Constructors, history, wire, and runtime enforcement remain to be read; no tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIyhiCVHKf8ruO8DFTpSYNRhz5G3RDjtzK+xST6bAqx24Oit7uAh1mf7FYacbfqv/lLMsWYvpJqcrvCht5zWdA4="}
