the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEoR36GS9xkg/gOhwPrI15Dx7I/GvBgIQP5r+Zib17IFp/svy8gpxoU+5DLF4VaX5MkLlCc9zNYPBsR2GuaWGQY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2671,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:49.096322573Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"009aa021-26d4-5296-90cc-0d189d15d1d9","title":"[L356] E1 harness textual identities and paths have fixed portable-shape and byte limits","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L356.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/orchestration/peritus-harness/src/domain/identity.rs:7-47`, `src/domain/value.rs:5-10,22-42,62-82,102-118,138-179,192-225`.\n- Behavior: component IDs are limited to 128 ASCII bytes with an alphanumeric first character and only alphanumerics, dot, underscore or hyphen afterward. Owner strings are at most 256 bytes, provenance 4,096 bytes, media type 255 visible-ASCII bytes. Paths are at most 4,096 bytes, 256 segments, 255 bytes per segment and enforce Windows device-name/trailing-dot/trailing-space restrictions on every platform; backslash and colon are forbidden. Sources must be below `.peritus-harness/components/`; targets cannot name control metadata at any segment.\n- Consequence: valid host-platform filenames or longer provenance can fail harness declaration before execution. Root containment and protected metadata are authority/integrity boundaries distinct from representational byte limits; fixed portability rules are a product policy, not a timer. Later manifest loading and materialization callers remain under review.\n- Repair direction: represent native filesystem identities losslessly with explicit portability compatibility, and externalize long provenance to digest-bound content. Keep no-follow containment and control-root protection. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQE3JiRgSmRCjbjAWO0M00nfPsLOPQe45ZTOmyVmLPbANf4mHHjg3X3WxJg6bkcXe7CetyD9MpBZNRuUSIY7qmA0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2672,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:49.098806456Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"009aa021-26d4-5296-90cc-0d189d15d1d9","comment_uuid":"20cef573-e363-4d9c-86ab-64078ad1b2b6","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L356: E1 harness textual identities and paths have fixed portable-shape and byte limits.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/orchestration/peritus-harness/src/domain/identity.rs:7-47; src/domain/value.rs:5-10,22-42,62-82,102-118,138-179,192-225. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nrepresent native filesystem identities losslessly with explicit portability compatibility, and externalize long provenance to digest-bound content. Keep no-follow containment and control-root protection. No tests run.\n\nPreserve: canonical digest and schema identity, shared writer/reader admissibility, malformed-input rejection before allocation, exact causal ordering, actual provider/OS capability boundaries and preserved accepted historical evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQISRWAuSlPkpXIT3S866ZPlkp9pk4YousMr5JiwphEgT4oTaju1Vb+FdWzjzzfHr+G8N9Q81ysIfNc3O4kzZ8AY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2673,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:49.101121805Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"4a56210d-85c3-535f-bc86-bb3fb455a7d1","title":"[L357] E1 feature lists can pass construction and encoding but fail canonical reconstruction","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L357.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/orchestration/peritus-harness/src/domain/compatibility.rs:87-117,190-197`, `src/domain/component_canonical.rs:98-144`, `src/domain/graph.rs:29-35,124-155,163-179,279-295`, `src/domain/graph_validation.rs:11-72,185-211,340-365`.\n- Behavior: compatibility and environment constructors require canonical feature order but impose no feature count limit; graph checking checks dependencies and content totals, then accumulates required feature unions without a count limit. Canonical encoding writes complete feature lists. Both declaration and graph decoders reject a feature list longer than `max_dependency_edges`, even though feature requirements are not dependency edges. Feature text separately has a fixed 128-byte lowercase ASCII limit.\n- Consequence: a checked graph can encode bytes it cannot later decode. For example, with the dependency-edge limit tightened to one, a declaration can require two supported canonical features and zero dependency edges, pass checking, and fail reconstruction. This is inferred from the completely read pure constructors and decoder; whether persistence catches it before commit remains to be traced. No fixture executed.\n- Repair direction: use an explicit feature-capacity model consistently on admission, encoding and restoration, or externalize paged feature inventories. A dependency-edge quota must not silently govern an unrelated feature list at restart. Round-trip admissibility is a prerequisite for publishing durable state; migrate wire and caller checks together.\n\n- Persistence trace: `src/durability/commit.rs:107-126,140-185`, `src/wire/state.rs:17-18,56-66`, `src/wire/event.rs:35-51,58-75`, `src/durability/recovery.rs:91-114` encode and publish the supplied checked transition without an admission round-trip; first restore decodes the nested graph and fails. Thus the pure mismatch has a reachable commit-before-recovery route under these E1 APIs, assuming required artifacts are finalized and ordinary C0 conditions hold. No executed reproduction or installed-use claim.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQO2xzEnMxgRiFbXfnS6jU0tkjHYBKcdFmGUxFQ1jScS6kG3ei5gxm350gUYRhr8IjRuO+rxVpraKVgxbosehug4="}
