{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2675,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:49.105509097Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"9a4f02f0-817f-5776-b2a2-2af3f00e8c79","title":"[L358] E1 revision history has lifetime count and whole-snapshot byte exhaustion without retirement","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L358.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/orchestration/peritus-harness/src/domain/history.rs:31-100,108-157,160-188,292-318`, `src/domain/revision.rs:54-64,284-297`, `src/domain/limits.rs:25-36`.\n- Behavior: history retains every complete immutable revision, including branches, in one vector. The 10,000-revision compiled ceiling rejects the next append. Every append also serializes a sorted snapshot of all revisions, each containing its complete graph, and rejects it above the configured state bound (16 MiB compiled). A rejected append pops only the new revision. There is no retirement, rollover, paging, or limits-amendment method in the fully read history API.\n- Consequence: evolution can stop at a lifetime revision count or combined metadata size even when each revision is valid and current materialization is small. Restore clones every encoded revision and rebuilds history through append, repeatedly re-encoding all prior revisions; lineage lookups are linear, ancestor traversal repeats them, and branch-tip queries scan all revision pairs. These synchronous growth risks are source-grounded; no installed timing or new runtime reproduction is claimed. Traversal bounded by retained history length is an integrity termination bound, distinct from the arbitrary 10,000 history ceiling.\n- Repair direction: persist content-addressed revision objects and indexed append segments while keeping exact predecessor/protected-asset/rollback evidence. Checkpoint a durable frontier rather than all complete graph descriptions; permit indefinite history without resetting lineage identity. Aggregate/checkpoint enforcement and recovery callers remain under review.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGQsKEnkjq/jk6IUOWzePyFI90asysvJkaWB+6wE8eimJNdcOJIoly2TJ8TTXHk7OLL3ALAXbBoB8T6OrkxQbwU="}
