ll producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEPXJLNeQM/Z5xeInR0JfQzXTdcwQ0TNVcFxxSrq0kUEdNV1EA9KSg6nXR5um7ngYcEWzYLSb0OMTJqNcTGOeQE="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2677,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:49.110263511Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"b658c941-9c16-5181-8223-132b3493ce7b","title":"[L359] E1 protected harness assets freeze configuration and manifest position across successors","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L359.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/orchestration/peritus-harness/src/domain/catalog.rs:121-134,241-245`, `src/domain/graph_validation.rs:292-312`, `src/domain/revision.rs:195-202`.\n- Behavior: compiled protected classes include gate definitions/parsers, context transforms, memory injection policy, provider capability/profile, redaction/tool exposure policy, analysis/metrics, and evolution strategy. Each protected fingerprint includes its declaration's absolute manifest position as well as its complete content/metadata/dependencies. Every successor requires exact equality of the full protected inventory. Adding an evolvable declaration before a protected one therefore shifts its position and rejects the successor even when the protected declaration is unchanged.\n- Consequence: ordinary configuration evolution and harmless insertion/reordering can require a new lineage through this API. This is not a provider-session TTL, nor proof that the installed application takes that route. Security/trust boundaries need explicit authorized migration, but declaration position unnecessarily couples unrelated edits to protected identity.\n- Repair direction: bind protected identity to stable component identity and semantic declaration fields; use a separate explicit authorized policy-revision/migration path for protected configuration. Preserve approval, evaluator and authority invariants without making manifest layout a continuity blocker. Runtime/administrative callers remain under review; no tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEw/V4IwvH/bEIuLQkAuHKn1qBbrPg7exycmhbvxzM7FYrRVCA7jCpLcxPpsB47q6TRd4taCvDobasz5wHiJWA0="}
