ers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLQeYJ6yJGHyWCanMY7rgxxX29g3i52/ACt6wx57mmTDdnUP4G+PelSVT9RIuG/aDEn78Fagg/W7LY6BIQO3mwY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2679,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:49.114867793Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"3d61f536-be63-56b2-8295-75045745e41d","title":"[L360] E1 full diagnostic history prevents terminal failure or conflict settlement","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L360.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/orchestration/peritus-harness/src/aggregate/reducer/settlement.rs:101-123`, `src/aggregate/reducer.rs:195-236`, `src/aggregate/command.rs:36-81`, `src/domain/limits.rs:36`, `src/materialization/failure.rs:35-57`, `src/materialization/failure.rs:91-105`.\n- Behavior: recording a materialization failure or reconciling a conflict removes pending work only in a cloned candidate state, then rejects if 1,024 retained failures (or a tightened maximum) already exist. The rejected transition leaves the original pending plan intact. The entire closed command vocabulary has receipt retirement but no failure retirement, diagnostic rollover, or limit amendment. Successful settlement separately rejects a full hot receipt map, but can recover by explicitly retiring a settled receipt first.\n- Consequence: diagnostic capacity can block recording a true terminal failure and preserve a pending plan that blocks later plans for the same workspace. No cancellation command provides an alternate cleanup path within this aggregate. Failure records already contain fixed-size identities, a failure code, a diagnostic digest, an observed timestamp, and a causal event; they do not retain diagnostic text. The timestamp is descriptive. This is a lifetime failure-count quota, not a timer. The successful-receipt retirement route is an actual exception and must not be described as absent.\n- Repair direction: record terminal disposition independently of the bounded hot failure vector. Segment or index the existing fixed-size failure references and retain a checkpoint frontier; cleanup/settlement must always remain admissible. The synchronous runtime executes C1 before deciding success/failure settlement (`src/runtime/driver.rs:136-153`, `156-212`). A quota rejection propagates an error without returning the effect receipt or a successor state; the durable plan remains pending. A recovered execution then encounters the changed target if C1 already advanced it. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCUbtmApSsyeJso7OE0z6b8a2MwebhxhkBMzlNJV2e5m17Uei7H9qQS6Z/Uo96mcqFtxt4A3ZFzngmgVKHC3ZAo="}
