ts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDeciU8xTEr3Atnr/MjzWybGOd3K/BLIwZDVYqInEsUsoziTzokzYR4jvjwzZu6sIgjVaRJrJ5naIDrlK73XQAI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2681,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:49.119874757Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"47212841-e49b-5008-a3a5-f05b498a0352","title":"[L361] E1 pending-plan admission omits a limit that checkpoint decoding enforces","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L361.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/orchestration/peritus-harness/src/aggregate/reducer/settlement.rs:15-45`, `src/aggregate/reducer.rs:165-170`, `src/aggregate/state.rs:173-190,268-291`, `src/durability/commit.rs:107-126,140-185`.\n- Behavior: planning checks exact revision binding, duplicate plan identity, and one pending plan per workspace, but never checks total pending cardinality against `max_receipt_history`. Encoding writes the complete pending map. Decoding rejects it above that receipt-history limit. Commit encodes the candidate checkpoint without decoding it first.\n- Consequence: under a receipt-history limit of one, two otherwise valid plans for distinct workspaces can be admitted and committed into a checkpoint that cannot restore, despite small payloads. This is a source-derived scenario, not an executed test or evidence that the installed runner has reached it. The per-workspace serialization rule is separate from the decoder-only aggregate quota.\n- Repair direction: ensure admitted state remains reconstructible; separate pending admission from receipt-retention policy and negotiate host capacity without invalidating durable work. Retain independent pending records rather than a complete map inside one checkpoint. Migrate reducer, decoder, commit validation, and recovery together.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQL/jNkAgAOP5etQRhbLZbHcwo/cKEDEmJgK72sVx4B2GS682AYCPphumOTf/JLghPQCQELSwPZjQ5Vc5BV1I3QM="}
