ected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large-file and many-path capture/restore, divergent preimage rejection, interrupted staging/publication/restore, then reopen and continue the same conversation with an exact restored workspace. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHyW2XsCdFSZT4bT6kRbCN4PR6Atj2ElmTQsOsI8+EZrLfwWMvV/JEl9MuoTgLfni411A/8diET3XFm+yRlUlAQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2683,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:49.124231783Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"6ed37dab-2fda-581b-a58d-a7b2c04d8cf4","title":"[L362] E1 sixteen-MiB policy is narrowed by nested eight-MiB codec fields","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L362.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/orchestration/peritus-harness/src/aggregate/command.rs:170-183,263-269`, `src/aggregate/state.rs:139-145,173-203`, `src/wire/state.rs:52-66`, `src/wire/command.rs:97-109`, `src/wire/event.rs:94-112`, `src/durability/commit.rs:113-126,344-374`; production codec bounds previously completely read under L009.\n- Behavior: E1's compiled event and state capacities are 16 MiB, but canonical production encoding caps one opaque field at 8 MiB. Complete history is one state field, the full state identity is another opaque field, and the complete canonical state is wrapped in another field for family 81. Command/event semantic data is similarly one opaque field. Capacity errors from these encoding paths are classified as `Quarantine`, before the explicit E1 length checker can return a recoverable configured-limit rejection.\n- Consequence: durable mutation or settlement can stop below advertised E1 capacities, and a proposed allocation failure can receive an integrity-quarantine disposition. Retirement shrinks hot receipt content, but adds permanent retired receipt IDs; that set is subject to the production 65,535-item collection ceiling and whole-state bytes. There is no retirement-ID rollover command in the fully read aggregate vocabulary.\n- Repair direction: align domain admission, canonical transport and durable checkpoint representation. Use separately addressed history/plan/receipt segments and small frontier checkpoints; represent recoverable capacity pressure separately from corrupted durable input. Exact binding and malformed-input rejection remain necessary. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAU9vLuW23s35V7lOYEmATHgEMnpZN9HTq8pWKXCSZt7i1Xeae1N+2LiGv+euNCQyxf9KoAJuZj/diuqnXRScwQ="}
