m authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCTDpBWFCaPd2F+po0ywU0dQ8nHJ6Ozi0z2fgQIQnLidjm4OcPTsXquQ22zsKmKdXtFdT1MyIK3O4z8F/bY5aw0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2685,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:49.128417772Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"22b58551-c423-5590-bd7e-403852039f3a","title":"[L363] E1 exact older commit retries require replay instead of returning prior acceptance","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L363.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/orchestration/peritus-harness/src/aggregate/reducer.rs:25-35,96-125`, `src/durability/commit.rs:129-139,214-260`.\n- Behavior: direct reducer decisions require the command's original fence to equal current state, so an exact repeated command against current state is stale before semantic reduction. Commit-level resolution recognizes its exact accepted C0 batch, but then compares that command's successor against the current checkpoint. It returns the prior acceptance only if the checkpoint still equals that successor; a later same-harness checkpoint produces `ReplayAggregate` even when command/event bytes match exactly.\n- Consequence: an exact retry after unrelated subsequent work has an additional replay barrier. This code correctly distinguishes advancement from corruption; it does not quarantine simple advancement. Whether callers turn this into repeated replay or make forward progress requires the runtime driver, which remains under review.\n- Repair direction: resolve exact historical acceptance independently of the current checkpoint, return its original receipt plus current frontier, and validate current state separately. Keep conflicts on reused identities and current-state fences for new commands. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBkCop239Z4k3DZvueWtpiaa/6f9Pj/ACaCQ6IWW6nc1bxqKuJWKvCsggv9VJ+sVy8ELW8grnsLZcnJ1agZ/XAo="}
