\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMNToFpWzCtmr4Kd6k/fKwPUCFtlmJu48nEtooulPF3Ij0/9JI/C6YmGn5BA6TFD1k8vxZqkagfISloCOsJsIwI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2687,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:49.133194611Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"26601576-590d-59ed-a265-2b8983e992f2","title":"[L364] E1 recovery repeatedly rebuilds complete history and re-encodes state","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L364.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/orchestration/peritus-harness/src/durability/recovery.rs:42-54,83-129`, `src/wire/event.rs:58-75`, `src/aggregate/reducer.rs:58-89,159-237`, `src/aggregate/state.rs:168-203`, `src/domain/history.rs:108-157,292-318`, `src/replay.rs:54-65`, `src/projection.rs:29-40`.\n- Behavior: loading obtains every aggregate record, decodes each event, checks it by reducing against prior state, and then reduces it again to retain the result. Checkpoint decoding separately reconstructs complete revision history through repeated append/serialization. `HarnessReplay::rebuild` replays all collected events once more. Every reducer decision clones retained state and hashes its complete canonical identity, including sorted complete history. Projection rebuild/repair also replays from genesis.\n- Consequence: recovery and ongoing mutation cost grows with all retained revisions/plans/receipts/diagnostics rather than the current change. This is synchronous whole-prefix work, with no internal yield/cancellation boundary. It is a source-grounded performance risk, not a measured explanation of the live lockup or an artificial timeout.\n- Repair direction: validate durable indexed segments once, resume from a checked frontier and contiguous suffix, reuse immutable objects, and compute incremental exact state certificates. Preserve independent validation without discarding state or restarting lineage. Runtime entry points remain under review; no tests or timing measurements run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMCarGLWIBwiCD1nZpIb/DgXxa10OtOJks0jfDDM+13cOINuq7WFADJQFa9bbSMRqXP/dQfSfzRhcqKy/BWTcQo="}
