dy owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQObq52fpIT6gZ7n2V79Sb3aWRHvMfnqTtShzGFZO+8x2NLu0DD73X6KR5k3Tmx6JB5xe/Q7wmFmYGTg2cK7OBww="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2691,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:24:49.142647475Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"9bc059ac-5f53-5036-a353-9aff8277cd52","title":"[L366] E1 public rollback reason bypasses validation and can produce an unreadable durable plan","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L366.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/orchestration/peritus-harness/src/materialization/plan_model.rs:43-94`, `src/materialization/planner.rs:103-120`, `src/materialization/plan_codec.rs:63-79`, `src/materialization/plan_codec.rs:101-107`; persistence path in L357/L361.\n- Behavior: the rollback helper and decoder require a nonempty reason with no control characters and at most 1,024 bytes. The public enum exposes its raw String field. The planner accepts that enum without revalidation and computes a valid plan identity by encoding the supplied string under the larger production string bound. Thus a directly constructed rollback with 1,025 ordinary ASCII bytes, an empty string, or controls can be built and encoded but cannot be decoded. The aggregate admits the private checked plan without decoding it, and the commit path publishes encoded checkpoint/event bytes without a round-trip check.\n- Consequence: successful in-memory construction does not guarantee restart readability. This is a source-derived public-API counterexample, not an executed reproduction or a claim about the installed user's current run. A rollback narrative cap is not an elapsed deadline.\n- Repair direction: make validated rollback text an opaque value, validate at every public construction boundary, and make encoder/admission/decoder acceptance agree before durability. Store longer narratives by artifact reference rather than invalidating recovery. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQM+AUKvydzr02yptAc3vInGjccaoi0NbFFtDcWvO6OjTd4w+aEtEN5YGIJM7ednqBCE5ONGxH3HciE5VZ5MHSgI="}
