ve the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:24:48.544Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQM6YViP5SqCmNwn9M6UeBjqzr7dUJhrUauXxWpts+WZuw46jM5eoCw1RHDc/X8QA3i8jUmCP6O6Ix0DDPYkkowY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2693,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.036247846Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"8cdd6887-821b-523c-9d09-1f7eba139756","title":"[L211] Native runtime profiles forbid protocol resumption while Codex privately resumes its retained thread","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L211.\n\n- Source: `crates/model/peritus-provider-openai/src/runtime/config.rs:66-96`; `crates/model/peritus-provider-anthropic/src/runtime/config.rs:66-95`; OpenAI `runtime/request.rs:74-110,128-184`; `runtime/provider/invocation.rs:78-113`.\n- Both runtime configs require StatelessReplay/ResumeKind::Unsupported/BestEffortLocalAbort and a narrow closed capability set. Codex nevertheless opens a host-bound session namespace and explicitly uses **exec resume <exact thread ID>** when recovered. Its prompt supplies the complete current Peritus request as authoritative input, rather than relying on stale native history. No private profile transformation occurs in the config constructor, but the protocol label does not prove native context loss.\n- Codex rejects protocol continuation/store/background/extensions, sampling/seed/stop sequences, adaptive reasoning and visible summaries. Reasoning Disabled becomes high; concrete efforts are forwarded. Media is inline images only, written as PNG/JPEG/WebP/GIF files; audio/document/reasoning/extension blocks fail. Host tools remain inert proposals, and native tools/rules/config are disabled to preserve sole Peritus effect authority.\n- The production Codex provider uses TokioProcessTransport, so L210 byte-overflow termination applies to its turns. It awaits full process output before returning normalized model events; authentication is an untimed login-status subprocess with **64 KiB stdout/stderr** on every start. Final-response file admission is separately bounded by the protocol max text size (**16 MiB**, L017).\n- **All named config/provider/request/invocation files fully read; persistent namespace producer and Claude invocation path pending.** Same-thread use is source-confirmed, not a new live reconnect test.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFPuWfKU0gpPXCeYcKvgS0F/E5ffGX8QIDQQAIS3F+Y3VBawu4/xzbfINnBe3oWVLE9yyAIjXZBoptXRKuV/Bw4="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2694,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.046135206Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"8cdd6887-821b-523c-9d09-1f7eba139756","comment_uuid":"537ba03e-8140-4ad5-a167-943516a128e4","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L211: Native runtime profiles forbid protocol resumption while Codex privately resumes its retained thread.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/model/peritus-provider-openai/src/runtime/config.rs:66-96; crates/model/peritus-provider-anthropic/src/runtime/config.rs:66-95; runtime/request.rs:74-110,128-184; runtime/provider/invocation.rs:78-113. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nRepresent protocol response-cursor resumption, native conversation continuity and effect authority as separate explicit capabilities. Advertise Codex same-thread reattachment truthfully while retaining inert host tools and authoritative current Peritus inputs. Version profile negotiation and persist the exact native identity so recovery does not infer context loss from StatelessReplay or enable native side effects to obtain persistence.\n\nPreserve: definitely-unaccepted versus ambiguously-accepted request state, exact native thread/profile identity, ordered provider observations, tool-result protocol, explicit cancellation and real provider/model capabilities. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBdnvkQHSF9hFDa3n8NV1PgC8frSexvlBWsp+X/myfz9/ADCCA4sWgMs84znoPYBMogGRfhU2/l6Cwk3PKS3AQU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2695,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.048957015Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"e221201b-6640-5b84-a08a-ab0147a5f36b","title":"[L229] Approval registry size and exact-successor policy can block the entire daemon at startup","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L229.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/startup/registry.rs:27-38,44-110,119-134,160-179`; `crates/state/peritus-approval/src/authentication/credential.rs:15-18,92-126,150-177`; `src/digest.rs` in that crate.\n- A credential snapshot is limited to **4 MiB / 4,096 entries / 11 distinct ordered approval roles per credential**. Disabled credentials count toward the entry ceiling. The configured payload must be a regular file at its exact canonical path; symlinks, alias components, absent files, oversized bytes and noncanonical encoding fail startup. Unlike workspace registrations, there is no fallback from a missing configured payload in this path.\n- Configuration must exactly match durable revision, generation, digest and bytes, or supply **revision = current + 1** with **greater generation**. The previous durable snapshot is verified before a successor is considered, so corrupt old state cannot be repaired merely by supplying a new good snapshot. Arbitrary reset/rollback would weaken revocation and authority; global startup dependence and lack of an explicit repair path are separate daily-use blockers.\n- Decision preimages are capped at **4,096 bytes** and key-ID/signed-message preimages at **256 bytes**; these are canonical encoding limits, not inference deadlines. Exact Ed25519 key/signature lengths are algorithm requirements. **Registry implementation, credential projections and startup tests fully read; tests not run.** No automatic credential expiry duration was inferred from these size bounds.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNOkcg+3Nmd73j1Jx1+0j6M+hB6hfpii68vmvpRUR5x342Z++jZaqnNj6CparuMMF7VMUSQ6V2b4qFLPXRfPGg8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2696,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.051195333Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"e221201b-6640-5b84-a08a-ab0147a5f36b","comment_uuid":"e3ce6055-e5a4-495e-aaf5-cbd137f6db40","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L229: Approval registry size and exact-successor policy can block the entire daemon at startup.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/startup/registry.rs:27-38,44-110,119-134,160-179; crates/state/peritus-approval/src/authentication/credential.rs:15-18,92-126,150-177; src/digest.rs. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nKeep a paged approval credential catalog with exact monotonic revision/generation and revocation evidence. Start a scoped repair/read interface when configured or historical credential evidence is unavailable, rather than prevent the entire daemon from opening. Provide explicit authenticated recovery/adoption without rollback or reset of accepted authority; canonical signature/key checks remain mandatory.\n\nPreserve: explicit user authority, credential secrecy, exact target/resource binding, fencing, scope confinement, replay rejection for changed command content and fail-closed acceptance evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: renewal/adoption under the same authorized identity, revoked authority, stale epoch/revision, cross-scope requests, lost acknowledgements and restart, proving legitimate continuation without admitting unauthorized or duplicate effects. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLzivk0DEngXpj62mzm8CjH20wX8ZSMI4VZWbRKCPbHbGRg4LlVW2KKJkSAgjHUihYxnFTE7J2Rf1LjUuBPDJwg="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2697,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.053368416Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"95e83aaa-c199-5487-8077-ddc2975152fc","title":"[L230] Workspace startup checks every retained registration, including removed and unconfigured rows","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L230.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/startup/workspace.rs:56-131,133-195,198-220`; `crates/runtime/peritus-workspace/src/registration.rs:16-31,90-122,131-140,218-285`.\n- Missing, invalid or oversized configured registration files fall back to the durable journal. Startup still requires an exact inventory of project-referenced workspace IDs and recovered registrations; an unrecoverable configured workspace fails the whole catalog. Refresh retains exact resource/environment/repository/worktree/transaction authority and verifies the current detached Git worktree, rather than authorizing a relocated directory implicitly.\n- Reconciliation scans **all durable rows in 256-row pages**. It decodes each registration **before** testing whether the row is removed or no longer configured. Consequently a malformed retired/unrelated registration blocks otherwise healthy configured workspaces. The page size is not a lifetime cap; the loop follows every page. One failed trusted-folder verification also fails the full catalog.\n- C1 adds **32,768 bytes per registration path / 262,144 bytes for the nested worktree manifest / list bound 8 / codec depth 4**, plus the **1 MiB total registration bound** imported from `crates/state/peritus-journal/src/application/workspace_types.rs:7-11,57-74`. C0 permits pages up to 4,096; startup selects 256 and follows continuation. Paths must be absolute UTF-8 without dot traversal; transaction roots cannot overlap registered Git paths. Necessary identity/path checks should remain distinct from arbitrary size ceilings and whole-catalog recovery coupling. **Both full implementations read; no removed-row corruption fixture run.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFxiTNWQURMi391ecXgAoo+JWQC+kgfqF1YBppgStUXDAQ1UJlJaJdE1v+YV3ZUhjE20d07vF2Kv2MAMFkkiXgA="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2698,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.055873830Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"95e83aaa-c199-5487-8077-ddc2975152fc","comment_uuid":"978b00c5-2c8c-43d5-b76f-f43ff0be7b54","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L230: Workspace startup checks every retained registration, including removed and unconfigured rows.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/startup/workspace.rs:56-131,133-195,198-220; crates/runtime/peritus-workspace/src/registration.rs:16-31,90-122,131-140,218-285; crates/state/peritus-journal/src/application/workspace_types.rs:7-11,57-74. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nSeparate catalog row identity/status indexing from full registration payload validation. Retired/unconfigured malformed records should remain visible repair evidence without blocking healthy configured workspaces. Reconcile each active workspace through its exact ownership/environment facts and typed capability status; relocation requires explicit authorized adoption, never an implicit path replacement.\n\nPreserve: canonical digest and schema identity, shared writer/reader admissibility, malformed-input rejection before allocation, exact causal ordering, actual provider/OS capability boundaries and preserved accepted historical evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDux8ahi+Jx/j0XuSmSbLqRGES1QrXMhhR1hOVfOhg3tAs4qgLydLfk3AYFbO989I6Wwleobv84gA5I4R5lDWw4="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2699,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.058277909Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"ca40855e-412d-59aa-9f11-3b61d49e0d68","title":"[L231] Shutdown diagnostics are capped at 16 failures and clean status ignores recorded failures","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L231.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/shutdown.rs`; `src/shutdown/work.rs`; `src/shutdown/tests.rs`; worker limits and elapsed shutdown waits are recorded separately in L199/L200.\n- The coordinator retains at most **16 failures**; another failure is a CorruptState error instead of an additional retained diagnostic. Work encoding must accommodate all **8 work categories** and the longest numeric descriptor; these minimum representation requirements are not work-duration limits. Counts and stage mutations are prohibited after completion, and ordered stage progress is required.\n- The coordinator selects Clean versus Unclean from whether remaining-work counts are empty, **without including the recorded failure vector** in that choice. Thus its public state machine can produce Clean with recorded failures and zero remaining counts. Whether a production teardown caller reaches that exact combination remains to be connected; it must not be presented as an observed clean shutdown.\n- Worker cancellation retains its first reason, and channel closure selects Shutdown. Worker tests use short fixture waits; they add no production deadline beyond L200. **Shutdown and worker modules plus tests fully read; no tests run.** Diagnostic capacity must not prevent recording actual cleanup outcome.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","