. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large histories and non-ASCII fields, queue/connection pressure, delayed acknowledgements, subscription gaps, disconnect/reconnect and daemon restart, proving snapshot recovery, preserved selection/context, responsive controls and no duplicate command. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDZGqlth1iJ5dqKPShN+sdg4/Qp7o5+Hey/qTx6luPDAP5DkW9yoz5JGsvakNJ6U36/eSbiovn43AWWCiyvMAAQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2719,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.103776244Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"00fc867b-547f-5733-9d51-5724ae2fd241","title":"[L241] TUI cleanup uses nested fixed eight-second deadlines; reconnect retains the durable session","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L241.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-tui/src/client.rs:20-21,123-173,220-237`; `runtime.rs:35-36,181-197,271-276`; `runtime/connection.rs:36-53,101-122`; `model.rs:421-445,480-491,519-560`.\n- ClientSession orderly close has a fixed **8-second absolute deadline** for queue admission, writer acknowledgement and writer join. Socket shutdown also has an **8-second** timeout. Runtime connection close wraps both pending-outbox drain and ClientSession close in another **8-second** grace, so remaining cleanup time can be shorter than an inner allowance. Expiry aborts/drops connection IO ownership; it can leave final detach/unsubscribe frames undelivered. These are client cleanup limits, not inference termination.\n- Same-process reconnect asks for **model.retained_session()**, then falls back to the configured session. The model retains the session across disconnect and clears protocol/pending request observations while preserving recovery/drafts through their separate paths. Ordinary cleanup sends CancelSubscription and DetachTerminal; it does not issue a product-run cancellation in this inspected function.\n- Prior ClientSession close is awaited before new connection negotiation, with its errors ignored by the reconnect attempt. Handshake itself has no elapsed deadline and is polled beside UI input; existing fixtures assert stalled handshakes/writers still allow quit. Product-mode reconnect exits to the launcher for daemon recovery, whose reopen selection remains a separate pending caller read. **All runtime/client sources and connection fixtures fully read; tests not run.** No existing-session failure was repaired during this audit.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJf/hwi/QUBuRy3Zb4r4TL6RzNDzWXiqH00LdjTeGpV2Q7X+YNFNOJjAzaR+ZDMmgps3K36PK/uxTa6nQoSmDAE="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2720,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.105874804Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"00fc867b-547f-5733-9d51-5724ae2fd241","comment_uuid":"aa2bf9ac-bff3-4af4-b4f4-004bba965572","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L241: TUI cleanup uses nested fixed eight-second deadlines; reconnect retains the durable session.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-tui/src/client.rs:20-21,123-173,220-237; runtime.rs:35-36,181-197,271-276; runtime/connection.rs:36-53,101-122; model.rs:421-445,480-491,519-560. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nSeparate UI exit/transport detach from durable logical operation settlement. Drain or persist unsent/accepted frames with exact receipt state and reconnect under the retained session; nested eight-second cleanup windows must not define whether an operation completed. Explicit socket shutdown may abandon only the attachment after its unresolved work is durably recoverable, keeping quit responsive.\n\nPreserve: committed command/event identity, exact causal and digest roots, exclusive ownership, atomic publication, reference-safe artifact retention and verified recovery from the last durable frontier. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQK8Lrt/vNhKizzH0pGHZDGclxAUW11zCdIhGAgeH1lyfdsRR89eWD0c08/O/AlNUdqcMyeZVHPtgiX+w/Pb1fgk="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2721,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.107969185Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"51f4b58c-4650-5645-a89f-8f343b21a756","title":"[L242] TUI send-queue exhaustion forces disconnect and drops the remaining transport outbox","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L242.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-tui/src/runtime/connection/outbox.rs:7-28,36-50`; `runtime/connection.rs:36-38,96-99,125-156`; `runtime.rs:266-269`; `client.rs:95-102,110-120,184-217`.\n- The runtime outbox retains **128 pending frames plus one active send**; the independently owned client writer channel holds **256 commands**. Input and client-observation channels hold **128 / 512** entries. These are fixed capacities, with no reservation for heartbeat replies or cleanup in the inspected FIFO structures.\n- A push beyond the pending ceiling returns Task; runtime immediately routes that error through sent, which resets the outbox, drops the ClientSession and marks the model disconnected. All remaining transport frames are discarded together. Draft/receipt recovery must distinguish definitely unsent frames from those already queued/written; that model recovery is still being traced. Capacity exhaustion is escalated from one rejected submission to loss of the whole connection.\n- Reader observations await the shared event channel, and writer error reporting uses that same channel. A stalled main reducer can therefore delay receiving/replying to heartbeat events under the server cutoff. Actual responsiveness fixtures cover a small filled writer setup, not the 128-frame overflow or prolonged event-channel saturation. **Entire outbox, runtime wiring, IO tasks and fixtures fully read; tests not executed.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDoJcAOSjkR/9mZkj41LrjNadxJvQrnFPQKiZmCO7nJ5q8KGydF0JmtRhZWCRYFka1X0SICMLhp1Fo6Ow3YYZgI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2722,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.110022796Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"51f4b58c-4650-5645-a89f-8f343b21a756","comment_uuid":"950bac19-535f-42c2-9bd4-fee54ec5f02a","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L242: TUI send-queue exhaustion forces disconnect and drops the remaining transport outbox.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-tui/src/runtime/connection/outbox.rs:7-28,36-50; runtime/connection.rs:36-38,96-99,125-156; runtime.rs:266-269; client.rs:95-102,110-120,184-217. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nPersist queued transport intent with Prepared/Queued/Written/Accepted receipt phases and fair bounded backpressure. Queue saturation rejects or waits on the individual unsent submission without discarding the whole outbox or disconnecting owned tasks. Reserve heartbeat, cancellation and detach control progress, and reconcile accepted frames under the same session after any real transport loss.\n\nPreserve: committed command/event identity, exact causal and digest roots, exclusive ownership, atomic publication, reference-safe artifact retention and verified recovery from the last durable frontier. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQB2N4zTmx12fGuuz38OCPv8d7LSOgHufjwPpzxKEZnWZjpg02DdimvQFl5lx39Ue7rAGEV7SBCCFmReawkszgAg="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2723,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.112657542Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"57b752b7-a5fb-507c-aa94-52d63381be9e","title":"[L244] Prompt and terminal capacities differ across UI, wire and ownership layers","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L244.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-tui/src/model/interaction/prompts.rs`; `model/interaction/terminal.rs`; `crates/app/peritus-app-protocol/src/wire/prompt.rs`; `src/schema/fields/flows/prompt_terminal/prompt.rs`.\n- Ordinary prompt answers are checked against the codec's **1 MiB string** ceiling. Signed Base64 answers are decoded before the check and compared with the larger whole-frame bound even though the wire's opaque signed-decision field is limited to **8 MiB**. A narrower broker answer constraint can still reject a UI-admitted answer. Prompt wire/schema also allow **64 choices**, **65535 constraints**, and **1 MiB choice/text fields**. The editor's own input capacity remains to be traced before claiming the maximum practical answer size.\n- One unresolved PendingTerminalAttach suppresses another attach until a response or disconnect. Terminal input is bounded to **64 KiB per chunk** and resize to **4096 columns / 256 rows**. These are transfer/display bounds, not a command lifetime. Cancellation is gated by a current live input-capture binding; a client that lost the attachment cannot use this UI path to cancel the old process until it can recover a valid attachment.\n- The ownership check must remain exact; recovery should reacquire or expose authorized control of the same terminal, rather than inventing a new process or treating loss of display attachment as process completion. **All named files fully read; terminal registry callers and editor capacity remain pending.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNQt+jKo+hZYiWeKQacRyRaPdmC4WfLcz8owr9AA8ZQkiOuz8XZEqUTAu1pukKq9+rQgtSh0CWC8bON6IjzvkQM="}
