ons from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large histories and non-ASCII fields, queue/connection pressure, delayed acknowledgements, subscription gaps, disconnect/reconnect and daemon restart, proving snapshot recovery, preserved selection/context, responsive controls and no duplicate command. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCNKlK0NOb+FkAd++pI+pxouQKhFoex+RCaJfBjI8iTE/GXVo2NDedHtNMBvGqB2bgdL9ZUpCiUOTYNQID9/fwI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2727,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.121364066Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"a22cb379-7700-5f2d-9b56-0dbaa343f428","title":"[L246] One outstanding observation can suppress later polling; recent-list replacement can lose an older selection","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L246.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-tui/src/model/product/observation.rs:53-101,104-126,141-151`; `model/product/interaction.rs`; `model/product.rs:263-279`.\n- If any ProductQuery or ProductExactQuery remains pending, polling returns before requesting fresh product observations or a product interaction snapshot. There is no elapsed expiry in this path. Removing a timer without a recoverable, correlated query lifecycle leaves a stalled response capable of suppressing the display indefinitely while the connection still appears live. Response routing and transport-disconnect recovery are documented separately; the actual lost-response condition has not been reproduced.\n- A recent-list response replaces the entire runs vector and retains settlements only for that vector. An exactly queried older run is inserted at index zero and becomes selected when absent. Since recent and exact queries can both be pending, their response order can remove or reselect that older run. Interaction results are ignored unless they match whichever run is selected at response time. This is a selection/projection recovery hazard, not an execution quota.\n- Inspection scroll positions are **u16**. The complete render/product root saturates the content scroll maximum at **u16::MAX (65535 rows)**; wrapped content beyond that offset is inaccessible through this scroll projection without a separate paging path. **Complete product root, observation, composer, resume and interaction files read; no behavioral test executed.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIgyVKG0ftQxLQXbfrxvNQ0VToW7IIKSxZRCWPLph5jsfkKkUoCovbzreKRpBNcFC5R76pJsczROGI5gPfD28QY="}
