idence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAAWY09T3kmchcheVWdQ5fyJflsAj8yQ1ZP4IH6cKvfHw+oPoHDnHvitPfZ3ayPM+h+jbpEycO9/J4Tn6zak9wE="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2729,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.125573578Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"db4614ac-d53d-51a5-9cd6-b0de3e6c13f0","title":"[L247] Global event pages validate every row and reject interior gaps; future cursors are silently empty","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L247.\n\n- Source: `crates/state/peritus-journal/src/sqlite/query/records.rs:27-99,102-188,209-248`; `sqlite/query.rs`; `sqlite/reader.rs`.\n- The global query accepts **1..4096 records per page**, computes actual retained MIN/MAX in one transaction, and performs exact frame/digest/hash and contiguous-position validation. No event-retention deletion or age timer exists in this file. Aggregate queries still load the entire aggregate history into a Vec without paging here; one malformed row aborts the whole result.\n- A cursor at or beyond latest returns an empty page without rejecting a cursor ahead of the actual journal. Thus an ahead-of-store cursor can leave consumers waiting for positions that no longer exist after a store rollback unless a caller explicitly detects and reconciles it. The TUI/server higher-level validation for this case remains to be traced; no rollback reproduction is claimed.\n- JournalReader holds a deferred read snapshot for its lifetime and rejects exact store/schema drift. Fixed-length identities and positive i64-backed sequence values are integrity/representation requirements, not elapsed deadlines. **All three files fully read; append/schema and recovery callers still pending.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9