and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKTnRJJChqAwk5aWtp463Qd86xACN7UaDcGKakgNMFca2EZ0gSUtCcfMnoNZpWVpocMMS4h/xW6FOO5RPBasBg8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2731,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.130309945Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"ec8461e4-767f-5ae1-bfdb-935139190438","title":"[L248] Preview mutation shares one unresolved receipt gate, including Stop; launch readiness is fixed at two seconds","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L248.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-tui/src/model/product/preview.rs:13,32-38,69-92,143-181,224-228,298-336`; `product/preview/profile.rs`; `product/preview/terminal.rs`.\n- The TUI always supplies **2000 ms readiness**, **None wall limit**, and interactive=true for a preview launch. The readiness value is a concrete selected bound; it must not be confused with a two-second lifetime for the running preview. Host readiness behavior is recorded separately from this client selection (L206).\n- Any unresolved Workbench control receipt or pending Workbench request blocks a new preview action before action dispatch, including Stop. A pending result query suppresses another result refresh. The recovery model must resolve the exact durable receipt while keeping authorized process cancellation reachable; merely dropping a timer leaves these single-owner gates potentially stuck.\n- The launch parser uses split_whitespace without quoting/escaping. An executable, source/build path or individual argument containing spaces cannot be represented correctly through this UI command. Source/build digests can only come from the current loaded file preview/page or the exact managed-candidate identity; this is an observation accessibility restriction, not permission to drop identity checks.\n- Ordinary preview actions select the last launch irrespective of whether it is Running, while terminal attachment searches backwards for a Running interactive launch. A failed newer launch can therefore hide an older running launch from Stop/play/capture in this UI path. Capture exposes only a nonzero decimal/hex **X11 window ID**; feedback requires an already successful capture; behavior check requires exact stdout. **Entire preview module and children fully read; no launch reproduction.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIhJ9IgOF45EXrMP2BU67DPvBGiEptfP4VyPKjZrZNY5VxI0sSHN0uXQ3Tu0AsIo+p8THFgbJrxurnWADF6POAY="}
