{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2733,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.134911202Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"fd0e7c9a-f101-52c0-8130-de25b3734d4b","title":"[L249] Structured-review navigation stays on the loaded page and repeat refresh has no in-flight guard","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L249.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-tui/src/model/product/review.rs:31-68,115-217,266-295`; `product/review/editor.rs`; `product/review/state.rs`.\n- The structured-review request always starts at **offset zero**. File, hunk and comment keys move only within the loaded page; the complete review module contains no next-page request. Server page size and overflow behavior are being traced through the protocol next. A larger total_comments count is displayed, but that count alone does not make later comments accessible.\n- Repeated refresh submits another request without checking whether a review query is pending. Enough submissions can reach the fixed transport outbox failure/disconnect path in L242. There is no elapsed deadline here.\n- Comments are unavailable while operation.may_start_execution is false (the UI labels this a terminal effect boundary). One unresolved durable receipt blocks another edit. Exact query/anchor freshness is preserved, with explicit draft rebind instead of silently moving a comment to a changed candidate; this is an identity invariant to retain in a repair. **All review implementation files fully read; paging callers still pending.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50