{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2735,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.139343373Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"ba2f706f-f16c-5aa6-bf04-96365403212d","title":"[L250] Journal schema has narrower durable identity fields and all-history state retention","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L250.\n\n- Source: `crates/state/peritus-journal/src/sqlite/schema.rs`; `sqlite/append.rs`; `sqlite/apply_rows.rs`; `sqlite/preconditions.rs`.\n- SQL fixes app-command idempotency keys at **256 bytes**, whereas the wider protocol/config maximum recorded in L029 is **4096 bytes**. App error codes are **128 characters**; prompt maximum-answer bytes are **1..1 MiB**; workspace registrations **1 MiB**; state keys **1..1024 bytes**; history node byte_length **0..16 MiB**, level **0..4**, and payload **512 bytes**. Character-count SQL constraints must be compared with byte-count API checks before treating them as interchangeable.\n- Every state revision installs immutable history nodes and a history row. These source files perform no retirement, journal-event deletion or elapsed expiration. Aggregate event kinds and lifecycle states are closed numeric sets; SQLite counters are signed **i64** despite wider u64 API values. These are storage/version representation boundaries, not short running-session deadlines.\n- Every append attempt invalidates the previous replay-generation observation, including rejected or indeterminate attempts. A caller cannot reuse that observation unchanged after a transient storage failure; it must perform exact recovery/replay. CAS, command-digest and authority checks are necessary consistency rules. **All named schema/write/precondition files fully read; production idempotency admission remains pending.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_