{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2737,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.143562313Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"04bb4f05-8eda-5bad-a4fe-9b8c48a3ccc7","title":"[L252] Terminal output loss disables input and cancellation even when the process may be running","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L252.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-tui/src/terminal.rs:56-90,104-121,141-194`; `model/interaction/terminal.rs` (L244).\n- TerminalSession explicitly describes output_unavailable as “process may still be running”, but can_capture requires output to be available, a live connection and Attached phase. The inspected UI cancellation path shares can_capture. Losing output therefore disables cancellation through that path even though process existence is not settled.\n- Scroll is **u16** and every new output resets it to zero, so viewing earlier output is disrupted while a command continues writing. The complete transcript adapter retains **2048 scrollback lines**, defaults to a **24×80** screen, and clamps resize to **1..256 rows / 1..4096 columns**. Older display content is evicted, not the process. Pipe input remains below the negotiated chunk bound to reserve one newline; its pending acknowledgment blocks further local edits (L253). No new command time limit exists in this projection. **Terminal root, transcript and line-input files fully read, including inline tests (not executed); server ownership paths pending.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQN88V