sor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCyweda8+QIm3pHdWOlmy/vgQ2tWqJMUlixLLrdIaThOhrnbVKXkTEdZMk7aCvONj1IoAn7i/SYFTrvFsxiPdwQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2739,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.147935155Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"7f5e28e0-35ea-58c7-bbcb-e785c337f7d9","title":"[L253] Editor limits preserve rejected drafts, but signed-approval capacity is checked against the wrong layer","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L253.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-tui/src/model/editor/input.rs:16-39`; `model/editor.rs:48-68,146-177`; `terminal/line_input.rs:19-62`; prompt limits in L244.\n- Message/review editors use MAX_WORKBENCH_INPUT_BYTES (**8192**), process-ID drafts **256 bytes**, and ordinary prompt answers the codec string ceiling (**1 MiB**). Signed-approval paste uses **ceil(max_frame_bytes / 3) × 4** Base64 characters, approximately **22 MiB** for a 16 MiB codec frame, although the signed wire field is opaque **8 MiB**. This admits much larger text/decoded data than the request can serialize; it is a layer mismatch rather than a native-context limit.\n- Editor paste removes control characters except newline/tab and rejects an oversized insertion while retaining the prior text. Pending editor drafts are kept in in-memory maps/queues; disconnect restores them with an ambiguity warning, not automatic replay. This is not durable client draft persistence across process termination.\n- Pipe text must be strictly smaller than maximum_chunk_bytes to reserve the terminating newline. While awaiting acknowledgment, keyboard/paste editing is disabled. Oversized pipe paste is silently ignored. The model exposes no timed pending reset in these files; the acknowledgment/disconnect lifecycle must carry the same input identity and avoid an indefinite editing lock. **All four implementation files fully read; inline pipe tests read, not run.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBKtiR9hQCO5iaQRstqJ7idXLozPPf4qYdx6HfO14LYroeKytx0iQv4cdubTBx0jg8MhSvThb2isi3z6HgRe5gY="}
