{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2741,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.152126210Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"6af65945-d579-5066-9016-ba95f79d0cbb","title":"[L254] Structured diff is a whole bounded object, while only comments are paginated","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L254.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-app-protocol/src/workbench/review.rs:7-15,26-36`; `workbench/review/page.rs:254-290`; TUI navigation in L249.\n- A page includes the complete structured diff with at most **512 files**, **4096 hunks**, and **32768 visible lines**, plus **256 comments** and **two evidence entries**. The constructor rejects exceeded collections with MalformedFrame rather than exposing a recoverable diff continuation. This can block structured review for larger changes even when comment paging would otherwise work.\n- Paths must be nonempty, at most **4096 bytes**, relative normal components and outside leading .git. Exact run/workspace/candidate/diff identities and positive response revision are necessary consistency checks. Comments carry 8192-byte WorkbenchInputText and a u32 total_comments count; the client first-page-only navigation is separate from these wire/schema capacities.\n- The complete parser returns LimitExceeded when the file/hunk/line ceilings are reached; it does not truncate into a paged continuation. Raw-diff fallback and server page selection remain to be traced before claiming exactly how an oversized repository change appears to the user. **Review root, page, parser, diff, anchor and tests fully read; tests not run; server callers pending.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHA