predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGht+XUl+J6/7+VqfWzUB15OeA+hX6KBhPbSfbB1y3vETNFARVXvXumc0vckoTUekK37D8NvmfKL0APrsN7zgg0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2743,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.156235453Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"34b9ac54-db16-5932-8e1b-d4b6ba798e81","title":"[L258] Durable sessions have no age limit, but closing is irreversible and command recovery has no continuation cursor","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L258.\n\n- Source: `crates/state/peritus-journal/src/application/session_store.rs`; `application/session_types.rs`; `application/command_store.rs:169-199`; `application/command_types.rs`.\n- The session store contains **no TTL, session-count ceiling or age retirement**. It keeps the same SessionId across explicit protocol-negotiation updates. Active→Draining→Closed is monotonic and Closed cannot be reopened through this adapter. Transport loss must therefore remain separate from durable session closure (the inspected daemon disconnect path does preserve this separation, L236).\n- Opening an existing session requires exact actor/authority/created/protocol/version facts. Protocol refresh must use observe_application_session_negotiation, which updates metadata in place rather than opening a new identity. The lifecycle advance checks the old state in a separate read, then UPDATEs only by session_id; concurrent independent connections could defeat the advertised monotonic check unless callers serialize them. Actual concurrent production use is not established here.\n- Unsettled-command recovery returns **1..4096** rows ordered by command_id without a cursor/offset. This is not a 4096-command lifetime quota, but a still-unresolved first page cannot be bypassed to enumerate later rows through this method. One malformed row fails the entire batch. Pending/Indeterminate commands are durable with no elapsed auto-settlement; completion/rejection requires exact receipts. **All session/principal/command implementation files fully read; startup recovery callers and paging behavior partly covered elsewhere.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFC+ulFZ6/TRNkHciurbPs43NHfzjGUGImiGoVFcL0r9rxkqRTFqTza6HYUsqUA5lvgVJc91i+7rLcGUak2hQwQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2744,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.158548558Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"34b9ac54-db16-5932-8e1b-d4b6ba798e81","comment_uuid":"4fed814d-d1c6-4f21-8f82-3f9e0f162d95","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L258: Durable sessions have no age limit, but closing is irreversible and command recovery has no continuation cursor.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/state/peritus-journal/src/application/session_store.rs; application/session_types.rs; application/command_store.rs:169-199; application/command_types.rs. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nSeparate durable session identity from client attachment and explicit retirement, providing reopen/adoption when authority permits. Page outstanding command recovery with stable cursors and exact historical receipts. An explicitly closed authority grant must not be silently reused; retain its history and allow an authorized successor attachment/epoch without erasing the conversation.\n\nPreserve: committed command/event identity, exact causal and digest roots, exclusive ownership, atomic publication, reference-safe artifact retention and verified recovery from the last durable frontier. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKJLskNVs5g6SCbhn4gVFq2V16pVJvoGpFrdz3FKNdFRyejDWD08vueVnXl4INsZSVVBIDYwRlS0spux/4/CdAY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2745,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.160697251Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"b7f61043-5e7d-58fc-9dbb-80cd3f38b9c9","title":"[L259] Prompt targets persist without a timer, but discovery/republication is absent from the durable adapter","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L259.\n\n- Source: `crates/state/peritus-journal/src/application/prompt_store.rs`; `application/prompt_rows.rs`; `application/prompt_types.rs`; TUI prompt clearing in L245 and broker bounds in L235.\n- Durable target bindings and exact settlement frames are each **1..16 MiB**; maximum_answer_bytes is **1..1 MiB**. Frames are hashed before acceptance. The adapter stores Awaiting/Answered/Cancelled indefinitely, with no expiry clock, renewal operation, or target-count retirement policy.\n- This complete adapter can register, look up and settle a target **by exact PromptId**. It exposes no actor/session page of outstanding targets and no replay/republication operation. The TUI clears prompts when retaining/reopening presentation state; its model does not discover them on startup in the inspected protocol path. A still-Awaiting durable target therefore needs a producer-owned discovery/reissue path before it is usable after client-process restart. Full server publication wiring remains pending, so missing end-to-end replay is a hypothesis to trace, not a claimed reproduction.\n- Immutable actor/session/revision/freshness/cancellation/binding identities are necessary authorization facts. Recovery must republish the same current target or explicitly renew an obsolete authority binding within the same work/session identity; retaining an unanswerable target forever or inventing a new conversation is not recovery. Exact answer replay includes the original request identity and bytes. **All prompt adapter/types/row files fully read; no new fixed elapsed limit found.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPm+VO1RXlyfGq13DlO49byBsElZiT2Pq+KrRZxp6iuRQXMWd6zLhv+RTtO9BHMYzgQWY1KaOuwSWfb13glZ6Qc="}
