e the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQC/YE6g/a2m0NMYpDhAcYJqP0kkC5J47FLnbdfV5XHrbD6H8VhQy/4ajalE6DKYYFd3v5LpRymfv6vNxFHvJBwI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2751,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.173602373Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"35dc73c4-5e80-5b1d-8645-a4c3cf2f0478","title":"[L262] Application artifact catalog has no failed-upload transition or recovery enumeration","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L262.\n\n- Source: `crates/state/peritus-journal/src/application/artifact_store.rs`; `application/artifact_types.rs`.\n- Artifact metadata bounds are **1..255 ASCII media-type bytes** and a nonnegative size at most **i64::MAX**; this adapter chooses no smaller artifact-size quota or elapsed expiry.\n- The complete API supports begin/get/complete by exact ArtifactId. It declares Uploading/Available/Failed, but supplies no operation to mark failed, enumerate outstanding uploads, retire metadata, or reopen a failed identity. Exact begin repeats existing metadata/state; completion permits Uploading or exact Available replay only. Unknown completion returns IdempotencyConflict, despite the method documentation promising NotFound, which changes recovery classification to Terminal (L257).\n- An interrupted upload needs caller-owned durable inventory and explicit resume/abandon behavior; the type name Failed alone does not implement it. Actual producer/abandon wiring and whether this catalog is selected in a live upload remain pending, so no live orphan blockage is asserted. **Both artifact catalog implementation files fully read; no execution performed.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAA