{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2755,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.182513004Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"f2b6413c-1297-58f7-8a34-60dd2b82ec07","title":"[L264] Outbox delivery has a fixed 30-second lease and configured shutdown abort, with no renewal during delivery","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L264.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/outbox/pump.rs:10-11,31-50,61-107`; `outbox/clock.rs`.\n- The sole production pump selects **30-second leases** and an **idle poll every 25 ms**. The poll is a cadence, not a work deadline. router.deliver is awaited without an elapsed work timeout, but the lease is not renewed while it runs. A concurrent claimant or restart must reconcile the exact effect/fence instead of treating elapsed ownership as proof that no effect happened.\n- shutdown uses the configured positive Duration (defaults and maximum in L202), then aborts the task on timeout and returns without joining the aborted task. An in-progress native/cross-store settlement can therefore be interrupted at the shutdown cutoff; durable recovery must resolve it, not assume completion from task cancellation.\n- Lease ticks allocate **2^32-second slots** below a shifted durable authority epoch and a signed-SQL-range base. Duration zero or a lease not fitting the remaining slot returns RecoveryRequired. These long representation boundaries are separate from the selected 30-second lease; rollover/shift behavior was not executed or qualified here.\n- Production has one sequential pump, so L251's invalidation of a still-active final claim requires another claim operation to overlap it; ordinary single-pump sequential delivery alone does not establish that reproduction. **Complete pump/clock/route implementations read; no concurrent lease test run.** The fully read `peritus-journal/src/sqlite/tests/outbox_tests.rs:10-63` covers reclaim at expiry with max_attempts=3 and accepts an old fence after final acknowledgment. It does not cover exhaustion invalidating an unexpired final attempt.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFMFVB/ughiARIktLCtSUnyy6wjXODn1jhlEIGIoJ8Tbow8GcMbOT9ElMakj0dqibBYXwOShk8jDSVUK/WUQRgE="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2756,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.184819629Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"f2b6413c-1297-58f7-8a34-60dd2b82ec07","comment_uuid":"8bfd85d4-8827-4f01-b5ff-1ddc988d9541","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L264: Outbox delivery has a fixed 30-second lease and configured shutdown abort, with no renewal during delivery.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/outbox/pump.rs:10-11,31-50,61-107; outbox/clock.rs; peritus-journal/src/sqlite/tests/outbox_tests.rs:10-63. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nRepresent outbox dispatch as renewable fenced ownership of one durable delivery intent, with exact settlement receipts independent of a 30-second wall lease. Renew/reconcile while delivery is live and preserve uncertain accepted destinations on shutdown. Cancellation or attachment loss must not permit a second owner to duplicate the effect after an arbitrary lease expires.\n\nPreserve: explicit user authority, credential secrecy, exact target/resource binding, fencing, scope confinement, replay rejection for changed command content and fail-closed acceptance evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: renewal/adoption under the same authorized identity, revoked authority, stale epoch/revision, cross-scope requests, lost acknowledgements and restart, proving legitimate continuation without admitting unauthorized or duplicate effects. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFtulLultgbT1MOiNoY2DfbcCWE4HOwIZ/D/YOowTgJl1Xr/z//+njY23S/NBV6VK0vmM8LQWz4Xc3Ucc50BxwE="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2757,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.187087267Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"5d7acbbd-0ad6-56b8-b137-5a20149d857b","title":"[L265] One unsupported destination or exhausted message can force the whole daemon read-only","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L265.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/outbox/claims.rs`; `outbox/router.rs:52-88`; `outbox/handlers.rs`; `outbox/claims/orchestrator.rs`; `outbox/pump.rs:88-104`.\n- Claimed destinations are a closed inventory of **14**. The router also has a caller-configured maximum and requires unique handlers. Production children cover four destinations; the complete durable port adds ten. An out-of-inventory destination or known destination without a configured handler is Unsupported/Operator; a malformed known claim is CorruptState/ReadOnly.\n- On a delivery error, reaching max_attempts or receiving CorrectRequest/ReadOnly/Operator calls enter_read_only for the **entire daemon**, then ends the pump. There is no per-message dead-letter/recovery state in this dispatcher. A single route/config/version mismatch or exhausted row can therefore block unrelated daily work.\n- The E0 decoder binds directive.maximum_deliveries exactly to the durable row's max_attempts. Their numerical equality is necessary integrity; the producer-selected finite attempt count and scoped recovery policy still need tracing. Native handlers await durable owning-API settlement and return false; false means already settled, not permission to skip settlement. **All router/handler/claim implementations fully read; producer attempt policy remains pending; normal startup port selection is now confirmed in L269.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGjVKZxltYBygpToIpWK8zWu2i6VK6JkhdSLgxkmq/GmBpKn8I4t4Q0IaHEBHWjebnQDXzlIJmL2lSxfcVIqbQs="}
