nce. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNUfbCQO+VBD4t1ZEZQ7GtfgWqNPeJw7PxVswLvi/syd5/khbzYtbwEB1f8jTaViMLGMGB7tmDtIilp04/g2lgo="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2759,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.191206936Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"591ebf3b-ebd5-543a-98b6-1f8a999b27e7","title":"[L268] Credential-registry retry checks stale head before it can recover its exact committed command","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L268.\n\n- Source: `crates/state/peritus-journal/src/authority/registry_commit.rs:30-75,84-110`; `sqlite/append.rs:69-104`; startup exact-snapshot handling in L229.\n- A registry install derives deterministic command/event IDs from the same store/expected revision/new revision/generation/digest. But commit_credential_registry first compares the current head with the install's **old expected revision**. After a successful commit, repeating the exact same install fails StaleRegistry before append's exact-command replay branch can return the already committed result.\n- This is a retry/recovery ordering gate, not an elapsed deadline. The underlying C0 append can recover exact committed commands, but this wrapper prevents reaching it. An ambiguous acknowledgment needs exact command resolution before rejecting changed head facts; generating another identity would lose the idempotency boundary.\n- Startup already has separate exact-current-snapshot handling, so this finding does not assert that every restart fails. Actual lost-ack callers and existing conformance coverage remain to be read. **Complete registry wrapper and append implementation read; no lost-ack reproduction executed.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc