{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2760,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.193432384Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"591ebf3b-ebd5-543a-98b6-1f8a999b27e7","comment_uuid":"c8dba900-fc55-4abc-a246-79e42ddaa5ba","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L268: Credential-registry retry checks stale head before it can recover its exact committed command.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/state/peritus-journal/src/authority/registry_commit.rs:30-75,84-110; sqlite/append.rs:69-104. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nResolve an exact historical credential-registry command receipt before applying current-head admission. Return its immutable result plus the current frontier; changed content under the same identity remains a conflict. Preserve monotonic revocation and credential facts without replaying an already committed change just because its acknowledgement was lost.\n\nPreserve: explicit user authority, credential secrecy, exact target/resource binding, fencing, scope confinement, replay rejection for changed command content and fail-closed acceptance evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: renewal/adoption under the same authorized identity, revoked authority, stale epoch/revision, cross-scope requests, lost acknowledgements and restart, proving legitimate continuation without admitting unauthorized or duplicate effects. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHRDoZlAFLN3wuKyyiM8XEuom9ZNmMZHbvBVMb3huOsY01DqEhCxRroMiJabcMVCHmIMH3ZpFo8oFMrXx7Uq/Qo="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2761,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.195630708Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"6b7f5853-34a6-589e-8dda-4001f2dccfc1","title":"[L269] Normal daemon startup installs four handlers for a fourteen-destination outbox protocol","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L269.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/startup/runtime/runner.rs:144-151`; `outbox/handlers.rs:14-44`; `outbox/router.rs:78-88`; `outbox/claims.rs`; global failure policy in L265.\n- Normal writable startup calls DestinationRouter::production_children with capacity **64**. That factory installs only the four child handlers. The separate production durable port supplies ten additional agent/kernel/quality/workflow destinations, but the normal startup runner does not select it.\n- If one of those ten supported durable destinations is produced in this daemon, decoding succeeds and routing fails for a missing handler. The pump classifies that as Operator and forces the entire daemon read-only. Increasing router capacity cannot repair absent routes; protocol admission, installed ownership, and recovery must agree before accepting a durable row.\n- This is a source-confirmed startup/routing mismatch. Actual production callers that enqueue those ten destinations still need reading; it does not establish that every ordinary product-run mutation uses this outbox path. **Complete startup and route implementations read; no enqueue/runtime reproduction executed.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAA