nvariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKreccIckmVqawT2eD4Cb+YUnUtF1dy8Uit79JJBmjj6/qf/+AuvNlftxFMIGiAP52H75poStxw5+wEb7aTu7As="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2763,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.200220827Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"65a662a1-40e6-5f93-8676-273147febd00","title":"[L270] Domain commits can fail after becoming durable and reject retries against changed registry facts","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L270.\n\n- Source: `crates/state/peritus-journal/src/domain/commit.rs:8-38`; `domain/approval.rs:123-136`; `domain/approval_use.rs:152-160`; `domain/approval_use/resolution.rs`.\n- Common commit_state consumes a move-only successor, commits append, then performs a separate fallible historical state read. A storage/observation failure at that point returns Err after the exact command and state are durable. Correct recovery must resolve that command identity before re-planning or treating the result as absence. Callers must preserve enough immutable inputs to recover a consumed successor; their behavior is not established by this adapter alone.\n- Approval transition and consumption check the current credential registry before entering append's exact replay path. Rotation between the original commit and retry can reject the old intent with StaleRegistry. The dedicated approve-once resolver avoids mutable-head validation, but reconstructing its request still requires an observation matching the original registry binding. This is an identity/recovery gate, not permission to extend old authorization validity or a work timeout.\n- Exact state revisions advance once and reject u64 exhaustion. CancelHeld additionally requires a current durable Begin lineage; already activated or terminal reservations cannot be canceled as never-activated. These authority/conservation constraints need an explicit alternate recovery path, not removal of proof checks.\n- Budget transitions embed up to three separately production-bounded frames into one **16 MiB state value**, so aggregate encoding can fail despite each frame fitting independently. Canonical budget-frame errors become InvalidInput. **All domain commit adapters fully read; caller retry and lost-ack qualification pending.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPrTY+TI6omQIIFcKhTG3TZU3ETAwpKVSQV9SZOULrbs4J+R4I/4ZMCmMlevnJtZmUYHojdx7Hgrq06mVocsRQk="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2764,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.202436476Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"65a662a1-40e6-5f93-8676-273147febd00","comment_uuid":"9dcb0741-a94f-4d94-ac3d-6ad6290bddf0","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L270: Domain commits can fail after becoming durable and reject retries against changed registry facts.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/state/peritus-journal/src/domain/commit.rs:8-38; domain/approval.rs:123-136; domain/approval_use.rs:152-160; domain/approval_use/resolution.rs. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nSeparate durable commit acknowledgement from post-commit registry/projection refresh. Resolve exact historical receipts first and reconcile current state independently, returning known committed outcomes even if a later derived operation fails. Retain original typed errors and prevent both duplicate effects and quarantine caused by treating changed current facts as a failed old commit.\n\nPreserve: committed command/event identity, exact causal and digest roots, exclusive ownership, atomic publication, reference-safe artifact retention and verified recovery from the last durable frontier. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAESF6IK/qc3ztWpptSWgBt7HAlkN/Rt7Du1EfasOXRFlFTcFoqhXp0NcKZ9jHuUt4LFHMziF7UBhTTlqCRQ9g4="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2765,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.204772704Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"5f23bc0e-a25e-5ca9-991d-e4a465d589e8","title":"[L271] Kernel recovery replays all retained history and hashes the complete growing aggregate at every step","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L271.\n\n- Source: `crates/state/peritus-journal/src/domain/kernel.rs:22-23,45-49,174-183`; `domain/kernel/capsule.rs`; `domain/kernel/recovery.rs:54-102,124-138`; `domain/kernel/state_digest.rs:13-83`; `domain/kernel/commit.rs`.\n- A replay capsule accepts at most **64 input references**, each identity **1..256 bytes**, with strict canonical ordering and no duplicates. Full command/envelope frames use the production codec; the combined capsule must also fit the durable state bound. Kernel commits accept exactly one matching event and store one immutable capsule per event. Version/kind/phase/role inventories are closed.\n- Recovery loads the complete event chain, reads every corresponding capsule, invokes the application resolver for every historical input, and compares each emitted event and full successor digest. The digest serializes every accumulated run, attempt, turn, action, review, and waiver each time. With a growing aggregate, cumulative replay work can grow quadratically; there is no resumable checkpoint or paged recovery path in this adapter.\n- One missing capsule or unresolvable historical input aborts the entire aggregate. Resolver errors are replaced by static InvalidInput text, discarding the driver's detail. No elapsed deadline or session expiry is imposed here, but permanent dependence on every old input and repeated complete-state work are daily-driving recovery risks.\n- Expiry instants, remaining-use limits, and the five budget dimensions are serialized as authority facts; these files choose no short default. **Complete kernel persistence/recovery implementation read; no growth benchmark or damaged-input execution performed.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMDwaOGKaKcGJSVu6pjBdcMbS/POQJgUVlDfYRg8B6EGXcEMQEp4hgP3W6x8viU3+YskvYHKSotuITKMyWmaXg0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2766,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.206927657Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"5f23bc0e-a25e-5ca9-991d-e4a465d589e8","comment_uuid":"a54cfc1a-151a-4076-9398-073362b1c6cd","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L271: Kernel recovery replays all retained history and hashes the complete growing aggregate at every step.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/state/peritus-journal/src/domain/kernel.rs:22-23,45-49,174-183; domain/kernel/capsule.rs; domain/kernel/recovery.rs:54-102,124-138; domain/kernel/state_digest.rs:13-83; domain/kernel/commit.rs. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nIntroduce indexed incremental kernel projections and verified checkpoint/suffix replay, with paged immutable event/state history. Routine commands validate affected transitions and roots instead of cloning and hashing the complete lifetime aggregate at every event. Full integrity verification remains resumable and exact, preserving authoritative causal and authority evidence.\n\nPreserve: exact candidate revision and artifact binding, complete finding/provenance conservation, independent reviewer evidence, truthful gate outcomes, protected user constraints and acceptance fail-closed on invalid evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQH9oAmc9shguGXFS5/hNhcNg6r7LYYxiHT07oRD/SdUwGDn4ZTl2JExvZOFOJGlUzF9hNGv7Q/QPPr2Ur21rZgk="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2767,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.209301384Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"9dca0480-44f7-5da1-ac3e-4afb7ef20323","title":"[L274] Status, cancellation, and shutdown wait behind synchronous work in one authority FIFO","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L274.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/authority/owner.rs:48-69`; `owner/handle.rs:117-124`; `owner/runtime.rs:24-369`; `owner/error.rs`.\n- The owner has one bounded queue (**1..65,536** capacity; caller default in L202). Every facade call awaits queue space, then a oneshot reply. Status, read-only transition, transfer cancellation, draining, and Stop have no separate reserved admission or service lane.\n- The owner processes one message fully before receiving another. Journal queries, full replay/reconstruction, hashing, artifact I/O, and dispatch are synchronous within that Tokio task. A slow or stuck operation delays diagnostics and cancellation for every client and can starve ordinary runtime workers. No elapsed cutoff exists here, but removing timeouts alone cannot repair that progress dependency.\n- Dropping the caller's reply receiver does not withdraw an accepted message: reply ignores send failure after completing the work. Recovery must preserve/resolve command identity after caller loss. Busy/Storage is labeled Retry; the owner sends that result and continues, without retrying it itself.\n- Session mutation and prompt registration/answers require global mutation readiness. Prompt status/correlations and retirement operate on the in-memory broker; the closed owner message inventory contains no durable outstanding-prompt enumeration/republication command. This closes L259's owner-interface trace, while producer republication remains pending.\n- **Complete owner and facade source read; no head-of-queue stall or live lockup reproduction performed.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGJcaB2M/QITIahfd9CIkvqNy60vIn0GHhqAyGUnrKdHiPtQzM1tR50QXRl4QhloaMuoI0sUAoidzOw53K/AQA4="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2768,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.211237255Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"9dca0480-44f7-5da1-ac3e-4afb7ef20323","comment_uuid":"b2e851f3-4486-4430-ab60-6bf039e7f1c5","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L274: Status, cancellation, and shutdown wait behind synchronous work in one authority FIFO.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/authority/owner.rs:48-69; owner/handle.rs:117-124; owner/runtime.rs:24-369; owner/error.rs. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nSeparate status/cancellation/shutdown control from blocking serialized effect work through a responsive owner state machine. Move hashing, replay and native waits to owned cancellable workers, installing results under exact revision fences. Reserve control progress and persist stop intent so no ordinary authority FIFO can make the user wait behind unbounded synchronous work.\n\nPreserve: explicit user authority, credential secrecy, exact target/resource binding, fencing, scope confinement, replay rejection for changed command content and fail-closed acceptance evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: renewal/adoption under the same authorized identity, revoked authority, stale epoch/revision, cross-scope requests, lost acknowledgements and restart, proving legitimate continuation without admitting unauthorized or duplicate effects. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMaxSMi40bTzn4PNOJymfHjjmQlYECiS9dgk4IHLAh7txDgAaaT1O9NI19NSRRb4ttc0zVfE9ow7YmCglE6rPgE="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2769,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.213351018Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"3964d483-2f37-5dd1-89ad-687158dcd550","title":"[L275] Installed native child handlers reject supported start and cancellation work for missing orchestration inputs","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L275.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/authority/owner/orchestrator/children/collaboration.rs:25-31`; `children/scheduler.rs:24-28`; `children/gates_review.rs:19-29`; `children.rs:119-134`; error policy L265.\n- The installed Collaboration destination explicitly rejects **StartWriter, StartReview, and StartFixer** because native scheduler work/reservation inputs are absent. The installed Scheduler destination explicitly rejects **CancelChildren** because the native work root is absent. These become Unsupported/Operator, which the production pump turns into whole-daemon read-only.\n- Gates/Review handlers support pause/resume only. Lifecycle delivery requires retained exact child heads and the immediate durable pause successor for resume. Those identity checks are necessary; protocol publication must carry sufficient inputs and route to an owner that can execute its admitted kind.\n- This is an independent implementation/admission gap even when a destination handler is installed. Actual E0 producers and ordinary product-run linkage remain pending; no claim that every user stop traverses Scheduler is made. **All installed child implementation read; no emitted-directive reproduction run.** `authority/owner/orchestrator_tests.rs:118-166` actually publishes StartWriter to Collaboration, but calls settle_claimed_directive directly and bypasses child admission/execution. Child tests call native helpers with their missing inputs already supplied and test membership, not actual unsupported E0 handoff delivery.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDUwrdZ/EcHe6VsrFX83FMcCEVkIJ/vS3/sxKWIWxkFoxWcDQ9WOUX5cB4ViBZU3giok11cuR0uLBD3PdH0f3Ao="}
