until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large histories and non-ASCII fields, queue/connection pressure, delayed acknowledgements, subscription gaps, disconnect/reconnect and daemon restart, proving snapshot recovery, preserved selection/context, responsive controls and no duplicate command. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJdpFrR12ypfJacoLsPKgHJjBluW8A2xNuMF6H7QlZBbYPD+YYmwBophDZZqcRJ8s9eFgtCmMPFXLmucW1kesgw="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2771,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.217606238Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"034681b8-5b39-586f-8dee-8c78763b4e66","title":"[L276] Native child retry recovery only recognizes the most recent committed command and repeatedly replays full history","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L276.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/authority/owner/orchestrator.rs:48-71`; `children/collaboration.rs:187-201,222-265`; `children/scheduler.rs:132-175`; `children/gates_review.rs:214-257`.\n- Exact D2/D3 retry helpers inspect only events.split_last. If a command already committed but a later child event exists before recovery, the helper reports stale fence instead of resolving the earlier exact command identity. Immediate lost-ack retries can succeed; progress after the commit creates another admission barrier. Caller/concurrency qualification is still pending.\n- Child admission replays the complete current child, then commit helpers reload/rebuild it; retry may replay the complete predecessor prefix again. E0 settlement independently replays full current history and the publication prefix. Per-directive work therefore grows with retained history while holding the sole authority owner (L274).\n- The child effect commits before separate E0/outbox settlement. Interruption between these steps requires immutable exact-command recovery across both owners; merely acknowledging a new lease cannot prove a second effect is safe. **Complete implementation read; no interleaved later-event/lost-ack execution or growth benchmark performed.** Fully read D2/D3 child tests retry each command immediately after restart, before any later successor exists; the later-event exact retry barrier is outside their cases.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCT0X41ws8WSMmQk0iCz4BwmJS6cFP8NWsPcxw4hRK/ytRs4akofosTw9L3PNL9ipHyeE274CLstL/nRgV64Ngw="}
