ive evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQP6CZfUq7IS67oPSSzB8GNtA2zLeYMKXqD/xUj/BB1nxFWVTzL1e4oS/T4Ro9ibfqKQ3NEO1jsnN/5dyTJR94gM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2773,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.221796642Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"d8aa74fa-1832-5e6f-bdea-c5f2f0b5dd23","title":"[L278] Application dispatch admits a closed subset and erases the reason for semantic or capacity rejection","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L278.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/domain/dispatch.rs:51-63,87-92,156-169,277-299`; `domain/dispatch/{debugger,evaluation,evolution,harness}.rs`; `command/service.rs:129-147`.\n- The dispatcher recognizes ten numeric families. Gate commands are restricted to **PauseRun/ResumeRun**; fresh scheduler genesis requires **StrictRecoveryQueueV2**, while exact historically settled commands have a separate retained-result path. These are explicit ingress capability/schema barriers, not elapsed deadlines.\n- All decode errors become MalformedFrame and all reducer/check failures become InvalidCommandFrame. Capacity, stale-state, unsupported transition and other actionable causes are lost at this boundary. All external persistence/replay errors receive a generic Reconcile wrapper instead of preserving typed recovery instructions; the underlying error remains only as source.\n- Most handlers load/rebuild the complete retained aggregate before committing; some do it even before rejecting an invalid checked command. This runs under the single authority owner (L274). There is no independent per-aggregate recovery lane or continuation in these ingress files.\n- Terminal rejection reconstruction searches numeric tags **1..65535** for a matching closed error name. That is bounded lookup work, not a work/session quota. **Complete dispatch and tests read; actual source-level domain bounds and current digest recovery still pending.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQH2z+X733dgqLIn9Kvwpz2U3RznRvDVBk5yYaPLxWe2wE2YiB0wkSX5zw6Osa7yt+gQhjeWurIiqwz6HD3Hzywo="}
