 Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large histories and non-ASCII fields, queue/connection pressure, delayed acknowledgements, subscription gaps, disconnect/reconnect and daemon restart, proving snapshot recovery, preserved selection/context, responsive controls and no duplicate command. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLXNaIhuNle1tnM3V6HMMpKNruI/2cX84+qdOKP6sh0IKOfpcqUxNxkKvg+/PCEWfLJ9ToLO3hFfykkbTkLX9AM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2775,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.226124439Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"c9d8beff-b1de-52aa-9a8f-71eae61407a2","title":"[L279] Artifact transfers share finite registries and first-sixteen download polling can starve later transfers","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L279.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/artifact/client.rs:12,25-28,64-80,89-100`; `artifact/service.rs:60-68,80,101-102,142-150,335-342`; normal caller limits in L202/L029.\n- Per-connection transfer capacity reuses AppProtocolLimits.max_idempotency_entries, while the authority has a separate positive configured maximum for all uploads/downloads. Capacity returns ResourceLimit/Retry; one active upload per artifact identity is enforced. No expiry or automatic stale-transfer collection occurs in these implementations; explicit cancel, completion, abandonment or owner destruction removes entries.\n- Each tick selects the first **16 downloads in sorted transfer-ID order**, with no rotation cursor. With more than sixteen active downloads, later entries receive no chunk until enough earlier transfers finish. One error or blocked sequential write/authority response interrupts the pump. This is a fairness/progress limiter, not a retention window or elapsed work timeout.\n- Downloads prefer chunks at most **64 KiB**, within the negotiated maximum; zero chunk limits are rejected. Upload admission applies the configured per-object bound. The service tests use a four-transfer tiny-byte fixture and do not exercise the >16 fairness boundary. **Complete transfer implementation/tests read; no concurrent download reproduction executed.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHEhxelPzWQGHoZdQs+R57e89pzVyl3ohirqXVTPmgyf2Ghm0TV8D+lQTAoEp1cUZq/YOumvwOP0q8lXvc0KKQU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2776,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.228225953Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"c9d8beff-b1de-52aa-9a8f-71eae61407a2","comment_uuid":"75ed4cbb-38bd-4fd3-afe7-9a55f9ce9341","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L279: Artifact transfers share finite registries and first-sixteen download polling can starve later transfers.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/artifact/client.rs:12,25-28,64-80,89-100; artifact/service.rs:60-68,80,101-102,142-150,335-342. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nSeparate bounded active artifact transfer slots from immutable historical publication receipts, using fair cursor-based polling rather than the first sixteen IDs. Persist acknowledged progress and reclaim settled slots only after exact publication/recovery evidence exists. Cancellation and new eligible transfers must remain responsive under a stalled old transfer.\n\nPreserve: canonical digest and schema identity, shared writer/reader admissibility, malformed-input rejection before allocation, exact causal ordering, actual provider/OS capability boundaries and preserved accepted historical evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQO2DzF+WCaTKpUe+1g/iLB+1hrtoxVRimas6+2yMD3lJgtDnKInAOwDuTz/B/UnSfE50j/lWHLsWV1S11RRRWw8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2777,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.230439833Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"46cd853e-772e-5fa4-b687-b3141d55a77f","title":"[L281] Private artifact claims are permanent exact bindings without adoption, rebinding, or retirement","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L281.\n\n- Source: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/artifact/scope.rs:17-18,42-155,178-210`; `artifact/service/tests.rs:174-295`.\n- A private claim is exactly **80 bytes**, one event and revision **1**: actor, conversation, workspace, and metadata fingerprint. Any different existing claim or older unscoped artifact rejects adoption. Exact same scope/metadata can restart a complete upload; foreign/legacy paths cannot bypass that ownership binding.\n- There is no expiry, rebinding, migration or retirement operation in this adapter. Canceling a transfer leaves the durable claim and Pending catalog facts; journal catalog adapters likewise have no failed/purge recovery API (L262). Their eventual lifecycle/garbage-collection callers remain pending.\n- These are ownership and representation constraints, not grounds to discard a session or disable authorization. A durable cleanup/import/migration contract must be explicit. **All private claim source and tests read; no age-related blocker asserted.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQD3u5QprJSHaxSvrdY978VnGSopyy2bUYjB6GSpWXD0SwxnPz5Nqt6DI73tRqPR6dWeeEBNKmfaSbw3JV97PZQc="}
