d invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPfIu3hJq+kF/KGOHzECMl4wa4PeVlPR9fgg4w2/qfFGjVeJ5eI1Bzv8njuGVG80YI1m5tqRun11uuUSwYTG8QM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2779,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.234712108Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"9a4ce769-4830-5519-b3cd-db6511351401","title":"[L283] Scheduler capacity and lifetime retention have immutable finite ceilings with no unlimited setting","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L283.\n\n- Source: `crates/orchestration/peritus-scheduler/src/limits.rs:134-211`; `binding.rs:10-19,125-156`; `durability/semantics.rs:14-45`.\n- All eleven limits must be positive and at or below compiled maxima: **65,535 queued work and 65,535 retained work**, **4,096 workers**, **1,024 dependencies per work**, **256 resource dimensions**, **4,096 active reservations**, **1,024 attempts per work**, **32,767 bypasses**, **256 directives per poll**, and **16 MiB minus 16 bytes** for each payload and complete checkpoint. Queue and reservations must fit retention. There is no unlimited variant.\n- Limits and resource capacity are immutable parts of the aggregate's binding and canonical digest. Fresh creation requires StrictRecoveryQueueV2; an existing checkpoint must preserve its exact schema. These interfaces expose no in-place limit/capacity change or schema migration.\n- These declarations mix concurrency, batch, representation, fairness and historical retention bounds. Whether retained terminal work can be retired, and how each bound rejects normal work, are being traced in the reducers. Representation and resource constraints must not be silently treated as elapsed deadlines or fixed by losing run identity. **Complete limits, binding and append-schema policy read; admission/retirement callers pending.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQI/Ahp/NOZ5a5dp+JqHiIZpwu0Jlhm7eX6Bbix0+El/S5ZveQvv+UUZC7fyxYAgAimhvgBE5qnCwJyBUHbXXQwI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2780,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.237006371Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"9a4ce769-4830-5519-b3cd-db6511351401","comment_uuid":"61a7a536-20f2-4164-ad3d-25e4b0ce8b1d","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L283: Scheduler capacity and lifetime retention have immutable finite ceilings with no unlimited setting.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/orchestration/peritus-scheduler/src/limits.rs:134-211; binding.rs:10-19,125-156; durability/semantics.rs:14-45. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nReplace mandatory lifetime scheduler quotas with paged immutable work/dispatch/command history and a bounded active scheduling frontier. Version bindings to describe real in-flight resource capacity and optional explicitly selected policy, while permitting indefinite logical continuation. Preserve dependency and reservation truth, exact receipts and independently admitted controls across schema migration.\n\nPreserve: resource reservations, dispatch fencing, dependency truth, opaque identity versus causal order, monotonic stop intent, exact historical receipts and truthful child/effect settlement. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long task/message/command histories, smaller configured bindings, saturation with cancellation and acknowledgements, delayed start/completion races, terminal roots with live descendants, lost receipts after subsequent progress, and save/reopen equivalence. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNRmpGllwtPVaUqqyhNPV5olfr9+cA1MjQzqo54gzZDln93dOXaIYA79wbOUAKNTf2MKkiBDChfwF7jwNq6qcAo="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2781,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.239321637Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"0ad9b08a-65ea-5766-b757-8815da1291da","title":"[L284] Scheduler replay reuse covers one aggregate and persistence recovery loses actionable error distinctions","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L284.\n\n- Source: `crates/orchestration/peritus-scheduler/src/session.rs:15-19,35-50,65-88`; `durability.rs`; `durability/binding.rs`.\n- A session caches exactly one aggregate. Switching runs, reopening the connection, an external commit, or any other append attempt invalidates reuse and requires observe_replay plus complete scheduler replay/checkpoint verification. Any failure discards the cache; exact committed-command resolution also returns no successor observation, causing the next access to replay again. This session is a journal cache, not the provider's native context window.\n- A command's bound payload or complete-state overflow is classified through binding_error as **Journal/Quarantine**. Generic journal errors become **ReplayAggregate**, losing distinctions such as Busy versus corruption at this boundary. These are recovery/blocker classifications, not elapsed work deadlines.\n- commit_transition resolves an exact committed command before checking the current head, but its helper still loads the current checkpoint. If it has advanced beyond that receipt, it returns an aggregate-advanced replay error instead of that helper returning the historical success. Application-ledger resolution can return the original batch directly; the callers therefore have different recovery contracts.\n- The stored domain request digest is SHA256 of the exact encoded scheduler command bytes, matching the application admission digest. Binding verification is separate; no digest mismatch is asserted here. **Complete durability, binding, cache and schema policy read; no performance or failure-injection test executed.**\n\n- Additional complete test evidence: `crates/orchestration/peritus-scheduler/tests/versioned_durability.rs:134-139` explicitly expects an already committed genesis exact retry to fail after aggregate advancement with `Journal / ReplayAggregate`; this is an existing enforced expectation, not solely an untested source inference.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKDBWEdrp8jDhEX47trEVtApQaIWvokBzShPAS62fltpZiRfXYXP83B6eIeQ7h6SxEciF6j+FJjmP/DR+1FOSQg="}
