m authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long task/message/command histories, smaller configured bindings, saturation with cancellation and acknowledgements, delayed start/completion races, terminal roots with live descendants, lost receipts after subsequent progress, and save/reopen equivalence. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCtkFPtG97bh7howMVyjKd/ur+8PhOcFK6scKB5yzOcZ3BrI50nUaFB5lEN0fP940HoEkhY0GH3sp9bm/JJMrgs="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2783,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.243840700Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"458d0408-f3e0-5385-8087-2c71ebe96522","title":"[L287] Completed work and dispatch identities consume permanent scheduler retention, while temporary capacity is treated as corrected input","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L287.\n\n- Source: `crates/orchestration/peritus-scheduler/src/reducer/apply/admission.rs:46-72`; `admission/checks.rs`; `dispatch.rs:71-85`; `apply.rs:80-143`; `error.rs:113-124`; `command/kind.rs`.\n- Admission rejects when the **entire retained work vector** reaches the immutable retained-work ceiling, including terminal records. It also checks versioned queue pressure, required retained dependencies/parent, global resources and a registered worker with the exact owner/class/capacity. The supporting worker may be lost or draining, but cannot be Removed; immediate execution feasibility is a separate decision.\n- Dispatch separately rejects **65,535 historical dispatch IDs**, even when no reservations are active. Work, dispatch and command history have no retirement operation in the closed command dispatcher. RemoveWorker affects only worker lifecycle; it does not retire work history.\n- Active-reservation capacity and retention/history capacity are mapped to LimitExceeded/**CorrectInput**. Only NoFeasibleWork receives RetryLater. At application ingress, this reason becomes generic InvalidCommandFrame (L278), so a temporary scheduling saturation does not retain an actionable retry contract.\n- Queue/resource/dependency constraints require safe backpressure and continuation; historical capacity requires durable archival/frontier separation. Resetting run identity is not such a continuation. **Complete admission/dispatch implementation and proof contracts read; worker lifecycle, queue accounting and callers still being traced.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDfDqytw8t5ovFu43XR+SuQlQJxX56DWum7AytgXxm9gswlM6BmpqdIk8tI4VmxPQ4jl0ZHSMw3uP33Qo2xIVAY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2784,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.246258745Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"458d0408-f3e0-5385-8087-2c71ebe96522","comment_uuid":"e52494e3-a2cc-4da1-96f3-3163b735db92","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L287: Completed work and dispatch identities consume permanent scheduler retention, while temporary capacity is treated as corrected input.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/orchestration/peritus-scheduler/src/reducer/apply/admission.rs:46-72; admission/checks.rs; dispatch.rs:71-85; apply.rs:80-143; error.rs:113-124; command/kind.rs. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nMove completed work and dispatch identities into indexed immutable receipt history, retiring them from the active capacity frontier without deleting replay/dependency truth. Temporary queue/resource pressure is a recoverable wait with exact pending intent, not CorrectInput. Administrative controls remain admissible and same-run continuation retains all committed identities.\n\nPreserve: resource reservations, dispatch fencing, dependency truth, opaque identity versus causal order, monotonic stop intent, exact historical receipts and truthful child/effect settlement. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long task/message/command histories, smaller configured bindings, saturation with cancellation and acknowledgements, delayed start/completion races, terminal roots with live descendants, lost receipts after subsequent progress, and save/reopen equivalence. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFG540tE2PMqLrfvvdARy4G4Kz3GFnuOmK8XdZP596SFv2nL1sjfksgF2l3CynNhe8CgOltx6aAK4l4bQGAvBgE="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2785,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.248474934Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"327dea99-84e0-5fa7-9686-48cda848fd9e","title":"[L288] Every work item has an immutable attempt ceiling and recovery policy that can make exhaustion terminal","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L288.\n\n- Source: `crates/orchestration/peritus-scheduler/src/work.rs:150-195`; `work/phase.rs`; `work/terminal.rs`; `reducer/apply/dispatch.rs:108-120`; `apply.rs:231-250`.\n- maximum_attempts is a mandatory positive u16 AttemptNumber, no greater than the immutable scheduler attempts limit (compiled maximum **1,024**). Dispatch and explicit RetryWork reject once that item's bound is exhausted; no unlimited variant or bound-extension command exists in the work definition/vocabulary.\n- RetryPending awaits an explicit RetryWork. Ownership loss is bound at admission to RetrySafe, Ambiguous or Fail; terminal vocabulary includes Exhausted, Ambiguous and Abandoned. The complete loss classifier/release now confirms: Cancelling becomes Cancelled; RetrySafe requeues only with attempts remaining and otherwise becomes terminal Exhausted; Ambiguous and Fail become terminal under their bound policies regardless of remaining attempts.\n- These are attempt/lifecycle gates rather than wall-clock deadlines. Recovery needs evidence-based ownership reconciliation and a durable policy for continued authorized work; automatic duplicate execution is not safe merely because a limiter is unwanted. Ordinary FailWork with Retryable also becomes terminal Exhausted at the immutable bound; otherwise it releases to RetryPending, and RetryWork requires that phase plus attempt room. **Complete work definition, phase, terminal, dispatch, retry/failure mutation and single-reservation loss classification/release read; batch loss and effect-shell recovery callers pending.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLcnYnqOFfaII222wLvO+C7SNcCxXJHgdFa1aYGO8Jx+fWGpsTdazfI5SRDugwYjmeu/bjMjeBuoy7CmiLB8+go="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2786,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.250763236Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"327dea99-84e0-5fa7-9686-48cda848fd9e","comment_uuid":"41c86fe9-67bc-4bee-bec2-1700da6339d8","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L288: Every work item has an immutable attempt ceiling and recovery policy that can make exhaustion terminal.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/orchestration/peritus-scheduler/src/work.rs:150-195; work/phase.rs; work/terminal.rs; reducer/apply/dispatch.rs:108-120; apply.rs:231-250. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nSeparate execution attempts from the lifetime work identity and classify definitely-unstarted, transient failure and uncertain accepted dispatch explicitly. Continue safe recoverable attempts under the same work/context without a mandatory immutable attempt quota. Preserve fences and effect reconciliation, and require explicit policy or truly unrecoverable evidence for terminal exhaustion.\n\nPreserve: resource reservations, dispatch fencing, dependency truth, opaque identity versus causal order, monotonic stop intent, exact historical receipts and truthful child/effect settlement. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long task/message/command histories, smaller configured bindings, saturation with cancellation and acknowledgements, delayed start/completion races, terminal roots with live descendants, lost receipts after subsequent progress, and save/reopen equivalence. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCujpOIRHBy1BF/cVMNye+Iy+W5dl/LuIU/HxownRN5rAo6OpaeBjNZUhWCWLVt4pPF7qNoB1JHJhDjaOEt1Ews="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2787,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.252810866Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"d793a029-b248-5ba5-b6c2-843e7fb6b247","title":"[L289] Scheduler replay repeatedly clones and hashes retained state, and estimated size is an additional admission gate","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L289.\n\n- Source: `crates/orchestration/peritus-scheduler/src/reducer.rs:63-82,89-116`; `state.rs:308-322`.\n- Each command clones the full state, applies the command, refreshes it, checks estimated_encoded_bytes, appends its identity and hashes the complete successor. Replay invokes that reduction for every historical event, with retained event/command ID sets. As state grows, reconstructing all prefixes can accumulate quadratic copying/hashing work; no latency measurement was performed.\n- The estimate starts at **1,024 bytes**, adds **512 per worker**, **512 per work plus 16 per dependency/resource entry**, **384 per reservation**, and **16 per historical command/dispatch identity**. It can reject before exact encoding even if the actual frame would fit; exact encoding still enforces its own cap afterward. The estimate is tested before appending the next command ID.\n- This is a state-size/performance blocker, not an elapsed timeout. Integrity checking must remain grounded in exact durable facts while checkpoints and bounded frontier state avoid repeated whole-history rebuilding. Canonical hashing has now been fully read: it streams SHA256 while traversing every retained state field, rather than constructing a separate complete hash buffer. Worker refresh scans all retained workers and counts reservations after each event. **Complete reducer, estimator, canonical hashing and outer refresh/worker refresh read; wire encoding and inner dependency rounds pending.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMdHAE2SZRyRp8jJBYh12WoYeNT3w5qKaaIkzyoUvVBs0CMyIBnxDc1FZ1lke9A3LJbCv2ogkaBUJjsbu3XMzwc="}
