r; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long task/message/command histories, smaller configured bindings, saturation with cancellation and acknowledgements, delayed start/completion races, terminal roots with live descendants, lost receipts after subsequent progress, and save/reopen equivalence. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPpT67zvmD1bJhvat2E8lRB5NF2CypoP17SeSDgAyCynEYuMgHKmeqQ5d27l6EL+/WYZniBwCBldUvvyyBFXZAY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2789,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.257209030Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"4265b31b-dc52-5c35-9e61-832378afd2d6","title":"[L291] Removing scheduler workers does not free registration capacity, and drain/terminal lifecycles have no reopening path","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L291.\n\n- Source: `crates/orchestration/peritus-scheduler/src/reducer/apply/worker_control.rs:9-34,68-83`; `worker.rs:107-141`; `state/mutation/scheduler_phase.rs`; `reducer/apply/control/finalization.rs:129-198`.\n- Registration compares the **entire retained worker vector** with the immutable worker limit (compiled maximum **4,096**). RemoveWorker only sets Removed; it deletes no record. A removed identity cannot be restored Available or registered again, and it still consumes retention. Repeated replacement workers can exhaust registration even with no live ownership.\n- Worker concurrency must be **1..active_reservations**, execution classes are nonempty/canonical among five supported classes, and resource dimension/capacity checks are finite. Descriptor fields have no update command; quiescent Lost/Draining workers can return Available only before removal.\n- DrainScheduler closes new work and worker admission. Pause/Resume can preserve or return to Draining, but there is no Undrain. FinalizeScheduler requires all work terminal and no reservation, then closes the aggregate against every new command; complete history remains retained. These are explicit lifecycle barriers, not elapsed deadlines.\n- Persistent daily use needs a defined replacement/retirement and continuation contract under the existing durable identity, with truthful ownership and terminal evidence. **Complete worker admission/control, phase transitions, insertion and finalization read; no replacement-capacity reproduction executed.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQICHBRK+ww2ndYZYMq/XoA1EwGBxp/9PIrbeuJAa6X/zgGP0IFenxKxgxJbDWKqM9DoDtr3Zb5nkg/yvrENT7Q4="}
