authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long task/message/command histories, smaller configured bindings, saturation with cancellation and acknowledgements, delayed start/completion races, terminal roots with live descendants, lost receipts after subsequent progress, and save/reopen equivalence. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDxt0anwZr/PttiTkIg9fYo9tHH/l3FxfgmmolRNVU4kuQGi+d3ivb0jaiz+DZxTPfwEnVeFaAJartfSAUVapw4="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2791,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.261642364Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"598585c7-2188-5c6e-8991-9a54d6770335","title":"[L299] Collaboration has nine immutable positive quotas and retains terminal/acknowledged history","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L299.\n\n- Source: `crates/orchestration/peritus-collaboration/src/limits.rs:5-82`; `binding.rs:12-19,45-56,114-126`; `canonical.rs:117-134`; `command.rs:12-106`; `reducer/apply.rs:65-108,160-234`; `state/mutation.rs:10-37,80-89`.\n- Compiled ceilings are **65,535 retained tasks**, **depth 256**, **4,096 direct children**, **262,144 retained messages**, **4,096 recipients per task**, **1 MiB referenced payload per message**, **4,096 artifact references per task**, **16 MiB minus 16 command bytes**, and **64 MiB minus 16 state bytes**. All nine must be positive; there is no unlimited/disabled value. Exact binding digest fixes them for the aggregate.\n- Task/message insertion measures complete retained vectors. Terminal tasks and acknowledged messages remain retained, direct-child counts include terminal children, and message artifact counts include acknowledged deliveries. Completion with an artifact handoff can fail when previous message handoffs consumed the task's artifact quota. The closed command vocabulary provides no retirement, history frontier, limit mutation, or migration command.\n- These are lifetime and structural admission blockers, not elapsed-time deadlines. Increasing a configured value cannot exceed the compiled ceiling or change an already-bound aggregate. Canonical framing, final cursor growth, delivery/finalization and real daemon applicability are being traced separately. **Complete limit, binding, command and admission/mutation sources read; no runtime saturation experiment or live-instance attribution claimed.**\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKbtJtb307FUZWaf+F3bNiQg81nnTR95ikMJgcMDKRAofHSjh4CxVR9TpFUdhVHukSQ2UER+IvCJIgxcaCwYug0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2792,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.263838248Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"598585c7-2188-5c6e-8991-9a54d6770335","comment_uuid":"15980516-d87e-4f28-bc1f-f084cd3fc8c7","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L299: Collaboration has nine immutable positive quotas and retains terminal/acknowledged history.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/orchestration/peritus-collaboration/src/limits.rs:5-82; binding.rs:12-19,45-56,114-126; canonical.rs:117-134; command.rs:12-106; reducer/apply.rs:65-108,160-234; state/mutation.rs:10-37,80-89. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nVersion collaboration into immutable paged task/message/receipt history and an indexed active task/delivery frontier. Remove mandatory total-history/attempt quotas, keeping physical in-flight resource bounds and explicit user policy separate. Acknowledgements and terminal tasks release active capacity while causal/artifact evidence and exact historical retry receipts remain durable.\n\nPreserve: resource reservations, dispatch fencing, dependency truth, opaque identity versus causal order, monotonic stop intent, exact historical receipts and truthful child/effect settlement. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long task/message/command histories, smaller configured bindings, saturation with cancellation and acknowledgements, delayed start/completion races, terminal roots with live descendants, lost receipts after subsequent progress, and save/reopen equivalence. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAIZPGB23MARlDBQBuJFnk2LiupcZUu4tMtXy5aWKuWEr+gjjpa1TPV5yHh2aj/CjNPDzVmUFsPMZA8OHgrmgAs="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2793,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.266410099Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"aed29396-08dd-5166-9833-cee253793794","title":"[L367] E1 planner can admit more file operations than its C1 executor permits","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L367.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/orchestration/peritus-harness/src/materialization/planner.rs:38-83`, `src/materialization/planner.rs:93-101`, `src/materialization/executor.rs:158-201`, `src/runtime/driver.rs:136-153`, `src/runtime/driver.rs:181-212`; C1 bounds in L006 and E1 component bounds in L355.\n- Behavior: the planner installs every declaration in the new graph and adds a delete for each prior owned file absent from that graph. It checks nonempty operations, path collisions, and installed-byte total but not C1's 1,024-operation ceiling. Two valid revisions with 1,024 disjoint small-file target paths can therefore produce 2,048 operations while satisfying E1's graph and byte bounds. The plan can commit before `PatchSet::new` rejects it during execution. The runtime classifies this as `PatchRejected` and attempts durable failure settlement; it does not divide the plan into work units.\n- Consequence: an admissible revision replacement can deterministically fail materialization because of a downstream synthetic batch ceiling. Normal durable failure settlement clears pending work when failure capacity is available; L360 describes the additional settlement blocker. No example was executed, and target ownership/security checks must remain intact.\n- Repair direction: plan against the exact effect representation, or use resumable bounded patch batches with durable progress and a complete ownership frontier. Operation-count batching must not impose a lifetime ceiling on a valid revision change. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGOQeUK7CaAVyLjSbw96ULXUtAzpxXTIqRN1MVsd+1XVrV4XpBeJ31zceQ6f6QsPzmFzn2oK3Lye7J4tAQcqSQA="}
