ation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFl4/Sp0VnplXF8METTarHBXUWHZeL/akTMi4oToQQ7K9219bLMlZtcGGzpnfzeh8EBKRqQZVX4HcUQUCqIc9wI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2795,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.270872180Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"5aeb1f8e-8fcf-5046-97b5-a807b60a745e","title":"[L368] E1 component inventory imposes an undocumented directory-to-file ratio ceiling","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L368.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/orchestration/peritus-harness/src/manifest/inventory.rs:24-50`, `src/manifest/loader.rs:200-225`; portable source-path depth rules in L356.\n- Behavior: inventory counts every descendant directory and file and rejects once their total exceeds eight times the configured component count. This is separate from the declared-file/component ceiling. It uses `UnsafeEntry` even for ordinary no-follow directories. Tightening components to one makes a single valid component nested more than eight entries below the root fail inventory although its source path passes the domain's much larger depth bound. Empty directories count too. Listing is complete per directory before that global check; there is no continuation cursor.\n- Consequence: harmless directory organization can block loading an otherwise valid manifest. This is a synthetic structural quota, not evidence of an unsafe entry or elapsed timeout. The default 1,024-component policy permits 8,192 descendant entries; it has no unbounded alternative under the current policy API.\n- Repair direction: traverse a durable/paged inventory with explicit resource accounting and separate safety violations from capacity. Directory batching should not permanently invalidate a legitimate component set. Preserve no-follow, exact declared inventory, and path confinement. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQG9DchprdZJ1Xrq6UrZ6V75AuYpb9J2jtjLIb7+t3PNp7ZREq5ejvQFc9ZeySjc+fsMCSAiPoihYuAGZgnXisQI="}
