lable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQH51wlFcs5sXHUeNr10cP4lkHA5T3qtP8n4YCMATK6yv2mNv/EAdHCM6PM2+ZXzZXLaNpGzINBNdNSUDWJfaIwE="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2797,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.275071818Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"0103847f-ef5f-5ff7-be02-17ca6e5d3fef","title":"[L369] E1 loader enforces aggregate payload capacity after reading all component bytes","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L369.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/orchestration/peritus-harness/src/manifest/document.rs:66-79`, `src/manifest/loader.rs:61-81`, `src/manifest/loader.rs:228-263`; graph aggregate validation and compiled ceilings in L355.\n- Behavior: parsing validates each declaration but does not construct the checked graph. `load_harness` reads and hashes every declared payload into a BTreeMap; only the separate subsequent `LoadedHarness::check` validates graph relationships and the aggregate materialized-byte limit. Under compiled bounds, 1,024 individually valid 8-MiB payloads can be read before the 8-MiB aggregate rejection. No cumulative loader byte budget or streaming frontier bounds that work. Exact size/digest checks are useful integrity protections but occur on the full allocated payload.\n- Consequence: an input that is certain to exceed aggregate policy can consume substantial synchronous I/O, hashing, and memory before rejection. The roughly 8-GiB upper combination follows the per-component and count bounds; it is not a measured allocation or installed-run diagnosis. Existing C1 or host restrictions may reject earlier. This is late resource validation, not a new timer.\n- Repair direction: validate declaration totals and the graph before payload reads, then stream checked artifacts with bounded resident memory and resumable progress. Keep complete digest and inventory verification. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4"