{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2799,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.279371906Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"8885ff96-0445-50c0-a52a-0829385339ca","title":"[L370] S2 failure disposition imposes one clarification and forbids evaluator recovery","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L370.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/orchestration/peritus-obligations/src/failure.rs:24-57`, `src/failure.rs:76-113`, `tests/failure_matrix.rs:24-53`, `README.md:14-16`.\n- Behavior: once the caller reports that an ambiguity question was used, every contract ambiguity maps to `Settle`, even when `recovery_available` is true. Before that fact it maps to one material question. An external-evaluator failure always maps to `Settle` and ignores recovery availability. Provider/harness failures have explicit recovery dispositions when the supplied fact is true; only actual candidate defects authorize a fixer. Runtime and formal specification encode the same matrix, and the tests explicitly require it.\n- Consequence: this policy can end work for unresolved ambiguity after one question, or for a recoverable evaluator outage. It is a synthetic recovery policy rather than a clock deadline. This pure selector receives caller-supplied facts and does not itself persist a lifetime question counter or destroy a provider session; downstream use still needs inspection. The candidate-defect ownership distinction remains useful and should not be removed to permit recovery.\n- Repair direction: model unresolved clarification and unavailable evaluators as durable waiting/recovery states with explicit continuation. Permit further material clarification based on current uncertainty rather than a fixed question count, and preserve candidate quality across evaluator recovery. Coordinate formal matrix and tests. Tests read but not run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBZhv16+PMt8I31jX16nDcX3FEydL/thyddjjRy1yRW353OxvlKM9D2eAduvc9JngA/ohnLViFnnhhdfPMgedwY="}
