{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2801,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.283698777Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"985793ef-2dd3-53bb-a027-1a5a325bb084","title":"[L371] S2 qualification repeats full path and alternative scans without a resumable work boundary","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L371.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/orchestration/peritus-obligations/src/qualification/verdict.rs:203-232`, `src/evidence/binding.rs:205-243`, `src/qualification/evaluation/alternatives.rs:74-123`, `src/qualification/evaluation/alternatives.rs:147-233`, `src/qualification/evaluation/alternatives.rs:236-323`, `src/canonical/encode.rs:10-24`, `src/canonical/encode.rs:216-270`.\n- Behavior: each mandatory path calls a fresh linear search from the beginning of the observed path vector, even though both identity sets are canonical. A requirement with P mandatory/observed paths therefore has quadratic path-comparison work. Alternative group collection uses linear membership tests; each group traverses the complete ledger and each distinct evaluated branch traverses it again. Total group/branch identities are bounded by ledger entries, so these outer traversals can add quadratic ledger work, not an independently multiplied cubic bound. Complete ledger canonicalization allocates and copies all retained clause/schema/path bytes into one vector before hashing; the 1,024 vector capacity is an initial allocation, not a byte ceiling.\n- Consequence: synchronous qualification and canonicalization can do substantial work on large admissible inputs without yielding or retaining a progress frontier. Binary condition/evidence lookups and the linear schema subset matcher are real exceptions. This is a source-derived resource/progress risk, not a measured stall, a timer, or proof that the installed product uses alternative requirements. The earlier product caller creates Hard requirements and normally at most sixteen disjoint full clauses under its source cap.\n- Repair direction: merge canonical path sets with cursors, index group/branch membership once, and stream canonical hashing without a second full ledger allocation. Preserve exact qualification semantics and use resumable traversal where host responsiveness requires it. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPm64kCOAWf/BQGieWCrJtcvX2nLYlNFcsljdQoE44ikgvO6uskiuoxelByIV2MOOypvK/4UW74iTGHHONf48gE="}
