adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQISbBxZQQXR70PE4WAHe1WT4yYv2iLdtwfJJC+iS6Xj+h2OsgICW7atOF0zaStSV6eO6QFDBytF9Q9LvHxL7iQY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2803,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.288162185Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"4b1ac926-fcea-52c4-a727-0f2974444585","title":"[L372] S1 snapshot admission conflates stable section identity order with dependency order","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L372.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/orchestration/peritus-run-knowledge/src/snapshot.rs:138-190`, `src/snapshot/validation.rs:115-143`, `src/snapshot/validation.rs:146-224`, `src/identity.rs:11-75`, `tests/topology.rs:60-71`, `tests/topology.rs:97-113`, `src/model/topology.rs:109-139`.\n- Behavior: snapshot sections must be strictly increasing by their opaque sixteen-byte section IDs, and each dependency must occur before its consumer in that same vector. The IDs have no declared topological meaning. Thus a consumer with ID 4 depending on section ID 5 is rejected in ID order as a forward dependency; reversing those two sections is rejected as noncanonical order. The graph can be acyclic and still have no admissible representation with those stable IDs.\n- Consequence: callers must assign or replace identities to satisfy an incidental storage order, or lose a valid grounded knowledge graph. This is a structural admission blocker rather than a time limit or session deletion. The tests explicitly require forward-dependency and descending-ID rejection. The example is derived from complete source; those tests were read, not executed.\n- Repair direction: keep canonical identity order for storage and equality, compute dependency traversal separately, and reject actual missing dependencies/cycles. Coordinate runtime validation and its formal model; retain identity and lineage checks. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCDuj7CuleasIcSY9dAdLdpLbWcGNjPiKUAipWXhMgfTIwDH0NZiAMbKhd41mr1MknoOyLI8DsyGwZ5SXQgjzAY="}
