nd invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJHZ7EC2QK5xFqgkQOi9A+6IWSadismHeKGs37vsMyuL8Dd0OniU/gdOUq5PzISBBBGU0bKwVvUP5psKMMfpngw="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2805,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.292515888Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"f0ee41e6-e4d9-551f-9ea4-12f3594edec8","title":"[L373] S1 knowledge capacities are finite admission policies without an unlimited mode","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L373.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/orchestration/peritus-run-knowledge/src/limits.rs:29-64`, `src/source/validation.rs:20-26`, `src/section.rs:127-135`, `src/snapshot.rs:138-190`, `src/binding.rs:98-135`, `src/change.rs:29-68`.\n- Behavior: all four caller-selected limits must be positive finite `usize` values: snapshot sections, current catalog sources, sources per section, and dependencies per section. Constructors reject oversized vectors rather than paginate them. This crate imposes no default or compiled maximum: callers can construct a larger policy. A policy with fewer than three sections is accepted even though every snapshot requires the three mandatory inventory/map/requirement sections. Bindings and sections validate their own constructor policy and do not retain it; snapshot admission checks its global section count but does not recheck each section's source/dependency counts against the snapshot policy.\n- Consequence: a finite policy can reject otherwise valid knowledge growth. Independently selected policies also make the snapshot policy an incomplete statement of admitted per-section capacity. The admission test permits `usize::MAX`, and `tests/snapshot_admission.rs:152-166` explicitly expects nested policy differences to be accepted. These are immutable snapshots/catalogs that callers can replace, not proven lifetime quotas or mandatory expiry. Writer/Reviewer/Fixer role restrictions are an explicit role contract, not a clock or capacity rule.\n- Repair direction: distinguish finite caller resource policies from required structural invariants, support resumable catalog/section paging, validate policy consistency at snapshot admission, and offer an explicit unlimited policy where a host can support it. Preserve source identity/digest binding. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLTw4KolNDhg9v7v3W62RTMt2jwyFjHe7Y/W6LDmZUyYYFD139SfIdp26b51w09WIG3K6LdZQ98Q+POUk+TjkA0="}
