e all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDTxtq7sk9pvzv6xm57Vi/2gi6A7TGEVorKZrX9TGIXcOfYw+eIxplE4Mj4OheT08O9YjanIAkYm6zjmU2/RpQ8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2811,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.305511750Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"e8f9f353-9abd-543f-ae64-f30660cace08","title":"[L376] B1 mutation leases always have finite expiry and cannot renew after the boundary","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L376.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/state/peritus-leases/src/scope.rs:88-114`, `src/command.rs:57-91`, `src/claim.rs:15-22`, `src/transition/lifecycle.rs:79-110`, `src/transition/lifecycle.rs:171-215`, `src/transition/lifecycle/deadline.rs:28-43`, `src/transition/validation.rs:189-215`, `src/state/validity.rs:10-35`.\n- Behavior: acquisition and renewal require a strictly positive finite `u64` millisecond duration. There is no untimed duration/claim representation. The deadline is observation time plus duration with checked overflow. Renewal requires an exact current claim, an observation strictly before expiry, and a new deadline strictly later than the old one. Observation at the deadline rejects renewal as `ClaimExpired`; requesting a nonextending deadline yields `DeadlineNotExtended`. Renewing also changes claim version, invalidating outstanding old claims.\n- Consequence: a long pause or late renewal can leave a holder unable to resume through renewal, even if the holder/session still exists. This is an authority validity deadline, not an internal wall-clock timer or proof that a provider session is deleted. The README expressly requires fencing/reconciliation and says expiry cannot prove holder quiescence; that recovery is being audited separately. No caller-selected production duration is established by these files.\n- Repair direction: separate durable holder/session identity from optional timed authority validity. If untimed authority is appropriate for local daily driving, represent it explicitly and preserve generation fencing, quiescence, and authorization checks. Timed configurations need durable recovery/renewal orchestration that reports expiry without discarding run context. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKb6CEr5qhThUOKCkufr5nAyvaybk5FQlc/f5nMczMSWTLjW4z4q3415XIheAaONAakBlIuGQKtaDw345eUKdAY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2812,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.307657344Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"e8f9f353-9abd-543f-ae64-f30660cace08","comment_uuid":"31ce43f7-3f08-486a-97b8-627a237b91af","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L376: B1 mutation leases always have finite expiry and cannot renew after the boundary.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/state/peritus-leases/src/scope.rs:88-114; src/command.rs:57-91; src/claim.rs:15-22; src/transition/lifecycle.rs:79-110; src/transition/lifecycle.rs:171-215; src/transition/lifecycle/deadline.rs:28-43; src/transition/validation.rs:189-215; src/state/validity.rs:10-35. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nseparate durable holder/session identity from optional timed authority validity. If untimed authority is appropriate for local daily driving, represent it explicitly and preserve generation fencing, quiescence, and authorization checks. Timed configurations need durable recovery/renewal orchestration that reports expiry without discarding run context. No tests run.\n\nPreserve: explicit user authority, credential secrecy, exact target/resource binding, fencing, scope confinement, replay rejection for changed command content and fail-closed acceptance evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: renewal/adoption under the same authorized identity, revoked authority, stale epoch/revision, cross-scope requests, lost acknowledgements and restart, proving legitimate continuation without admitting unauthorized or duplicate effects. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIPQAU5353S4XuQ7RSL00Q93IZwCc+dfyGWRQe0kdOWy2Uq30N/lOHsMBe6mdTHdmboT4g8mVeO12QARYXHFjQ4="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2813,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.309692727Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"e2c48096-5cfd-5bd8-ab1b-ea9c07973882","title":"[L377] B1 a dirty or indeterminate lease inspection makes quarantine unrecoverable","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L377.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/state/peritus-leases/tests/phase_matrix.rs:40-66`, `tests/phase_matrix.rs:241-261`, `tests/transitions.rs:190-232`, `crates/state/peritus-leases/src/transition/reconciliation.rs:44-55`, `src/transition/reconciliation.rs:94-106`, `src/transition/lifecycle.rs:65-71`, `src/transition/fencing.rs:31-37`, `src/transition/fencing.rs:123-129`, `src/transition/fencing/release.rs:28-36`, `src/transition.rs:50-84`, `src/binding/command.rs:18-29`, `src/model.rs:54-119`, `src/model/concrete.rs:171-200`.\n- Behavior: reconciliation accepts only `Reconciling`. A correlated `Dirty` or `Indeterminate` inspection moves the aggregate to `Quarantined`. The abstract and concrete reachability models also have no outgoing Quarantined edge. The complete exported reducer families have no quarantine recovery transition: acquisition requires Available; renewal/use/release/expiry/holder-loss/discontinuity/revoke require Active; reconciliation itself rejects Quarantined. A later correlated `SafeToAcquire` observation therefore cannot resolve the same quarantined aggregate.\n- Consequence: a temporary inability to inspect safety becomes a permanent same-aggregate availability blocker. Quarantine is a valid protective state; the missing path to establish safety afterward is the blocker. Pure mint can create an unrelated new logical aggregate but does not replace a durable existing aggregate or preserve its generation automatically. Installed persistence/admin recovery remains a separate boundary.\n- Repair direction: make quarantine an inspectable recoverable state with explicit correlated reinspection/remediation commands and monotonic fencing. Keep acquisition blocked until current holder-quiescence and resource-safety evidence is validated. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCCsz5jEpHbVb/8txCWpKJwcSHVtNd38Qg8P/+IBsEB+s8Lw1HmB0aAJ9vs1aRRa5K1RAKCvdumUlMRrX54yFgg="}
