frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: renewal/adoption under the same authorized identity, revoked authority, stale epoch/revision, cross-scope requests, lost acknowledgements and restart, proving legitimate continuation without admitting unauthorized or duplicate effects. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFbVJNcA8Ur6T/CPlpsbyjr+JSRJCnn/y0WJGHTeX/HKconz4MIZbv/br167nciF1VE0eL0cp2CIvL2zvb++cwM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2815,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.313808414Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"66482955-018a-5a3c-b12e-f4d3f17b9772","title":"[L378] B1 authority-clock discontinuity recovery is unavailable in several nonactive phases","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L378.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/state/peritus-leases/src/transition/lifecycle.rs:65-78`, `src/transition/validation.rs:147-152`, `src/transition/fencing.rs:123-133`, `src/transition/reconciliation.rs:245-261`, `src/transition/fencing_apply.rs:135-168`.\n- Behavior: Available acquisition requires the stored authority epoch and monotonic tick floor. The explicit clock-discontinuity reducer requires Active, so it cannot rebind an Available aggregate after a changed epoch. A Reconciling aggregate can reset its epoch only when its original cause was ClockDiscontinuity; expiry, holder loss, release, and revocation reconciliation reject a later epoch change even with a safe correlated observation. Quarantined has no recovery command (L377).\n- Consequence: a durable lease with no active holder, or one already being reconciled, can lose all continuation paths after an authority-clock restart/change. This is a source-derived phase/clock contract gap; these files do not establish which installed host changes epochs on restart. Same-epoch regression may become usable if time catches up, whereas a different epoch cannot pass ordinary comparison.\n- Repair direction: represent clock rebinding as a durable command permitted in safe nonactive phases and during pending reconciliation, preserving generation/correlation rather than reminting identities or bypassing quiescence. Coordinate formal phase/clock invariants. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCHKiBvjlHDicmURaTaBvjI2v45Im++ddlOaf8D3jiv8jVWpDtjskARQbktFwnAcHZR6ppDOAbiMLUiOg22f2wQ="}
