n must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: renewal/adoption under the same authorized identity, revoked authority, stale epoch/revision, cross-scope requests, lost acknowledgements and restart, proving legitimate continuation without admitting unauthorized or duplicate effects. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQK4xloiQiZrq9i9h8PBI7Zvq9DTOR+E/oa3IECx2C17K5MhcHbr8fUfNkYHIYLMN5bW0lPkrL1TKcL4CcAno+g4="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2817,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.317841835Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"588f9d45-0f2f-5903-bb22-5580ec42f5ee","title":"[L379] B1 expired-claim recovery guidance does not name the required fencing transition","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L379.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/state/peritus-leases/tests/failure_contract.rs:40`, `crates/state/peritus-leases/src/failure.rs:166-191`, `src/transition/authority.rs:54-66`, `src/transition/lifecycle.rs:178-183`, `src/transition/fencing/expiry.rs:55-74`, `src/transition/authority.rs:78-81`.\n- Behavior: `ClaimExpired` is classified only as `Reauthorize`. Renew/use both reject the expired active lease before policy intersection; consuming a fresh policy capability cannot change that expired lease. Expiry requires an explicit fence followed by correlated reconciliation, or release with exact quiescence can make the next generation available. An accepted lease use is also limited by the earlier of lease expiry and policy validity, not lease duration alone.\n- Consequence: a generic recovery dispatcher following the advertised class can repeatedly reauthorize and hit the same lease expiry without advancing lease recovery. This is a misleading recovery contract, not proof that a particular installed dispatcher loops. Rejections preserve the unchanged aggregate and attempted use command, so the data needed for proper recovery is not discarded here.\n- Repair direction: return typed lease-recovery work that distinguishes policy refresh from expired-holder fencing/reconciliation, and retain the pending command/session context while resolving it. Removing a run deadline must not leave an unreported policy/lease expiry behind. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQG57v1oxOP7g85Br7bAy6RP71q7LjMTIyDQ1joLpqX7UzDDSsN9i6+feOm317Bmg5yHi/Si3Z/uAqkaP4hIFMwQ="}
