variants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: renewal/adoption under the same authorized identity, revoked authority, stale epoch/revision, cross-scope requests, lost acknowledgements and restart, proving legitimate continuation without admitting unauthorized or duplicate effects. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGtOEFM7rkkTNyj9zUVkS+DlRZCXrxTNIU7x/LCvnoEXr7jKLvN6bAS1tgpk66rXd9CwrPkWvuQSi9D0ITTxMQM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2819,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.322243618Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"f241a4b8-3b04-5d3b-860d-fbe9516c19e9","title":"[L380] B1 approval requests and credential snapshots have frozen collection and byte ceilings","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L380.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/state/peritus-approval/src/request.rs:16-27`, `src/request.rs:201-215`, `src/request/participant.rs:41-94`, `src/authentication/credential.rs:15-18`, `src/authentication/credential.rs:150-177`, `src/digest.rs:21-26`, `src/digest/canonical.rs:68-90`, `src/codec/decision.rs:20`, `src/codec/value.rs:263-354`.\n- Behavior: one approval request permits at most 256 exact permissions, 256 producing participants, 256 review participants, ten risk classes, four independence requirements, and a 65,536-byte complete semantic digest preimage. A credential snapshot permits 4,096 entries and a 4 MiB complete canonical preimage; a credential permits eleven nonempty canonical role labels. Decision preimages are 4,096 bytes, key-ID/signature-message preimages 256 bytes, and signed decision codec records 4,352 bytes. Constructors and codecs reject over-limit inputs without paging or caller-selected larger bounds.\n- Consequence: legitimate larger permission/provenance requests or retained credential sets cannot be represented through this authority path. Whole-record byte ceilings can reject below collection ceilings. Ten risks/four independence requirements/eleven roles currently equal the closed enum cardinalities, so those particular numbers are schema boundaries rather than independent retry or daily-use quotas. The snapshot cap includes Disabled credentials; these pure files do not prove the installed registry lacks retirement. Exact cryptographic lengths and duplicate/order checks are validation constraints, not artificial run deadlines.\n- Repair direction: version the bounded authority representation, separate per-message admission from durable provenance/credential retention, and support canonical paged references or explicitly configurable aggregate policy. Preserve complete digest binding and safe decoding; never silently omit participants or permissions. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQA2J3nrf4Cu2+S1DanKLot6DxGYbjqJCHStcIXv2Eez37DGhy3ocAYY3TYOqeY2Uf/WYZ7PgZMLajvl0Ku7cgQY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2820,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.324520287Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"f241a4b8-3b04-5d3b-860d-fbe9516c19e9","comment_uuid":"b89b0aad-3052-495b-be20-054d634d0d2b","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L380: B1 approval requests and credential snapshots have frozen collection and byte ceilings.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/state/peritus-approval/src/request.rs:16-27; src/request.rs:201-215; src/request/participant.rs:41-94; src/authentication/credential.rs:15-18; src/authentication/credential.rs:150-177; src/digest.rs:21-26; src/digest/canonical.rs:68-90; src/codec/decision.rs:20; src/codec/value.rs:263-354. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nversion the bounded authority representation, separate per-message admission from durable provenance/credential retention, and support canonical paged references or explicitly configurable aggregate policy. Preserve complete digest binding and safe decoding; never silently omit participants or permissions. No tests run.\n\nPreserve: explicit user authority, credential secrecy, exact target/resource binding, fencing, scope confinement, replay rejection for changed command content and fail-closed acceptance evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: renewal/adoption under the same authorized identity, revoked authority, stale epoch/revision, cross-scope requests, lost acknowledgements and restart, proving legitimate continuation without admitting unauthorized or duplicate effects. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKSQc8KmTQ+y9MVtpZSzhl9CrEymy/jcxGxpRV5i8/Evzxlf9T6qZk7IIXDqFszW9VNRdbnwLJzPqLWWKLUvzgM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2821,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.326554055Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"e3c8da38-73c1-58d4-9e79-369f57b8b7da","title":"[L381] B1 approval waiting and approved use are limited by the earliest of five validity deadlines","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L381.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/state/peritus-approval/src/request.rs:43-54`, `src/authentication.rs:151-161`, `src/authentication.rs:251-267`, `src/state/resolve_helpers.rs:30-50`, `src/state.rs:172-185`, `src/state/lifecycle.rs:8-48`, `src/state/lifecycle.rs:104-143`, `src/state/use_reducers.rs:111-125`, `src/state/use_reducers.rs:246-258`, `src/failure.rs:224-228`.\n- Behavior: requests, challenged policy scope, approval requirements, and credentials carry explicit validity windows; every signed decision also carries an exclusive expiry. Authentication requires all four windows and the decision expiry to contain the observation. Resolution stores their earliest expiry. Pending expiration uses the earliest of request/scope/requirement; resolved but unconsumed action/amendment approval also refuses use at the stored boundary. Expired is classified Terminal. Rejected resolution/use preserves the unchanged aggregate, so an Expired error can leave the phase Pending or ApprovedOnce until a separate expire command is applied.\n- Consequence: waiting for the user, delayed dispatch, or a pause can make an otherwise retained request/grant unusable. A fresh signature alone cannot extend the old request/scope/requirement. These are supplied authority deadlines, not internal sleep timers or evidence of provider-context deletion; actual production durations and replacement-request orchestration remain caller concerns. Scope use counts independently support Unlimited.\n- Repair direction: keep run/context lifetime separate from optional authority validity and provide a durable refresh/reapproval frontier retaining the exact pending intent. If local authority can be untimed, represent that policy explicitly. Timed expiry must trigger reviewable renewal/replacement rather than terminalizing the whole run. Preserve one-use and exact action/amendment binding. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFw3sAgR72/ZrixL7k0Gy6qo9SCi3Fb+qs+5qUrpOcnpX4E2xP/VK04Y9kDQfNjViyIiuGgDgeHcrz2vG0TlyQg="}
