{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2823,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.331103396Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"32f2cb3d-6452-54df-9203-ddd58c535062","title":"[L382] B1 exact approval replay still depends on current credential state before returning idempotence","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L382.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/state/peritus-approval/tests/lifecycle.rs:73-149`, `tests/approval_model_traces.rs:42-75`, `tests/approval_model_traces.rs:331-345`, `crates/state/peritus-approval/src/state.rs:109-169`, `src/state/validation.rs:176-237`, `src/state/validation.rs:251-273`, `src/authentication.rs:190-207`, `src/authentication.rs:251-267`, `src/state/types.rs:9-18`.\n- Behavior: a retained resolution first matches the decision digest, then revalidates the observation against the supplied registry, and only afterward returns an Idempotent transition. Registry revision must still equal the signed observation's revision; missing, disabled, reissued, or otherwise changed credentials can reject an exact previously accepted response. Fresh authentication of identical signed bytes additionally checks present time and rejects after any validity deadline. Reusing an already authenticated observation can avoid the fresh verifier time check, but cannot bypass reducer registry revalidation. The expiry-replay test preauthenticates both observations at the original time and retains the same registry; generated traces likewise preauthenticate against original time and keep the registry unchanged.\n- Consequence: reconnect/acknowledgment recovery cannot reliably recover a historical accepted response through this API after unrelated registry revision advancement, credential changes, or freshly checked expiry. The original resolution remains stored; the rejection grants no new authority and does not erase context. This is a replay/recovery availability issue, not a proposal to accept revoked credentials for new effects or proof of an installed reconnect loop.\n- Repair direction: resolve exact historical command/decision identity from a durable accepted-result record independently of present authorization, returning only unprivileged historical facts. Keep current credential/expiry checks for new approval or use authority and preserve consumed state. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGKT80w4e3/CxihiaUCnUn6AaKuIcw6MiLJx2YZazCFT57Zv/o1sLAxtdnXvcEyRfWQQMPP4dBhClnMSlkWFkQk="}
