{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2825,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.336390340Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"c328d556-8d6c-53d3-a22b-b2825b6f72f5","title":"[L383] B1 approval clock changes have no continuation path in the examined resolved reducers","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L383.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/state/peritus-approval/src/request.rs:151-168`, `src/authentication.rs:251-267`, `src/state/lifecycle.rs:120-133`, `src/state/use_reducers.rs:111-125`, `src/state/use_reducers.rs:246-258`, `src/state.rs:301-318`, `src/failure.rs:224-228`.\n- Behavior: ordinary authentication, consumption, and expiry require the original authority epoch and nonregressing floor. A changed epoch is Terminal. Cancel accepts only Pending; ApprovedOnce and AmendmentAuthorized cannot be cancelled through that reducer. The examined lifecycle/use reducers offer no clock rebind or approval refresh command.\n- Consequence: an accepted unconsumed approval can become unusable and also unable to expire/cancel normally after an authority-epoch change. New logical requests can be constructed, but replacing a durable existing request while retaining intent and audit identity requires an explicit integration path. Whether the installed host changes this epoch on restart is not established here.\n- Repair direction: model clock invalidation and durable approval replacement as explicit recoverable work, preserving the original decision and pending action. Require renewed authority where appropriate without dropping session context. All 66 approval crate files, including reducer/model source and tests, are now read. The closed model also has no clock-rebind or refresh edge. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQD0bGupomlhFLvSDC61agUg1EX+UyB5pD7AkVGDh2aOmfZuceXrf4WkD5pc1lleMWn0ejMTmLfTshJIu3UxaKQY="}
