rived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: renewal/adoption under the same authorized identity, revoked authority, stale epoch/revision, cross-scope requests, lost acknowledgements and restart, proving legitimate continuation without admitting unauthorized or duplicate effects. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKIWnV7jgiFj1ZnnwEmZq6wDShGXagNnAKPo75sg+6A/JUHYa5rrqtM+wMKqgYn5/uz7enaoJKl0gaURzpBwYA8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2827,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.341308073Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"aec31127-eb85-52cd-b5d5-98c04851cd0c","title":"[L384] B1 encoding a request after authority-time advancement disagrees with its semantic digest","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L384.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/state/peritus-approval/src/digest.rs:313-316`, `src/codec/request.rs:29-31`, `src/codec/request.rs:53-68`, `src/state/resolve_helpers.rs:66-104`, `src/state.rs:187-188`, `src/state/use_reducers.rs:129-130`, `src/state/lifecycle.rs:136-139`, `src/request.rs:295-299`, `tests/codec.rs:35-49`.\n- Behavior: the semantic request digest's field 18 uses immutable `challenge_epoch`/`challenge_tick_millis`. The canonical request encoder instead writes `request.authority_time()` into field 18, hashes the complete frame, and rejects when that hash differs from the stored semantic digest. Successful resolution, consumption, or expiration advances `authority_time` while explicitly preserving original challenge fields and digest. Once that floor differs from the challenge, encoding this otherwise valid request fails with RequestDigestMismatch. The decoder also reconstructs challenge and current floor from the same single field.\n- Consequence: this public codec cannot persist/round-trip ordinary advanced request state. A caller that serializes the successor request for checkpoint/reconnect can hit a persistence blocker after a valid transition. The source explains the failure without a byte/quota excess; merely raising limits would not repair it. Installed C0 may persist original request plus transition journal instead, so this finding does not claim every installed approval commit fails. The codec test read covers a newly created request only; no tests were executed.\n- Repair direction: define immutable signed challenge facts and mutable aggregate clock state as separate canonical fields/records, sharing the exact signed preimage encoder. Version decoding to preserve both and verify round trips after resolution, consumption, expiry, and replay without changing the original signed request digest.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJovDK+lo30l+M1p1W9lvvPjD3XfRPaDNctSKQWJhqiYlNxBCKOyWKmTLv7tvEcjMcc1JLkxMdIIvuW6eDtRWg8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2828,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.343618820Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"aec31127-eb85-52cd-b5d5-98c04851cd0c","comment_uuid":"1ca87038-534d-4809-be7c-e4f79fb1ff10","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L384: B1 encoding a request after authority-time advancement disagrees with its semantic digest.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/state/peritus-approval/src/digest.rs:313-316; src/codec/request.rs:29-31; src/codec/request.rs:53-68; src/state/resolve_helpers.rs:66-104; src/state.rs:187-188; src/state/use_reducers.rs:129-130; src/state/lifecycle.rs:136-139; src/request.rs:295-299; tests/codec.rs:35-49. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\ndefine immutable signed challenge facts and mutable aggregate clock state as separate canonical fields/records, sharing the exact signed preimage encoder. Version decoding to preserve both and verify round trips after resolution, consumption, expiry, and replay without changing the original signed request digest.\n\nPreserve: explicit user authority, credential secrecy, exact target/resource binding, fencing, scope confinement, replay rejection for changed command content and fail-closed acceptance evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: renewal/adoption under the same authorized identity, revoked authority, stale epoch/revision, cross-scope requests, lost acknowledgements and restart, proving legitimate continuation without admitting unauthorized or duplicate effects. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLzDXmKF2qjWlt+XQxNNk0XV5VpmVZ3GHkm3+25Ml82EsAD1BvjIvfVBbdSvp4mKVoUClA+8/T4yKibbUnZBLQA="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2829,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.345962709Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"9f37c457-4127-53e1-ae5b-7c5741f69067","title":"[L385] B1 approval rendering omits most maximum-size permission and provenance sets","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L385.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/state/peritus-approval/src/render.rs:14-23`, `src/render.rs:79-117`, `src/render/builder.rs:62-77`, `src/render/collections.rs:20-81`, `src/render/facts.rs:141-229`, `tests/rendering.rs:112-159`, `tests/rendering.rs:200-222`.\n- Behavior: the projection is frozen at 16,384 bytes including a 96-byte suffix reservation, with complete fields capped at 256 bytes. It considers only the first 64 permissions and first 64 actors from each provenance set, although each set can contain 256. Further capacity pressure omits whole optional fields. Rendering processes producing/review participants before permission summaries. Omission counts and truncated=true are retained; mandatory scalar digest/authority facts must fit or rendering fails. This API has no offset/page/full-detail parameter.\n- Consequence: a maximum accepted request can show only one quarter of each set through this projection. The tests explicitly require this truncation and exact omitted counts. That is a visibility/review completeness limiter rather than loss of the signed underlying data or a run timer. Integration may offer other full-detail views; those consumers remain to be traced. ASCII/control rejection is a separate deliberate safe-rendering rule. Subsequent complete primitive-type reads establish that CapabilityName is at most 128 ASCII bytes (L391); the renderer 256-byte field cap is not independently shown to reject an otherwise accepted capability name.\n- Repair direction: retain a small preview while supplying digest-bound navigable complete permission/provenance details before an informed approval. Keep omission disclosure and mandatory facts, and distinguish representation failures from terminal run failures. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMGpuSdWTtD1IuE7frp+CtyeSKhducUEvPWYC0jUrxjAU2R6rBkGDdeyxszqWSgcs59rQ/gSPxfhxTdDOwpzCQo="}
