{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2831,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.350786843Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"4520bc81-cac2-516c-82b2-177235ee2fa0","title":"[L386] Policy validity is obligatorily finite even when logical uses are unlimited","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L386.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/foundation/peritus-policy/src/validity.rs:86-149`, `src/validity.rs:168-191`, `src/capability_scope.rs:90-108`, `src/boundary.rs:43-53`, `src/ceiling.rs:15-20`, `src/use_limit.rs:32-48`, `src/capability.rs:87-126`, `src/capability.rs:233-320`, `src/amendment/preview.rs:162-197`, `src/ceiling.rs:118-129`, `src/boundary.rs:321-329`.\n- Behavior: every capability scope, parent authority boundary, and ceiling grant carries a same-epoch finite validity window, with an exclusive upper bound. There is no untimed validity variant. The separate use counter does support unlimited uses, but that does not remove time expiry. Successful use preserves the original window. The provided amendment operation replaces one restriction tier and copies the original ceiling, grant validity, and boundary validity unchanged; it cannot extend an expired parent ceiling.\n- Consequence: long-lived work needs an external path to obtain genuinely fresh time authority, rather than repeatedly using or amending the expired capability. No particular wall-clock duration, internal timer, session deletion, or installed expiry frequency is established by these pure policy types. The u64 tick ceiling and checked arithmetic are representation bounds; using its maximum value is still a finite window. Freshly constructing an entirely new authorized policy is distinct from the restricted amendment API.\n- Repair direction: make untimed authority an explicit supported state where appropriate; keep finite expiry when explicitly required by the authority issuer. Preserve session and pending action identity independently of authority lifetime, and provide an explicit durable renewal or successor-authority workflow instead of treating expiry as completion or context loss. No production changes or tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOp2z1/Noq4iWPSncUS2bKjFZoWV8/IvW/MRF9bOA0RLigf1U/WJwEajAGT87PLXOPrsl1UzUkASlmbR8V40PgQ="}
