tomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: renewal/adoption under the same authorized identity, revoked authority, stale epoch/revision, cross-scope requests, lost acknowledgements and restart, proving legitimate continuation without admitting unauthorized or duplicate effects. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDT4zEYtzPSFJbEcMH2w1DaGutkV0Z4c2x2V1ismXGfOgDjrjtUdPH2m3pSezujRSiKfpB1D1XLCT1RBhbeWtgM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2833,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.355139053Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"416eb039-1811-5b81-85e7-03d6cbccde9a","title":"[L387] Policy clock-epoch recovery guidance cannot repair the retained authority floor","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L387.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/foundation/peritus-policy/src/time.rs:52-137`, `src/capability_use_model.rs:63-95`, `src/capability_failure.rs:10-138`, `src/failure/metadata.rs:36-48`, `src/decision.rs:16-58`.\n- Behavior: a clock-epoch mismatch is classified as Reobserve. The authority state and capability preserve their original epoch on failure, and subsequent observations must still use that exact epoch. Reobserving a new epoch cannot advance or rebind either value. A same-epoch regression can recover by obtaining a tick at or beyond the retained floor, but changing epochs is a different operation. The failed capability-use result retains the unchanged capability and error, while the owned use request is not included in that result.\n- Consequence: a generic handler that follows Reobserve against a clock whose epoch has changed can repeat the identical rejection indefinitely. The pure crate has no internal retry loop or session teardown, and an actual installed clock change remains to be established. Callers must separately retain pending action intent and distinguish clock catch-up from obtaining fresh authority; otherwise recovery lacks the request that failed.\n- Repair direction: classify epoch change separately and route it to an explicit successor-authority transition with preserved pending action identity. Keep clock regression checks, avoid silently accepting a new epoch as existing authority, and return or durably retain the exact rejected request for recovery. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOlJkbJNW8wUGojjruelmm8JFs0NLqXmFSVFW/Fm+lvy1flvRmvBR2p0XYDU/dOo+wnObf2l/KqTqp4PNs7k3g8="}
