leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: renewal/adoption under the same authorized identity, revoked authority, stale epoch/revision, cross-scope requests, lost acknowledgements and restart, proving legitimate continuation without admitting unauthorized or duplicate effects. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBHigZnjypN0GqvVC6Ph9bAjpj5hJzgJIcRE9m1S+H2S05qjQHRSiAd41Ql/rHxC60XbT44sSar6yPVRu6Fw5wo="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2835,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.359600409Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"2d24e7f6-75ce-51c8-8d4a-cd4fb9b8fe8f","title":"[L388] Every overlapping ceiling grant constrains the entire request, including expired grants","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L388.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/foundation/peritus-policy/src/evaluation_predicates.rs:11-72`, `src/ceiling.rs:75-79`, `src/evaluation_constraints.rs:173-203`, `src/evaluation.rs:192-218`, `tests/cases/constraints_approval.rs:76-137`, `tests/cases/constraints_approval.rs:293-320`, `tests/cases/reference_model.rs:38-57`.\n- Behavior: coverage uses a union of grants, but effective validity and use limits intersect every grant whose identity and any requested permission match. Grant applicability has no observed-time condition. Already complete coverage does not stop additional grants from tightening the whole scope. One expired matching grant remains effective even if another grant supplies valid current coverage. Cross-epoch and disjoint-window grants are admitted as canonical inputs, then produce whole-request semantic denial during evaluation.\n- Consequence: retaining an old overlapping grant alongside its intended successor can make fresh authorization remain Expired or EmptyConstraintIntersection. Reauthorization against the same definition does not change that result, and restriction-only amendments preserve the ceiling as described in L386. Tests explicitly require all-applicable intersection, including contradictory epochs; this is current contract behavior, not a claim that the installed daemon has rotated grants this way or that the reducer itself loops.\n- Repair direction: distinguish explicit restrictive constraints from alternative or superseded grants in the authority model. Select or retire grants through a reviewed successor-authority transition, retain history as evidence, and report the exact blocking grant/window. Preserve deliberate security restrictions while making renewal possible without replacing a session. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCXp+xqEPP8QMzj24T/0TcxW3e9rLoeD9NyjGD+NYpfrii4i33b1RGZiXvrcgyzMNzMKh1UbW52m8mB7gX3ipgk="}
