ry root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: renewal/adoption under the same authorized identity, revoked authority, stale epoch/revision, cross-scope requests, lost acknowledgements and restart, proving legitimate continuation without admitting unauthorized or duplicate effects. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJi/Kv3rVOTDLwEMDOwrWElqeU7F3uHD/1cfTg+f8tU7GkYpvRzHUQGwK6l4ABX7DJUu9nPDENuzr/w3kVD5JQI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2837,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.364441359Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"35fefe1c-2525-54ea-a32f-7bab52b2b993","title":"[L389] Policy evaluation repeatedly scans canonical sets and recurses over unbounded input collections","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L389.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/foundation/peritus-policy/src/scope.rs:303-350`, `src/scope_selector.rs:120-140`, `src/scope_selector/containment.rs:100-250`, `src/evaluation_predicates.rs:11-95`, `src/operation.rs:208-288`, `src/operation_access.rs:28-75`, `src/operation_risks.rs:70-138`, `src/operation_risk_fold.rs:61-113`.\n- Behavior: canonical permission membership scans the whole vector without stopping when sorted order has passed the target; subset and selector checks repeat that lookup for each input value. Coverage scans grants separately for each requested permission. Operation validation performs a fresh recursive registry lookup per permission, and risk derivation repeats those searches for each of ten risk categories. Executable denial/coverage/operation helpers recurse with depth proportional to grant, rule, permission or descriptor counts. The pure constructors do not impose independent count caps on those collections.\n- Consequence: equally growing permission sets already give quadratic subset/matching work, and growing permission/registry inputs multiply lookup cost. Deep recursive helpers depend on the build's stack behavior rather than an iterative implementation. This is source-grounded workload and stack-growth potential; no benchmark, stack overflow, installed input scale or live lockup has been demonstrated. Mathematical spec functions and proof blocks are distinct from the executable helpers cited here; six policy tiers and ten risk variants are enum cardinalities, not daily quotas.\n- Repair direction: use merge walks, exact indexed or binary lookups, and iterative scans while retaining the verified ordering and exact-pair contracts. Avoid solving the scalability problem by adding a small lifetime quota or timer; isolate expensive evaluation from control responsiveness. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBkbUtaViKJWUMWvYEj0F7bqo4Qj1JzheW4rkkBEB/FBaC7WRYwpe3F9h9pKpGM1PgSXudT0Y7757yOocYqAywM="}
