{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2839,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.369055031Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"688649e8-eff9-5a52-a351-63e64a6ff036","title":"[L390] Policy can create an approval challenge whose approval window has already expired","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L390.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/foundation/peritus-policy/src/evaluation.rs:192-234`, `src/evaluation_approval_result.rs:54-76`, `src/rule.rs:237-297`, `tests/support/reference.rs:159-190`, `crates/state/peritus-approval/src/request.rs:187-236`, `crates/state/peritus-approval/src/request.rs:333-360`, `crates/state/peritus-approval/src/authentication.rs:151-161`, `crates/state/peritus-approval/src/authentication.rs:251-267`.\n- Behavior: evaluation checks the observed tick against the effective capability scope, then only checks that approval validity has a nonempty intersection with that scope. It does not check that the observed tick lies inside the resulting approval window before returning ApprovalRequired. The approval-request constructor checks collection bounds and computes its digest without rejecting a challenge whose requirement expired before evaluated_at. Authentication later requires the requirement window to contain its observation.\n- Consequence: for example, effective scope [5,90), approval requirement [0,20), and evaluation at tick 30 produce a challenge with approval window [5,20) and retained time floor 30. It can be packaged as a request, but no nonregressing same-epoch approval observation can satisfy it. Fresh user approval cannot repair this request. The independent scalar reference model repeats the missing temporal check, and the completely read policy test suite exercises empty intersections and scope expiry rather than this nonempty-but-already-expired challenge. This example is derived from the executable branches, not an executed reproduction or a claim about current prompt production.\n- Repair direction: validate approval eligibility at challenge construction, represent future validity as a resumable wait where applicable, and route expired requirements to an explicit refreshed-authority path that retains action/session identity. Do not present an impossible approval prompt or retry it unchanged. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIzZxUv5bqkFGQoLltcGquVT2OiaiV2stt//e2vXz5tX3xtYY5WYQBe9kvLOBQUTR+8yIvTNB30uWYBpi4/vmQ8="}
