nd keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJAkD+H9Xs+NTuy6zXBWwy06ShLj4g9ZDsCY4jcgccutqyx2E3a1mbQeBfnXonRxfopP4nsvyB+Jr/hFCksaGgY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2845,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.382617282Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"801f2975-5f4b-5b22-8719-fc0299fc38f1","title":"[L394] Acceptance graph construction and its executable certificate use cubic scans and input-sized recursion","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L394.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/foundation/peritus-spec/src/gate.rs:222-260`, `src/gate.rs:308-364`, `src/gate_model.rs:71-131`, `src/gate_model.rs:144-225`, `src/gate_model.rs:250-328`, `src/gate_model.rs:349-361`, `src/gate_model/canonical.rs:30-48`, `src/gate_model/canonical.rs:68-135`, `src/contract/validation.rs:12-49`, `src/contract/validation.rs:111-183`.\n- Behavior: GateGraph::new repeatedly scans canonical definitions from position zero for each selected gate; contains_gate scans the accumulated order. Even N independent gates in ascending order cause roughly the sum over i of the sum over j<=i of j comparisons, hence cubic growth. The constructor then runs a separate ordinary-Rust execution_order_is_valid certificate: uniqueness and declaration checks repeat linear searches, and canonical execution repeats first-eligible scans with full-order searches. These are executable fn bodies, distinct from erased spec/proof code. Search, uniqueness, dependency, definition-order, and canonical-order routines recurse to collection length, with no independent graph-size bound in the pure spec constructors. Cross-contract evidence validation also scans complete declarations once or twice for every gate-evidence edge, and scans gates/categories for evidence producers.\n- Consequence: large valid contracts can spend substantial synchronous CPU time constructing/rechecking an unchanged certificate, while stack usage can grow with graph/order/dependency size. That can resemble a stall despite the absence of a wall deadline. These are source-derived growth and stack risks, not measured performance, reproduced stack overflow, or proof of the installed lockup. Small three-node graph tests cover order/cycles, not large-input responsiveness.\n- Repair direction: construct indexed adjacency, indegrees, identity-to-position maps and a canonical eligible queue once; refine iterative executable checks against the same proof relation, without repeating full graph construction. Index cross-component evidence declarations and preserve immutable certificates. Do not solve responsiveness by adding a timeout or silently dropping gates. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFPk19cii1e4HLuuktoP9Op3wecbCiIsV6WR/NnowaSVGfsCKeGurM7xNR9S9axw3nLC44kFy3XqpqzGJL1ERAw="}
