{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2847,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.387433438Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"88547246-4934-5fa0-9026-6dd6c515276a","title":"[L395] B2 acceptance refuses successful observations beyond the finite completion counters","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L395.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/foundation/peritus-quality-policy/src/ordinal.rs:11-98`, `src/evaluator.rs:130-148`, `src/evaluator/gates.rs:173-189`, `src/evaluator/reviews.rs:192-205`, `src/decision.rs:90-122`, `tests/cases/completion_limits.rs:16-123`.\n- Behavior: one-based gate attempts and review-cycle ordinals are positive u16 values. The evaluator copies mandatory contract maxima (L393) into the decision, rejects any current passing gate with attempt>max_gate_attempts, and rejects any current review with cycle_ordinal>max_review_cycles. Equality at the configured ceiling is accepted. Tests explicitly require passing attempt 3/failed acceptance at 4, and acceptable cycle 4/failed acceptance at 5; u16::MAX is the greatest representable ordinal and is tested as valid at a matching maximum.\n- Consequence: work can execute and pass its actual success rule yet fail acceptance solely because a synthetic attempt/cycle counter is exceeded. Setting only wall timeout None does not change this result. This crate has no timer, persistence, lifecycle mutation, or context deletion; the pure failure can be reevaluated with another contract/evidence set. Existing orchestration consumers determine whether they convert it into an irreversible run state. Failed gate observations are already nonpassing independently of their ordinal; this additional limit check specifically rejects successful gate results.\n- Repair direction: make execution-count budgets optional explicit policy, use wide checked sequence identity independently of budget enforcement, and support budget adjustment while retaining durable run/context identity and exact successful evidence. Keep actual gate predicates, reviewer independence, and authority checks. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQK+3NdecYWnUhv3Fj8w9Sv6yy9rc9kMNVFfCjTQblbNkY4hhVyuY4biRjC7K61sWQ6FujdvXfxhcHz1HjIE2JA0="}
