vidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHOvG/3Tf0loBU+7NrMhBngEz4Z1S4NtCW6ZV9sPY7xADxZvTJZO7CevwpOZk/bwSaAU0wd3F7MTgBBRUvbJ3gQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2849,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.391899442Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"5e183789-bf37-5307-a842-6bc54c224a0b","title":"[L396] B2 canonical snapshots couple identity order to cycle order and disallow repeated finding/approval history","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L396.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/foundation/peritus-quality-policy/src/evidence/reviews.rs:49-103`, `src/evidence/ordering.rs:13-33`, `src/evidence/authority.rs:41-69`, `src/canonical/collections.rs:45-65`, `src/review.rs:122-132`, `tests/cases/construction.rs:29-82`, `tests/cases/canonicality.rs:166-214`, `crates/foundation/peritus-spec/src/contract/validation.rs:227-231`.\n- Behavior: reviews must simultaneously increase by every byte of ReviewCycleId and by positive u16 cycle ordinal. Two reviewer observations cannot share one ordinal, so this model consumes one cycle for each reviewer rather than representing several reviewers in one cycle. A legitimate chronological pair whose IDs sort in reverse cannot be made canonical merely by reordering it: one ordering fails the ID check and the other fails the ordinal check. All finding IDs must be globally unique across reviews, even if two independent reviewers report the same finding with identical disposition/digest. Gate IDs are unique across the entire gate snapshot, and semantic approval subjects are unique across the entire approval snapshot, without including revision in those identity keys. Tests explicitly enforce duplicate finding, duplicate ordinal, descending ordinal, and repeated approval-subject rejection.\n- Consequence: this is a current-snapshot representation, not an appendable multi-revision attempt/review/approval history. Feeding retained historical facts directly into it can reject them before acceptance is evaluated; honest corroboration of one stable finding also requires caller-side normalization or distinct finding identities. Simultaneous independence/quorum cannot be represented using a shared cycle ordinal, explaining the quorum<=cycle-limit coupling in L393. The installed ID generation and normalization paths remain to be traced; no live UUID-order failure is claimed.\n- Repair direction: keep stable identities separate from chronology, retain multi-observer finding provenance and disposition revisions explicitly, and derive a checked current acceptance projection from durable history. Preserve contradiction detection and independent-review counting; do not delete history or forge fresh identities solely to appease canonical order. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFdpYDNThYOJIrVBwm2WmXzsvKY4iDHQj5OAViPh9A4sCBzR3VUsQirD226BmbeXMGzM5J6xLZihZHxMoc2vqgc="}
