acement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: renewal/adoption under the same authorized identity, revoked authority, stale epoch/revision, cross-scope requests, lost acknowledgements and restart, proving legitimate continuation without admitting unauthorized or duplicate effects. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCaCKVM3FpsP8ZiNfTLqscVRb98QHWEzoyElz9EW5H9s3MVs716YhomnnV24MCrHeGnwpNV4hozEa3JLn483VAU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2851,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.396196689Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"74bb1a4e-6df6-5111-847c-04817deb99c7","title":"[L397] B2 rejects any stale observation and checks all current reviews beyond an already valid quorum","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L397.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/foundation/peritus-quality-policy/src/evidence.rs:105-122`, `src/evaluator/freshness.rs:137-211`, `src/evaluator/reviews.rs:179-313`, `src/evaluator.rs:23-49`, `tests/cases/freshness.rs:7-82`, `tests/cases/reviews.rs:281-309`.\n- Behavior: every supplied gate/review/artifact/approval/waiver must match the exact requested seven-component revision tuple. One stale observation makes the whole decision unacceptable rather than merely ceasing to contribute. Separately, all current reviews participate in category, cycle-budget and configured independence checks, including extra reviews beyond quorum and complete category coverage. The explicit test supplies a valid initial review plus additional reviews sharing a context; acceptance is rejected because all reviews participate. There is no accepted-subset/quorum-selection parameter.\n- Consequence: accumulation is not monotone: adding unused stale evidence or an extra current review can turn otherwise complete evidence into failed acceptance. Keeping audit history in this current aggregate therefore blocks ordinary iteration unless callers produce a separate normalized projection. Exact freshness of contributing evidence and reviewer independence are deliberate acceptance rules; wholesale rejection of unrelated retained observations is the integration-sensitive boundary. This crate preserves inputs and returns unmet conditions; it does not drop a session or create a fresh context. No current installed failure is established.\n- Repair direction: retain immutable historical evidence and select an explicit exact-revision acceptance set with full required coverage, valid independent quorum, and disclosed excluded/contradictory facts. Separate stale/noncontributing history from current authority and blockers. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQANtA9gyLKDE4xbT1DCdmRZCq+RRzsFp9YONciFgN1BOpn0mLrtoM0438gsdd00WT8VmWBMofty7ajSh5eoMTQw="}
