{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2853,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.400785496Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"1a10cab1-9c42-575e-9f05-25eb002aab26","title":"[L398] B2 treats superseded or unnecessary authority facts as current acceptance failures","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L398.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/foundation/peritus-quality-policy/src/evaluator/authority.rs:18-32`, `src/evaluator/authority.rs:173-304`, `src/evaluator/authority/supplied.rs:15-53`, `src/evaluator/authority/waiver.rs:17-67`, `src/evaluator/authority/waiver.rs:101-117`, `src/evaluator/authority/blockers.rs:31-96`, `tests/cases/authority.rs:192-228`, `tests/cases/authority.rs:322-396`, `tests/cases/waiver_semantics.rs:142-181`.\n- Behavior: every supplied current waiver is validated, including waivers for findings below the blocking threshold. A waiver retained after its finding becomes resolved is rejected as AlreadyResolved. Every current approval is also checked for an expected subject; an acceptance approval where approval is not required, or an approval for a waiver no longer valid for the current finding, becomes an UnexpectedApproval failure. The low-severity tests explicitly reject invalid waivers/approvals without an UnwaivedBlocker; resolved-finding rejection is covered among the waiver scenarios. There is no inactive/superseded authority-fact representation in this input aggregate.\n- Consequence: retaining previously relevant authority facts alongside current resolved findings can prevent acceptance even though that finding no longer needs a waiver. This is an integration-sensitive current-set boundary, not evidence that historical authorizations should silently override an active denial or forbidden waiver. The pure evaluator neither persists nor deletes sessions, sets timers, or proves the installed lockup's cause.\n- Repair direction: preserve the immutable authority history and derive an explicit current projection with supersession and finding-resolution semantics. Validate active decisions and disclose contradictory facts; distinguish historical approvals from approval requirements that must actually be satisfied. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIP/XHIth0ZX2K7BBChfnSZzHRKcvIpuPkq3ar+7vteafRpNZEn+PlLUuKf36w3byeNTR6QNPOz4GNPgWyW8mQQ="}
