{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2861,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.419425147Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"0a49584d-95cd-59a1-a5ef-caac8016a24f","title":"[L402] B0 pause loses the fixer phase and excludes pending/reviewing runs from session pause","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L402.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/foundation/peritus-kernel/src/reducer/run.rs:85-106`, `src/reducer/attempt.rs:97-120`, `src/reducer/attempt.rs:123-146`, `src/reducer/turn.rs:32-50`, `src/reducer/session.rs:18-30`, `src/reducer/session.rs:46-56`, `tests/transition_matrix.rs:95-113`, `tests/transition_matrix.rs:326-355`.\n- Behavior: PauseRun allows Running or Fixing but stores only Paused. ResumeRun always restores Running. A run/attempt pair in Fixing therefore becomes Running/Fixing after pause/resume; ResumeAttempt requires Fixing/Fixing, StartTurn requires an Active attempt, SubmitAttempt also requires Active, and StartAttempt rejects while the current attempt remains bound. FailAttempt can abandon the attempt and allow a new one, but normal resumption of the same fixer attempt is unavailable. The tests cover Running pause/resume and direct Fixing resume separately, not this composition. Pending and Reviewing runs cannot pause, and any unpaused live run prevents PauseSession.\n- Consequence: pausing ordinary fixer work can strand the current attempt behind mutually incompatible phase guards. Pausing review/pending work also fails at the control boundary. This is a source-derived reachable transition sequence, not an executed reproduction or a diagnosis of the installed UI lockup. The kernel has no process suspension or provider-session deletion.\n- Repair direction: preserve an explicit resume phase and checked parent/child continuation state, including pending and reviewing phases. Restore the exact legal workflow after resume; verify composed pause/resume paths across phases. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQI8DpHaQU3vJgnyRNynQ4RYrEB6hydrK/BFk/dOPBcxQmTZaK/Lp4aEma3krgMd4DY9rOuRsC/UqKhUwKFE6fwk="}
