{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2863,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.423997856Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"e290f18f-66d1-544e-b328-356b2b6fbb16","title":"[L403] B0 revalidates and clones the complete growing session history on every command","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L403.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/foundation/peritus-kernel/src/aggregate.rs:20-37`, `src/aggregate.rs:241-285`, `src/aggregate/lookup.rs:13-278`, `src/aggregate/validation.rs:18-46`, `src/aggregate/validation.rs:49-230`, `src/reducer.rs:120-131`, `src/reducer.rs:159-160`, `src/reducer.rs:175-201`, `src/reducer.rs:305-328`, `src/reducer/refinement.rs:154-211`, `src/reducer/run.rs:128-178`.\n- Behavior: command preflight validates the entire aggregate, including pairwise command/event/child uniqueness and repeated linear parent lookups. The reducer clones every accumulated identity and entity vector, appends identities, audits retained accepted runs, and validates the whole next aggregate again. Terminal entities and accepted command/event IDs remain in the vectors; there is no retirement command. Even a pause/cancel request traverses the complete history. Contract binding is checked again on every command; its separately audited graph validation can add further work (L394).\n- Consequence: command/event pairwise validation is quadratic in lifetime event count, producing potentially cubic cumulative validation work across a long session. Child cross-products and full retained-state copies add synchronous CPU/allocation work. No low fixed command-count quota is declared in this core; checked u64 event-sequence overflow is a representation boundary. No latency benchmark, memory exhaustion, or live incident was measured. Ghost proof models are not the executable cost.\n- Repair direction: preserve immutable history outside a compact live projection, maintain verified identity/parent indexes and incremental invariants, and assemble checked transitions without cloning and rechecking all prior work. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQL0oyYWV1g2MVejtCcTlLEJqeQ7fPBuX7jkKXKIL2bnab8XsHIXIxtCr5LajehYOSxYrGnYFnO/7f0RW/sI5WwQ="}
