{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2865,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.428464872Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"e0a57086-dee3-5a48-bfc3-e864ee2645a9","title":"[L404] B0 rejects exact command replay rather than returning a prior logical result","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L404.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/foundation/peritus-kernel/src/envelope.rs:8-27`, `src/reducer.rs:305-335`, `src/aggregate/lookup.rs:221-242`, `src/transition.rs:81-112`, `tests/adversarial.rs:225-259`.\n- Behavior: preflight checks current revision, predecessor and contract before command/event uniqueness. Repeating an originally accepted envelope after its head advances therefore fails CausalHeadMismatch; repeating an already accepted command ID at the current head fails DuplicateCommand. The aggregate retains accepted IDs but not a request-content/result lookup for exact replay. Tests deliberately require duplicate identities to reject, with unchanged aggregate returned to the caller.\n- Consequence: a caller that loses the result cannot recover it by simply retrying the reducer command; it must reconcile with durable event/receipt state elsewhere. This is a logical reducer contract, not proof that the installed commit layer lacks exact-retry receipts or quarantines such retries. The core preserves rejected state and does not drop a session.\n- Repair direction: distinguish exact already-committed requests from conflicting identity reuse at the durable boundary and return the matching receipt/projection without rerunning effects. Make required reconciliation explicit in callers. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"