{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2867,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.433371945Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"c2903ded-5bc2-5e4b-9d10-fc907d25bbed","title":"[L405] B0 permits only one waiver request per finding for the entire aggregate lifetime","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L405.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/foundation/peritus-kernel/src/reducer/waiver.rs:53-85`, `src/reducer/waiver.rs:108-119`, `src/reducer/waiver.rs:241-290`, `src/aggregate/lookup.rs:76-87`, `src/state/waiver.rs:8-26`, `tests/transition_matrix.rs:246-270`.\n- Behavior: RequestWaiver rejects if any stored waiver has that finding ID, regardless of phase, run or review cycle. Granted, denied and invalidated requests remain stored; invalidation has no reopening/successor edge, and GrantWaiver only accepts Requested. There is no separate waiver-request identity or revision-keyed successor in this projection.\n- Consequence: a denied or invalidated request prevents a later separately authorized waiver decision for the same finding in this aggregate. A later run/review with the same finding identity also collides. This is an authority-lifecycle restriction, not a reason to bypass an active denial or manufacture another finding ID; a genuinely superseding decision must retain provenance. No production caller behavior or live failure is established.\n- Repair direction: preserve immutable decisions and model explicit request identities, current finding/revision binding and checked supersession, with an authorized successor request that does not erase earlier denial/invalidation. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAA