e the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCJ0UBN/tdA8rwKKNeveT+fRATcwmFMLLtmqLC6rlQAqikm4GEh8//bOEZT7Hcz19wNZYvSYT5AATivj/7dSiwg="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2869,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.438342526Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"8d875ee7-3abd-50a9-b245-7cf4ad3a1c04","title":"[L406] B3 acceptance/amendment decode hard-codes production limits inside caller-selected codec limits","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L406.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/foundation/peritus-protocol/src/acceptance/contract.rs:117-140`, `src/acceptance/contract.rs:182-187`, `src/acceptance/contract.rs:229-250`, `src/policy/amendment.rs:61-76`, `src/policy/amendment.rs:104-109`, `src/policy/amendment.rs:145-159`, `crates/foundation/peritus-codec/src/limits.rs:20-49` (complete reread).\n- Behavior: callers can construct explicit CodecLimits with larger values. AcceptanceContractDto and PolicyAmendmentDto decode their content under the reader's limits, then clone and convert using CodecLimits::PRODUCTION instead of those reader limits. Digest verification reserializes the whole content using the production 16 MiB frame / 65,535 item / 1 MiB string / 64 nesting ceilings. Any inner codec or domain failure is collapsed to InvalidDomainValue. Constructors, explicit try_into_domain and encode paths can use the caller-supplied larger limits.\n- Consequence: selecting larger outer limits cannot extend these two decode families past the inner production ceilings; a collection accepted by the outer reader can fail reserialization under 65,535. Raising configured limits alone can therefore leave recovery/round-trip failure, with its limit-specific cause hidden. This is a source-derived inconsistency; no large-message reproduction, installed incident, or automatic session deletion was observed.\n- Repair direction: propagate one consistent limits/representation policy through digest and checked conversion, preserve the actual limit error, and support versioned chunked/content-addressed representations where a whole aggregate would exceed message capacity. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNKRpUCSdrGM0WpIAQXx2ZDBuygdbtJqAJptchch9PQBeLmCaJRqyphlxCc7zzB24CLUVCfGx5KWGTvz9vBh0A8="}
