ns from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPVNVHlk08othuL5iCPhdEeppza1M+F3CA6++AAA/a4pWndAHilpHJHQLVGgkKo6hAOwM3nXHZBQt+5ezWBLGw4="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2871,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.443268933Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"3f0289b4-e455-58a4-89bd-c714cc13e70b","title":"[L407] B3 agent DTO constructors check only opaque payload capacity before admitting complete records","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L407.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/foundation/peritus-protocol/src/agent/wire.rs:12-25`, `src/agent/command.rs:113-144`, `src/agent/command.rs:209-225`, `src/agent/event.rs:115-146`, `src/agent/event.rs:211-227`, `src/agent/state.rs:149-187`, `src/agent/state.rs:277-298`, `tests/agent.rs:148-165`, `tests/fixtures/v1/agent-command.bin` (complete 315-byte inspection).\n- Behavior: new() validates the opaque bytes using a temporary writer containing only that length-prefixed field, then retains metadata and the payload. Full command/event/state encoding adds identities, revision, phases, counters, digest claims and frame overhead later. For example, a source-derived command with the golden fixture's field shapes and a 900-byte payload can pass the isolated check under frame 1,024 / payload 1,008 / opaque 1,000 limits, while its complete frame is 1,199 bytes and cannot encode under the same limits. The existing constructor test covers opaque excess, not metadata overhead. Hashing separately allocates a domain-prefixed copy of the payload; constructor validation also creates a serialized copy.\n- Consequence: successful construction does not establish complete-frame representability, even when callers use the same explicit limits afterward. A caller that treats new() as pre-admission wire validation can encounter a later capacity failure. No effect dispatch/commit ordering or installed failure is established solely by these inert DTO files. The production opaque and frame bounds themselves were already recorded in L009.\n- Repair direction: validate complete canonical records before durable/effect admission, with one shared size calculation or checked full encoding and structured capacity errors. Avoid redundant complete payload copies where streaming hashing/encoding can preserve exact semantics. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFk+aIDqtWPL7I0+UiOlrHY8CUUgSfk2yzwrrXKtjPcxSBVrCnXjL5u69uiSliqQWdWk3sHrm22wEYDnIexfdgE="}
