{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2873,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.447699627Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"79a8dc80-db73-536f-91a2-35dd4ec5a2cb","title":"[L415] E2 debugger jobs freeze 24 compiled ceilings that callers can only reduce","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L415.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/analysis/peritus-debugger/src/limits.rs:5-86`, `src/limits.rs:95-165`, `src/limits.rs:203-235`.\n- Behavior: production defaults and maximum representable policies are subjects 256; traces 4,096; events 131,072; causal edges 524,288; artifact citations 32,768; artifact bytes 256 MiB; timeline entries 131,072; claims 16,384; causes per claim 64; contrary citations 256; patterns 8,192; members per pattern 4,096; component links 32,768; report bytes 64 MiB; model input 32 MiB; model output 16 MiB; model events 262,144; model tokens 4,000,000; model attempts eight; retries seven; accounted wall time 86,400,000 ms (24 hours); diagnostics 131,072; complete state 16 MiB; event payload 16 MiB minus its 16-byte frame header. The values array is private. `tightened` starts from compiled defaults, requires positive ascending unique overrides, and rejects any larger value. No unlimited mode exists. `check` rejects excess rather than truncating, and reports CorrectInput even when the ceiling cannot be raised.\n- Consequence: callers cannot provision a larger debugger job through the public policy API; diagnosis of a large or long-lived run may fail on these compiled ceilings. Wall-time policy presence is confirmed, but measurement/enforcement and retry recovery are being traced in the owning paths before claiming an actual debugger timer. These are debugger limits, not evidence of the installed agent's live timeout.\n- Repair direction: distinguish configurable resource admission from synthetic lifetime limits, support large evidence through current projections/paging or incremental analysis, and preserve durable diagnosis identity across resource-policy changes. Remove mandatory elapsed-time and attempt ceilings where progress and explicit cancellation should control lifetime. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFO3l4tcsgqOS4933j0ioHs9+xGe1KXj5kGL1fpQ7sQ9b6fTm32dlLivZE55sY0+yP/ldvX9Uved/DjjtpoqXAc="}
