{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2875,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.452370995Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"12a0bbbc-4f01-5431-907c-117cf2f68eb5","title":"[L416] E2 narrow evidence queries still index all C0 records and validate/clone all same-subject observations first","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L416.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/analysis/peritus-debugger/src/selection/engine.rs:27-99`, `src/selection/engine.rs:129-186`, `src/selection/provenance.rs:12-54`, `src/selection/provenance.rs:57-70`, `src/query.rs:227-240`, `src/selection/manifest.rs:275-295`.\n- Behavior: selection first builds an event index for every record in the complete integrity export. It traverses every trace and observation, linearly finds a matching subject, validates exact C0 frame/projection provenance, and clones each matching subject into a candidates map before applying trace/time/kind/outcome filters. An incomplete run/attempt binding in any observation sharing a queried session rejects selection even when that observation would not match the later filters. Selected entries are fully copied and sorted before most event/trace/edge ceilings are checked. Ancestor expansion checks event capacity while expanding, but starts from the complete direct-match set. Ordinary artifact provenance scans the export's reference list for each artifact. Complete canonical manifest bytes are allocated and hashed after selection.\n- Consequence: shrinking a query or tightening its selected-event ceiling does not bound upstream indexing, frame checks or candidate allocations. A single malformed same-session observation outside the requested filters can block otherwise valid diagnosis. Potential costs scale with total journal/trace history, subject count and artifact references; no benchmark, installed lockup or corrupted production trace is claimed. Exact provenance checks are necessary, but their scheduling and scope remain significant for daily diagnosis.\n- Repair direction: use verified indexed/ranged upstream selection with bounded incremental work, validate required provenance as evidence is admitted, and distinguish a source-integrity fault from an unrelated incomplete trace outside the query. Expose cancellation/progress and capacity before full materialization while preserving complete requested evidence. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOpBysKPTgyMuAQUsIe70KI4d27w7gXGec5r1vvkjJhIZrWMFbQTy8nVNMwNTFquJqjG1UpMgSYozgHf7fTooQo="}
