{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2877,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.457151139Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"11e1e2ee-6d03-5c25-ac91-f825fe44073f","title":"[L417] E2 model plans forbid provider context continuation even with storage opt-in","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L417.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/analysis/peritus-debugger/src/model/plan.rs:99-168`, `src/aggregate/reducer/apply/model.rs:17-45`, `src/aggregate/command.rs:20-123` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: A debugger model request must have no continuation, disabled reasoning, exactly the C6-derived messages, no tools, and the exact strict proposal schema. The storage opt-in can permit provider storage/background/cache settings but does not relax the continuation prohibition. One job has one frozen model plan and no amendment/rebind command.\n- Consequence: A caller cannot submit a provider continuation handle to reconnect this optional debugger analysis to an existing model context. Retrying this plan resubmits its fixed request. The inert schema/tools restrictions protect evidence and authority boundaries; they do not require discarding a model context. This is debugger-specific source behavior, not proof that the installed writer uses this path or lost its context here.\n- Repair direction: Represent persistent model conversation ownership and an exact durable continuation separately from mutation authority and structured proposal validation. Preserve the inert output contract while allowing a verified same-context continuation. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLFqgIg6xPBwrWWYtVeG3hqt+nvJ0ZRhMcRWsM5jsWQUC+oeZd1a8t+332nm2T/DdLF+6Oxkbn5XlqZU/Q9gDQ0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2878,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.459525331Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"11e1e2ee-6d03-5c25-ac91-f825fe44073f","comment_uuid":"f0d8d183-03b5-44f3-ab1c-000b82428d27","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L417: E2 model plans forbid provider context continuation even with storage opt-in.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/analysis/peritus-debugger/src/model/plan.rs:99-168; src/aggregate/reducer/apply/model.rs:17-45; src/aggregate/command.rs:20-123. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nRepresent persistent model conversation ownership and an exact durable continuation separately from mutation authority and structured proposal validation. Preserve the inert output contract while allowing a verified same-context continuation. No tests run.\n\nPreserve: definitely-unaccepted versus ambiguously-accepted request state, exact native thread/profile identity, ordered provider observations, tool-result protocol, explicit cancellation and real provider/model capabilities. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIxjHkhlJOdCGHhTQ93VRu2srMxqRUokpRlV7qr1o/c6VGkTci+8IVVpnhWYSx/9sUSfhUrCClEIeS+nwHFv9QY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2879,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.461867708Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"164d4db4-800f-5867-9ebb-28f4250bab5e","title":"[L418] E2 restart advertises an already-started attempt resume that its executor cannot perform","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L418.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/analysis/peritus-debugger/src/runtime/recovery.rs:43-69`, `src/runtime/model.rs:75-117`, `src/runtime/mod.rs:11-20`, `src/model/mod.rs:1-11`, `src/aggregate/reducer/apply/model.rs:48-68`, `src/aggregate/reducer/apply.rs:69-132`, `src/aggregate/command.rs:20-123` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Recovery selects `ResumeModelAttempt` for a durable ModelRunning job with an available directive. The exported executor requires ModelPending, then unconditionally commits MarkModelAttemptStarted; the reducer also only accepts that start in ModelPending. No separate resume executor or lifecycle command is exported in the read modules.\n- Consequence: Feeding the recommended recovery action back into the ordinary executor fails binding before provider I/O. Calling the lower-level runner alone does not supply the missing durable claim/start/settlement orchestration. This is a source-derived interrupted-attempt recovery gap, not an executed crash reproduction or established cause of the user's current session. The selector also treats an unavailable pending/running directive as quarantine; temporary ownership contention cannot be distinguished from missing/corrupt owner state by its boolean input.\n- Repair direction: Provide one attempt execution path that explicitly distinguishes first start from verified same-attempt recovery, retains the durable identity and provider continuation, and settles the reclaimed claim. Model claim contention as wait/reobserve rather than corrupt-state quarantine. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGr2FPAuGecsgvM5wBaEN37byvLnL1f2oIbySNV8vrWvW1Yk1YUDu6SyGFZXNheFFRPBdUpja8uhqoF0uzcwwQo="}
