om authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDPqjAC55ALr0sWWTTL4Yv+US5hYH309gm8jR6RZqHUq1yR+iR8XDnVzK9vbGZjuqjQ+xHMGpN4Pj9Mu3OW82gU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2881,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.466830110Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"1fda0f55-5264-5fe3-bfa1-7e6665e41cab","title":"[L419] E2 collapses permanent provider failures into retries and records zero failed-attempt usage","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L419.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/analysis/peritus-debugger/src/model/runner.rs:73-197`, `src/runtime/model.rs:211-231`, `src/aggregate/reducer/apply/model.rs:131-161`, `src/aggregate/types/model.rs:20-102` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Profile validation, provider start, and provider pull failures are normalized to ModelProtocol with Retry using their display text. Durable normalization then calls all such failures MalformedStream and records event_count and total_tokens as zero, even if a stream already emitted events/usage. Retry policy requires finite positive attempts (type ceiling 32, plan admission additionally constrained by L415's default 8); exhaustion returns the job to deterministic report preparation. Frozen model ceilings are checked separately for each result/failure, without cumulative failed-attempt usage.\n- Consequence: Unsupported configuration or other permanent provider failures can repeatedly submit the same request until the synthetic attempt ceiling instead of explaining the correction required. Distinct transport/profile failures and consumed failed-attempt usage disappear from the durable record; quota decisions and diagnosis cannot use accurate aggregate consumption. Model-budget/invalid-proposal failures are intentionally nonretryable, and exhausting optional model work does not itself delete the run context or forbid deterministic reporting.\n- Repair direction: Preserve typed provider failure, recovery certainty, continuation, and observed usage through failure settlement. Retry only failures whose recovery can change the outcome, with an explicit user policy for stopping, and account consumption across attempts without conflating protection with task termination. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKAiF1iGvI35mD5evpjZ42z7H/k5WKrhndlo2qXm6jNqxG3rpGXIUfxvd6W8fu0fPkhDBHCuSeiDnf2vpKvLnwE="}
