{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2885,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.475851697Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"2e03e91a-4f24-5e83-8c50-d5e58226aca0","title":"[L421] E2 model and report directives have a separate compiled sixteen-delivery ceiling","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L421.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/analysis/peritus-debugger/src/durability/commit/outbox.rs:14-86`, `src/durability/directive.rs:169-241,279-283` in the same crate; C0 exhaustion behavior is covered by L251 and L265.\n- Behavior: Every model-attempt directive and every report-publication directive is created with max delivery attempts = 16. This is independent of the frozen model attempt/retry policy. The typed claim only accepts a Claimed C0 message; there is no debugger command for replenishing an exhausted directive.\n- Consequence: Repeated claim loss, transport/process interruption, or failed settlement can exhaust delivery while durable work is still pending/running or a report remains unpublished. Removing a model retry ceiling alone would leave this hidden delivery ceiling. Existing owner-level administrative recovery, if any, is not established by these modules; source inspection is not an executed exhaustion reproduction.\n- Repair direction: Separate durable delivery/reconciliation from an optional user-defined semantic attempt budget. Keep the same directive and job identities recoverable after interruption, with an explicit delivery state that can wait/reclaim rather than permanently exhaust. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZh