ncilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQE0I6CaIdQkb2NiBrGTs6P7YPqenDWu061hHHLpLn+SHVTVCO7rn0ZbpG16a/6DgTZ1kT73st/WEK7wpqc3k2AI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2887,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.480484232Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"04060ce4-3887-5fa0-a41f-2aeefeedbd2e","title":"[L422] E2 exact durable retry depends on the current checkpoint and the original claim fence","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L422.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/analysis/peritus-debugger/src/aggregate/reducer.rs:99-137`, `src/durability/commit.rs:81-120,196-244`, `src/durability/commit/claim.rs:65-77,126-139` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Pure reduction checks the latest state fence and terminal status before doing work. The commit layer correctly resolves an existing exact request before current-head checks, but only returns its batch when the current checkpoint is the exact successor; an advanced checkpoint returns ReplayAggregate. Claimed-start and settlement request digests include the C0 claim fence, so a newly reclaimed fence is a different exact request even with the original transition identities.\n- Consequence: A generic retry that simply reconstructs the original transition from current state, or repeats it under a replacement claim, cannot transparently recover the original result. Recovery must first resolve the original operation and distinguish durable completion from still-owned work. This is a required recovery contract, not evidence that replay errors delete context; returning replay for an advanced checkpoint is explicit and preferable to falsely returning the older state.\n- Repair direction: Retain the original request/claim receipt and authoritative outcome separately from current state. Resume from the latest reconstructed state while preserving historical completed-operation recognition across claim replacement. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQG4+9AYBwvzk/esip2x6eqj+EpIIFFe2AaMljireADcbg3wFEYlnZTwo/i5jqGdvtfTKHm51AqXZYKvEqSMmtgk="}
