ffects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIfq1IFTPsCdMz37GNDN3mDNwNV6b4zSzfIQfv6ZUKSczGG23cgUuhscWoeiXnYHXPVUznKFiJqOo/08gEvORAE="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2889,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.485485449Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"4f64e007-9311-5914-9f46-3e74fbcbd53c","title":"[L423] E2 published-report reconciliation has no matching publication execution branch","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L423.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/analysis/peritus-debugger/src/runtime/recovery.rs:71-89`, `src/runtime/publication.rs:56-118`, `src/aggregate/reducer.rs:99-128`, `src/aggregate/reducer/apply.rs:153-174`, `src/runtime/mod.rs:19-20` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: A Published job with missing/unverified staged artifact or missing admitted evidence selects ReconcilePublication. The exported publication executor requires ReportReady and a claimed directive, while Published is terminal and cannot accept another transition. Normal publication admits evidence before atomic settlement; interrupted admission before settlement is therefore recoverable while still ReportReady.\n- Consequence: The Published missing-owner branch cannot be handled by replaying ordinary publication against the current state. It needs a separate owner repair/reverification path or a clear unrecoverable integrity outcome. A missing boolean observation may also mean transient lookup failure rather than actual loss; the selector cannot distinguish those conditions. No claim is made that already-admitted evidence or artifacts can never be restored through other owner APIs.\n- Repair direction: Distinguish interrupted pre-settlement publication, temporary owner observation failure, and repair of a completed publication's dependencies. Implement recovery actions with matching execution APIs and preserve the existing report/job identity. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-