{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2893,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.495344939Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"c5c3ab46-97f1-52ef-a346-c27c6eaf1436","title":"[L425] E2 analysis and validation repeatedly scan complete evidence before checking most output caps","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L425.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/analysis/peritus-debugger/src/timeline/builder.rs:172-270`, `src/causal/analyzer.rs:112-138,223-345`, `src/causal/candidate.rs:116-164,255-311`, `src/clustering/fingerprint.rs:12-43,65-87`, `src/clustering/engine.rs:146-242`, `src/component/mapping.rs:120-228`, `src/report/validation.rs:159-325`, `src/report/canonical.rs:7-35`, `src/durability/replay.rs:73-126`, `src/wire/event.rs:55-71` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Timeline construction scans the full manifest for each subject and validates each citation through the manifest lookup. Analyzers construct/copy/validate every cause before final dedup/count checks; each diagnostic group copies all successful citations for that subject. Fingerprinting repeatedly looks up cited events and their causal predecessors. Agglomeration uses pairwise group comparison/removal. Component mapping repeats revision/declaration and successful-subject scans. Report validation revalidates the citations again and linearly finds each recommendation parent, then allocates the whole canonical report before the byte cap. Durable loading reduces each event in frame checking and again in loading; rebuild replays the prefix again.\n- Consequence: The read functions have input-sized nested scans, repeated byte/citation copies, and late rejection despite positive compiled limits. With linear manifest lookup, a complete timeline alone can require quadratic lookup work in event count; recommendations can require quadratic claim comparisons. These synchronous APIs expose no cancellation/progress parameter. This is a performance/blocking risk inferred from source, not a benchmark or attribution of a live hang; model history/replay in this aggregate is separately limited to 32 attempts and does not have an unbounded attempt-history growth claim.\n- Repair direction: Use verified indexes and incremental validation/canonical hashing, admit output capacity before allocation, and expose resumable work/progress/cancellation without discarding the analysis or model context. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKTxwhrdknhjY9zX248qsVoYCIXbt/W8bbp/pFYGrg8NQC/wztH93Med24ZmkrcqhwJTnHuxYMVu/24tZIGVSw8="}
