adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNcq8bwhwvNygXnfuew50QLzWKSp3EmOe3niyxsGOPygxnCIsghNiFenuut3RVbm4lVfCIvyZfn9+4XhhP3kww0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2895,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.500049823Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"5ad8e00c-fcf6-5f42-9f3e-c51c47d95dae","title":"[L426] E2 supported observations are rejected by five English substring heuristics","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L426.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/analysis/peritus-debugger/src/report/claim.rs:56-79`, `src/causal/candidate.rs:17-37` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Observation construction lowercases text and rejects it if it contains ` might `, ` likely `, ` probably `, ` recommend`, or ` should ` anywhere. It does not inspect quoted source text or the actual proposition. Statements also have a hard 4,096 UTF-8-byte ceiling, nonempty requirement, and control-character restrictions.\n- Consequence: An exact supported observation quoting a source such as a message containing “should” can be refused as supposedly inferential despite its citation. Conversely, a wording without those five substrings can pass regardless of its semantics. The byte/control bounds are serialization/display constraints; the substring rule is an additional synthetic admission blocker for diagnostic prose, not an execution timeout.\n- Repair direction: Encode the observation/inference distinction through typed evidence obligations and provenance rather than English word matching. Store complete supported statements with bounded display pages. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBXRnyLhpDj9PR34qIVBCNLI0FMXV0MT41kHVUH/cXfOic9KQ7CPltr4pzZd+7FL389DcGPco7+Aw1tvZHDWUw8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2896,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.502511275Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"5ad8e00c-fcf6-5f42-9f3e-c51c47d95dae","comment_uuid":"099bc749-8bc2-4b24-ae6d-72869eb49835","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L426: E2 supported observations are rejected by five English substring heuristics.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/analysis/peritus-debugger/src/report/claim.rs:56-79; src/causal/candidate.rs:17-37. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nEncode the observation/inference distinction through typed evidence obligations and provenance rather than English word matching. Store complete supported statements with bounded display pages. No tests run.\n\nPreserve: exact candidate revision and artifact binding, complete finding/provenance conservation, independent reviewer evidence, truthful gate outcomes, protected user constraints and acceptance fail-closed on invalid evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDVjUB6whi8uIxZYLhVPWd+JmF8q71kAFZZzMjb3CY1HuaQ2BngxiyBj0oDC5wNB/1V1fam4VNNSPLoMCEBdGAk="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2897,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.504838958Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"b3280a4d-2b76-5b7f-a545-04bfa03083d7","title":"[L427] E2 model schema and semantic statement limits measure different units","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L427.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/analysis/peritus-debugger/src/model/plan.rs:21-43`, `src/model/proposal.rs:78-149`, `src/causal/candidate.rs:17-37`, `src/model/runner.rs:109-167` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: The advertised JSON schema permits statement maxLength 4,096, while DiagnosticText enforces at most 4,096 UTF-8 bytes. JSON Schema string length counts Unicode characters rather than UTF-8 bytes. Proposal validation first deserializes the complete typed JSON before checking its output-byte bound; findings/recommendations/citations then have whole-proposal canonical ordering and provenance requirements. The runner only accepts one completed structured item and a successful Stop terminal.\n- Consequence: Schema-valid non-ASCII statements can be rejected by semantic validation; for example, 2,000 ordinary three-byte characters fit the schema length but exceed DiagnosticText's byte ceiling. This is a source-derived example, not an executed provider response. Provenance, strict output shape, and authority separation are deliberate integrity controls; their whole-proposal failure behavior should not be misreported as arbitrary run/session expiration.\n- Repair direction: Advertise and validate the same explicit text-length contract, normalize canonical order where safe, retain typed rejection causes, and perform byte admission before full allocation. Keep provenance and inert output requirements. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQL4WzHgUBuuVyX32egX/rG0OGyoOphriP12py7zmxtnCX7apgNdSsVhYB3I/0Dffv7St4nJuNPXfEfQB/UvNlA8="}
