{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2899,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.509461590Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"4ee506f0-c9bc-5cb8-b924-e023690b0ef4","title":"[L429] E3 campaigns require six positive finite resource ceilings and a finite retry policy","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L429.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/analysis/peritus-eval/src/limits.rs:5-81`, `src/profile/policy.rs:23-69,127-171`, `src/profile/binding.rs:250-330`, `src/dataset/manifest.rs:30-65`, `src/accounting/ledger.rs:60-100` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: EvaluationLimits requires positive values no higher than compiled tasks 2,048, rollouts 16,384, attempts per rollout 16, bootstrap replicates 100,000, pass@k values 32, and complete state bytes 16 MiB. Production defaults reduce attempts to 8, bootstrap to 10,000, and pass@k count to 16. Retry policy requires a positive finite attempt maximum within the limit; ledger overage reports Terminal. A profile's selected tasks × two arms × rollouts per task must fit its frozen rollout ceiling. Dataset tasks must fit their construction limit. Metric policy requires at least one positive canonical k and bootstrap replicate, and only confidence 950,000 millionths is supported.\n- Consequence: Callers cannot request an unlimited campaign/retry history or larger workload through these APIs, and receive ReduceScope or terminal accounting errors instead of lossless batching. The confidence constant is a supported statistical-method contract, not a running deadline. These are evaluation-specific source limits; ordinary installed agent runs are not shown to execute through E3 by this inspection.\n- Repair direction: Make workload/retry stopping explicit user policy and page durable task/rollout/attempt storage. Keep statistical methods versioned and their supported confidence parameters explicit rather than confusing them with task longevity. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLvGwYI417VsUpA1QKF1JlUG5Rsqs3GlgBke1S48GZQdH5i4XE3QPoTvrB4ycLkM9UaivqnrGekp9KCQw0HDaAk="}
