ssor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBs3pwubopGdam6mr8vpHHFqdDxxJNI2iUafLS42a+OhwENnA8zc8GSNNFKsU0No2qb6WjcsqV9e4gBXgwyF/QU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2901,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.513897620Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"6d3cedca-f9c0-5017-b482-ca58f096ab94","title":"[L430] E3 execution requires a wall deadline and has no untimed representation","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L430.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/analysis/peritus-eval/src/profile/binding.rs:98-168,195-218,222-330`, `src/execution/directive.rs:35-67,149-183`, `src/execution/port.rs:56-129` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: ExecutionBinding stores deadline_micros as u64 and rejects zero, along with zero concurrency. The positive deadline participates in its immutable digest and is copied into both candidate and evaluator stage directives. There is no None/Untimed variant. The E3 execution wrapper itself runs synchronous external ports and does not measure elapsed time or install a watchdog; enforcing the requested deadline is delegated to runtime composition.\n- Consequence: Every valid evaluation profile requires an artificial wall ceiling even when the user requests persistent untimed work. Changing it creates a different execution/profile identity. The read source proves the mandatory contract but does not establish which external owner enforces it, what value an installed evaluator uses, or that it caused the current session timeout. Concurrency's u16 width is a physical scalar constraint, separate from the positive-only policy.\n- Repair direction: Represent an explicit optional user deadline separately from process ownership, cancellation, isolation, and measured elapsed usage, and propagate untimed execution consistently through both stages and their canonical identities. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGTqJzxf7iFVQjn+0kjK2X2NnZ+sUvN3uBxlS8C5acOO1bjPu3JA3QFNT22NU0Vmmx2JvF3/wOhzlKkH3UlREQg="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2902,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.516173325Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"6d3cedca-f9c0-5017-b482-ca58f096ab94","comment_uuid":"4c512928-57d1-4816-b063-3914d859a287","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L430: E3 execution requires a wall deadline and has no untimed representation.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/analysis/peritus-eval/src/profile/binding.rs:98-168,195-218,222-330; src/execution/directive.rs:35-67,149-183; src/execution/port.rs:56-129. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nRepresent an explicit optional user deadline separately from process ownership, cancellation, isolation, and measured elapsed usage, and propagate untimed execution consistently through both stages and their canonical identities. No tests run.\n\nPreserve: exact candidate revision and artifact binding, complete finding/provenance conservation, independent reviewer evidence, truthful gate outcomes, protected user constraints and acceptance fail-closed on invalid evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEPhgjBnNp+DS176xZTRbYhnLXNf6rNUXqO7qxTZlRdWPTCRJkvdBoJevgUvawo6DbqIo6a6ZqZaae6QgXpE4gI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2903,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.518596553Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"97f16741-6b83-5a79-9e7d-f14725857aa3","title":"[L431] E3 blocking stage effects cannot observe cancellation through the execution-port contract","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L431.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/analysis/peritus-eval/src/execution/port.rs:12-36,56-129,132-165`, `src/execution/directive.rs:12-28,137-147`, `src/execution/observation.rs:11-51,249-260` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: execute_rollout probes cancellation before candidate execution and again before evaluator execution. Each port call is synchronous and receives a directive without the CancellationProbe or a cancellation token. No probe is made after evaluator return before constructing its verdict. Required trace completeness and optional teardown completeness are validated after effects; invalid observations return Quarantine. Failed-stage observations retain only a class/digest/retryable flag, not resources consumed before failure.\n- Consequence: E3 itself cannot interrupt a stuck stage through this trait, regardless of durable cancellation becoming true during the call. An external adapter could independently observe cancellation, so an inevitable hang is not claimed. Post-effect validation can leave the wrapper without a returned complete rollout record despite completed work, and failed-attempt consumption is unavailable through this failure type. The downstream reducer only admits SettleRollout in Running, so a late ordinary verdict cannot legally override Cancelling; explicit cancellation settlement is required (aggregate/reducer.rs:274-305). The blocker is interruptibility and retained partial observations, not cancellation dominance.\n- Repair direction: Give effect ownership an interruptible, resumable contract carrying cancellation and exact stage/continuation identity. Retain partial outcomes and failed-stage resource observations before reconciliation or retry. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQM/U1oh2dAVgdHI9ScyOiP2XBBle2HQ82tuJmZ2FIIK7pYRYw955I/gCsxiLnilXSeoVapSCkEbaVJ1CBYRPeQs="}
