cts reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMAdFYMdSFLy49W8DadNR7sdSjwqgP2yRCLioiMloayRJ3C0p5u9DoKzgJiPcNlj4PSJS5kcxDZn0iJAO9Tuwgk="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2905,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.524105259Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"f8e53bb0-2946-5fac-81ca-1386c5e2fd7d","title":"[L432] E3 accepts a frozen profile whose component policies disagree with its final limits and provider","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L432.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/analysis/peritus-eval/src/profile/binding.rs:250-330,407-459`, `src/profile/provider.rs:165-201`, `src/profile/policy.rs:12-69,118-170`, `src/dataset/manifest.rs:24-70`, `src/aggregate/state.rs:185-195`, `src/durability/commit.rs:82-94` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: The final profile rechecks selected rollout cardinality, but does not recheck dataset task count, retry maximum, bootstrap count or pass-k count against the final EvaluationLimits. Previously checked components can come from different limits. Model controls incorporate the provider used at construction into a digest, but retain no independently checked provider binding; the final profile accepts a separate provider snapshot without comparing it. Aggregate checkpoint serialization uses CodecLimits::PRODUCTION rather than the frozen profile's state_bytes.\n- Consequence: A tighter advertised profile can still contain components constructed under larger limits, or seed controls checked for a different provider. This postpones rejection or permits policies that do not match the purported frozen contract. For example, a two-task dataset can be admitted with final tasks=1 if the independent rollout ceiling accommodates it. These are source-derived constructor/enforcement gaps, not executed examples or proof of an installed provider failure.\n- Repair direction: Validate the complete profile as one coherent contract; retain and compare provider bindings and distinguish explicit workload policy from storage limits. Any intentional limit should be enforced at its ownership boundary and remain recoverable. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQACLxPfT6hzvn44HJcF+pQhLz6TFNWCg0uRF/Y11M3iFxAbNetU8HnhfiSc0B69TNolFUwzZqiXoZ57LuUzjnwY="}
