ers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFSv5pV1EADwGf1nM6ol5hxYMgSIP3711YscqxEyTdd2zNkKVVBLFjSSAVfN0ZeXzmfwiA+TMejLHeN0QJL5fAU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2907,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.529379128Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"526ac80b-1718-5bd9-a17a-da379741d66c","title":"[L433] E3 refuses cancellation once deterministic analysis begins","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L433.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/analysis/peritus-eval/src/aggregate/reducer.rs:285-293,337-365`, `src/aggregate/command.rs:13-111`, `src/aggregate/types.rs:20-79`, `src/runtime/mod.rs:75-105` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: CancelCampaign returns a quarantining binding error in Analyzing or ReportReady. The command vocabulary has no pause/resume operation for those phases. FailCampaign can force failure, but is not cancellation or suspension with resumable work.\n- Consequence: A caller cannot request normal durable cancellation after statistical analysis starts or while publication is pending. This is an explicit phase blocker even when no external rollout remains. It does not prove the installed writer uses E3, and it does not establish that session context is deleted.\n- Repair direction: Model cancellation and suspension as durable intent across every nonterminal phase, with analysis/publication safe points and retained results. Preserve publication integrity instead of using a blanket late-phase cancellation rejection. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOnP8sggLgeJ7NbhvaB6c6JT2RMQd4dXAiiFkjJeUJXsyp7ftJLf+ZwtvfDR+tpRiN1kXI6RJV1CdByosDYidw8="}
