ance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQK+dMKI7A35CgQ0XfZgx57KK40HpPEDw9kYOAmHOxsUECR1dCS+NrqwlqSW3n4bo1KSIsIRdpbtr9c0OeAQu8gM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2913,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.546094129Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"5bfc7c9f-84e5-52a5-bdc9-991404f93bb8","title":"[L436] E3 committed-command replay fails after the aggregate advances and binds effect retries to a claim fence","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L436.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/analysis/peritus-eval/src/aggregate/reducer.rs:96-123`, `src/durability/commit.rs:96-119,363-420` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: The pure reducer requires the latest predecessor before deciding a command. C0 commit resolution runs before current-head validation, but resolve_existing still requires the current checkpoint to equal the old command's exact successor. After a later command advances the state, the old committed receipt produces Recovery/Quarantine. Claimed and settlement request digests also include the outbox fence; reclaiming the same message changes the digest for the same command identity.\n- Consequence: An exact successful command can cease to be retryable after unrelated progress, and an effect retry under a new owner fence can conflict unless the caller retains and reconciles the original receipt and identities. This can obstruct reconnection without any actual context expiration. Immediate duplicate retries may work; this finding concerns later-state replay and reclaimed claims.\n- Repair direction: Resolve durable command/effect receipts independently of the current successor checkpoint, then load the latest state. Distinguish logical effect identity from delivery ownership while preserving stale-owner rejection. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCYik85S5jBAlOxu6eJbsVRMqAb13S/12MvZFXDs0A955Eae8+ETnEeO2SoX5tAapYxV0mgseaSz19w31+GoWAo="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2914,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.548517300Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"5bfc7c9f-84e5-52a5-bdc9-991404f93bb8","comment_uuid":"3fe7e573-99ff-47d4-af76-75694ddd7ca0","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L436: E3 committed-command replay fails after the aggregate advances and binds effect retries to a claim fence.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/analysis/peritus-eval/src/aggregate/reducer.rs:96-123; src/durability/commit.rs:96-119,363-420. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nResolve durable command/effect receipts independently of the current successor checkpoint, then load the latest state. Distinguish logical effect identity from delivery ownership while preserving stale-owner rejection. No tests run.\n\nPreserve: exact candidate revision and artifact binding, complete finding/provenance conservation, independent reviewer evidence, truthful gate outcomes, protected user constraints and acceptance fail-closed on invalid evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLTCfTzZqiG+S2TxSO7fMLnOlIdm8PbivMBzpGnl1SLIoCLJVkcYbMdO+9ZUhe7Y8KxGiYHkhUrTGuaoGjcYFQY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2915,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.550774613Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"702dbb9f-0109-5346-812f-4ce09d2eb9f3","title":"[L437] E3 recovery can request analysis from ReportReady and treats terminal publication as complete without owner checks","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L437.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/analysis/peritus-eval/src/runtime/recovery.rs:57-90`, `src/aggregate/reducer.rs:337-372`, `src/runtime/publication.rs:60-73` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: A ReportReady state with verified report bytes, no admitted evidence and no outstanding publication directive falls through to complete rollout counts and BeginAnalysis. StartAnalysis accepts only Planned/Scheduling/Running, so that decision is illegal from ReportReady. Terminal phases return Complete before checking artifact/evidence/publication observations. Publication execution itself requires ReportReady.\n- Consequence: Missing publication intent after recovery has no explicit E3 repair decision and can lead a caller toward an illegal transition. Missing owner evidence after Published is not detected by this decision table. Other owners can perform integrity checks, so inevitable silent loss is not claimed. The healthy ReportReady case with an outstanding directive correctly selects RetryPublication.\n- Repair direction: Make recovery exhaustive over durable phase and exact owner receipts. Recover or reconcile missing publication intent rather than restarting analysis, and verify required terminal ownership before declaring recovery complete. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAA