{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2917,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.555355735Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"6d3d9ff7-5906-51be-9810-40da2a35eca0","title":"[L438] E3 repeatedly copies and replays the complete campaign instead of resuming bounded work","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L438.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/analysis/peritus-eval/src/aggregate/reducer.rs:22-30,69-93,172`, `src/aggregate/state.rs:115-117,185-195,346-418`, `src/durability/replay.rs:36-48,76-101`, `src/wire/event.rs:52-70`, `src/wire/state.rs:15-18,55-66`, `src/durability/commit.rs:82-94`, `src/runtime/publication.rs:87-88` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Every transition clones and canonically hashes the complete rollout map and retained batch artifacts. C0 loading activates each frame through apply_event and then applies it again; rebuild replays the entire history again. State frames clone and nest the entire canonical checkpoint under production byte bounds. rollouts() creates a complete Vec even when recovery only needs an any() probe. Publication exports the complete journal for evidence admission. These synchronous paths expose no cancellation/progress probe.\n- Consequence: At R retained rollouts and E events, transition/recovery work includes O(E*R) full-state copying/hashing after the plan is populated, with repeated replay passes and full-history allocation. Larger profiles can spend increasing time rereading/rebuilding rather than executing new work. Nested codec limits can reject a full checkpoint even if individual components fit. This is source-level cost analysis, not a benchmark or attribution of the live session's loop.\n- Repair direction: Preserve immutable history while making validated checkpoints and effect receipts support incremental recovery, streaming projections and bounded resumable analysis. Keep cancellation/status independent of full-campaign serialization. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAx+qoPBW78oS8ZdBy5HfpF93v3urd+XV91x22xrR3OpBS8l1zXwEymqJKMK9P8CdmhAVfHnhtt+Z267+DqFIgg="}
