rs, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPzzCSTX9A+Fibr642lQ1d1wA0kELu5LVEAsatwlvU7nsDjh3zZFtiM8fc6eO9k6wRKif4BsysovJIYVoJ/FAAI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2925,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.574391395Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"12c5b6a8-4977-5971-82a1-5f504f109d89","title":"[L443] F0 silently evicts rollback targets from the long-lived production pointer","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L443.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/analysis/peritus-evolution/src/pointer/reducer.rs:161-184,239-243,245-255,272-300,313-319`, `src/pointer/rollback.rs:156-176`, `src/pointer/state.rs:206-210`, `src/limits.rs:22-33` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Each activation appends a history record; when the retained history length equals activation_history, append_history removes index zero first. The compiled maximum is 256 and a caller may tighten it to 1. RollbackProposal and both rollback preparation/activation require the target activation to remain in that suffix. With limit=1, even the immediately previous activation is absent after a new activation. No pointer command expands the window or loads an older target from immutable journal history.\n- Consequence: Authorized rollback becomes impossible through the normal F0 pointer contract solely because enough later activations occurred. The authoritative journal may retain every event; this is checkpoint-target eviction, not deletion of evidence or model session context. The pointer continues promoting rather than halting at capacity, so the blocker is historical reachability rather than a promotion-count ceiling.\n- Repair direction: Resolve rollback targets from durable immutable activation history with exact provenance and compatibility checks. Bound the hot projection/cache independently of target eligibility and preserve stable target identity across checkpoint compaction. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQO4lsEooXAs+J4PoMgZJ69/R1AT5lWtpueQ7kwkVOLL30vqVXOa6wWQ+DjybVbYvxmMmXnc9u/tvzRRpQcMkDQc="}
