{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2931,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.588494534Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"28d77166-1e1b-5ed4-80c2-8de88c8e48ba","title":"[L446] F0 rejects multiline human-authored explanation text","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L446.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/analysis/peritus-evolution/src/change/text.rs:16-27`, `src/change/manifest.rs`, `src/change/prediction.rs`, `src/selection/assessment.rs` in the same crate; text ceiling also recorded in L442.\n- Behavior: BoundedText requires nonempty text, exact trimmed form, the configured byte bound and no character for which is_control is true. Newlines, carriage returns and tabs are therefore rejected alongside unsafe control characters. The same wrapper is used for hypotheses, alternatives, prediction falsification and selection explanations.\n- Consequence: Ordinary multiline rationale cannot be represented even when it is well within the byte limit. This is an input-format blocker for evolution evidence, not a model execution deadline or demonstrated installed-session failure.\n- Repair direction: Define allowed whitespace explicitly and preserve ordinary structured prose. Restrict unsafe control sequences without making every explanation a single line. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJhpf+ecMG/CFJyVTYsdJ1iLNAARSMD/sll9/hsy6y/DtsiHb5RulGj6ChUI4m5+Y2pcPpyZrrVp2VYCI+akzgk="}
