{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2933,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.592952102Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"d09a23ec-77d8-5a07-a25c-ab0c3995a508","title":"[L447] F0 accepts mandatory failure-class predictions that its attribution engine can never confirm","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L447.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/analysis/peritus-evolution/src/change/prediction.rs:160-170`, `src/attribution/engine.rs:68-69`, `src/attribution/record.rs:158-160`, `src/selection/engine.rs:85-90` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Prediction construction admits a FailureClass subject for metrics other than TaskPassAtK. Attribution unconditionally returns Unavailable with UnsupportedFailureClass for that subject. Every mandatory prediction whose result is not Confirmed counts as a mandatory failure, and selection requires that count to be zero.\n- Consequence: A syntactically accepted mandatory failure-class prediction makes its candidate permanently ineligible through the current engine. More runs or waiting cannot satisfy it. The mandatory-evidence rule itself is a valid quality contract; admitting a requirement the engine cannot evaluate is the blocker. No installed campaign was reproduced.\n- Repair direction: Validate evaluability at admission or implement class-specific measurements and uncertainty handling. Return a repairable unsupported-capability result before freezing a campaign requirement. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKF/5M3H