{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2937,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.602085115Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"9cc37ab0-914d-5892-898e-724d646bd9b1","title":"[L449] F0 publication is permanently bounded to sixteen delivery claims","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L449.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/analysis/peritus-evolution/src/durability/directive.rs:17,206-258`; C0 exhaustion semantics documented in L251/L265.\n- Behavior: Both CampaignDecision and HarnessActivation directives are built with MAX_ATTEMPTS=16. This limit counts C0 delivery claims and has no F0 configuration, unlimited representation or replenishment command. It is separate from campaign evaluation attempts and human approval.\n- Consequence: Sufficient delivery failures can exhaust durable publication even though the intended artifact and activation remain valid and recoverable. RetryPublication alone does not provide a fresh eligible claim once C0 has exhausted the row. This is an explicit synthetic retry ceiling, not a finding that sixteen failures occurred in the live session.\n- Repair direction: Keep durable publication intent pending until confirmed completion, explicit cancellation or an actionable integrity failure. Bound pacing and concurrent work independently of lifetime recoverable deliveries, and provide authorized reconciliation without changing evidence identity. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLlH3Ke7NQgXQZkNwCQ4ayQTFpUFUtZVv3hY3oAKMf9iZL8rWiPAvs