{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2940,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.608747608Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"c443a582-368f-5293-b116-89ed5e305cb0","comment_uuid":"1b2ccef3-0f85-4718-bb4d-67b01d65814d","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L450: Ordinary F0 committed-command replay fails after later checkpoint progress.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/analysis/peritus-evolution/src/durability/campaign.rs:192-228; src/durability/pointer.rs:165-201. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nValidate the immutable producing transaction and its original installed state independently of the latest projection. Return the existing receipt without regressing current state, retaining conflicting-request and causal-fence rejection for genuinely new mutations. No tests run.\n\nPreserve: exact candidate revision and artifact binding, complete finding/provenance conservation, independent reviewer evidence, truthful gate outcomes, protected user constraints and acceptance fail-closed on invalid evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQM8ZndltssmXGy7Z2vSj5vLhCsfl/A9gEBRrh/uPyLHsRkaG7MWLYsnVGzDyu+NTmtANijiAcFe4avm4iXLHNAY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2941,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.611145187Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"52010d2b-d9c6-5002-8d10-573f2f50aaae","title":"[L451] F0 recovery can report terminal completion without checking retained artifact/evidence observations","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L451.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/analysis/peritus-evolution/src/runtime/recovery.rs:11-19,48-68`, `src/durability/directive.rs:224-247`, `src/runtime/publication.rs:46-85` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Recovery checks artifact_verified and evidence_admitted only when publication_directive is true. With an Active pointer and terminal campaign, false publication_directive yields Complete even when both owner observations are false. Promotion/rollback activation creates a separate publication directive; publication ACK occurs after evidence admission, but ACK status alone is not a check that the owners still retain matching content.\n- Consequence: The F0 classifier alone cannot distinguish a fully published terminal activation from one with acknowledged/absent pending delivery but missing referenced owner records. A pending directive still produces the appropriate reconciliation decision. Higher-level integrity scans may catch owner loss; this is a recovery-contract gap, not proof that the current daemon ignored corruption or deleted context.\n- Repair direction: Derive required publication obligations from durable activation/evidence state and verify their owner receipts before declaring completion. Treat delivery state as transport progress rather than the complete publication truth. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBkCecZP6ooXPhY+1hGLlJ0kltb4diMUHt4Vk+NF5RNQjIwdZ+vXD2a3VCFfDigPrWb43fjnTXbbiKPaMgypFg4="}
