e evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQK174EICu7GadlK15zwIRd52qfVhHfUKtS3DhgUWOMqy1fxpuCfQNDPelBswtHVOWPo9R6WYmN9wS6VsMPXOHA4="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2945,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.621235565Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"112057e8-f832-5204-84dc-5d346187b4e4","title":"[L453] An accepted out-of-range probability threshold cannot survive F0 wire decoding","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L453.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/analysis/peritus-evolution/src/change/prediction.rs:85-118,151-176`, `src/wire/semantic/change.rs:251-285`, `src/wire/campaign.rs:32-44,350-363` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: MetricValue exposes ProbabilityMillionths directly. Its probability helper rejects values above 1,000,000, but Prediction::new only checks numeric variant compatibility and subject/metric rules, so direct enum construction bypasses the range check. Semantic writing emits the raw u32, while semantic reading always calls the bounded helper.\n- Consequence: An accepted prediction can encode successfully and then fail canonical read/replay. For example, a directly constructed ProbabilityMillionths(1,000,001) threshold is incompatible with the wire contract despite passing the prediction constructor. This is an admission/restore mismatch, not a legitimate deadline; the probability range itself is mathematically required. No executed reproduction is claimed.\n- Repair direction: Enforce numeric domain invariants at every public admission boundary or use a validated probability type that cannot be bypassed. Verify encode/decode parity before committing accepted semantic state. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMSXj+tnqhHzEU/tT2SrC8DagJk3vxAKKklCMbiKZ0cFczPAQcu5JAe5O+vagQcSlywtfaWZ/rrgRGjirSjLAAQ="}
