nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJ6VDVoYLPM0lV7hzU3iaNDYgfxlGlwVVye56mKdKbDrJfGJ8b2CcPrI17WU5UtKYhGEI4lt9CuymOX1jmLUsQw="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2947,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.626218129Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"8e276769-3073-5466-a46a-9e3735c95f27","title":"[L454] F0 wraps complete growing checkpoints in a fixed eight-MiB opaque payload","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L454.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/analysis/peritus-evolution/src/wire/campaign.rs:279-281,318-330`, `src/wire/pointer.rs:299-301,338-350`, `src/wire/semantic/campaign.rs:9-10,75-77`, `src/wire/semantic/state/campaign.rs:13-62`, `src/wire/semantic/state/pointer.rs:14-42`, `src/durability/campaign.rs:34-48`, `src/durability/pointer.rs:33-47` in the same crate; production codec limits in L009.\n- Behavior: Inner semantic codecs hard-code CodecLimits::PRODUCTION. Checkpoints serialize all retained manifests, diagnoses, evaluation metrics, attributions, assessments or pointer history into one byte vector; the outer frame writes that vector as a single bytes field. Its eight-MiB opaque-field limit applies even though the whole-message ceiling is sixteen MiB. F0 has no independent state-size configuration or incremental checkpoint representation.\n- Consequence: Individually valid additions within every F0 collection/text bound can still make the next complete checkpoint uncommittable. Cancel/fail also serializes retained state, so it does not provide a general size-reduction path. Expanding an outer caller codec cannot lift the hard-coded inner contract. This is a source-derived scaling ceiling, not evidence that an evolution checkpoint reached it in the live run.\n- Repair direction: Persist immutable evidence once by verified reference and checkpoint a paged projection. Reserve reliable control/settlement operations independently of aggregate evidence volume while preserving exact provenance and replay integrity. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJiK0X4rKGsijZjj0E+lDTa3t/DUCqH75OT7rYduKOl46JFeyV88rFcjY79PmfcJztGzgFT4m5dm9rKO9uDYaQ4="}
