ections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBiCU7fPwiTsqELMcMABiNqRmAGp4q+2pvIAfbFKdJaSlECS+6lz8KCawYFzhcYWUDMh4BOJ0fZ/8uA7Ue9V/gw="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2961,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.658073634Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"1af9e091-324c-53f7-a549-d23c62ef33ac","title":"[L462] C5 archives, events and rate observations add compiled ceilings beyond request bounds","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L462.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/model/peritus-model-protocol/src/message_codec.rs:6-7,17-31,60-72`, `src/event_codec/primitive.rs:5-19`, `src/rate_limit.rs:90-104`, `src/event_codec/decode.rs:220-228` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: a profile-independent message archive has a fixed 64-MiB total ceiling and still applies max_messages. Event envelopes have another fixed 64-MiB total ceiling, collection maximum 1,024 and depth maximum 32. String and byte bounds combine several domain maxima. A rate-limit observation must contain between one and 64 windows; it cannot carry more provider dimensions even if the encoded frame would fit.\n- Consequence: a conversation valid for the 512-MiB canonical-request encoder can exceed the separate 64-MiB archive format. These APIs expose no larger-frame or paged representation. Provider reset values, retry-after values and cache TTLs are inert observations here; they do not expire local sessions or impose a wall-clock timeout. The archive ceiling's installed effect depends on its separately tracked callers.\n- Repair direction: store exact conversation history in authenticated pages and select provider context separately; make transport/observation capacity explicit and avoid converting a storage ceiling into loss of the session. Retain closed-tag and sequence integrity checks. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihm