he predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQD/BDwljrH1wciZFXEyxQujJx2VJLvjywkvSpZOVljbLQdeGGArag4sIX3hFUG0wm3QLfQ6fALFlKSaMvQjtIQM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2963,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.663467282Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"0acdc6f8-4322-55da-9503-4fba6fa77938","title":"[L463] C5 reconstruction materializes full bounded content before aggregate request checks","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L463.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/model/peritus-model-protocol/src/canonical_decode.rs:35-67`, `src/canonical_decode/content.rs:11-53`, `src/request/validation.rs:44-55`, `src/message_codec.rs:46-55`, `src/event_codec/decode.rs:64-73` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: canonical decoding constructs the full nested message collection, then ModelRequest admission checks total blocks and total media. Per-message counts and individual payloads are bounded, but aggregate request limits are enforced after their allocation. Canonical request, message and event decoders then encode the reconstructed value again for byte parity, retaining the original input while producing a complete second byte buffer. These are synchronous operations with no progress cursor or cancellation parameter.\n- Consequence: configured aggregate ceilings do not bound all intermediate allocation to that aggregate, and large retained histories can cause substantial uninterrupted copying/parsing. Fixed frame and nested limits still bound the formats; this is not an unbounded-parser claim or a measured explanation of the current lockup. No benchmark run.\n- Repair direction: enforce cumulative budgets while traversing nested values and stream canonical validation/digests over durable pages. Expose resumable progress to the owner without weakening exact-byte validation. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJiv3Sqy9uXOrk/MfZExoxqDJZg/xr1l1EbrZTKxPMwoiFZ8PDumXNiEWoXBXEQvEsOqE4ln+gSns+yhRUsrjQY="}
