eady owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQB9U0IP79G9ujGCRboxCFa7AvTsaYM5o1BKqcOQ4vtw9hFEpYAOP0hXWrS9dUW5kn86Zx/6oq2fLMdkDvvprlQY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2965,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.667948213Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"c87dc753-7d8a-595b-81b4-dc2996f36e4e","title":"[L464] C5 retry algebra still requires a finite attempt and delay policy","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L464.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/model/peritus-model-protocol/src/retry.rs:72-94,119-128,170-178,192-205`, `tests/retry_matrix.rs:32-44,92-120` in the same crate; layered production policies are separately documented in L228.\n- Behavior: max_attempts is a mandatory positive u32 with no Unlimited form. Attempts stop before scheduling when attempt plus one reaches that value. max_elapsed_millis is optional and None genuinely disables this planner's elapsed horizon. Base delay must be positive, max_delay must be at least base, and a provider Retry-After above max_delay produces a terminal planning refusal even with no elapsed horizon. The pure planner itself neither sleeps nor kills a request.\n- Consequence: removing wall-clock limits alone leaves count and provider-delay blockers in the recovery contract. The ten-second elapsed horizon, four attempts and two-second delay in retry_matrix are fixture inputs, not installed defaults. Ambiguous acceptance and partial output without exact resumption are independent integrity constraints, not synthetic deadlines.\n- Repair direction: separate ongoing, user-cancellable recovery scheduling from finite request budgets, and retain exact identity/acceptance facts while waiting the provider's required delay. Provide an explicit unbounded attempt policy rather than a sentinel numeric maximum. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLjoptU+iu37tbjexd6Kzxwz4OdrBnTGAVpKB24Bd4QeqIM/kyi9s4KXO4W1XpLn3F2NLV6jWfN951VXQyuamAE="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2966,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.670447206Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"c87dc753-7d8a-595b-81b4-dc2996f36e4e","comment_uuid":"93fc4a93-dafd-4080-8318-201aeb8aadf5","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L464: C5 retry algebra still requires a finite attempt and delay policy.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/model/peritus-model-protocol/src/retry.rs:72-94,119-128,170-178,192-205; tests/retry_matrix.rs:32-44,92-120. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nseparate ongoing, user-cancellable recovery scheduling from finite request budgets, and retain exact identity/acceptance facts while waiting the provider's required delay. Provide an explicit unbounded attempt policy rather than a sentinel numeric maximum. No tests run.\n\nPreserve: definitely-unaccepted versus ambiguously-accepted request state, exact native thread/profile identity, ordered provider observations, tool-result protocol, explicit cancellation and real provider/model capabilities. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEw3I4aLKkqqmslJEEGy6hpNTR18XqtWvPt0AlcqhH0TeUEJIprNtyKPeh8zZDNqEuLvcoUoBHumitSIgD7JBA8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2967,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.672691105Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"1deab1f1-3a9f-51d1-abfe-80627cf1865b","title":"[L465] C5 exponential retry backoff can wrap to zero despite a positive minimum","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L465.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/model/peritus-model-protocol/src/retry.rs:192-197,208-217`.\n- Behavior: the exponential delay uses checked_shl with a shift already clamped to 63. checked_shl rejects an out-of-range shift count, but does not detect discarded high bits. Thus its unwrap_or(u64::MAX) does not protect arithmetic overflow in these allowed shifts. With base_delay_millis 100, attempt 63 or greater, no Retry-After and zero jitter, the shifted value is zero and the calculated delay is zero despite validation requiring a positive base.\n- Consequence: a caller permitting enough safe retries can lose all backoff and repeatedly resubmit immediately. This is a reachable source-level planner defect; currently audited production layers with smaller retry counts do not establish that the live session reached this case. Removing those count limits without fixing the arithmetic would expose it more broadly.\n- Repair direction: calculate exponential growth with saturating multiplication or an explicit overflow predicate, then apply the intended delay policy. Preserve nonzero scheduled waits and cancellation across long recovery sequences. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLP0FDkGhcZhQDE83Aw3sHBif9vTEBvTqZ2q7sL8W+fKY3T7Id6t7W7kqh5S2ZD47SkOkKPysTuegazYv5J1ugc="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2968,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.674915616Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"1deab1f1-3a9f-51d1-abfe-80627cf1865b","comment_uuid":"0e8c8f31-ba43-45e2-bd77-757bb5bf1cb7","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L465: C5 exponential retry backoff can wrap to zero despite a positive minimum.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/model/peritus-model-protocol/src/retry.rs:192-197,208-217. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\ncalculate exponential growth with saturating multiplication or an explicit overflow predicate, then apply the intended delay policy. Preserve nonzero scheduled waits and cancellation across long recovery sequences. No tests run.\n\nPreserve: definitely-unaccepted versus ambiguously-accepted request state, exact native thread/profile identity, ordered provider observations, tool-result protocol, explicit cancellation and real provider/model capabilities. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEqXyyV+bUaFlrr1DnFRRPO5dcYVX6lCHX7SoeSu4/MHTNzJhOQtCnoqiTkYhqbo1Y0906FQV6otvIHbu0pkiwc="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2969,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.677058132Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"2d5ec060-8d70-5f04-b2e0-9fc882d9a7c8","title":"[L466] Provider-core metadata and credential bounds are compiled independently","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L466.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/model/peritus-provider-core/src/credential.rs:9-10,22-30,56-60,73-83`, `src/endpoint.rs:7,27-56,81-89`, `src/diagnostic.rs:8,37-48`, `src/redaction.rs:7,19-30` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: opaque credential references are capped at 512 bytes, credentials at 16 KiB, prefixed credential-header intermediates at 16 KiB plus 128, endpoint input at 4,096 bytes, diagnostic values at 512 bytes and redacted identifiers at 1,024 bytes. Downstream HTTP header constructors add separately audited ceilings. Endpoint canonical serialization occurs after the input-length check, so the checked bound is input bytes rather than a guaranteed bound on normalized URL bytes.\n- Consequence: larger embeddings cannot widen these capacities through an exposed configuration. These are transport/metadata admission checks, not elapsed timers or session TTLs. Control-character, secret-bearing URL and unsafe-header checks protect syntax/privacy and should remain distinct from size policy; no oversized live credential/endpoint failure was observed.\n- Repair direction: unify domain and transport size admission, bound the stored normalized representation consistently, and expose justified capacity policy independently of credential isolation. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEq7j5Dn/ae2Q5bP+3Rcwu6mE4VJWmfa+Uja7TfuZQAat0kWf84+7UqgkJSaebVnUjmE5dYtT2UXVIAIcSw4Vgc="}
