lready owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFfUcBxjHlKK8HMBSbdDgmV7fcUaPs3I93CJsrJsU5OWH1TrDWzuzqbf+wMQqMGGh/fno6JsPr6DZGAsuADqvw8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2973,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.686524988Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"9ccd6af2-f445-52cb-ae7e-e2fae81b283d","title":"[L468] Live provider qualification bypasses normalized response legality","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L468.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/model/peritus-provider-core/src/qualification.rs:313-352`, `src/connection.rs:79,163-185`, `tests/qualification_recovery.rs:181-198,202-225` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: verify_live_provider tracks whether any TextDelta contains a nonwhitespace byte, then accepts ResponseCompleted as LiveCanary. It does not drive ResponseReducer or interpret Finish reasons. Its fake provider test explicitly expects success for TextDelta followed by ResponseCompleted without ResponseStarted, ItemStarted, ItemCompleted or Finish. By contrast, later connection-test tool stages do use ResponseReducer.\n- Consequence: malformed, unclosed or provider-incomplete output can qualify the route even when an ordinary model turn would fail its C5 contract. Readiness then overstates what was actually established and can send daily-driving work into recovery loops. This is a source/test-contract finding, not evidence that your currently selected provider emitted that grammar.\n- Repair direction: qualify through the same normalized reducer and accepted terminal policy used by ordinary work, retaining context/capacity/refusal causes. Readiness should certify a completed usable response rather than the presence of two event shapes. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN