{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2977,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.695800571Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"258bdf92-c897-51e0-b2e5-3556e401b00a","title":"[L470] Compatible API defaults retain finite retry and private production capacities","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L470.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/model/peritus-provider-compatible/src/config.rs:21-22,159-172,189-204,242-262,315-331`, `src/client.rs:142-180,211-228,280-283` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: default retry policy has no elapsed horizon, but permits three total attempts, 100-ms initial delay, two-second maximum delay/Retry-After and a 64-MiB cumulative request-byte budget. Callers can replace that finite RetryPolicy. HTTP, SSE framing and protocol limits remain private fixed production values with getters but no public replacement method. Fixed custom headers are capped at 16 and each at 4,096 bytes; mapped observations allow only one rate-limit dimension group.\n- Consequence: untimed transport does not imply persistent recovery. Count/delay/byte ceilings can still stop an otherwise recoverable outage, and adapter callers cannot widen underlying transport/protocol capacities. cumulative_bytes is consulted after a failed attempt rather than admitting the next encoded body against the remaining byte policy before send; it is a retry stop observation rather than a complete per-send capacity invariant. No installed compatible-route failure reproduced.\n- Repair direction: separate retained session/recovery state from finite per-request budgets, expose deliberate capacity configuration and maintain cancellable provider-directed recovery rather than category-based restart. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQG7/repNlL595lcY5HBIxwAl2CjDuWCNSaHxAmENo4P8bNbB5MN0ambo6Tvja6OGow6zF/BTlRIjD6F5NARegg4="}
