umers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKw1t6P9UPT3daFlqJTA9CX5WYeh/ckztXwy5YohWny2EjC/wv1qYbPCPNIhIpq6J5XwOreEDES0D9I+ksV1rQU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2981,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.704319259Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"72841455-7ca7-534f-85fc-2f92d079265d","title":"[L472] Compatible Retry-After parsing silently loses provider scheduling information","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L472.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/model/peritus-provider-compatible/src/client/metadata.rs:66,72-82,166-172,183-196`, `src/client.rs:211-228`, `src/config.rs:196-200` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Retry-After must fit 64 bytes and parse as an integer number of seconds no greater than 86,400. Larger integers or any other representation, including an HTTP-date, become None rather than a retained unsupported scheduling observation. A retained delay above the default two-second policy causes RetryPolicy::plan to return an error before the already-built normalized HTTP failure can be emitted.\n- Consequence: one response can cause an immediate default backoff after its provider-required wait was discarded; another can become generic InvalidRetry instead of preserving RateLimited/status/acceptance facts. This is independent of an elapsed horizon and can drive repeated rejections or prevent automatic recovery. Actual HTTP-date/provider behavior was not queried; this is a parser/policy finding from source.\n- Repair direction: retain provider scheduling data with explicit units/parse status, support its documented forms, and schedule cancellable recovery without throwing away the normalized rejection when local policy cannot schedule it. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFasJYWiqd0XE9SNhitbJkyH1j+Qq2iHFVQ1bt7jaWBCsCPTAs+JhUbtu6AJfmrwCM3mwGguD7XtXcwSObeoZwQ="}
