nregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGGtx6+W1oP54HDVd/hl8h7YX9xomWAWyQyEXb9PQvj3NcdptArr739pB7xGE75q3TbiwIZ8P+kkHY2QM+JISQs="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2983,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.708597423Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"081c3b9e-9016-56de-a875-250f9d3ab557","title":"[L473] Optional compatible observations can fail an already accepted response","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L473.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/model/peritus-provider-compatible/src/client/metadata.rs:13-45,175-196`, `src/client.rs:247-259`, `src/stream/chat.rs:126-168`, `src/stream/chat/fields.rs:9-38,52-64`, `src/stream/responses/terminal.rs:94-113` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: mapped request IDs are capped at 512 bytes and numeric headers at 64. Invalid UTF-8/numbers or inconsistent rate windows fail success metadata conversion before the event stream is returned. Undeclared usage is fatal; complete reported totals must equal input plus output exactly. Closed top-level ancillary field sets and bounded ancillary canonicalization can likewise fail the entire stream.\n- Consequence: optional telemetry can block usable model output, including after HTTP acceptance. A pre-stream core error can also lose normalized acceptance/status facts needed by outer recovery layers (L228). Required response/tool/identity grammar is a separate integrity contract; this finding does not justify ignoring correctness-critical provider output. No malformed live metadata observed.\n- Repair direction: retain malformed or oversized optional observations as bounded diagnostic evidence without invalidating independently valid output, and carry typed acceptance facts through any truly fatal failure. Keep usage unknown when it cannot be trusted; do not fabricate or refund accounting. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOz7GLZZgmwc1t0QtwXPZQ0bNuIUzVLgd9WENJkqERWb8zNEGyQKSSSs8guaQXIhMLGExQWxexcZ/Oz08unApAE="}
