ants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAtBq/RSB8fSxKsew+d8FEzMn0BOMfdudL8MisznfgXQ+hbcaW7VWwCREMdg1EZgrz6jjVmswVU/eigNGMS2vQQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2985,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.713156365Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"b8f19fd6-f7a8-5f77-b6f3-323944190af2","title":"[L474] Compatible catalog discovery rejects safe configured queries and custom operation paths","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L474.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/model/peritus-provider-compatible/src/config.rs:175-189,279-283`, `src/client/catalog.rs:14-18`, `crates/model/peritus-provider-core/src/hosted.rs:73-84`.\n- Behavior: inference configuration explicitly permits fixed safe endpoint queries and an exact custom operation path. ModelProvider discovery derives the catalog by testing the full serialized URL for a raw /responses or /chat/completions suffix. A query prevents either suffix match. The routine does not dispatch to the separately reviewed hosted-service catalog endpoints; some hosted services use a different metadata origin/path.\n- Consequence: valid configured inference routes may be undiscoverable through this adapter API, requiring an explicit model ID. The method reports a capability limitation rather than inventing a replacement model. Its effect on current settings depends on the caller path, which remains separately tracked.\n- Repair direction: bind an explicit reviewed catalog endpoint to configuration, use parsed URL components for safe derivation when supported, and let exact-ID selection proceed when discovery is unavailable. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGjf3gN+9Frwhz5+LuG4RZ/7fY50ZlwrjsZFZMUbn6mhrs+iZ7zVa1uGmS557l5k+2NcYyGsw0P/L028AtJY2Qw="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2986,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.715354956Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"b8f19fd6-f7a8-5f77-b6f3-323944190af2","comment_uuid":"834437ec-83b1-4cfb-95b1-6fea1e83c75b","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L474: Compatible catalog discovery rejects safe configured queries and custom operation paths.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/model/peritus-provider-compatible/src/config.rs:175-189,279-283; src/client/catalog.rs:14-18; crates/model/peritus-provider-core/src/hosted.rs:73-84. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nbind an explicit reviewed catalog endpoint to configuration, use parsed URL components for safe derivation when supported, and let exact-ID selection proceed when discovery is unavailable. No tests run.\n\nPreserve: definitely-unaccepted versus ambiguously-accepted request state, exact native thread/profile identity, ordered provider observations, tool-result protocol, explicit cancellation and real provider/model capabilities. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGhGYHz/DSLIbRFSYzypJDl0GgS+gtspCoCX/6XSTgXdh3z7eiQqCvFjoGRwgXDymDqOIMeQ8zZaAQquxwpyOAI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2987,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.717405747Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"bb180e7d-cae2-535e-b3c4-30689492d286","title":"[L475] Compatible rejection recovery waits for the entire error body first","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L475.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/model/peritus-provider-compatible/src/client.rs:196-205,211-234`, `src/client/response.rs:10-23` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: even after a non-success status is known, start reads the entire bounded body to EOF before building the typed failure or planning an authorized retry. It stores the complete bytes to hash them. Transport/body cancellation is observed, but no incremental rejection event or recovery cursor is returned while the body is pending.\n- Consequence: a stalled error body can hold authentication/rate-limit/transient failure reporting and recovery pending indefinitely despite decisive headers already arriving. A body read/size failure replaces the original status classification. This is an ownership/progress blocker, not a reason to reintroduce arbitrary elapsed termination. No stalled live server reproduced.\n- Repair direction: durably expose the typed header rejection promptly, capture bounded body evidence with streaming digests and owned cancellation, and decouple optional body completion from safe recovery scheduling. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBkGMqMlJPsECLrIlNW83eV7l7SaBMfonSkguM9d21C20HjhTwwhSWW0Gqv8Ha