rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDZvQsO9IZUUm8uy3rPt0M/+dewsBp7mfh2uRZPiKAX83DXm0lagvFG7X/jr53HZ8nwCBm4qpUKsqAnEYML8kQw="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2991,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.726134055Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"6735b7a2-0a83-5839-a8c1-c09099b7a026","title":"[L477] Compatible normalization expands IDs and packs indices beyond the original value contract","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L477.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/model/peritus-provider-compatible/src/stream/chat.rs:304-327,330-354`, `src/stream/chat/tools.rs:28-45`, `src/stream/chat/hosted.rs:132-137`, `src/stream/responses.rs:351-360` in the same crate; C5 identity caps are recorded in L457.\n- Behavior: response IDs accepted up to 512 bytes are extended by -message, -refusal, -reasoning or tool suffixes, then reconstructed as ItemId under the same 512-byte ceiling. Responses nonzero content parts likewise append a suffix to the already checked wire item ID. Responses index normalization uses output_index times 65,536 plus content_index without first constraining content_index below 65,536.\n- Consequence: legal maximum-width provider identity values cannot normalize, so valid output can fail during item creation. Large but representable coordinate pairs can collide in the packed index or overflow u32. The item-count ceiling does not itself establish a coordinate bound. No live identity at these widths observed.\n- Repair direction: use separate bounded composite identities or collision-resistant derived identities tied to original evidence, and checked injective coordinate representations with explicit domain admission. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFu/fmOpvma8+rieOq3QUzOcWsHHhHBtHZNn+sCGG9MYml54ZXk9ktWY2CBvi4O1h82y9tm38I0+t3LZjQ26Wws="}
