ncilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKPRyjzK6rMnxFHwYCXMH7cgGcDc9aSwwLuAFvi+1LLNRSnJ7kw2g/jtxRwahWfWB61WNM6LaRUNK8rIzm7Qrw0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2993,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.730452733Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"af267399-0daf-50af-8828-4fe7a3d83ec4","title":"[L478] Hosted reasoning accumulation repeatedly scans and serializes all retained reasoning","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L478.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/model/peritus-provider-compatible/src/hosted_reasoning.rs:28-87`, `src/stream/chat.rs:246-253`, `src/stream/chat/hosted.rs:125-155`, `src/stream/responses_state.rs:103-121` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: reasoning detail fragments search the full stored detail array for matching id/index; each append serializes the complete accumulated reasoning map before checking the maximum. On completion it serializes another wrapper and copies all bytes into a vector of at most 16-KiB fragments. Responses item closure separately scans all parts to find its own parts. These operations are synchronous with no cancellation/progress cursor.\n- Consequence: a long sequence of small reasoning fragments can produce quadratic cumulative scanning/serialization despite bounded final bytes. Limits checked only after appending/serialization do not bound intermediate work to the stated final ceiling. This is source-derived scaling, not a benchmark or proof of the installed lockup.\n- Repair direction: maintain indexed reasoning identities and incremental canonical size/digest state, stream completion fragments, and make large retained-output traversal resumable under owned cancellation. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQF1Eh4LiyU8Z7ZUdM6UhhYCTyZPDugIQWzYryxNhpSj9fmGkRjMJfln7cTxoeZl0eLq4PwqLgcqRVwUDwoDCPQ4="}
