\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBI6+d4c3b60oF0c5/7elTV+l9WH0j9Jw9jExoDyn2tlQQuwo1idtTTBR0w62+yVUIVzlyt4VXLdZdaLfLr4cgo="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2995,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.735234531Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"89ac30b7-4dbe-5cb2-ac96-e9f07c773738","title":"[L479] Compatible streams can hide a known malformed suffix behind an already queued completion","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L479.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/model/peritus-provider-compatible/src/stream.rs:164-211`, `src/stream.rs:215-267`, `src/stream.rs:286-327`; `crates/model/peritus-provider-core/src/stream.rs:61-85`.\n- Behavior: a parsed chunk is processed synchronously and terminal events are queued immediately. A later data frame in that same parsed batch is rejected because terminal is already set, but the failure is appended after the queued completion. The owned stream returns the completion and permanently stops pulling at its first terminal event. A later network chunk is not read once the adapter is terminal either.\n- Consequence: the adapter can already know about malformed data yet report successful completion to its caller. This is an ownership and terminal-publication error, not a missing timeout. The result also depends on where transport chunks divide frames. No live reproduction or test execution is claimed.\n- Repair direction: define a consistent logical terminal boundary and validate already parsed input before publishing its one terminal outcome. Do not leave a known failure behind a terminal that prevents its delivery; do not wait indefinitely for transport EOF to finalize a legitimately completed response. Add chunk-partition regressions when repair is authorized.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQA