cers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQF78vCyvaq6vEd5IeFZC+3M4MTdRbc9t2vNE29LuzqTuZ8LrVNmv619QHv3vp+BtejI6jGsRULe2gzf3SrxOmQ8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":2997,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.739661314Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"decebc72-005d-5f78-8ca8-5fdd56dc5acd","title":"[L481] Anthropic direct request controls are restricted by adapter mappings, including cache TTLs that do not expire sessions","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L481.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/model/peritus-provider-anthropic/src/profile.rs:15-37`, `src/request.rs:80-105`, `src/request.rs:159-242`, `src/request.rs:245-371` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: the profile requires stateless Messages replay, unsupported cursor resume and local cancellation. Requests force streaming; reject deterministic seeds, stored/background continuation, extensions, unresolved artifacts and audio; require Draft 2020-12 schemas and strict schema output. Adaptive thinking rejects sampling, minimal/ultra effort and concise/detailed summary controls. Cache breakpoints accept only 300 or 3600 seconds; explicit cache keys fail.\n- Consequence: unsupported selections block before submission, even though local transcript retention can persist independently of the stateless API contract. Cache TTL is provider prompt-cache policy, not a session deadline. These restrictions must be separated from synthetic run limits before removing them; this audit makes no external claim about all current provider features.\n- Repair direction: negotiate exact adapter mappings and show unsupported choices before a run starts; retain local state and route replay without inventing provider resume guarantees. Preserve provider-required wire constraints while removing synthetic orchestration policy. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8e