idence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFWu3JL1b712W10SmHxeAkUZE0oCNvOR5ZN/p1sJk9BdoZFkgzfzy0cWhOMVgdmbROgHjweLI51Gq4mNmX5DaAg="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3001,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.751500536Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"e9f3a800-3ddb-594a-b1a9-b7fa69931b9e","title":"[L483] Anthropic terminal publication suppresses errors detected later in the same parsed batch","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L483.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/model/peritus-provider-anthropic/src/stream.rs:66-99`, `src/stream.rs:109-162`, `src/stream/state.rs:128-130`, `src/stream/state.rs:191-216`, `src/stream/message.rs:63-73` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: message stop immediately marks state terminal and queues completion. A later event in the parsed batch is rejected; the outer fail function refuses to emit failure once state is terminal and drains the original completion. It then stops reading the body. Cancellation also leaves queued output untouched when normalization already reached terminal, even if the caller has not yet consumed it.\n- Consequence: the declared rejection of post-terminal input is silently suppressed and cancellation behavior follows internal buffering rather than the public delivery boundary. This is the same class of terminal ownership gap as L479, with suppression instead of a hidden second terminal. No timeout is needed to fix it.\n- Repair direction: share a defined terminal publication/cancellation boundary across adapters, validate already parsed input before publication, and preserve exactly one observable terminal outcome. Add whole-chunk, split-chunk and cancellation-after-buffering cases when repair is authorized. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAA