w operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQH1KewnKWo8CrfSbAXYDRghOWur4Jga6tFf28t2iGrvPpyaYN/OK+o64GG3jXLJW6Y4TTALNcyeN57kOKbtPQQY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3003,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.757255876Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"041b1240-69e7-558c-ac25-0655150f6489","title":"[L484] Anthropic thinking signatures are limited to one delta and tool argument progress is buffered until block closure","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L484.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/model/peritus-provider-anthropic/src/stream/content.rs:108-188`, `src/stream/state.rs:21-36`, `src/stream_tests.rs:84-105`, `src/stream_tests.rs:146-158` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: a thinking block accepts exactly one signature delta and requires it before close; a second signature delta fails regardless of combined size. Tool argument deltas are accumulated under the production argument limit and emit only heartbeats until content-block stop, when the whole argument is completed/healed and then emitted. Existing thinking fixtures use one signature and cancellation is tested before any buffering.\n- Consequence: one-delta cardinality is a synthetic normalization restriction distinct from a byte budget; fragmented signature input cannot be assembled. A long unfinished tool argument can make semantic argument progress invisible while the stream remains alive. This is a source-level contract limitation, not a claim that a live Anthropic response currently emits multiple signature deltas.\n- Repair direction: accumulate bounded signature fragments with explicit completion semantics, and publish accountable argument progress without authorizing execution until the complete validated call closes. Test buffering and fragmentation rather than only the smallest happy-path shape. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIfFz8Qddw+Cbnx5gs8s9n1EXeqMmezxez/rP1hBLuw6bm3YZ9S/j4WFlEEBRgaUlXxoYFOajmNzc1/g+7LxqgM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3004,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.760854765Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"041b1240-69e7-558c-ac25-0655150f6489","comment_uuid":"a7d7e032-2e19-4890-9a48-b8e019c90e14","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L484: Anthropic thinking signatures are limited to one delta and tool argument progress is buffered until block closure.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/model/peritus-provider-anthropic/src/stream/content.rs:108-188; src/stream/state.rs:21-36; src/stream_tests.rs:84-105; src/stream_tests.rs:146-158. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\naccumulate bounded signature fragments with explicit completion semantics, and publish accountable argument progress without authorizing execution until the complete validated call closes. Test buffering and fragmentation rather than only the smallest happy-path shape. No tests run.\n\nPreserve: definitely-unaccepted versus ambiguously-accepted request state, exact native thread/profile identity, ordered provider observations, tool-result protocol, explicit cancellation and real provider/model capabilities. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNjx2Qd+Qx9Z140Gm6vg/NDSpTWvIJ1zsuyqhzzOIaW8BUvipTFP8F+OzTqLK6x1VDp3Iu4OY5MXJEuGNi8tagw="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3005,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.763521368Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"d3d14313-5879-58eb-9428-6fc375073044","title":"[L486] Google gateway routing accepts an Interactions configuration that loses its gateway prefix, and discovery uses beta despite stable-only documentation","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L486.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/model/peritus-provider-google/src/config.rs:57-78`, `src/request.rs:67-75`, `src/client.rs:205-231`, `src/client_tests.rs:176-211`, `README.md:3-12`; `crates/model/peritus-provider-core/src/endpoint.rs:76-89`, `src/catalog/http.rs:12-14`, `src/catalog/http.rs:61-149`.\n- Behavior: the gateway constructor accepts either Google dialect at the two exact OpenCode prefixes. Generate concatenates that prefix, while Interactions calls with_path, which replaces it with /v1/interactions. Only Generate gateway routing is tested. Discovery calls /v1beta/models?pageSize=1000 despite the README saying beta is never used. Shared discovery paginates but fails the whole inventory above 16 pages, 4 MiB per page, 16 MiB total or the catalog entry bound; it exposes no resumable partial inventory.\n- Consequence: an accepted configuration can submit to an unintended route and block inference. Discovery has different version/routing behavior from inference and all-or-nothing capacity gates. Page size 1000 is a request size, not the entire catalog ceiling. No actual gateway/network failure is claimed.\n- Repair direction: encode route family and gateway prefix in one validated endpoint contract, reject unsupported dialects during construction, keep discovery version policy explicit, and make large catalogs resumable. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPfx8Hhv+Q97Snu43FxSqza2TVaocXLQPgOsIUgd6lTEbipIzcE6dVx3GmoWYYEClk08aPXLJElOJfJmD5DUkQ0="}
