ce and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQK7yB/L6Of1xLgC6YRylQRxbKMyFdXloSc5rpJYyf6968UWUs+HO4TQB7eRZNas4uDLXO8dsJVLc5X+GYWhGzww="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3011,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.780313496Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"8eb80890-fa88-5fdb-83c8-b81c6c44def5","title":"[L489] Google streams repeat compiled deduplication and terminal-publication ceilings, and repeated cache observations hit a separate 64-event gate","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L489.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/model/peritus-provider-google/src/stream/state.rs:81-109`, `src/stream/state.rs:124-147`, `src/stream.rs:75-108`, `src/stream.rs:118-170`, `src/stream/generate.rs:84-100`, `src/stream/value.rs:100-104`; `crates/model/peritus-model-protocol/src/reducer/events.rs:46-57`.\n- Behavior: the adapter retains at most 4096 SSE identities, fails on a conflicting reused id, and has no eviction/configurable replay horizon. Completion is marked internally before delivery; a malformed later parsed frame is detected but fail suppresses it once terminal, and cancellation leaves already normalized terminal output queued. Generate emits a cache-hit observation on every usage-bearing chunk with a positive cached-token count; the reducer rejects observation 65.\n- Consequence: a long valid identified/cached stream can fail on local compiled counts, and a known malformed suffix can still be reported as completion. Cache observations do not represent 64 independent cache resources or expiring sessions; repeated accounting alone consumes the gate. These are source-derived conditions, not a measured live Google failure.\n- Repair direction: unify terminal publication/cancellation boundaries, use explicit deduplication horizons, and retain cumulative/high-water cache observations without a fatal append-only count. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGh6KMRuXwDy3Kq6/FTWDl+u9mNUjzqNXfSkYXpBGr0xj5eikEhRqTkfUVkdDNg6X2QOrxFCOBRSOITygPR+rwg="}
