om authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQONr/WUIvSLCkvqNiuR//g2alM+GV9DBBwMrbUEPquK+F16j4g+EXkk35GrAFQhvTj3kRe6vsF0HJ+9pu3FO7gk="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3017,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.796844625Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"519c1861-653f-581b-b413-68a2902486a0","title":"[L492] Anthropic and Google reuse one provider frame identity for multiple normalized events, causing C5 to discard required semantics as duplicates","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L492.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/model/peritus-provider-anthropic/src/stream/state.rs:108-124`, `src/stream/state.rs:191-216`, `src/stream/message.rs:33-42`; `crates/model/peritus-provider-google/src/stream/state.rs:81-120`, `src/stream/interactions.rs:142-163`, `src/stream/interactions.rs:322-335`, `fixtures/v1/interactions_success.sse:19-21`, `fixtures/v1/interactions_tool_thinking.sse:21-39`; `crates/model/peritus-model-protocol/src/reducer/stream.rs:51-83`, `src/reducer/stream.rs:152-172`, `src/reducer/events.rs:146-183`, `src/reducer/terminal.rs:73-90`.\n- Behavior: all semantic events expanded from a provider frame inherit the same SSE id and raw digest. C5 records the first and treats subsequent matching ids/digests with the next local sequence as duplicates, advancing sequence but skipping application. Google tool step start therefore keeps ItemStarted and discards ToolCallStarted; later arguments have no registered call. An identified Google completion frame starts with Usage, so its cache/Finish/ResponseCompleted events are skipped. Anthropic start metadata/usage expanded under one id is similarly discarded. Compatible explicitly binds identity only to its first expanded event, demonstrating a different contract.\n- Consequence: provider-frame identity and normalized-event identity are conflated. An otherwise valid stream can fail tool assembly or finish EOF as incomplete; metadata/accounting can disappear. The Google corpus already includes these identified frames, but the adapter qualification collects raw normalized events rather than applying C5 reduction. This is a cross-module source diagnosis, not a test run or proof of the current native executable lockup.\n- Repair direction: deduplicate provider frames once before expansion; give normalized children stable distinct identities or bind provider identity only to the first child under an explicit shared contract. Qualify the complete adapter-to-reducer-to-next-request path. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEayASb6NwuoBsx3hlT8iymLSkZzjOzCyBnoFFZhdzzlv4Gb+oA1JyFBZS0l9j/ZP2cLh4PaAlgg1Xj2weIR2gE="}
