n under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMd4alp1k3FFATMbmlEy07CMq+AbDKjDiH5QeesNUjZEM23r0ItsOYExwwufv5bzUoPR+yhFRBbP2x2CFXIwYwQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3019,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.802664469Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"a0ad88c4-b932-5990-9a0d-3165f120234c","title":"[L494] OpenAI exact-resume cursor does not restore stream assembly state","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L494.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/model/peritus-provider-openai/src/client.rs:103-115,257-302`; `src/request.rs:1-221`; `src/stream.rs:47-73`; `src/stream/state.rs:38-85`; `src/stream/decode.rs:109-120`; `src/stream/output.rs:117-176,197-249`; `src/stream/terminal.rs:155-167` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: resume admission requires an observed/restored response identifier and sequence, and the request sends `starting_after`. Every resulting stream nevertheless starts local sequence zero and an empty `ResponseState`: no started response identity, last provider sequence, item/part map, tool input, or accumulated text. Restoring a persisted continuation adds only its response identifier to the admission set. Selecting a model composes a new client with a new admission set.\n- Consequence: suffix events for a previously started response cannot pass lifecycle, item, part, or terminal validation unless the provider replays all prerequisite state. Replaying creation into a fresh decoder also does not establish continuity with the prior normalized reducer. This is an exact-resume contract gap in the direct Responses adapter, not a demonstrated cause of the installed native Codex lockup.\n- Repair direction: persist and restore the decoder/reducer state and sequence boundary together, or explicitly reconcile a provider snapshot before admitting suffix events. Model selection and client reconstruction must retain the durable response authority. Verify disconnects inside text, reasoning, and tool arguments through the production reducer. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGnMhXy/tp25HLshsl17cjEKmGGxRfXhayPZ1ZTddZeOXvaV3YNONKVlH+JlzSxlERit6XPyRDUuKsSLVKYGpQY="}
