{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3021,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.808032936Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"60f77db6-2697-505b-9d54-48d83a440bf4","title":"[L495] OpenAI background response registration silently stops after 4096 identities","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L495.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/model/peritus-provider-openai/src/stream/terminal.rs:28-36`; `src/client.rs:65-115,283-302`; `src/client/cancel.rs:93-127` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: a newly created background response is inserted into a process-local set only while its length is below 4096. Reaching the bound produces no failure or warning. Completion does not retire identities; successful confirmed cancellation removes one. Persisted-continuation restoration inserts identities through a separate path without this bound. New client/model composition resets the set.\n- Consequence: later background responses can run successfully but become locally ineligible for exact resume or confirmed cancellation. The inconsistent restoration path also means the numeric cap is not a consistent resource bound. This is a lifetime registration limiter, not a session TTL.\n- Repair direction: replace the ephemeral admission cache with durable response records and explicit active/terminal lifecycle reconciliation; capacity pressure must not silently revoke an already accepted response's resume/cancellation rights. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQD8QcquXqgCo3626jWrGFQRT