{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3023,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.812406626Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"9fa03809-149d-5858-ae50-38cfd4dacd39","title":"[L496] OpenAI terminal queue can hide malformed suffixes and defer local cancellation","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L496.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/model/peritus-provider-openai/src/stream.rs:104-152,183-198,230-275`; `src/stream/decode.rs:11-64`; `src/stream/terminal.rs:50-80` in the same crate; the previously read provider-core owned stream terminal boundary.\n- Behavior: an entire parsed SSE batch is decoded before queued normalized events are returned. A malformed frame after a completion in that batch appends `ResponseFailed` behind the queued completion. The owned stream stops at its first terminal event. Pending events are also popped before the underlying body is asked to observe cancellation.\n- Consequence: an already discovered suffix contradiction can be invisible to consumers, depending on transport chunk boundaries. Buffered events can continue to be delivered after local cancellation. This repeats the terminal-publication boundary problem recorded for the other adapters; it is not an idle timeout.\n- Repair direction: validate the batch before publishing completion, define one consistent policy for contradictory terminal suffixes, and apply cancellation at the event-delivery boundary. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFBQEUj/GuNQS/LqZeLt66ROv/D4qx7thFfER