{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3025,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.817549909Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"7911061b-dd41-5c1d-8eb2-8da35b0e2f73","title":"[L497] OpenAI request admission and whole-value encoding expose secondary blockers","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L497.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/model/peritus-provider-openai/src/config.rs:1-218`; `src/profile.rs:1-67`; `src/client.rs:173-183`; `src/request/input.rs:14-51,54-60,153-228`; `src/request/options.rs:13-37,62-78,114-137` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: the adapter fixes HTTP/framing/protocol bounds and defaults to three attempts, 100 ms base delay, 2 s maximum delay/Retry-After, and 64 MiB cumulative request bytes with no elapsed deadline. Exact capability profiles reject unknown or unsupported extension declarations. Sampling seed/stops are unsupported; parallel-call allowance must equal the negotiated maximum; prompt-cache ephemeral TTL must be exactly 1800 seconds. Input validation does not reject unresolved Peritus-artifact media or non-UTF-8 reasoning replay, which can fail during encoding after credential resolution. Whole messages, schemas, tool results, and inline-media base64 are materialized before HTTP byte admission.\n- Consequence: removing elapsed deadlines leaves finite retry and serialization/admission blockers. Valid protocol objects can fail later projection or exceed encoded HTTP bounds through escaping/base64 expansion. The 30-minute value governs provider prompt-cache projection; it does not expire local sessions. A provider-specific capability/schema requirement is distinct from an arbitrary local execution deadline.\n- Repair direction: carry explicit unlimited/replenishable retry semantics, validate projection requirements before credential resolution, resolve artifact references through the media boundary, and admit encoded representations consistently with protocol bounds. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIsn94LqmcV2ng5WElI4GxDkt4fGE/hnWi0RFiG9jjNilUmcXdcw0VxUHtx7TrpHhCqTwS0BQuxHgvc23WAC8ww="}
