{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3027,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.822181850Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"b7a881a6-26c2-5920-a3f3-24527bbac51e","title":"[L498] OpenAI optional metadata and whole error bodies can block response classification","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L498.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/model/peritus-provider-openai/src/client.rs:212-257`; `src/client/response.rs:12-27`; `src/client/cancel.rs:38-89`; `src/stream/metadata.rs:21-35,47-96,173-250` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: rejected requests and cancellation replies are read to EOF under the fixed response byte bound before status handling. Optional request identifiers over 512 bytes, numeric/reset/retry headers over 64 bytes, invalid UTF-8, or inconsistent rate windows raise local errors. Retry parsing accepts integer milliseconds/seconds up to one day, ignores other formats, and the default 2 s retry policy can reject otherwise parsed delays. Reset parsing accepts integer unit groups up to seven days; unsupported fractional forms are ignored. Successful SSE responses can be rejected by optional metadata parsing before a stream is handed to the caller.\n- Consequence: a stalled error body delays a known status until cancellation, while optional observations or Retry-After policy errors can displace the useful provider failure or accepted response. Reset and Retry-After values are metadata/retry policy, not local session expiry timers.\n- Repair direction: publish the known status/acceptance first, consume diagnostics incrementally, and isolate optional metadata errors from response correctness while honoring provider backoff without an arbitrary 2 s ceiling. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCn4JItQ+tnx0aFtBz+zZn8KsT+JQF/uotQHmVPD1zJVgvExIwinOy3MXiiElFwFw7WbsYN62Nk44424VIIRaQ4="}
