nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMKYagpb3FD2rz5nuDed2YOGyQNpecXkBr5Y8bo10W9TaRuhOtXhNxjLa7qggF2rDYVC0IMSh4/myP9mYYPbzg0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3033,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.836715892Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"aee826dc-47f2-5158-850f-9fdb56b7762e","title":"[L503] MCP task completion and disconnect handling lack active-session reconciliation","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L503.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/extensions/peritus-mcp/src/server.rs:130-177,180-265`.\n- Behavior: request tasks are added to a JoinSet and joined only after the input loop ends; completed tasks accumulate throughout a long-lived connection. Clean EOF does not signal cancellation or abort active requests before waiting for every task. Writer failures are not selected alongside the input loop. A panicked request skips active-map removal, while task errors/panics are observed only after EOF. The server context/lifecycle is process-local and initialization is permitted exactly once.\n- Consequence: a disconnected client can leave shutdown waiting indefinitely on bridge work, an idle reader can delay detection of a failed writer, and a panicked request can leave its identifier permanently classified active on the surviving connection. Long-lived sessions retain completed-task bookkeeping. These are ownership/reconciliation gaps; the absence of an arbitrary deadline is not itself the defect.\n- Repair direction: reap completions while serving, react to writer/disconnect events, clean active identifiers through owned guards, and reconcile admitted work with durable daemon session authority before closing or reconnecting. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJ5WFqdRbF+QBXza5tOPKcteA52snZXfRBVzAGUm1dYLXMTUT8hsp3Fhkb/Bnvv165cB0Hn29VDUJfshac5OZA8="}
