{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3035,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.841258889Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"5c7b8afe-20df-5442-8973-5d44f7bc56b3","title":"[L504] MCP strict protocol and post-result serialization bounds can terminate a usable connection","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L504.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/extensions/peritus-mcp/src/protocol.rs:7-8,19-29,60-225`; `src/jsonrpc.rs:26-79`; `src/server.rs:97-108,317-354,378-436,467-509`; `src/framing.rs:7-42,45-67`; `src/bridge.rs:93-167` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: only protocol version 2025-06-18 is admitted; DTOs reject unknown fields. Client/server identities are nonempty and at most 128 bytes, instructions at most 16 KiB, tool/prompt names at most 128 bytes without controls, and resource URI at most 4096 bytes. Requests and responses must fit the same configured message limit. A whole bridge result is converted/serialized before response-size rejection, which fails the writer rather than returning a per-request bounded result. Public resource/prompt projection DTOs described as bounded do not enforce per-field bounds. List pagination first obtains the entire bridge collection, then slices it using an unversioned numeric offset into the current collection.\n- Consequence: richer protocol metadata can be rejected; a successful large resource/tool result can close response delivery after the operation has already completed. Count pagination does not bound page bytes or avoid full collection allocation, and concurrent collection changes can skip/repeat entries. These format/version/resource boundaries are distinct from local deadlines.\n- Repair direction: negotiate supported protocol versions, preserve forward-compatible metadata where safe, enforce projection limits before effect/whole allocation, page at the authority source with a stable snapshot cursor, and return bounded per-request failures without taking down the writer. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKzB3D2bHQzHVNzk3TDKRPqZ8IQ1JSpCEXhcsvBv4uArzFtsPYqA6RTVEcZGHuUJumCO84mgmzsck3L99ZrT1ws="}
