ts together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAmvDJeS58G0w8qomy3JM/RxLS+rMFAHMHPew/gD9q/mNDDFnGyvED+lxoRJfZzRsaoRJw5yl8OdrNXPaouwewg="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3037,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.846586504Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"66356dca-0d9a-53fa-af67-36afbef4bad3","title":"[L505] MCP error shortening can panic at a Unicode boundary","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L505.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/extensions/peritus-mcp/src/error.rs:54-62,137-144`; `src/jsonrpc.rs:148-158`; `src/server.rs:204-209,498-501,512-527`; `tests/server.rs:249-286` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: bridge codes/details use String::truncate at byte offsets 128/1024, MCP details at 1024, and JSON-RPC failure messages at 512. No character-boundary adjustment is made. A longer UTF-8 value whose character spans the chosen offset causes truncate to panic instead of producing a typed error. Parser/bridge details can contain input-derived strings. Tests cover cooperative cancellation with a one-second test guard and one malformed ASCII frame, but not Unicode truncation, response backpressure, hung disconnect, or panic cleanup.\n- Consequence: the diagnostic limiter can itself panic the reader/request path, interacting with L503's stale active-id and cleanup behavior. This is a source diagnosis, not a executed crash reproduction.\n- Repair direction: truncate on verified character boundaries and preserve task/session cleanup under any diagnostic failure; qualify the real control and disconnect paths. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMHTD0jz0MbtIDuS135yyf6avkNedykOeqfaCkfo0dRk++khxjh7X2Rk8ZTEUy0qnyKevVcBVAp79FS5k4sdigU="}
