ther; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQA3pBTgBVV2Cg720PzHsnQzTXhupEPSNnQz1VGUYOgLSuqbmcdEoAZ15BwhPkF62ptDJ4PZNWXwDNOXuet2otw8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3041,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.855965743Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"f441d325-5bc6-59f3-ac72-981cb3544a55","title":"[L507] Plugin payload and frame constructors disagree with fixed deserialization limits","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L507.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/extensions/peritus-plugin-sdk/src/payload.rs:21-65,89-105,108-159`; `src/canonical.rs:8-78`; `src/framing.rs:15-54`; `src/protocol/wire.rs:5-58`; `src/protocol/request_wire.rs:41-74`; `src/protocol/response_wire.rs:96-134` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: production JSON limits are 1 MiB canonical/input bytes, depth 32, 16384 total members/elements, and 256 KiB per key/string. New/parse accept caller-provided bounds, but every Serde deserialize forces production bounds. All floating-point values are rejected. Payload validation/canonical rendering traverses complete Value trees; protocol serialization converts nested payloads into fresh Value trees and frame encoding allocates the whole JSON before enforcing its positive u32 frame maximum. Duplicate JSON members are already collapsed by Value parsing, so canonicalization cannot establish their original uniqueness.\n- Consequence: a payload created under broader bounds can encode successfully but fail on decode despite an enlarged frame quota. Legitimate decimal-valued tool inputs/results fail this plugin representation. Whole-value conversion/canonicalization and escaping can produce a late frame-bound failure after earlier logical admission; widening frame bytes does not widen payload admission.\n- Repair direction: bind consistent recursive/payload/frame policies to both encoding and decoding, choose a documented numeric domain suitable for tool results, and enforce duplicate/member/encoded-size correctness at the parser boundary before whole copies. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAbeL3N5r5rVfKoqyNaF62PlXjnz1ZhjSQxZh68orJ8Jch+5vLf/Pc0IT3XyfqjIHcsHwlNR5Lf+UtXvwQXBGAw="}
