er; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKmwPenJUVRjHQ8UWCC1dr0rbVzA4pk8jZogptQ64X8/9A+9BjsWSLFD/kVorRQAZCPJIvSmzb7cdcALjMfYgwg="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3043,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.860156224Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"274d1729-c83f-52c4-b2ee-f71617c29900","title":"[L508] Plugin SDK identity and diagnostic restrictions include another Unicode panic path","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L508.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/extensions/peritus-plugin-sdk/src/identity.rs:20-23,57-84,121-129,187-204`; `src/manifest.rs:55-70,278-289,362-391,485-500`; `src/error.rs:34-40`; `src/manifest/wire.rs:94-131`; `src/protocol.rs:22-38,113-125` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: plugin/capability identities are canonical lowercase hierarchical ASCII up to 128 bytes; request identifiers are 1-128 non-control UTF-8 bytes; version components are u16. Entrypoints have a 512-byte safe relative path, at most 64 arguments, and 4096 bytes per argument without NUL. Capabilities must be strictly sorted/unique with at most 256 declarations. Signature key/algorithm/signature bounds are 128/64/4096 bytes. Strict manifest/protocol DTOs reject unknown fields. Public invocation/failure text fields described as bounded are plain strings without constructors enforcing those bounds. SDK diagnostic shortening blindly truncates at byte 512, which can panic inside a longer multibyte character, including TOML/Serde input-derived errors.\n- Consequence: local identity/manifest widths impose interoperability limits; diagnostic reporting can panic instead of returning typed failure. Deserializing some subordinate manifest structs bypasses constructor validation, so complete manifest validation remains essential. These are schema/admission bounds, not elapsed timers.\n- Repair direction: keep protocol identities and validated manifest invariants explicit, preserve unknown-version negotiation where compatible, enforce DTO bounds consistently, and make diagnostic shortening Unicode-safe. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLxuFkinK3J7ILzzTpS0xPJOSfWU2M6OLw6rAcihd/Iq1hb7o1cQnbYzkuNC8Y7a6npmY4/rq5H2hfYPAz7+SAk="}
