{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3045,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.865204212Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"61d9897d-351f-5296-b52e-0e1e0165cb18","title":"[L509] Plugin host lifetime quota can be exhausted by rejected work","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L509.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/extensions/peritus-plugin-host/src/quota.rs:16-55`; `src/host.rs:153-175,230-266,407-421`; `src/authority.rs:106-133`; `src/transport.rs:145-162` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: lifetime usage increments before concurrent admission. A concurrency rejection refunds the active count but not lifetime usage. Successful completion releases only active capacity; lifetime count never refills within an instance. Exhaustion is labelled RetryLater although waiting cannot restore it. Mandatory manifest/host invocation duration drives a Tokio response-read timeout. The authority grant must carry a nonzero deadline and is forwarded to the plugin, but the host neither checks it against a clock nor uses it to narrow the invocation timeout. Host configuration/narrowed quotas are not validated on construction/start.\n- Consequence: bursts of rejected work can permanently disable an otherwise idle plugin. Zero host ceilings can produce immediate failures despite positive manifest quotas. A compulsory local duration survives the product's earlier deadline removals, while the separate purported authority deadline is not enforced consistently. No numeric production host defaults are inferred from the five-second/16-request test fixture.\n- Repair direction: make lifetime usage recoverable or explicitly unlimited, account only admitted effects and refund rejected reservations, represent untimed invocation policy end to end, and validate explicit authority/capacity semantics consistently. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLlSo2R1kTgVo3HWpjuxowgET6NwpMJ9bTmNnX4haZ8H8BILejjWDfyrw+xe5NAI/d/lT0LLSMndtjCqxsGH9gs="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3046,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.867846747Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"61d9897d-351f-5296-b52e-0e1e0165cb18","comment_uuid":"c9345ee5-fe24-4f1d-97db-d6d99657e770","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L509: Plugin host lifetime quota can be exhausted by rejected work.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/extensions/peritus-plugin-host/src/quota.rs:16-55; src/host.rs:153-175,230-266,407-421; src/authority.rs:106-133; src/transport.rs:145-162. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nmake lifetime usage recoverable or explicitly unlimited, account only admitted effects and refund rejected reservations, represent untimed invocation policy end to end, and validate explicit authority/capacity semantics consistently. No tests run.\n\nPreserve: canonical digest and schema identity, shared writer/reader admissibility, malformed-input rejection before allocation, exact causal ordering, actual provider/OS capability boundaries and preserved accepted historical evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBOrbkj7grwlHlZSYOapuPRmRblyZ475RMDqRifPUt9fYi1wc/aOKPKyAktigZ2kJD96FaJSgt0cmObKUQJ8aQg="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3047,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.870131010Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"9f65a261-fa8d-59e4-ba9d-2bc93175a98d","title":"[L510] Plugin cancellation and deadline handling can hang before termination","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L510.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/extensions/peritus-plugin-host/src/transport.rs:91-162,165-219`; `src/host.rs:230-266,314-332` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: exchange first awaits a single transaction mutex, writes/flushed the complete request, and only then starts the cancellable response-read timeout. Queue wait and input writes have no cancellation select. On cancellation/timeout it awaits another full cancellation-frame write before termination. If the plugin has stopped reading stdin or the pipe is full, that write can wait indefinitely. Stop uses the same transaction and write path, so its shutdown timeout does not cover acquiring the transaction or sending shutdown.\n- Consequence: local cancellation can be blocked by a different invocation, large input, or the attempt to deliver cancellation itself. Nominal invocation/startup/shutdown deadlines cover only response reads and cannot guarantee cleanup. Removing synthetic deadlines must be paired with interruptible ownership/control progress, not a blind deletion of the only eventual response exit.\n- Repair direction: make queue/write/read ownership cancellation-aware, reserve a control path that cannot depend on the stalled plugin consuming stdin, and proceed with explicit termination/reconciliation when cooperative notification cannot progress. No tests run or hang reproduction claimed.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMsI7+ZI+LoVGTtL1vY87JtRBZd6HCfDbfemiM1yXy+61m8kTrDcvWd40+Mltr2b9b/9qtEA6dMZM6c/VW6j+w4="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3048,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.872465496Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"9f65a261-fa8d-59e4-ba9d-2bc93175a98d","comment_uuid":"aed1fd06-31d1-4652-87fc-8b6c477ff6ee","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L510: Plugin cancellation and deadline handling can hang before termination.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/extensions/peritus-plugin-host/src/transport.rs:91-162,165-219; src/host.rs:230-266,314-332. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nmake queue/write/read ownership cancellation-aware, reserve a control path that cannot depend on the stalled plugin consuming stdin, and proceed with explicit termination/reconciliation when cooperative notification cannot progress. No tests run or hang reproduction claimed.\n\nPreserve: canonical digest and schema identity, shared writer/reader admissibility, malformed-input rejection before allocation, exact causal ordering, actual provider/OS capability boundaries and preserved accepted historical evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQG9oF3NDHYkA4qSwd3YPOMzdHTz5XHMVK87ifmXqTqJ+0Djhe3+78Wi1gvuCLl4P4jgY/9C9nJIkH6DWw0qMOwk="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3049,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.874675447Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"272e2696-4c52-5ed4-abee-eff02adddba6","title":"[L511] Plugin failed-state handling and queued authority cannot support durable recovery","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L511.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/extensions/peritus-plugin-host/src/host.rs:126-135,210-273,290-305,314-357`; `src/transport.rs:58-64,97-142,165-169`; `src/quota.rs:21-32` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: all exchanges serialize through one transaction mutex despite higher concurrent-request quotas. Invocation lifecycle/authority/quota checks happen before queueing and are not rechecked after acquiring that mutex. Any exchange error, including a pre-cancelled token or request-encoding error before submission, marks the whole instance Failed; those paths need not terminate its process. Failed instances remain in the map and block start until stop removes them. Some invalid invocation status responses instead return RestartPlugin while leaving the lifecycle Ready. Registry, counters, transport handles, and lifecycle state have no persistence/reattachment API; process drop kills the child. Kill/wait errors are discarded.\n- Consequence: cancellation of unsent work can disable the entire plugin, queued work can proceed using stale lifecycle/authority observations, and requested restart is not a direct available transition. Losing the host loses the process/context and evidence needed to distinguish completed effects. Higher admission concurrency does not create parallel wire progress.\n- Repair direction: bind dispatch to fresh authority after admission, distinguish unsent cancellation from failed/possibly accepted execution, align recovery disposition with actual transitions, and journal invocation/instance identity with explicit reconnect or reconciliation semantics. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCjt+Zwf6KnmL3NqvMIANWd+i2hHegv8K/Jcvne7a9YFdy5f9+Q2/xniPu26PQK2/HrlyMENk9hKa2UoboLj8AU="}
