reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: renewal/adoption under the same authorized identity, revoked authority, stale epoch/revision, cross-scope requests, lost acknowledgements and restart, proving legitimate continuation without admitting unauthorized or duplicate effects. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEf10HlurOW4Ah/hmqgAURJQKJ5vxH6IX3iHLckf8QlrB/mNv6qitG+x52M8VHZZtDSLJEosXFSciLz4dN9ljQY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3051,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.879202553Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"9dd8d031-464f-5b08-81bf-e1385182e030","title":"[L512] Plugin discovery cardinality and whole-catalog failure can block unrelated extensions","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L512.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/extensions/peritus-plugin-host/src/discovery.rs:30-37,141-179,187-227,238-259`; `src/trust.rs:73-86`; `src/host.rs:136-155` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: production discovery permits 16 roots, 256 plugin versions, 256 KiB manifests, and 512 MiB artifacts. It collects and sorts every immediate directory entry before filtering plugins, then synchronously reads/parses each manifest and hashes each accepted artifact in 64 KiB chunks. A root I/O error, invalid manifest, duplicate identity/version, or 257th plugin returns an error for the entire catalog; no partial usable catalog is returned. The host keeps an immutable discovery snapshot. Start trust checks stored discovery digests rather than re-reading the artifact bytes before launch.\n- Consequence: one unrelated invalid/excess plugin can prevent obtaining any catalog; entry-count pagination/cancellation is absent and large discovery work is synchronous. Cached discovery/trust does not establish the current bytes at dispatch. Exact trust verification itself is an integrity boundary, not an artificial deadline to delete.\n- Repair direction: expose per-plugin diagnostics and a recoverable catalog, perform bounded incremental discovery with stable current artifact identity, and retain explicit trust admission while removing unrelated catalog-wide blockers. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFW09EKNet9YRjjBn+kuHkA1Zz4hwAS9G8yCP+bjWZXYP+hYkhtoBDDlgvYSS+V6c1pULIYWhvPqLcB3ufxRnQM="}
