it frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQICu95TV6Hm6MIlEcvtje6LuReVPJmpucnjHusV3JXbd7Pw6XvRMBVtn/fSLfL+yn76PrrLuo1Kqe3ZmDzTmhwc="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3055,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.888618474Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"9231726b-e75a-533b-9589-5191ad65bd9f","title":"[L514] Telemetry queues impose finite item counts and bounded shutdown flushing","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L514.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/observe/peritus-telemetry/src/buffer/mod.rs:17-55`, `src/buffer/state.rs:105-186`, `src/export/pump.rs:83-139`, `src/export/types.rs`.\n- Behavior: Capacity and batch size are mandatory positive counts, capacity cannot exceed 1,000,000 items, and overflow can reject newest or drop oldest. There is no spill path or wait for capacity. Enqueue constructs the encoded prefix before rejecting a new record. Capacity counts records, not their encoded bytes. Shutdown attempts at most the caller-selected batch count and returns Pending with queued records retained when that count is exhausted. Export and exporter shutdown are synchronous calls without a cancellation channel.\n- Consequence: These controls can discard or reject observational records and can stall an exporter caller indefinitely. A large record still has large memory cost inside a small item-count queue. This crate's documented observational role does not establish that these controls themselves cancel agent work; that requires caller evidence. No telemetry session TTL is introduced here.\n- Repair direction: Separate loss policy, memory accounting, durable spill and explicit drain progress from agent execution authority. A finite flush count must preserve an actionable continuation. Synchronous exporters need an ownership and cancellation contract rather than an assumed timer guarantee. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFJ4uiQaj7YlkMQfHIoK56LqawnAVDEpOcTeV4yad9asZgPCUu5LRN+3VJbHwD1G+ip5lolV/RH7vdqtXfDPOwY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3056,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.891145291Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"9231726b-e75a-533b-9589-5191ad65bd9f","comment_uuid":"329ef7e2-1c60-466b-9ff1-62f29ab503b0","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L514: Telemetry queues impose finite item counts and bounded shutdown flushing.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/observe/peritus-telemetry/src/buffer/mod.rs:17-55; src/buffer/state.rs:105-186; src/export/pump.rs:83-139; src/export/types.rs. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nSeparate loss policy, memory accounting, durable spill and explicit drain progress from agent execution authority. A finite flush count must preserve an actionable continuation. Synchronous exporters need an ownership and cancellation contract rather than an assumed timer guarantee. No tests run.\n\nPreserve: canonical digest and schema identity, shared writer/reader admissibility, malformed-input rejection before allocation, exact causal ordering, actual provider/OS capability boundaries and preserved accepted historical evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFCAqKMZx+kRN1bUWXWbLdo4EXCuqaeImBZJwBnzBPcxo1nh+vDAZGHAytoL5L03wLUbffUN9tgLeLAnoj3sDgk="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3057,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.893342050Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"569363fb-fc6d-5177-a660-1002c24dc3bc","title":"[L515] Failed telemetry export batches are rebuilt rather than pinned for retry","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L515.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/observe/peritus-telemetry/src/export/pump.rs:83-109`, `src/buffer/state.rs:105-186`, `src/export/types.rs`, `tests/buffering_export.rs:42-63`.\n- Behavior: A pump reads a fresh prefix of the current queue for every flush. It does not retain the exact previously failed batch. Enqueue after a failure can extend a partially full batch; DropOldest can evict records in the failed batch. Batch identity includes record sequence/content, so these changes produce a different batch identity. Exact acknowledgements are checked before retirement, which is a necessary integrity guard.\n- Consequence: The stated exact-batch retry behavior is not preserved across intervening enqueue. If remote acceptance happened before acknowledgement loss, rebuilding a different batch cannot by itself establish idempotent batch retry. Event-level downstream deduplication may compensate, but is not proved here. The test retries a full two-record batch without interleaved enqueue.\n- Repair direction: Persist a pending export batch and its acknowledgement identity until resolved, and define how overflow interacts with records already in flight. Test acknowledgement loss plus interleaved enqueue and overflow. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEe