ce and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQF5grEZeLTmiaV3Or25J9pIsNIZmQaohoPcaF82cr8YCHjfWw07evqbfr1aJ5fZjraJlupv3k2xVg22O+g+dEAg="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3059,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.897811358Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"57380ae2-752e-5992-8ca1-47c06867c2a2","title":"[L516] Telemetry projection and checkpoint recovery replay whole trace histories","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L516.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/observe/peritus-telemetry/src/projection.rs:148-233`, `src/recovery.rs:42-98`, `src/metrics.rs:155-172`.\n- Behavior: Projection collects and globally sorts observations, then scans each trace's observations again for each ended span and clones associated diagnostics into that span. Diagnostics also remain standalone records. Recovery takes a complete projection, re-encodes and hashes the prefix from genesis to verify the checkpoint, then enqueues the entire suffix under the queue's current overflow policy.\n- Consequence: Work grows with spans multiplied by observations plus sorting and copying; this is source-derived complexity, not a measured live stall. Recovery has no incremental cursor or cooperative cancellation in this layer. A smaller queue can reject or drop historical telemetry during recovery, with explicit counts. Checked metric counters are observational accounting, not agent execution quotas.\n- Repair direction: Use durable verified projection cursors and per-span indexes, and preserve replay progress across capacity pressure. Define recovery loss separately from execution recovery. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5A