blication/restore, then reopen and continue the same conversation with an exact restored workspace. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBYfPS7DT49DjEnBC04ra7vwVAtPCN3BYqQ6Mnns7poMW6mwBfMbMUlWNC2Z5lHoDYLu/cGKNYVFBKXznr5RwQw="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3061,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.902343348Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"95144790-1dc4-55db-bc6d-2702aa0d3a54","title":"[L517] The newest telemetry checkpoint can block recovery despite retained older checkpoints","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L517.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/observe/peritus-telemetry/src/storage.rs:20-21`, `src/storage.rs:105-109`, `src/storage.rs:151-224`, `src/storage.rs:318-362`, `tests/checkpoint_recovery.rs:171-189`.\n- Behavior: The store selects the highest checkpoint filename sequence and decodes only that file. A corrupt or incorrectly bound newest file fails loading without trying a retained older checkpoint. V1 checkpoints are rejected; V2 is an exact 152-byte format. Retention must be positive. Opening the store cleans matching temporary files under a single-owner assumption. Persisted identical checkpoints can retry finalization; mismatched content at the same sequence is rejected.\n- Consequence: Retaining older valid checkpoints does not supply a usable recovery fallback on the newest-file failure path. Format, binding and checksum checks are integrity requirements; removing those checks would not repair recoverability. Windows directory syncing is a no-op in this implementation, so the Unix durability path cannot certify Windows power-loss behavior.\n- Repair direction: Preserve quarantine diagnostics for a bad newest checkpoint while selecting an older verified checkpoint and replaying the journal suffix. Make format migration and ownership explicit. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLbSAekHrd6LD9DOaDyyecPRYhmJOxjgcKL91/S+dSPH2mzZJRWM3bXnlKQYAoq8ngu7UP5EdBCUdj3kpPxB6wI="}
