eptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIhERQmuAUQDj9kFaOxMPxkCJPlvVFQZzhPXYKSDsZKOtmZ6a338/rz7I4Y/OHMSkogLO9wKg2X4chFpaShsfgA="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3065,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.912665611Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"50f37338-4ef4-53f8-9151-93bf0dd099e8","title":"[L520] Trace recording treats wall-clock regression as an invalid lifecycle transition","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L520.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/observe/peritus-trace/src/domain/observation.rs:13-35`, `src/projection/fold.rs:70-94`, `src/error.rs:197-212`, `tests/support/mod.rs:23-48`.\n- Behavior: Wall nanoseconds and monotonic ticks must both be nonzero. Every subsequent observation in a span must have both values greater than or equal to the previous observation. A lower wall timestamp is rejected even with an advancing monotonic tick. The fixtures give wall time and monotonic time the same increasing integer.\n- Consequence: A normal backward wall-clock correction can fail observational recording. A monotonic counter reset across restart also needs an explicit generation/continuation contract; retaining a span alone does not establish that contract. This is a source-derived rejection path, not a diagnosis of the installed session. The previously documented caller paths that propagate trace errors make such recording failures relevant to daily use.\n- Repair direction: Preserve wall timestamps as descriptive facts while ordering transitions through durable sequence and a monotonic generation. Record clock discontinuities without turning them into execution authority. Test backward wall correction with forward causal progress and restart with a new monotonic origin. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAA