w operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNlhYziadvyXpZ6eSB8P6cN6ptjHCbkq227oSwHhwYGcyXN8ChZQedxD/a8ek9NN+5EPZBA0PQxoZ9cwvL7T8ws="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3067,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.917423360Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"225a0b86-77fe-5b82-9036-2abce802d21a","title":"[L521] Every new durable trace observation replays the complete aggregate history","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L521.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/observe/peritus-trace/src/storage.rs:102-119`, `src/projection/state.rs:263-295`, `src/projection/encoding.rs:10-71`, `src/recovery.rs:28-66`.\n- Behavior: Each new record loads every earlier observation in that trace, rebuilds its projection from genesis, and then validates the candidate. Applying each observation clones the current complete span map for failure atomicity. Observations retain both the decoded domain value and canonical frame bytes; event identities and spans are not retired. Projection encoding and invariant hashing copy the entire accumulated projection. Single-trace recovery loads the complete chain; all-trace recovery integrity-exports the entire journal.\n- Consequence: One replay costs observations multiplied by current span count in the worst case; repeated append can compound that cost. There is no incremental projection cursor, chunked recovery, cancellation or progress callback in these paths. This is complexity derived from the code, not measured latency. Keeping sessions persistent will expose growing history rather than eliminating this cost.\n- Repair direction: Maintain a durable validated projection head and apply only journal suffixes, use narrowly staged mutations for failure atomicity, and preserve resumable replay progress. Exact committed-command replay already resolves before history replay and should remain idempotent. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAfD2HMekuU8GUSEcH/90w5EEpodt1oHSyvLmpu9mz5dIU3PCvDJzCs0qEnGoYLaNh/9PXySccdhgQG6NWv1DAM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3068,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.919616212Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"225a0b86-77fe-5b82-9036-2abce802d21a","comment_uuid":"b15dc0ac-d102-4091-bbac-63535192600f","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L521: Every new durable trace observation replays the complete aggregate history.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/observe/peritus-trace/src/storage.rs:102-119; src/projection/state.rs:263-295; src/projection/encoding.rs:10-71; src/recovery.rs:28-66. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nMaintain a durable validated projection head and apply only journal suffixes, use narrowly staged mutations for failure atomicity, and preserve resumable replay progress. Exact committed-command replay already resolves before history replay and should remain idempotent. No tests run.\n\nPreserve: exact candidate revision and artifact binding, complete finding/provenance conservation, independent reviewer evidence, truthful gate outcomes, protected user constraints and acceptance fail-closed on invalid evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDqRtTLpWipvlxw44UhK7MFBJFbAiQnfx8GyYSM6vZbMMouZw4I7AAZRwyitVk8R06Nv5SEzK7lGIuSyxWAmJwQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3069,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.922510380Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"9f40fada-dae8-5976-a476-a19dbffe79e4","title":"[L522] Trace causal contracts require the exact latest event and classify missing predecessors as terminal integrity","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L522.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/observe/peritus-trace/src/projection/fold.rs:23-39`, `src/projection/fold.rs:63-79`, `src/projection/state.rs:255-307`, `src/projection/mod.rs:60-74`, `src/error.rs:197-212`.\n- Behavior: A child must start under an open parent and explicitly name that parent's current latest event. A span advance must name its exact predecessor and preserve its binding and parent. All declared predecessors must already exist in the same trace; trace session identity cannot change. A missing or superseded parent predecessor is CausalIntegrity, whose recovery class is TerminalIntegrity. Projection folding maps every trace failure to journal repair guidance.\n- Consequence: A caller holding an observation built before another parent update can receive terminal-integrity guidance for a stale observational plan. There is no trace-local reobserve/replan distinction for that case. Exact ordering, duplicate-content binding and session association are necessary correctness contracts; they do not require treating every stale caller plan as corrupt authoritative history.\n- Repair direction: Separate stale-plan rejection before commit from invalid committed history during replay, with actionable reobservation for the former. Preserve immutable committed identity and exact duplicate resolution. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLWYzlbeFfHwUIICTG7N0V+DIH23+RxrBEZcTQwxXMvj45fUGqrUUAw4SZ8NAP4k04q4FwnisOKrhj5zZ6z/4Ak="}
