sor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGzbVP+2xkefCdkP8yl6hJMIEg3XUAzmQ70yND4S+Fg4+jQp9ZsaZNq6CBFOtR/Scsu+E5nxJw73DSzn9Gzk6QQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3071,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.927376860Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"520a8050-37ad-5645-a621-6d102f151715","title":"[L525] Git command byte ceilings fail whole operations and do not bound their duration","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L525.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-git/src/command.rs:12-13`, `src/command.rs:108-137`, `src/command.rs:213-249`, `src/repository.rs:118-125`, `src/error.rs:6-7`.\n- Behavior: Every subprocess has a mandatory positive stdout ceiling, default 16 MiB and hard maximum 64 MiB. Stderr is capped at the smaller of that ceiling and 16 KiB, then a failed-command diagnostic retains at most 4,096 bytes. Reader threads keep draining to EOF after detecting overflow. The owner waits for process exit, then joins the stdin writer and both readers, before returning an error for excess output. The overflow error has Quarantine recovery guidance even when the command exited successfully.\n- Consequence: A large status/diff/worktree/config response or noisy stderr can reject a completed operation. Output retention is bounded, but execution and pipe completion are not: no cancellation channel, process ownership handoff or continuation exists here. Reader/writer failure is observed after the blocking process wait and can strand that wait if a pipe stops being drained. There is no production elapsed timer in this adapter.\n- Repair direction: Treat observation size as paged or streamed data and retain exact completion identity for mutating operations. Provide cancellation and pipe/process supervision through owned execution, without replacing this gap with an arbitrary wall deadline. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQI5opTyg6BjlioMTmfSuBUIOZPLm37v6xpTbcVFOInxaAcsUV7+TthL37fcW3BzvnIGVFIUEozJ31+2YO4fqtAU="}
