y owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQA8suB71PXHA9PdezkM4AwETHVBDbvFwhYCZmAJxo+xDlFMwVzqyHlv6JZfUwkPGgUYJuBXu8swWpLreze2sLQw="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3073,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.932713683Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"aa184d88-4bb4-5115-a10c-94de3d7eb9a1","title":"[L526] Git repository admission excludes filter-configured repositories and non-UTF-8 roots","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L526.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-git/src/repository.rs:25-53`, `src/repository.rs:164-185`, `src/repository.rs:251-280`, `src/repository.rs:327-346`, `src/command.rs:77-101`, `src/command.rs:171-195`, `src/name.rs:5-32`, `src/baseline.rs:11-12`, `src/baseline.rs:78-91`.\n- Behavior: Discovery defaults to requiring the exact root; a caller can explicitly allow descendants. Canonical root/Git/common paths must be UTF-8 and are all bound into repository identity. Any configured filter.*.clean, smudge or process key is rejected before protected operations, even if no selected path uses that filter. Hooks, global/system configuration, prompting, signing and repository-selection environment are disabled. Worktree names are at most 96 bytes from an ASCII alphanumeric/dash/underscore alphabet, with leading dash and git/peritus reserved; revision expressions are nonempty, non-option-like, control-free and at most 1,024 bytes.\n- Consequence: Ordinary repositories using Git LFS or other external filters in local configuration are unsupported rather than executed under a supervised filter contract. Non-UTF-8 filesystem roots and broader worktree names are unsupported. Identity and option-injection protections are necessary; disabling unrelated programs does not itself establish a recoverable route for affected repositories. Fixed author dates are reproducibility metadata, not execution deadlines.\n- Repair direction: Make unsupported repository features explicit before admitting work, and supply a supervised compatible filter path when needed. Preserve exact-root/repository identity and argument/environment protections. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGQnXIwepdhOTqInE2mvA8VLwYkoyq5RU7W+PMI5BgbdFy53BF0m7ekkMx567JzpuS/22U+lMBgz82xw3bhsKwg="}
