{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3075,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.938048317Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"ae63d2f3-5afb-566f-95c8-487ec2c7f331","title":"[L527] Git status rejects complete observations at fixed counts, paths and parser boundaries","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L527.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-git/src/status.rs:14-16`, `src/status.rs:262-319`, `src/status/porcelain.rs:15-55`, `src/status/porcelain.rs:261-277`.\n- Behavior: Status collects all untracked files and matching ignored paths, including submodule state. Parsing admits at most 100,000 entries, 64 MiB total and 4,096 bytes per path; the command's default 16 MiB output ceiling applies first. Paths must be UTF-8, control-free canonical relative forms. Any unsupported header/record, unborn HEAD or excessive entry/path rejects the entire observation with Quarantine guidance. Status then runs write-tree and maps every unsuccessful status of that command to absent index_tree without distinguishing conflicts from other failures.\n- Consequence: A large or unusual working tree has no status pagination route and can become quarantine-class failure. A legal Git filename containing a newline or non-UTF-8 bytes can also block observation. Ignored content is deliberately visible, but inclusion consumes the same finite observation capacity. An unavailable index tree does not communicate its underlying cause.\n- Repair direction: Preserve safe raw-path identity independently of presentation, stream status with an exact observation boundary, and distinguish representational/capacity failures from repository corruption and actual index conflicts. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"sig