{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3077,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.943555624Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"7b883a36-9562-5ebc-a27a-56d1a30b12e8","title":"[L528] Structured Git diff and history have additional fixed, nonpaged observation ceilings","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L528.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-git/src/diff.rs:12-15`, `src/diff.rs:65-82`, `src/diff.rs:141-187`, `src/diff.rs:201-225`, `src/history.rs:12-13`, `src/history.rs:55-68`, `src/history.rs:109-129`, `src/history.rs:140-183`.\n- Behavior: Diff must select positive bounds no larger than 100,000 changed paths and 8 MiB of patch bytes. Both complete Git outputs are collected before smaller request bounds are checked; all split name-status fields are collected before count validation. History selects 1..1,024 commits via Git max-count, but has no continuation token or incomplete-result marker. Every selected subject must be UTF-8, at most 4,096 bytes, and each author timestamp must parse as u64; one incompatible commit rejects the complete history observation.\n- Consequence: A legitimate larger diff cannot be represented through this API. A finite history result does not communicate whether more history exists; caller-guided traversal must reconstruct that separately. Per-request bounds do not prevent generating a larger response first. Byte, entry, subject and representation limits are distinct from execution deadlines.\n- Repair direction: Add exact commit/path continuation and artifact-backed or streamed patch data, with explicit complete/incomplete observations and per-entry diagnostic handling. Preserve immutable commit-pair identity. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},