{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3081,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.953219513Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"fcb9e212-be90-5de7-a2f0-6a3be3520f85","title":"[L530] Git handle recovery has strict path, topology and schema requirements but no TTL","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L530.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-git/src/manifest.rs:20-30`, `src/manifest/worktree.rs:66-101`, `src/manifest/worktree.rs:152-212`, `src/worktree/lifecycle.rs:189-258`, `src/worktree/recovery.rs:131-186`, `src/manifest/snapshot.rs:71-111`.\n- Behavior: Manifests accept exactly schema 1 under shared production codec limits, require UTF-8 absolute paths and reject trailing bytes. Worktree destinations must have a leaf identical to the validated name and reside outside the opened repository root and Git storage. Ordinary manifest reopening requires the original detached baseline HEAD. There are separate recovery functions for exact interrupted creation and for a previously trusted worktree's current detached HEAD; the latter preserves working changes and adopts the currently observed commit/tree as the recovered baseline. Snapshot refs and repository identity are revalidated exactly.\n- Consequence: An advanced HEAD cannot use ordinary original-manifest reopening but does have an explicit current-worktree route. An in-repository .worktrees directory is unsupported by this adapter. Moving a repository changes its path-bound identity; old manifests do not automatically rebind. Git handles, worktrees and retained snapshot refs do not expire on a wall timer or disappear merely because a typed handle is dropped.\n- Repair direction: Preserve explicit trusted recovery and binding checks, add intentional format/path migration when needed, and ensure higher callers select current-worktree recovery where appropriate. Do not mistake these durable handles for ephemeral provider contexts. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKp4ssYsLXhBlClBbm7TbB0YlPD9rGbRg6EmQvIzgcquFv3CsS6jHH6jDRfwzxZ9NtpH9bU/TwgMWqetBau9wwg="}
