{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3083,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.958025575Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"5b722b98-44ce-597e-a598-78234f3d7800","title":"[L531] Snapshot admission and clean reconciliation include ignored path state","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L531.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-git/src/snapshot/operations.rs:90-105`, `src/status.rs:227-252`, `src/reconcile.rs:49-60`, `src/reconcile.rs:110-155`, `src/worktree/lifecycle.rs:119-132`.\n- Behavior: Snapshot creation requires the current complete status digest to equal the candidate's prior recorded status, in addition to matching detached HEAD and index tree. That digest includes reported ignored paths. Reconciliation defaults to disallowing ignored paths but permits an explicit allow_ignored choice. RequireClean removal refuses every reported status entry, including ignored paths; ForceRegistered is a distinct explicit effect policy.\n- Consequence: New ignored paths between candidate and snapshot creation can invalidate the candidate even without a change to its staged tree. Ignored build/log artifacts prevent default clean classification and clean removal. This is a policy distinction, not evidence that files may be discarded automatically. Conflicts and attached topology remain explicit indeterminate states.\n- Repair direction: Bind candidate content and observational dirtiness separately, define intentional ignored-content policy at callers, and retain exact registration/effect authority for destructive cleanup. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3