tance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEDIN26K1sutv9fVNbfbYgxpRQlHP/Y/dN9pY/gFO9il15Jewmj6Xyyx+btOZrKDDa0GhsOdrRUmkerQkPIUbAQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3085,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.962607025Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"9ad5d231-99dc-54cd-b7c2-66c6a14665ef","title":"[L532] Some Git effects lack an idempotent completed-cleanup recovery result","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L532.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-git/src/worktree/lifecycle.rs:119-185`, `src/snapshot/operations.rs:247-272`, `src/snapshot/support.rs:82-140`, `src/snapshot/quarantine.rs:33-69`.\n- Behavior: Worktree removal validates the existing canonical root before issuing removal; retry after completed removal fails because the root is absent. Snapshot release first requires the retained ref to exist and match; retry after completed ref deletion fails reconciliation. Candidate/staging, restore, ref updates and worktree creation can also finish effects before later observation, output or manifest errors are returned. In contrast, snapshot quarantine explicitly recognizes its exact already-completed state, and interrupted worktree creation has a dedicated recovery route.\n- Consequence: A crash or lost receipt after cleanup can leave callers with error guidance instead of a proven completed result. This adapter alone has no command ledger that resolves those cleanup outcomes; a higher-level durable caller may compensate and must be examined before claiming a live dead end. Removing identity checks would lose safety without establishing completion.\n- Repair direction: Resolve cleanup through durable intent, expected identity and post-effect observation, distinguishing exact completed absence from unproven absence or replacement. Preserve the existing compare-and-swap and quarantine behavior. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQI7zrZCKWpa/x2DrKAMRC1epm3B4xQiLObuqd+hkY2oEk8UmqGVZUtKJPQYQm30LiiTR+WCtDa46LiXhFdyhGQA="}
