ile candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOufC0kezFlsEzi5+sa/2X8mixCYh+OIP0JnXsROwtgXmAX1DcrLpCwqvrjGitvN2nOhA+TayqKgPde3ybwJpAA="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3091,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.976773282Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"ac6e33c0-ed5d-51bc-b62e-391a08605491","title":"[L536] Proxy cancellation can block on unsupervised host calls and header reads","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L536.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-network/src/resolution.rs:29-46`, `src/credential.rs:292-299`, `src/proxy/worker.rs:41-48`, `src/proxy/worker.rs:142-160`, `src/proxy/http.rs:246-258`, `src/proxy/mod.rs:153-188`, `src/proxy/owner.rs:106-145`.\n- Behavior: DNS resolution and credential acquisition are synchronous trait calls without cancellation. Request/response header readers perform one-byte blocking read_exact calls without observing the cancellation token. Shutdown and Drop cancel the token, then synchronously join the owner and its workers. Socket timeouts apply to individual calls, not a cancellation wakeup; header bytes arriving before each read timeout can keep parsing alive after owner cancellation. The owner's accept error returns through ? before its cancel/join/revoke epilogue, dropping worker join handles rather than resolving them.\n- Consequence: Mandatory time values do not prove that shutdown can recover: blocked DNS/provider calls and continued header reads can hold joins. Increasing the timeout also increases the time before some workers notice cancellation. The early-error path violates the documented complete-owned-join contract in this layer; no live reproduction is claimed.\n- Repair direction: Supervise cancellable host operations and owned socket shutdown, keep teardown on every exit path, and persist unresolved ownership instead of either detaching it or imposing another arbitrary deadline. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAj7owUSdVpbLhibgOVbg7MZUB6rqAn7WOEClxnG6Olcjl0uotllz21kvzYgyaubdxkkdF2NUwradEt/cnKdxgY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3092,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.979117115Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ac6e33c0-ed5d-51bc-b62e-391a08605491","comment_uuid":"aed471fb-adf6-413c-8f64-acfe6b494b9a","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L536: Proxy cancellation can block on unsupervised host calls and header reads.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/runtime/peritus-network/src/resolution.rs:29-46; src/credential.rs:292-299; src/proxy/worker.rs:41-48; src/proxy/worker.rs:142-160; src/proxy/http.rs:246-258; src/proxy/mod.rs:153-188; src/proxy/owner.rs:106-145. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nSupervise cancellable host operations and owned socket shutdown, keep teardown on every exit path, and persist unresolved ownership instead of either detaching it or imposing another arbitrary deadline. No tests run.\n\nPreserve: canonical digest and schema identity, shared writer/reader admissibility, malformed-input rejection before allocation, exact causal ordering, actual provider/OS capability boundaries and preserved accepted historical evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEHusy3AZd/JLO25KTVeMFMays7/gDy3LCRQd9A3lwxfcbP0P4TGU/No7OrcEtIsI28y1/MuCC+EDqbJaE/AOQA="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3093,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.981610197Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"596742c8-57df-5108-ba47-c82f34839450","title":"[L537] Connection duration accounting uses different origins for different phases","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L537.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-network/src/proxy/worker.rs:41-67`, `src/proxy/worker.rs:91-118`, `src/proxy/connect.rs:104-172`, `src/accounting.rs:92-98`.\n- Behavior: HTTP elapsed accounting starts after the entire client request header is read. DNS and connect occur before the next elapsed check, and upstream response-head reads do not consult that clock. CONNECT starts a new Instant separately inside each upload/download relay, excluding its earlier header/resolve/connect phases. Per-read/write socket timeouts reuse the complete connection duration. Elapsed accounting rejects strictly greater-than duration while owner lifetime stops at greater-than-or-equal.\n- Consequence: The mandatory connection duration is neither a consistent whole-connection limit nor reliable cancellation. It can terminate a progressing transfer yet exclude expensive startup/header phases. A timer field is not evidence of a complete recovery contract.\n- Repair direction: Remove implicit execution lifetimes and define observable phase progress and ownership cancellation consistently. If a user explicitly selects a deadline, represent its origin and scope once rather than restarting it per phase. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIWnlCIVIif4j5WUHjPzL6HYdTcZxEkJdg9G/TQKoz6IGSilth91CkDXrzuT9XeSmTHVjmjFtIFoTYP1FFZNKAU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3094,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.983980472Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"596742c8-57df-5108-ba47-c82f34839450","comment_uuid":"5df9b575-a093-4260-9851-f72e56dcd00c","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L537: Connection duration accounting uses different origins for different phases.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/runtime/peritus-network/src/proxy/worker.rs:41-67; src/proxy/worker.rs:91-118; src/proxy/connect.rs:104-172; src/accounting.rs:92-98. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nRemove implicit execution lifetimes and define observable phase progress and ownership cancellation consistently. If a user explicitly selects a deadline, represent its origin and scope once rather than restarting it per phase. No tests run.\n\nPreserve: canonical digest and schema identity, shared writer/reader admissibility, malformed-input rejection before allocation, exact causal ordering, actual provider/OS capability boundaries and preserved accepted historical evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQD1dsTZDDf2gk/HnAyqFl4wNFcfoi6UqIszL8yt9Sn+I/pK9Z0G0qMPrA9SKN1U69CYs1clDsrJEYP+EoXSqhAI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3095,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.986452081Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"6a6d17a6-2aa6-5914-9c72-e9ebb63fc03c","title":"[L538] Managed DNS and protocol compatibility can reject otherwise usable connections","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L538.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-network/src/resolution.rs:35-46`, `src/proxy/connect.rs:18-34`, `src/matcher.rs:103-151`, `src/plan.rs:206-233`.\n- Behavior: System resolution revalidates every returned address and fails the whole result if any answer is denied. Connect sorts admitted addresses and tries only the first, with no attempt at the remaining admitted answers when that address fails. Matching reconstructs/clones the complete network rule contract for each request and resolved IP. UDP requirements are rejected because no exact datagram relay is implemented; managed requests support TCP only. Special-address and explicit-deny checks are retained security boundaries.\n- Consequence: A mixed answer set or an unavailable first admitted address can block a destination even when another authorized answer is reachable. This is a compatibility/recovery limitation, not a reason to remove destination authorization. Repeated contract reconstruction adds synchronous work; no measured bottleneck is claimed.\n- Repair direction: Preserve deny precedence and special-address authority while defining selection among independently admitted addresses and cancellable connection attempts. Supply an explicitly admitted datagram path where required. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEBoneMZx6wsje/EVBN18Yl3omH3p6kYuEnzKgbtINrFbZPy130wk3wNDRs0sHkP/doVEkNps0KO5+r8h5QaSwM="}
