and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQD08gqp6NQd5iUqkGeENpuSoqcC1pH6jsns0Ly7/mAcbHE89dYnXD1B4BSEBbd5bLihWcfrE9W0j5MePq3UMzwM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3097,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.990866976Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"c734e806-1d34-5276-bd31-70a8d629f5df","title":"[L539] Upstream credentials require expiry and use counts, but exhaustion is silently omitted","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L539.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-network/src/credential.rs:103-183`, `src/credential.rs:250-272`, `src/credential.rs:301-317`, `src/proxy/worker.rs:142-160`.\n- Behavior: CredentialLease requires positive uses and a nonzero wall-clock expiry, with no renewal or unlimited mode. It binds owner, plan, transport, port and host matcher and decrements before material acquisition or request encoding/write. The worker catches every consume error, including expiry/exhaustion/revocation/mismatch, and returns Ok(None), forwarding the request without the configured injection. Provider acquisition failure still consumes the use. Header names are at most 128 bytes and material at most 16 KiB, with injection-safe characters required.\n- Consequence: An exhausted or expired proxy credential can appear to clients as an upstream authentication failure rather than the actionable ReacquireCredential error defined by the lease. Failed acquisition can exhaust all uses before any successful authenticated request. These leases are credential authority, not provider context/session TTL; their expiry must not be casually equated with context deletion.\n- Repair direction: Make optional versus required credential injection explicit, propagate reacquisition state and retain exact pending use resolution. Keep host/owner/plan and header-injection protections. Define intentional authority renewal independently of synthetic transport lifetime. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNar9fad5UDuMVS/YmyD7eLrCshHYsw9Fx12CCRNgHiy1XPVq/BZJjsMd6WX1k9JuexzLo7Hi/3T/Aw421kokw8="}
