fects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: renewal/adoption under the same authorized identity, revoked authority, stale epoch/revision, cross-scope requests, lost acknowledgements and restart, proving legitimate continuation without admitting unauthorized or duplicate effects. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNQGzqBro0Rt283PYchZRqL6X3DOG0SLgIr19TNFK1dZMtqMDa5bKuXPm+6vvVvS5ee7JhZNETzJF148zlmL/QY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3099,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:50.995252754Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"048d5d17-e80f-55d2-91eb-99a3fa77a8b7","title":"[L540] HTTP header effects occur before network byte ceilings are charged","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L540.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-network/src/proxy/worker.rs:50-76`, `src/proxy/worker.rs:91-104`, `src/proxy/worker.rs:176-201`, `src/proxy/connect.rs:175-186`, `src/proxy/owner.rs:215-228`.\n- Behavior: CONNECT success, upstream request headers and final response headers are written before their byte charges are checked. Body relay charges before forwarding. Per-connection accounting mutates before the shared total charge, so total rejection can leave the local account charged for a chunk never forwarded. Aggregate budget is lifetime state with no refill. Discarded redirect bodies also consume it.\n- Consequence: A byte-limit error can occur after an upstream request has already triggered an effect or after a success header was sent. Retrying that generic connection failure cannot by itself prove safe replay. Configured byte counts mix forwarded control bytes, discarded bodies and reserved/unforwarded chunks. These are not execution timers but can stop useful work.\n- Repair direction: Reserve/resolve exact transmission accounting before effects and preserve uncertainty for requests whose remote outcome is unknown. Separate user-selected network budget from observational counters and connection backpressure. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBYnvPUp7ZMkfcznSDJ9QSkYUkMRoUFIKYQnVafehMUFXgbF9tenZtDIiPaa9WvlZQRVMATLHA0jxeiChB/oswQ="}
