{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3105,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.010340459Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"52bf82e0-a4c3-5529-8664-dc634b509757","title":"[L543] Inherited listener handoff assumes a complete record from a stream read","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L543.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-network/src/proxy/inherited.rs:159-197`, `src/proxy/inherited.rs:200-283`.\n- Behavior: A Unix stream channel sends a fixed record plus one SCM_RIGHTS descriptor. Receive requires one recvmsg to return exactly the complete record bytes and exactly one descriptor; a short stream delivery is rejected and received descriptors are closed. It does not retain a partial record for continuation. The receiver polls nonblocking every five milliseconds and observes explicit cancellation; proxy lifetime timing begins only after the listener is received and owner::run starts.\n- Consequence: Stream segmentation is represented as an invalid handoff rather than resumable framing. A slow handoff has no implicit timer in this layer, which is consistent with explicit cancellation, but the returned endpoint remains absent until successful framing. Five-millisecond polling is cadence, not a session deadline.\n- Repair direction: Define descriptor-bound stream framing with retained partial bytes or use a matching message-oriented channel contract. Preserve exact descriptor count, loopback and close-on-exec validation. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3Nz