{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3107,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.015088314Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"f731b755-d359-5240-a68e-a5a0f4525510","title":"[L545] Secret delivery requires finite expiry and use budgets and cannot renew an active lease","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L545.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-secrets/src/lease.rs:27-35`, `src/lease.rs:59-84`, `src/lease.rs:92-135`, `src/preparation.rs:34-47`, `src/preparation.rs:59-120`, `src/delivery.rs:170-205`.\n- Behavior: Every secret lease requires nonzero remaining uses and a nonzero expiration timestamp. Expiry permanently changes its state before owner and execution scope checks, and successful delivery decrements its lifetime use count. There is no unlimited representation or renewal operation. Preparation permits at most 128 leases and reuses the timestamp captured when the preparation object was constructed. Material lookup occurs before delivery validates the live lease, and a file-staging failure does not return the moved lease for retry.\n- Consequence: A continuing authorized execution can lose credential delivery solely because of these finite budgets; a delayed preparation can also check an old time. An incorrectly scoped attempt at or beyond expiry can change lease state. These are source-level behaviors; installed caller values and native recovery integration remain separate questions.\n- Repair direction: Separate authority revocation from arbitrary lifetime budgets, support explicit unlimited or renewable authorized delivery, validate scope before state mutation, obtain the current time at the actual check, and preserve retryable ownership on staging failure.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHBJp1WCgnj1kMNSfrQSAG75DYeyu9au/7dwmWIzjiu+zEumnR37PWramY3cfBpqL0XTaqROmJfezTtFPuTs2QE="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3108,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.017268183Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"f731b755-d359-5240-a68e-a5a0f4525510","comment_uuid":"7450cc44-0a5b-4017-8244-fd47f27f3558","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L545: Secret delivery requires finite expiry and use budgets and cannot renew an active lease.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/runtime/peritus-secrets/src/lease.rs:27-35; src/lease.rs:59-84; src/lease.rs:92-135; src/preparation.rs:34-47; src/preparation.rs:59-120; src/delivery.rs:170-205. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nSeparate authority revocation from arbitrary lifetime budgets, support explicit unlimited or renewable authorized delivery, validate scope before state mutation, obtain the current time at the actual check, and preserve retryable ownership on staging failure.\n\nPreserve: explicit user authority, credential secrecy, exact target/resource binding, fencing, scope confinement, replay rejection for changed command content and fail-closed acceptance evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: renewal/adoption under the same authorized identity, revoked authority, stale epoch/revision, cross-scope requests, lost acknowledgements and restart, proving legitimate continuation without admitting unauthorized or duplicate effects. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLIOxVzfP6wwi3fN5af5dyutv0uCqKz0HfMIyLQNVRKVxq2h2sFUOTWdZnhciEv0kHTgdd4heJKRNadLGj/QCwY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3109,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.019515749Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"693a1427-c736-5a8d-9e86-59420d7d9877","title":"[L546] Redaction fingerprint construction expands the entire secret before applying its count limit","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L546.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-secrets/src/material.rs:8-22`, `src/fingerprint.rs:51-75`, `src/fingerprint.rs:80-89`, `src/fingerprint.rs:116-133`.\n- Behavior: Material accepts up to one MiB. Redaction construction hashes every sliding fragment of length four through 64, collects all hashes, sorts and deduplicates them, then rejects more than 65,536 unique fingerprints. For a one-MiB input, this constructs 63,961,124 fingerprint entries before deduplication. Each hash builds another temporary byte vector. Matching scans the fingerprint vector synchronously.\n- Consequence: An input allowed by the material boundary can incur tens of millions of allocations and hashes, substantial memory use and sorting before a later rejection. No cancellation or progress boundary is provided. The expansion is derived from the loops, not a measured stress run.\n- Repair direction: Define a redaction representation and algorithm whose construction and matching costs are bounded by the accepted material size; reject unsupported inputs before expansion or process them incrementally with cancellation. Preserve the security purpose of redaction.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQL6fGAaO7Ry5uYYkw4Gt1oY20vlr8TZUZJwbluHlvCgqMmmfKUKXUzWL0jAl6LD75KZQKgoYZ5QUO5z0C/pdhgQ="}
