stale epoch/revision, cross-scope requests, lost acknowledgements and restart, proving legitimate continuation without admitting unauthorized or duplicate effects. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQH4FzRGN82AXYPAjh4xRjN7NYLb5H4nCGpLiWDoI9/yvj0CBBzazKuHF9FqTw0Y7VTvdeDI/nOosLSAwelnf4w8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3113,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.029078803Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"5a9482eb-f8e3-50b5-98b3-668fe1b15698","title":"[L548] Failed file staging and destructor cleanup can lose ownership of secret artifacts","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L548.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-secrets/src/delivery.rs:178-205`, `src/delivery.rs:229-285`.\n- Behavior: Staging creates a lease-named file exclusively, writes and syncs it, then adds it to the session only on success. If write or sync fails, an attempted removal error is ignored, leaving a possible partial file outside the artifact list. A later exact retry encounters the existing name. Explicit release retains failed removals for retry, but Drop discards release errors and destroys the owner object.\n- Consequence: A partial artifact can survive without a retryable ownership record; process teardown can discard the only cleanup state. A finite lease does not solve this recovery gap. No injected filesystem failure or crash was executed during this audit.\n- Repair direction: Journal ownership before creating artifacts, preserve cleanup failures durably, and reconcile exact existing artifacts on recovery and retry. Retain explicit idempotent release and restrictive file permissions.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCU6gpJyEEV9PHavN2bR+kocFq4/BwQQhNWIEyH8Cu40V0Bkpxqri1qn4o5m8PwxDu9gCDW+JulXUKjVXKcZMg4="}
