{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3115,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.034092796Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"bab6f09b-40ee-5886-9a8c-b21fc36c50ff","title":"[L549] Secret recovery classifies supplied metadata without reattaching the delivery session","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L549.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-secrets/src/recovery.rs:23-81`, `src/delivery.rs:170-205`, `tests/secrets.rs:177-202`.\n- Behavior: The recovery record contains owner, lease, reference, execution digest and live/released flags with a checksum. Classification accepts a supplied resource-present Boolean and optional lease; it can classify a record as live with no supplied lease. The crate supplies no record serialization, session rehydration or exact live-file/path attachment. Absence is clean only when the stored record already says released.\n- Consequence: These metadata checks alone cannot reconnect a restarted executor to its previous secret delivery or prove cleanup of an interrupted owner. The tests construct metadata and Boolean observations rather than performing native restart attachment.\n- Repair direction: Persist recoverable ownership and exact native identities, reconcile interrupted creation and release, and rebuild the continuing session only from verified resources. Keep checksum and scope checks as integrity requirements.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQB+JNYR/RntiWhHHtbUzHoyv+HfYKCSGdnMgVAznmFniXBnxAP0cD0DMpmZ3qMQQZJZ8kvEEFQvwbgBbf6bvwwA="}
