{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3117,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.038607081Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"c37c52c7-744c-5a42-9152-ac7538593220","title":"[L550] Credential-store availability probing hides causes and blocks synchronously","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L550.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-secrets/src/store.rs:60-80`, `src/store.rs:95-146`, `src/store.rs:151-160`, `src/store.rs:226-232`, `src/reference.rs:1-86`.\n- Behavior: Platform-store operations perform a synchronous availability probe using `store_status().is_ok()` before access. Probe failures collapse to unavailable/retry instead of retaining locked or denied causes, even though later keyring errors have more specific recovery classifications. Lookup retrieves and hashes all returned bytes before material-size validation. References bind a resource/version digest, but the persistent namespace is configured outside the reference. A repeated remove of a missing entry reports missing rather than completed cleanup.\n- Consequence: A locked store can be presented as retryable unavailability, and a blocked native probe has no cancellation path in this crate. Namespace drift and late size rejection can prevent otherwise authorized credential access. Version-digest and owner checks are integrity controls rather than synthetic session deadlines.\n- Repair direction: Preserve native failure causes, make host calls cancellable, validate admitted sizes before expensive processing where the backend permits, persist the effective namespace binding, and reconcile already-completed removal explicitly.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLCprkwz3qQ9spHQac7YB+hX5Rm1vPDDp8pybHkQLa+EZHd0h+EehCAO7lzQdA9RglO4Ij3HuqtCd0dmScgLogs="}
