tion under the same authorized identity, revoked authority, stale epoch/revision, cross-scope requests, lost acknowledgements and restart, proving legitimate continuation without admitting unauthorized or duplicate effects. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCWS8MFwNjDSDLRe9bM8q3wn2mSn5tAd7U+6G8HkO3UBTW5sOGVAH+66wwhMY1p2e9wPn/V55hK79m6zY45OIgM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3119,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.043602037Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"eea8385a-e53a-5918-986f-c2c42d81f9bf","title":"[L552] Patch preparation can leave a manifestless blocker and quarantine has only 100 names","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L552.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-patch/src/transaction/apply.rs:62-103`, `src/transaction/apply.rs:114-147`, `src/transaction/storage.rs:20-36`, `src/transaction/recover.rs:39-69`, `src/transaction/recover.rs:298-334`.\n- Behavior: The transaction directory is created and synchronized before final files are staged and before the first manifest is persisted. Root synchronization failure returns immediately; later preparation failures attempt cleanup but ignore its outcome. Exact retry rejects an existing directory. A manifestless directory is quarantined as indeterminate. Quarantine tries only the base name and suffixes one through 99, then returns a fencing error.\n- Consequence: An interruption before the manifest exists can leave a directory that blocks retry and cannot establish safe completion from this crate's recovery contract. Repeated quarantine conflicts exhaust a fixed name budget. Successful installation exposes cleanup-pending status, but pre-mutation and restored failures do not expose ignored cleanup failure separately.\n- Repair direction: Durably record transaction ownership and preparation state before creating effects, reconcile safe interrupted preparation, retain cleanup status on every exit, and use collision-resistant quarantine identities without a fixed lifetime name budget.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNYcCsmX3v9cN7f6Jemeqrl0P37cBxJNn6WlxwmOQumy69NVwdz9eIiDum2S5NDwnAcnHIarw3byZa6vOAC0xww="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3120,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.046323088Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"eea8385a-e53a-5918-986f-c2c42d81f9bf","comment_uuid":"b417906b-b5e5-4696-810d-abc4085536f0","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L552: Patch preparation can leave a manifestless blocker and quarantine has only 100 names.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/runtime/peritus-patch/src/transaction/apply.rs:62-103; src/transaction/apply.rs:114-147; src/transaction/storage.rs:20-36; src/transaction/recover.rs:39-69; src/transaction/recover.rs:298-334. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nDurably record transaction ownership and preparation state before creating effects, reconcile safe interrupted preparation, retain cleanup status on every exit, and use collision-resistant quarantine identities without a fixed lifetime name budget.\n\nPreserve: canonical digest and schema identity, shared writer/reader admissibility, malformed-input rejection before allocation, exact causal ordering, actual provider/OS capability boundaries and preserved accepted historical evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQC8HvcXlgvg9vL7NBDLP3BUCGATTXm0Z6GcFJ/E5XSAJRRq4NydNe6MTls1cVRzCrNBxkY45Aop6SKsmoAsupgg="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3121,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.048675582Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"b8a2c120-ab2e-5f17-84fb-ca175acb0898","title":"[L553] Patch cleanup removes the local completion evidence and repeated recovery fails on absence","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L553.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-patch/src/transaction/apply.rs:139-147`, `src/transaction/storage.rs:114-121`, `src/transaction/roots.rs:29-38`, `src/transaction/recover.rs:31-38`, `src/transaction/recover.rs:273-283`.\n- Behavior: Successful application returns an installed manifest but deletes the transaction directory when cleanup succeeds. Recovery first requires that directory to exist. Cleanup removes the directory before synchronizing its parent; a failed parent synchronization reports cleanup pending even though the directory can already be absent. Repeated recovery then fails root inspection rather than returning already-applied or already-cleaned.\n- Consequence: Exact completion replay depends on a durable caller receipt outside this adapter. Local disappearance alone cannot distinguish completed cleanup from missing ownership, and a reported cleanup-pending result can lead to a retry that has no directory to inspect. Higher-level receipt integration must be assessed separately.\n- Repair direction: Persist a compact completion/release receipt before retiring large staging data, and reconcile exact repeated cleanup through that receipt, including the removed-directory/unsynced-parent boundary.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCmYiF+UytLv+zvzof/SswsfXiMsELNFu+WmRv9IavAShPuEG8GrKvKhxtnis0W6FYg2br7gtCKCQKB7xyyUuwQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3122,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.051095278Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"b8a2c120-ab2e-5f17-84fb-ca175acb0898","comment_uuid":"e5140948-c791-4ad7-8c54-4c36ecd76332","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L553: Patch cleanup removes the local completion evidence and repeated recovery fails on absence.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/runtime/peritus-patch/src/transaction/apply.rs:139-147; src/transaction/storage.rs:114-121; src/transaction/roots.rs:29-38; src/transaction/recover.rs:31-38; src/transaction/recover.rs:273-283. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nPersist a compact completion/release receipt before retiring large staging data, and reconcile exact repeated cleanup through that receipt, including the removed-directory/unsynced-parent boundary.\n\nPreserve: canonical digest and schema identity, shared writer/reader admissibility, malformed-input rejection before allocation, exact causal ordering, actual provider/OS capability boundaries and preserved accepted historical evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNm1MCyMfahgbmxCd+wwYGpKT6uM/bYX3vQqszXxjpF93RlF/q8kqTlEcdzSIRPYndWw/U9pAPHq2aBeHRp5owk="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3123,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.053502744Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"68c9b9ee-7a29-56fe-b320-5d2cbe77b8f4","title":"[L554] Patch filesystem work is synchronous and has platform and exact-observation restrictions","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L554.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-patch/src/transaction/apply.rs:150-171`, `src/transaction/apply.rs:188-210`, `src/transaction/filesystem.rs:34-85`, `src/transaction/filesystem.rs:102-146`, `src/transaction/filesystem.rs:189-228`, `src/transaction/filesystem.rs:295-347`, `src/transaction/roots.rs:41-72`, `src/line_endings.rs:25-80`.\n- Behavior: Targets above the shared production file bound cannot be exactly observed for a patch. Symlinks, special nodes and nested repositories are rejected. Non-Unix executable-mode patches are rejected before staging. Same-device root validation is implemented on Unix; other platforms accept that check unconditionally and can fail later during rename. Full file reads/hashes, repeated pre/post/rollback observations, directory discovery, normalization, writes and synchronization run synchronously without cancellation or a progress cursor.\n- Consequence: This path has no synthetic wall-clock deadline, but blocked filesystem I/O cannot be canceled through the API and an accepted multi-file operation has no incremental recovery progress interface. File-size and platform representation limits can prevent legitimate edits. Exact preimage checks, disjoint roots and unsafe-target rejection protect mutation integrity and must remain effective when limits change.\n- Repair direction: Support scalable exact observation and durable incremental progress, expose cancellable host operations, and validate native volume/mode capabilities before effects rather than treating unsupported checks as successful.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEvNJ0NwQxDeDGtNtFKyyBdPso2M0WOP463oCcpbJ1bvRSRPzH9aUAJtsTcG5UlFr3T/6ZFs5+kVF41RGBzaEwg="}
