{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3125,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.058499755Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"4c1035c1-e219-5067-98ba-c51aae52e229","title":"[L556] Sandbox time limits are optional but six resource dimensions still require finite bounds","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L556.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-sandbox/src/resource.rs:53-147`, `src/resource.rs:150-201`, `src/process_policy.rs:5-14`, `src/process_policy.rs:65-92`, `src/terminal.rs:152-176`, `src/terminal.rs:267-291`, `src/reference/session.rs:160-184`.\n- Behavior: `with_optional_time` represents absent wall and CPU bounds as zero on the canonical wire and skips their finite comparison. Memory, disk, output, handles, processes and concurrency still require positive finite quantities. Process policy separately requires a finite simultaneous process maximum and a denied/bounded descendant allowance. Terminal output also requires a positive finite byte budget. The reference usage API only adds usage in all dimensions; it has no release/decrement or gauge update for simultaneous resources. Untimed counters still reject arithmetic overflow. Reference accounting enforces contract limits rather than the smaller requirements.\n- Consequence: Removing timers does not remove output/storage/capacity ceilings. Treating a simultaneous handle/process/slot count as cumulative charging would eventually exhaust a continuing session, although native callers must be inspected before asserting they use that reference pattern. The optional-time implementation is an existing repair and must not be mislabeled as a mandatory execution deadline.\n- Repair direction: Preserve explicit absence of time bounds, give other policy budgets an intentional unlimited representation where authorized, and separate lifetime consumption from current/peak resource measurements with correct release and durable accounting.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJDZwSVQ26cc35Fvf0rTxRAQ+LifcJSsVsHLC6srJQxLCWzuWeAmDDVfEHKGxSTWXKyPOHXbmhEBuwuBcC0UEAk="}
