tion must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOe+y+zFgx7o94ZdR8iLJ6D+XTVHh7RChjfn8uuvO1et4SD9lxWvJ3HZlFbIBdP/Mc2AMRyRR45mlBCNKxnOtQk="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3127,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.063355403Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"d885d240-eef2-5914-887f-640640ced539","title":"[L557] Untimed sandbox plans still require backend wall and CPU timer features","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L557.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-sandbox/src/plan.rs:194-249`, `src/admission.rs:68-95`, `src/backend.rs:121-161`, `src/verified.rs:73-99`.\n- Behavior: Feature derivation unconditionally inserts WallTime and CpuTime along with the other resource features, regardless of the optional time limits. Admission rejects any missing feature before preparation. Features also cover default filesystem, descendant and network denial; these controls are necessary even for effects the plan forbids. Admission compares declared support bits and kind, not actual runtime enforcement observations.\n- Consequence: An otherwise sufficient untimed native backend can be rejected solely because it cannot enforce timers the plan does not request. Declared completeness is not qualification of operational liveness or restart attachment. This does not show the installed backend currently lacks those bits.\n- Repair direction: Derive timer requirements from actually configured bounds while retaining enforcement of default denial and every requested authority boundary. Qualify descriptor claims against native execution separately.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOAbwJ7PCBA0YlyNp6ZXK5F1CpX