ressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQB6xqXCWHVH5ueYQy2/itu5rtqung/TYvS7E5gxD+4Rrq9b5ifb7X4rFF8q8paSE80Ms2Z8S5IEtnHGRfPsW8Q8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3129,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.068326938Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"4d229e15-94ff-5c84-8012-303b92b0102a","title":"[L558] Sandbox contracts impose fixed rule, requirement and representation ceilings","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L558.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-sandbox/src/requirements.rs:8-58`, `src/requirements.rs:84-111`, `src/filesystem.rs:5-43`, `src/filesystem.rs:269-280`, `src/environment.rs:5-29`, `src/environment.rs:60-80`, `src/network.rs:6-37`, `src/network.rs:276-287`, `src/secret.rs:6-51`, `src/secret.rs:105-116`, `src/process_policy.rs:65-92`, `src/backend.rs:6-58`.\n- Behavior: Filesystem/network rule sets and file/network/secret requirements cap at 256; inherited and literal environment names each cap at 256. Secret grants and root executables cap at 128. Logical paths cap at 4,096 UTF-8 bytes and forbid backslashes; environment/backend identities and brokered-handle labels cap at 128 bytes with restricted ASCII syntax. DNS names use 253-byte/63-byte label protocol bounds. Most collection caps are applied before deduplication, while root-program count is checked after sorting/deduplication.\n- Consequence: Duplicate-heavy or legitimately larger contracts can be rejected before compilation even if their effective authority is modest. Portable representation choices can exclude native names and paths. DNS protocol rules and traversal/authority checks serve different purposes from fixed collection ceilings.\n- Repair direction: Canonicalize before effective-size admission, support scalable contract representation and native path/name semantics, and preserve protocol and authority validation as limits are redesigned.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKS0916b8qMWNBoKwj7zF/hA+GIS7dC5SRgm33pCG+5SDsmmOzwO2DDwg11znmYvMDinQH4KYnM7VCfJwb4cVww="}
