put and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQG/5ceIyCkQzumE5Yb4Ok/AAGk2trrmZO6Uu32HXjsObjv6v5c98hbFxoVBztZJn6ekPMeilDE2ZM8SK96zFWQ8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3147,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.109250573Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"3aa2fc20-2eb1-599a-ac3b-47abb262a34c","title":"[L568] Linux capability probing can block indefinitely before execution is prepared","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L568.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-sandbox-linux/src/backend.rs:27-33`; `src/preparation.rs:83-96`; `src/probe.rs:108-117,305-347`; `src/descriptor.rs:105-154` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Backend creation and authorized preparation run native probes. Probe commands use blocking `Command::output`; diagnostic truncation occurs after all output has been collected. Proxy connection probing is blocking. Executable hashing checks a 128 MiB metadata size and then reads the whole file without a read-time bound or cancellation. Baseline admission also requires PTY capability even for pipe-based commands.\n- Consequence: A hanging probe can lock preparation indefinitely without a synthetic deadline being involved. A growing executable can exceed the pre-read size check. Unneeded PTY failure or a changed probe digest can reject an otherwise usable plan.\n- Repair direction: Make probing cancellable, stream bounded diagnostics and hashes, and bind capability requirements to the requested execution. Preserve exact integrity checks while giving probe changes a supported reconciliation path.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKzlYR1h6b9iP81P8b4qBzk/JrCja7vbfVvZPK7AZqZaUPJF1wIokZPyO89mAThviWpoGwFe6HEdcz3H62A29wQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3148,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.111565969Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"3aa2fc20-2eb1-599a-ac3b-47abb262a34c","comment_uuid":"527125c4-f725-4a2c-8f2b-50d47e016935","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L568: Linux capability probing can block indefinitely before execution is prepared.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/runtime/peritus-sandbox-linux/src/backend.rs:27-33; src/preparation.rs:83-96; src/probe.rs:108-117,305-347; src/descriptor.rs:105-154. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nMake probing cancellable, stream bounded diagnostics and hashes, and bind capability requirements to the requested execution. Preserve exact integrity checks while giving probe changes a supported reconciliation path.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIvp5NltZvtX40FmNdS44oUhYgPBYwH7drVFAHTzvUaoi8Gk3C6UVPiuwj1HQPOcQ+Ia4XmlqALfcjc5OAL6yQk="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3149,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.113702383Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"00bb66b5-7a4c-5845-82b2-77e57224948d","title":"[L569] Linux activation consumes its status owner before a blocking observation","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L569.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-sandbox-linux/src/exec_status.rs:23-66`; `src/session.rs:219-257`; `src/native/helper.rs:115-125,248-281` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Activation takes the execution-status owner and removes its protected launch handle before reading the status stream. The read waits for EOF or the oversized-record limit and has no cancellation path. Even a complete fixed-size failure record still needs stream completion. Empty EOF is interpreted as success. Helper manifest and protected-payload reads are also blocking.\n- Consequence: A stalled writer can hang activation, while an observation error leaves the same activation without the handle needed to retry it. Removing timeouts alone does not repair this ownership gap.\n- Repair direction: Use a framed, cancellable activation handshake with durable ownership and an explicit execution-success acknowledgment. Commit the lifecycle transition and consumption of attachment handles together.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNSd59V4GgBB+7Lr5dS5uafqrM7GwtdoI2LGXL8vYUa7+KN9ORvjq47uvAlxiBVZ6ja+M+HjPMURWXhOnA1OqAE="}
