{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3159,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.137079006Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"907881d3-d79c-5fa6-aa66-ac28a767534a","title":"[L579] Workspace action consumption has a hard 1,024-action per-revision ceiling","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L579.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-workspace/src/consumption.rs:18-20,99-107,129-154`; `src/folder_mutation.rs:233-269`; `src/folder_mutation/outcome.rs:32-35`; `src/state.rs:111-116` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Committing action 1,025 in one revision returns an indeterminate/quarantine error. Restore counts every ledger entry toward the same bound. Git candidate installation clears the in-memory map for a successor revision; ordinary-folder patch outcomes retain the unchanged revision, and reopening reloads that revision's durable markers. Neither ledger pruning nor compaction is supplied here.\n- Consequence: Ordinary-folder daily use can accumulate an unavoidable cap at a fixed registered revision. Reopening the gateway does not reset it. Failed operations also consume entries once their markers have been committed.\n- Repair direction: Keep durable deduplication independently of a synthetic lifetime action quota. Provide indexed, versioned storage and safe retirement/compaction of completed outcomes, retaining exact replay protection.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQC9lR/OlgNctM4uvyel8m52Bl71EHp19fFOfV6YJtQFHzwrZWwiWeQjezxIfL/IiJhDfJkTdgmGuXiyH2Pk6pwU