{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3161,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.141915600Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"499e7390-40a6-557d-978f-b95e87e2acde","title":"[L580] A failed workspace action-marker write can poison later opens","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L580.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-workspace/src/consumption.rs:79-126,139-154,167-180,221-246`; `src/writable.rs:65-67`; `src/folder_mutation.rs:110-111,221-233` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Action markers are created exclusively at their final names, then written and synchronized. Errors leave the path in place; the in-memory map is updated only after success. Restore reads each entire file before checking its exact fixed size, and one malformed, inaccessible, misnamed, or mismatched marker rejects the complete revision ledger.\n- Consequence: A partial write can make an exact retry appear already consumed and prevent later workspace opens. A complete write followed by synchronization failure is also an ambiguous committed effect without a reconciliation result. Oversized corrupt marker files are fully allocated before rejection.\n- Repair direction: Persist a recoverable marker state machine with atomic bounded writes, reconcile exact interrupted writes, and retain the difference between absent, in-flight, and completed actions. Bound reads before allocation and isolate corruption without fabricating completion.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPoLozbq40MUA5hnB/u3i8