{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3163,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.146448857Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"8df83025-1791-5412-a26e-7e47a5f627dd","title":"[L581] Workspace authority is consumed before several effect-free failures","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L581.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-workspace/src/gateway.rs:58-95`; `src/mutation.rs:76-89`; `src/folder_mutation.rs:219-250`; `src/rollback.rs:99-120` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Authorization commits the replay marker before patch planning/application. A stale patch or preimage conflict can therefore fail without changing target bytes but still make the same action unusable. Rollback similarly consumes authority before successor-counter and target-lineage validation. Reused actions return `ReceiptReused` and require reauthorization rather than exact operation reconciliation.\n- Consequence: A transient or late validation failure forces a new action and adds to the durable per-revision cap. The crate cannot resume the same authorized intent even when it establishes that no target effect occurred.\n- Repair direction: Complete inert validation before durable consumption, and give the exact intent a recoverable prepare/effect/complete lifecycle. Retrying that lifecycle must reconcile its existing result rather than execute a second independent mutation.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLvfCr50hRvc/7A0lIk1mmCT+cfbLDO/Loboq/w+I0RYWJQNR7XY06Dt7uSxJO12AuSnwP5Jzndxbj2pnykpAwg="}
