{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3165,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.150895153Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"4125beff-0748-530a-8936-036f4fe5b159","title":"[L582] A dirty Git workspace can lose the only object needed to finalize its candidate","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L582.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-workspace/src/mutation.rs:13-20,60-65,111-119`; `src/candidate.rs:64-75,282-302`; `src/rollback.rs:99-100`; `src/gateway.rs:50-70`; `src/reconcile.rs:233-250` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: A successful patch leaves the workspace dirty and returns a private-field `MutationOutcome`. Candidate creation requires that outcome and the dirty condition. Patch application and rollback require the clean condition. Restart reconciliation can classify a restored workspace dirty, but these APIs do not reconstruct or decode the required mutation outcome from its durable patch/action metadata.\n- Consequence: After losing the in-memory outcome, the target API has no supported candidate-finalization path for the successfully applied patch. A known dirty workspace also cannot invoke rollback through this gateway. Exact dirtiness is correctly reported, but continuation remains unavailable here.\n- Repair direction: Persist and restore the exact mutation outcome and candidate obligation. Admit independently authorized rollback/reconciliation from known dirty state with explicit preimages and lineage checks, instead of requiring the clean state that the repair is meant to establish.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednu