{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3167,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.155613434Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"43bcecd7-2d91-51f9-ad22-7470d2964532","title":"[L583] Candidate and rollback completion cross multiple uncoordinated durable effects","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L583.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-workspace/src/candidate.rs:87-150,162-180`; `src/rollback.rs:119-189,201-219`; `src/publication.rs:61-74`; `src/state.rs:111-116`; `src/manifest.rs:244-272` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Candidate creation retains a Git snapshot before checking successor-revision exhaustion. Snapshot publication then finalizes a separate artifact and updates logical state only in memory. Artifact failure compensates by releasing the retained Git reference; a failed compensation leaves the condition indeterminate. The public manifest is encoded here but has no restore decoder. Git/artifact errors are generally replaced with static context.\n- Consequence: Revision exhaustion can leave a retained snapshot without a returned completion. Interruption between retention, publication, and state installation needs caller coordination that this boundary does not supply. The already consumed action cannot simply resume, and generic errors hide the precise failed stage.\n- Repair direction: Preflight counter advancement and maintain a durable completion obligation for every stage. Reconcile the exact snapshot, artifact, and successor state idempotently, with typed underlying causes and a supported decoder/restoration path.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5Mt