{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3171,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.164693594Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"665b1167-7965-58b3-b5a6-c4b2a88af4f6","title":"[L585] Workspace namespace binding writes have no interrupted-write repair path","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L585.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-workspace/src/transaction_namespace.rs:30-60,74-100,148-171,203-220`; `src/folder.rs:18-49`; `src/writable.rs:31-67` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: A namespace binding is written directly to its final exclusive-create path. A partial write remains there; future opens accept an existing binding only when its complete bytes exactly match. Workspace roots and detached baseline identity must remain exact. Folder identity requires UTF-8 and binds the canonical path plus native directory identity (or creation timestamp).\n- Consequence: Interrupted initialization can permanently reject that namespace until explicit repair. Renaming/moving a registered folder changes identity and cannot reconnect by the old binding; non-UTF-8 roots are unsupported. Identity checks are integrity boundaries, not session timers.\n- Repair direction: Reconcile incomplete initialization through exact atomic binding states, and provide explicit authorized migration/relocation when required. Preserve directory identity and namespace isolation instead of bypassing mismatches.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEnXGG6u0ixP+jrgYzgULAcwQi1kv+u6AK5qHcQrHUyBUf8iJA