{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3173,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.169225559Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"7c077648-a56a-5aca-9172-7340e5aa91ef","title":"[L586] Workspace mutation admission inherits finite capability and lease expiry gates","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L586.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-workspace/src/gateway.rs:242-285,330-352,359-389`; `src/verified.rs:131-158`; `src/authorization.rs:14-26` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Every mutation requires one exact dispatched kernel event, matching capability and lease-use receipts, the same holder/session/generation, an active successor lease, current authority epoch, observation before claim expiry, and capability validity at that observation. Missing time currency is folded into the generic incomplete-authority error. This boundary supplies no lease renewal or same-intent continuation operation.\n- Consequence: An expired receipt blocks a queued mutation even if the user's run is still intended to continue. These are inherited authorization lifetimes, not a timer loop implemented in C1, and removing identity checks would not establish persistent authority.\n- Repair direction: Renew or rebind authority through a durable owner and resume the same exact intent with current receipts. Expose which time/holder dimension failed and preserve action identity during supported reconciliation.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNia34nzsDYzbQvLBi7s5635m/NI1wZ62TtQKhDVKWDPA