t and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMkZzi32/HnQqH9E/NjRidvwrbFOloRUFnX7rt8QHkM5vd67MoOEgXj+/BY87eF7WKdd0CsdS7IIYBF4gHNlgAY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3175,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.173518859Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"0ec6db9d-86b8-5289-ba07-efe481b90349","title":"[L590] macOS manifests can encode a body that their decoder rejects","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L590.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-sandbox-macos/src/canonical.rs:5-7,44-48,75-84,131-137`; `src/manifest.rs:24-29,290-329`; `src/manifest/codec.rs:43-58` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: The canonical writer and manifest frame permit up to 512 KiB. The body is enveloped using `Writer::bytes`, which does not impose the 256 KiB string/byte-field limit. The decoder reads that entire body through `Reader::bytes`, which rejects anything above 256 KiB. Fields and collections separately have 256 KiB and 4,096-item limits.\n- Consequence: A successfully constructed, checksummed manifest with a body above 256 KiB can fail in the helper decoder despite remaining within its declared frame bound. A near-maximum profile or combined ordinary arguments/environment can reach the mismatch. This is source-derived; no executable reproduction was run.\n- Repair direction: Give opaque envelope bodies their own symmetric encode/decode bound, preflight the complete native representation, and qualify the exact boundary through the real helper before consuming authorization.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMgqu80A7dYGJJCt/hkMoyp0Nc8ScA0O4d2ZJ/iUbOS+vQUZ9rwyoQaG/tZG5XqZQ2vqN9pqnCLt/kVwq9uQ/wg="}
