{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3181,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.186667012Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"bcd78b84-19db-51f0-a7bc-701632c3c859","title":"[L593] macOS helper activation has blocking reads without cancellation","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L593.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-sandbox-macos/src/exec_status.rs:18-65,114-136`; `src/manifest/codec.rs:142-163`; `src/helper.rs:34-65` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: The execution-status owner reads through EOF or a 33-byte upper bound with no production timeout, nonblocking readiness, or cancellation interface. Empty EOF means success. The helper synchronously reads its framed manifest and writes readiness/activation before replacing itself with the target. Unit tests add a one-second socket read timeout, but production preparation does not.\n- Consequence: A stalled status/manifest writer can lock activation without any synthetic deadline. The tests do not establish cancellation or recovery from that stalled handshake. The exact session ownership behavior remains a separate file-level audit item.\n- Repair direction: Use explicit framed execution acknowledgment and cancellable I/O under durable execution custody. Preserve exact helper identity and distinguish target exec success from helper disappearance.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQH3BnwC7Px6UwcCrRYWokuDlIE+xui5+7cRCnHT8JUaA0qvnbEHyymMnhfAJzjmUkENiBmqH4orMxVsCxbCPyQc="}
