{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3183,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.190814799Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"6752deb4-4c54-5fb9-820e-79627d70d0a9","title":"[L594] macOS preparation repeats bounded synchronous integrity work and collapses resource failures","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L594.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-sandbox-macos/src/preparation.rs:102-121,123-145,188-215`; `src/preparation/resources.rs:15,27-54,87-158,180-230`; `src/error.rs:124-140,199-206` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Every preparation synchronously resolves paths and reads/hashes the installed helper with a 16 MiB cap; secret staging files are capped at 1 MiB. Reads are bounded during reading but have no cancellation. Additional protected roots must exist and remain canonical; secret-file destinations must have canonical existing parents and be absent. Proxy, secret, and protected-handle failures are replaced with generic errors, while OS errors preserve only their error kind. Diagnostics cap detail at 512 bytes with UTF-8-safe truncation.\n- Consequence: Slow storage can block preparation, and callers cannot reliably distinguish transient preparation/cleanup causes from a reauthorization requirement. Integrity/path checks are necessary evidence boundaries; the helper/material limits are representation gates rather than session TTLs.\n- Repair direction: Stream integrity work with cancellation and explicit progress, preflight selected delivery paths, and preserve typed underlying failures and exact cleanup obligations for resumable preparation.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3