ression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQL9qyxYjWpjDZSl8HpuU8LlmW4B1ESSqfuCBPQNz26c6VM5JDIbqdxWcrUSgiGwu7v+d15y+epfmK43fOfpROQs="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3185,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.194927374Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"8b85fb90-3ebc-5c12-bdfe-ff9f70819075","title":"[L595] macOS support probing uses mandatory synthetic deadlines and weak native evidence","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L595.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-sandbox-macos/src/probe.rs:190-198,227-232,272-318`; `src/probe/native.rs:17-54,76-125` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Probe configuration requires a positive connect timeout with no untimed option. The same duration governs Seatbelt and keychain subprocess polling; expiration kills and waits for the probe, while a `try_wait` error returns without explicit reaping. Deadline construction uses unchecked `Instant` addition. OS-version output is collected synchronously before its size check. The Seatbelt probe compiles an allow-default profile despite the evidence field describing deny-default support; process containment runs a single `/usr/bin/true`, and resource support checks existing rlimits rather than installing all advertised controls. An absent proxy endpoint counts as supported.\n- Consequence: A slow but compatible host can be classified unsupported, and a passing probe does not establish the advertised selected-policy containment or resource enforcement. Boolean evidence obscures timeout versus unsupported behavior. These are source findings, not observed macOS execution results.\n- Repair direction: Make probe cancellation explicit and duration optional, preserve typed probe failures and cleanup ownership, and qualify the actual selected deny-default policy and enforcement path rather than replacing missing evidence with optimistic booleans.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGDNeO45SEo4phJ0JU04TDsi9BCv+qiIgzzyfuBKsff2nICE2vnRKAb2REHvJ6JajYEHPTUvJtJVru6TAGmz1Ak="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3186,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.197291536Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"8b85fb90-3ebc-5c12-bdfe-ff9f70819075","comment_uuid":"d67d0e8c-aa0b-47fb-b19c-fc43f46acc08","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L595: macOS support probing uses mandatory synthetic deadlines and weak native evidence.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/runtime/peritus-sandbox-macos/src/probe.rs:190-198,227-232,272-318; src/probe/native.rs:17-54,76-125. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nMake probe cancellation explicit and duration optional, preserve typed probe failures and cleanup ownership, and qualify the actual selected deny-default policy and enforcement path rather than replacing missing evidence with optimistic booleans.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCbqqAhB1Rd5Vq7v/gyOyjQeWvDV2W4WQpYvKqVBDbRkPIhACDYouYDI4/9OwKFhUZHRL65sATxOoP0fpu51mAQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3187,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.199454940Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"800e4cae-933b-5275-a89e-f41f64bda623","title":"[L596] macOS resource supervision has fixed traversal ceilings and fragile live sampling","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L596.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-sandbox-macos/src/resource_monitor.rs:21-23,42-75,118-167,183-279`; `src/resource_monitor/pids.rs:20-54`; `src/resource.rs:94-108,130-139` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Initial preparation and one-second disk samples traverse the entire workspace synchronously, rejecting more than one million entries. Any directory-entry or metadata error, including a concurrently removed file, becomes `SupervisorFailure` with cancel-and-reap. Disk usage subtracts an initial whole-workspace baseline and retains the greatest difference. Process enumeration has a fixed 16,384-member buffer and FD enumeration a 512 KiB buffer; exact-capacity results fail instead of growing. Failed per-process resource or FD queries can be skipped. CPU accounting sums live members plus root child accounting, with an explicit conservative double-counting comment. All eight resource dimensions must have hard or supervisor support, even when time limits are omitted.\n- Consequence: Large or actively changing repositories can terminate otherwise valid work, and synchronous samples delay cancellation. Net-baseline disk accounting can hide growth after unrelated deletion, while incomplete native samples can undercount usage. Sampling cadence is not a run deadline. CPU and wall-time omission are represented by zero; CPU zero is skipped by both the monitor and native rlimit installer.\n- Repair direction: Use resumable, cancellation-aware sampling that tolerates disappearance races, grow enumeration buffers with explicit capacity reporting, preserve unknown measurements, and distinguish omitted budgets from required control dimensions. Audit CPU aggregation against actual descendant lifetime accounting.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCRRLA6qYsewM6Km4chZzgm+rR/QBOXeOLDZRj/nduKPrclr/ECIYGEyvNz/LL/DpunccVkXDFrn//ymClg9fwY="}
