{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3197,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.222576932Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"98d75edb-2119-510d-bae7-d56f395682dd","title":"[L601] macOS observation limits describe different collections","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L601.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-sandbox-macos/src/session.rs:27,136-141,174-232`; `src/session/lifecycle.rs:95-131`; `src/session/observation_mapping.rs:42-70` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Configured observation capacity is silently clamped to 4,096 and values below five fail preparation. The bound applies to common lifecycle observations; native preparation separately appends all control/resource/proxy/secret mappings without checking it. A valid five-observation lifecycle therefore has more than five rich native observations. Phase changes precede lifecycle append errors, but the currently closed normal lifecycle requires at most five common observations, including cancellation.\n- Consequence: The limit is a representation/configuration gate with inconsistent collection semantics, not evidence of an ordinary running session timing out or exhausting its legal five-event lifecycle.\n- Repair direction: Define separate truthful retention contracts for lifecycle and rich control evidence, or use durable paged observations; validate reported capacities without a silent clamp.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEWmTTDdVGAwK0uuiDekeczdI+w0cmPy+vI7EV1Q9l03yBOLkGPFwO+FoLCd77jeswD