{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3199,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.226836602Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"eb2d9758-514f-5676-be1c-29a59bd61331","title":"[L602] macOS activation removes status ownership before fallible verification","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L602.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-sandbox-macos/src/session/lifecycle.rs:17-46`; `src/session/adapter.rs:47-49`; `src/session/cleanup.rs:24-34` in the same crate. Related status-channel blocking is recorded in L593.\n- Behavior: After containment checks, activation releases the protected exec-status handle from the launch, then performs status observation. If that observation fails, the phase remains prepared but the handle has already been removed; an identical activation retry fails with absent ownership. If observation succeeds, phase and recovery are changed before the lifecycle observation is appended.\n- Consequence: An interrupted or failed activation handshake cannot be resumed from the same prepared owner. Cleanup may still abandon that owner, but repeating activation cannot restore the consumed status capability.\n- Repair direction: Model activation as a durable staged transition with status validation and a committed ownership handoff, retaining enough evidence for exact retry or reconciliation after every fallible boundary.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCgObgHhok2YCqLAfxjo+r9J1tbA8aYo155NX7zju78pGDdtWanaXbsdWeJYOYtSZ5unHAEGFMjA3/iyZCH3ZQc="}
