{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3201,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.231364749Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"9dfdf3b4-6741-5098-a19e-6eac18c805b3","title":"[L603] macOS protected-secret metadata has separate finite capacities","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L603.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-sandbox-macos/src/secret.rs:14-16,47-59,161-172,204-241`.\n- Behavior: Protected-secret collections are capped at 128 before canonicalization; labels at 256 ASCII bytes; payloads at one MiB and must be nonempty. Native descriptors must be nonstandard positive signed-32-bit values. Some payload/label bounds are deferred from protected-handle construction to manifest conversion. Destination collisions are checked globally; label collisions are checked only between adjacent entries after sorting by descriptor.\n- Consequence: Oversized otherwise meaningful material fails a finite representation gate rather than a session deadline, potentially late in preparation. This utility's adjacency check alone does not establish global label uniqueness; later native launch validation is a separate boundary.\n- Repair direction: Unify selected delivery capacities and validate them before authority consumption; use one globally unique descriptor/label/destination representation, with streaming delivery for larger material where supported.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIaou0psswmRLHxr7mf7CnVLwKWExIq7upDZAig7f3ozHJlPk+/+jI9KFNm7IQpidm+CZnNdbDfqbYOx/i9FkQU="}
