{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3205,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.241105900Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"a685b204-d03b-5d99-9d5f-7e21a61a3e85","title":"[L606] Windows preparation consumes channel owners before later fallible compilation","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L606.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-sandbox-windows/src/channels.rs:33-53,63-85,117-170,173-184`; `src/preparation.rs:125-204,330-353`; `src/config.rs:44-56` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Managed proxy and secret preparations are taken from configuration before their preparation and staging succeed. Network preparation precedes secrets; terminal/resource/manifest/launch validation and native ACL installation follow channel allocation. A configured proxy forbids deny-all plans; configured secrets forbid secret-free plans. File-delivered material is reread in full. Errors replace the underlying proxy, lease, handle, and file failures with generic cancel-and-reap diagnostics.\n- Consequence: Exact preparation cannot simply retry after a transient downstream failure, and a general configured backend cannot handle plans omitting its optional channel requirements. Late failure relies on best-effort owner destruction rather than a durable preparation rollback transaction.\n- Repair direction: Preflight selected paths and all representation gates before consuming channel preparations, then retain a durable staged transaction with retryable ownership and underlying error evidence.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW