stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPQgYOkhRN9RbDpmkYakUrRkgVUsABBCMYg5hidspIe0WWBHsUybAaVypEtNUf62UhI8BIb3RTxwHlzbo79rmAU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3207,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.245715482Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"953de286-8f5c-5b63-b5fc-29250838ae18","title":"[L607] Windows path and ACL projection imposes workspace-shape and finite-root gates","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L607.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-sandbox-windows/src/filesystem.rs:13,29-82,85-102,135-177`; `src/filesystem/path.rs:12,28-56,65-83,188-220,235-258`; `src/native/path.rs:10-32`; `src/preparation.rs:304-326` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Protected roots and external read-only inputs each cap at 256 before deduplication. Paths cap at 32,767 UTF-16 units and reject UNC/device/ADS/traversal/reserved syntax; identity folds ASCII case only, and native canonicalization uses lossy text conversion. Every resolved native object and existing ancestor must exist and be reparse-free; protected roots must remain on the workspace volume. Any allow rule containing a protected root is rejected, so a broad workspace allow combined with protected metadata cannot be represented even with explicit deny entries. Native ACL installation also requires every exact target to exist.\n- Consequence: Normal broad workspace grants or creation rules for absent objects can fail despite a checked plan. These are policy/representation and filesystem-shape blockers rather than session expiration; path-integrity requirements need a safe representable implementation, not blanket removal.\n- Repair direction: Compile component-aware deny-dominant permissions using native identities, negotiate explicit path capacities, and support checked parent-based creation without requiring the new object to exist.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHT9XT0sIcCvlzVAgx2HHiVsVy23nKDm22AumNXC+9xIKbjkBxSOKPQmuDdYi1o4vWPKIen/IEgU3uB0sAwFVQc="}
