ce and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLmY0qxZchK8k4JhcaauagoPjSWxBP7k7KtDgO4CVEFxiwXJDjK82YYQLLrlbsFjLmBtzKvEmsnKz99jIPfkTA4="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3209,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.250257450Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"de41e444-863c-515d-b6b2-7e1b22abbb0b","title":"[L608] Windows ACL rollback ownership is not durable across owner loss","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L608.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-sandbox-windows/src/filesystem/acl.rs:112-140,167-174`; `src/filesystem/acl/reversal.rs:18-58,91-139,160-201` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: ACL backup filenames use only ACL-plan digest and entry index. The list of backup paths and restore parents is retained in the transaction's in-memory reversal vector. Save/apply/restore invoke synchronous `icacls.exe` from PATH with no cancellation. Failed installation attempts restoration but discards that restoration result before returning the original error; `Drop` also ignores restore errors. Explicit restore correctly retains unsuccessful reversals for same-owner retry, while successful backup deletion failures are ignored.\n- Consequence: A crash or failed drop can leave modified ACLs and backup files without a reconstructible pending reversal list. Concurrent equal plans share backup filenames without per-operation identity here. Synchronous ACL tooling can block preparation and release indefinitely.\n- Repair direction: Persist each exact preimage and reversal obligation under a unique transaction before mutation, serialize conflicting ACL owners, and implement cancellable resumable application/reversal with explicit cleanup outcomes.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOHn56NujOiUmSze33kRcf4Upl25JXav71fOtStsDeCv1832v9Xujw2jrj3LBLtCj9kHnyj40v6w6NVkdB5rQQM="}
