ve the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBDmdgH68nAtt8fMa0QQ3oO7DGPb8/fDGZnY47OEOcDQgvYmWoLeQw2waabtK/9dhnqxFs1iPpMa8EIW5wAKZAE="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3213,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.259669358Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"0f1530ef-b69c-5f0f-bb1f-63a49b3470a7","title":"[L610] Windows kill-on-close jobs tie target lifetime to the helper owner","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L610.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-sandbox-windows/src/process.rs:80-105`; `src/native/job.rs:20-58,65-74`; `src/native/mod.rs:21-41`; `src/native/launch.rs:91-127` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Every Job Object is unnamed, kill-on-close, and owned in helper activation state. It installs finite active-process and memory limits plus an optional CPU limit; CPU zero correctly omits `JOB_OBJECT_LIMIT_JOB_TIME`. CPU milliseconds must fit signed 64-bit 100-nanosecond representation. The helper creates the target suspended, assigns it to that job, resumes, and waits indefinitely for root completion. Target/job identity and ownership are not made durable by these native routines.\n- Consequence: Helper owner death or final job-handle closure kills the target tree, so an otherwise persistent logical session cannot survive that ownership loss. The infinite wait is not a synthetic run deadline; the persistence blocker is owner lifetime. Representation overflow can reject a very large explicit CPU budget.\n- Repair direction: Keep native containment ownership in a durable supervisor with explicit adoption/handoff and independently inspectable job identity; preserve no-CPU-deadline semantics while negotiating representable explicit budgets.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQL7QD2sY+KJai5nNxcOvkJ+2HX21H0RMDTiyaCMdqYYApK3/RtXYlL56C5+h96owsgodrWCKfDZSgGnA70ohWQE="}
