g commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOsMSFFRvqpp9FbDhsuUfIsPknkDXrBdgWXxPo7HpQAQgEZgc06p7q/ZnOfvjz0e9HTQ5hViFWB6a4FyJTbBtQE="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3215,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.264086646Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"3e100cb5-a5cf-56c6-b568-e9bd016a6976","title":"[L611] Windows ConPTY control workers have detached and blocking ownership","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L611.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-sandbox-windows/src/native/handle.rs:40-66,69-164`.\n- Behavior: Terminal dimensions are accepted as unsigned 16-bit earlier but converted to signed 16-bit during native activation. Input and control thread join handles are immediately discarded. Input relay and signal control hold the same writer mutex across blocking write/flush; close-input control needs that mutex. Read errors, malformed controls, resize failure and write failure silently stop workers. Terminal destruction closes the console without joining those workers.\n- Consequence: Backpressure can prevent control and input-close progress, and a worker can silently disappear without a session failure observation. Native teardown cannot establish worker quiescence from retained joins; late console controls can race owner destruction. The 8,192-byte relay chunk is a throughput choice, not a lifetime quota.\n- Repair direction: Retain and supervise workers, interrupt blocked I/O through explicit cancellation, serialize console lifetime and controls, and validate native terminal dimensions before consuming execution authority.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNaHvB1cHPftJqwtck43nvaTiJBot1WOifdPmsOzAhD/Qln5zbewLIBGBxENBeEWuRJ82u/idufjO88BmPgxtgs="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3216,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.266472172Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"3e100cb5-a5cf-56c6-b568-e9bd016a6976","comment_uuid":"4cb32713-f906-4852-846d-27204582a453","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L611: Windows ConPTY control workers have detached and blocking ownership.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/runtime/peritus-sandbox-windows/src/native/handle.rs:40-66,69-164. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nRetain and supervise workers, interrupt blocked I/O through explicit cancellation, serialize console lifetime and controls, and validate native terminal dimensions before consuming execution authority.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQL+5Xp8uO8NjeRSIgEncSRaMJvEApBXdMUKysk+cvlhIzHmHx6fxVmjPqktCGAaDafxyZKf7rLe9IUqZkE0Cvw0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3217,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.268726104Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"631634bc-9665-5f42-baa2-2ca115aab67d","title":"[L612] Windows secret reader rejects material exactly at its advertised one-MiB boundary","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L612.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-sandbox-windows/src/native/secret.rs:16-17,29-80,93-123`; `src/channels.rs:155-184` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Protected secret reading checks `len == 1,048,576` before attempting the EOF read. Exactly one MiB is therefore rejected even if the next read would prove EOF. Reads are synchronous with no cancellation and close the inherited source handle before returning the read outcome. Environment delivery requires UTF-8. File delivery uses ordinary `fs::write`, allowing create/truncate and retaining no exact file-cleanup owner in staged secrets, whose state contains only environment entries.\n- Consequence: Material at the declared maximum fails activation; a partial read cannot retry the closed source. File creation/write failure can leave material whose cleanup is not represented by this helper staging owner. Surrounding session teardown is being inspected separately. These are capacity and staged-effect problems, not timeouts.\n- Repair direction: Read at most maximum plus one byte with an explicit length/EOF contract, preserve ownership through fallible staging, and retain exact private-file cleanup obligations through helper and session recovery.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAA