ance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQN7mkHei6RnVqBXHDS/XqnnBgGX5sjY+V+dq6xK4Vdttu4WpoTs8Y/ZyT6uRk9h8pvtSWstvEdE+g9EQcOKaBg8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3223,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.282738381Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"7295b09e-655d-58ad-a069-b4dafa99ea85","title":"[L615] Windows proxy cleanup has a permanent retry-required dead end","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L615.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-sandbox-windows/src/session/teardown.rs:12-36,39-63`; `src/session.rs:144-147,265-316`; `src/release.rs:15-36` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Proxy release takes its owner before shutdown. A shutdown error or incomplete join sets `RetryRequired`; later calls immediately fail without retaining an owner or offering a reconciliation method. Release still attempts independent ACL/filter/secret/handle cleanup, but reports aggregate booleans and loses underlying failures. Exposed partial progress includes only ACL and proxy states. Error translation quarantines retry-required native cleanup instead of preserving its recovery guidance.\n- Consequence: A transient proxy shutdown failure permanently prevents complete release within this owner. Independent progress and missing owner evidence cannot be reconstructed from the recovery record. ACL and WFP same-owner retries retain their owners correctly, so the proxy dead end is a distinct ownership bug.\n- Repair direction: Keep retryable proxy/join ownership and persist all cleanup dimensions, preserving underlying causes and an explicit reconciliation transition rather than an unrepairable enum state.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHB6XwfAVlJYO9Sin6Z3MaXGoIqNtRSZRN5FCKiHc/RHb3LMdTdWsGcEoKI9/5dRZ4/4RNJpXbGjl9Yxcqc44Qo="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3224,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.285133530Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"7295b09e-655d-58ad-a069-b4dafa99ea85","comment_uuid":"944a6607-5f92-4460-b592-3a88743edf61","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L615: Windows proxy cleanup has a permanent retry-required dead end.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/runtime/peritus-sandbox-windows/src/session/teardown.rs:12-36,39-63; src/session.rs:144-147,265-316; src/release.rs:15-36. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nKeep retryable proxy/join ownership and persist all cleanup dimensions, preserving underlying causes and an explicit reconciliation transition rather than an unrepairable enum state.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCT+JM8uXagm2Q8hDE9WlI5NgDuo0wHSx4lID4YPm8F2b8JRdKeJAZPQRByXwrQCny1J7F5z4TANFiIOXJBGZA0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3225,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.287388957Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"813b4cb8-6e01-5051-82ed-ed51333e9e2b","title":"[L616] Windows managed networking adds a five-second native transaction wait and ephemeral filter ownership","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L616.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-sandbox-windows/src/native/wfp.rs:38-75,78-140,262-265,324-330`; `src/network_filter.rs:22-40,53-60`; `src/network.rs:23-42`; `src/native/wfp/keys.rs:18-36` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: WFP sessions set `txnWaitTimeoutInMSec` to 5,000, use dynamic nonpersistent ownership, and permit only IPv4 loopback TCP. Public route construction accepts loopback IPv6, which fails later during native installation. Probe installs a disabled block but does not exercise actual permitted connections or both enabled block filters. Filters select package SID rather than one process; no per-run AppContainer uniqueness check occurs here. Explicit release retains a failed engine close for retry, while drop ignores failure. Calls are synchronous and underlying BFE statuses become generic errors.\n- Consequence: The fixed five-second field is a native transaction wait policy, not an execution lifetime; these routines do not start a WFP transaction, so deadline activation is not established by this read. Dynamic filters cannot be adopted from this owner record after restart. Route-family mismatch fails after earlier allocation. Shared package identities require concurrent-run qualification rather than assuming process-specific filtering.\n- Repair direction: Align route negotiation with native IPv4 support before consumption, remove an unjustified fixed transaction-wait policy or make selected native semantics explicit, and keep filter ownership durable with exact package isolation and connection-level qualification.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMQbhCmtHkN4hBGTBHuL9HhYZEfqDFcb4a+ekNGohmfUPl8TPnSvROFCUXnNFFWhCsy0J7Azq5MbC4r238gy+gg="}
