{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3229,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.296506173Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"2d62f08d-4c47-55b9-93a7-5dfa45315a03","title":"[L618] Windows helper narrows target status and hides post-activation failure causes","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L618.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/runtime/peritus-sandbox-windows/src/native/launch.rs:108-127`; `src/helper_process.rs:9-13,34-44`; `src/runner.rs:139-168` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Native target exit is read as unsigned 32-bit then clamped to signed-32-bit maximum; helper entry converts the resulting signed value to unsigned eight-bit ExitCode, replacing values outside 0-255 with generic failure. Post-activation target execution/observation errors are replaced by reserved TargetCreate. Phase-aware classification correctly preserves the reserved numeric range when activation has been observed, but cannot restore discarded wide status or failure causes.\n- Consequence: Windows target errors and platform exception values can lose their original identity, undermining root-cause diagnosis and recovery selection. Actual target status publication is constrained by the helper's artificial eight-bit representation rather than the native Windows status width.\n- Repair direction: Carry exact native target termination and structured post-activation failures through the authenticated status channel and journal independently of helper process exit.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE