{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3231,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.301718862Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"656d342c-1208-5200-9d56-a028e417d5b4","title":"[L620] Evidence storage retains a five-second contention timer and fixed SQLite representation bounds","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L620.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/state/peritus-evidence/src/sqlite/store.rs:23-64`; `src/sqlite/connection.rs:7-44`; `src/sqlite/row.rs:158-173`; `src/error.rs:81-94` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Default options install a five-second SQLite busy timeout. The API requires a Duration rather than an explicit wait-until-canceled policy. Connection setup also fixes SQLITE_LIMIT_LENGTH at 32 MiB and disables attached databases; journal positions must fit positive SQLite INTEGER. Busy and locked failures preserve their source and return Retry, but this crate supplies no persistent wait/retry owner.\n- Consequence: Ordinary database contention can interrupt evidence work at an artificial elapsed-time threshold. Integer, attachment, and row-size restrictions are storage/protocol constraints, not run deadlines; removing the timeout must not erase their error distinctions.\n- Repair direction: Carry cancellation and a durable contention continuation through the storage owner; separate optional operational waiting policy from schema representability. Source review only; no tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDbCS/axArGCp2hO22BecORqPzKYPcbo2P+JOnrnEQW5M6+Q7WQ6u3IKy3mx5TEUhMmrOyuPmgfodaA2DhVYsAM="}
