on: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQK1Im9p4bKzWDTZ0nHyamoSttpqeQLr6sF+UgsybMRAWw5/ngKEyIVk1htUNHiGnoELSyxPYpFlP+3gkNAQFzA4="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3233,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.307165130Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"4e3b83bd-6428-5542-b940-8c47cb542eab","title":"[L621] Evidence and bundle limits reject legitimate scale, sometimes after output has already been written","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L621.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/state/peritus-evidence/src/record.rs:10-13,58-69,103-110`; `src/manifest.rs:12,198-275`; `src/bundle/plan.rs:20-65,94-191,206-238`; `src/bundle/assemble.rs:43-70,80-119,137-159`; `src/bundle/verify.rs:15,54-75,227-275` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Evidence caps artifact and cause lists at 4,096 and canonical tags at 64 bytes. Bundle defaults require positive finite limits: 4,096 entries per section, 1 GiB per entry, and 4 GiB total. The manifest independently hard-caps sections at 4,096, so increasing the public entry limit cannot raise the portable bound. Planning loads/verifies requested records and artifacts before its count rejection; it does not establish entry/total byte feasibility. Assembly writes earlier sections and artifact headers before late size/hash/total failures. Portable metadata has a separate fixed 32 MiB reader cap; sized reads allocate their vector before the total-byte check.\n- Consequence: Large valid work can fail late despite successful planning and leave partial caller-owned output. These are per-record/export bounds rather than session expiry; their fixed format ceiling and configurable operational budgets are presently conflated.\n- Repair direction: Version or stream large collections; preflight the exact serialized byte plan, publish completed output atomically, and expose resumable export cursors instead of forcing whole-export failure. Check remaining budgets before allocation. Source review only; no tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDMyMUKlhmr2+FOqXXB7v3RQQ1x20N2GLpkuUtnCkXzNNgKZSDXThd2oeO0mxfvtGovms/F7FDmRiuzeIQEb5QU="}
