, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEiKkwWm53epLu4KPFrcxVxl4qGFZgeP3+k3fJH/j69btuXivNqJ/z8uiNDVsMR5Q5wiHIjTquD6IRcWwIbbXwk="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3235,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.312354044Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"f2123253-989a-5b55-acb2-aa7a31d9a3d2","title":"[L622] Admitted causal history across revisions cannot be represented by the current portable bundle policy","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L622.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/state/peritus-evidence/src/causality.rs:35-67`; `src/bundle/plan.rs:94-119,206-238`; `src/freshness.rs:35-76`; `tests/admission.rs:137-176`; `tests/freshness.rs:27-89` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Admission requires causal parents to exist and have earlier journal positions; it does not require their revision to equal the child's. Bundle planning requires all records to be current against one supplied revision, every causal parent to be included, and all included records to share the same exact revision tuple. Explicit invalidation is durable and dominates drift; no elapsed-time TTL appears in this freshness implementation.\n- Consequence: A valid current record citing an older-revision parent has no successful bundle selection: omitting the parent breaks ancestry, while including it breaks currentness/revision equality. This is a source-derived history/export incompatibility, not proof that the installed run hit this path. The ancestry test only uses one revision.\n- Repair direction: Distinguish historical causal provenance from a present-tense authority assertion. Preserve and export historical ancestors with their original bindings while checking current authority only where required. Source review only; no tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQA