ants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKqlX7+dETLh7SLr5XvFGar7jzfLtQVN6MZiJJvpXH2gUKX3KM9/QRV3ahXaOjJFS3FxXFfQtvSJ0eisb9D48ws="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3239,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.323931599Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"3909f6ec-8d3f-5cd2-bc13-e6c016aac408","title":"[L624] Evidence startup holds a write transaction for a full catalog scan and has no quarantine reconciliation operation","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L624.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/state/peritus-evidence/src/sqlite/quarantine.rs:49-76,84-106,159-199`; `src/sqlite/row.rs:56-104,107-155`; `src/sqlite/store.rs:57-64` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Every open begins an immediate transaction, materializes every active identity, and fully validates each record plus normalized collections and artifact roots before commit. CorruptCatalog rows receive a digest-bound copy in quarantine and remain in the original table; load rejects any quarantined identity. This module exposes observation/count APIs but no restore or reconciliation operation. Malformed identity bytes fail the identity scan before individual containment; other scan failures abort startup.\n- Consequence: Startup work grows with the entire catalog while holding the writer lock, interacting with L620's five-second contention failure. Quarantine correctly prevents corrupt evidence from being silently reused, but a repaired dependency does not itself make that identity usable again.\n- Repair direction: Retain corruption checks and copied evidence, but make verified scan progress durable and bounded per transaction; implement explicit digest-checked reconciliation/rebuild ownership rather than a permanent unusable identity with an operator-only recovery label. Source review only; no tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBLI0EJhet1xg09NsE53ZEz6wQAGREJqDhOIGo50+32/yGckU1LhiroQ9ZdqaunQSVHQi3sfZFepMtSWb3Qu8gQ="}
