{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3243,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.334285230Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"81b7d98d-e2d6-512a-b791-5f1affc2716d","title":"[L627] Any journal advance forces an in-memory genesis rebuild rather than incremental continuation","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L627.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/state/peritus-projection/README.md:20-32`; `src/catalog.rs:124-155`; `src/rebuild.rs:45-55`; `src/replay.rs:75-129`; `src/fold.rs:44-94`; `src/sqlite/store.rs:80-125`; `src/agent.rs:86-119` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Startup compares against the exact final position/head and selects RebuildFromGenesis on any position change. Replay requires the complete contiguous export from position one, creates fresh state, folds all records, encodes the entire state, and computes another whole-state invariant encoding. Checkpoints bind digests rather than providing a typed state decoder or replay cursor. Candidate work exists only in memory until the final install. Each configured projection independently drives this path; this crate has no incremental catch-up, automatic startup coordinator, or cancellation/continuation API.\n- Consequence: An interrupted or contended rebuild repeats old reads and computation from genesis; costs grow with retained history. Agent projection entries retain phase/counters/digests, not the complete context or reducer state needed to resume a turn. A valid derived checkpoint alone does not establish session reconnection.\n- Repair direction: Persist an integrity-bound typed checkpoint and aggregate cursors, apply verified suffixes, and retain rebuild phase progress without changing the authoritative run/context identity. Source review only; no tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEiPu27tN1FmO5wFH/NJjt2fy0sjZERjrce7h8Ax0ASQ3cu7Tr0s8VV5R0xwuO8HPW7euvPY4QzQdso7gvn/rww="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3244,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.336583038Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"81b7d98d-e2d6-512a-b791-5f1affc2716d","comment_uuid":"f59298d8-2ef6-4264-a138-f095e0fed887","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L627: Any journal advance forces an in-memory genesis rebuild rather than incremental continuation.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: src/catalog.rs:124-155; src/rebuild.rs:45-55; src/replay.rs:75-129; src/fold.rs:44-94; src/sqlite/store.rs:80-125; src/agent.rs:86-119. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nPersist an integrity-bound typed checkpoint and aggregate cursors, apply verified suffixes, and retain rebuild phase progress without changing the authoritative run/context identity. Source review only; no tests run.\n\nPreserve: committed command/event identity, exact causal and digest roots, exclusive ownership, atomic publication, reference-safe artifact retention and verified recovery from the last durable frontier. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCqNnbRvQ62VQdy+2HsMgvB/fPUjdmn3ibBCoqXVc4qglTvL60GM1e1KVXcX6FHULu0lrMBanmd+l2E2vM0eBgQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3245,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.338878734Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"75884c13-2a1d-5021-970a-01abef84788d","title":"[L628] Projection installation compares generation ownership but does not check that its candidate still represents the current journal","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L628.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/state/peritus-projection/src/sqlite/swap.rs:22-91,147-191`; `src/sqlite/schema.rs:3-28`; `tests/rebuild.rs:27-88` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Atomic install validates the candidate's own payload digest/count and compares only the caller's expected active generation. It checks no authoritative current journal position/head in the install transaction. A journal advance without a competing projection install leaves that CAS unchanged, so an older candidate can still become active; a later startup then asks for another genesis rebuild. All old generation payloads remain in SQLite, with no garbage-collection operation in this crate. Identical valid bindings are reused and a stale generation CAS rolls back atomically.\n- Consequence: Busy active journals can repeatedly obsolete expensive rebuilds without a suffix catch-up plan. Repeated changed bindings retain complete duplicate derived payloads and grow disk usage. This is a consistency/work-amplification gap; no installed recurrence is claimed.\n- Repair direction: Compare the candidate's authoritative journal binding at activation or atomically catch up to a verified suffix; retain the old active generation until success and reclaim only unreferenced derived generations under an explicit retention owner. Source review only; no tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPlDWdYSsjm68RJsecJnseg36rTYqmVbuAqEaSzJ0I/7HhXZbvzjEC8fi+sQwqVfM0J7hJJxxkJa7NMSzbtgfww="}
