e the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAvFE/Slw2/xHmYUpfFVmD0tBmeFvIOGTsVOYEjomo5RecReaqpoCux7krQ4UYaVyABm3UYnfIwK0l3SWrayCQg="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3247,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.344465562Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"be34317d-5d27-556e-bb89-534adba4a0fc","title":"[L629] Malformed projection metadata bypasses the advertised reasoned rebuild plan","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L629.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/state/peritus-projection/src/sqlite/store.rs:80-125,157-209`; `src/catalog.rs:124-155`; `src/sqlite/swap.rs:178-191`; `tests/rebuild.rs:90-125` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: plan_startup propagates load_active parsing failures rather than returning a rebuild reason. Invalid generation/position/count values or wrong digest lengths therefore return CorruptCatalog/Rebuild directly. A valid-length payload corruption does reach PayloadCorrupt and can be replaced. Reuse verifies payload bytes and schema/head/position bindings but does not independently reconstruct or bind the stored invariant digest and record_count; they can differ from the payload without changing that reuse decision.\n- Consequence: An embedding caller that only handles RepairAction can stop startup instead of rebuilding a nonauthoritative catalog. Current tests qualify payload-byte corruption, not malformed catalog fields or inconsistent invariant/count metadata. The safety of authoritative journal data is not inferred from derived-catalog reuse.\n- Repair direction: Normalize derived-catalog corruption into an explicit rebuild/containment plan, validate complete checkpoint metadata, and preserve original diagnostic bytes without treating projection corruption as a reason to repair valid journal history. Source review only; no tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkih