{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3249,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.349060098Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"d3babb92-4688-51a7-a4c7-f647478116b4","title":"[L630] Global projection replay rejects a changed revision or unsupported historic family before an unrelated fold can proceed","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L630.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/state/peritus-projection/src/replay.rs:83-99,133-182`; `src/artifacts.rs:124-129,175-179`; `src/journal_catalog.rs:120-138`; `src/authority.rs:118-143`; `tests/rebuild.rs:128-183`; `tests/rebuild/journal_fixture.rs:33-65` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Every projection checks all records against the frozen family/schema registry and forbids changing an aggregate's exact revision digest. The journal fixture can durably append such a revision change, which replay then rejects. Artifact folds ignore event payloads but still pass through these global gates. Typed payload checks occur in individual relevant folds; the generic catalog accepts registered framed bytes, and authority family 94 has no typed decoder here.\n- Consequence: One incompatible historical record can prevent every projection rebuild, including projections unrelated to that family. Removing timers does not repair this history-compatibility barrier. Registry/header validity and typed replay/reducer validity are distinct contracts.\n- Repair direction: Define versioned history migrations/decoders and explicit aggregate revision transitions, preserving exact immutable provenance; make the journal admission and projection replay contracts agree. Do not silently skip authoritative corruption. Source review only; no tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCFM538r/Rx9U0mxXI8E6qI2KlU5gEI7KNbNOEQ/8yAevfyvx/VAsM7v60kyokJyP3lBTgNy0Cy5z+qCAIu3wQ4="}
