lready owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQG+YnDvvJ8BF0V8gfDVDrOFyieDHOxlbcClwz7Ft/LjK4KuBH29ugRmj4EE9O/POM5L5Uv9rXFCea95luJrZrgA="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3253,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.358118139Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"7cf6ea42-13ec-5d34-94fc-0cbad6727013","title":"[L635] Filesystem traversal/search loses progress at bounds and silently excludes some search scope","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L635.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/tools/peritus-tools-fs/src/read.rs:239-324,327-365,377-395`; `tests/filesystem_tools.rs:50-60`.\n- Behavior: Traversal materializes the entire selected subtree and returns an error at the next entry beyond the bound, discarding observed entries. It stops recursing at maximum_depth without a scope-truncated marker. Search first performs that whole walk, reads each eligible file, ignores binary and over-per-file-bound files, and only accounts UTF-8 bytes after the read. Total-byte or match overflow returns an error and discards all matches, with no continuation cursor. Preview text always contains the first UTF-8-safe 512 bytes of the line, even when the match occurs later. Case-insensitivity is ASCII-only. One no-follow symlink inspection failure rejects the entire traversal, as the test explicitly expects.\n- Consequence: Broad code exploration may repeatedly redo the same reads instead of obtaining the next page; a no-match success does not establish absence in skipped/deeper files. The 64 MiB scanned-text allowance does not bound bytes read from binary files. Rejecting traversal/special nodes is an integrity boundary, but whole-job failure is a separate recovery choice.\n- Repair direction: Return a truthful scope/skip summary and digest-bound continuation with retained partial results; budget actual I/O before reading and center match previews on the hit. Preserve no-follow guarantees while making unrelated unsafe entries separately reportable. Source review only; no tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAZR2++9WUwge9jRub82yxuS/df4nNZQLHbWZmy+LAf4We0XauLCCeUkJ+SmBxfp8u5+faOxTQiDMz7KOEXjvgs="}
