{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3257,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.367928575Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"0af38dda-d5fd-5e44-b22a-4bd49c80ba89","title":"[L637] Filesystem dispatch is synchronous, loses error distinctions, and retains candidate handoff only in its live object","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L637.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/tools/peritus-tools-fs/src/catalog.rs:115-118`; `src/dispatcher.rs:71-78,132-174,201-228,273-303,311-357`; `src/error.rs:77-94,125-131`; `src/read.rs:377-390` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Descriptors now have no timeout, but ControlSet::NONE and synchronous start provide no pause/cancel/progress handle. Terminal timing uses the same pre-execution AuthorityInstant as start and completion. Workspace inspection preserves only a broad recovery class, discarding the underlying code/source; every apply_patch error is collapsed to Workspace/Reconcile. CorrectInput failures request NewAction with no recovery route; Reobserve/Reauthorize also require a new action. A successful MutationOutcome for the later candidate step is held in an Option on the live FsDispatcher and can only be taken once; no reconstruction API exists here.\n- Consequence: Removing deadlines does not make long filesystem operations interruptible or restartable, and generic errors cannot tell a retry owner which exact state needs recovery. Losing the dispatcher loses this handoff value, connecting to the workspace candidate recovery gap already documented in L582. This is source behavior, not a fresh diagnosis of the live session.\n- Repair direction: Preserve typed redaction-safe causes and durable operation/outcome references, distinguish retry/reobserve/reconcile semantics, measure real completion, and introduce cancellable phase ownership without adding a new lifetime cutoff. Source review only; no tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEhsspu6XtDfsgKuXraF0REULCU0997TZuFRBZbFZU2f1RMyCWxItxVYNy9UBX2uIKfAWseZIEhewwOopLiZkQE="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3258,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.370277393Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"0af38dda-d5fd-5e44-b22a-4bd49c80ba89","comment_uuid":"ece063f6-dff3-419f-b6ef-56a50802c52d","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L637: Filesystem dispatch is synchronous, loses error distinctions, and retains candidate handoff only in its live object.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/tools/peritus-tools-fs/src/catalog.rs:115-118; src/dispatcher.rs:71-78,132-174,201-228,273-303,311-357; src/error.rs:77-94,125-131; src/read.rs:377-390. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nPreserve typed redaction-safe causes and durable operation/outcome references, distinguish retry/reobserve/reconcile semantics, measure real completion, and introduce cancellable phase ownership without adding a new lifetime cutoff. Source review only; no tests run.\n\nPreserve: exact candidate revision and artifact binding, complete finding/provenance conservation, independent reviewer evidence, truthful gate outcomes, protected user constraints and acceptance fail-closed on invalid evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQABePeOuGVVw6m5d5pKMbr7WS5TQMibg9Jxb+RTOR5e0/cXJIXG0GKLNOJyR5xb89s/hnM+OeqHdYHrCo6IvrAc="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3259,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.372618615Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"b1a46624-1e80-5549-8f6f-cb5e9331f5a3","title":"[L643] Git observation and rendering ceilings have no continuation protocol","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L643.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/tools/peritus-tools-git/src/schemas.rs:9-24`; `src/input.rs:8-60,125-137`; `src/render.rs:14-16,30-140,146-200`; `crates/tools/peritus-tool-protocol/src/result.rs:327-351` and the production JSON limits recorded in L636.\n- Behavior: Git diff accepts at most 100,000 entries and 8 MiB of patch; history accepts at most 1,024 commits. The renderer then keeps the first 500 items, at most 32 parents per commit, and only the first 48 KiB of patch, with truncation flags but no next cursor or patch byte-range request. Rendering also has to fit the independent production JSON and prepared-call output bounds. Model/human renderings are summaries; fuller detail is in structured output.\n- Consequence: A caller cannot page through a selected large result using this API. Long paths, subjects, or many-parent history can fail shared JSON construction rather than yielding a retrievable partial result. This is a source-derived composition gap, not a measured installed-session timeout or proof about downstream context delivery.\n- Repair direction: Make complete immutable observations retrievable by cursor or artifact, with bounded individual pages and consistent envelope accounting. Preserve truthful completeness metadata without requiring callers to repeat the same prefix.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNd0RcTI1xLnlFtpRdiB3DpOJ8PjiHlLZcNdKgsj0EuFdkIb8KgX572OuRlj4LlohWu6GxJW6uIrP069GzCOzAE="}
