ffects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEgYOU+JCYoHk1EOfQrZBW+k+lROkK+IVhIqNwZjJVsQRBYn3M9MfdXYXuVlOa489Eqiy8sgQXCrg2VePvFphAw="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3261,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.377290130Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"faad2d50-2429-5d29-994c-6a9f0510151f","title":"[L644] Git mutation can succeed before its terminal envelope is rejected","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L644.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/tools/peritus-tools-git/src/dispatcher.rs:117-173,185-233`; `src/dispatch_support.rs:23-45`; `src/render.rs:52-78`; `crates/tools/peritus-tool-protocol/src/result.rs:327-351`; workspace restart dependency in L582.\n- Behavior: Candidate/rollback dispatch consumes process-local optional mutation/candidate context, performs the workspace operation, renders, retains the resulting outcome, then builds the terminal result. Its preflight accepts 128-byte model/human limits instead of validating the eventual complete rendering. The rollback sentence `Restored {commit} as successor snapshot {snapshot}.` needs 129 ASCII bytes for a valid 64-character commit and 32-character snapshot, so that accepted bound can fail after the effect. Both result text lengths are checked by the protocol. Candidate result/JSON errors can likewise arise after publication.\n- Consequence: The effect and successful reply are not atomic. A caller can see a protocol error despite an applied mutation, while continuation depends on the same in-memory context/outcome rather than a durable receipt adoption API. The 129-byte boundary is derived from source; it was not executed against a SHA-256 repository.\n- Repair direction: Validate or safely render reply capacity before effect, and persist an exact-action result/reconciliation receipt that a replacement process can adopt without repeating the mutation.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPdrOuu6/HzqNKwDPTyuj8X1EYmBUnGMz4fkHWzIa6D0YGttuLfhsALJatqSNvkK7kPxik52iJ0PlySyLsucuwE="}
