sion: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHFgOxSXtxDnWVr3iHvHkbC5OHCojbuH/O6VGFg554mczDN9Iup0ViOf5hhFdlBErWgN719uMI9kyxxjoGis6A8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3263,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.381787676Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"c51f1b71-96e4-5d5f-86ac-be1c5d6aa0cf","title":"[L645] Registered Git merge is permanently unsupported; errors do not provide progress or retry detail","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L645.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/tools/peritus-tools-git/src/catalog.rs:29-54,119-132`; `src/dispatcher.rs:145-150,185-233`; `src/read.rs:195-225`; `src/dispatch_support.rs:65-117`; `src/error.rs:1-121`.\n- Behavior: The catalog advertises `git.merge` as lease-required history mutation, but both dispatcher and read implementation return Unsupported. That failure is Infrastructure/Workspace with NewAction and no recovery route. Workspace failures are broadly collapsed into reconciliation guidance; read retry guidance becomes reobservation. The catalog timeout is None and synchronous execution declares no controls or progress, recording the pre-execution authority instant as completion.\n- Consequence: A planner can repeatedly select an advertised operation that cannot run or retry without useful causal detail. Long synchronous work has no local progress/control surface. These are capability/error-contract blockers; there is no Git descriptor execution deadline left to remove.\n- Repair direction: Publish only supported operations or implement merge with durable authority and result recovery. Preserve actionable error/retry distinctions and report actual timing/progress for long observations.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IA