{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3265,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.386516818Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"2a0f91d9-e856-54eb-8228-83ad6c3719d4","title":"[L647] Quality defaults now omit execution deadlines but retain finite output and protocol limits","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L647.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/tools/peritus-tools-quality/src/catalog.rs:35-86`; `src/definition.rs:9-10,43-48,122-195,264-307`; `src/discovery.rs:124-143`; `src/plan.rs:43-92`; `src/dispatcher/run.rs:99-163`.\n- Behavior: Both quality descriptors and automatically discovered checks use None for execution timeout. Explicit definitions can still select a positive timeout through the legacy constructor or optional-timeout constructor; the plan, definition, and call must agree exactly. Default discovered output is 8 MiB; descriptors allow 8 MiB total output, 32 KiB model/human renderings, 4,096 controls, three artifacts, and 65,536 progress events. Definitions require positive finite output/parser bounds, gate names at most 128 bytes, source labels 256, environment profile names 64, and checked C2 argv.\n- Consequence: No synthetic quality default execution timer is present here. Output/representation ceilings and their cross-layer consistency still matter for long daily-driving checks, independently of user-selected deadlines and authority identity checks.\n- Repair direction: Keep omitted execution deadlines omitted through composition; separate explicit user constraints and integrity bindings from retrievable output/progress retention capacity.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCUkfCDyFESBDQxpjsuXvIYGGBzFuwJ5q2VB7yHc1cCw8XddzpVmAn7vg7opXyW8+F0rimunpNxQPqTefVSZAAk="}
