onregression: large histories and non-ASCII fields, queue/connection pressure, delayed acknowledgements, subscription gaps, disconnect/reconnect and daemon restart, proving snapshot recovery, preserved selection/context, responsive controls and no duplicate command. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQP07OySuk1UCg73gCXAh4k4Fd/WRaY4M8w3wURzLrmLTyIAL9Gm/NQEVQvN7t2vWvyNkFxMY+v4crL5B9Jomxwo="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3269,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.395783267Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"75f7241d-5e45-5546-9c54-da3a46694938","title":"[L649] Hidden quality rendering truncation and progress caps can turn successful work into incomplete evidence","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L649.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/tools/peritus-tools-quality/src/render.rs:9-39`; `src/execution/active.rs:18,76-100,129-140`; `src/execution/terminal.rs:35-78,82-105`; `src/result.rs:237-265,280-324`.\n- Behavior: Output rendering escapes the full retained byte slice before limiting it. Its shared text helper silently truncates at 16 KiB, below the advertised 32-KiB rendering limit. An escaped output between 16 and 32 KiB is returned with Complete metadata despite that additional truncation; a larger chosen tail is truncated again at its end. Progress above the selected event count is discarded and marked progress_truncated. The quality decoder considers that flag incomplete evidence even if the process, complete artifacts, output parser, and success predicate passed, changing a success into IncompleteEvidence with fresh-action reauthorization guidance.\n- Consequence: Model/human output can be misleadingly labeled complete, and a long successful check can be blocked solely by an informational progress count. The renderer also spends memory/time constructing bytes it will discard. These conclusions are source-derived, not an executed large-output check.\n- Repair direction: Render only the requested window with accurate truncation metadata; make progress pagination/loss distinct from result evidence completeness so progress capacity cannot invalidate a proven successful execution.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDax3B7rAF7qMfhROsJdO6XHQkEaqOj9uwt61apaycXcfKqfc+5uMaJdFKGAOiCW2xlBEzKlewYnoE3QX8KSBwI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3270,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.398003782Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"75f7241d-5e45-5546-9c54-da3a46694938","comment_uuid":"be94b07d-a24b-4a02-9a8c-150a1ac61744","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L649: Hidden quality rendering truncation and progress caps can turn successful work into incomplete evidence.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/tools/peritus-tools-quality/src/render.rs:9-39; src/execution/active.rs:18,76-100,129-140; src/execution/terminal.rs:35-78,82-105; src/result.rs:237-265,280-324. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nRender only the requested window with accurate truncation metadata; make progress pagination/loss distinct from result evidence completeness so progress capacity cannot invalidate a proven successful execution.\n\nPreserve: canonical digest and schema identity, shared writer/reader admissibility, malformed-input rejection before allocation, exact causal ordering, actual provider/OS capability boundaries and preserved accepted historical evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQF6893NPh+GHQU8FyNhiaHQ3v63kYXwu32Y/KGf+uEgbghENnxI4xwHUr4Gq4IxHoO0aDWAkXZZ1LvKdpUuIvgs="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3271,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.400199659Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"2942d1e2-111f-5b5f-b76c-14da38046e29","title":"[L650] Quality parsing depends on volatile event delivery rather than complete published artifacts","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L650.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/tools/peritus-tools-quality/src/execution/active.rs:20-63,83-93,116-127,143-177,216-235`; `src/parser.rs:25-70`; `src/observation.rs:104-139`.\n- Behavior: Selected parsers accumulate stdout/terminal bytes solely from process events in 256-event polls. Any sequence gap (including non-output events) or parser-buffer overflow permanently marks parsing incomplete. Complete output artifacts are published afterward, but the parser does not reopen those artifacts to recover missing bytes. The cursor, definition, parser buffer, flags, owner, and result are local memory. recover merely polls that same live object; there is no reconstruction/adoption constructor. With OutputParser::None the parser returns NotRequested immediately, while infrastructure/output completeness is still independently required.\n- Consequence: A lagging consumer can classify a correct check as InvalidResult despite complete recoverable output, and replacing the quality execution object cannot reconnect its parsing context. Complete evidence must remain required; the blocker is the delivery-dependent way it is obtained.\n- Repair direction: Parse content-addressed complete output or persist a resumable parser cursor/state, and implement durable same-operation owner/result adoption. Preserve failure on actually incomplete or invalid output.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEiDJRQLiApdKPknS6wei3FXbSfgiUZ8hCvR3S0WcqC6PTw3k9UNh9Y9NnW2fnwOcZ4XvXRKB9os0XnZnjzgMgM="}
