e and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJkKGa7+K9KQKH3LsistKGLW5MfqU14dURif9xeK7LEMOpC3bDMXn+LjBYbDYpxpowAGqCNoHj9W/IcWcCnSigg="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3273,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.405182445Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"473306b7-880e-5f7f-ad0e-f2c3b01cef63","title":"[L651] Quality completion consumes ownership before fallible publication and envelope assembly","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L651.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/tools/peritus-tools-quality/src/dispatcher/run.rs:179-207`; `src/execution/active.rs:143-177`; `src/execution/terminal.rs:35-78,107-130`; `crates/tools/peritus-tool-protocol/src/result.rs:327-351`.\n- Behavior: Launch takes the plan/backend/artifact store before the fallible gateway launch. Finalization takes the process owner before wait_and_publish, parser classification, result structure, timing, artifact references, and terminal-envelope creation. Only a fully built ToolResult is cached. Publication can return retained C2 terminal facts, but there is no durable local owner/result handoff for a later error. Preflight permits the spool bound to equal the entire call output bound, whereas the terminal protocol counts artifact bytes plus structured JSON against that same bound.\n- Consequence: Completion at the allowed artifact-byte ceiling can fail on metadata headroom after the work and publication occurred. A subsequent poll/recover can encounter quality-owner-missing rather than recover the finished result or retry artifact publication. The capacity boundary and restart gap were inspected, not experimentally reproduced.\n- Repair direction: Persist terminal facts and publication receipts before consuming ownership; reserve metadata capacity or account artifacts independently, and make final result assembly/publication retryable without rerunning the check.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAF6tc3woZTCt0Z+pLTzLBBPmVTioc8y4jchPXEMYesb62Okcv3LUZgZsx7K6dYa1Re7Jy2LtCmAndDguROXHQg="}
