{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3275,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.409667247Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"5e2e0150-4861-5397-acec-64df9a940e82","title":"[L652] Quality timeout/cancel/recovery classification can contradict its own decoder and remove recovery","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L652.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/tools/peritus-tools-quality/src/observation.rs:123-139`; `src/execution/terminal.rs:133-199`; `src/result/contract.rs:9-67`; `src/result.rs:248-265,280-324`; `src/execution/failure.rs:11-55`.\n- Behavior: Classification gives parser failure precedence, producing candidate InvalidResult when parsing is incomplete. Terminal failure construction separately gives TimedOut, Cancelled, or RecoveryIndeterminate disposition precedence. The decoder accepts those statuses only with candidate Infrastructure, so a timed-out/cancelled/indeterminate execution with incomplete parsing becomes MalformedOutput with Retryability::Never and RecoveryRoute::None. Process SelectBackend is also collapsed into reauthorization rather than retaining backend-selection guidance.\n- Consequence: The adapter can manufacture an envelope its own consumer rejects, obscuring the original interruption and disabling the recovery route that the terminal initially carried. Removing default timers alone cannot repair cancellation/restart behavior.\n- Repair direction: Derive structured outcome and terminal failure from one consistent classification, retain causal parsing/exit facts separately, and preserve the required recovery owner/route. Add producer-to-decoder cases for interrupted parsers.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFdiQ7qjEX3fFZ3AwqizwTLQMi5e5S/OLcmCp2q4bAsGfZcQIbrf+428DX75+L47Sig4I5qFvA8HKv2abCxgaQA="}
