ave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDpHsiM9rExZm0Vhx336W8Wv8vsQOD74W6HBWA+H24hGSS6it2dncfDgDhyAQQka7IHndHMEXY2CiZRus6n0awc="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3277,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.414113311Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"9286f030-ec40-517f-a7a7-8d4b47585dcc","title":"[L653] Quality working-directory declarations are not enforced consistently","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L653.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/tools/peritus-tools-quality/src/definition.rs:98-113,228-232`; `src/acceptance.rs:92-107`; `src/plan.rs:43-92`; `src/dispatcher/run.rs:99-163`; `src/snapshot.rs:109-127`.\n- Behavior: Acceptance hashes the definition's optional workspace-relative working directory. Plan compilation uses the independently supplied WorkingDirectory without checking that declaration; run validation compares argv, deadlines, and output but not the declared path. The clean-snapshot constructor instead requires the plan directory to equal the snapshot root exactly and be read-only, rejecting a valid directory within that snapshot. The plain constructor omits that extra clean-snapshot check.\n- Consequence: An explicit subdirectory check can run in a different directory or be rejected by the stricter constructor, despite an acceptance binding that describes the declared subdirectory. Default Cargo commands also need their write locations configured outside the read-only snapshot; this audit does not assume any particular installed environment profile.\n- Repair direction: Resolve the declared directory relative to the validated snapshot, bind that exact path/access into the execution plan, and validate the same relationship at every constructor and dispatch boundary.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBKm22U89xE4P21WokwMqfAmzcgBCWvZJnEh7iTRSSWNJGFhP4RAZh6iEJRSocMKFg8H2aMNYkJgXE7DEqCt3Q4="}
