s reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDQOOvRNrHw4wzXAUmdgzM9CJbeQn3Uck8P8LVevkFRAtsuTulWTheol4+zkt7EYAOGM0PrH/SA8HtpyBCp8NwE="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3283,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.427287182Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"6d176d0f-f9e0-5fb1-89f0-e2d3d44df11a","title":"[L660] Account status can block foreground setup and misclassify infrastructure failure as sign-out","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L660.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-provider-onboarding/src/account.rs:14,55-76,84-115,164-177,180-229`; `src/account/windows_tests.rs:18-99`.\n- Behavior: Account status uses synchronous Command::output with no local cancellation/progress surface and only checks the 64-KiB stdout/stderr cap after collecting both complete streams. Catalog observation probes Codex then Claude sequentially. Any unsuccessful status exit is SignedOut; launch failure, oversized output, or malformed Claude JSON becomes NeedsAttention without its actual diagnostic. Successful interactive login synchronously repeats status. Windows uses CREATE_NO_WINDOW and a Claude title opt-out; its regression exercises console isolation with a ten-second transport fixture.\n- Consequence: A hanging/noisy status command can hold up the calling UI despite the nominal output bound, and an infrastructure failure can send the user through unnecessary login again. These observations do not justify adding a synthetic session deadline. The Windows ten seconds are fixture values.\n- Repair direction: Make status discovery cancellable/asynchronous with incremental retention and explicit unknown/infrastructure outcomes, preserving credential-safe causal diagnostics and the existing console isolation.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQG4b1eaxI2nDcOnFa3/CM/UEtEswJfUPhPwGIfKL/8xXeyqB9hskYIzw4ueBrrQjQcMsIWPm0PyuKKmOJ5bl9AM="}
