{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3285,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.432030179Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"d8f90195-eda8-5c61-af1a-7f367ed9e267","title":"[L661] Provider installation has no execution/download timer here; a size gate and nonpersistent effect handoff remain","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L661.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-provider-onboarding/src/install.rs:32-60,72-111,126-154`; `README.md:7-10`; `src/direct.rs:87-125`.\n- Behavior: The approved installer download is HTTPS-only and at most 1 MiB by curl option and post-download metadata. It deliberately has no --max-time/--connect-timeout; run_command polls indefinitely at 100 ms. The README still claims download time limits. Installation uses a temporary script and ordinary child process with no durable adoption/cancellation state; on try_wait error it kills/waits that child, ignoring cleanup results. Direct credential publication precedes final non-secret profile validation; failed validation discards credential removal errors and returns the profile error.\n- Consequence: The installer timer was already removed in actual code. Size rejection remains, and interruption or cleanup failure has no persistent repair receipt in this crate. Credential cleanup after profile rejection can leave an unpublished resource, distinct from provider authentication or session expiration.\n- Repair direction: Align documentation with source; retain user cancellation and exact durable installation/credential-publication reconciliation without reintroducing synthetic time limits. Validate non-secret profile shape before effects and preserve cleanup failures.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBacInfMbbSMIvZ92LXThTO2Og/NGKZgc1wLagc2K3uFbPzvsC3jIx5XqKDHgYKyi4yu7T7dCqqTCaMF+7CAjAo="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3286,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.434425775Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"d8f90195-eda8-5c61-af1a-7f367ed9e267","comment_uuid":"6d63656d-b34d-4062-ae4f-6abe19c56ab3","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L661: Provider installation has no execution/download timer here; a size gate and nonpersistent effect handoff remain.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-provider-onboarding/src/install.rs:32-60,72-111,126-154; src/direct.rs:87-125. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nAlign documentation with source; retain user cancellation and exact durable installation/credential-publication reconciliation without reintroducing synthetic time limits. Validate non-secret profile shape before effects and preserve cleanup failures.\n\nPreserve: definitely-unaccepted versus ambiguously-accepted request state, exact native thread/profile identity, ordered provider observations, tool-result protocol, explicit cancellation and real provider/model capabilities. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJM7r3OzNbPWaSmuj5j4JkwbkaxuXaVMQQCEa88vFRxkQU1DvafYDutCwJ5cvI+j6x+doyMwoRtkDC8tVcG5iAs="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3287,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.436566636Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"056baa89-16c3-53d7-8bc7-c1413263e151","title":"[L662] Model onboarding blocks its caller while discovery owns an unreachable cancellation token","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L662.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-provider-onboarding/src/models.rs:14-29,32-125,128-143`; `src/direct.rs:59-74`; `src/error.rs:5-13`.\n- Behavior: Synchronous model discovery creates a scoped thread/current-thread Tokio runtime and joins it. It uses a fresh CancellationToken that callers cannot cancel, with HTTP/metadata limits delegated to provider-core. Anthropic/Google requests select page sizes 1,000, and compatible discovery requires an endpoint ending exactly in /responses or /chat/completions. Unknown/manual-model handling is delegated to the caller; model discovery does not silently supply a bundled list.\n- Consequence: Avoiding a nested async-runtime error does not make setup responsive or resumable; a slow discovery still blocks the calling thread with no UI cancellation handoff. Request shape/endpoint gates and provider-core bounds are distinct from inference/session lifetime. Pagination behavior remains owned by the separately reviewed provider-core discovery implementation.\n- Repair direction: Expose asynchronous cancellable metadata discovery and retain exact errors/selected-model facts, with explicit paging where the provider advertises it. No model/provider request was sent during this audit.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFLCfkJKKMwErKaIrIcc0nPzWWe98jgyRF8PkHpykfRzcClx7EG6uVmGulcQ0DzViCQsl7PN+X4OlvLfVcPGGQM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3288,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.438890641Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"056baa89-16c3-53d7-8bc7-c1413263e151","comment_uuid":"c283c482-9bf0-4fc9-b916-670a33b0a8fc","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L662: Model onboarding blocks its caller while discovery owns an unreachable cancellation token.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-provider-onboarding/src/models.rs:14-29,32-125,128-143; src/direct.rs:59-74; src/error.rs:5-13. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nExpose asynchronous cancellable metadata discovery and retain exact errors/selected-model facts, with explicit paging where the provider advertises it. No model/provider request was sent during this audit.\n\nPreserve: canonical digest and schema identity, shared writer/reader admissibility, malformed-input rejection before allocation, exact causal ordering, actual provider/OS capability boundaries and preserved accepted historical evidence. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQH2YsFrNYPmKD9qoFD3kGUAIfl0Rs//YbbZJk6weEjSn+mflY6Fgq6suzJ08ARLcqSH28rvF0KMuYqttSvDdxgY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3289,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.441220339Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"c328505a-468a-5e77-8548-73610eaa2ac3","title":"[L663] Interactive daemon startup now has no synthetic readiness deadline, but readiness is only endpoint reachability","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L663.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-launcher/src/app.rs:72-99`; `src/daemon.rs:54-78,121-191,193-255,258-278,372-386`; `README.md:3-6`.\n- Behavior: The ordinary launcher explicitly uses DaemonSupervisor::without_deadline. Its optional constructor still permits a caller-selected readiness timeout; shutdown uses the same optional setting. Readiness is a socket/pipe connection without protocol/store/configuration negotiation. Sibling --version and the shutdown CLI run synchronously with Command::output, collecting full output without a local bound/cancellation. Spawned daemon ownership is detached from the terminal; successful readiness drops the Child handle while the daemon continues. Log files append indefinitely.\n- Consequence: No default launcher startup timer remains here, despite older bounded-readiness wording. A connectable but unhealthy endpoint can pass this readiness predicate; synchronous probes or a stalled endpoint can hold up the async launch caller. This does not prove the installed session was hung at this boundary.\n- Repair direction: Establish daemon identity/health and durable launch ownership through the protocol, move blocking subprocess work off the application event thread, and expose cancellation/progress without synthetic lifetime deadlines.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJ9r/BxBvFTG/4S1wyuuBHBg67toyKM4tA4k4w/wzhaeUGroe1hNU0XLJm2W6iVYNLXZotNluskQRdhIbjx/ZA0="}
