egression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCNdPau6WGtYwm504JuyQw9SBPxiZMGkJfMNKcPLE2yufKN5e/4R3jVwNbQz4toYPJhDQOB1pg349zsLMpMCbQg="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3291,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.445551934Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"467a4695-11b7-5e68-9513-fdce257127b1","title":"[L664] Immutable launcher snapshots can repeatedly replace the same shared daemon","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L664.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-launcher/src/app.rs:77-116`; `src/daemon.rs:145-190,198-233,281-341`; `src/bootstrap/configuration.rs:73-87,354-368`.\n- Behavior: Each launch retains one PreparedProduct/configuration snapshot throughout its recovery loop. The endpoint is derived from the stable installation/store identity. ensure_ready shuts down a reachable daemon whenever the applied marker differs from that snapshot's configuration path or the current daemon-file hash. It does not refresh/adopt current product configuration or negotiate the running daemon's actual generation. The marker is truncated/rewritten after endpoint reachability, contains a configuration path rather than configuration-content hash, and is not tied to an authenticated daemon process instance.\n- Consequence: If two live launcher windows hold different configuration generations, each can replace the shared daemon when its TUI reconnects, producing repeat shutdown/reconnect cycles and repeated pressure on runtime/context recovery. A missing/partial marker can also trigger replacement. This is a source-derived causal scenario, not an observed reproduction of the user's current lockup.\n- Repair direction: Give shared-daemon configuration reconciliation one durable owner, negotiate/adopt a compatible current generation, and coordinate required replacement with retained active-run/context ownership. A reconnecting presentation client must not repeatedly impose a stale configuration snapshot.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQE0w80+cF31BmEvg6yrdXEbCE9CNDfVenbElH2MdtLbtOqf6umELWHAtOv8Yi49m0/x6FwkUysYiaIyrJPml9A8="}
