ariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCLPHT2kM5Hpg1nXSIklTdHTXRfmLDVkqlFG18F0gme/hzUdsqTYPbUiNrnpmLgdTZ81gMHrURtnSY2WuZ7qbwU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3295,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.454270042Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"4882caea-5e1e-50ee-90d0-6c4806c63d38","title":"[L666] Product-state fallback can leave the next generation permanently occupied by corruption","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L666.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-launcher/src/persistence.rs:26-51,54-116,119-159,161-178,235-248`; `src/bootstrap.rs:44-49,71-98,179-198`.\n- Behavior: Startup scans/sorts all generation files and falls back from invalid newer payloads to the newest valid state. It does not quarantine or reserve past those rejected generation numbers. A later change increments the recovered state by one; commit refuses an existing final filename with different bytes. Thus valid generation N plus corrupt N+1 permits fallback but blocks the next changed state at N+1. The recovery test uses a far-future corrupt generation and only reloads, so it avoids this immediate-successor collision. Pending publication is removed/restarted; mutable recovery files are replaced by truncating the final file in place. All generation files are retained, with unbounded reads/scans and no content-size check at this boundary.\n- Consequence: Apparent fallback recovery can strand provider/workspace/bootstrap changes indefinitely. Interrupted mutable registration/settings replacement can leave a malformed final artifact. These are source-derived recoverability gaps; no corruption was injected into live product state.\n- Repair direction: Allocate a new durable generation past every observed/reserved generation or quarantine conflicting candidates with explicit provenance, prove the next save after fallback, and atomically replace recovery files with synchronized receipts.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJ8YK8wfMsExgATfR+rbnwSQ6md3Xmumim8cOxDWQnCPhnslhudLBt5ssiJzQxsaI477kl/ctCWNUgL700lYlwY="}
