nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPgPZGLetB7H6k0Ukp0FlKfomHKAx8QODFVaRXEU4vwXGh7OGrgRFWgOp/howYwImUcD+8wrlDZ/QHBST5fi+AU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3297,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.458984439Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"b3a50b70-0a83-5a77-9836-56a401cbaf0d","title":"[L667] Generated provider ceilings are fixed by route kind rather than the selected model","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L667.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-launcher/src/bootstrap/configuration.rs:161-190,224-263,275-338`; `src/bootstrap/configuration/hosted.rs:13-46`; `src/bootstrap/configuration.rs:73-87`; `src/bootstrap/configuration/compatibility.rs:3-19`; `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/config/product.rs:8-23`.\n- Behavior: Account/OpenAI routes receive 200,000 input and 64,000 output tokens; Anthropic 200,000/32,000; Google 1,000,000/65,536; compatible 200,000/32,000; hosted routes 32,768/4,096. Every profile sets 64 tools/eight parallel calls; inline media is 32 MiB or one byte and capability claims are assembled from route kind. Model catalog metadata does not set these values. Existing generated bytes must match exactly apart from one legacy timeout spelling. That retained provider_turn_timeout_seconds=600 field is accepted but ignored by current daemon policy, not an active deadline.\n- Consequence: The selected model can be restricted by a hardwired conservative declaration or assigned capacities/features it does not have. Hosted 4,096-token output is a request-shaping ceiling independent of actual provider capacity. Arbitrary edits to generated ceilings fail immutability checks. The ignored legacy timeout must not be misreported as a current limiter.\n- Repair direction: Retain discovered/explicit model capacity and supported features as versioned provider facts, distinguish user policy from provider capacity, and preserve correct no-timeout compatibility during migration.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFtAQfm5p9X2s8RoovQkG2GUHzadD7rrY2GsFKOfABC5Q6+1cAsmbRMM1Qpz4xRE9WsLtDrp6sKRRgZDDdstOQg="}
