{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3299,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.463476725Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"ca16d6d8-68f1-56d5-ba5e-62f863bebf90","title":"[L668] Workspace selection can silently fall back from current-directory errors or regenerate forgotten lineage","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L668.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-launcher/src/workspace_setup.rs:18-38,103-159,211-246`; `src/workspace_setup/discovery.rs:26-64,86-119,123-137`; `src/workspace_setup/managed.rs:47-69,73-161,166-235`.\n- Behavior: An explicit path fails visibly, but implicit current-directory discovery errors are ignored before reusing the stored active workspace or prompting. A discovered current folder/repository supersedes that active choice. Exact root+identity lookup searches only recent profiles; a miss creates fresh random project/workspace/resource/environment IDs. Git trust creates or recovers a detached managed worktree at the selected HEAD; direct folders retain the selected root. Health errors collapse to NeedsRepair. Automatic advanced-baseline refresh rewrites the registration before persisting the new profile/digest; registration replacement is in-place truncation.\n- Consequence: A discovery error can select an older workspace without its actual cause, and a forgotten/evicted folder can receive a new lineage rather than adopt its existing run identity. Interrupted registration refresh can temporarily mismatch the durable profile/configuration and inhibit reopening. The managed Git copy is an explicitly disclosed product choice; this audit does not identify the live process cwd from source alone.\n- Repair direction: Preserve discovery diagnostics and exact requested scope, resolve existing durable lineage outside the recent list, and make registration/profile/configuration refresh one recoverable publication protocol.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQB2SlFDdD+DuPsL8ldlgPvsvHD4EmPolbLICmj9MlQtHAmhWvGyRcaDOemXnuEoyO8/15wj7oXSgFUxMYGAvYQ4="}
