{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3301,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.468785042Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"6009e476-6dce-54c7-910e-ae8fe2d5aeb7","title":"[L669] Provider setup can disable durable routes on transient status failure and block even offline startup","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L669.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-launcher/src/provider_setup.rs:24-31,91-153,184-234,237-287`; `src/provider_setup/models.rs:65-127`; `src/provider_setup/connection.rs:6-76`; `src/provider_setup/direct.rs:21-42`.\n- Behavior: Every ordinary launch synchronously probes both account tools before checking prior setup/offline choices. NeedsAttention follows sign-in repair; declining or failing to restore readiness removes the route from the persisted enabled set and can choose another default/disable failover. A thrown login error instead exits startup. Retained model IDs are reused, and catalog failure permits an explicit manual model ID. Direct credentials are stored before the multi-provider selection is committed; cancelling later setup/test/publication has no enclosing credential-publication receipt. Settings remove replaced credentials even while old immutable configurations remain. Connection testing joins a blocking worker and has no caller cancellation handle.\n- Consequence: A slow unused account probe can block direct-only/offline launch. Temporary status failure can become a durable route/configuration change, feeding the shared-daemon replacement behavior in L664. Deleting an old key can prevent continuation of older route generations; cancelled setup can leave an unpublished key reference. Explicit failover consent and manual model selection are legitimate user choices, not synthetic deadlines.\n- Repair direction: Separate observed health from retained route intent; allow presentation/offline launch independently of optional probes, persist exact setup/publication ownership, and retain credential references while active durable generations require them.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQErOwNaeK5QI+pDvfV3A6l/xQCHYuKuDlkDNdeJQXKKWTKmD1oHhOGIkNRxk+3zBkXtcWaSNiNUpZnWqDXRoUQk="}
