{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3303,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.473758062Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"34691ec1-f89d-5d55-8142-140d74664895","title":"[L670] Optional startup update discovery remains on the critical launch path without cancellation or durable download continuation","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L670.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-launcher/src/app.rs:72-79`; `src/update.rs:13-44,85-118`; `src/update/release.rs:57-83`; `src/update/download.rs:15-107,125-172`; `src/update/install.rs:9-78,90-120`; `src/update/process.rs:18-108`.\n- Behavior: Default-on cached release discovery is awaited before workspace/provider setup or TUI entry. The six-hour interval suppresses update polling; it does not expire sessions. HTTP clients configure no explicit timeout/cancellation here; release/checksum bodies are read completely before the 64-KiB/exact-hex check. Archives stream with a 1-GiB cap, but retry deletes the same release staging directory rather than resuming and has no update lock. Extraction/native install/version check explicitly pass None to the optional-deadline process helper. Its stdout drains with bounded retention but joins until EOF; a descendant holding the pipe can prevent return. Windows defers update into an untracked helper that waits for the parent PID and verifies only the CLI version.\n- Consequence: An optional network operation or helper can hold up daily startup, and interrupted/repeated updates lose download progress or collide in staging. The source contains no active synthetic default updater execution timer; removing timers does not provide UI responsiveness, cancellation, or durable continuation automatically. Platform/architecture and exact release-tag admission remain separate packaging gates.\n- Repair direction: Run optional discovery outside launch-critical work under a cancellable owner, persist resumable download/install receipts, coordinate staging ownership, and verify completion of the complete installed application/daemon pair.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDzVb06jWadXtE3b2XOL7tdKthIRekB/mdhjjYLHrZl3CAIvIBCGgD9OqTHJVi9a1nqlDfMVbjP5cbq/7GFR0QQ="}
