ust leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQG2Tlbms3M3NuPP2FsrJjZBsY8fJfQ8Mjv+ljJ7gaaZT9nVhmlnBG+8zyCf8ieRCuja74ZcrzhOQqDPfE3MVXA0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3305,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.478279785Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"754598d9-46b6-558f-837e-33aeca08fce2","title":"[L671] Hidden credential input has a smaller cap and an incomplete terminal-mode acquisition rollback","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L671.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-launcher/src/provider_setup/direct.rs:19,108-178,181-199`; `src/terminal.rs:34-63`.\n- Behavior: Credential entry rejects more than 16 KiB and embedded pasted controls before the lower credential-store API. RawInputGuard::enter enables raw mode and bracketed paste, then flushes stdout before constructing the guard. A flush error returns without a guard destructor or explicit rollback, unlike the preceding bracketed-paste error path. Normal guard drop attempts cleanup but discards cleanup errors. Ordinary prompt cancellation/EOF exits setup and is not an execution lifetime deadline.\n- Consequence: An acquisition failure can leave the terminal in raw/paste mode, which can look like a locked-up interaction. This was found in source; it is not established as the cause of the user's current session symptom. The credential capacity is a selected input bound, not provider session expiry.\n- Repair direction: Construct ownership immediately after raw-mode acquisition and unwind every later failure, retaining cleanup diagnostics when restoration fails. Keep explicit user cancellation distinct from session expiration.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE