evoked authority, stale epoch/revision, cross-scope requests, lost acknowledgements and restart, proving legitimate continuation without admitting unauthorized or duplicate effects. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFCdBgDRvY6F4qRm4NyLIaYRgeNUlXtnjNUAH7hflNXCqQ2+l3bU8qiQWpvcFzObEuqlkRw61OVhIZkLpSS3Mw8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3307,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.482942808Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"e64984f5-66da-5dec-9f16-f2573c6ba6fe","title":"[L672] CLI default deadlines are removed, but interactive launch ignores supplied session and timeout options","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L672.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-cli/src/args.rs:18-85,216-258,366-389`; `src/args/types.rs:17-20,70-76`; `src/runner.rs:22-26,52-66,145-198,200-251` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Parsing starts with no timeout. Event count is optional; its default flow-control window is 64. A user-supplied positive timeout remains supported, accepts the entire u64 range, and is later added to an Instant without a checked-add path in shutdown. Open/resume forward endpoint and repository/run selections but do not forward `--session` or `--timeout-seconds`; zero-argument invocation is a separate launch path. Update/settings enforce terminal requirements. Completion lists omit the runs command family.\n- Consequence: These sources do not establish a remaining default CLI execution deadline. They do establish silently ignored interactive session selection and timeout settings, and an explicit huge-duration overflow risk. Whether the launcher/TUI chooses the correct durable run/context is separate from parsing a session option. Exact identities and candidate confirmation protect integrity and are not time limiters.\n- Repair direction: Express interactive target/session policy in the launch interface and reject unsupported combinations; use overflow-safe optional deadlines for explicit caller choices. Keep default work lifetime unbounded. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNWWWOvDBh3Q79AM1B+zt9D29TvmdDLYNJLJ1S3XrruBFmjllaTqkLmoMzfPqOW1xhAV2vu2bMSgjR3nrwZKPA8="}
