{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3309,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.487773469Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"275ab98c-d93e-50b2-acd1-0321ce4b0ee3","title":"[L673] CLI event watch exits on disconnect or history gaps and does not durably resume delivery","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L673.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-cli/src/events.rs:27-88,91-146,201-243`; `src/output.rs:16-55`; `src/runner.rs:68-80`; `src/operation.rs:177-244,260-264`; `src/id.rs:37-53`; `src/error.rs:63-69,127-145` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: The event loop reads indefinitely and exits on any read/heartbeat error or gap, even when snapshot acceptance was requested. Deduplication stores only one negotiated window of IDs in memory; count and subscription state are also volatile. The CLI exposes start/session and event cursors in output but saves no resume receipt or cursor. New invocations generate new request identities. Writes/flushes to stdout execute synchronously on the same current-thread runtime before acknowledging delivery; a blocked output sink prevents further event, heartbeat, and Ctrl-C selection progress. Submit reads envelope/payload files fully before negotiated-bound validation. Structured remote recovery details are collapsed into a message/category.\n- Consequence: Durable server history and the lower client API do not by themselves make this watcher or command invocation reconnect to its original operation. An indefinitely blocked output sink is a progress blocker with no synthetic time limit involved. A cursor gap is terminal here rather than an explicit snapshot/replay transition. This is source-derived behavior, not a reproduction of the user's running TUI.\n- Repair direction: Give subscriptions and effect requests persistent identity/cursor receipts, reconnect/reconcile them without redispatching effects, and separate output backpressure from connection liveness. Bound file ingestion before allocating it and preserve typed recovery information. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQK7951AqcJwFgY7n9f4WR5lNzGWLVdrhJavjjoyHSEdXwsJJMuHg+oV0HA5kN3vQ3nYJOt/grsWdVAL1vkFhlQ8="}
