st leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOrXo5Gq0qQnv0UyFVq+9kSuVQ9FHv9/oLgOQaMoHH1pGoWissLvjBfzxeIyjCQdoa5F3T0Iy6UL3fa8P4gu7g0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3311,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.492488064Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"b0da721c-0eca-5f94-9b57-1ac6c3e84d89","title":"[L674] CLI artifact transfers lose resumable progress and output replacement has a destructive failure gap","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L674.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-cli/src/artifact.rs:54-91,112-198,211-258,278-319,322-378,381-385`; `src/args/artifact.rs:74-105` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Download/upload allocate fresh transfer identities; chunk offsets, ordinals, digests, temporary filenames, and request identities live only in the invocation. Disconnect exits without reconciling the transfer. Receive errors remove the partial file and ignore removal errors; no remote cancellation is attempted. A publication error instead leaves an unrecorded part file. Upload hashes the entire input, reopens it, sends each chunk under a fresh request identity, and checks size only afterward; server digest verification remains necessary. Default upload chunk size is 64 KiB, constrained by the negotiated chunk maximum; these are transport framing bounds, not work TTLs. Forced output publication removes the previous output before fallible rename; non-force existence-check/rename is not an atomic no-replace operation, and directory sync is absent.\n- Consequence: The resumable protocol cannot resume this CLI invocation without a retained transfer receipt; interruption repeats I/O and may strand server state. A rename failure after forced deletion can lose the user's previous output. Integrity checks on bytes and digest should remain; the missing persistent transfer/publication state is the blocker. Source-derived, no failure injected.\n- Repair direction: Persist transfer/source digest/offset/temp publication state, reconcile an exact transfer after reconnect, and publish with atomic platform-appropriate replace/no-replace plus directory durability. Preserve partial verified data through recoverable failures. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFrz4sLysmW87oC+UmzfRT5BOp5jybJbcgIPsgfChD0KQUtdn7fRKEwQrJqQMal0ZQbopdMtYrs0nOzbhAFq3Qw="}
