already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNq7M0w0w1b9/xGhlsnyWkv9bbU34lX/SrwvoaChbYhEPdlnOUfuAodjVpiqPrwnD9csP80AYnVdUhPjvsP8KA8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3313,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.497348958Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"d44d5207-b2e1-51c5-afda-0369422ee4d5","title":"[L675] CLI terminal stdin buffers until EOF and terminal following has no reconnect state","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L675.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-cli/src/terminal.rs:21-82,83-159,162-198,210-236,239-250,353-360`; `src/output.rs:35-47,74-110` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: File terminal input streams negotiated chunks, but stdin is read to EOF into one unbounded Vec in a blocking task before any bytes are transmitted. An open stdin producer therefore prevents initial input indefinitely. Output follow stores stream state only in memory and exits on disconnect, unavailable output, or sequence validation failure. Ctrl-C exits without issuing an explicit detach/cancel. Attachment IDs are printed, but there is no cursor resume command or durable receipt here. A single sanitizer spans all streams, removes control strings until their terminator, and decodes each safe chunk lossily; split UTF8 and an unterminated control string can distort/suppress human output. Resize accepts the full u16 range even where native backends later narrow dimensions.\n- Consequence: Input can appear frozen despite no execution deadline, and a live process cannot automatically restore its original output observation after connection loss through this CLI path. It correctly warns that unavailable output does not prove termination. Native ownership recovery and output replay must be established separately.\n- Repair direction: Stream stdin in bounded chunks while serving heartbeat/cancel control, retain attachment/offset/sequence receipts, and reconnect against an authoritative stream disposition. Preserve incremental UTF8 and independent stream sanitizer state. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBnmbPHFq0UimaimTRAz01VaEHwI5Nxos1eb+ctxLn/yk/X4pF28zaRp9vsE+wHWb4gEaH862S3fNVNOPqSR/wY="}
