nAcceptance and nonregression: valid boundary values and values just beyond each synthetic cap, final wrapper/receipt growth, non-ASCII strings, arbitrarily split frames/pages, malformed or conflicting data, mixed-version decode and save/reopen round trips. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJrD8sOjNxVG5B+Vym12JGspYXPBYI39Oa5FBbNHESDpLtraNdmTTDuQmOkjcCepPUmXreydVI5SYlnunOJUJQY="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3315,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.502242749Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"0a751f7b-27a8-596b-9d07-eafdb62494f6","title":"[L676] Product-run CLI executes candidate commands without a persistent process owner and accumulates all list pages","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L676.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-cli/src/product_run.rs:46-64,72-137,140-181,185-212,231-258`; `src/runner.rs:68-80`; `src/product_run/presentation.rs:14-44,69-126` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Runs list increments an offset, requests pages until a short page, and retains every result before output; no stable history snapshot or streaming pages are used. Local candidate execution synchronously recomputes a digest then calls Command.status inside the current-thread async runtime, with inherited I/O and no independent cancellation, process receipt, or owner reconciliation. No timeout is added. Accept/commit legality and optional unqualified-digest confirmation are checked in separate queries, then the mutation request contains only run ID and action; the confirmation digest is not carried into that request.\n- Consequence: Large/changing history can delay listing and consume unbounded client memory. A long-running candidate command blocks client runtime progress and is outside the daemon-owned durable process recovery contract. CLI confirmation alone does not bind the subsequent server mutation to the candidate observed; whether server serialization independently prevents that race needs the protocol/daemon evidence. Candidate identity checking is necessary integrity, not a synthetic limiter.\n- Repair direction: Stream stable run-history pages and route candidate execution through a durable process owner with explicit cancellation/reconciliation. Carry candidate identity/expected operation generation in exact mutation requests rather than relying on a pre-request check. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOyT8gpUswy18XHixUPQg3AWmAEVgukza+RFHQqtzsY0X22CSGyCLqTq1udavm6O0dTilN1fhz43hg5F2iW6TQ8="}
