redecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKPRRXmocbBZKnEA6x2nQnkmOu8qqXA+8kEk5PkUliyYrBMsewpJdNQXBS4wJrNo3TSq2T7YAPIiAQOkPnNe1g4="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3317,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.507097010Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"f3881d0c-b863-520d-abd5-4845f262ac48","title":"[L678] Embedded workflow creates synthetic acceptance obligations even without elapsed deadlines","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L678.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-product-runner/skills/independent-reviewer.md:3-27`; `skills/maintainable-developer.md:3-19`; `workflows/production-engineering.md:3-13,120-162`; `skills/repository-architect.md:1-8`; `README.md:128-157` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Independent-review prompt treats any production source over 500 lines as a concrete finding. General developer/reviewer workflow requires finite attempt bounds for external retry/pagination, an approved design, and exact package formatter/build/tests/lint evidence. It applies many domain-specific evidence rules to every run with a proportionality clause. These are model instructions; this read alone does not prove that every item is a deterministic host gate. README documents 48-turn/512-tool segments and continuing fixer/reviewer cycles rather than a terminal cycle ceiling.\n- Consequence: Removing clocks leaves synthetic source-size and attempt-count obligations capable of driving extra review/fix work. Pagination must prove progress, but a universal finite total-page rule is different from rejecting repeated cursors or caller-selected cancellation. Request-specific correctness, exact effects, actual requested tests, and dependency compatibility remain necessary; a prompt-only style rule should not silently expand a small task into unrelated restructuring.\n- Repair direction: Derive blocking acceptance obligations from the user's goal and concrete repository contracts. Keep workload segmentation separate from goal/session identity and make external loop progress/recovery explicit without a universal total-work ceiling. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQH6cTC9PZA+bDHueAJvnP1yjrbJ6rdafL6VJ1W0HhkpR0TyQZCjvk5ZPco2EPjpb7cclSNMsblEi+zDGIzvBggU="}
