candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQP+3SW+hxLgaQQ01iQAgs4IAQcW9KKG1o7ZjUuu2IYsKXHAT+zB7hV+9IHsz4tG3p9VWIKDmRBEzWRXDwVVwsAM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3319,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.511412481Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"d18d347b-81e5-527f-b124-3e4b9778b9ae","title":"[L685] Exact command retries require original request and correlation identities, which a fresh CLI invocation cannot supply","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L685.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-app-protocol/src/command/binding.rs:138-190,236-269`; `src/command/idempotency.rs:114-135,146-172`; `src/command/result.rs:99-105,148-165` in that crate; `crates/app/peritus-cli/src/operation.rs:190-205`; `crates/app/peritus-cli/src/id.rs:37-53`.\n- Behavior: Command digest includes actor, durable session, application request ID, correlation ID, idempotency key, expected revision, and exact frame bytes. Matching session/actor/key with a different digest is a conflict. A new CLI invocation generates fresh request/correlation identities even if the user supplies identical command files, session, and idempotency key; its grammar offers no original request/correlation option. Result replay preserves the original request ID; this result is explicitly not a durable C0 receipt.\n- Consequence: Repeating the same visible CLI command after an uncertain reply cannot perform exact replay through this binding. Preserving only session and key is insufficient. The binding protects effect integrity, but lack of a durable complete request receipt makes the protection a practical reconnect blocker.\n- Repair direction: Retain and reopen the full original bound request/operation identity, then reconcile/replay its final receipt. Separate durable operation identity from transient connection correlation if the revised contract deliberately permits that, without weakening duplicate-effect protection. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPESCPM5NlDzIMR23nzWqZUtyRpxkAW4dvMECD8FtOb4Q6k62EvKukdg+DQ8RDM0ia/4gNTcJAJy/vUUu6R0sAg="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3320,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.513645671Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"d18d347b-81e5-527f-b124-3e4b9778b9ae","comment_uuid":"16415a77-ffba-4187-9173-bd345016f65b","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L685: Exact command retries require original request and correlation identities, which a fresh CLI invocation cannot supply.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-app-protocol/src/command/binding.rs:138-190,236-269; src/command/idempotency.rs:114-135,146-172; src/command/result.rs:99-105,148-165; crates/app/peritus-cli/src/operation.rs:190-205; crates/app/peritus-cli/src/id.rs:37-53. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nRetain and reopen the full original bound request/operation identity, then reconcile/replay its final receipt. Separate durable operation identity from transient connection correlation if the revised contract deliberately permits that, without weakening duplicate-effect protection. No tests run.\n\nPreserve: durable logical session and run identity, exact command receipts, atomic snapshot/cursor binding, explicit authority, selected UI state, complete history retrieval and owned-effect reconciliation. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large histories and non-ASCII fields, queue/connection pressure, delayed acknowledgements, subscription gaps, disconnect/reconnect and daemon restart, proving snapshot recovery, preserved selection/context, responsive controls and no duplicate command. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNKOEwROfGTLeJ8N6h3ZcKjBgfjAcdVdyKPazenxjxhjko7N8gTfRKZq/uNev3jljna0ftvRBzw9IcdDaqMaLwM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3321,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.515841828Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"90b81915-e2a6-54f8-a9d2-281c76e14653","title":"[L686] Pure idempotency window has a 4096-entry production ceiling and explicit oldest retirement","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L686.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-app-protocol/src/limits.rs:39-53,92-118,215-225`; `src/command/idempotency.rs:84-112,114-135,146-206` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Default retained final-entry capacity is 4096 and negotiated peers select the smaller capacity. The pure window keeps every final result until explicit retire_oldest; admission rejects an unmatched key when full. Lookup scans retained entries linearly. There is no storage spill, pagination, or restore constructor in this type. Recording the same digest again returns AlreadyRecorded without checking equality of the supplied final result. This is a reusable pure contract; its use in the installed daemon must be established at callers, not inferred from its name.\n- Consequence: A caller that never retires or spills entries has a count-based lifetime blocker; arbitrary retirement instead loses exact replay evidence. A framing collection bound should not become a durable session's cumulative work quota. This read does not assert that the user's live daemon uses this pure window as its only receipt store.\n- Repair direction: Store durable operation receipts independently of bounded in-memory caches and page them for lookup. Retire only through an explicit archival/tombstone policy that preserves duplicate-effect semantics; validate conflicting final facts. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGRXC1zGDvfj/GkidrBlc9h0nsdTm8mhRXOJ5AnCwLsdBIcLcb7OFsjs7JgEnqPDvL1llkK2lHDfSeR3+q4AUgc="}
