egression: large histories and non-ASCII fields, queue/connection pressure, delayed acknowledgements, subscription gaps, disconnect/reconnect and daemon restart, proving snapshot recovery, preserved selection/context, responsive controls and no duplicate command. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOqRYZN6PykkfVe6/Nhc9N1CfKshY6EkH1SAQVy9KwzteJdoSQ+2nNrP8pVSXls9GA8iZYZdkWDZ9HNSEOozgQE="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3323,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.520310531Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"7175c6be-8778-5d45-b026-26a13f1460c5","title":"[L687] Artifact transfer protocol conserves bytes but has no resumable interrupted phase or restoration API","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L687.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-app-protocol/src/artifact/metadata.rs:70-94,138-161`; `src/artifact/state.rs:98-154,178-235,238-270,273-333`; `src/artifact/verified.rs:7-65` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: State.new starts every transfer at zero bytes/ordinal. Chunks require exact identity, next ordinal, offset, and declared total; duplicate chunks are rejected rather than replayed by this state. There is no paused/interrupted phase or public constructor for retained progress. Digest mismatch is terminal failure. Completed records a protocol observation and explicitly does not imply persistence/finalization. Chunk/media/detail limits are selected by negotiated/caller framing; declared artifact total is u64, not a hardcoded goal byte quota.\n- Consequence: Byte conservation proofs do not prove the existence of a durable transfer owner after restart. Exact request replay or host-retained reconstruction must supply what the pure type lacks. Removing integrity checks would not repair this recovery gap.\n- Repair direction: Persist exact transfer progress/publication state and provide checked restore/reconcile transitions that retain digest/offset identity. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3J