{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3325,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.525393029Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"6de15e64-2797-5b1e-93b4-a76f8c939957","title":"[L688] Heartbeat and shutdown contracts contain no clock-based liveness or six-step execution deadline","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L688.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-app-protocol/src/daemon/heartbeat.rs:15-19,38-85`; `src/daemon/status.rs:20-31,41-64`; `src/daemon/shutdown.rs:117-142,183-209,261-370`; `src/limits.rs:39-53` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Heartbeat state verifies exact monotonic u64 sequence and distinct last nonce without time semantics. Shutdown request/accept/progress/completion are exact correlated observations; total steps is caller-selected positive u32 and cannot change during progress. Equal progress may repeat indefinitely. Default diagnostics are 4096 bytes and remaining-work lists 256 items, both negotiated framing capacities. Clean requires an empty supplied remaining list, not direct worker inspection. Neither six steps nor a wall-clock cutoff is built into this pure contract.\n- Consequence: Any real heartbeat expiry, forced drain timer, false external readiness, or missing work from a bounded completion list originates in the host/caller, not these DTO state machines. Source bounds and truthful lifecycle correlation remain separate from task/session lifetime.\n- Repair direction: Trace host ownership/liveness and complete remaining-work reporting; keep durable goal lifetime independent of transient connection observations. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoL