{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3327,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.529969318Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"dfd04989-9704-5347-8ba5-3a2ec0fdd9fc","title":"[L691] Product controls are not fenced to the observed candidate or operation generation","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L691.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-app-protocol/src/product/control.rs:55-76`; `src/product/operation.rs:190-221,255-266`; `src/product/snapshot.rs:29-69,134-151`; `src/product/settlement.rs:24-47`; `src/product/phase.rs:72-88` in the same crate; `crates/app/peritus-cli/src/product_run.rs:72-137`.\n- Behavior: ProductRunControl transmits only run ID and action. It cannot carry the candidate digest or current operation generation observed during confirmation. Operation identity is a bounded string; the constructor checks text and requires uncertainty for OutcomeUnknown but does not forbid retry/accept flags for that state or reconcile phase/control inconsistency. Phase helpers classify WaitingForUser and RecoveryRequired as terminal until explicit input; retryable is a broad Failed/Cancelled/RecoveryRequired classification. Settlement validates candidate run/workspace/qualification but DTO construction alone does not prove an external owner or side-effect state.\n- Consequence: A client-visible legal control and local digest confirmation can become stale before the server admits it. These pure projections cannot be used as authority tokens or generic permission to replay uncertain work. The durable host must independently gate exact operation state, and missing fencing can turn valid user control into a conflict or wrong-candidate action.\n- Repair direction: Carry exact expected candidate/operation lineage in mutation requests and validate it at the authoritative owner; make legal controls derive from that owner's typed state. Preserve waiting/recovery within the durable goal rather than treating terminal phase as session disposal. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGG8I5flwEvhLhuBpELj1btselp7h9+mElW7FALRHQHzzQZolD0BPyQRKltwEO39HX4XoSdLz5CGOojAGK5Idw4="}
