ve evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMvIdAYLXUEXrbL/Br8wpgOndef7IDRpmUkluaEV0HGA8xHx5uk/vDSsJ0jnwCh6vBmD6lIMoz1sZY+aIauIVAc="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3329,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.534250654Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"adfd5119-5b4d-52bb-a1d5-f31e1554961f","title":"[L692] Goal projections remove time/resource budget fields while preserving mandatory runner acceptance","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L692.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-app-protocol/src/workbench/execution.rs:6-43`; `src/workbench/goal.rs:54-79,93-133`; `src/workbench/goal/projection.rs:19-48,82-121,168-186,190-255` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Goal/start DTOs select no elapsed, request, tool, token, cost, disk, or memory ceiling. Usage is observational; u32 request/tool aggregate methods saturate and checked u64 token/cost aggregation becomes unknown on overflow. Goal definitions require at least one mandatory RunnerAcceptance criterion, even when a caller wants another task/evidence type. Criteria can include graphical/human evidence that the installed phase marks Unavailable. Criteria use u16 representation; reason text is 512 bytes and the projection requires positive revisions/attempt and exact Pausing/pause-mode consistency. It does not independently prove all criteria satisfied for an Achieved value.\n- Consequence: These DTOs do not reintroduce an eight-hour goal budget. Remaining acceptance/evidence constraints may still block a daily-driving task that is outside strict coding acceptance; their appropriateness must come from the user's goal and supported capabilities. Integer representation and observation text bounds should not become silent total-work limits or false evidence claims.\n- Repair direction: Support goal-specific acceptance contracts with explicit unavailable evidence and resumable blocked states; keep accounting separate from stopping policy and prove achievement at the host. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQELxnsVX5tCIu21y6IxvK35cx/wMXTNttMRKNz2pyLPqMw1KO7dXVDu3OHhovT8CFJfriyuYPGevu1AykZ0pUww="}
