le.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLyKQfiS2wSnaHeUhAm4jAZfZYZPFEcVORKCwLiqNamEQWp5l5ySb+gEjyk/sUbrtEMxiDXgHtjhCBBv+1tWWwg="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3331,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.538712491Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"e878e015-9a0a-553e-b1f3-3f3f76357753","title":"[L693] Model catalogs and product observations have whole-response capacity boundaries without pagination at those DTOs","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L693.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-app-protocol/src/product/models.rs:6-7,23-33,133-148,167-197`; `src/product/snapshot.rs:35-54`; `src/doctor.rs:9-10,77-92,123-137`; `src/doctor/tests.rs:31-67`; `src/envelope/response.rs:65-149` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Model catalog accepts at most 4096 entries, IDs/labels at most 512 bytes, and error at most 4096 bytes; it is one Vec with no page cursor. Default model choice retains configured identity, manual entry is explicit, and unknown tool support stays unknown. Product snapshots bound each task/detail field independently to existing 64 KiB/1 MiB constants without testing overall response feasibility here. Doctor reports permit up to 65535 findings with 64-byte label and 1024-byte text; duplicate detection is quadratic. Its forty-finding wire fixture proves removal of the former small cap, not maximum composite capacity. No cache TTL or execution timer is in these DTOs.\n- Consequence: Raising individual collection/text capacities does not guarantee a combined framed response fits negotiated codec limits. Oversized observations can fail reporting of already-retained work even when the goal is unbounded. Timestamp/cache flags are provenance, not session expiration.\n- Repair direction: Page large catalogs/observations and prove whole-message feasibility before publication while preserving full evidence in durable storage. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHk9uQpm/v8glrBX6NgmqEpVqx+2o4G4UV9qqWn+2Q/gdY7XuNDytCefmFpg+ue8y0dBZD/B5g6GmQf0KxXMJg0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3332,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.540807707Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"e878e015-9a0a-553e-b1f3-3f3f76357753","comment_uuid":"fc29b9eb-eca6-42f2-84e7-1f7be9d85468","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L693: Model catalogs and product observations have whole-response capacity boundaries without pagination at those DTOs.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-app-protocol/src/product/models.rs:6-7,23-33,133-148,167-197; src/product/snapshot.rs:35-54; src/doctor.rs:9-10,77-92,123-137; src/doctor/tests.rs:31-67; src/envelope/response.rs:65-149. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nPage large catalogs/observations and prove whole-message feasibility before publication while preserving full evidence in durable storage. No tests run.\n\nPreserve: durable logical session and run identity, exact command receipts, atomic snapshot/cursor binding, explicit authority, selected UI state, complete history retrieval and owned-effect reconciliation. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large histories and non-ASCII fields, queue/connection pressure, delayed acknowledgements, subscription gaps, disconnect/reconnect and daemon restart, proving snapshot recovery, preserved selection/context, responsive controls and no duplicate command. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQM8loFS+TaSUmDcVAyqc2AwG3PlVTYwlWeoKv9CRXV//q2xDnI2fZw2SKUTHStzYDll8iv0FpITVJjOVthvPaAI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3333,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.542911458Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"74b30340-aa6f-545f-a702-c6e2852b5c1a","title":"[L694] Closed application envelopes lack explicit artifact failure and stream-offset restoration messages","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L694.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-app-protocol/src/envelope/event.rs:96-134`; `src/envelope/request.rs:71-93,96-198`; `src/envelope/control.rs:52-68`; `src/envelope/response.rs:11-43,46-62`; `src/artifact/state.rs:98-108` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Events include artifact metadata/chunk/completion, but no typed artifact-failed/cancelled event despite those terminal pure-state phases. Artifact-open carries transfer/artifact IDs, no requested verified byte offset; terminal attach similarly has no resume cursor in these request variants. A subscription gap is explicitly a snapshot/resubscription recovery condition; CLI treated it as terminal in L673. Several observation constructors simply assemble values, including zero subscription-start window or inconsistent backpressure cursors; validation remains a wire/host responsibility. Feature gating is additive and exact.\n- Consequence: Recovering a disconnected observer needs more than a new socket: it needs authoritative transfer/terminal disposition and retained position. These envelopes do not by themselves expose every recovery transition. Absence of a failure event can leave an observer waiting unless the host closes/reports through another route, which must be traced rather than assumed.\n- Repair direction: Provide typed durable status/offset reconciliation and terminal failure observations while preserving exact integrity bindings and negotiated compatibility. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDN3OAtguSi5E3jxdMX2sjliW2xBdt4JZ5utfrpFDJFBk4T0LtQqyEVypDZ8RsGsXFi3cJj7ClzhA8wYa+sJ8AQ="}
