{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3335,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.547582327Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"5641a4ac-9344-529e-8395-9451528c9073","title":"[L695] Default protocol recovery advice does not establish safe restoration of the original operation","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L695.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-app-protocol/src/error/code.rs:176-214,260-270`; `src/error/mod.rs:133-241` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Default retry classes recommend reconnecting for session mismatches, submitting new requests for idempotency conflicts, and recovery for idempotency capacity. Human explanations suggest waiting or restarting for capacity, restarting artifact transfers, and reattaching or starting a new terminal. No default code selects SameRequest or Never. These are classifications and prose, not implementations of receipt lookup or owner restoration. In L685, changing request/correlation IDs changes the command digest even with the same idempotency key; in L686, pure capacity has no automatic retirement or spill.\n- Consequence: Generic restart/new-request advice can leave the original effect or native process unresolved, and restart does not necessarily retire durable capacity. The error taxonomy cannot certify that repeating an operation is safe or that reconnecting restores its provider context. This is a source finding, not a measured restart failure.\n- Repair direction: Resolve durable operation receipts and native ownership before choosing replay, continuation, explicit replacement, or terminal disposition; expose capacity recovery that actually preserves receipts. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPXu1cY82TAypJDWYcf5fPJRq7zY09bdPbVyn8MId/LRZDGFZj0jfITANsppM8HPJUW+egbkOuZpYCuzNZ4ouQQ="}
