nection pressure, delayed acknowledgements, subscription gaps, disconnect/reconnect and daemon restart, proving snapshot recovery, preserved selection/context, responsive controls and no duplicate command. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCj9Z0kkQdKz6pPdeI3kBXd0YnfpuAOwCQ364vVBk3ADoWOk1p9f/OrOY/NEjmbOCMlgumpFmBgLO/ksMWWPXQo="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3337,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.552749065Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"c5573985-ed51-5dce-a7cb-12d91c8c78b7","title":"[L696] Error display paths preserve different amounts of recovery information","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L696.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-app-protocol/src/error/mod.rs:14-76,108-125,250-267`; `src/error/diagnostic.rs:16-57`; `src/identity.rs:13-119` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: AppProtocolError stores code, retry disposition, subsystem, optional diagnostic, and local codec source. actionable_message includes the three machine fields in prose; Display includes code and diagnostic only. Diagnostic contraction preserves machine fields while shortening UTF-8 text. The identity types require nonzero exact 16-byte IDs and nonempty idempotency keys of at most 128 bytes. These are identity/representation constraints, with no session lifetime or context-owner validation in these files.\n- Consequence: Callers that use Display can lose retry/subsystem information available on the same error; CLI string conversion in L673 needs this distinction. Nonzero protocol, invocation, conversation, or attachment IDs prove shape, not preservation of a native owner or provider context.\n- Repair direction: Carry structured recovery fields consistently across local/wire/CLI paths and bind context identity to durable restoration evidence. Retain exact identifier integrity checks. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZ