egression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQM5+L8Dg0yAzSCkfgP84EKb2c9flnbT+SJd4BO2PGVD7OuvajXERwkLvHHMM5iXIF8Wc6Och/pvoN9Q25FZILwo="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3341,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.562055620Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"8173217d-68d7-5857-8a26-8f8d7786c639","title":"[L698] Negotiation carries requested session identity but does not verify that selection restores it","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L698.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-app-protocol/src/version/negotiation.rs:81-119,277-306,333-344`; `src/version/negotiation/selection.rs:16-66,83-94`; `src/wire/hello.rs:43-72,119-159,189-199`; `src/version/range.rs:5-10`; `src/verified/mod.rs:42-69` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: ClientHello carries an optional requested_session. Selection takes an independently supplied established_session and returns it for compatible/downgraded negotiation; it does not compare it to the requested identity or inspect persistence. ServerHello validates session presence against compatibility only. The generic negotiation proof takes a selected_session boolean. Features are canonical, duplicate-free, bounded by explicit item counts, and selected by intersection; resource ceilings are pointwise minima. Current implementation advertises protocol 2.0 only.\n- Consequence: A successful handshake alone cannot prove same-session recovery or native context-window restoration. Host/client checks are necessary and remain separate audit targets. Version/feature compatibility and exact ID checks are integrity constraints; no elapsed session expiration is imposed here.\n- Repair direction: Bind acceptance to authoritative durable session restoration and report mismatches explicitly; separate observer negotiation from provider-context adoption. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SH