{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3343,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.566581144Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"911c40ce-3df4-5ab4-8d03-6c4cb265048c","title":"[L699] Improvement inbox uses whole bounded collections with quadratic duplicate validation","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L699.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-app-protocol/src/improvements.rs:6-7,81-93,189-210,239-263`.\n- Behavior: Proposal/evidence text is limited to 4,096 UTF-8 bytes. Each candidate requires nonempty evidence with at most 65,535 entries; the inbox accepts at most 65,535 candidates. Duplicate checks scan each prior prefix. List returns the whole inbox type, including dismissed history, with no page/cursor in this file. Evaluation is explicit and separately bound to conversation/run/workspace; listing is non-running.\n- Consequence: Growing retained history can hit fixed cardinality or frame capacity and quadratic validation cost even when execution has no timer. This constructor does not establish how the host retains or pages history.\n- Repair direction: Page durable history and enforce duplicate identity through indexed storage; preserve explicit evaluation authority and inert evidence boundaries. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGtrjVdhmHfvPQBEne7J7FBWjWImt+gSTlB3G0Sdt8ifewVBBWqm1O6TCg9rliFDiTXP4l7dihUBr/Hi7e+r4gM="}
