{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3347,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.575564683Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"b8b36fa6-055c-5b64-8973-efe8393ad92e","title":"[L701] Public application encoding allocates a full validation decode and collapses semantic error causes","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L701.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-app-protocol/src/wire/mod.rs:82-100,112-126,137-148,155-177`; `src/wire/primitive.rs:13-15`; `src/wire/command.rs:30-60`; `src/wire/artifact.rs:69-92` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: encode_app_message constructs a complete frame and then decodes it to apply domain limits, allocating owned message values again before discarding them. Persistent prompt binding decoding re-encodes for canonical equality. Result-page persistence always uses production codec ceilings. The generic invalid helper maps every constructor error to InvalidDomainValue, discarding its particular domain cause. Command keys/embedded frames and artifact chunks are read owned before their narrower domain validation.\n- Consequence: Fixed representation bounds remain operational gates and validation can multiply memory/copy cost. A domain capacity/integrity failure can emerge as generic malformed input, whose default recovery is a new request (L695), instead of a precise repairable capacity cause. This is not a default elapsed deadline.\n- Repair direction: Validate domain sizes before allocation, carry precise bounded error classification, and provide paged/artifact representations for large durable values rather than fail-after-encoding. Preserve canonical exact-byte checks. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+