{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3349,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.579866743Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"bf80bd79-6a18-5a66-b23d-17283f8619c2","title":"[L702] Direct 16-bit history counts bypass negotiated generic collection checks","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L702.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-app-protocol/src/wire/doctor.rs:24-66`; `src/wire/improvements.rs:63-130`; `src/wire/primitive.rs:135-168,182-202`; `src/wire/response.rs:293-309`; `src/wire/subscription.rs:99-116` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Doctor findings and improvement candidate/evidence counts use raw u16 reads/writes rather than read_collection_len/write_collection_len. Decoders allocate Vec capacity from the count before proving enough payload for the entries, without a domain page bound. Improvement distinctness is checked only after decoding. By contrast, version/features, subscription windows, backpressure and subscription-start fields perform explicit negotiated count/zero/order checks; this closes the observation-constructor gap noted in L694 for those wire paths.\n- Consequence: A tiny truncated frame can cause allocations based on up to 65,535 declared items, and negotiated generic collection ceilings do not constrain those particular raw-count fields. Whole inbox/doctor history can exceed frame capacity even when each individual entry and count passes its constructor.\n- Repair direction: Use consistent preallocation ceilings and paginated durable history, with explicit whole-message feasibility. Keep positive window and cursor ordering checks. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAA