ories and non-ASCII fields, queue/connection pressure, delayed acknowledgements, subscription gaps, disconnect/reconnect and daemon restart, proving snapshot recovery, preserved selection/context, responsive controls and no duplicate command. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNBcG4bNxLSHOwfSiPgvOb0CvJcRVmpm1MLdCbf1zVEp6duJjs6cJO9HSXVqiUJajDyWJJgLtcdhxEtNz3oBbgI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3351,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.584343861Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"ef138f08-9e8b-5762-8873-10465f8b82a9","title":"[L703] Wire product observations preserve settlement integrity but do not add context or candidate fences to controls","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L703.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-app-protocol/src/wire/product.rs:20-35,110-149,177-201,228-270`; `src/wire/product/observations.rs:9-50`; `src/wire/product/settlement.rs:24-38,51-68,82-97`; `src/wire/request/support.rs:47-61`; `src/wire/event.rs:43-103,123-150` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Product controls carry run ID and action only, retaining L691's absence of exact candidate/generation binding. Snapshot text is copied before constructor size validation. Observation pages are limited to 256 complete snapshots and frame ceilings still apply. Settlement decoding rebuilds a reducer and validates disposition/checkpoint provenance instead of accepting a claimed disposition blindly. Artifact-open carries transfer/artifact IDs only and event tags include metadata/chunk/completion, without a typed transfer failure/status/resume offset; terminal unavailability is separately expressible.\n- Consequence: Observational qualification consistency is useful integrity, but does not establish safe effect retry, context restoration or resumable byte transfer. Large valid snapshots can still make a count-valid page impossible to send within one frame.\n- Repair direction: Bind effecting controls to exact durable candidate state and expose paged/restorable positions and outcomes. Retain settlement provenance validation. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signe