{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3357,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.597351245Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"0a45c2fa-4d71-55f3-a7e5-95338ea09bc2","title":"[L706] Compaction proposals require strictly smaller byte handles and one whole preview","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L706.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-app-protocol/src/workbench/compaction.rs:6-7,20-26,56-64,97-107,154-195,222-225`; `src/wire/workbench_compaction.rs:23-38,41-100` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Optional focus is capped at 1,024 bytes. Every replacement must be nonempty and strictly smaller than its source. Preview generations/revisions are positive, entries are unique ordered by invocation, at most 65,535, and aggregate byte sums must fit u64. Empty previews are accepted but not applicable. Wire allocates all entries from a raw u16 count and applies the proposal as one complete payload. Preserved recent/pinned/unresolved/unsavable counts are observations; byte reduction alone does not prove preservation of model understanding.\n- Consequence: Applying a very large historical compaction can hit whole-frame/cardinality gates; unsavable sources legitimately remain. These types describe an explicit public-reply prompt view, not adoption or recovery of the original provider window.\n- Repair direction: Persist scalable preview manifests with exact confirmation and source provenance; distinguish byte compaction from native context continuity. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTI