{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3359,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.601371873Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"cef11a42-ae31-5f8e-8956-ed5a961828c6","title":"[L707] Brief projection limits exact proposals and rejects empty file observations","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L707.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-app-protocol/src/workbench/brief.rs:12-15,53-62,111-127,208-224,238-257,284-287`; `src/wire/workbench_brief.rs:81-138`; `src/workbench/brief/tests.rs:20-79`; `src/wire/workbench_brief/tests.rs:4-29` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Four closed user-confirmed fields and eight exact agent reply proposals are allowed. Proposal text uses the queue's 8,192-byte cap and its digest is checked; omitted proposals are reported as a count. Attachment observations require 1..64 MiB, labels at most 4,096 bytes, and at most 65,535 observations. Empty-file metadata accepted by context rows (L704) is rejected here. Wire prechecks field/proposal counts but allocates the whole observation vector from raw u16 count without a separate page limit. Confirmed, proposed, and observed authority are kept distinct.\n- Consequence: Brief construction/display can fail for otherwise meaningful empty files or excessive retained observations. Proposal omission is disclosed but the brief itself has no continuation page. Tests check small projections/count rejection, not large-history feasibility or native resume.\n- Repair direction: Page optional source history, represent empty files consistently, and preserve exact user confirmation and inert observation boundaries. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNlpt5qhEzWXyJc1s1DA3IaZO2V0933bsFsaB8hzygKNpYybIBU4r0cVM5R9n3BSAsnuREyTSWts3HPwZwAiuwE="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3360,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.603478855Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"cef11a42-ae31-5f8e-8956-ed5a961828c6","comment_uuid":"f8d6ce10-a78c-440e-98e4-cb29b01ef212","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L707: Brief projection limits exact proposals and rejects empty file observations.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-app-protocol/src/workbench/brief.rs:12-15,53-62,111-127,208-224,238-257,284-287; src/wire/workbench_brief.rs:81-138; src/workbench/brief/tests.rs:20-79; src/wire/workbench_brief/tests.rs:4-29. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nPage optional source history, represent empty files consistently, and preserve exact user confirmation and inert observation boundaries. No tests run.\n\nPreserve: durable logical session and run identity, exact command receipts, atomic snapshot/cursor binding, explicit authority, selected UI state, complete history retrieval and owned-effect reconciliation. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large histories and non-ASCII fields, queue/connection pressure, delayed acknowledgements, subscription gaps, disconnect/reconnect and daemon restart, proving snapshot recovery, preserved selection/context, responsive controls and no duplicate command. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQB2lFPn6++alEwaRbw3u4avkbU8UTvh+ZZB47GzTMdEE/5qUk4Fe4Z43NzDAc62/upwdfdOXnlEAkyeW0/93ag0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3361,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.605570972Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"09a0cb4a-6475-5787-81a5-eeeea627c3f6","title":"[L708] File and image history pages impose a 256-retained-reference ceiling","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L708.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-app-protocol/src/workbench/files/page.rs:18-26,126-137`; `src/workbench/images/page.rs:24-32,144-162,169-172`; `src/wire/workbench_files/page.rs:44-74`; `src/workbench/images/tests/page.rs:19-32`; `src/wire/workbench_image_page/tests.rs:26-38` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: File/image page offsets cannot exceed 256 and total retained references cannot exceed 256, even though each response is already paginated to 32 rows. Image totals explicitly include excluded references and file page documentation retains immutable history. File queries require positive revisions even at page zero; image queries allow current revision zero only for the first request, with responses requiring a committed revision. Tests explicitly reject a 257-reference image page/offset.\n- Consequence: Long-lived conversations can become impossible to represent once retained attachment history exceeds this synthetic total cap; deselection is not deletion. This is not merely a per-frame memory bound. Host admission/retention behavior still needs caller tracing.\n- Repair direction: Remove total-history/offset policy ceilings, retain durable indexed history, and keep exact revision-fenced bounded pages and explicit user selection. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5