{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3365,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.614306407Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"d92f5b24-42c9-5b73-9e55-47ab3add9400","title":"[L710] Raster admission has fixed encoded, geometry, frame and format gates","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L710.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-app-protocol/src/workbench/images.rs:17-20,67-78`; `src/workbench/images/metadata.rs:6-17,45-64`; `src/workbench/images/tests.rs:31-65`; `src/wire/workbench_images.rs:80-95` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Original image must be 1..4 MiB, dimensions each 1..8,192, canvas at most 16,777,216 pixels and frame count 1..64. Only PNG/JPEG/GIF/WebP are represented. Labels are 1,024 bytes. The DTO validates metadata shape; it explicitly does not prove actual decoding or selected-provider support. Tests admit exactly 4 MiB/4096x4096/64 frames and reject stated excesses; no conversion/scalable alternative is present in these files.\n- Consequence: Ordinary high-resolution screenshots or animations can fail irrespective of the configured provider's actual supported capacity. Decoder resource containment is legitimate, but fixed original-media retention and provider-input policies are currently coupled.\n- Repair direction: Retain immutable originals as artifacts and offer explicit derived previews/input transformations according to actual decoder/provider capability, preserving exact consent and provenance. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1