tories and non-ASCII fields, queue/connection pressure, delayed acknowledgements, subscription gaps, disconnect/reconnect and daemon restart, proving snapshot recovery, preserved selection/context, responsive controls and no duplicate command. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPgfYOXl7RMtmLBwL4UlRskuVilaqo55cSJUhCU/kdAaMyjFljP0lIrjztXkevFaGqDh7lVzPj8OCIf14XDYEQ4="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3369,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.622796501Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"d0d802ff-ef4f-5eb0-bc7a-098069fe77c4","title":"[L712] Checkpoint and rewind coverage use whole 65,535-item lists and production-sized preview hashing","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L712.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-app-protocol/src/workbench/checkpoints.rs:6-7,347-369,385-394`; `src/workbench/checkpoints/rewind.rs:188-213`; `src/wire/workbench_checkpoints.rs:174-186,229-241,267-288,332-354` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Names are 256 bytes, relative paths 4,096 bytes, each coverage/exclusion/effect list at most 65,535 entries, and exclusion/effect descriptions 512 bytes in previews. All preview facts are encoded together under production codec limits to form the confirmation fingerprint. Wire allocates raw-u16 list capacities without the generic collection ceiling, with path length validated after owned copying. Per-file captured size itself is u64 without a fixed byte policy here.\n- Consequence: A large workspace can hit list or whole-preview codec limits before consent can be represented, despite individual files being supported. Raw-count allocation retains L702's issue. Exact preimage/postimage/conflict checks protect user changes and are not synthetic deadlines.\n- Repair direction: Bind consent to durable paginated coverage manifests and stream their hash while retaining complete exact path decisions and visible exclusions. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3N