cts reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEZJ0w5r/ffMfDo0W46wm5+I7HRBBqEWZ+jxrq3Gqu/shJq028zT2HY01sxa8iObd8H2R16+Bve0sc5qXCs2Cw4="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3377,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.639790252Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"293f7f7e-c3ae-5eec-b52c-1fb90f25bc73","title":"[L717] Preview profiles still require a finite readiness deadline even when the process wall deadline is absent","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L717.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-app-protocol/src/workbench/launch/profile.rs:173-230,267-275`; `src/wire/workbench_launch/profile.rs:64-86` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: readiness_millis is a required u64 and zero is rejected. wall_millis is optional; wire zero means absent. If a wall deadline is supplied it must be positive and at least the readiness deadline. There is no representation for waiting for readiness without a synthetic duration. Inherited-host networking and terminate-owned-tree cancellation are explicit lifecycle/authority posture, not elapsed-time limits.\n- Consequence: Removing the process wall deadline alone leaves a mandatory readiness limiter in the profile. The daemon's readiness observation and timeout consequences still require complete caller inspection; this is a source-level capability restriction, not a measured cause of the live lockup.\n- Repair direction: Represent readiness as an observable persistent state with cancellation and user-selected optional duration, separate from process ownership and retained output. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQP96lsN9ZKL/0sOq3rxTyDALEKOEM46FT30DoC+kHGvtXaHnp7mIQ9clXTOm99ylgoCODzPYf27n4K8KRpHnowM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3378,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.641952831Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"293f7f7e-c3ae-5eec-b52c-1fb90f25bc73","comment_uuid":"a749d1d5-b982-4d88-acbe-febf66597ffd","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L717: Preview profiles still require a finite readiness deadline even when the process wall deadline is absent.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-app-protocol/src/workbench/launch/profile.rs:173-230,267-275; src/wire/workbench_launch/profile.rs:64-86. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nRepresent readiness as an observable persistent state with cancellation and user-selected optional duration, separate from process ownership and retained output. No tests run.\n\nPreserve: exact process birth/tree identity, confined authority, one-use dispatch receipts, monotonic cancel intent, truthful terminal/ownership settlement, complete output accounting and platform OS constraints. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEYx5iQiogA/Ih6VrGi9tDQ6uNC004QjTFos6sfGkKm7JbQep2mcRImD1IRFTkf0/ZmjJdU1TDLTCjN2LuyTFwE="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3379,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.644011784Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"a1ebf5ad-09d5-54f3-8f36-2f3d9234e5c7","title":"[L718] Whole launch histories, output and review diffs remain coupled to a single response frame","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L718.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-app-protocol/src/wire/workbench_launch.rs:22-32,121-140,175-220,319-337`; `src/wire/workbench_launch/output.rs:1-40`; `src/wire/workbench_review.rs:108-147,170-193`; `src/wire/workbench_goal.rs:32-36,96-105`; `src/wire/interaction.rs:166-182,225-231` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: Launch-result queries identify scope/run without an offset or cursor. Results encode complete launch/interaction/capture/feedback collections, each raw-u16 count up to 65,535; output adds the full results page plus full stdout/stderr entries. Review pages paginate comments but repeat all structured diff files/hunks/lines, bounded per domain collection. Goal criteria also use raw-u16 capacities rather than generic collection checks. By contrast interaction activity/model counts are checked against 256/4,096 before allocation. Several strings/byte vectors are copied before their smaller domain checks. Goal active/wall milliseconds and capture timestamps are observations, not stopping deadlines.\n- Consequence: Long histories or wide diffs can become unrepresentable in the aggregate frame despite individually valid records, and every review-comments page repeats the complete diff. Raw-count preallocation extends L702. More history should not prevent retrieving current work or recovery information.\n- Repair direction: Persist complete histories and expose revision-stable pages/ranged output and diff artifacts; validate counts and lengths before allocation. Retain exact anchors and consent. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJxEs3HCKp7As1UB/grPldhnAZ/6ZTtKhXLLKI+usZ1T+gexMSkp5uUVcABciEMtJYlkjAV+5Gtyqlu8mQILBwo="}
