ration must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQP1cQE0cRyAdwlN82NaMZjgKbaExiVw5rnZneeGhCs2I2Oo91ZobQcEAaOV7kSL4q1H1NOOZzRbvXcGFtMbhvwc="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3381,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.648318263Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"ab185691-eff6-51a1-953c-0a02f83e2385","title":"[L723] Instance admission can misreport filesystem failures and strand temporary publication files","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L723.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/instance/lock.rs:19-55,100-148`; `src/instance/record.rs:1-95` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: every failed `try_lock` becomes AlreadyRunning. Instance publication uses a PID-named `create_new` temporary file; this path has no stale-temp reconciliation. Windows removes the previous instance record before renaming the successor, and its directory-sync helper is inert.\n- Consequence: a filesystem/locking failure can look like a live competing daemon; a crash-left temporary file can reject publication when its PID is reused. Windows publication can lose the prior birth record across the remove/rename interval. These are source-derived failure conditions, not a diagnosis of the running instance.\n- Repair direction: distinguish lock contention from other failures; reconcile temporary publication against exact ownership facts; make record replacement recoverable. Retain exclusive state-root ownership and native process-birth verification. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKWEeQpCUtmElC0Wg9TPN2dXpCPwni+eU6FRiaWRJD/kfOJ6CvdUW/R5Lq1iH6dP5Q0y+JxxJv1Wi3kJ+OapHgE="}
