{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3383,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.652616644Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"c243489a-da39-5390-854f-c54a0e9ac008","title":"[L724] Windows IPC has an independent fixed 65-instance native ceiling","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L724.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/ipc/windows.rs:11-12,68-81,311-335`; `src/ipc/windows/native/identity.rs:1-101` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: every server pipe uses MAX_PIPE_INSTANCES=65. Accept rearms a successor pipe before returning the accepted connection; failure to allocate that successor disconnects the arrival and reports a resource error.\n- Consequence: the native pipe allocation ceiling can reject arrivals independently of configured daemon connection limits, including the pending accept instance. SID/token allocation and pointer-range bounds serve a different purpose: native identity containment.\n- Repair direction: derive native admission from explicit configured resource policy and account for the pending accept instance; expose pressure and recovery without discarding an authenticated resumable owner. Preserve principal authentication and native buffer validation. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQG6CG7hHvcDxxLZ2AxhKk9dmKP0Ln+5VL9UXAjZf0xlvl/IgQgVPPYUoXjRZOizCU2Zouav9PORcIJxnWPvUyw4="}
