{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3385,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.657014424Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"7da24304-19de-5779-a45e-680ca82a3733","title":"[L725] Terminal restart recovery intrinsically refuses all reattachment","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L725.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/terminal/recovery.rs:1-48`; `src/terminal/bridge.rs:55-88,151-211`; `src/terminal/bridge/owner.rs:59-78`; `src/terminal/registry.rs:74-90`; `src/terminal/registry/lookup.rs:1-64` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: every RestartTerminalDisposition returns false from permits_attachment, including LiveControlUnavailable for an exactly identified live owned process. New registries and bridges start with empty owner/replay maps and zero offsets. Preview session reassignment exists only inside the surviving registry and requires no attachments; direct-process access requires the original actor/session.\n- Consequence: terminal control and replay die with the daemon, despite a live native process tree. Same-process detach/reconnect tests cannot establish restart persistence. This proves a terminal ownership gap; it does not by itself prove the live provider context was dropped.\n- Repair direction: keep native control in a recoverable supervisor with authenticated durable ownership and output offsets; restore registry state from verified receipts. Preserve birth and actor checks rather than merely changing the disposition Boolean. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAA