{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3387,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.661675169Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"20a50119-6b79-5936-9ff7-c4f66d339890","title":"[L726] A new terminal attachment must replay its whole history into a smaller pending queue","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L726.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/terminal/limits.rs:1-80`; `src/terminal/bridge.rs:172-211`; `src/terminal/bridge/observation.rs:145-162`; `src/terminal/attachment.rs:87-115` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: production retains up to 4,096 replay events/8 MiB, but permits only 1,024 pending events/2 MiB per attachment. Attach enqueues the whole retained prefix before draining. Replay eviction permanently sets replay_complete=false; a subsequent attachment is rejected rather than resuming from an acknowledged offset.\n- Consequence: retained history that fits the replay store can already be too large to reattach. Beyond replay capacity, the bridge refuses new replay attachments for its remaining lifetime. No elapsed timeout is needed to encounter this blocker.\n- Repair direction: persist output with explicit available ranges, acknowledged offsets and bounded streaming replay. Treat storage pressure as resumable flow control, not permanent loss of attachment eligibility. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGfc0kpTB0nBLXHO/Sm5AVDbaIHjrfnNlg640rY58bBBeqG9ZoX1C2fnmuTX5zr57YG2F8yPWO4Ewikvih3HPA0="}
