{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3389,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.666167433Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"ff71fb92-0f40-57d1-986d-35bc8e21be35","title":"[L727] Terminal observation can overflow an attachment before giving it a delivery opportunity","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L727.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/terminal/limits.rs:1-80`; `src/terminal/bridge.rs:260-267`; `src/terminal/bridge/observation.rs:35-93`; `src/terminal/attachment.rs:87-115,160-183`; `src/session/connection/terminal_tests/native.rs:1-127` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: a poll observes up to eight 256-event process pages before draining at most 128 delivery events. That producer batch exceeds the 1,024-event pending ceiling even before smaller client chunk sizes multiply events. Overflow faults the attachment; its error omits an exact missed byte range. A sequence gap faults the whole bridge.\n- Consequence: a burst can trigger loss of an otherwise responsive attachment; slowing the reader is not the only cause. Existing native tests show isolation for a 4 KiB burst and continuation of a sibling, not large-history reconnect or owner restart.\n- Repair direction: couple observation to downstream capacity or a durable spool, retain retry offsets and distinguish per-reader pressure from corrupted producer ordering. Preserve exact sequence/stream identity validation. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNzLIpvF0oZQ3Sveow/o9h03MFw9OQ