{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3391,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.670948942Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"23baadc7-bfb3-557e-a23d-0a26cc7b1899","title":"[L728] Terminal completion receipts expire by volatile FIFO capacity and original session binding","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L728.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/terminal/registry/receipts.rs:1-111`; `src/terminal/registry/transitions.rs:1-61`; `src/terminal/registry.rs:135-159,323-343`; `src/terminal/registry/tests.rs:1-261` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: detach/cancel receipts live only in registry memory, are bound to the original attachment actor/session, and evict oldest entries at the attachment-count limit (4,096 in production). Shutdown clears them. Registry construction does not restore them.\n- Consequence: exact duplicate operations can stop resolving after enough unrelated retirements, daemon restart, or session identity replacement. This is count-based forgetting rather than an elapsed deadline; documentation about expired history should identify that distinction.\n- Repair direction: retain durable, scope-bound operation receipts and reconcile a reconnect with the same logical owner. Use explicit retention/compaction proof rather than silently forgetting an unresolved retry identity. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDnctnpfXAvDBSj25qGrJH0gLGMY8V4uxkJ6IEczkUyv5e5K+iETmduy6/+Hsqy+XaphAPe+g7MgBR4aR3NF9QA="}
