{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3395,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.679799550Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"52a570ce-8279-5d27-8f62-be854047194f","title":"[L730] Recovery and upload compensation paths suppress persistence or cleanup failures","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L730.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/session/request/media.rs:35-47,76-88`; `src/product_run/execution/baseline.rs:1-29`; `src/product_run/execution/handoff.rs:1-35` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: upload registration failure attempts cancellation but ignores its result. Baseline loading failure makes a candidate nonactionable and RecoveryRequired, then ignores persist_record failure. Handoff failure reporting ignores snapshot replacement/interaction append failures after assembling complete detail text.\n- Consequence: the original error can hide unresolved transfer cleanup or a failure to make recovery state durable. The in-memory candidate is gated, but restart behavior depends on which earlier record survived. These paths require caller/recovery reconciliation; no live failure is asserted here.\n- Repair direction: retain both original and compensation failures with a durable retry identity; commit recovery disposition before acknowledging it. Bound projection work through streaming/paging without dropping the failure receipt. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQL2QgoAj9TxpLrfpjpDgPu+gS4FTwDJkBpIu+xrCpJwMTiQvL0fDAmMlo2KELk7BuJTEbKSJik