{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3397,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.684476102Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"e6e9a48a-8540-5f06-83b3-bddce65602cf","title":"[L731] Best-effort diagnostics can block and unbounded diagnostics can fail status projection","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L731.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/diagnostic.rs:1-7`; `src/lifecycle.rs:92-95,113-123`; `src/error.rs:89-100,130-133` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: best-effort diagnostics synchronously lock/write stderr and ignore I/O errors. Read-only lifecycle diagnostics and error constructor details are accepted without local bounds; lifecycle status later validates the negotiated projection. Error Display drops recovery/source fields.\n- Consequence: a slow/full stderr pipe can stall its caller, while an oversized stored diagnostic can make the status observation itself fail. Unlimited execution time does not resolve either blocking condition. This is source-derived, conditional on output/projection state.\n- Repair direction: use a bounded nonblocking diagnostic sink with retained structured recovery metadata; project oversized detail through a stable reference/page rather than failing the status contract. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQASJmQD8qh1Gezs8i7bb0fgyM60Y4rPvVbyzR2B2Nq2VnSkasOBtM/BGuyTd/BfWaktGhlrzi7+LUzVqazBdGg0="}
