{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3401,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.693233925Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"ccda3929-d1fc-5927-b0c6-d93b9ae5946f","title":"[L733] Hosted routes retain finite retry counts and model metadata only in process memory","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L733.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/component/hosted.rs:25-34,58-104,106-150,154-222`; `src/component/credentials.rs:29-63,103-140` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: hosted Anthropic/Google composition uses without_deadline with two retries, a fixed backoff schedule and a 64 MiB retry-body budget. Model discovery replaces a volatile catalog. Selecting an alternate model on mixed-protocol services requires catalog dialect metadata; selected_profile inherits the configured profile, while this selector consults discovered metadata only for dialect/tool support. Credential errors intentionally omit secret store contents. The Windows restart fixture tests vault access in another real process, not provider-context adoption.\n- Consequence: removing elapsed deadlines leaves count/byte retry gates. After daemon recreation an alternate mixed-protocol model can require rediscovery before selection; this catalog is not a durable context owner. Configured profile limits must not be assumed to describe a newly selected model merely because discovery succeeded.\n- Repair direction: persist versioned model capability metadata or rediscover as resumable preparation; drive retry policy from explicit recoverable operation state. Preserve credential privacy and advertised lack of tool support as a real capability condition. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxu