{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3405,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.701751968Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"0b7797f3-b68b-5c4b-8ff1-bf844867e00c","title":"[L735] Conversation creation rescans all immutable control history and every restore reservation","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L735.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_control/storage/library.rs:193-217`; `src/product_control/storage/reservations.rs:6-55`; `src/product_control/storage/library.rs:21-175` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: conversation_ids starts at global position zero on every call and synchronously decodes 4,096-record pages to EOF. Reservation checks invoke it, load every conversation and walk its restores. A retention gap or unexpected frame family rejects rebuilding; any source-load error rejects the creation/reservation check. Fork publication itself atomically writes source/child records, lineage and exact operation receipt with conflict reconciliation.\n- Consequence: more daily history increases complete-history work on new creation and branching; a single unreconstructable source can block an unrelated child admission. No elapsed deadline exists in these loops, so removal of timers alone leaves growing synchronous work. The atomic receipt path is meaningful persistence evidence but does not retain a native model context.\n- Repair direction: maintain a verified rebuildable catalog/reservation projection with durable incremental positions, page recovery and isolate unrelated damaged entries. Preserve exact source/child ownership, command fingerprint and atomic lineage publication. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHSXakg5z6WOq8VHnQFFAW9MirHvBFx4adN4agNFlP+VP4XYauakVEVdXpeI8urfkm3SenEePKzSXQJAn5YOfgA="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3406,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.703890165Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"0b7797f3-b68b-5c4b-8ff1-bf844867e00c","comment_uuid":"6f445824-a448-490e-98d3-031c61931057","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L735: Conversation creation rescans all immutable control history and every restore reservation.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_control/storage/library.rs:193-217; src/product_control/storage/reservations.rs:6-55; src/product_control/storage/library.rs:21-175. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nmaintain a verified rebuildable catalog/reservation projection with durable incremental positions, page recovery and isolate unrelated damaged entries. Preserve exact source/child ownership, command fingerprint and atomic lineage publication. No tests run.\n\nPreserve: exact snapshot/preimage identity, protected paths, ancestor and symlink safety, writable-fork coverage, conflict detection, one logical restore transaction and exact effect receipts. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large-file and many-path capture/restore, divergent preimage rejection, interrupted staging/publication/restore, then reopen and continue the same conversation with an exact restored workspace. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGozqzWVBSaOuqzFHO7xY30NuzU3ChePQq20e00rOsHgUI67y9ZtemoW+8PTEmu5sNxL/R/M8Vfrhe93CKODWgs="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3407,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.706116650Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"e8999a5a-e76e-5bd8-8efa-cddbb0c4b275","title":"[L736] File and image consent archives add fixed 16 KiB proof ceilings and full-byte reconstruction","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L736.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_control/storage/files.rs:17-39,42-102`; `src/product_control/storage/images.rs:36-76,79-140`; `src/product_control/storage/initialization.rs:13-62`; `src/product_control/storage/permissions.rs:13-58` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: file consent and confirmed image preview must be nonempty and at most 16 KiB. Archived images retain the original fixed MAX_IMAGE_BYTES ceiling; reconstructing media copies the complete bytes and hashes the archive. File reconstruction copies complete selected text. Both archive proof and operation receipt are published together and checked against the exact producing position; initialization retains an exact manifest digest and permissions use a revision fence.\n- Consequence: growth in legitimate preview/consent detail can reject admission even when the selected artifact fits its own size gate. Reads/replays operate on full archives rather than ranges. These proof checks are durable integrity/consent controls; they should not be removed with synthetic time limits.\n- Repair direction: use versioned structured consent records or bounded references/pages with complete retrievable detail, and stream artifact verification. Preserve atomic byte/proof publication, producing-position checks and workspace policy revision fences. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxu