{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3409,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.710382275Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"900834e4-6965-5621-bf26-9e579e763bda","title":"[L738] Legacy goal operation identities intentionally block newer host accounting without migration","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L738.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_control/tests/goal.rs:82-144,146-227`.\n- Behavior: v2 tool accounting scopes identity to role and loop invocation and preserves exact usage across store reopen. The legacy fixture commits v1 reserve/complete operations, then expects both newer reserve and completion requests to reject with UnsupportedSchema and leave the original usage unchanged.\n- Consequence: an older active goal carrying those legacy receipts can encounter an explicit schema blocker even after time/count budgets are removed. This fail-closed behavior prevents ambiguous duplicate debits; removing the check without migration would lose that guarantee. The fixture does not attempt migration or resume native provider state.\n- Repair direction: provide a receipt-grounded migration/reconciliation path that determines original role/invocation identity or reports the exact unresolved fact while retaining the goal. Preserve rejection of contradictory identities and never fabricate a debit. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPPWiEYN4hgZSqubB/+qGGts9qWBlg5DZyxCPtSc+B/tQJJnT+uEzXV84m0fR4G7fjG/inZf5fMjHfZXH59RIQg="}
