rted count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFocQcQ3/Mb+GfkhbR0FcJVlAsBg7gjQold1KKDy3zUqgHDbrooNyEqZxUNIEE1l0mNcEpyrzrTzra3gwOLRfA0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3411,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.714581230Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"909b810d-efc4-5af1-bcac-7eeb1676a5b5","title":"[L739] Library pagination still performs full-history work and can construct an invalid exact snippet","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L739.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_run/library.rs:24-105,141-190,233-249`; `crates/app/peritus-app-protocol/src/workbench/library.rs:9-13,29-36,127-137,337-348`; L735.\n- Behavior: every page rebuilds the entire conversation catalog, loads each full conversation before actor/workspace filtering, searches all retained input revisions and reply archives, then sorts all matching rows before slicing. An unrelated failed load aborts the page. The excerpt takes 192 bytes of context on each side plus the literal, so a valid 256-byte query can produce a 640-byte snippet; the DTO rejects more than 512 bytes. Handoff labels silently truncate at 1,024 bytes. Page queries carry an offset but no immutable catalog revision.\n- Consequence: paging bounds returned rows rather than source work. Long valid literal matches with surrounding text can fail the whole library as corrupt projection. Changes between requests can shift offsets and repeat or omit rows. These are source-derived conditions; no performance or runtime failure is claimed.\n- Repair direction: query a verified incremental catalog with a stable revision cursor; fit exact excerpts to their negotiated budget while retaining the complete match and source reference. Isolate damaged unrelated records and make truncation retrievable. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGTDGBCDJg98IIck9aor+r45qsr6zNyibJLUNXu17d9vnIWSrhs/fJJIJRICvNOEl0eEoXhxZGOxO8hCSTV/gg8="}
