{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3413,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.718943059Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"c2019885-ab0a-595f-8d57-591f57e8a081","title":"[L740] Model discovery freshness can gate start and uses an independent cancellation token","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L740.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_run/catalog.rs:34-116,119-163,167-194`; L733.\n- Behavior: a cached catalog is reused for 300 seconds; expiration triggers awaited discovery with a fresh CancellationToken unrelated to the caller's token. A per-provider try-lock returns cached/unavailable observations rather than queuing another discovery. Nonmanual selections must be present in the resulting list; manual selections skip that check but still resolve the adapter. select_model failures collapse to ProviderUnavailable, losing the adapter's detailed cause.\n- Consequence: 300 seconds is a metadata freshness interval, not a session deadline, but a stale-cache start can wait on discovery. A stalled discovery holds its slot until its future resolves or is dropped. Lost selection causes can obscure mixed-protocol metadata/capability failures. Interactive selections correctly disallow silent model failover.\n- Repair direction: keep an explicit cancellable, resumable discovery operation and durable metadata revision; separate refresh pressure from admission of a previously verified selection. Preserve explicit model choice and detailed failure ownership. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW