{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3415,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.723284204Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"1f8fc773-4125-582c-9380-8d149c13e0ef","title":"[L741] Stored-schema and provider failures can advertise recovery actions that do not address their cause","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L741.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_run/error.rs:9,33-78,87-176,179-255,267-277,380-391`; L738.\n- Behavior: UnsupportedSchema from stored control state maps to Reconnect/Negotiation, and the regression test explicitly expects that classification. ProviderUnavailable maps to InvalidIdentifier/NewRequest; selected adapter causes have already been discarded. Duplicate run diagnostics direct starting a new run. Persistence failures direct restarting after restoring write access. Public diagnostic construction truncates to 1,024 bytes.\n- Consequence: reconnecting the same protocol does not migrate legacy durable receipts, and a new request ID does not repair an unavailable model or ambiguous committed operation. Repeating those actions can preserve the underlying blocker while replacing attempt identities. Recovery instructions can also be truncated independently of typed classification.\n- Repair direction: classify durable schema migration separately from handshake negotiation, retain exact provider/operation causes and resolve existing identities before prescribing a new run. Provide durable recovery state and retrievable full diagnostics. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3J