producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large histories and non-ASCII fields, queue/connection pressure, delayed acknowledgements, subscription gaps, disconnect/reconnect and daemon restart, proving snapshot recovery, preserved selection/context, responsive controls and no duplicate command. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIGaMM8iE9RdbH4Vo4d0RI4UemL5wDIxDz9d3nPWYqVARxi5m5WfvrxxYDE39w86dfzSaO+DqBB0mhoLm7yB8AQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3421,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.737201550Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"7d145c05-237b-5625-990d-b4c29c05ac76","title":"[L744] Deliverable controls hold the global run lock through unowned synchronous Git and file operations","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L744.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_run/deliverable.rs:25-158,230-283`; `src/product_run/deliverable/commit.rs:52-112,126-178,181-241`; `src/product_run/deliverable/commit/attempt.rs:67-82` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: control_deliverable acquires the records write lock before candidate validation, discard recovery, patch export, recursive nested commits, hashing and persistence. Committed export and commit helpers use std::process::Command output with whole stdout/stderr capture and no C2 owner/cancellation handle here. Git hooks/signers run inside that synchronous call. Recovery matching hashes the whole saved patch and candidate source to EOF.\n- Consequence: a blocked Git hook, signer, child or file operation can prevent record access/control for unrelated runs. Unbounded wall time permits the wait but does not provide progress, cancellation or native adoption. Whole output capture can grow before any public diagnostic bound applies. These are conditional source-derived blockers, not a measured live hang.\n- Repair direction: retain a durable explicit deliverable-operation owner and native effect receipt, perform cancellable observation outside shared locks, and publish a fenced result only after reconciliation. Stream output/hashing with progress and exact ranges. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAohA4AmJp0b7WB4pTAYYs8/A+wTU+AP5PByiXIciJ63uElyXbHCNavgwCHZjm1RfsRgnWvom0Ga0BVlBZwXVQ4="}
