he predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large histories and non-ASCII fields, queue/connection pressure, delayed acknowledgements, subscription gaps, disconnect/reconnect and daemon restart, proving snapshot recovery, preserved selection/context, responsive controls and no duplicate command. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLPBYQzSiX14W0xxAer++9KG9JiRqPsek5wzEkGfrulEFu5htoAtQqQ+i710Z0YmjKdASHThY0Ef6+sv8POZ2QQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3423,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.741639912Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"8eb0d3f4-dafe-5d18-9d43-843afe9ebb1a","title":"[L745] Commit recovery retains source proof but not an exact native commit-operation receipt","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L745.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_run/deliverable/commit/attempt.rs:14-82`; `src/product_run/deliverable/commit.rs:22-112,146-178`; `src/product_run/deliverable/commit/handoff.rs:9-67` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: the saved attempt contains workspace path, selected-path digest, candidate-source digest and patch digest; its decoder caps the sidecar at 64 KiB. Before commits change nested HEADs, the patch and run projection are persisted. Retry can reconcile changed repository context when source/patch still match. Each Git effect then runs synchronously, with HEAD resolved after completion; no expected per-repository parent/commit identity or started-child receipt is stored by this helper. Handoff clears resume when rebinding a changed repository context.\n- Consequence: source proof meaningfully avoids redoing unrelated content changes, but a crash in a nested commit or after a hook effect lacks an exact native operation outcome in this sidecar. Retry has to inspect current Git state; a matching saved patch does not prove which original commit completed. The sidecar size bound is a representation limit, not execution expiry.\n- Repair direction: persist per-repository effect intent, expected parent/tree and exact resolved commit identity, with crash reconciliation before further commits. Retain saved patches, source fencing and explicit user authorization rather than restarting an ambiguous effect. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMgGpb7P2BW3fBM5Y55WiuI5+0sevKUaimlqV8bcaDv6Q96vxCp6wS6xrwlqVwhm+fyCR50BGEIOMYaMk4zQBAM="}
