redecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQM/rkrIpy7ShdNtssY/c4Wgbg8TbgYMHp3UZTp0PoEdkG5DoMBVgeb7fAQxi6y/Wr4pfsnJUK3U5/4h6oJ+ilgc="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3425,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.746130530Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"4f3805fc-7027-5e6e-9559-ff0fa53d706f","title":"[L746] Export retries treat an existing path as an immutable result without verifying its bytes","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L746.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_run/deliverable.rs:36-52,185-204,238-283`; `src/product_run/persistence/deliverable.rs:7-48` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: saved export/repeated-action eligibility tests only nonempty export_path and is_file. Export writes a whole patch to a fixed per-run .patch.new path, syncs it and renames to the fixed .patch destination; Unix syncs the directory, while this path has no equivalent Windows directory sync. Persisted deliverables store the path but no export digest.\n- Consequence: an externally changed file can satisfy the existing-result check, and path existence alone does not identify the original immutable export. Late publication/projection failure remains recoverable only through the saved path/current run state, rather than a verified export receipt. Fixed output publication can replace earlier bytes before the run record is updated.\n- Repair direction: use a content-addressed export receipt with exact digest/length and recoverable publication state; verify original bytes before acknowledging a repeated operation. Preserve returning a verified saved export independently of mutable workspace admission. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc