{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3427,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.750517849Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"5669aff7-7e2d-5132-8e49-7cbe4f688d84","title":"[L747] Pending discard intentionally reserves the workspace but malformed old state blocks new admission","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L747.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_run/deliverable/discard.rs:36-117,130-157`; `src/product_run/deliverable/discard/reservation.rs:29-120`; `src/product_run/deliverable/discard/transaction.rs:42-96,99-164`; `src/product_run/deliverable.rs:100-138,162-182` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: discard retains candidate/baseline/checkpoint binding, lower-layer restore plan and completion proof independently of the run projection. A completed temporary acknowledgment can be recovered after rename failure; reservation alone is never completion. New workspace work scans every same-workspace run and rejects any pending intent or read error, directing retry of the original Discard. Record readers enforce a derived detail-size ceiling, and locked Prepared reads take at most 1,025 bytes. Recovery labels stop listing paths near the public detail limit but identify the remaining directory.\n- Consequence: a legitimate interrupted restore remains a workspace safety gate until reconciled; corrupted/stale same-workspace sidecars can also block unrelated admission without a migration/quarantine mechanism in this path. Windows directory sync is inert. These durable safety reservations are not artificial time limits and must not simply be disabled.\n- Repair direction: expose each exact pending owner and missing/conflicting recovery fact, reconcile or quarantine malformed sidecars with evidence preservation, and publish completion durably before releasing reservation. Retain exact preimage/plan fencing, atomic acknowledgment and no-false-completion checks. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNq6l6O0h8dUaEIivTaVqaK0DygGSvv1vUpRCjgY9jhevg+uXc/SfF1dM+hNDfmRlpA7/Vjn89yChguQ8OsxxAo="}
