{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3429,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.754922228Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"f57c2205-7137-54be-b006-c90953f3a4bd","title":"[L748] File preview shares image decoder admission and repeats complete verification on confirmation","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L748.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_run/workbench/files.rs:51-73,75-146,149-200`; `src/product_run/workbench/files/import.rs:18-89,101-135`; `src/product_run/workbench/images.rs:91-147,161-197` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: local file preview/confirmation uses the same try-acquired image_decodes semaphore as raster decoding, even for plain text. Busy requests immediately return Backpressure. Blocking file jobs retain the permit if their awaiting client disappears; image jobs also retain their permit through decode. Preview and new confirmation reread/redecode and compare the exact preview; original committed receipts resolve before redoing that work. Imports read whole selected artifacts under the fixed file/image byte ceilings.\n- Consequence: a stalled or saturated image/file worker can reject unrelated text previews, with no queue/resume position in this API. Repeated consent verification is necessary integrity work, but its scheduling and complete reads can become admission blockers. Client disconnect does not stop a started blocking read.\n- Repair direction: separate fair I/O/decoder admission, retain cancellable pending operations and source-version receipts, and stream selections while preserving exact consent comparison and no detached publication. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//