{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3433,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.764328692Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"fc2bcce1-b6dc-57b1-8d7d-eb0bc67c9291","title":"[L750] Brief projection skips larger replies and can reject a legitimate empty file","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L750.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_run/workbench/brief.rs:61-133`; `src/product_run/workbench/mapping.rs:50-90`; L707 and L709.\n- Behavior: the brief exposes only MAX_WORKBENCH_BRIEF_PROPOSALS (eight) newest replies that fit WorkbenchInputText (8 KiB); other replies increment an excluded count with no proposal cursor. It projects every retained file/image observation into one result. File observations use selected bytes directly, while WorkbenchBriefObservation requires a positive byte count; selected empty text is admitted by the file path contract. Accepting a reply as a brief also reconstructs it as bounded ControlText.\n- Consequence: larger exact public replies disappear from proposal selection rather than offering a structural continuation; a retained empty file can fail the whole brief projection instead of remaining a valid zero-byte source. Full retained-source projection remains frame-coupled even when source pages exist elsewhere.\n- Repair direction: page exact proposals/observations and model empty source observations consistently. Keep explicit user acceptance, immutable reply digests and exact author/source binding. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZz