{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3435,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.768411948Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"e993a2fd-45db-5cd0-a26d-daadecade362","title":"[L751] Initialization effect and final control receipt have an unreconciled publication gap","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L751.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_run/workbench/folder_mutation.rs:33-87`; `src/product_run/workbench/folder_mutation/init.rs:115-165,168-213`; `src/product_run/workbench.rs:262-266` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: apply_init first resolves a C0 RecordInitialization receipt, then revalidates the old proposal/preimage, applies the authorized C1 patch, and finally publishes manifest/receipt to C0. Its comment explicitly says a failed final publication remains unresolved because C1 has consumed the action. The public receipt lookup only searches the C0 operation/archive; this path does not reconstruct the missing C0 receipt from the installed C1 transaction.\n- Consequence: if the patch succeeds and final control publication fails, an exact retry can encounter the now-changed initialization preimage before reaching lower-layer consumption, while receipt lookup still returns absent. This preserves against blindly reapplying an effect but leaves successful authorized work without its completion acknowledgment.\n- Repair direction: journal the cross-layer initialization intent and reconcile the exact installed C1 manifest into the original C0 operation receipt before any new proposal validation. Preserve owner, revision, action and proposal fingerprints. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signatur