d effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJ2WWSUIBapatmP7Ok73xSDl9haK49qd3bfy6t+opkOIFO/AhplwgpwjcKrKaPjvZOgdXxaYSWsgrClf57cR8A4="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3437,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.772547664Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"00b09a40-b709-5d21-a6d4-67d22d5a3a66","title":"[L752] Review pages recompute the complete candidate and require execution eligibility","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L752.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_run/workbench/review.rs:199-234,261-321`; `src/product_run/workbench/review/projection.rs:12-72`; L718.\n- Behavior: each comment page loads the entire control record, takes the shared run-record read lock, requires may_start_execution, hashes the live candidate, parses the whole snapshot diff, and repeats all diff files plus two evidence states. Only comments are sliced. One stale/malformed projection rejects the page; comments preserve exact anchor digests and distinguish stale/dismissed/addressed state.\n- Consequence: a nominally read-only review depends on execution-admission state and complete repository work under the record lock. More diff/history grows per-page work and single-frame pressure; paging comments does not page the candidate. Exact current-anchor checks protect against applying feedback to changed source and must remain.\n- Repair direction: use a verified immutable candidate/diff observation with independent read eligibility and paged source coverage; require exact current fencing when mutating or starting feedback execution. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQI6rNu92Wcv9f