ulti-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAi68MZhX6ZVjb3ULkbaE1EpGrrkPQRqV4VHAVpqZurHzH3EjBu1H0+SgGiysafsc/EYUDptX9gEs6x+OawQmgs="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3439,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.776513810Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"7461303b-b05f-5cf1-af46-5119b91428ae","title":"[L753] Accepted review feedback can lose its execution handoff and exact retry does not restore it","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L753.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_run/workbench.rs:120-150,157-202`; `src/product_run/workbench/review.rs:81-196` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: the ordinary command commits AddReview/RebindReview to C0, then calls resume_feedback only for a fresh accepted receipt. Handoff can subsequently reject active workspace/operation state, fail adapter resolution or fail run-record persistence. An exact retry returns the existing C0 receipt early and never retries that handoff. Before persistence, resume_feedback replaces cancellation handles, mode, snapshot, progress (with defaults) and settlement in memory, with no rollback in this function.\n- Consequence: a user can receive a handoff error after their feedback was durably accepted; retry can then acknowledge the feedback without starting its intended work. A failed save can leave an in-memory queued projection without a spawned owner. Starting feedback also resets aggregate progress rather than retaining the prior attempt base.\n- Repair direction: persist a resumable feedback-execution handoff with the original command identity, reconcile it on both fresh and duplicate receipt paths, and commit/rollback the run transition before spawning. Retain explicit feedback modes and current-candidate checks. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIXoONtMPmkEOmlCY+AGhafWvYt/DwAtm0ZJNEa6x1U0ZjmtLRU11X3W5Ub25BQRDwaDYGfwIJ7fy72x3xxSJA0="}
