riants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large-file and many-path capture/restore, divergent preimage rejection, interrupted staging/publication/restore, then reopen and continue the same conversation with an exact restored workspace. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJK8SEl5VZSKWsMCoVJyOfcHQzbC4xUACTyH4vbq1G3VeewKL1lYgPiTCO5z314egkmbsg0vO7y5k3OvHdZyAQE="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3443,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.785696202Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"c078bb71-37d1-526d-bcbe-cc0389eed0c2","title":"[L755] Improvement backfill is whole-history work and its evaluation prompt still prescribes a bounded budget","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L755.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_run/improvements.rs:14-75,83-134`; `src/product_run/improvements/store.rs:178-222,260-280`; `src/product_run/improvements/evaluation.rs:13-44,98-181,188-240` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: every inbox action first loads the entire existing inbox and scans every same-workspace run under run/store locks. Candidate reads allocate complete SQLite JSON before checking MAX_STATE_BYTES; every inbox reconstructs all candidates, including dismissed ones, with no page cursor. Evidence summaries are truncated to 4,096 bytes. SQLite uses a five-second busy timeout. Explicit evaluation serializes all launches, reads/parses the entire target Cargo.toml, queues each evidence source sequentially and ends its directive with 'Use the normal bounded run budget.'\n- Consequence: growth increases synchronous collection/projection work and can hide detailed original failure evidence. The SQLite wait is a storage contention policy, not provider context lifetime, but its failure surfaces through a generic inbox internal error. The prompt retains a synthetic budget expectation even though current execution defaults may have removed that budget. Failure/cycle>=3 collection only suggests investigation; it does not stop work.\n- Repair direction: page and incrementally backfill verified observations, retain complete source evidence references, expose cancellable contention recovery and remove obsolete budget instructions consistently with actual run policy. Keep evaluation explicitly authorized and untrusted observations inert. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPnw0UJm3yJipoeUMCWyAyx29/plOgMT5GRma7wefa8NtmtL8OPWwYINhbAUTCJf00WcU8M4a3gNZ4RFtxvFiQ0="}
