{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3447,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.794827080Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"8b6e0356-6e30-5add-b138-a40b4256f065","title":"[L757] A suggestion has only one durable evaluation reservation across all future attempts","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L757.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/product_run/improvements/store.rs:139-175,230-258`; `src/product_run/improvements/evaluation.rs:46-97,157-173`; `src/product_run/improvements/store/tests.rs:36-79` in the same crate.\n- Behavior: candidate identity hashes normalized proposal plus workspace, without harness/source revision. Once evaluated, evidence freezes. Reserve returns the original run/conversation when actor, target and provider IDs match, even if a new run ID was supplied; changing those owners/selection is rejected. Evaluation replays deterministic prepared commands and StartExecution for the original identity.\n- Consequence: exact replay prevents duplicate launch, but the same suggestion cannot express a later separately authorized evaluation after a failed/finished attempt or a harness revision. A new requested run identity is silently replaced by the first reservation. This is a permanent attempt-identity restriction rather than an elapsed timer.\n- Repair direction: preserve the immutable first evaluation receipt while modeling subsequent explicitly authorized evaluations as separate attempts fenced to source/harness revision. Keep duplicate retry resolution and frozen evidence for each original attempt. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTk