{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3449,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.799528784Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"c2f2e689-0baa-5013-aeb5-4d0ee95bd6d2","title":"[L759] Formal readiness predicates prohibit diagnostics while startup remains incomplete","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L759.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-daemon/src/verified.rs:58-87,89-131,135-179,189-228`; L731.\n- Behavior: the verified finite model admits mutations only in ReadyReadWrite and diagnostics only in ReadyReadWrite, ReadyReadOnly or Draining. Starting and Unavailable admit neither. Startup transitions must follow the exact fixed phase sequence. The executable wrappers refine those enum predicates; the proof does not model I/O progress, native supervisor ownership or restart adoption.\n- Consequence: while long recovery remains Starting, this admission contract provides no diagnostic surface to explain progress or the particular stalled phase. Proving exact phase ordering is distinct from proving startup eventually completes or preserves an active context. Integrity readiness gates must remain even when elapsed limits are removed.\n- Repair direction: expose an authenticated read-only startup/recovery progress channel independent of mutation readiness and prove durable recovery transitions at actual effect/context owners. Preserve fail-closed mutation admission and exact phase ordering. No tests or formal verification run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKv1