d non-ASCII fields, queue/connection pressure, delayed acknowledgements, subscription gaps, disconnect/reconnect and daemon restart, proving snapshot recovery, preserved selection/context, responsive controls and no duplicate command. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQN/I/4NgNuWqyOg8+bUPPXZro3aOkqyGwnD9aKOWab2f3ZzG+H+qgry6KTY5exe9jgteCk2nxazfXmzJpaPlWwE="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3451,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.804193327Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"6fc2e08f-1d9d-5a97-861e-2d332432fe08","title":"[L784] TUI composition duplicates whole drafts before its fixed task-size rejection","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L784.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-tui/src/input/composer.rs:1-187`, `input/selection.rs:1-50`, `input/output.rs:1-141`, `input/terminal.rs:1-88`, and `model/chat/keys.rs:1-195`, all completely read; crate manifest and README completely read.\n- Behavior: Paste filters and allocates the whole incoming text before checking `MAX_PRODUCT_TASK_BYTES`; keyboard insertion stops silently at that same task bound. Composer layout constructs rows, spans, and per-character byte/cell stops for the entire draft, including during vertical movement and mouse hit testing. The one-to-six composer-row clamp and fixed modal geometry are viewport choices, not limits on stored lines. Transcript copying freezes only the visible rows. Control-byte sanitization prevents pasted text from becoming terminal commands, and pasted slash-command tokens require an explicit keyboard intent.\n- Consequence: The fixed protocol task cap still prevents a larger daily-driving instruction from being entered, while a maximum-size draft/paste can consume substantial synchronous UI work before rejection or display. There is no execution timeout in these layout/encoding helpers. Full source reading established the cost pattern, not a measured live freeze.\n- Repair direction: Support durable referenced/chunked instructions and viewport-local layout; enforce negotiated inline capacity before unnecessary copying. Preserve UTF-8 boundaries, terminal sanitization, and explicit command intent.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHdDhfev3p+YWhe0PPhHtCLazCg6gNTQteguTS1W+J2/UcLTy+xeARZkp3ZIN5sgcZe3h6eBzFsZZV+fOgRSGgI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3452,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.806428755Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"6fc2e08f-1d9d-5a97-861e-2d332432fe08","comment_uuid":"05985f52-1173-49a1-bdb4-0778aebd4e54","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L784: TUI composition duplicates whole drafts before its fixed task-size rejection.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-tui/src/input/composer.rs:1-187; input/selection.rs:1-50; input/output.rs:1-141; input/terminal.rs:1-88; model/chat/keys.rs:1-195. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nSupport durable referenced/chunked instructions and viewport-local layout; enforce negotiated inline capacity before unnecessary copying. Preserve UTF-8 boundaries, terminal sanitization, and explicit command intent.\n\nPreserve: durable logical session and run identity, exact command receipts, atomic snapshot/cursor binding, explicit authority, selected UI state, complete history retrieval and owned-effect reconciliation. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large histories and non-ASCII fields, queue/connection pressure, delayed acknowledgements, subscription gaps, disconnect/reconnect and daemon restart, proving snapshot recovery, preserved selection/context, responsive controls and no duplicate command. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNV7Lvd4hY6/pQKVEfT4+kN+uwTbxBGkYBjPS9RJ3gLvF0YksA+CKwrV+is328jvHhHDsC/w2y2sXUnzAECW8g0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3453,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.808748559Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"8b4e583f-bf33-592a-b224-867b8932cfea","title":"[L785] Chat progress is gated by volatile pending lookups and a missing binding can detach the run","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L785.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-tui/src/model/chat.rs:1-299`, `model/chat/binding.rs:1-145`, and `model/chat/commands.rs:1-218`, completely read.\n- Behavior: A pending chat query, open, binding, or product-message binding suppresses all `poll_chat` work, including the goal poll. Submission and model changes wait for volatile mutation/binding bookkeeping. The first send on an unchecked saved run performs a binding lookup and requires the user to send again. If a run remains selected without a durable workbench destination after that path, sending clears the run/binding and asks for another Enter to start a new conversation. Binding depends on negotiated `WorkbenchRunBinding`. Opening another workspace also blocks on an unsent draft; active mode changes require an explicit stop. Command dispatch closes the file panel before it validates the command and generally leaves goal-inspection mode for unrelated commands.\n- Consequence: A slow/unresolved lookup can suppress visible progress even though daemon work continues. The detach/new-conversation fallback can make an unavailable original destination look like ephemeral session behavior; it does not recover the original native context. Mutation serialization and exact workspace routing protect authority and need durable reconciliation rather than deletion. The current live session's lockup was not reproduced by this source read.\n- Repair direction: Separate independent observation streams, preserve the original durable run/destination through lookup failure, and expose reconciliation state with a retry that retains identity. Trace pending-request expiration and reconnect ownership in the runtime and receipt handlers.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQH9i740C3fad148YN2NTgkw/WKfXIw41Fb3sQQom8vTpWKFalflE8vuZWQvlKnZM4ApeNh5hldY8tUiz+tYL+Ak="}
