econcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLDvTJYjcyTVr9W3h5wHkhn4DaXQRa1fsO+VyYnnLjYkZPQA8V5IUQAEGisz5C7iofUU615hcgR31HUYE2YqIgU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3455,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.813242732Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"a64e058b-295a-594e-9ebf-31df9aca04ef","title":"[L786] Selection overlays consume control keys, and model updates clear intent before send success","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L786.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-tui/src/model/chat/navigation.rs:1-258`, `model/chat/doctor.rs:1-99`, `model/chat/picker.rs:1-34`, `model/chat/models.rs:1-305`, `model/chat/models/effort.rs:1-92`, `model/chat/working.rs:1-70`, `model/chat/catalog.rs:1-214`, and `model/chat/catalog/entries.rs:1-264`, all completely read.\n- Behavior: Terminal-selection mode handles every key before chat control routing and consumes it until Esc/F2 or paste restores live mode; Ctrl-R and normal quit/cancel keys therefore do not reach their usual handlers while it owns input. Clipboard copying has one pending operation per selection. Doctor and model discovery deduplicate pending reads, with Esc removing their local request tracking. Manual model IDs bypass catalog membership explicitly; effort choice does not require discovery. Saving model/effort clears the command and closes pickers before `request` can fail to send; a no-run selection exists only in the current UI model. The working indicator resets by busy period/run and only reports elapsed observation time, with no deadline or stop condition.\n- Consequence: An input-owner mode can resemble an unresponsive UI; its release is a local mode transition, not provider reconnection. An offline/failed model update requires reconstructing the cleared intent, and process restart loses unsent UI-only selection. The busy timer is not an artificial execution limiter. No live UI or tests were exercised in this audit.\n- Repair direction: Make input ownership and release continuously visible, preserve exact model-update intent until durable acknowledgement, and reconcile it through reconnect. Keep explicit manual-ID/command boundaries and observer-only elapsed accounting.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQN+4l8OzonKGsvNh5dSXYK4tWeJgfy6ICVuy2KGupYoMo0ThMLu7BEr/KDX5t0QAY8lgP1SXula5YYVZIOPljAE="}
