ariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large histories and non-ASCII fields, queue/connection pressure, delayed acknowledgements, subscription gaps, disconnect/reconnect and daemon restart, proving snapshot recovery, preserved selection/context, responsive controls and no duplicate command. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBdloT8Wu0GmcgRRApiQF+1PYO+K0aYm251FjuiCNX0IAOk2T0fr3Y8lkSg9vfmjFE3AnYAV05KXFR6DnKOUfgs="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3457,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.817517438Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"62d76711-b08a-5f50-aca0-ddb1049e38de","title":"[L787] The composer accepts a larger draft than durable chat admission can represent","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L787.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-tui/src/model/chat/workbench/conversation.rs:1-338` and `sessions.rs:1-147`, completely read; task-sized editing gate in L784.\n- Behavior: Normal chat admission converts the entire draft to `WorkbenchInputText` and rejects anything outside 1–8,192 bytes. The composer instead permits `MAX_PRODUCT_TASK_BYTES`. Sending then stages creation, queue admission, execution discovery/start, and continuation through separate receipts. New titles are derived from at most 64 characters; explicit session titles and literal searches are capped at 256 bytes, and library requests ask for 64 rows with pagination. An archived session requires explicit unarchive. The continuation command has no independent operation identity, as recorded in L716.\n- Consequence: A valid editable draft can become unsendable at Enter. A queued input can survive while later execution admission fails or remains unresolved; the UI cannot infer that receipt acceptance means the original native window was recovered. Title/search page capacities differ from execution budgets and authority checks must remain explicit.\n- Repair direction: Unify the editable/admitted input contract using durable referenced text, and make queue-to-execution continuation an idempotent operation with a recoverable worker identity. Preserve archive, workspace, and user-stop authority.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNxqoU5XHnUSehdpnKGmf0ge8tswAvrvugzIu2MgN+t7tgOkeRkeIWWsSm25XYuDp49d6z21PLDuHT0cqzY33gQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3458,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.820004176Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"62d76711-b08a-5f50-aca0-ddb1049e38de","comment_uuid":"2d709585-aecf-4fe2-b21a-7b6e5b2f8807","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L787: The composer accepts a larger draft than durable chat admission can represent.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-tui/src/model/chat/workbench/conversation.rs:1-338; sessions.rs:1-147. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nUnify the editable/admitted input contract using durable referenced text, and make queue-to-execution continuation an idempotent operation with a recoverable worker identity. Preserve archive, workspace, and user-stop authority.\n\nPreserve: committed command/event identity, exact causal and digest roots, exclusive ownership, atomic publication, reference-safe artifact retention and verified recovery from the last durable frontier. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKzV02yRZBW+QZm8CmoY/jc4NJaIGbu1fxHvOvV73DyJMSMfP1kX52twe4/NsGLkMJ5y4EJR155bLVEfOZBggQM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3459,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.822554161Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"e3846a2d-582e-54e4-a061-d226928f2e20","title":"[L788] Exact control recovery exists only in the retained UI model, and some messages overstate admission","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L788.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-tui/src/model/chat/workbench.rs:1-394`, `refresh.rs:1-96`, `receipts.rs:1-341`, `receipts/correlation.rs:1-40`, `receipts/recovery.rs:1-37`, `receipts/rejection.rs:1-54`, and `receipts/error.rs:1-236`, all completely read. Response callers `src/model/protocol/response.rs:1-383` and `response/control.rs:1-187` were fully reread.\n- Behavior: An original workbench command and draft are retained in `WorkbenchUi.unresolved`; reconnect queries that exact operation before explicit replay. Receipt matching checks operation, destination, and accepted revision. For ResumeGoal, a read-only recovered receipt deliberately leaves the operation unresolved and requires `/sessions retry` because worker launch is separately persisted. Ordinary review receipts label explanation/revision work as started, although the admission/launch split in L753 can prevent execution. Most panel error state uses only the error code rather than diagnostic/recovery detail. A normal disconnect clears pending request maps but retains this command only in the process-local model.\n- Consequence: This is stronger than creating a new operation on reconnect, but it is not a durable client outbox that survives loss of the UI process. A missing launch or receipt may fence later edits indefinitely; a claimed start can obscure that distinction. Exact receipt and consent fencing should remain, while recovery must identify accepted-but-unlaunched work.\n- Repair direction: Persist client intents and their settlement state, bind launch reconciliation to the accepted operation, and report admission separately from observed launch. Surface the retained diagnostic/recovery source without replacing uncertain operations by new identities.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQC/HhM7fpdZnyRUtMBVXYnzrgA+uZJuKyumVZvXTorjbigJz250Ts7HAybhCjgt9kFnbB65NC+vsoncrvoUT2wI="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3460,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.824763160Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"e3846a2d-582e-54e4-a061-d226928f2e20","comment_uuid":"6e64f347-d14c-4c66-a229-c824468210f0","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L788: Exact control recovery exists only in the retained UI model, and some messages overstate admission.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-tui/src/model/chat/workbench.rs:1-394; refresh.rs:1-96; receipts.rs:1-341; receipts/correlation.rs:1-40; receipts/recovery.rs:1-37; receipts/rejection.rs:1-54; receipts/error.rs:1-236; src/model/protocol/response.rs:1-383; response/control.rs:1-187. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nPersist client intents and their settlement state, bind launch reconciliation to the accepted operation, and report admission separately from observed launch. Surface the retained diagnostic/recovery source without replacing uncertain operations by new identities.\n\nPreserve: durable logical session and run identity, exact command receipts, atomic snapshot/cursor binding, explicit authority, selected UI state, complete history retrieval and owned-effect reconciliation. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large histories and non-ASCII fields, queue/connection pressure, delayed acknowledgements, subscription gaps, disconnect/reconnect and daemon restart, proving snapshot recovery, preserved selection/context, responsive controls and no duplicate command. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJnKPAR8NlA8Ip3NGbKzuxZKctap+g0qGxtO2aQYiz+NZgw/80IDaTOjk3vSQ13HQ8jMkDzyFEJhB1NQ32MNpwc="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3461,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.826995363Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"16788852-7cbc-54c9-8897-f224dc3fb9f1","title":"[L789] Removing request expiry left global pending-read gates without independent progress recovery","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L789.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-tui/src/model/chat/workbench/navigation.rs:1-181`, `navigation/cancel.rs:1-80`, and `tests/timeouts.rs:1-99`, completely read. `src/model.rs:1-607`, `src/model/protocol.rs:1-305`, `src/model/product/observation.rs:1-153`, and `src/runtime.rs:1-347` were fully reread to trace the caller path.\n- Behavior: The current reducer does not expire requests by elapsed ticks. The timeout-named tests explicitly advance to tick 10,000 and require slow reads/model updates to remain pending. `workbench_request_pending` globally combines local file/image reading with virtually every workbench query, receipt, mutation, and preview lookup. Refresh and new chat admission return without sending while any such item is pending. Esc abandons ordinary inspection tracking, but if a chat submission or unresolved mutation exists it retains the entire workflow; reconnect clears transport requests and re-queries the same retained receipt. Slow recent/exact run queries suppress dashboard polls, while chat and preview polling run before that dashboard gate. Chat itself still has the lookup gate in L785.\n- Consequence: A never-returning read or reconciliation step can permanently block independent controls despite the removal of artificial deadlines. The tests establish absence of time-based disconnection, not eventual progress, cancellation of the host operation, or native recovery. The README still describes read-only request timeouts/expiry, which does not match this current reducer.\n- Repair direction: Give independent observations independently supersedable ownership, provide cancellation/reconciliation transitions for pending operations, and preserve accepted-mutation identities through durable recovery. Do not substitute another execution deadline for these missing transitions. No tests were run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLX3iKNygDdK20OKFrO58p2eamXN/qatFM7sDvJJBlFy4rdzSBe6FHlVH6Rpw+Shv/JzBK1kHIqFPbNkwPQhnAA="}
