{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3463,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.832177880Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"fac5d399-4c9e-5bab-9459-6df3648b1490","title":"[L790] Canceling an attachment panel does not cancel its capacity-one blocking file reader","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L790.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-tui/src/runtime/files.rs:1-40`, `runtime/images.rs:1-32`, `runtime/interrupts.rs:1-36`, and `runtime/product.rs:1-190`, completely read; runtime dispatch fully reread as cited in L789.\n- Behavior: File and image readers each admit one `spawn_blocking` job until their JoinSet produces a completion. Panel dismissal changes reducer ownership and suppresses late continuation, but these reader APIs have no cancellation operation. A second read reports that another read is still finishing. Thread work uses the existing synchronous whole-source readers (L261) and remains active through a stuck filesystem read. The event loop otherwise selects local job completions alongside input, connection, ticks, and process interrupts. Product launch facts scope run/conversation/latest selection to the caller's workspace; they are not fresh health evidence.\n- Consequence: A slow or stuck old read can prevent a new explicit attachment read after its panel was dismissed. It does not by itself stop daemon work, and introducing a timer would not cancel a blocking filesystem thread or make effects recoverable.\n- Repair direction: Implement cancellable/chunked reads with independently owned reader generations and explicit completion settlement; permit unrelated requests to progress without falsely claiming the old job stopped.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQILLE5niWL1JsSYBdE4qQak0RB1+YBWxLd+I6jqHlqTxmNClX/zw4p187m+K3XO+yL5tHVeUx4Spovq3sZ22JgM="}
