{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3465,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.836870984Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"f44cccbf-5850-5417-92f8-4bf92dbb4b42","title":"[L791] Foreground candidate execution suspends the whole UI reducer without a durable process owner","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L791.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-tui/src/runtime/candidate.rs:1-144`, `candidate/foreground.rs:1-152`, and `runtime/terminal.rs:1-221`, all completely read; caller `src/runtime.rs:1-347` fully reread.\n- Behavior: Running a candidate checks the exact repository digest, parses a direct executable/argument command, stops the terminal input worker, suspends the full-screen terminal, and awaits a blocking child-status task. That await does not pump `next_effects`, daemon events, subscription acknowledgements, local reads, or model polls. Interrupt signals are consumed while waiting for the foreground command to exit. Unix transfers the terminal to the child's process group, observes stops with waitpid, and waits for shell SIGCONT before foreground restoration; handoff failure kills that group. This child has no durable C2 launch receipt or reconnect/adoption identity here. The 100 ms input poll/park is a scheduling cadence, not a lifetime cap; selection mode deliberately skips all subsequent redraws until release.\n- Consequence: A long-running or interrupt-resistant candidate can keep the interface unavailable while its connection event queue stops draining; loss of the owning client cannot adopt this same process through these APIs. Natural command duration and OS job-control waits must not be replaced by a synthetic execution deadline. Candidate digest/foreground ownership checks are integrity boundaries.\n- Repair direction: Keep connection/control progress alive during terminal handoff and route candidate launches through a durable process owner with explicit cancel, exit, and adoption receipts. Preserve correct foreground process groups and exact candidate authorization.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCISA8zK3dHs4beiCOhE8KYZfSedVv8YglFBDPX8KN7CMmr4jfGH06dqbtChMfoZd4ZuM9M03DYQzqNActv5dgg="}
