ble.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBZpPjZ7zQWZqA2CKn2PFWGY6hqoYrtnza8R8VK/OXXw7ETvX73XLsSehhAjUS0x86KrJ7r8kuaciv4seIbsmgk="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3467,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.841554281Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"89b69d04-c251-5ba8-add3-40cb22b9bfa3","title":"[L792] Clipboard writing has no default deadline but a hung helper holds its sole slot","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L792.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-tui/src/runtime/clipboard.rs:1-216`, completely read.\n- Behavior: Production clipboard copy passes `None` to the optional native-helper timeout. The 100 ms/one-second deadlines appear only in tests that deliberately select a timeout. The writer permits one pending job; it sends all text to wl-copy/xclip/pbcopy, closes stdin, and waits for exit. Only a missing helper falls back to OSC 52; other helper errors are returned. The fallback synchronously writes and flushes terminal stdout from the async task. kill-on-drop covers the immediate helper, without a durable owned-process record or explicit in-UI cancel API.\n- Consequence: A stalled helper occupies the copy slot until completion/drop, and a blocked fallback terminal write can stall the runtime. There is no artificial production clipboard deadline to remove. Whole selection encoding and stdout work are not progress-aware.\n- Repair direction: Provide an owned, cancellable clipboard operation and avoid blocking the UI executor on terminal transport; retain exact inert Unicode bytes and truthful failure/acknowledgement reporting.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPRvo550BG