nnect and daemon restart, proving snapshot recovery, preserved selection/context, responsive controls and no duplicate command. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIEWdY6iL9qHng+G8oH50GfCOGxkArrcixQkgx25zOp34Qfy5JSmbLln5IzZQ6PaorUz4GU+qZO8/XcLDaTE4AQ="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3469,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.846366507Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"8edbcff7-1734-5b91-878d-f38fc3e85a2e","title":"[L794] A stale compaction preview is refreshed with the same obsolete revision","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L794.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-tui/src/model/chat/workbench/compaction.rs:1-117`, `context.rs:1-176`, and `brief.rs:1-163`, completely read; stale snapshot refresh scope and inspection error handlers in L788.\n- Behavior: `/compact` builds its request from the retained conversation snapshot; `refresh_compaction` clones that exact stored request. On compaction inspection failure, the error handler clears the preview but leaves both request and conversation snapshot. Automatic checkpoints can advance the aggregate revision without a UI mutation receipt. General pre-command snapshot refresh handles checkpoint/rewind/fork and selected session metadata actions, but not compaction. Therefore pressing refresh can repeatedly query the same obsolete revision until the operator separately refreshes the conversation. Context/queue pages have explicit revision and offset validation, while brief edits require exact inspected proposal identity. Compaction focus is limited to 1,024 bytes and brief text to 8,192 bytes.\n- Consequence: This is a state-refresh loop rather than an elapsed-time failure. Exact revision/consent checks prevent applying an obsolete preview and must remain. Context inspection displays metadata and does not reconnect a provider window.\n- Repair direction: On an obsolete preview request, obtain a fresh aggregate snapshot, rebuild a newly inspectable preview, and require confirmation of that new preview. Preserve the original draft and source intent; do not replay a previously consented mutation against changed contents.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJK3AK3xu+xVLXk4RMmSHg8H3t9b+VHjreb+wb/x8ifYYvdO5Ui86zxSByckvEzsGRrh1j/xaO20TwJm6P4ynwk="}
