sessions through repeated compaction and segment boundaries, source/dependency changes, non-ASCII and large evidence, interrupted checkpoint publication, then reopen the same lineage and prove that valid grounding is reused and stale targets are reread. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHDaQ6oO8T7d+miYwTDXMhdJtDQaDAmA4807IkVOqyxtJNqtupUzWG2UaG6xJm1TxshRwTT6l8AJWTB992n04Ac="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3471,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.851399917Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"3dd0ec14-b291-55aa-8710-d6e168dc73a1","title":"[L795] Queue reorder requires every pending ID but the composer cannot hold the largest valid order","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L795.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-tui/src/model/chat/workbench/queue.rs:1-257`, `library.rs:1-133`, and `fork.rs:1-106`, completely read; larger fixed queue/domain bounds in L705 and composer bound in L784.\n- Behavior: Reorder accepts one textual list containing all pending 32-hex IDs and constructs the whole vector before the input-order validator. The protocol admits up to 65,535 IDs, requiring about 2.16 MiB of textual identifiers and separators, beyond the 1 MiB composer task bound. Queue text itself remains capped at 8,192 bytes. Paged row selection preserves exact input revision/identity, and aggregate refresh does not reinterpret an old row against a reordered list. Library navigation is paged; fork requires exact checkpoint references and truncates only the generated title at a UTF-8 boundary.\n- Consequence: The UI cannot express a valid maximum-size reorder even though the underlying order type accepts it. Page sizes/title presentation do not end execution. Immutable row/checkpoint/workspace checks are authority boundaries, not synthetic runtime ceilings.\n- Repair direction: Represent reorder as durable incremental moves or an uploaded/reference-backed exact order, with a revision fence and completion receipt. Retain identity-based selection and independently progressing page reads.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/