{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3473,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.856623209Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"24ca3c2b-58bf-5cc6-b9f8-4f743959fd20","title":"[L796] Goal drafting is local and goal controls inherit the global read fence","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L796.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-tui/src/model/chat/workbench/goal.rs:1-282`, `goal/draft.rs:1-161`, and `goal/refresh.rs:1-31`, all completely read.\n- Behavior: Objectives and graphical criterion descriptions are limited to 8,192 bytes. An unconfirmed draft resides only in WorkbenchUi, permits one optional graphical criterion, and always includes the existing mandatory runner-acceptance criterion. Confirming first saves the exact objective in the brief, then starts the goal after a separately correlated brief refresh. Pause/resume refuse to send while any global workbench request or unresolved command is pending; missing goal inspection asks the user to repeat the control after reading. A refreshed control is retained only while goal identity and draft still match. There is no time, token, turn, or tool budget in these UI goal constructors.\n- Consequence: A pending unrelated read can delay even an explicit goal pause/resume, and loss of the UI can lose the unconfirmed draft or the next stage of confirmation. Mandatory acceptance criteria describe completion authority; they are distinct from a synthetic lifetime cap. A native-context recovery guarantee still requires the durable execution-owner work recorded earlier.\n- Repair direction: Make explicit goal controls independently admissible against the exact goal identity, persist unconfirmed/partially confirmed user intent, and settle staged brief/goal admission durably. Keep user confirmation, safe-boundary pause semantics, and exact criterion identity.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNSJCJylLaNPNHSoROWYk2ejd915v1cFxTFiS6egEcxRMhnjHigjjSVaFpFNTZoRuT2Adq12pdSj7ai5MaiKywk="}
