{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3475,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.861183669Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"7c92ec4b-f134-5581-99de-69357a4a425e","title":"[L797] Restore recovery receipts release the UI's exact-operation retry record","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L797.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-tui/src/model/chat/workbench/checkpoints.rs:1-290`, `checkpoints/receipts.rs:1-161`, `memory.rs:1-279`, `permissions.rs:1-158`, and `init.rs:1-137`, all completely read.\n- Behavior: Checkpoint/restore matching retains exact operation, checkpoint, destination, revision, and original command. Rewind refresh obtains a fresh snapshot and builds another inspectable preview, unlike compaction in L794. After any matching restore receipt, including RecoveryRequired, `clear_checkpoint_command` takes the unresolved command; the UI clears the rewind request/preview and retains only the restore receipt with instructions to inspect recovery. `/sessions retry` can no longer replay that removed original command through this record. Checkpoint names are capped at 256 bytes. Guidance mutations select only an active ID in the current page and fence both record/dependency/conversation revisions. Permissions intersect immutable host authority, and init requires exact equality to the reviewed proposal.\n- Consequence: Durable server history survives, but client retry ownership ends before restore recovery is settled. An operator receives an instruction rather than an executable reconciliation transition. Guidance paging and permission/proposal checks protect user scope and should remain; none of these files adds an execution timer.\n- Repair direction: Retain a durable recovery operation until the restore transaction settles, expose its actual reconciliation action, and distinguish accepted recovery state from completed effect. Preserve exact preimages, proposal consent, forget semantics, and host authority.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLCtOSyQ/aggDWvYQM5EQOs2mCGmAslOKyfc/CGaAWgWuxW4bfmz+zmUJcCR98Bechcgfnq6LfqLYcj3ti7pDQI="}
