ceptance and nonregression: renewal/adoption under the same authorized identity, revoked authority, stale epoch/revision, cross-scope requests, lost acknowledgements and restart, proving legitimate continuation without admitting unauthorized or duplicate effects. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDIkyMUlTaxcNxUiJk9a1z+F/MEieMea9e79J0/DtnVDKxF5jqM7L9PwRcHDmbr1oK0Sl2Rn4NDPejVQkdaxQAs="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3477,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.865586747Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"7183cded-1ee6-5ab3-9fa7-2e997a03d202","title":"[L798] Attachment previews select launcher role defaults instead of the active conversation's provider","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L798.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-tui/src/model/chat/workbench/images.rs:1-245`, `files.rs:1-341`, and `files/import.rs:1-300`, all completely read; `src/model/chat.rs:278-284` and binding/receipt callers already fully read.\n- Behavior: Image reads, workspace-file previews, external-text imports, and their confirmation checks take the writer profile from `ProductUi::providers`, which represents the launcher's next-run role selection. Ordinary chat uses `chat_providers`, which first prefers the selected run snapshot's actual providers. Attachment model choice is separately taken from `chat.models.writer`. Thus opening an existing conversation with a different provider can pair its model with the launcher's default profile for preview/consent. Confirmation consistently checks that same launcher profile, rather than resolving the conversation's authoritative provider.\n- Consequence: A daily-driving attachment can be rejected by an unrelated default profile's model/media capabilities, or inspected against the wrong provider selection. The exact consent checks themselves are necessary; their source of identity must be corrected. This source-derived mismatch was not reproduced against the installed daemon.\n- Repair direction: Resolve provider/model selection through the same exact conversation/run binding used for chat, and invalidate a preview only when that authoritative binding changes. Keep byte digest, workspace, model, and user-confirmation identity together.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGdZaPvn2hRUHw0xEwOT6SxIVl4uhIocygeNN6NiKssyojZ4ZekoPheqmE5tfPZEc/9ojH77K87GXmv1FRLgUgM="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3478,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.867810173Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"7183cded-1ee6-5ab3-9fa7-2e997a03d202","comment_uuid":"5cc1d8a6-f54a-480a-ba2a-bcc076db972f","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L798: Attachment previews select launcher role defaults instead of the active conversation's provider.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-tui/src/model/chat/workbench/images.rs:1-245; files.rs:1-341; files/import.rs:1-300; src/model/chat.rs:278-284. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nResolve provider/model selection through the same exact conversation/run binding used for chat, and invalidate a preview only when that authoritative binding changes. Keep byte digest, workspace, model, and user-confirmation identity together.\n\nPreserve: definitely-unaccepted versus ambiguously-accepted request state, exact native thread/profile identity, ordered provider observations, tool-result protocol, explicit cancellation and real provider/model capabilities. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long provider outages and Retry-After, split transport chunks and large streams, ambiguous acceptance and duplicate events, cancellation during recovery, adapter restart and route changes, proving same-thread reconnection and no duplicated accepted request/effect. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBwW0GMhmXbD5hATg1ilJ0KC9PZZvBRhwu8O8sY5SNhBQOmLP0907DBjeazqDVNlBZTSTXB3np8qVU5h9eAihAc="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3479,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.870381675Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"119cd067-e0f9-5ab3-baeb-321470c91ce9","title":"[L799] Attachment upload offsets are acknowledgement-driven but discarded on reconnect","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L799.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-tui/src/model/chat/workbench/images/upload.rs:1-201`, `images/page.rs:1-121`, and `files/import.rs:1-300`, all completely read, together with the attachment parents in L798.\n- Behavior: The UI reads selected content into memory, uploads at most 64 KiB per chunk (also respecting negotiated capacity), and advances only after the matching transfer/step acknowledgement. Upload identity, bytes, and next offset live in WorkbenchUi. Interrupt handlers take/drop the upload and request state on disconnect; reconnect asks the user to explicitly preview again rather than querying a persisted accepted offset. Failed chunk construction also drops upload state. Ordinary panel dismissal can send explicit transfer cancellation, but dropping import state is not itself a durable host cancellation receipt. A missing ACK remains behind the global workbench pending gate in L789. Attachment histories use pages rather than an execution lifetime limit.\n- Consequence: A transfer interruption can force another whole read/upload with fresh identities and can strand unrelated controls until the pending ownership changes. Chunking here does not establish resumable transfer after UI/daemon replacement. There is no default per-upload time deadline to remove.\n- Repair direction: Persist transfer identity/digest and acknowledged offsets, query host settlement after reconnect, and resume/cancel that exact transfer before allocating a replacement. Allow unrelated observation/control channels to progress independently.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEG7wzeQu7zWOuqofeE/eD3QMbOpG1VJzfSHD354JnYrA8Q9NEiK1cTwLmUEKSNPxUm9JT7EWQVohaayIVHetQA="}
