nd already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large and multi-file candidates, repeated valid repair cycles, changed candidate facts, delayed reviews, local/offline verification, restart mid-gate and cancellation, proving correct repair handoff without accepting a failed candidate or rereading unchanged evidence forever. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLcl/px3q84IiOKKY4JOF08rTzB9PA+ZGhn/IHQJRWgoQx3MMzuWWX4RTAau+65yaRXRJeKV5Z0p/bulY5TbHAU="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3483,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.880424072Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"9ad36daf-d6df-5da4-adb0-e4ecb1f76200","title":"[L801] TUI rendering processes whole retained content before taking visible rows","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L801.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-tui/src/render/chat.rs:1-285`, `chat/transcript.rs:1-171`, `chat/inspector.rs:1-89`, `chat/doctor.rs:1-100`, `editor.rs:1-147`, and every workbench content renderer receipted in this batch, all completely read.\n- Behavior: Each transcript draw sanitizes and wraps every retained activity before selecting the viewport. Tool rows are fully built/wrapped before the collapsed view keeps three opening and three final rows and inserts an explicit omission marker. Composer/modal/image editors lay out the entire draft before selecting visible rows. Inspector draw and scroll-limit calculation each build all content lines and wrap them; library selection also rebuilds its preceding items. Doctor chains fresh daemon findings with the launcher's retained report and rebuilds the combined text. Goal criteria, checkpoint paths/exclusions, briefs, and other already-bounded payloads are likewise expanded into whole display vectors.\n- Consequence: A small viewport does not bound synchronous formatting/allocation work. Frequent tick/event redraws can become expensive for large valid snapshots, even when middle tool output is hidden. This is a source-derived cost pattern, not a measured freeze in the original running instance. Collapsed previews and viewport geometry do not terminate daemon execution.\n- Repair direction: Cache immutable formatted generations and virtualize rows/content so redraw and navigation cost follow the visible region. Keep exact source references and explicit omission markers; fetch historical pages rather than requiring a whole transcript to render first.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCPQB8ROwE9juZKQOOo9PXSwqu1C0x4JsvVz2qHPkHCFrc12LfPE8XZRw9IYLBRVJizDiqixfeSfQDbgg47lCwA="}
