n\nAcceptance and nonregression: long-running commands, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGfGzITlE4bWOj72HqbWGgoNZqfpWsIjOc5fVcJ7D5AiX/Uip6DYA84M/yede5Vk8aGwgZ0OCSdkWTnZg6IJYQ8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3485,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.884818207Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"33eaa4c1-073f-5456-9b34-f39135b2908a","title":"[L802] Some display bounds can hide recovery details or omit wide characters","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L802.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-tui/src/render/prompts.rs:1-141`, `chat/transcript.rs:134-170`, `status.rs:1-82`, `tabs.rs:1-81`, and `chat/status.rs:1-51`, all completely read; additional content renderers in this batch completely read.\n- Behavior: Prompt scrolling uses u16 offsets and saturates its maximum at 65,535 wrapped rows, unlike the workbench inspector's usize row slicing. Transcript wrapping skips a grapheme whose cell width exceeds the available width; at width one a wide character can disappear from visible/copyable rows. General status uses a single unwrapped line, while chat uses two unwrapped lines, so long recovery messages are clipped by terminal width. RecoveryRequired always advertises `/retry` without consulting the operation's legal-control set; the control handler can then refuse that action. Queue previews disclose their three-line/160-character truncation and offer exact full-text inspection, while briefs disclose the existing eight-proposal/8,192-byte exclusions. These are presentation/input-access boundaries, not execution deadlines.\n- Consequence: A narrow display can obscure the cause/action needed to leave a blocked state, and sufficiently long valid prompt projections would outgrow the scroll representation. A displayed retry hint does not prove that a recovery transition is legal or executable. None of these findings establishes the current live lockup by itself.\n- Repair direction: Use addressable row paging/usize navigation, preserve indivisible wide graphemes through resizing, and derive visible recovery actions from the same legal-control/reconciliation state as dispatch. Keep exact authority IDs and distinguish observed accounting from unavailable provider counters.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKxoCK0Qv5JhhR5YcVi+mj/8GLhuk3J1yBzLOYuiQ8jjkxswUVvEAI1kCLRJFGe5EhOOeDUCq50eJOCf0B460QM="}
