econcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: large histories and non-ASCII fields, queue/connection pressure, delayed acknowledgements, subscription gaps, disconnect/reconnect and daemon restart, proving snapshot recovery, preserved selection/context, responsive controls and no duplicate command. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQC8uYg9e3EajNAf5a35bqkUTLIQfUSHh7NK4TOzs2H31zan04i8oLsInkwWK+GnODhF/v+/xDWImZodVZuI6KQo="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3487,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.889560103Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"aae80fb2-8c33-558b-8cdf-d26345e75204","title":"[L805] Web operation capacity can be consumed forever by already reconciled transport children","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L805.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-web/src/state.rs:17,261-298`; `src/daemon/receipts.rs:253-345`, `src/operations.rs:13-75`, `src/files/edit.rs:46-85` in that crate.\n- Behavior: the ledger admits at most 4,096 records when no completed record is removable; completed eviction follows BTreeMap identity order. Generic postcondition recovery returns a successful observation and stores the parent result, but does not complete its native transport record. Those unresolved children are hidden from the pending-operation list and are removed only by manual review, which returns early if the parent already has a result. File saves bypass the admission guard by directly inserting records.\n- Consequence: recoveries can accumulate invisible unresolved children until new actions are refused. Completed receipt eviction also removes the persisted deduplication basis for a previously used operation identity. A file-save bypass can enlarge a fully unresolved ledger further. These are count-based synthetic admission and retention bounds, not timeouts. Source-derived; not reproduced against the installed gateway.\n- Repair direction: atomically settle parent and transport disposition on proved recovery, retain durable identity tombstones independent of display history, and separate paging/storage policy from action admission.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBiSLbmrxNCJCnXDPdBnY/HyOup3nHMYhOmOwEKssi+dhs0z6IrsecY/99NYtvnKEsOeFVpUK2/Q7pPo2OFdNQ0="}
