{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3491,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.898843708Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"7dd507bb-eab4-5ec6-bc61-49787abc5ad5","title":"[L807] Web attachments are accepted at sizes that the durable message cannot send","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L807.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-web/src/files/attachments.rs:28-111`; `src/daemon/chat.rs:14-33` in that crate.\n- Behavior: staging accepts text snapshots up to 48 KiB and up to 16 selections; its error promises a 64 KiB combined message limit. Sending embeds all selected content and metadata as JSON, then rejects the complete message above 8 KiB. A separate 256 MiB retained-attachment metadata quota has no removal action in the fully read API dispatcher; deleting bytes alone does not remove the metadata sum.\n- Consequence: valid staged attachments, including a single large snapshot, become unsendable; encoding/metadata further reduce usable text capacity. Normal repeated attachment use can reach a permanent cache-admission blocker. Exact source/session/digest checks are integrity requirements, not synthetic lifecycle limits.\n- Repair direction: use durable attachment handles and chunked source admission consistently with the daemon, disclose the actual assembled capacity before accepting selections, and provide explicit durable snapshot removal/storage reconciliation.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQG6GRs1vHx6iA/I/VB6MSc8QrMloDxyYT55s+ZlJ7ji5SQJyti7dTjV3g