, output and stdin pressure, stalled helper/input readers, control-queue saturation, late start/exit races, parent loss and restart, proving cancellation responsiveness, no PID-reuse adoption and no duplicate process dispatch. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQF7HW9J32wGVeF2prk67RSyFW89+VpY8wWZYYNBYjONn8jZETxkuytTTBv1rPTQkIwCbnpzPabjuMau47N7hvwo="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3495,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.908062449Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"44da6e4f-faa5-51d7-93ee-7264b7d50fb1","title":"[L809] Web state schema failure becomes a fresh workspace, and receipt replacement lacks directory durability","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L809.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-web/src/state.rs:19-54,77-125,127-149,223-257,300-351`.\n- Behavior: any workspace JSON deserialization failure, including unknown fields, invokes best-effort quarantine and then uses an empty workspace even if quarantine failed. The schema has no versioned migration. save syncs the temporary file before replacement but does not sync the parent directory; every update clones and pretty-serializes all projects, sessions, receipts and attachments while holding one mutex. Nesting traverses ancestor links without a visited set for a preexisting persisted cycle.\n- Consequence: incompatible/corrupt metadata can silently detach saved session/operation ownership and seed a new conversation; subsequent saves may replace state after a failed quarantine. Crash durability of the renamed receipt is not established by file sync alone. Long histories and preexisting lineage cycles can stall shared state access. Source-derived; no power-loss or malformed-cycle experiment run.\n- Repair direction: version and migrate state explicitly, preserve incompatible originals and unresolved identities without fresh-state substitution, durably sync replacements, page records independently, and validate lineage on load.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIOhGVp8ifERYyixCJyYExFZ83XogPjmlPCRMHQQh4+Q5SjiqiJyTNflBzkHwls78cNq97wu9GdCRR4TyPSHiw8="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3496,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.911093350Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"44da6e4f-faa5-51d7-93ee-7264b7d50fb1","comment_uuid":"9ed1bfb6-a240-4765-a569-4ea2bb4d1a2c","author":"6ME5","content":"Systemic repair plan for L809: Web state schema failure becomes a fresh workspace, and receipt replacement lacks directory durability.\n\nOwning contract and implementation boundary: crates/app/peritus-web/src/state.rs:19-54,77-125,127-149,223-257,300-351. Apply the change through the constructors, live callers, durable writer and restart reader for this boundary, not as an isolated constant increase.\n\nversion and migrate state explicitly, preserve incompatible originals and unresolved identities without fresh-state substitution, durably sync replacements, page records independently, and validate lineage on load.\n\nPreserve: committed command/event identity, exact causal and digest roots, exclusive ownership, atomic publication, reference-safe artifact retention and verified recovery from the last durable frontier. Separate a physical allocation/page limit and a genuine authority or integrity check from a cumulative work allowance. Keep transient contention/capacity observable and recoverable under the existing logical task; do not discard accepted state or substitute a fresh session to get around it.\n\nCompatibility/migration: retain decoders and exact receipts for previously accepted records. If representation or lifecycle semantics change, introduce a versioned migration under exclusive ownership; verify a complete replacement frontier before atomic publication and keep the old recovery root until adoption is durable. Rebuild derived projections from authoritative evidence. Update all producers, consumers and invariants together; a rejected new operation must leave the predecessor usable and already owned effects reconcilable.\n\nAcceptance and nonregression: history beyond the reported count/byte boundaries, lock contention lasting beyond the old patience window, lost commit acknowledgements followed by later progress, torn uncommitted tails and true committed corruption, then reopen and resolve exact historical receipts. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKcx/6bzG+SH00ESBDamaON+HEeOeWZ0W29VXbNiMBYb+RhZMPLyxZo5sRIXDZIWGqGpkaapOHPSa2/5dC4Smgo="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3497,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.913386233Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"c265d26d-53eb-597e-bc33-dec25a5c85e6","title":"[L810] Web daemon discovery and request sessions do not preserve a native owner binding","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L810.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-web/src/daemon.rs:29-112,134-149,194-261,281-323`; `src/daemon/receipts.rs:24-44,223-236`, `src/sessions.rs:97-212`, `src/daemon/readiness.rs:8-88` in that crate.\n- Behavior: configuration and product snapshots are selected separately by lexicographically last filename, without binding the selected product state to the config/store. Every raw request and retry opens a new Client with no retained app SessionId; the prepared message retains conversation/run/workspace/provider/model/text but not endpoint/store/native process ownership. Opening a run requires an already-open project whose separately discovered facts match. Doctor checks current admission and explicitly defers authentication until use.\n- Consequence: stored browser sessions are persistent presentation identities, while connections and endpoint discovery can change independently. They do not establish continuity of an active native provider window, and discovery failure can force setup or project reopening despite retained daemon work. Transport sessions must not be confused with provider context windows. No live-instance reproduction is claimed.\n- Repair direction: bind durable browser operations and discovery to explicit store/workspace/endpoint ownership, reconcile that binding on restart, and qualify native context adoption separately from metadata reopening.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAQPRdpCjN5EU1uR7S/+K2bhytx8I8M+LzC7sHhkZI9I13p/eT4fDET2SZ31WAM/+KMRdCvHUBC8jAVi6QKFOQE="}
