histories and non-ASCII fields, queue/connection pressure, delayed acknowledgements, subscription gaps, disconnect/reconnect and daemon restart, proving snapshot recovery, preserved selection/context, responsive controls and no duplicate command. Exercise the precise source-described failure path and the relevant byte/count/elapsed boundaries listed in this finding, plus ordinary small inputs. Check that legitimate work progresses after the former blocker while malformed input, conflicting identity, stale preimages and unauthorized scope still reject. Add fault injection at the affected acceptance/publication/recovery boundary and run the affected integration and formal checks on the final implementation. Source-derived risks remain distinct from executed reproductions; completion requires this evidence, not a promise that a plan alone cannot break anything.","created_at":"2026-10-06T13:27:49.900Z","kind":"decision"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKNb5ytZwjd7vpsdiw9Dv9Z7C1WadaRf0thVDhgBysz5mH4YtnsilPqYsp6ToeJwKRoqOl6GVt9M9MqyuKNllAs="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3499,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.917586495Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"9604bd2c-9789-556e-858e-e3c962f91346","title":"[L811] Web paging and Git actions still wait for whole-content work","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L811.\n\n- Evidence: `crates/app/peritus-web/src/files.rs:17-43,61-95`; `src/daemon.rs:372-392`, `src/git.rs:13-80,81-125`, `src/git/workflows.rs:8-47`, `src/api.rs:181-214` in that crate.\n- Behavior: directory pages collect/stat/sort the entire directory before selecting 250 entries; text previews fully read/hash up to 50 MiB. Run listing aggregates every daemon page before returning HTTP data; refs/remotes inventory runs sequential whole-output Git commands. Git output waits without a deadline under the project mutation lock, with kill_on_drop only for the direct child and no cancellation route for the owning operation.\n- Consequence: pagination does not bound work done per response. Large histories/output and stalled hooks/signers/network children can make UI requests appear locked and prevent same-target actions indefinitely. Natural external readiness/integrity failures and ordinary Git dirty-worktree protections must remain explicit; adding a blanket timeout would not repair ownership.\n- Repair direction: expose durable cursors and incremental result work, and own native Git effects with observable lifecycle, independent controls and reconciliation of uncertain outcomes.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MT