{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3509,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.940159670Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"fa7f6d03-3abb-5e95-8072-c334bf9eb9a4","title":"[L817] Activity ordering can discard authoritative state, and control replies can move between sessions","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L817.\n\n- Evidence: `webui/src/lib/conversations.ts:1-10`; `webui/src/lib/workspace.svelte.ts:235-236`.\n- Behavior: The merge guard compares activity-tail identifiers and rejects the whole incoming conversation if its tail is older, including incoming phase and legal controls. Control dispatch sends the selected session identity before awaiting the action, then reevaluates the current selected identity when assigning its response.\n- Consequence: Truncated or older activity snapshots can hide newer recovery/cancel/model state. Switching selection while a control request is pending can assign the old session's returned conversation to the new session. These are state-authority/identity errors, not legitimate lifetime limits.\n- Repair direction: Merge authoritative fields by their own revisions, keep activity ordering local to activity data, and capture the destination identity across every asynchronous effect. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQORgValFopHn4i4thRTZu7f/1MOqF5zl1fBuZOnRRSgavyWLgFTev26se0e3UhTK5NC2NkietFLvVPOaLahkTgI="}
