{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3511,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.944847357Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"3ae4f9e8-6f6c-5bbc-bc8c-a01179d8e238","title":"[L818] Alias depth and editor undo impose additional synthetic boundaries","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L818.\n\n- Evidence: `webui/src/lib/workspace.svelte.ts:207-210`; `webui/src/lib/components/TextEditor.svelte:1-84`.\n- Behavior: Alias dispatch declares a cycle once recursion exceeds eight even for an acyclic chain. Editor undo keeps at most 200 changes and 2000000 cumulative UTF-16 units; trimming can remove a single newly added edit that exceeds that budget. Undo history belongs to the mounted component and is lost on remount.\n- Consequence: Valid long alias chains fail, and a sufficiently large accepted paste can have no immediate undo. These are command-graph and editing limits, separate from provider capacity or session lifetime.\n- Repair direction: Detect repeated alias identities rather than counting valid expansions, and preserve reversible edits through stable draft-owned history or durable deltas with explicit user-controlled retention. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGc3O7iOzYFBt9hsaKLByd7gjz5+p6/9GlH2fnx/DsB1q8r95Bg3QBlRngPwlSD56HOvDKP3uX8IG294yqppzgs="}
