{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3513,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.949214954Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"fd265147-ab51-58ed-a820-f65a2c71b87e","title":"[L819] Browser improvement capacity claims and text counters disagree with daemon admission","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L819.\n\n- Evidence: `webui/src/lib/components/Improvements.svelte:1-52`; `webui/src/lib/components/Overlays.svelte:1-49`; actual improvement capacity evidence L699 and web text admission L812.\n- Behavior: The improvements view announces a full inbox at 32 although the audited daemon capacity is 65535. Its textarea maxlength is 4096 JavaScript units while daemon admission counts 4096 UTF-8 bytes. Session title editing similarly permits 256 units against a 256-byte backend value. The composer has no equivalent preflight for its smaller durable message bound (L807).\n- Consequence: The interface can falsely report capacity exhaustion or accept input that is rejected only after submission, especially non-ASCII text. These stale presentation/admission limits do not prove a runtime deadline.\n- Repair direction: Derive visible capacity and validation from the authoritative schema and validate the exact encoded value while preserving drafts and unresolved effects. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQN2Hz1Ud0Vbxwsg8NcGL1jMUr3JbbMgo1JYmv36502D6uXsw2dSOoZ807Fr2ZcP3+zBtx5b6JyENEwRzTY2w/AI="}
