{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3517,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.958147699Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"3f47feff-9dc1-5a2f-a002-fc778f55b9af","title":"[L821] Explorer paging lacks consistent request and directory identities","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L821.\n\n- Evidence: `webui/src/lib/components/Explorer.svelte:1-40`; `webui/src/lib/components/FileNode.svelte:1-30`; whole-directory server work L811.\n- Behavior: Root results are guarded only by project identity; concurrent refresh/load-more in the same project can race, and load-more remains available during a request. Child nodes cache results without a project-generation check. Recursive expansion has no canonical directory cycle identity. Filtering searches only pages already loaded.\n- Consequence: Duplicate or stale nodes, stale children across project changes, and indefinitely expandable in-project symlink cycles can obstruct navigation. The 250-entry page is not a whole-directory search or a lifetime limit; expansion requires user actions and is not an automatic infinite traversal.\n- Repair direction: Bind results to project/directory/query generations, reconcile page identity, and use canonical ancestry to identify cycles while preserving access to legitimate directories. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQB1Lq3bQDKVVmJGH43sy2VCTqbvI8s/nkNWrI3eaXtYX4WggLgV6d/LSUzgztPoyyO90W3gWoeZJdz9cLz/5AAw="}
