{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3519,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:27:51.962379690Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"868e3530-983d-5e90-9a4f-e9e43110bb66","title":"[L823] Settings save can overwrite edits made while the request is unresolved","description":"Source finding: docs/daily-driving-limiters-audit.md — L823.\n\n- Evidence: `webui/src/lib/components/Settings.svelte:6-14`, `19-33`.\n- Behavior: Saving disables only the Save button. Preference controls, view switching, import, and Reset remain active. A successful awaited response replaces ui.preferences, ui.config, and the editor source, even when newer edits were made during that request. Reset can submit another mutation while an earlier save remains unresolved. Import reads the whole selected file before gateway admission.\n- Consequence: A slow or hung save leaves an unresolved operation without protecting the user's newer configuration draft; a later response can replace it. This is an ownership/revision issue, not a reason to kill the request after an arbitrary duration. Whole-file import also precedes the gateway's action-body bound.\n- Repair direction: Capture immutable submitted values and draft revisions, reconcile the response to its original draft, preserve later edits, and give unresolved configuration effects a reachable recovery path. No tests run.\n\nScope: implement and verify the systemic repair recorded in the decision comment. Source-derived behavior remains distinct from a reproduced live incident.","priority":"high","labels":["daily-driving-limiter"],"parent_uuid":"f89861db-18b8-4237-83e6-344f4e472dd4","created_by":"6ME5"},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQE6nqNz7c02x3mvyMK/fq0ZDYVlE+52JqKo7FTXbH79IUO2T1y6naiwsz/kIJpnKTaTAKztuJhZQ6EFm2q0tKgw="}
