{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3531,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T15:53:21.633931516Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"d1db310b-7731-5d58-9369-497f32b29bef","comment_uuid":"0f174a9f-9951-46ce-a5f2-a3c9d404fbaa","author":"6ME5","content":"[action] Inspecting issue #105 typed checkpoint coverage and range/directory restore paths; #104 committed and pushed; monitoring PR 112 CI.","created_at":"2026-10-06T15:53:21.629615058Z","kind":"note","signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAm66MSe+aRQ7h/PaQJK5W3foRirGGEEw+0yIGSAV74cnyiHUcP90S8+A642+8myuU530Ft7UEHrqkDepMsIAYDA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQB8TzXoqBDYFfKhYezPNjyq8XcxIC6Mq2pFLfmrWT+H9D0fQvxQvc/HP+D18UppMMnTf48DwkTQWsRxUww3yLww="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3532,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T16:14:13.806207512Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"d1db310b-7731-5d58-9369-497f32b29bef","comment_uuid":"dcf1376d-20d2-4c05-81d1-965878a44f18","author":"6ME5","content":"Issue #105 is in progress on fix/persistent-execution, based on 1e872d134cd6ab9a3937069ef8eec264736fe0c5. No issue-completion commit or closure yet.\n\nConfirmed cause: selected ranges are discarded by capture_selected_coverage, and C1 has no empty-directory operation, so automatic directory checkpoints record only an exclusion.\n\nImplemented the required C1 foundation: typed EmptyDirectory preimages with checked DirectoryMode, create/delete-directory operations, one mixed file/directory transaction, staged directory permissions, complete postimage verification, backup rollback and restart reconciliation. Directory manifests use schema 3; existing file-only schema 1/2 formats and identities remain unchanged. Snapshot metadata retains wide counts and large-file support. File-only tool/harness callers explicitly reject a directory preimage rather than accidentally replacing a directory as a regular file.\n\nDirectory backup observation and cleanup now preserve an external child added through an existing handle. Cleanup uses nonrecursive removal and retains the manifest on failure. Tests reproduce interrupted mixed installation, original-directory inode/permission restoration, nonempty and permission-conflicting preimages, external children in backups and installed directories, legacy manifest decoding, downgrade rejection, authority binding to directory permissions, and a snapshot containing a file above 8 MiB plus 1,025 directory targets.\n\nVerified on the current foundation:\n- cargo test -q --locked -p peritus-patch -p peritus-tools-fs -p peritus-harness -p peritus-workspace --all-features --no-fail-fast -- --test-threads=1\n- strict all-target/all-feature Clippy for patch, tools-fs and harness\n- Windows GNU cross-compilation for patch, workspace, tools-fs and harness; native Windows runtime tests not run\n- strict cargo verus verify for those four packages; this does not claim formal proof of all ordinary filesystem effects\n- ordinary-api-check and architecture-check against HEAD plus the exact 19 issue paths, excluding unrelated pre-existing provider work\n- earlier full workspace all-target/all-feature compilation passed\n\nStill required before closure: typed checkpoint coverage and directory versions through capture, durable writers/restart readers, automatic sealing, restore planning/evidence and client projections; selected-range restoration preserving surrounding current bytes, with the exact materialized postimages used for recovery settlement; negotiated wire compatibility and end-to-end regressions. Preserve explicit exclusions for deselected/imported or wrong-folder sources and external effects.\n\nPR 112's pushed #104 head currently has 310 successful, 5 skipped, 52 running and 86 queued checks, with no failures reported at this observation.","created_at":"2026-10-06T16:14:13.792329734Z","kind":"note","signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAqah1y6Yi1LZIdNHQ6eD/L2BoQXaVgG/Vw97wx/++frzt3qaKcsZjPNEPphO9mhCN0vjN9wM0cSbcsREeE135CA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQB/uBf5j52vqPk/1DUSKaJN7KRkr5wGYS5WXNR3x0LjjWF8qDfI1qvDt/LZDKGXknljGRZGNF3A5ZlICYQ7FtwY="}
