{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3534,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T17:11:47.936086948Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"d1db310b-7731-5d58-9369-497f32b29bef","comment_uuid":"d78e31d4-6561-494f-af45-75024cc03a92","author":"6ME5","content":"[action] Issue #105: typed coverage, selected-range overlays, exact recovery postimages, directory restoration and negotiated client projections implemented. Core suites and partial cold-restart regression pass; final daemon, compatibility and source-boundary verification remain before commit.","created_at":"2026-10-06T17:11:47.922808139Z","kind":"note","signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAefjJv9Ab0R/f1PW+7C+NdHHdTC1Sl+phQ0vn+LLckRpNXrPekK4IN6yIvzPJq+6w2GPzEQISWEwNmKltbsmaDQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEtsBSoTsD2o8JLjyf02i29d90Xc0WdUxVp3/cw4Y7cBiHG5Uj9v7bc4IhJooeedK4E8qKY15v1v5Y6dAx8bHQ0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3535,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T17:32:57.982167512Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"d1db310b-7731-5d58-9369-497f32b29bef","comment_uuid":"c0a52158-1f3f-4a16-9c7a-d74d6a5c84ff","author":"6ME5","content":"Issue #105 integration is implemented and undergoing final verification; not committed or complete yet.\n\nThe checkpoint manifest now distinguishes whole files, selected intervals, absent paths and empty directories. Multiple selections of one path are retained and canonicalized. Range restoration streams exact saved selections over the retained current preimage, preserving every surrounding current byte and portable file mode. Directory type and permissions restore through the same authorized, recoverable C1 transaction, including file/directory replacement and recovery undo.\n\nBefore filesystem effects, the durable prepared restore records the exact materialized postimages. Reopening reconstructs the plan from authoritative saved and recovery snapshots and checks the same patch and preview identities; settlement and recovery-checkpoint sealing use the actual merged targets. This removes the old false assumption that a partial restore equals the whole original file.\n\nNew coverage and directory records are versioned. Legacy capture bytes, whole-file wire encodings, file-only manifest schema 1/2, accepted directory exclusions and previously prepared version-one restores remain usable. The optional negotiated checkpoint-coverage feature prevents a legacy peer from receiving a misleading whole-file projection or starting an unsupported typed mutation; ordinary legacy file operations remain unchanged. No new execution deadline, retry budget, range-count ceiling or total file-size ceiling was introduced.\n\nExecuted evidence on the current integration:\n- Full affected core suites passed for patch, workspace, product-runner, app-protocol, app-client, tools-fs and harness, including the snapshot above 8 MiB with 1,025 directory targets.\n- Final daemon/TUI checkpoint filter passed: 43 daemon unit tests, both affected integration tests and 9 TUI tests.\n- Production service scenarios cover partial-range capture/restore, surrounding-byte preservation, divergent-preimage rejection, restore before/after C1 interruption, exact receipt replay after cold reopen, directory permission restoration, file/directory replacement and recovery undo.\n- Streamed selection resolution above 64 MiB and 2,048 disjoint selected intervals passed, along with legacy encodings and old prepared restore identity checks.\n- Final strict all-target/all-feature Clippy across all nine affected packages passed.\n- Full workspace all-target/all-feature compilation, formatting and diff checks passed.\n- Windows GNU all-target cross-compilation passed; no native Windows runtime qualification is claimed.\n- Final architecture and ordinary API checks passed against HEAD plus the exact 83 issue paths, excluding unrelated pre-existing provider and document edits.\n\nStrict final Verus verification is now running. It is a boundary/formal contract check, not a claim that all ordinary filesystem effects have been formally proved. Remaining work before commit: finish that check and the final selected-change review, then commit and push only issue #105 to existing PR 112.","created_at":"2026-10-06T17:32:57.966888255Z","kind":"note","signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAC2Jqem7WOltoWFz70Jjp3UrX/SIogdpBi9qmrjzfVAzunCtRWA6pJKY4j3b9jGbAZGzl9EPsVWRYJBQW+Hj5Dg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNEFV9D1UfePqOI5+4twOlUCqSUOqbcC1ZhtunS/X