{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3575,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T19:20:32.114850811Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"9a6dfce0-f7af-5007-9212-db912e47510a","comment_uuid":"64362b27-07ed-4bce-b631-f6d9cf9301fe","author":"6ME5","content":"Grounded #108 design: remove component/path/depth admission ceilings and their repeated predicate. Keep historical constants only for legacy encoding classification, with platform-aware validation of new UTF-8 relative paths; Unix-native punctuation/control/trailing-dot/device-style names must not inherit Windows alias rules. Traversal, NUL, rooted paths, protected metadata and no-follow/reparse boundaries remain authority checks. Separate lossless tagged native child names from escaped display text and effect-authorizing WorkspacePath; non-UTF-8 names, links/special nodes and unavailable child metadata become typed per-entry exclusions instead of aborting usable siblings. Keep protected entries hidden. Introduce owner-backed retained directory observations and checksum-bound cursors with physical pages, full storage verification and validated resume boundaries; no total entry/page budget, session expiration or ambient rescan on resume. Migrate FS discovery/search to carry and render exclusions and bind them into versioned digests while preserving old exclusion-free digests. Remove the duplicate path schema cap through an optional string maximum API, preserving existing bounded schema bytes. Extended/native path authority and transaction storage need a new version because legacy readers reject these paths and schema-four pages require each record to fit: keep schemas one through four and their identities/receipts exact, stream version-five logical metadata across deterministic byte pages under one synchronized publication root, and reject malformed partitions/unsupported platform encodings before effects. Simply skipping bad names would hide incomplete results; removing constants alone would leave consumer/schema/recovery rejections. Independent traversal/search/render/JSON policies (#685/#109/#202) remain separate, without adding a replacement cumulative blocker. Verify old-boundary failures, host-native and raw names, unsupported siblings, durable cursor reopen, stale/corrupt/foreign state, native path transaction interruption/recovery, legacy fixtures, actual FS dispatch, platform compilation, strict lint and affected formal/local policy checks.","created_at":"2026-10-06T19:20:32.110171757Z","kind":"decision","signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAW7BE8kWDG79dXifOxtoJAsc0g5cyYGH8/LFfpRTz2Njc/jO7TrYoCN72a1RePO0gRrEzXOrSE1JqzREzP6ZcAw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIc59i9ewa3vgl9TvkMj2YeyRs3/lfxpfQ3HTKY3Z4SWnvxB6sayA/uyJqZIkMJz0L9lxn3a2mAKH4+S1iDFDg0="}
