{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3597,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T20:55:55.233568098Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"27df59d6-19ba-593d-b363-47e5993d64a1","comment_uuid":"eec8ed71-3f53-42a2-99b9-6715b8924c2a","author":"6ME5","content":"The complete caller suites caught a persistence coupling: schema-one manifest selection still used the moving production codec profile, so removing default quotas could classify a 65,536-directory patch as legacy while the frozen legacy decoder rejected it. Freeze only historical inline identity and schema-one encode/decode classification to LEGACY_V1; larger valid patches continue into the existing paged transaction representation. Boundary tests compare against the historical profile. Client request/event exchanges also invalidate a connection on any returned error, so the client frame owner now waits through typed allocator pressure with retained retry progress, matching daemon receipt rather than forcing a replacement connection. No product limits are increased or substituted.","created_at":"2026-10-06T20:55:55.219472209Z","kind":"decision","signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAUkwnxsePTxFUa+YU2cx/KvBaoglrZ8ZJ5Gq22m87yY4vv+oY9fRFwiX3tim9UkvDALclpNG9aUIS0tNqapdnCQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQK6WMo1SRLyL1Hzt/OSNDvJzNRSV54+QBB2esXzoboDE2IXHJEGPe+IE5uvsrUibQ27Ge6KzXPYNTCOP2V5hVAo="}
