{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3634,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T22:48:55.988108543Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"7dba4e90-7fcd-4daa-b57b-1d3085aa762a","comment_uuid":"7b71a5cb-12e5-4ee4-aa4d-9190ba6471b9","author":"6ME5","content":"OS cause reproduced directly: run33 of the separate OS-cause experiment exited101 because std::process::Command::output on a just-copied auth fake returned Os code26 / ExecutableFileBusy / Text file busy (/tmp/peritus-issue825-os-cause-33.log); the failed run is retained and the loop stopped. Source fs::copy creates executable writers while other fixture threads fork; Linux fork can inherit those writers until exec closes them, so parent copy completion is insufficient to ensure the inode has no writer. The manual execve ETXTBSY and fork descriptor inheritance contracts support this mechanism (https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/execve.2.html and https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/fork.2.html). Repair the fixture owner by hard-linking the immutable built binary in private directories on the same artifact filesystem; no executable-copy writer, fork mutex, sleep, retry or deadline change. Deterministic Linux regression holds a writer on a legacy copy, observes ExecutableFileBusy, then verifies the new immutable alias has the Cargo artifact device/inode and executes the real auth rejection while that writer remains live; after dropping the writer the legacy copy executes too. Cleanup removes only the private alias and retains the source artifact. Native Windows/macOS qualification must confirm alias naming and filesystem semantics. Source-parent tempdirs avoid an actual cross-device failure here: /tmp and the Cargo cache are different filesystems. Historical discarded auth predicate cannot be retroactively recovered; new spawn/trace defects have concrete reproduction and root repair.","created_at":"2026-10-06T22:48:55.981298062Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAokCPr8S7QxV1zsRDZpm6nZVklOyt089gsFrGNZaoqRgzNZpL6c6XyCPq1CSdRC/GXGBp1HtNf8nHD2fv2/Z4CA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJp7TgvH/qHuLQQIPoc/RExSG3x0ZVR94xkIq6OcoM+n98fHbX+nt4yhSg5ik1nAxe9TfZJRuiaW8pNNOWo0SQ0="}
{"agent_id":"6ME5","agent_seq":3635,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T22:53:13.829834597Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"7dba4e90-7fcd-4daa-b57b-1d3085aa762a","comment_uuid":"29b5aeaf-5099-4c93-a992-8be94b9fd524","author":"6ME5","content":"Final regression review found and corrected an invalid test isolation premise, not a failing provider assertion: /tmp/peritus-issue825-repaired-exercise-5.log failed only when the regression tried to execute its legacy copied binary after dropping the local writer; all14 provider cases and new immutable-alias execution passed. Parallel test forks can inherit the intentionally injected writer, so local drop still does not guarantee final kernel writer release. Preserve both busy-before-release and executable-after-final-release assertions by owning the injected writer in a dedicated single-case child test process; other parallel test forks cannot inherit that child-owned descriptor. The parent observes child completion and success with no sleeps, retries or deadline. This provides additional concrete evidence for the original copy/fork ownership mechanism and avoids recreating that race inside the regression. Also moved the core spawn receipt regression into its own module after repository source-layout check correctly flagged the parent process test at407 lines; no rule override or skipped check. All failed experiments remain separate retained logs. Final-state qualification is being rerun;825 still OPEN.","created_at":"2026-10-06T22:53:13.815950728Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3gDv1stiLN1YhgJ9dMhoOBjZhbEednuPkV+1IAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAopLQ6f7oqbZ/3TJHZ4EalxeQqBo/4iSlb5Tq5NEH0Q6CEALWzIXVJuHvLKwNut5eSjS5Igcq5Mvc8Pxsd9l1Dw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:eV8eZPaZxut5mrkihmvsOTrGWClwD+B/HR//do+oIeI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQq5MtA3